шение ясности в документации","Оптимизация коммитов и сообщений об ошибках","Эффективное написание для разработчиков","Стандарты письма для технической прозы","Советы, чтобы избежать плохих паттернов письма"],"ar":["تحسين الوضوح في المستندات","تحسين الرسائل والرسائل النصية","كتابة فعالة للمطورين","معايير الكتابة للنصوص الفنية","نصائح لتجنب الأنماط السيئة للكتابة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["清晰简洁写作","代码注释","文档写作","用户界面设计","技术写作","开发者文档"],"ja":["明確簡潔な書き方","コードの注釈","ドキュメントの作成","ユーザーインターフェイス設計","テクニカルライティング","開発者ドキュメント"],"ko":["명확하고 간결한 작성","코드 주석","문서 작성","사용자 인터페이스 디자인","기술 작성","개발자 문서"],"es":["escritura técnica","documentación clara","comunicación efectiva","redacción de commit messages","escritura de mensajes de error","mejora de la documentación"],"fr":["écriture technique","documentation claire","communication efficace","rédaction de messages de commit","écriture de messages d''erreur","amélioration de la documentation"],"de":["technisches Schreiben","klare Dokumentation","effektive Kommunikation","Formulierung von Commit-Messages","Schreiben von Fehlermeldungen","Verbesserung der Dokumentation"],"pt":["escrita clara","desenvolvedores","documentação","commits","mensagens de erro","prosa técnica","padrões de escrita"],"ru":["ясное написание","разработчики","документация","коммиты","сообщения об ошибках","техническая проза","стандарты письма"],"ar":["كتابة واضحة","مطورين","مستندات","رسائل","رسائل نصية","نصوص فنية","معايير الكتابة"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.503Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"writing-clearly-and-concisely","description":"Use when writing prose humans will read—documentation, commit messages, error messages, explanations, reports, or UI text. Applies Strunks timeless rules for clearer, stronger, more professional writing.","bodyPreview":"# Writing Clearly and Concisely\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite with clarity and force. This skill covers what to do (Strunk) and what not to do (AI patterns).\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill whenever you write prose for humans:\n\n- Documentation, README files, technical explanations\n- Commit messages, pull request descriptions\n- Error messages, UI copy, help text, comments\n- Reports, summaries, or any explanation\n- Editing to improve clarity\n\n**If you''re writing sentences for a human to read, use","body":"# Writing Clearly and Concisely\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite with clarity and force. This skill covers what to do (Strunk) and what not to do (AI patterns).\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill whenever you write prose for humans:\n\n- Documentation, README files, technical explanations\n- Commit messages, pull request descriptions\n- Error messages, UI copy, help text, comments\n- Reports, summaries, or any explanation\n- Editing to improve clarity\n\n**If you''re writing sentences for a human to read, use this skill.**\n\n## Limited Context Strategy\n\nWhen context is tight:\n\n1. Write your draft using judgment\n2. Dispatch a subagent with your draft and the relevant section file\n3. Have the subagent copyedit and return the revision\n\nLoading a single section (~1,000-4,500 tokens) instead of everything saves significant context.\n\n## Elements of Style\n\nWilliam Strunk Jr.''s *The Elements of Style* (1918) teaches you to write clearly and cut ruthlessly.\n\n### Rules\n\n**Elementary Rules of Usage (Grammar/Punctuation)**:\n\n1. Form possessive singular by adding ''s\n2. Use comma after each term in series except last\n3. Enclose parenthetic expressions between commas\n4. Comma before conjunction introducing co-ordinate clause\n5. Don''t join independent clauses by comma\n6. Don''t break sentences in two\n7. Participial phrase at beginning refers to grammatical subject\n\n**Elementary Principles of Composition**:\n\n8. One paragraph per topic\n9. Begin paragraph with topic sentence\n10. **Use active voice**\n11. **Put statements in positive form**\n12. **Use definite, specific, concrete language**\n13. **Omit needless words**\n14. Avoid succession of loose sentences\n15. Express co-ordinate ideas in similar form\n16. **Keep related words together**\n17. Keep to one tense in summaries\n18. **Place emphatic words at end of sentence**\n\n### Reference Files\n\nThe rules above are summarized from Strunk''s original text. For complete explanations with examples:\n\n| Section | File | ~Tokens |\n|---------|------|---------|\n| Grammar, punctuation, comma rules | `02-elementary-rules-of-usage.md` | 2,500 |\n| Paragraph structure, active voice, concision | `03-elementary-principles-of-composition.md` | 4,500 |\n| Headings, quotations, formatting | `04-a-few-matters-of-form.md` | 1,000 |\n| Word choice, common errors | `05-words-and-expressions-commonly-misused.md` | 4,000 |\n\n**Most tasks need only `03-elementary-principles-of-composition.md`** — it covers active voice, positive form, concrete language, and omitting needless words.\n\n## AI Writing Patterns to Avoid\n\nLLMs regress to statistical means, producing generic, puffy prose. Avoid:\n\n- **Puffery:** pivotal, crucial, vital, testament, enduring legacy\n- **Empty \"-ing\" phrases:** ensuring reliability, showcasing features, highlighting capabilities\n- **Promotional adjectives:** groundbreaking, seamless, robust, cutting-edge\n- **Overused AI vocabulary:** delve, leverage, multifaceted, foster, realm, tapestry\n- **Formatting overuse:** excessive bullets, emoji decorations, bold on every other word\n\nBe specific, not grandiose. Say what it actually does.\n\nFor comprehensive research on why these patterns occur, see `signs-of-ai-writing.md`. Wikipedia editors developed this guide to detect AI-generated submissions — their patterns are well-documented and field-tested.\n\n## Bottom Line\n\nWriting for humans? Load the relevant section from `elements-of-style/` and apply the rules. For most tasks, `03-elementary-principles-of-composition.md` covers what matters most.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:42:01.163Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Language Agents needing to refine prose for human readability, such as those utilizing LangChain or AutoGPT for content generation.","zh":"非常适合需要完善散文以适应人类可读性的语言代理，例如使用 LangChain 或 AutoGPT 生成内容的代理。","ja":"LangChain または AutoGPT を使用してコンテンツを生成するなどの、人間の読み手にとっての文章を洗練する必要がある言語エージェントに最適です。","ko":"LangChain 또는 AutoGPT를 사용하여 콘텐츠를 생성하는 등의人类가 읽기 쉽게 文章을 다듬는 언어 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de lenguaje que necesitan refinar la prosa para que sea legible por humanos, como aquellos que utilizan LangChain o AutoGPT para la generación de contenido.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de langage ayant besoin d''affiner la prose pour une lisibilité humaine, tels que ceux utilisant LangChain ou AutoGPT pour la génération de contenu.","de":"Perfekt für Sprachagenten, die Prosa für die Lesbarkeit durch Menschen verfeinern müssen, wie z.B. solche, die LangChain oder AutoGPT für die Inhaltsgenerierung verwenden.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem que precisam refinir a prosa para legibilidade humana, como aqueles que utilizam LangChain ou AutoGPT para geração de conteúdo.","ru":"Идеально подходит для языковых агентов, которым необходимо усовершенствовать прозу для чтения человеком, таких как те, которые используют LangChain или AutoGPT для генерации контента.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء اللغويين الذين يحتاجون إلى تعدين النص لقراءة البشر، مثل أولئك الذين ياستخدمون LangChain أو AutoGPT لتوليد المحتوى."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft concise commit messages, clear documentation, and readable error messages using Strunk principles and avoiding detrimental AI patterns, thereby enhancing user experience through improved UI copy and technical explanations.","zh":"使代理能够使用 Strunk 原则编写简洁的提交消息、清晰的文档和可读的错误消息，并避免有害的 AI 模式，从而通过改进的 UI 副本和技术解释来增强用户体验。","ja":"Strunk の原則を使用して、エージェントが簡潔なコミットメッセージ、明確なドキュメント、および読みやすいエラーメッセージを作成できるようにし、有害な AI パターンを回避することで、UI コピーおよび技術的説明の改善を通じてユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させる。","ko":"에이전트가 스트런크 원칙을 사용하여 간결한 커밋 메시지, 명확한 문서 및 읽기 쉬운 오류 메시지를 작성할 수 있도록 하여, 유해한 AI 패턴을 피하고 사용자 경험을 개선하기 위한 UI 복사본 및 기술적 설명을 향상시킵니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear mensajes de confirmación concisos, documentación clara y mensajes de error legibles utilizando los principios de Strunk y evitando patrones de IA perjudiciales, mejorando así la experiencia del usuario a través de una mejor copia de interfaz de usuario y explicaciones técnicas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des messages de validation concis, une documentation claire et des messages d''erreur lisibles en utilisant les principes de Strunk et en évitant les modèles d''IA préjudiciables, améliorant ainsi l''expérience utilisateur grâce à une meilleure copie d''interface utilisateur et à des explications techniques.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, verständliche Commit-Mitteilungen, klare Dokumentationen und lesbare Fehlermeldungen unter Verwendung der Strunk-Prinzipien und unter Vermeidung schädlicher KI-Muster zu erstellen, wodurch die Benutzererfahrung durch verbesserte Benutzeroberflächenkopie und technische Erklärungen gesteigert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar mensagens de commit concisas, documentação clara e mensagens de erro legíveis usando os princípios de Strunk e evitando padrões de IA prejudiciais, melhorando assim a experiência do usuário por meio de cópias de UI aprimoradas e explicações técnicas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать краткие сообщения о фиксации, ясную документацию и читаемые сообщения об ошибках с использованием принципов Странка и избегая вредных моделей ИИ, тем самым улучшая опыт пользователя за счет улучшения копий интерфейса пользователя и технических объяснений.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من صياغة رسائل الالتزام الموجزة، والوثائق الواضحة، ورسائل الخطأ القابلة للقراءة باستخدام مبادئ سترانك وتجنب أنماط الذكاء الاصطناعي الضارة، مما يعزز من تجربة المستخدم من خلال نسخ واجهة المستخدم المحسنة والشرح التقني."},"useCases":{"en":["Refining README files for clarity","Optimizing technical explanations for non-technical stakeholders","Editing reports for concise summaries"],"zh":["为清晰度改进 README 文件","为非技术利益相关者优化技术解释","编辑报告以获得简明的摘要"],"ja":["明確性を高めるために README ファイルを改良する","非技術的な利害関係者向けに技術的解説を最適化する","簡潔なまとめを得るためにレポートを編集する"],"ko":["명확성을 높이기 위해 README 파일을 개선하다","비 기술적인 관련자들을 위한 기술적인 설명을 최적화하다","간결한 요약을 얻기 위해 보고서를 편집하다"],"es":["Refinar archivos README para claridad","Optimizar explicaciones técnicas para partes interesadas no técnicas","Editar informes para resúmenes concisos"],"fr":["Affiner les fichiers README pour la clarté","Optimiser les explications techniques pour les parties prenantes non techniques","Éditer les rapports pour des résumés concis"],"de":["README-Dateien für Klarheit verfeinern","Technische Erklärungen für nicht-technische Stakeholder optimieren","Berichte für prägnante Zusammenfassungen bearbeiten"],"pt":["Refinamento de arquivos README para clareza","Otimização de explicações técnicas para partes interessadas não técnicas","Edição de relatórios para resumos concisos"],"ru":["Уточнение файлов README для ясности","Оптимизация технических объяснений для не-технических заинтересованных сторон","Редактирование отчетов для кратких сводок"],"ar":["تعدين ملفات README للوضوح","تحسين التوضيحات الفنية للأطراف المعنية غير الفنية","تحرير التقارير لملخصات موجزة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Strunk principles","Limited to prose intended for human readers"],"zh":["需要了解 Strunk 原则","仅限于面向人类读者的散文"],"ja":["Strunk の原則を理解する必要がある","人間の読者向けの文章のみに限定される"],"ko":["스트런크 원칙을 이해해야 함","인간이 읽을 수 있는 文章만 해당"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de Strunk","Limitado a la prosa destinada a lectores humanos"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de Strunk","Limité à la prose destinée aux lecteurs humains"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Strunk-Prinzipien","Begrenzt auf Prosa, die für menschliche Leser bestimmt ist"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento dos princípios de Strunk","Limitado à prosa destinada a leitores humanos"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов Странка","Ограничен прозой, предназначенной для чтения человеком"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ سترانك","محدود بالنص الموجه للقراء البشر"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
