kdown-Format","Automatisieren Sie den Prozess der PRD-Erstellung"],"pt":["Recebe descrição da funcionalidade do usuário","Faz perguntas essenciais para esclarecimento","Gera PRD estruturado","Salva em formato Markdown","Criação personalizada de PRD"],"ru":["Получает описание функциональности от пользователя","Задает важные вопросы для уточнения","Генерирует структурированный PRD","Сохраняет в формате Markdown","Создание индивидуального PRD"],"ar":["يستقبل وصف الميزة من المستخدم","يسأل الأسئلة الأساسية للتوضيح","ينشئ مواصفات المنتج المنظمة","يحفظ بالتنسيق Markdown","إنشاء مواصفات المنتج المخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["prd","","","","",""],"ja":["PRD","","","","",""],"ko":["prd","","","","",""],"es":["generador de PRD","requisitos de producto","documentos de requisitos","automatización de PRD","creación de PRD","herramientas de PRD"],"fr":["générateur de PRD","spécifications de produit","documents de spécifications","automatisation de PRD","création de PRD","outils de PRD"],"de":["PRD-Generator","Produktanforderungen","Anforderungsdokumente","Automatisierung von PRD","Erstellung von PRD","PRD-Tools"],"pt":["Gerador de PRD","Documentos de Requisitos de Produto","Desenvolvimento de Software","Requisitos de Produto","PRD","Gerador de PRD online"],"ru":["Генератор PRD","Документы требований продукта","Разработка программного обеспечения","Требования продукта","PRD","Генератор PRD онлайн"],"ar":["مولد مواصفات المنتج","مستندات متطلبات المنتج","تطوير البرمجيات","متطلبات المنتج","PRD","مولد مواصفات المنتج عبر الإنترنت"]}},"owner":"CElyousfi","repo":"PalntsScanner","repoPath":"CElyousfi/PalntsScanner","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.503Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prd","description":"Generate a Product Requirements Document (PRD) for a new feature. Use when planning a feature, starting a new project, or when asked to create a PRD. Triggers on: create a prd, write prd for, plan this feature, requirements for, spec out.","bodyPreview":"# PRD Generator\n\nCreate detailed Product Requirements Documents that are clear, actionable, and suitable for implementation.\n\n---\n\n## The Job\n\n1. Receive a feature description from the user\n2. Ask 3-5 essential clarifying questions (with lettered options)\n3. Generate a structured PRD based on answers\n4. Save to `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`\n\n**Important:** Do NOT start implementing. Just create the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAsk only critical questions where the initial prompt i","body":"# PRD Generator\n\nCreate detailed Product Requirements Documents that are clear, actionable, and suitable for implementation.\n\n---\n\n## The Job\n\n1. Receive a feature description from the user\n2. Ask 3-5 essential clarifying questions (with lettered options)\n3. Generate a structured PRD based on answers\n4. Save to `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`\n\n**Important:** Do NOT start implementing. Just create the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAsk only critical questions where the initial prompt is ambiguous. Focus on:\n\n- **Problem/Goal:** What problem does this solve?\n- **Core Functionality:** What are the key actions?\n- **Scope/Boundaries:** What should it NOT do?\n- **Success Criteria:** How do we know it''s done?\n\n### Format Questions Like This:\n\n```\n1. What is the primary goal of this feature?\n   A. Improve user onboarding experience\n   B. Increase user retention\n   C. Reduce support burden\n   D. Other: [please specify]\n\n2. Who is the target user?\n   A. New users only\n   B. Existing users only\n   C. All users\n   D. Admin users only\n\n3. What is the scope?\n   A. Minimal viable version\n   B. Full-featured implementation\n   C. Just the backend/API\n   D. Just the UI\n```\n\nThis lets users respond with \"1A, 2C, 3B\" for quick iteration.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: PRD Structure\n\nGenerate the PRD with these sections:\n\n### 1. Introduction/Overview\nBrief description of the feature and the problem it solves.\n\n### 2. Goals\nSpecific, measurable objectives (bullet list).\n\n### 3. User Stories\nEach story needs:\n- **Title:** Short descriptive name\n- **Description:** \"As a [user], I want [feature] so that [benefit]\"\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** Verifiable checklist of what \"done\" means\n\nEach story should be small enough to implement in one focused session.\n\n**Format:**\n```markdown\n### US-001: [Title]\n**Description:** As a [user], I want [feature] so that [benefit].\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Specific verifiable criterion\n- [ ] Another criterion\n- [ ] Typecheck/lint passes\n- [ ] **[UI stories only]** Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n```\n\n**Important:** \n- Acceptance criteria must be verifiable, not vague. \"Works correctly\" is bad. \"Button shows confirmation dialog before deleting\" is good.\n- **For any story with UI changes:** Always include \"Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\" as acceptance criteria. This ensures visual verification of frontend work.\n\n### 4. Functional Requirements\nNumbered list of specific functionalities:\n- \"FR-1: The system must allow users to...\"\n- \"FR-2: When a user clicks X, the system must...\"\n\nBe explicit and unambiguous.\n\n### 5. Non-Goals (Out of Scope)\nWhat this feature will NOT include. Critical for managing scope.\n\n### 6. Design Considerations (Optional)\n- UI/UX requirements\n- Link to mockups if available\n- Relevant existing components to reuse\n\n### 7. Technical Considerations (Optional)\n- Known constraints or dependencies\n- Integration points with existing systems\n- Performance requirements\n\n### 8. Success Metrics\nHow will success be measured?\n- \"Reduce time to complete X by 50%\"\n- \"Increase conversion rate by 10%\"\n\n### 9. Open Questions\nRemaining questions or areas needing clarification.\n\n---\n\n## Writing for Junior Developers\n\nThe PRD reader may be a junior developer or AI agent. Therefore:\n\n- Be explicit and unambiguous\n- Avoid jargon or explain it\n- Provide enough detail to understand purpose and core logic\n- Number requirements for easy reference\n- Use concrete examples where helpful\n\n---\n\n## Output\n\n- **Format:** Markdown (`.md`)\n- **Location:** `tasks/`\n- **Filename:** `prd-[feature-name].md` (kebab-case)\n\n---\n\n## Example PRD\n\n```markdown\n# PRD: Task Priority System\n\n## Introduction\n\nAdd priority levels to tasks so users can focus on what matters most. Tasks can be marked as high, medium, or low priority, with visual indicators and filtering to help users manage their workload effectively.\n\n## Goals\n\n- Allow assigning priority (high/medium/low) to any task\n- Provide clear visual differentiation between priority levels\n- Enable filtering and sorting by priority\n- Default new tasks to medium priority\n\n## User Stories\n\n### US-001: Add priority field to database\n**Description:** As a developer, I need to store task priority so it persists across sessions.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Add priority column to tasks table: ''high'' | ''medium'' | ''low'' (default ''medium'')\n- [ ] Generate and run migration successfully\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n\n### US-002: Display priority indicator on task cards\n**Description:** As a user, I want to see task priority at a glance so I know what needs attention first.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Each task card shows colored priority badge (red=high, yellow=medium, gray=low)\n- [ ] Priority visible without hovering or clicking\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n### US-003: Add priority selector to task edit\n**Description:** As a user, I want to change a task''s priority when editing it.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Priority dropdown in task edit modal\n- [ ] Shows current priority as selected\n- [ ] Saves immediately on selection change\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n### US-004: Filter tasks by priority\n**Description:** As a user, I want to filter the task list to see only high-priority items when I''m focused.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Filter dropdown with options: All | High | Medium | Low\n- [ ] Filter persists in URL params\n- [ ] Empty state message when no tasks match filter\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n- FR-1: Add `priority` field to tasks table (''high'' | ''medium'' | ''low'', default ''medium'')\n- FR-2: Display colored priority badge on each task card\n- FR-3: Include priority selector in task edit modal\n- FR-4: Add priority filter dropdown to task list header\n- FR-5: Sort by priority within each status column (high to medium to low)\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- No priority-based notifications or reminders\n- No automatic priority assignment based on due date\n- No priority inheritance for subtasks\n\n## Technical Considerations\n\n- Reuse existing badge component with color variants\n- Filter state managed via URL search params\n- Priority stored in database, not computed\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n- Users can change priority in under 2 clicks\n- High-priority tasks immediately visible at top of lists\n- No regression in task list performance\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Should priority affect task ordering within a column?\n- Should we add keyboard shortcuts for priority changes?\n```\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\nBefore saving the PRD:\n\n- [ ] Asked clarifying questions with lettered options\n- [ ] Incorporated user''s answers\n- [ ] User stories are small and specific\n- [ ] Functional requirements are numbered and unambiguous\n- [ ] Non-goals section defines clear boundaries\n- [ ] Saved to `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:44:35.129Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing structured Product Requirements Document generation.","zh":"非常适合需要生成结构化产品需求文档的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが構造化された製品要件文書を生成する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"구조화된 제품 요구사항 문서 생성이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan generar documentos de requisitos de producto estructurados.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de générer des documents de spécifications de produit structurés.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungssysteme, die strukturierte Produktanforderungsdokumente benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de geração de Documentos de Requisitos de Produto estruturados.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходима генерация структурированных документов требований к продукту.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل التطوير التي تحتاج إلى توليد مستندات متطلبات المنتج المهيكلة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create detailed PRDs based on feature descriptions, utilizing markdown file format and generating files to a specific directory, such as `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`, and leveraging essential clarifying questions for precise requirements gathering.","zh":"使代理能够根据功能描述创建详细的PRD，利用markdown文件格式，并将文件生成到特定目录中，例如`tasks/prd-[功能名称].md`，并利用基本的澄清问题来收集精确的需求。","ja":"エージェントが機能説明に基づいて詳細なPRDを作成できるようにし、マークダウンファイル形式を利用し、ファイルを特定のディレクトリ（例：`tasks/prd-[機能名].md`）に生成し、正確な要件収集のための基本的な明確化質問を利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 기능 설명을 기반으로詳細한 PRD를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, 마크다운 파일 형식을 사용하고, 파일을 특정 디렉토리(예: `tasks/prd-[기능 이름].md`)에 생성하며, 정확한 요구사항 수집을 위한 기본적인澄清 질문을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear PRD detallados basados en descripciones de funciones, utilizando el formato de archivo markdown y generando archivos en un directorio específico, como `tasks/prd-[nombre-de-la-función].md`, y aprovechando preguntas esenciales de aclaración para una recopilación precisa de requisitos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des PRD détaillés basés sur les descriptions de fonctionnalités, en utilisant le format de fichier markdown et en générant des fichiers dans un répertoire spécifique, comme `tasks/prd-[nom-de-la-fonctionnalité].md`, et en exploitant des questions essentielles de clarification pour un recueil précis des exigences.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, detaillierte PRD auf Basis von Funktionsbeschreibungen zu erstellen, unter Nutzung des Markdown-Dateiformats und Erzeugung von Dateien in einem bestimmten Verzeichnis, wie z.B. `tasks/prd-[Funktionsname].md`, und nutzt wesentliche Klarstellungsfragen für eine präzise Anforderungserfassung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar PRDs detalhados com base em descrições de recursos, utilizando o formato de arquivo markdown e gerando arquivos em um diretório específico, como `tasks/prd-[nome-do-recurso].md`, e utilizando questões essenciais de esclarecimento para coleta precisa de requisitos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать подробные документы требований к продукту на основе описаний функций, используя формат файла markdown и генерируя файлы в определённом каталоге, таком как `tasks/prd-[название-функции].md`, и используя важные вопросы для уточнения для точного сбора требований.","ar":"تمكّن الوكالات من إنشاء وثائق متطلبات المنتج المفصلة بناءً على وصفات الميزات، باستخدام تنسيق ملف تعليمات markdown وتوليد الملفات إلى دليل محدد، مثل `tasks/prd-[اسم-الميزة].md`، وتوظيف أسئلة توضيحية أساسية لجمع متطلبات دقيق."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating PRDs for new feature implementations","Creating structured requirements documents for development teams","Automating the PRD creation process based on user input"],"zh":["为新功能实现生成PRD","为开发团队创建结构化的需求文档","基于用户输入自动化PRD创建过程"],"ja":["新機能の実装のためのPRDを生成する","開発チームのための構造化された要件文書を作成する","ユーザーの入力に基づいてPRD作成プロセスを自動化する"],"ko":["새로운 기능 구현을 위한 PRD 생성","개발 팀을 위한 구조화된 요구사항 문서 생성","사용자 입력에 기반한 PRD 생성 프로세스 자동화"],"es":["Generación de PRD para nuevas implementaciones de funciones","Creación de documentos de requisitos estructurados para equipos de desarrollo","Automatización del proceso de creación de PRD en función de la entrada del usuario"],"fr":["Génération de PRD pour de nouvelles mises en œuvre de fonctionnalités","Création de documents de spécifications structurés pour les équipes de d