","Compatibilité avec la mise en œuvre","Enregistrement du PRD sous forme de fichier Markdown"],"de":["Erstellung strukturierter PRD","Angepasste Klarstellungsfragen","Funktionsbeschreibung und Spezifikationen","Kompatibilität mit der Umsetzung","Speichern des PRD als Markdown-Datei"],"pt":["Criação de PRDs personalizados","Receba descrições de características do usuário","Geração de PRDs estruturados","Salva PRDs em formato Markdown","Perguntas clarificadoras essenciais"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных PRD","Получение описаний функций от пользователя","Генерация структурированных PRD","Сохранение PRD в формате Markdown","Существенные уточняющие вопросы"],"ar":["إنشاء مواصفات منتج مخصصة","استلام описات الميزات من المستخدم","إنشاء مواصفات منتج منظم","حفظ المواصفات في صيغة Markdown","أسئلة توضيحية أساسية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PRD生成器","产品需求文档","自动化工具","开发效率","功能描述"],"ja":["PRDジェネレーター","製品要件文書","自動化ツール","開発効率","機能の説明"],"ko":["PRD 생성기","제품 요구사항 문서","자동화 도구","개발 효율성","기능 설명"],"es":["PRD","generador de PRD","requisitos de producto","desarrollo de software","documentación de producto","especificaciones de producto","gestión de proyecto"],"fr":["PRD","générateur de PRD","exigences de produit","développement de logiciel","documentation de produit","spécifications de produit","gestion de projet"],"de":["PRD","PRD-Generator","Produktanforderungen","Softwareentwicklung","Produktdokumentation","Produktspezifikationen","Projektmanagement"],"pt":["Gerador de PRD","Documentos de Requisitos de Produto","Desenvolvimento de Produto","Requisitos de Produto","PRD","Gerador de Documentos"],"ru":["Генератор PRD","Технические Требования Продукта","Разработка Продукта","Требования Продукта","PRD","Генератор Документов"],"ar":["مولد مواصفات المنتج","وثائق متطلبات المنتج","تطوير المنتج","متطلبات المنتج","PRD","مولد الوثائق"]}},"owner":"eKoh951","repo":"hytale-gg","repoPath":"eKoh951/hytale-gg","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.503Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prd","description":"Generate a Product Requirements Document (PRD) for a new feature. Use when planning a feature, starting a new project, or when asked to create a PRD. Triggers on: create a prd, write prd for, plan this feature, requirements for, spec out.","bodyPreview":"# PRD Generator\n\nCreate detailed Product Requirements Documents that are clear, actionable, and suitable for implementation.\n\n---\n\n## The Job\n\n1. Receive a feature description from the user\n2. Ask 3-5 essential clarifying questions (with lettered options)\n3. Generate a structured PRD based on answers\n4. Save to `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`\n\n**Important:** Do NOT start implementing. Just create the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAsk only critical questions where the initial prompt i","body":"# PRD Generator\n\nCreate detailed Product Requirements Documents that are clear, actionable, and suitable for implementation.\n\n---\n\n## The Job\n\n1. Receive a feature description from the user\n2. Ask 3-5 essential clarifying questions (with lettered options)\n3. Generate a structured PRD based on answers\n4. Save to `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`\n\n**Important:** Do NOT start implementing. Just create the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAsk only critical questions where the initial prompt is ambiguous. Focus on:\n\n- **Problem/Goal:** What problem does this solve?\n- **Core Functionality:** What are the key actions?\n- **Scope/Boundaries:** What should it NOT do?\n- **Success Criteria:** How do we know it''s done?\n\n### Format Questions Like This:\n\n```\n1. What is the primary goal of this feature?\n   A. Improve user onboarding experience\n   B. Increase user retention\n   C. Reduce support burden\n   D. Other: [please specify]\n\n2. Who is the target user?\n   A. New users only\n   B. Existing users only\n   C. All users\n   D. Admin users only\n\n3. What is the scope?\n   A. Minimal viable version\n   B. Full-featured implementation\n   C. Just the backend/API\n   D. Just the UI\n```\n\nThis lets users respond with \"1A, 2C, 3B\" for quick iteration. Remember to indent the options.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: PRD Structure\n\nGenerate the PRD with these sections:\n\n### 1. Introduction/Overview\nBrief description of the feature and the problem it solves.\n\n### 2. Goals\nSpecific, measurable objectives (bullet list).\n\n### 3. User Stories\nEach story needs:\n- **Title:** Short descriptive name\n- **Description:** \"As a [user], I want [feature] so that [benefit]\"\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** Verifiable checklist of what \"done\" means\n\nEach story should be small enough to implement in one focused session.\n\n**Format:**\n```markdown\n### US-001: [Title]\n**Description:** As a [user], I want [feature] so that [benefit].\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Specific verifiable criterion\n- [ ] Another criterion\n- [ ] Typecheck/lint passes\n- [ ] **[UI stories only]** Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n```\n\n**Important:** \n- Acceptance criteria must be verifiable, not vague. \"Works correctly\" is bad. \"Button shows confirmation dialog before deleting\" is good.\n- **For any story with UI changes:** Always include \"Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\" as acceptance criteria. This ensures visual verification of frontend work.\n\n### 4. Functional Requirements\nNumbered list of specific functionalities:\n- \"FR-1: The system must allow users to...\"\n- \"FR-2: When a user clicks X, the system must...\"\n\nBe explicit and unambiguous.\n\n### 5. Non-Goals (Out of Scope)\nWhat this feature will NOT include. Critical for managing scope.\n\n### 6. Design Considerations (Optional)\n- UI/UX requirements\n- Link to mockups if available\n- Relevant existing components to reuse\n\n### 7. Technical Considerations (Optional)\n- Known constraints or dependencies\n- Integration points with existing systems\n- Performance requirements\n\n### 8. Success Metrics\nHow will success be measured?\n- \"Reduce time to complete X by 50%\"\n- \"Increase conversion rate by 10%\"\n\n### 9. Open Questions\nRemaining questions or areas needing clarification.\n\n---\n\n## Writing for Junior Developers\n\nThe PRD reader may be a junior developer or AI agent. Therefore:\n\n- Be explicit and unambiguous\n- Avoid jargon or explain it\n- Provide enough detail to understand purpose and core logic\n- Number requirements for easy reference\n- Use concrete examples where helpful\n\n---\n\n## Output\n\n- **Format:** Markdown (`.md`)\n- **Location:** `tasks/`\n- **Filename:** `prd-[feature-name].md` (kebab-case)\n\n---\n\n## Example PRD\n\n```markdown\n# PRD: Task Priority System\n\n## Introduction\n\nAdd priority levels to tasks so users can focus on what matters most. Tasks can be marked as high, medium, or low priority, with visual indicators and filtering to help users manage their workload effectively.\n\n## Goals\n\n- Allow assigning priority (high/medium/low) to any task\n- Provide clear visual differentiation between priority levels\n- Enable filtering and sorting by priority\n- Default new tasks to medium priority\n\n## User Stories\n\n### US-001: Add priority field to database\n**Description:** As a developer, I need to store task priority so it persists across sessions.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Add priority column to tasks table: ''high'' | ''medium'' | ''low'' (default ''medium'')\n- [ ] Generate and run migration successfully\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n\n### US-002: Display priority indicator on task cards\n**Description:** As a user, I want to see task priority at a glance so I know what needs attention first.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Each task card shows colored priority badge (red=high, yellow=medium, gray=low)\n- [ ] Priority visible without hovering or clicking\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n### US-003: Add priority selector to task edit\n**Description:** As a user, I want to change a task''s priority when editing it.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Priority dropdown in task edit modal\n- [ ] Shows current priority as selected\n- [ ] Saves immediately on selection change\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n### US-004: Filter tasks by priority\n**Description:** As a user, I want to filter the task list to see only high-priority items when I''m focused.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Filter dropdown with options: All | High | Medium | Low\n- [ ] Filter persists in URL params\n- [ ] Empty state message when no tasks match filter\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n- FR-1: Add `priority` field to tasks table (''high'' | ''medium'' | ''low'', default ''medium'')\n- FR-2: Display colored priority badge on each task card\n- FR-3: Include priority selector in task edit modal\n- FR-4: Add priority filter dropdown to task list header\n- FR-5: Sort by priority within each status column (high to medium to low)\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- No priority-based notifications or reminders\n- No automatic priority assignment based on due date\n- No priority inheritance for subtasks\n\n## Technical Considerations\n\n- Reuse existing badge component with color variants\n- Filter state managed via URL search params\n- Priority stored in database, not computed\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n- Users can change priority in under 2 clicks\n- High-priority tasks immediately visible at top of lists\n- No regression in task list performance\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Should priority affect task ordering within a column?\n- Should we add keyboard shortcuts for priority changes?\n```\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\nBefore saving the PRD:\n\n- [ ] Asked clarifying questions with lettered options\n- [ ] Incorporated user''s answers\n- [ ] User stories are small and specific\n- [ ] Functional requirements are numbered and unambiguous\n- [ ] Non-goals section defines clear boundaries\n- [ ] Saved to `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:45:05.088Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Product Development Agents needing structured product requirements documentation.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化产品需求文档的产品开发代理。","ja":"製品開発エージェントが構造化された製品要件文書を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"구조화된 제품 요구 사항 문서가 필요한 제품 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de productos que necesitan documentación de requisitos de producto estructurada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement de produits ayant besoin de documentation de exigences de produit structurée.","de":"Perfekt für Produktentwicklungsagenten, die strukturierte Produktanforderungsdokumentation benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de desenvolvimento de produtos que necessitam de documentação de requisitos de produto estruturada.","ru":"Идеально для агентов по разработке продукции, которым необходима структурированная документация требований к продукту.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير المنتج الذي يحتاج إلى توثيق متطلبات المنتج المنظم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate detailed Product Requirements Documents (PRDs) in Markdown format, utilizing clarifying questions and feature descriptions to produce clear, actionable, and implementation-ready documents, saved as .md files.","zh":"使代理能够生成详细的产品需求文档（PRD），以Markdown格式保存，利用澄清问题和功能描述生成清晰、可执行和可实施的文档，保存为.md文件。","ja":"エージェントが詳細な製品要件文書（PRD）を生成できるようにし、Markdown形式で保存します。明確化する質問と機能説明を使用して、明確で実行可能で実装可能な文書を生成し、.mdファイルとして保存します。","ko":"에이전트가 제품 요구 사항 문서(PRD)를 생성할 수 있도록 하여 Markdown 형식으로 저장합니다. 澄清하는 질문과 기능 설명을 사용하여 명확하고 실행 가능한 구현 가능한 문서를 생성하여 .md 파일로 저장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar documentos de requisitos de producto detallados (PRDs) en formato Markdown, utilizando preguntas aclaratorias y descripciones de características para producir documentos claros, accionables y listos para la implementación, guardados como archivos .md.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des documents de spécifications de produit détaillés (PRDs) au format Markdown, en utilisant des questions clarificatrices et des descriptions de fonctionnalités pour produire des documents clairs, actionnables et prêts à la mise en œuvre, enregistrés sous forme de fichiers .md.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, detaillierte Produktanforderungsdokumente (PRDs) im Markdown-Format zu generieren, indem sie klärende Fragen und Funktionsbeschreibungen verwenden, um klare, umsetzbare und implementierungsreife Dokumente zu erstellen, die als .md-Dateien gespeichert werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes gerem documentos de requisitos de produto detalhados (PRDs) no formato Markdown, utilizando perguntas esclarecedoras e descrições de recursos para produzir documentos claros, executáveis e prontos para implementação, salvos como arquivos .md.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать подробные документы требований к продукту (PRD) в формате Markdown, используя уточняющие вопросы и описания функций для создания rõчних, действенных и готовых к реализации документов, сохраняемых в формате .md.","ar":"يمكن للعميل توليد مستندات متطلبات المنتج المفصلة (PRDs) بصور Markdown، باستخدام أسئلة توضيحية ووصف الميزات لإنتاج مستندات واضحة ويمكن تنفيذها وجاهزة للتنفيذ، محفوظة كملفات .md."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating PRDs for new feature implementations","Creating structured product specifications","Clarifying product requirements through essential questions"],"zh":["为新功能实现生成PRD","创建结构化的产品规格","通过基本问题澄清产品需求"],"ja":["新しい機能実装のためのPRDを生成する","構造化された製品仕様を生成する","基本的な質問を通じて製品要件を明確にする"],"ko":["새로운 기능 구현을 위한 PRD 생성","구조화된 제품 사양 생성","기본적인 질문을 통해 제품 요구 사항 명확화"],"es":["Generación de PRDs para la implementación de nuevas características","Creación de especificaciones de producto estructuradas","Aclaración de los requisitos del producto a través de preguntas esenciales"],"fr":["Génération de PRDs pour la mise en œuvre de nouvelles fonctionnalités","Création de spécifications de produit structurées","Clarification des exigences de produit à l''aide de questions essentielles"],"de":["Erstellung von PRDs für die Implementierung neuer Funktionalitäten","Erstellung strukturierter Produktspezifikationen","Klärung der Produktanforderungen durch wesentliche Fragen"],"pt":["Geração de PRDs para implementações de novos recursos","Criação de especificações de produto estruturadas","Esclarecimento de requisitos de produto por meio de perguntas essenciais"],"ru":["Генерация PRD для реализации новых функций","Создание структурированных спецификаций продукции","Уточнение требований к продукту с помощью основных вопросов"],"ar":["توليد PRDs لتنفيذ ميزات جديدة","إنشاء مواصفات منتج منظم","توضيح متطلبات المنتج من خلال أسئلة أساسية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Does not support implementation, only PRD generation","Requires user input for feature descriptions and answers to clarifying questions","Output is limited to .md file format"],"zh":["不支持实现，只支持PRD生成","需要用户输入功能描述和澄清问题的答案","输出仅限于.md文件格式"],"ja":["実装はサポートせず、PRD生成のみをサポートする","機能説明と明確化する質問の回答のためのユーザー入力を必要とする","出力は.mdファイル形式のみに限定される"],"ko":["구현을 지원하지 않으며 PRD 생성만 지원합니다.","기능 설명 및 澄清하는 질문에 대한 답변을 위한 사용자 입력이 필요합니다.","출력은 .md 파일 형식으로만 제한됩니다."],"es":["No admite la implementación, solo la generación de PRD","Requiere la entrada del usuario para las descripciones de características y las respuestas a las preguntas aclaratorias","La salida está limitada al formato de archivo .md"],"fr":["Ne prend pas en charge la mise en œuvre, mais seulement la génération de PRD","Nécessite une entrée utilisateur pour les descriptions de fonctionnalités et les réponses aux questions clarificatrices","La sortie est limitée au format de fichier .md"],"de":["Unterstützt keine Implementierung, sondern nur die Erstellung von PRDs","Benötigt Benutzereingaben für Funktionsbeschreibungen und Antworten auf klärende Fragen","Die Ausgabe ist auf das .md-Dateiformat beschränkt"],"pt":["Não suporta implementação, apenas geração de PRD","Requer entrada do usuário para descrições de recursos e respostas a perguntas esclarecedoras","Saída limitada ao formato de arquivo .md"],"ru":["Не поддерживает реализацию, только генерацию PRD","Требует ввода пользователя для описаний функций и ответов на уточняющие вопросы","Выходные данные ограничены форматом файла .md"],"ar":["لا يدعم التنفيذ، بل توليد PRD فقط","يتطلب إدخال المستخدم لوصف الميزات والإجابة على الأسئلة التوضيحية","مخرجات محدودة بصيغة ملف .md"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
