re для VS Code","ar":"امتداد openspec-explore لبرنامج VS Code","en":"openspec-explore"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-explore是VS Code的扩展，允许开发者在Marked 2中打开和探索Markdown和AsciiDoc文件","ja":"openspec-exploreはVS Codeの拡張で、開発者がMarked 2でMarkdownとAsciiDocファイルを開いて探索できる","ko":"openspec-explore는 VS Code의 확장으로 개발자가 Marked 2에서 Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일을 열고 탐색할 수 있다","es":"La extensión openspec-explore para VS Code permite abrir archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc en Marked 2 para una mejor visualización","fr":"L''extension openspec-explore pour VS Code permet d''ouvrir des fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc dans Marked 2 pour une meilleure visualisation","de":"Die Erweiterung openspec-explore für VS Code ermöglicht das Öffnen von Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien in Marked 2 für eine bessere Visualisierung","pt":"A extensão openspec-explore é uma ferramenta para VS Code que permite abrir arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc no Marked 2.","ru":"Расширение openspec-explore — это инструмент для VS Code, который позволяет открывать файлы Markdown и AsciiDoc в Marked 2.","ar":"امتداد openspec-explore هو أداة لبرنامج VS Code تتيح فتح ملفات Markdown وAsciiDoc في Marked 2.","en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"definition":{"en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"features":{"zh":["在Marked 2中打开Markdown文件","在Marked 2中打开AsciiDoc文件","支持探索模式","允许创建OpenSpec文档","提高开发效率"],"ja":["Marked 2でMarkdownファイルを開く","Marked 2でAsciiDocファイルを開く","探索モードをサポート","OpenSpecドキュメントの作成を許可","開発効率を上げる"],"ko":["Marked 2에서 Markdown 파일 열기","Marked 2에서 AsciiDoc 파일 열기","탐색 모드 지원","OpenSpec 문서 생성 허용","개발 효율성提高"],"es":["Abrir archivos Markdown en Marked 2","Abrir archivos AsciiDoc en Marked 2","Mejora la visualización de documentos","Compatibilidad con VS Code","Facilita la exploración de código","Permite la creación de artefactos OpenSpec"],"fr":["Ouvrir des fichiers Markdown dans Marked 2","Ouvrir des fichiers AsciiDoc dans Marked 2","Améliore la visualisation de documents","Compatibilité avec VS Code","Facilite l''exploration de code","Permet la création d''artefacts OpenSpec"],"de":["Öffnen von Markdown-Dateien in Marked 2","Öffnen von AsciiDoc-Dateien in Marked 2","Verbessert die Visualisierung von Dokumenten","Kompatibilität mit VS Code","Erleichtert die Code-Exploration","Ermöglicht die Erstellung von OpenSpec-Artefakten"],"pt":["Abre arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc no Marked 2","Melhora a produtividade no VS Code","Permite a visualização de arquivos de forma eficiente","É uma ferramenta útil para desenvolvedores","Facilita a edição de arquivos de documentação"],"ru":["Открывает файлы Markdown и AsciiDoc в Marked 2","Улучшает производительность в VS Code","Позволяет визуализировать файлы эффективно","Это полезный инструмент для разработчиков","Облегчает редактирование документов"],"ar":["فتح ملفات Markdown وAsciiDoc في Marked 2","تحسين الإنتاجية في برنامج VS Code","تمكين العرض الفعال لملفات","هذا أداة مفيدة للمطورين","تسهيل تحرير مستندات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["VS Code扩展","Markdown文件","AsciiDoc文件","Marked 2","开发效率","openspec-explore","探索模式","OpenSpec文档"],"ja":["VS Code拡張","Markdownファイル","AsciiDocファイル","Marked 2","開発効率","openspec-explore","探索モード","OpenSpecドキュメント"],"ko":["VS Code 확장","Markdown 파일","AsciiDoc 파일","Marked 2","개발 효율성","openspec-explore","탐색 모드","OpenSpec 문서"],"es":["openspec-explore","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","extensión","visualización","código","desarrollo"],"fr":["openspec-explore","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","extension","visualisation","code","développement"],"de":["openspec-explore","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","Erweiterung","Visualisierung","Code","Entwicklung"],"pt":["openspec-explore","VS Code","Marked 2","arquivos Markdown","arquivos AsciiDoc","produtividade","desenvolvedores","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["openspec-explore","VS Code","Marked 2","файлы Markdown","файлы AsciiDoc","производительность","разработчики","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["openspec-explore","برنامج VS Code","Marked 2","ملفات Markdown","ملفات AsciiDoc","الإنتاجية","المطورون","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"gAmUssA","repo":"vscode-open-in-marked2","repoPath":"gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.503Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-explore","description":"Enter explore mode - a thinking partner for exploring ideas, investigating problems, and clarifying requirements. Use when the user wants to think through something before or during a change.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Enter explore mode. Think deeply. Visualize freely. Follow the conversation wherever it goes.\n\n**IMPORTANT: Explore mode is for thinking, not implementing.** You may read files, search code, and investigate the codebase, but you must NEVER write code or implement features. If the user asks you to implement something, remind them to exit explore mode first (e.g., start a change with `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff`). You MAY create OpenSpec artifacts (proposals, designs, specs) if the user asks—that''s c","body":"Enter explore mode. Think deeply. Visualize freely. Follow the conversation wherever it goes.\n\n**IMPORTANT: Explore mode is for thinking, not implementing.** You may read files, search code, and investigate the codebase, but you must NEVER write code or implement features. If the user asks you to implement something, remind them to exit explore mode first (e.g., start a change with `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff`). You MAY create OpenSpec artifacts (proposals, designs, specs) if the user asks—that''s capturing thinking, not implementing.\n\n**This is a stance, not a workflow.** There are no fixed steps, no required sequence, no mandatory outputs. You''re a thinking partner helping the user explore.\n\n---\n\n## The Stance\n\n- **Curious, not prescriptive** - Ask questions that emerge naturally, don''t follow a script\n- **Open threads, not interrogations** - Surface multiple interesting directions and let the user follow what resonates. Don''t funnel them through a single path of questions.\n- **Visual** - Use ASCII diagrams liberally when they''d help clarify thinking\n- **Adaptive** - Follow interesting threads, pivot when new information emerges\n- **Patient** - Don''t rush to conclusions, let the shape of the problem emerge\n- **Grounded** - Explore the actual codebase when relevant, don''t just theorize\n\n---\n\n## What You Might Do\n\nDepending on what the user brings, you might:\n\n**Explore the problem space**\n- Ask clarifying questions that emerge from what they said\n- Challenge assumptions\n- Reframe the problem\n- Find analogies\n\n**Investigate the codebase**\n- Map existing architecture relevant to the discussion\n- Find integration points\n- Identify patterns already in use\n- Surface hidden complexity\n\n**Compare options**\n- Brainstorm multiple approaches\n- Build comparison tables\n- Sketch tradeoffs\n- Recommend a path (if asked)\n\n**Visualize**\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│     Use ASCII diagrams liberally        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                         │\n│   ┌────────┐         ┌────────┐        │\n│   │ State  │────────▶│ State  │        │\n│   │   A    │         │   B    │        │\n│   └────────┘         └────────┘        │\n│                                         │\n│   System diagrams, state machines,      │\n│   data flows, architecture sketches,    │\n│   dependency graphs, comparison tables  │\n│                                         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Surface risks and unknowns**\n- Identify what could go wrong\n- Find gaps in understanding\n- Suggest spikes or investigations\n\n---\n\n## OpenSpec Awareness\n\nYou have full context of the OpenSpec system. Use it naturally, don''t force it.\n\n### Check for context\n\nAt the start, quickly check what exists:\n```bash\nopenspec list --json\n```\n\nThis tells you:\n- If there are active changes\n- Their names, schemas, and status\n- What the user might be working on\n\n### When no change exists\n\nThink freely. When insights crystallize, you might offer:\n\n- \"This feels solid enough to start a change. Want me to create one?\"\n  → Can transition to `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff`\n- Or keep exploring - no pressure to formalize\n\n### When a change exists\n\nIf the user mentions a change or you detect one is relevant:\n\n1. **Read existing artifacts for context**\n   - `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`\n   - `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`\n   - `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`\n   - etc.\n\n2. **Reference them naturally in conversation**\n   - \"Your design mentions using Redis, but we just realized SQLite fits better...\"\n   - \"The proposal scopes this to premium users, but we''re now thinking everyone...\"\n\n3. **Offer to capture when decisions are made**\n\n   | Insight Type | Where to Capture |\n   |--------------|------------------|\n   | New requirement discovered | `specs/<capability>/spec.md` |\n   | Requirement changed | `specs/<capability>/spec.md` |\n   | Design decision made | `design.md` |\n   | Scope changed | `proposal.md` |\n   | New work identified | `tasks.md` |\n   | Assumption invalidated | Relevant artifact |\n\n   Example offers:\n   - \"That''s a design decision. Capture it in design.md?\"\n   - \"This is a new requirement. Add it to specs?\"\n   - \"This changes scope. Update the proposal?\"\n\n4. **The user decides** - Offer and move on. Don''t pressure. Don''t auto-capture.\n\n---\n\n## What You Don''t Have To Do\n\n- Follow a script\n- Ask the same questions every time\n- Produce a specific artifact\n- Reach a conclusion\n- Stay on topic if a tangent is valuable\n- Be brief (this is thinking time)\n\n---\n\n## Handling Different Entry Points\n\n**User brings a vague idea:**\n```\nUser: I''m thinking about adding real-time collaboration\n\nYou: Real-time collab is a big space. Let me think about this...\n\n      COLLABORATION SPECTRUM\n      ════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n      Awareness          Coordination         Sync\n          │                   │                 │\n          ▼                   ▼                 ▼\n      ┌────────┐         ┌────────┐        ┌────────┐\n      │Presence│         │Cursors │        │  CRDT  │\n      │  \"3    │         │ Multi  │        │Conflict│\n      │online\" │         │ select │        │  free  │\n      └────────┘         └────────┘        └────────┘\n          │                   │                 │\n       trivial            moderate           complex\n\n      Where''s your head at?\n```\n\n**User brings a specific problem:**\n```\nUser: The auth system is a mess\n\nYou: [reads codebase]\n\n     ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n     │              CURRENT AUTH FLOW              │\n     └─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                        │\n          ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐\n          ▼             ▼             ▼\n     ┌─────────┐  ┌─────────┐  ┌─────────┐\n     │ Google  │  │  GitHub │  │  Email  │\n     │  OAuth  │  │  OAuth  │  │  Magic  │\n     └────┬────┘  └────┬────┘  └────┬────┘\n          │             │             │\n          └─────────────┼─────────────┘\n                        ▼\n                  ┌───────────┐\n                  │  Session  │\n                  └─────┬─────┘\n                        │\n                        ▼\n                  ┌───────────┐\n                  │   Perms   │\n                  └───────────┘\n\n     I see three tangles. Which one''s burning?\n```\n\n**User is stuck mid-implementation:**\n```\nUser: /opsx:explore add-auth-system\n      The OAuth integration is more complex than expected\n\nYou: [reads change artifacts]\n\n     You''re on task 4: \"Implement OAuth flow\"\n\n     Let me trace what''s involved...\n\n     [draws diagram, explores options, suggests paths]\n\n     Want to update the design to reflect this?\n     Or add a spike task to investigate?\n```\n\n**User wants to compare options:**\n```\nUser: Should we use Postgres or SQLite?\n\nYou: Generic answer is boring. What''s the context?\n\nUser: A CLI tool that tracks local dev environments\n\nYou: That changes everything.\n\n     ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n     │         CLI TOOL DATA STORAGE                  │\n     └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n     Key constraints:\n     • No daemon running\n     • Must work offline\n     • Single user\n\n                  SQLite          Postgres\n     Deployment   embedded ✓      needs server ✗\n     Offline      yes ✓           no ✗\n     Single file  yes ✓           no ✗\n\n     SQLite. Not even close.\n\n     Unless... is there a sync component?\n```\n\n---\n\n## Ending Discovery\n\nThere''s no required ending. Discovery might:\n\n- **Flow into action**: \"Ready to start? /opsx:new or /opsx:ff\"\n- **Result in artifact updates**: \"Updated design.md with these decisions\"\n- **Just provide clarity**: User has what they need, moves on\n- **Continue later**: \"We can pick this up anytime\"\n\nWhen it feels like things are crystallizing, you might summarize:\n\n```\n## What We Figured Out\n\n**The problem**: [crystallized understanding]\n\n**The approach**: [if one emerged]\n\n**Open questions**: [if any remain]\n\n**Next steps** (if ready):\n- Create a change: /opsx:new <name>\n- Fast-forward to tasks: /opsx:ff <name>\n- Keep exploring: just keep talking\n```\n\nBut this summary is optional. Sometimes the thinking IS the value.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Don''t implement** - Never write code or implement features. Creating OpenSpec artifacts is fine, writing application code is not.\n- **Don''t fake understanding** - If something is unclear, dig deeper\n- **Don''t rush** - Discovery is thinking time, not task time\n- **Don''t force structure** - Let patterns emerge naturally\n- **Don''t auto-capture** - Offer to save insights, don''t just do it\n- **Do visualize** - A good diagram is worth many paragraphs\n- **Do explore the codebase** - Ground discussions in reality\n- **Do question assumptions** - Including the user''s and your own\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:45:30.370Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Knowledge Management Agents needing advanced Markdown and AsciiDoc file exploration capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级Markdown和AsciiDoc文件探索能力的知识管理代理。","ja":"高級なMarkdownおよびAsciiDocファイルの探索機能を必要とするナレッジマネジメントエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일 탐색 기능이 필요한 지식 관리 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Gestión de Conocimiento que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de exploración de archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de gestion des connaissances ayant besoin de capacités avancées d''exploration de fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc.","de":"Perfekt für Wissensmanagement-Agents, die erweiterte Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Datei-Explorationsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Gestão de Conhecimento que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de exploração de ficheiros Markdown e AsciiDoc.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Агентов управления знаниями, которым требуются расширенные возможности исследования файлов Markdown и AsciiDoc.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء إدارة المعرفة الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لاستكشاف ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to seamlessly open and preview Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2, facilitating efficient content investigation and OpenSpec artifact creation, including proposals, designs, and specs, while ensuring a strict explore mode to prevent unintended code implementation.","zh":"赋予代理无缝打开和预览Markdown和AsciiDoc文件的能力，使用Marked 2，促进高效的内容调查和OpenSpec工件创建，包括提案、设计和规格，同时确保严格的探索模式以防止意外的代码实现。","ja":"エージェントにMarkdownおよびAsciiDocファイルをMarked 2でシームレスに開き、プレビューする機能を付与し、効率的なコンテンツの調査およびOpenSpecアーティファクトの作成、提案、設計、仕様などを促進しながら、予期せぬコードの実装を防ぐために、厳格なエクスプローラーモードを保証します。","ko":"에이전트가 Marked 2에서 Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일을 무결점으로 열고 미리 볼 수 있는 기능을 부여하여 효율적인 내용 조사 및 OpenSpec 아티팩트 생성을 촉진하며, 제안, 설계, 사양 등을 포함하여 엄격한 탐색 모드를 보장하여 의도하지 않은 코드 구현을 방지합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a abrir y previsualizar archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc en Marked 2 de forma transparente, lo que facilita una investigación de contenido eficiente y la creación de artefactos OpenSpec, incluidas propuestas, diseños y especificaciones, al mismo tiempo que garantiza un modo de exploración estricto para prevenir la implementación involuntaria de código.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''ouvrir et d''apercevoir des fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc dans Marked 2 de manière transparente, ce qui facilite une enquête de contenu efficace et la création d''artefacts OpenSpec, y compris des propositions, des conceptions et des spécifications, tout en garantissant un mode d''exploration strict pour prévenir la mise en œuvre involontaire de code.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien in Marked 2 nahtlos zu öffnen und zu betrachten, was eine effiziente Inhaltsuntersuchung und die Erstellung von OpenSpec-Artefakten, einschließlich Vorschlägen, Entwürfen und Spezifikationen, erleichtert, während gleichzeitig ein strikter Explorationsmodus gewährleistet wird, um eine ungewollte Codeimplementierung zu verhindern.","pt":"Permite aos agentes abrir e visualizar perfeitamente ficheiros Markdown e AsciiDoc no Marked 2, facilitando a investigação eficiente de conteúdo e a criação de artefactos OpenSpec, incluindo propostas, designs e especificações, garantindo um modo de exploração estrito para evitar a implementação involuntária de código.","ru":"Позволяет агентам беспрепятственно открывать и просматривать файлы Markdown и AsciiDoc в Marked 2, способствуя эффективному исследованию содержимого и созданию артефактов OpenSpec, включая предложения, проекты и спецификации, обеспечивая при этом строгий режим исследования для предотвращения непреднамеренной реализации кода.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من فتح ومعاينة ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc بسلاسة في Marked 2، مما يسهل التحقيق الفعال في المحتوى وإنشاء قطع OpenSpec، بما في ذلك المقترحات والتصميمات والمواصفات، مع ضمان وضع استكشاف صارم لمنع تنفيذ التعليمات البرمجية غير المقصودة."},"useCases":{"en":["Exploring Markdown documentation","Investigating AsciiDoc files","Creating OpenSpec proposals and designs"],"zh":["探索Markdown文档","调查AsciiDoc文件","创建OpenSpec提案和设计"],"ja":["Markdownドキュメントの探索","AsciiDocファイルの調査","OpenSpec提案および設計の作成"],"ko":["Markdown 문서 탐색","AsciiDoc 파일 조사","OpenSpec 제안 및 설계 생성"],"es":["Explorar la documentación Markdown","Investigar archivos AsciiDoc","Crear propuestas y diseños OpenSpec"],"fr":["Explorer la documentation Markdown","Enquêter sur les fichiers AsciiDoc","Créer des propositions et des conceptions OpenSpec"],"de":["Markdown-Dokumentation erkunden","AsciiDoc-Dateien untersuchen","OpenSpec-Vorschläge und -Entwürfe erstellen"],"pt":["Exploração de documentação em Markdown","Investigação de ficheiros AsciiDoc","Criação de propostas e designs OpenSpec"],"ru":["Исследование документации Markdown","Исследование файлов AsciiDoc","Создание предложений и проектов OpenSpec"],"ar":["استكشاف وثائق Markdown","التحقيق في ملفات AsciiDoc","إنشاء مقترحات وتصميمات OpenSpec"]},"limitations":{"en":["Must not write code or implement features in explore mode","Requires VS Code extension and Marked 2 installation"],"zh":["探索模式下不能编写代码或实现功能","需要VS Code扩展和Marked 2安装"],"ja":["エクスプローラーモードではコードを書いたり機能を実装したりできない","VS Code拡張およびMarked 2のインストールが必要"],"ko":["탐색 모드에서 코드를 작성하거나 기능을 구현할 수 없음","VS Code 확장 및 Marked 2 설치가 필요"],"es":["No debe escribir código o implementar características en el modo de exploración","Requiere la instalación de la extensión de VS Code y Marked 2"],"fr":["Ne doit pas écrire de code ou mettre en œuvre des fonctionnalités en mode d''exploration","Nécessite l''installation de l''extension VS Code et Marked 2"],"de":["Darf im Explorationsmodus keinen Code schreiben oder Funktionen implementieren","Benötigt die Installation der VS Code-Erweiterung und Marked 2"],"pt":["Não deve escrever código ou implementar funcionalidades no modo de exploração","Requer a extensão do VS Code e a instalação do Marked 2"],"ru":["Не должен писать код или реализовывать функции в режиме исследования","Требует установки расширения VS Code и Marked 2"],"ar":["يجب عدم كتابة التعليمات البرمجية أو تنفيذ الميزات في وضع الاستكشاف","يتطلب تثبيت امتداد VS Code وتطبيق Marked 2"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
