нений","Позволить командной работе","Поддерживать контроль версий"],"ar":["حفظ التغييرات في المستودع","تأكيد التغييرات في الكود","إنشاء تاريخ للتغييرات","تمكين التعاون الفريق","الحفاظ على التحكم في الإصدارات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git Commit","代码仓库","版本控制","协作开发","Git命令行工具","代码提交"],"ja":["Gitコミット","コードリポジトリ","バージョン管理","コラボレーション開発","Gitコマンドラインツール","コードコミット"],"ko":["Git 커밋","코드 저장소","버전 관리","협作 개발","Git 명령줄 도구","코드 커밋"],"es":["commit git","confirmar cambios","repositorio git","desarrollo de software","colaboración en equipo","control de versiones"],"fr":["commit git","valider les modifications","référentiel git","développement de logiciels","collaboration d''équipe","contrôle de version"],"de":["commit git","änderungen bestätigen","git-repository","softwareentwicklung","teamzusammenarbeit","versionskontrolle"],"pt":["commit git","o que é commit","como funciona commit","git commit","desenvolvimento de software","controle de versões"],"ru":["коммит гит","что такое коммит","как работает коммит","гит коммит","разработка программного обеспечения","контроль версий"],"ar":["التزام جيت","ما هو الالتزام","كيف يعمل الالتزام","جيت التزام","تطوير البرمجيات","التحكم في الإصدارات"]}},"owner":"Scutoidzz","repo":"Wok","repoPath":"Scutoidzz/Wok","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.503Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"commit","description":"Git commit","bodyPreview":"Commit over git to the repo.","body":"Commit over git to the repo. "},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:46:25.628Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing version control integration via git","zh":"非常适合需要通过git集成版本控制的开发代理","ja":"開発エージェントがGitを介したバージョン管理統合を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"개발 에이전트가 Git를 통한 버전 관리 통합을 필요로 할 때 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan integración de control de versiones a través de git","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une intégration de contrôle de version via git","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine Versionskontrollintegration über Git benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de integração de controle de versão via git","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходима интеграция системы контроля версий через git","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يحتاج إلى دمج إدارة الإصدار عبر جيت"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage code revisions over git, utilizing protocols like HTTPS or SSH, and handling file formats such as .gitignore, enabling seamless collaboration and version tracking directly to the repository","zh":"赋予代理管理代码修订的能力，利用HTTPS或SSH等协议，并处理诸如.gitignore的文件格式，实现与仓库的无缝协作和版本跟踪","ja":"HTTPSまたはSSHなどのプロトコルを利用してコードのリビジョンを管理し、.gitignoreなどのファイル形式を処理することで、エージェントに力を与え、リポジトリへのシームレスなコラボレーションとバージョントラッキングを可能にします","ko":"HTTPS 또는 SSH 등의 프로토콜을 사용하여 코드 수정을 관리하고, .gitignore 등의 파일 형식을 처리함으로써 에이전트에게 권한을 부여하여 저장소로의 무결점 협업 및 버전 추적이 가능하도록 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar revisiones de código a través de git, utilizando protocolos como HTTPS o SSH, y manejando formatos de archivo como .gitignore, lo que permite una colaboración y seguimiento de versiones sin problemas directamente en el repositorio","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les révisions de code via git, en utilisant des protocoles tels que HTTPS ou SSH, et en gérant des formats de fichiers tels que .gitignore, permettant ainsi une collaboration et un suivi de version sans problème directement sur le référentiel","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Code-Revisionen über Git zu verwalten, indem Protokolle wie HTTPS oder SSH verwendet werden und Dateiformate wie .gitignore gehandhabt werden, was eine nahtlose Zusammenarbeit und Versionsverfolgung direkt im Repository ermöglicht","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar revisões de código via git, utilizando protocolos como HTTPS ou SSH, e lidando com formatos de arquivo como .gitignore, permitindo colaboração e rastreamento de versão sem interrupção diretamente no repositório","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять версиями кода через git, используя протоколы như HTTPS или SSH, и обрабатывая форматы файлов, такие как .gitignore, обеспечивая бесперебойное сотрудничество и отслеживание версий непосредственно в репозитории","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من إدارة المراجعات اللغوية عبر جيت، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل HTTPS أو SSH، وتحويل تنسيقات الملفات مثل .gitignore، مما يتيح التعاون والتتبع الإصدار دون انقطاع مباشرة إلى المستودع"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code commits","Updating repository versions","Tracking changes over git"],"zh":["自动化代码提交","更新仓库版本","在Git上跟踪更改"],"ja":["コードのコミットの自動化","リポジトリのバージョンの更新","Git上での変更の追跡"],"ko":["코드 커밋 자동화","저장소 버전 업데이트","Git에서 변경 사항 추적"],"es":["Automatizar confirmaciones de código","Actualizar versiones del repositorio","Seguimiento de cambios sobre git"],"fr":["Automatiser les validations de code","Mettre à jour les versions du référentiel","Suivi des modifications sur git"],"de":["Automatisieren von Code-Commits","Aktualisieren von Repository-Versionen","Verfolgen von Änderungen über Git"],"pt":["Automatizar compromissos de código","Atualizar versões do repositório","Rastrear alterações sobre git"],"ru":["Автоматизировать фиксацию кода","Обновлять версии репозитория","Отслеживать изменения через git"],"ar":["تأتمتة الالتزامات اللغوية","تحديث إصدارات المستودع","تتبع التغييرات عبر جيت"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git installation","Needs repository access credentials","Dependent on network connectivity for remote repositories"],"zh":["需要Git安装","需要仓库访问凭证","依赖于网络连接以访问远程仓库"],"ja":["Gitのインストールが必要","リポジトリへのアクセス資格情報が必要","リモートリポジトリにアクセスするためにネットワーク接続に依存"],"ko":["Git 설치가 필요함","저장소 접근 자격 증명이 필요함","원격 저장소에 접근하기 위해 네트워크 연결에 의존"],"es":["Requiere instalación de git","Necesita credenciales de acceso al repositorio","Dependiente de la conectividad de red para repositorios remotos"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de git","A besoin de credentials d''accès au référentiel","Dépend de la connectivité réseau pour les référentiels distants"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Installation","Benötigt Repository-Zugriffsberechtigungen","Abhängig von der Netzwerkverbindung für Remote-Repositorys"],"pt":["Requer instalação do git","Necessita de credenciais de acesso ao repositório","Dependente da conectividade de rede para repositórios remotos"],"ru":["Требует установки git","Требует учетных данных доступа к репозиторию","Зависит от сетевого подключения для удаленных репозиториев"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت جيت","يحتاج إلى بيانات اعتماد الوصول إلى المستودع","يعتمد على الاتصال الشبكي للمستودعات عن بُعد"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'gAmUssA', 'vscode-open-in-marked2', 'gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.503Z', '2026-02-18T11:45:34.923Z', NULL, '{"id":"gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"OpenSpec-onboard是一个VS Code扩展，帮助您打开Markdown和AsciiDoc文件，快速开始OpenSpec工作流程","ja":"OpenSpec-onboardは、VS Code拡張機能で、MarkdownとAsciiDocファイルを開き、OpenSpecワークフローを開始するのに役立ちます","ko":"OpenSpec-onboard는 VS Code 확장 기능으로, Markdown와 AsciiDoc 파일을 열고 OpenSpec 작업 흐름을 시작하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"Guía para implementar OpenSpec en tu proyecto de desarrollo","fr":"Guide pour mettre en œuvre OpenSpec dans votre projet de développement","de":"Anleitung zur Implementierung von OpenSpec in Ihrem Entwicklungsprojekt","pt":"Guia de configuração da extensão OpenSpec no VS Code para abrir arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc","ru":"Руководство по настройке расширения OpenSpec в VS Code для открытия файлов Markdown и AsciiDoc","ar":"دليل إعداد ملحق OpenSpec في كودVS لفتح ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc","en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门：VS Code扩展快速上手","ja":"OpenSpec入門：VS Code拡張機能の使い方","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기: VS Code 확장 기능 사용법","es":"Extensión de VS Code para OpenSpec: Onboard","fr":"Extension VS Code pour OpenSpec : Onboard","de":"VS Code-Erweiterung für OpenSpec: Onboard","pt":"Onboard com OpenSpec: Extensão do VS Code","ru":"Настройка OpenSpec: Расширение VS Code","ar":"التحكم فيOpenSpec: ملحق كودVS","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"OpenSpec-onboard是一个VS Code扩展，帮助您打开Markdown和AsciiDoc文件，快速开始OpenSpec工作流程","ja":"OpenSpec-onboardは、VS Code拡張機能で、MarkdownとAsciiDocファイルを開き、OpenSpecワークフローを開始するのに役立ちます","ko":"OpenSpec-onboard는 VS Code 확장 기능으로, Markdown와 AsciiDoc 파일을 열고 OpenSpec 작업 흐름을 시작하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"Guía para implementar OpenSpec en tu proyecto de desarrollo","fr":"Guide pour mettre en œuvre OpenSpec dans votre projet de développement","de":"Anleitung zur Implementierung von OpenSpec in Ihrem Entwicklungsprojekt","pt":"Guia de configuração da extensão OpenSpec no VS Code para abrir arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc","ru":"Руководство по настройке расширения OpenSpec в VS Code для открытия файлов Markdown и AsciiDoc","ar":"دليل إعداد ملحق OpenSpec في كودVS لفتح ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc","en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"definition":{"en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"features":{"zh":["打开Markdown文件","打开AsciiDoc文件","支持OpenSpec工作流程","VS Code扩展","快速上手","提高开发效率"],"ja":["Markdownファイルを開く","AsciiDocファイルを開く","OpenSpecワークフローをサポート","VS Code拡張機能","簡単に始める","開発効率を向上させる"],"ko":["Markdown 파일 열기","AsciiDoc 파일 열기","OpenSpec 작업 흐름 지원","VS Code 확장 기능","쉽게 시작하기","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Integración con VS Code","Compatibilidad con Markdown y AsciiDoc","Flujo de trabajo de documentación","Inicialización de proyectos","Verificación de estado de proyecto"],"fr":["Intégration avec VS Code","Compatibilité avec Markdown et AsciiDoc","Flux de travail de documentation","Initialisation de projets","Vérification de l''état du projet"],"de":["Integration mit VS Code","Kompatibilität mit Markdown und AsciiDoc","Dokumentations-Arbeitsablauf","Projektinitialisierung","Projektstatusüberprüfung"],"pt":["Abre arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc no Marked 2","Integração com o VS Code","Guia de configuração passo a passo","Suporte a workflows OpenSpec"],"ru":["Открывает файлы Markdown и AsciiDoc в Marked 2","Интеграция с VS Code","Пошаговое руководство по настройке","Поддержка рабочих процессов OpenSpec"],"ar":["يفتح ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc في Marked 2","التكامل مع كودVS","دليل إعداد خطوة بخطوة","دعم سير عمل OpenSpec"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","VS Code扩展","Markdown","AsciiDoc","工作流程","开发效率","快速上手","代码编辑"],"ja":["OpenSpec","VS Code拡張機能","Markdown","AsciiDoc","ワークフロー","開発効率","簡単に始める","コードエディター"],"ko":["OpenSpec","VS Code 확장 기능","Markdown","AsciiDoc","작업 흐름","개발 효율성","쉽게 시작하기","코드 편집기"],"es":["OpenSpec","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","documentación de proyectos","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["OpenSpec","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","documentation de projets","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["OpenSpec","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Projektdokumentation","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["OpenSpec","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","Extensão","Configuração"],"ru":["OpenSpec","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","Расширение","Настройка"],"ar":["OpenSpec","كودVS","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","ملحق","إعداد"]}},"owner":"gAmUssA","repo":"vscode-open-in-marked2","repoPath":"gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.503Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:45:34.923Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Developer Agents needing Markdown and AsciiDoc file handling in VS Code with Marked 2 integration.","zh":"非常适合需要在VS Code中处理Markdown和AsciiDoc文件并与Marked 2集成的开发者智能体。","ja":"Marked 2との連携により、VS CodeでMarkdownおよびAsciiDocファイルの処理を必要とする開発者エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Marked 2 통합 기능이 있는 VS Code에서 Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일 처리가 필요한 개발자 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollador que necesitan manejo de archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc en VS Code con integración de Marked 2.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant la gestion de fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc dans VS Code avec intégration de Marked 2.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsagenten, die Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien in VS Code mit Marked 2-Integration bearbeiten müssen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de manipulação de arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc no VS Code com integração do Marked 2.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-разработчиков, которым требуется обработка файлов Markdown и AsciiDoc в VS Code с интеграцией Marked 2.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء المطورين الذين يحتاجون إلى التعامل مع ملفات Markdown وAsciiDoc في VS Code مع تكامل Marked 2."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to seamlessly open and preview Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2, streamlining documentation workflows with openspec init and status checks via JSON output.","zh":"使智能体能够在Marked 2中无缝打开和预览Markdown与AsciiDoc文件，通过JSON输出的openspec初始化和状态检查简化文档工作流程。","ja":"エージェントがMarked 2でMarkdownおよびAsciiDocファイルをシームレスに開いてプレビューできるようにし、JSON出力によるopenspec初期化とステータスチェックを通じてドキュメントワークフローを効率化します。","ko":"에이전트가 Marked 2에서 Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일을 원활하게 열고 미리 볼 수 있도록 하여, JSON 출력을 통한 openspec 초기화 및 상태 확인으로 문서 워크플로를 간소화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a abrir y previsualizar archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc en Marked 2 de forma fluida, simplificando los flujos de trabajo de documentación con openspec init y comprobaciones de estado a través de salida JSON.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''ouvrir et d''apercevoir en toute transparence les fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc dans Marked 2, rationalisant les flux de travail de documentation avec openspec init et vérifications d''état via sortie JSON.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien in Marked 2 nahtlos zu öffnen und vorzuzeigen, wodurch die Dokumentationsworkflows mit openspec init und Statusprüfungen über JSON-Ausgabe rationalisiert werden.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a abrir e visualizar perfeitamente arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc no Marked 2, otimizando fluxos de trabalho de documentação com a inicialização do openspec e verificações de status via saída JSON.","ru":"Позволяет агентам беспрепятственно открывать и просматривать файлы Markdown и AsciiDoc в Marked 2, упрощая рабочие процессы документации с инициализацией openspec и проверкой статуса через вывод JSON.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من فتح ومعاينة ملفات Markdown وAsciiDoc بسلاسة في Marked 2، مما يبسط سير عمل التوثيق مع تهيئة openspec وفحوصات الحالة عبر إخراج JSON."},"useCases":{"en":["Onboarding new users through guided OpenSpec workflow cycles","Debugging OpenSpec initialization issues with JSON status checks","Generating documentation previews in Marked 2"],"zh":["通过引导式OpenSpec工作流周期为新用户提供入职指导","使用JSON状态检查调试OpenSpec初始化问题","在Marked 2中