n.go           # Entry point\n├── internal/\n│   ├── handler/              # HTTP handlers (Controllers)\n│   ├──","body":"# Backend Go Conventions\n\nThis skill provides specific conventions for Go backend development.\n\n## When to Use\n- Use this skill when working on Go projects\n- Use this skill when creating new handlers, services, or repositories\n- This skill builds upon `project-standards` skill\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Project Layout (Standard Go Layout)\n\n```\nproject/\n├── cmd/\n│   └── api/\n│       └── main.go           # Entry point\n├── internal/\n│   ├── handler/              # HTTP handlers (Controllers)\n│   ├── service/              # Business logic\n│   ├── repository/           # Database access\n│   ├── model/                # Domain models\n│   └── dto/                  # Request/Response objects\n├── pkg/                      # Shared libraries\n├── api/                      # OpenAPI/Swagger specs\n├── config/                   # Configuration\n└── go.mod\n```\n\n### 2. Architecture (Clean/Hexagonal)\n\n- **Handler (Controller):** Receives requests, validates, calls Service.\n- **Service (Usecase):** Contains Business Logic.\n- **Repository:** Interacts with the Database.\n\n**Important:** Interfaces should be defined where they are USED (Consumer), not where they are provided (Producer).\n\n```go\n// In service package (consumer defines interface)\ntype UserRepository interface {\n    FindByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*model.User, error)\n    Create(ctx context.Context, user *model.User) error\n}\n\ntype UserService struct {\n    repo UserRepository\n}\n\nfunc NewUserService(repo UserRepository) *UserService {\n    return &UserService{repo: repo}\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Error Handling\n\n#### No Panic\nOnly panic during app setup failure (e.g., db disconnect).\n\n```go\n// Bad - panicking in business logic\nfunc GetUser(id string) User {\n    user, err := repo.Find(id)\n    if err != nil {\n        panic(err) // Never do this!\n    }\n    return user\n}\n\n// Good - return errors\nfunc GetUser(id string) (User, error) {\n    user, err := repo.Find(id)\n    if err != nil {\n        return User{}, fmt.Errorf(\"get user %s: %w\", id, err)\n    }\n    return user, nil\n}\n```\n\n#### Wrap Errors\nUse `fmt.Errorf` with `%w` to preserve context.\n\n```go\nif err != nil {\n    return fmt.Errorf(\"create user failed: %w\", err)\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Naming Convention\n\n- **Package:** Short, lowercase, no underscores (e.g., `user`, `auth`).\n- **Interface:** Ends with `er` (e.g., `Reader`, `Writer`, `UserRepository`).\n- **Variable:** camelCase, acronyms all uppercase (`userID`, `httpClient`).\n- **Exported:** PascalCase for exported, camelCase for unexported.\n\n```go\n// Good\npackage user\n\ntype Repository interface {\n    FindByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*User, error)\n}\n\nvar defaultTimeout = 30 * time.Second // unexported\nvar DefaultClient = &http.Client{}     // exported\n```\n\n### 5. Context Handling\n\nAlways pass context as the first parameter.\n\n```go\nfunc (s *UserService) GetUser(ctx context.Context, id string) (*User, error) {\n    // Check context cancellation\n    select {\n    case <-ctx.Done():\n        return nil, ctx.Err()\n    default:\n    }\n    \n    return s.repo.FindByID(ctx, id)\n}\n```\n\n### 6. HTTP Handler Example\n\n```go\nfunc (h *UserHandler) GetUser(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n    id := chi.URLParam(r, \"id\")\n    \n    user, err := h.service.GetUser(r.Context(), id)\n    if err != nil {\n        if errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) {\n            h.respondError(w, http.StatusNotFound, \"user not found\")\n            return\n        }\n        h.respondError(w, http.StatusInternalServerError, \"internal error\")\n        return\n    }\n    \n    h.respondJSON(w, http.StatusOK, Response{\n        Success: true,\n        Data:    user,\n    })\n}\n```\n\n### 7. Testing\n\nUse table-driven tests.\n\n```go\nfunc TestUserService_GetUser(t *testing.T) {\n    tests := []struct {\n        name    string\n        id      string\n        want    *User\n        wantErr bool\n    }{\n        {\n            name: \"valid user\",\n            id:   \"123\",\n            want: &User{ID: \"123\", Email: \"test@example.com\"},\n        },\n        {\n            name:    \"not found\",\n            id:      \"999\",\n            wantErr: true,\n        },\n    }\n\n    for _, tt := range tests {\n        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            // Test implementation\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 8. Dependencies\n\n- **Framework:** Gin or Echo\n- **ORM:** GORM or SQLC\n- **Config:** Viper\n- **Logger:** Zap or Zerolog\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:47:25.604Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Go-focused Agents needing standardized backend development conventions.","zh":"适合需要标准化后端开发约定的 Go 专注代理。","ja":"Go に焦点を当てたエージェントが標準化されたバックエンド開発規約を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"Go에 중점을 둔 에이전트가 표준화된 백엔드 개발 규약을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes enfocados en Go que necesitan convenciones de desarrollo de backend estandarizadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents axés sur Go nécessitant des conventions de développement de backend standardisées.","de":"Perfekt für auf Go fokussierte Agenten, die standardisierte Backend-EntwicklungsKonventionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes focados em Go que necessitam de convenções de desenvolvimento de backend padronizadas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов, ориентированных на Go, которым необходимы стандартизированные соглашения по разработке бэкенда.","ar":"مثالي لعميل يركز على جوجل ويحتاج إلى اتفاقيات تطوير الخلفية الموحدة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to structure Go projects with standard layouts, utilizing HTTP handlers and services, while adhering to project standards like internal/handler and internal/services directories, enhancing code readability and maintainability with Go conventions.","zh":"赋予代理以标准布局结构 Go 项目的能力，利用 HTTP 处理程序和服务，同时遵守项目标准，如 internal/handler 和 internal/services 目录，提高代码的可读性和可维护性，符合 Go 规范。","ja":"HTTP ハンドラーとサービスを利用して、Go プロジェクトを標準的なレイアウトで構造化するエージェントの能力を提供し、内部/ハンドラーと内部/サービス ディレクトリなどのプロジェクト標準に従い、Go の規約に従ってコードの可読性とメンテナンス性を高める。","ko":"HTTP 핸들러와 서비스를 활용하여 Go 프로젝트를 표준적인 레이아웃으로 구조화하는 에이전트의 능력을 제공하며, 내부/핸들러 및 내부/서비스 디렉토리 등의 프로젝트 표준을 준수하여 Go 규약에 따라 코드의 가독성과 유지보수성을 향상합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes estructurar proyectos de Go con diseños de layout estándar, utilizando controladores HTTP y servicios, mientras se adhiere a los estándares del proyecto como directorios internal/handler y internal/services, mejorando la legibilidad y mantenibilidad del código con convenciones de Go.","fr":"Permet aux agents de structurer des projets Go avec des dispositions de layout standard, en utilisant des gestionnaires HTTP et des services, tout en respectant les normes de projet comme les répertoires internal/handler et internal/services, améliorant la lisibilité et la maintenabilité du code avec les conventions Go.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Go-Projekte mit standardisierten Layouts zu strukturieren, indem HTTP-Handler und Dienste verwendet werden, während die Einhaltung von Projektnormen wie internal/Handler- und internal/Dienste-Verzeichnissen gewährleistet ist, wodurch die Lesbarkeit und Wartbarkeit des Codes mit Go-Konventionen verbessert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a estruturar projetos Go com layouts padrão, utilizando manipuladores HTTP e serviços, enquanto adere a padrões de projeto como diretórios internal/handler e internal/services, melhorando a legibilidade e manutenção do código com convenções Go.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью структурировать проекты Go с использованием стандартных макетов, использующих обработчики HTTP и сервисы, а также соблюдая стандарты проекта, такие как директории internal/handler и internal/services, повышая читаемость и поддерживаемость кода с помощью соглашений Go.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على هيكلة مشاريع جوجل باستخدام تخطيطات موحدة ، باستخدام معالجات HTTP والخدمات ، مع الالتزام بمعايير المشروع مثل الدلائل internal/handler و internal/services ، وتحسين قابلية قراءة ومaintainability الكود مع الاتفاقيات جوجل."},"useCases":{"en":["Standardizing Go project layouts","Creating new handlers and services","Ensuring adherence to project standards"],"zh":["标准化 Go 项目布局","创建新的处理程序和服务","确保遵守项目标准"],"ja":["Go プロジェクト レイアウトの標準化","新しいハンドラーとサービスの作成","プロジェクト標準の遵守の確保"],"ko":["Go 프로젝트 레이아웃 표준화","새로운 핸들러 및 서비스 생성","프로젝트 표준 준수 보장"],"es":["Estandarizar diseños de proyecto de Go","Crear nuevos controladores y servicios","Asegurar el cumplimiento de los estándares del proyecto"],"fr":["Standardiser les dispositions de projet Go","Créer de nouveaux gestionnaires et services","Assurer le respect des normes de projet"],"de":["Go-Projektlayouts standardisieren","Neue Handler und Dienste erstellen","Die Einhaltung von Projektnormen sicherstellen"],"pt":["Padronização de layouts de projetos Go","Criação de novos manipuladores e serviços","Garantia de aderência a padrões de projeto"],"ru":["Стандартизация макетов проектов Go","Создание новых обработчиков и сервисов","Обеспечение соблюдения стандартов проекта"],"ar":["توحيد تخطيطات مشاريع جوجل","إنشاء معالجات وخدمات جديدة","ضمان الالتزام بمعايير المشروع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Specific to Go backend development","Requires understanding of Go project structure and conventions"],"zh":["仅限于 Go 后端开发","需要了解 Go 项目结构和约定"],"ja":["Go バックエンド開発に限定される","Go プロジェクト構造と規約の理解が必要"],"ko":["Go 백엔드 개발에만 국한됨","Go 프로젝트 구조 및 규약에 대한 이해가 필요"],"es":["Específico para el desarrollo de backend de Go","Requiere comprensión de la estructura y convenciones del proyecto de Go"],"fr":["Spécifique au développement de backend Go","Nécessite une compréhension de la structure et des conventions du projet Go"],"de":["Spezifisch für die Go-Backend-Entwicklung","Benötigt das Verständnis der Go-Projektstruktur und -Konventionen"],"pt":["Específico para desenvolvimento de backend Go","Exige compreensão da estrutura e convenções do projeto Go"],"ru":["Специфичен для разработки бэкенда на Go","Требует понимания структуры и соглашений проекта Go"],"ar":["محدد لتطوير الخلفية جوجل","يتطلب فهم هيكل واتفاقيات مشروع جوجل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
