ng des Codes","Dokumentation der Datenflüsse","Identifizierung von Integrationspunkten","Analyse der Eingangspunkte des Systems"],"pt":["Mapeamento da estrutura do código","Avaliação da qualidade do código","Documentação de dependências e fluxos de dados","Identificação de pontos de integração e entrada","Otimização da arquitetura para melhorar a manutenção e a escalabilidade"],"ru":["Картирование кодовой базы","Оценка качества кода","Документирование зависимостей и потоков данных","Определение точек интеграции и входа","Оптимизация архитектуры для улучшения обслуживания и масштабируемости"],"ar":["خريطة هيكل الكود","تقييم جودة الكود","توثيق الاعتماديات و تدفقات البيانات","تحديد نقاط التكامل و الدخول","تحسين هيكل الكود لتحسين الصيانة و القابلية للتوسع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码架构审查","代码库架构","结构映射","质量评估","模块和包管理","依赖关系分析"],"ja":["アーキテクチャレビュー","コードベースアーキテクチャ","構造マッピング","品質評価","モジュールとパッケージ管理","依存関係分析"],"ko":["코드 아키텍처 리뷰","코드베이스 아키텍처","구조 매핑","품질 평가","모듈과 패키지 관리","의존 관계 분석"],"es":["revisión de arquitectura","desarrollo de software","mejora del código","arquitectura de sistemas","diseño de software","evaluación de la calidad del código"],"fr":["révision d''architecture","développement de logiciels","amélioration du code","architecture de systèmes","conception de logiciels","évaluation de la qualité du code"],"de":["Architektur-Review","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Optimierung","System-Architektur","Software-Design","Qualitätsbewertung des Codes"],"pt":["revisão de arquitetura","análise de código","otimização de software","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software","qualidade de código","manutenção de software"],"ru":["обзор архитектуры","анализ кода","оптимизация программного обеспечения","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения","качество кода","обслуживание программного обеспечения"],"ar":["استعراض الهيكل","تحليل الكود","تحسين البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات","جودة الكود","صيانة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"FinesseAC","repo":"windows-ai-dev-station","repoPath":"FinesseAC/windows-ai-dev-station","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Architecture Review","description":"Comprehensive codebase architecture analysis with quality assessment and recommendations","bodyPreview":"# Architecture Review Protocol\n\nA systematic approach to analyzing and improving codebase architecture.\n\n## Phase 1: Structure Mapping\n\nMap the overall architecture:\n\n- **Modules/Packages**: List all major components\n- **Dependencies**: Map inter-module dependencies\n- **Data Flows**: Document how data moves through the system\n- **Integration Points**: External APIs, databases, third-party services\n- **Entry Points**: Main endpoints, CLI commands, event handlers\n\n## Phase 2: Quality Assessment\n\nR","body":"# Architecture Review Protocol\n\nA systematic approach to analyzing and improving codebase architecture.\n\n## Phase 1: Structure Mapping\n\nMap the overall architecture:\n\n- **Modules/Packages**: List all major components\n- **Dependencies**: Map inter-module dependencies\n- **Data Flows**: Document how data moves through the system\n- **Integration Points**: External APIs, databases, third-party services\n- **Entry Points**: Main endpoints, CLI commands, event handlers\n\n## Phase 2: Quality Assessment\n\nRate each area on a scale of 1-5:\n\n### Code Quality Metrics\n\n- [ ] **Separation of Concerns** (1-5): Are responsibilities well-divided?\n- [ ] **Code Reusability** (1-5): Is code DRY without being overly abstract?\n- [ ] **Error Handling** (1-5): Are errors handled consistently and thoroughly?\n- [ ] **Type Safety** (1-5): Are types used effectively?\n- [ ] **Naming Conventions** (1-5): Are names clear and consistent?\n\n### Architecture Metrics\n\n- [ ] **Modularity** (1-5): Can components be changed independently?\n- [ ] **Scalability** (1-5): Can the system grow without major rewrites?\n- [ ] **Testability** (1-5): Is the code easy to test?\n- [ ] **Maintainability** (1-5): Can new developers understand it?\n- [ ] **Security Posture** (1-5): Are security best practices followed?\n\n## Phase 3: Pattern Analysis\n\nIdentify patterns in use:\n\n### Design Patterns Detected\n\n- List each pattern found (Repository, Factory, Observer, etc.)\n- Note where they''re applied correctly\n- Note where they could be better utilized\n\n### Anti-Patterns Detected\n\n- God objects/classes\n- Tight coupling\n- Circular dependencies\n- Magic numbers/strings\n- Deep nesting\n- Code duplication\n\n### Inconsistencies\n\n- Naming convention violations\n- Style inconsistencies\n- Error handling variations\n- Logging inconsistencies\n\n## Phase 4: Technical Debt Inventory\n\nDocument technical debt:\n\n### Critical (Fix Immediately)\n\n- Security vulnerabilities\n- Data integrity risks\n- Performance blockers\n\n### High Priority (Fix Soon)\n\n- Scalability limitations\n- Major code duplication\n- Missing error handling\n\n### Medium Priority (Plan to Fix)\n\n- Inconsistent patterns\n- Missing tests\n- Documentation gaps\n\n### Low Priority (Nice to Have)\n\n- Minor style issues\n- Optional optimizations\n- Nice-to-have refactors\n\n## Phase 5: Recommendations\n\nProvide actionable recommendations:\n\n### Immediate Actions\n\n1. **[Action]** - Reason - Estimated effort\n2. **[Action]** - Reason - Estimated effort\n3. **[Action]** - Reason - Estimated effort\n\n### Short-Term Improvements (1-2 weeks)\n\n1. **[Improvement]** - Impact - Effort\n2. **[Improvement]** - Impact - Effort\n\n### Long-Term Initiatives (1+ months)\n\n1. **[Initiative]** - Strategic value - Resources needed\n2. **[Initiative]** - Strategic value - Resources needed\n\n## Deliverable\n\nGenerate `ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md` containing:\n\n1. Executive Summary\n2. Architecture Diagram (text-based)\n3. Quality Scores\n4. Patterns Analysis\n5. Technical Debt Inventory\n6. Prioritized Recommendations\n7. Risk Assessment\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:48:28.151Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing systematic architecture analysis and improvement capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要系统化架构分析和改进能力的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが体系的なアーキテクチャ分析および改善機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"시스템적인 아키텍처 분석 및 개선 능력이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan capacidades de análisis y mejora de la arquitectura sistemática.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de revue de code nécessitant une analyse et une amélioration architecturale systématiques.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die systematische Architekturanalyse- und Verbesserungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de análise e capacidades de melhoria de arquitetura sistemática.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, требующих системного анализа архитектуры и возможностей улучшения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى تحليل هيكلي منهجي وقدرات تحسين."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform thorough architecture reviews using structured protocols, including module mapping, dependency analysis, and data flow documentation, leveraging AutoHotkey hotkeys and automation scripts.","zh":"使代理能够使用结构化协议进行彻底的架构审查，包括模块映射、依赖分析和数据流文档，利用AutoHotkey热键和自动化脚本。","ja":"エージェントがモジュールマッピング、依存関係分析、およびデータフローの文書化を含む構造化されたプロトコルを使用して、包括的なアーキテクチャレビューを実行できるようにします。AutoHotkeyホットキーおよび自動化スクリプトを利用。","ko":"에이전트가 구조화된 프로토콜을 사용하여 철저한 아키텍처 리뷰를 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 모듈 매핑, 의존성 분석 및 데이터 흐름 문서화를 포함하여 AutoHotkey 핫키 및 자동화 스크립트를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar revisiones exhaustivas de la arquitectura utilizando protocolos estructurados, incluyendo mapeo de módulos, análisis de dependencias y documentación de flujos de datos, aprovechando hotkeys y scripts de automatización de AutoHotkey.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des revues d''architecture approfondies en utilisant des protocoles structurés, notamment la mise en correspondance de modules, l''analyse des dépendances et la documentation des flux de données, en exploitant les raccourcis et les scripts d''automatisation d''AutoHotkey.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, gründliche Architekturüberprüfungen unter Verwendung von strukturierten Protokollen durchzuführen, einschließlich Modulzuordnung, Abhängigkeitsanalyse und Datenflussdokumentation, unter Nutzung von AutoHotkey-Hotkeys und Automatisierungsskripten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar revisões arquiteturais abrangentes usando protocolos estruturados, incluindo mapeamento de módulos, análise de dependências e documentação de fluxo de dados, aproveitando atalhos e scripts de automação do AutoHotkey.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные обзоры архитектуры с использованием структурированных протоколов, включая картографирование модулей, анализ зависимостей и документирование потоков данных, используя горячие клавиши и скрипты автоматизации AutoHotkey.","ar":"يمنح العميل قدرة على إجراء مراجعات شاملة للهيكل باستخدام بروتوكولات منظمة، بما في ذلك تخطيط الوحدات و تحليل التبعيات و توثيق تدفق البيانات، واستخدام اختصارات وبرامج مساعدة آوتوهوتكى."},"useCases":{"en":["Mapping complex system architectures","Analyzing inter-module dependencies","Documenting data flows and integration points"],"zh":["复杂系统架构映射","模块间依赖分析","数据流及集成点文档"],"ja":["複雑なシステムアーキテクチャのマッピング","モジュール間の依存関係分析","データフローおよび統合ポイントの文書化"],"ko":["복잡한 시스템 아키텍처 매핑","모듈 간 의존성 분석","데이터 흐름 및 통합 지점 문서화"],"es":["Mapeo de arquitecturas de sistemas complejos","Análisis de dependencias entre módulos","Documentación de flujos de datos y puntos de integración"],"fr":["Mise en correspondance d''architectures de systèmes complexes","Analyse des dépendances entre modules","Documentation des flux de données et des points d''intégration"],"de":["Zuordnung komplexer Systemarchitekturen","Analyse von Abhängigkeiten zwischen Modulen","Dokumentation von Datenflüssen und Integrationspunkten"],"pt":["Mapeamento de arquiteturas de sistemas complexas","Análise de dependências entre módulos","Documentação de fluxos de dados e pontos de integração"],"ru":["Картографирование сложных системных архитектур","Анализ взаимозависимостей между модулями","Документирование потоков данных и точек интеграции"],"ar":["تحديد Sites هيكل نظام معقد","تحليل التبعيات بين الوحدات","توثيق تدفق البيانات و نقاط التكامل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Windows 11 AI-Native Dev Station setup","Limited to AutoHotkey and MCP configurations"],"zh":["需要Windows 11 AI原生开发站设置","仅限AutoHotkey及MCP配置"],"ja":["Windows 11 AIネイティブDev Stationの設定が必要","AutoHotkeyおよびMCPの構成のみ"],"ko":["Windows 11 AI 네이티브 개발 스테이션 설정이 필요함","AutoHotkey 및 MCP 구성만 가능"],"es":["Requiere una configuración de estación de desarrollo AI-Native de Windows 11","Limitado a configuraciones de AutoHotkey y MCP"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de station de développement AI-Native de Windows 11","Limité aux configurations AutoHotkey et MCP"],"de":["Benötigt eine Windows 11 AI-Native-Entwicklungsstation-Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf AutoHotkey- und MCP-Konfigurationen"],"pt":["Requer configuração do Windows 11 AI-Native Dev Station","Limitado às configurações do AutoHotkey e MCP"],"ru":["Требует настройки станции разработки AI-Native Dev для Windows 11","Ограничен настройками AutoHotkey и MCP"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد محطة تطوير الأجهزة الأصلية AI-الاصطناعية لنظام التشغيل Windows 11","محدود بإعدادات أوتوهوتكى و MCP"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2/openspec-verify-change', 'community', 'gAmUssA', 'vscode-open-in-marked2', 'gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2', 'openspec-verify-change', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z', '2026-02-18T11:48:52.214Z', NULL, '{"id":"gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2/openspec-verify-change","name":"openspec-verify-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-verify-change 是一个 VS Code 扩展，用于验证实现是否匹配更改规范","ja":"openspec-verify-change は、実装が変更仕様と一致することを確認する VS Code 拡張機能です","ko":"openspec-verify-change는 구현이 변경 사양과 일치하는지 확인하는 VS Code 확장입니다","es":"La extensión openspec-verify-change de VS Code verifica que la implementación coincida con los artefactos de cambio","fr":"L''extension openspec-verify-change de VS Code vérifie que la mise en œuvre correspond aux artefacts de modification","de":"Die VS Code-Erweiterung openspec-verify-change überprüft, ob die Implementierung mit den Änderungsartefakten übereinstimmt","en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-verify-change VS Code 扩展","ja":"openspec-verify-change VS Code 拡張機能","ko":"openspec-verify-change VS Code 확장","es":"Verificación de cambios con openspec-verify-change","fr":"Vérification de modifications avec openspec-verify-change","de":"Änderungsüberprüfung mit openspec-verify-change","en":"openspec-verify-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-verify-change 是一个 VS Code 扩展，用于验证实现是否匹配更改规范","ja":"openspec-verify-change は、実装が変更仕様と一致することを確認する VS Code 拡張機能です","ko":"openspec-verify-change는 구현이 변경 사양과 일치하는지 확인하는 VS Code 확장입니다","es":"La extensión openspec-verify-change de VS Code verifica que la implementación coincida con los artefactos de cambio","fr":"L''extension openspec-verify-change de VS Code vérifie que la mise en œuvre correspond aux artefacts de modification","de":"Die VS Code-Erweiterung openspec-verify-change überprüft, ob die Implementierung mit den Änderungsartefakten übereinstimmt","en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"definition":{"en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"features":{"zh":["验证实现是否匹配更改规范","支持 Markdown 和 AsciiDoc 文件","可选指定更改名称","自动获取可用更改列表"],"ja":["実装が変更仕様と一致することを確認する","Markdown と AsciiDoc ファイルをサポート","変更名をオプションで指定可能","利用可能な変更の一覧を自動で取得"],"ko":["구현이 변경 사양과 일치하는지 확인","Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일 지원","변경 이름을 옵션으로 지정 가능","사용 가능한 변경 목록 자동获取"],"es":["Verificación de implementación de cambios","Compatibilidad con Markdown y AsciiDoc","Integración con VS Code","Selección de cambios mediante herramienta de pregunta al usuario","Ejecución de comandos para obtener cambios disponibles"],"fr":["Vérification de la mise en œuvre des modifications","Compatibilité avec Markdown et AsciiDoc","Intégration avec VS Code","Sélection de modifications via outil de question à l''utilisateur","Exécution de commandes pour obtenir les modifications disponibles"],"de":["Überprüfung der Implementierung von Änderungen","Kompatibilität mit Markdown und AsciiDoc","Integration mit VS Code","Auswahl von Änderungen mittels Benutzerfrage-Tool","Ausführung von Befehlen zur Abrufung verfügbarer Änderungen"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-verify-change","VS Code 扩展","验证实现","更改规范","Markdown","AsciiDoc"],"ja":["openspec-verify-change","VS Code 拡張機能","実装の検証","変更仕様","Markdown","AsciiDoc"],"ko":["openspec-verify-change","VS Code 확장","구현 확인","변경 사양","Markdown","AsciiDoc"],"es":["verificación de cambios","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","implementación de cambios","arteactos de cambio"],"fr":["vérification de modifications","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","mise en œuvre de modifications","artefacts de modification"],"de":["Änderungsüberprüfung","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Implementierung von Änderungen","Änderungsartefakte"]}},"owner":"gAmUssA","repo":"vscode-open-in-marked2","repoPath":"gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-verify-change","description":"Verify implementation matches change artifacts. Use when the user wants to validate that implementation is complete, correct, and coherent before archiving.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifa","body":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifact exists).\n   Include the schema used for each change if available.\n   Mark changes with incomplete tasks as \"(In Progress)\".\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check status to understand the schema**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - Which artifacts exist for this change\n\n3. **Get the change directory and load artifacts**\n\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions apply --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n\n   This returns the change directory and context files. Read all available artifacts from `contextFiles`.\n\n4. **Initialize verification report structure**\n\n   Create a report structure with three dimensions:\n   - **Completeness**: Track tasks and spec coverage\n   - **Correctness**: Track requirement implementation and scenario coverage\n   - **Coherence**: Track design adherence and pattern consistency\n\n   Each dimension can have CRITICAL, WARNING, or SUGGESTION issues.\n\n5. **Verify Completeness**\n\n   **Task Completion**:\n   - If tasks.md exists in contextFiles, read it\n   - Parse checkboxes: `- [ ]` (incomplete) vs `- [x]` (complete)\n   - Count complete vs total tasks\n   - If incomplete tasks exist:\n     - Add CRITICAL issue for each incomplete task\n     - Recommendation: \"Complete task: <description>\" or \"Mark as done if already implemented\"\n\n   **Spec Coverage**:\n   - If delta specs exist in `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/`:\n     - Extract all requirements (marked with \"### Requirement:\")\n     - For each requirement:\n       - Search codebase for keywords related to the requirement\n       - Assess if implementation likely exists\n     - If requirements appear unimplemented:\n       - Add CRITICAL issue: \"Requirement not found: <requirement name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Implement requirement X: <description>\"\n\n6. **Verify Correctness**\n\n   **Requirement Implementation Mapping**:\n   - For each requirement from delta specs:\n     - Search codebase for implementation evidence\n     - If found, note file paths and line ranges\n     - Assess if implementation matches requirement intent\n     - If divergence detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Implementation may diverge from spec: <details>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Review <file>:<lines> against requirement X\"\n\n   **Scenario Coverage**:\n   - For each scenario in delta specs (marked with \"#### Scenario:\"):\n     - Check if conditions are handled in code\n     - Check if tests exist covering the scenario\n     - If scenario appears uncovered:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Scenario not covered: <scenario name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Add test or implementation for scenario: <description>\"\n\n7. **Verify Coherence**\n\n   **Design Adherence**:\n   - If design.md exists in contextFiles:\n     - Extract key decisions (look for sections like \"Decision:\", \"Approach:\", \"Architecture:\")\n     - Verify implementation follows those decisions\n     - If contradiction detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Design decision not followed: <decision>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Update implementation or revise design.md to match reality\"\n   - If no design.md: Skip design adherence check, note \"No design.md to verify against\"\n\n   **Code Pattern Consistency**:\n   - Review new code for consistency with project patterns\n   - Check file naming, directory structure, coding style\n   - If significant deviations found:\n     - Add SUGGESTION: \"Code pattern deviation: <details>\"\n     - Recommendation: \"Consider following project pattern: <example>\"\n\n8. **Generate Verification Report**\n\n   **Summary Scorecard**:\n   ```\n   ## Verification Report: <change-name>\n\n   ### Summary\n   | Dimension    | Status           |\n   |--------------|------------------|\n   | Completeness | X/Y tasks, N reqs|\n   | Correctness  | M/N reqs covered |\n   | Coherence    | Followed/Issues  |\n   ```\n\n   **Issues by Priority**:\n\n   1. **CRITICAL** (Must fix before archive):\n      - Incomplete tasks\n      - Missing requirement implementations\n      - Each with specific, actionable recommendation\n\n   2. **WARNING** (Should fix):\n      - Spec/design divergences\n      - Missing scenario coverage\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   3. **SUGGESTION** (Nice to fix):\n      - Pattern inconsistencies\n      - Minor improvements\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   **Final Assessment**:\n   - If CRITICAL issues: \"X critical issue(s) found. Fix before archiving.\"\n   - If only warnings: \"No critical issues. Y warning(s) to consider. Ready for archive (with noted improvements).\"\n   - If all clear: \"All checks passed. Ready for archive.\"\n\n**Verification Heuristics**\n\n- **Completeness**: Focus on objective checklist items (checkboxes, requirements list)\n- **Correctness**: Use keyword search, file path analysis, reasonable inference - don''t require perfect certainty\n- **Coherence**: Look for glaring inconsistencies, don''t nitpick style\n- **False Positives**: When uncertain, prefer SUGGESTION over WARNING, WARNING over CRITICAL\n- **Actionability**: Every issue must have a specific recommendation with file/line references where applicable\n\n**Graceful Degradation**\n\n- If only tasks.md exists: verify task completion only, skip spec/design checks\n- If tasks + specs exist: verify completeness and correctness, skip design\n- If full artifacts: verify all three dimensions\n- Always note which checks were skipped and why\n\n**Output Format**\n\nUse clear markdown with:\n- Table for summary scorecard\n- Grouped lists for issues (CRITICAL/WARNING/SUGGESTION)\n- Code references in format: `file.ts:123`\n- Specific, actionable recommendations\n- No vague suggestions like \"consider reviewing\"\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:48:52.214Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing advanced change verification and specification validation in Markdown and AsciiDoc files","zh":"非常适合需要在 Markdown 和 AsciiDoc 文件中进行高级变更验证和规格验证的开发代理","ja":"Markdown および AsciiDoc ファイルでの高度な変更検証および仕様検証を必要とする開発エージェントに最適","ko":"Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일에서 고급 변경 확인 및 사양 확인이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una verificación de cambios avanzada y validación de especificaciones en archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une vérification de changements avancée et de validation de spécifications dans les fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine erweiterte Änderungsprüfung und Spezifikationsvalidierung in Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de verificação avançada de alterações e validação de especificações em arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходима продвинутая проверка изменений и валидация спецификаций в файлах Markdown и AsciiDoc","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التطوير التي تحتاج إلى التحقق المتقدم من التغييرات والتحقق من المواصفات في ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to verify implementation matches change artifacts, utilizing Marked 2 for content preview, and integrates with openspec for listing and selecting changes, all while handling JSON data for seamless interaction","zh":"赋予代理人验证实现是否与变更工件匹配的能力，利用 Marked 2 进行内容预览，并与 openspec 集成以列出和选择变更，同时处理 JSON 数据以实现无缝交互","ja":"Marked 2 を使用してコンテンツのプレビューを行い、openspec と連携して変更を一覧表示および選択し、JSON データを処理して無停滞な相互作用を実現することで、実装が変更アーティファクトと一致することをエージェントが検証できるようにする","ko":"Marked 2를 사용하여 콘텐츠 미리 보기를 수행하고 openspec와 통합하여 변경 사항을 나열 및 선택하며 JSON 데이터를 처리하여 무중단 상호 작용을实现함으로써 구현이 변경 아티팩트와 일치하는지 에이전트가 확인할 수 있도록 하는 것","es":"Habilita a los agentes a verificar que la implementación coincide con los artefactos de cambio, utilizando Marked 2 para la vista previa de contenido e integrándose con openspec para la lista y selección de cambios, todo mientras manipula datos JSON para una interacción sin problemas","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier que la mise en œuvre correspond aux artefacts de changement, en utilisant Marked 2 pour l''aperçu de contenu et en intégrant openspec pour la liste et la sélection des changements, le tout en gérant des données JSON pour une interaction fluide","de":"Ermächtigt Mittel, die Implementierung mit den Änderungsartefakten zu überprüfen, indem Marked 2 für die Vorschau von Inhalten verwendet wird und sich in openspec für die Auflistung und Auswahl von Änderungen integriert, während JSON-Daten für eine nahtlose Interaktion behandelt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a verificar se a implementação corresponde aos artefatos de alteração, utilizando o Marked 2 para visualização de conteúdo e integrando-se com o openspec para listagem e seleção de alterações, tudo isso manipulando dados JSON para interação sem problemas","ru":"Позволяет агентам проверять соответствие реализации артефактам изменений, используя Marked 2 для предварительного просмотра контента и интегрируясь с openspec для перечисления и выбора изменений, все это при обработке данных JSON для бесперебойного взаимодействия","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من التحقق من تطابق التنفيذ مع مكونات التغيير، باستخدام Marked 2 لمعاينة المحتوى وتكاملها مع openspec لقائمة الاختيار والتغيير، مع معالجة بيانات JSON لتفاعل سلس"},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying change implementations against specifications","Automating change artifact validation","Debugging implementation mismatches in Markdown and AsciiDoc files"],"zh":["验证实现是否与规范相符","自动化变更工件验证","调试 Markdown 和 AsciiDoc 文件中的实现不匹配"],"ja":["実装が仕様と一致することを検証する","変更アーティファクトの検証を自動化する","Markdown および AsciiDoc ファイルの実装不一致をデバッグする"],"ko":["구현이 사양과 일치하는지 확인","변경 아티팩트의 확인을 자동화","Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일의 구현 불일치를 디버그"],"es":["Verificar la implementación de cambios frente a las especificaciones","Automatizar la validación de artefactos de cambio","Depurar las discrepancias de implementación en archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc"],"fr":["Vérifier la mise en œuvre des changements par rapport aux spécifications","Automatiser la validation des artefacts de changement","Déboguer les écarts de mise en œuvre dans les fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc"],"de":["Überprüfen der Implementierung von Änderungen gegenüber den Spezifikationen","Automatisieren der Validierung von Änderungsartefakten","Fehlerbehebung bei der Implementierung in Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien"],"pt":["Verificar implementações de alterações contra especificações","Automatizar validação de artefatos de alteração","Depurar discrepâncias de implementação em arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc"],"ru":["Проверка реализации изменений против спецификаций","Автоматизация валидации артефактов изменений","Отладка несоответствий реализации в файлах Markdown и AsciiDoc"],"ar":["التحقق من تنفيذ التغييرات مقابل المواصفات","تأتمة التحقق من مكونات التغيير","تصحيح أخطاء تنفيذ الملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires VS Code extension installation","Dependent on Marked 2 and openspec tools","Limited to Markdown and AsciiDoc file formats"],"zh":["需要安装 VS Code 扩展","依赖 Marked 2 和 openspec 工具","仅限 Markdown 和 AsciiDoc 文件格式"],"ja":["VS Code 拡張機能のインストールが必要","Marked 2 および openspec ツールに依存","Markdown および AsciiDoc ファイル形式のみ"],"ko":["VS Code 확장 프로그램 설치 필요","Marked 2 및 openspec 도구에 의존","Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일 형식만"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de la extensión de VS Code","Dependiente de las herramientas Marked 2 y openspec","Limitado a los formatos de archivo Markdown y AsciiDoc"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de l''extension VS Code","Dépendant des outils Marked 2 et openspec","Limité aux formats de fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation der VS Code-Erweiterung","Abhängig von den Tools Marked 2 und openspec","Begrenzt auf die Dateiformate Markdown und AsciiDoc"],"pt":["Requer instalação da extensão do VS Code","Dependente das ferramentas Marked 2 e openspec","Limitado a formatos de arquivo Markdown e AsciiDoc"],"ru":["Требуется установка расширения VS Code","Зависит от инструментов Marked 2 и openspec","Ограничен форматами файлов Markdown и AsciiDoc"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت ملحق VS Code","اعتمادية على أدوات Marked 2 و openspec","محدود بتنسيقات الملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
