에서 완료된 변경을 아카이브하는 기능","다양한 파일 형식을 지원","변경 이름 입력이 선택 사항","자동으로 변경 이름을 감지"],"es":["Abrir archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc en Marked 2","Archivar cambios en el flujo de trabajo experimental","Selección de cambios disponibles mediante la herramienta AskUserQuestion","Filtrado de cambios activos y ya archivados","Compatibilidad con VS Code"],"fr":["Ouvrir des fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc dans Marked 2","Archiver des modifications dans le flux de travail expérimental","Sélection de modifications disponibles à l''aide de l''outil AskUserQuestion","Filtrage de modifications actives et déjà archivées","Compatibilité avec VS Code"],"de":["Öffnen von Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien in Marked 2","Archivieren von Änderungen im experimentellen Arbeitsablauf","Auswahl von verfügbaren Änderungen mithilfe des Tools AskUserQuestion","Filtern von aktiven und bereits archivierten Änderungen","Kompatibilität mit VS Code"],"pt":["Arquivamento de alterações no fluxo de trabalho experimental","Integração com o VS Code","Suporte a Markdown e AsciiDoc","Ferramenta de seleção de alterações","Compatibilidade com o Marked 2"],"ru":["Архивация изменений в экспериментальном рабочем процессе","Интеграция с VS Code","Поддержка Markdown и AsciiDoc","Инструмент выбора изменений","Совместимость с Marked 2"],"ar":["أرشفة التغييرات في تدفق العمل التجريبي","التكامل مع برنامج VS Code","دعم Markdown و AsciiDoc","أداة اختيار التغييرات","التوافق مع Marked 2"]},"keywords":{"zh":["VS Code 扩展","Marked 2","Markdown","AsciiDoc","实验工作流","归档","代码编辑器"],"ja":["VS Code 拡張機能","Marked 2","Markdown","AsciiDoc","実験ワークフロー","アーカイブ","コードエディター"],"ko":["VS Code 확장","Marked 2","Markdown","AsciiDoc","실험 워크플로우","아카이브","코드 편집기"],"es":["VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","flujo de trabajo experimental","archivar cambios","AskUserQuestion","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","flux de travail expérimental","archiver des modifications","AskUserQuestion","développement de logiciels"],"de":["VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","experimenteller Arbeitsablauf","Änderungen archivieren","AskUserQuestion","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["openspec-archive-change","VS Code","fluxo de trabalho experimental","arquivamento de alterações","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["openspec-archive-change","VS Code","экспериментальный рабочий процесс","архивация изменений","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["openspec-archive-change","برنامج VS Code","تدفق العمل التجريبي","أرشفة التغييرات","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"gAmUssA","repo":"vscode-open-in-marked2","repoPath":"gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-archive-change","description":"Archive a completed change in the experimental workflow. Use when the user wants to finalize and archive a change after implementation is complete.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Archive a completed change in the experimental workflow.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show only active changes (not already archived).\n   Include the schema used for eac","body":"Archive a completed change in the experimental workflow.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show only active changes (not already archived).\n   Include the schema used for each change if available.\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check artifact completion status**\n\n   Run `openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json` to check artifact completion.\n\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used\n   - `artifacts`: List of artifacts with their status (`done` or other)\n\n   **If any artifacts are not `done`:**\n   - Display warning listing incomplete artifacts\n   - Use **AskUserQuestion tool** to confirm user wants to proceed\n   - Proceed if user confirms\n\n3. **Check task completion status**\n\n   Read the tasks file (typically `tasks.md`) to check for incomplete tasks.\n\n   Count tasks marked with `- [ ]` (incomplete) vs `- [x]` (complete).\n\n   **If incomplete tasks found:**\n   - Display warning showing count of incomplete tasks\n   - Use **AskUserQuestion tool** to confirm user wants to proceed\n   - Proceed if user confirms\n\n   **If no tasks file exists:** Proceed without task-related warning.\n\n4. **Assess delta spec sync state**\n\n   Check for delta specs at `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/`. If none exist, proceed without sync prompt.\n\n   **If delta specs exist:**\n   - Compare each delta spec with its corresponding main spec at `openspec/specs/<capability>/spec.md`\n   - Determine what changes would be applied (adds, modifications, removals, renames)\n   - Show a combined summary before prompting\n\n   **Prompt options:**\n   - If changes needed: \"Sync now (recommended)\", \"Archive without syncing\"\n   - If already synced: \"Archive now\", \"Sync anyway\", \"Cancel\"\n\n   If user chooses sync, execute /opsx:sync logic (use the openspec-sync-specs skill). Proceed to archive regardless of choice.\n\n5. **Perform the archive**\n\n   Create the archive directory if it doesn''t exist:\n   ```bash\n   mkdir -p openspec/changes/archive\n   ```\n\n   Generate target name using current date: `YYYY-MM-DD-<change-name>`\n\n   **Check if target already exists:**\n   - If yes: Fail with error, suggest renaming existing archive or using different date\n   - If no: Move the change directory to archive\n\n   ```bash\n   mv openspec/changes/<name> openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>\n   ```\n\n6. **Display summary**\n\n   Show archive completion summary including:\n   - Change name\n   - Schema that was used\n   - Archive location\n   - Whether specs were synced (if applicable)\n   - Note about any warnings (incomplete artifacts/tasks)\n\n**Output On Success**\n\n```\n## Archive Complete\n\n**Change:** <change-name>\n**Schema:** <schema-name>\n**Archived to:** openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/\n**Specs:** ✓ Synced to main specs (or \"No delta specs\" or \"Sync skipped\")\n\nAll artifacts complete. All tasks complete.\n```\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Always prompt for change selection if not provided\n- Use artifact graph (openspec status --json) for completion checking\n- Don''t block archive on warnings - just inform and confirm\n- Preserve .openspec.yaml when moving to archive (it moves with the directory)\n- Show clear summary of what happened\n- If sync is requested, use openspec-sync-specs approach (agent-driven)\n- If delta specs exist, always run the sync assessment and show the combined summary before prompting\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:49:12.067Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring seamless integration with VS Code and Marked 2 for efficient Markdown and AsciiDoc file management.","zh":"适用于需要与VS Code和Marked 2实现无缝集成的开发代理，以高效管理Markdown和AsciiDoc文件。","ja":"VS CodeおよびMarked 2とのシームレスな統合を必要とする開発エージェントに適しています。MarkdownおよびAsciiDocファイルの効率的な管理に役立ちます。","ko":"VS Code와 Marked 2와의无缝한 통합을 필요로 하는 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다. Markdown 및 AsciiDoc 파일의 효율적인 관리에 도움이 됩니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren una integración sin problemas con VS Code y Marked 2 para una gestión eficiente de archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une intégration transparente avec VS Code et Marked 2 pour une gestion efficace des fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine nahtlose Integration mit VS Code und Marked 2 für eine effiziente Verwaltung von Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de integração perfeita com o VS Code e o Marked 2 para gerenciamento eficiente de arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих бесшовной интеграции с VS Code и Marked 2 для эффективного управления файлами Markdown и AsciiDoc.","ar":"مثالية لعميل التطوير الذي يتطلب تكاملًا سلسًا مع VS Code و Marked 2 لإدارة ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc بفعالية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to archive completed changes in the experimental workflow using the openspec-archive-change command, leveraging JSON output from openspec list and integrating with the AskUserQuestion tool for user selection, all while supporting active change management and schema inclusion.","zh":"赋予代理人使用openspec-archive-change命令在实验工作流中归档完成的更改的能力，利用openspec list的JSON输出并与AskUserQuestion工具集成以实现用户选择，同时支持活动更改管理和模式包含。","ja":"エージェントが実験ワークフローで完了した変更をopenspec-archive-changeコマンドでアーカイブできるようにし、openspec listのJSON出力を活用してAskUserQuestionツールと統合し、ユーザー選択を実現しながら、アクティブな変更管理とスキーマの包含をサポートします。","ko":"실험 워크플로에서 완료된 변경 사항을 openspec-archive-change 명령으로 아카이브 할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하며, openspec list의 JSON 출력을 활용하여 AskUserQuestion 도구와 통합하여 사용자 선택을 구현하며, 동시에 활성 변경 관리 및 스키마 포함을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a archivar los cambios completados en el flujo de trabajo experimental utilizando el comando openspec-archive-change, aprovechando la salida JSON de openspec list e integrándose con la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la selección del usuario, todo mientras se admite la administración activa de cambios y la inclusión de esquemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''archiver les modifications complètes dans le flux de travail expérimental en utilisant la commande openspec-archive-change, en exploitant la sortie JSON de openspec list et en s''intégrant avec l''outil AskUserQuestion pour la sélection de l''utilisateur, le tout en supportant la gestion active des modifications et l''inclusion de schémas.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, abgeschlossene Änderungen im experimentellen Workflow mit dem Befehl openspec-archive-change zu archivieren, indem es die JSON-Ausgabe von openspec list nutzt und sich in die AskUserQuestion-Tool für die Benutzerauswahl integriert, während es die aktive Änderungsverwaltung und die Einbeziehung von Schemata unterstützt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a arquivar alterações concluídas no fluxo de trabalho experimental usando o comando openspec-archive-change, aproveitando a saída JSON do openspec list e integrando com a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para seleção do usuário, tudo isso enquanto suporta gerenciamento de alterações ativas e inclusão de esquemas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью архивировать завершенные изменения в экспериментальном рабочем процессе с помощью команды openspec-archive-change, используя выходные данные JSON из openspec list и интегрируясь с инструментом AskUserQuestion для выбора пользователя, все это при поддержке активного управления изменениями и включения схем.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من أرشفة التغييرات المكتملة في تدفق العمل التجريبي باستخدام أمر openspec-archive-change، مستفيدًا من الإخراج JSON من openspec list ومتكامل مع أداة AskUserQuestion لاختيار المستخدم، كل ذلك مع دعم إدارة التغييرات النشطة وإدراج السchemas."},"useCases":{"en":["Archiving completed changes in the experimental workflow","Managing active changes with openspec list --json","Integrating user selection for ambiguous change names"],"zh":["在实验工作流中归档完成的更改","使用openspec list --json管理活动更改","为模糊的更改名称集成用户选择"],"ja":["実験ワークフローで完了した変更をアーカイブする","openspec list --jsonを使用してアクティブな変更を管理する","曖昧な変更名のユーザー選択を統合する"],"ko":["실험 워크플로에서 완료된 변경 사항을 아카이브하는 것","openspec list --json을 사용하여 활성 변경 사항을 관리하는 것","모호한 변경 이름에 대한 사용자 선택을 통합하는 것"],"es":["Archivar los cambios completados en el flujo de trabajo experimental","Gestionar los cambios activos con openspec list --json","Integrar la selección del usuario para nombres de cambios ambiguos"],"fr":["Archiver les modifications complètes dans le flux de travail expérimental","Gérer les modifications actives avec openspec list --json","Intégrer la sélection de l''utilisateur pour les noms de modifications ambigus"],"de":["Abgeschlossene Änderungen im experimentellen Workflow archivieren","Aktive Änderungen mit openspec list --json verwalten","Benutzerauswahl für mehrdeutige Änderungsnamen integrieren"],"pt":["Arquivar alterações concluídas no fluxo de trabalho experimental","Gerenciar alterações ativas com openspec list --json","Integrar seleção do usuário para nomes de alterações ambíguos"],"ru":["Архивировать завершенные изменения в экспериментальном рабочем процессе","Управлять активными изменениями с помощью openspec list --json","Интегрировать выбор пользователя для неоднозначных названий изменений"],"ar":["أرشفة التغييرات المكتملة في تدفق العمل التجريبي","إدارة التغييرات النشطة مع openspec list --json","دمج اختيار المستخدم لأسماء التغييرات الغامضة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires VS Code extension installation","Dependent on Marked 2 for file preview","Limited to active changes, excluding already archived ones"],"zh":["需要安装VS Code扩展","依赖Marked 2进行文件预览","仅限活动更改，排除已归档的更改"],"ja":["VS Code拡張機能のインストールが必要","Marked 2に依存してファイルプレビューを行う","アクティブな変更のみを対象とし、既にアーカイブされた変更は除外する"],"ko":["VS Code 확장 프로그램 설치가 필요합니다.","파일 미리보기를 위해 Marked 2에 의존합니다.","활성 변경 사항만 해당되며, 이미 아카이브된 변경 사항은 제외합니다."],"es":["Requiere la instalación de la extensión de VS Code","Depende de Marked 2 para la vista previa de archivos","Limitado a los cambios activos, excluyendo los ya archivados"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de l''extension VS Code","Dépend de Marked 2 pour l''aperçu de fichiers","Limité aux modifications actives, excluant celles déjà archivées"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation der VS Code-Erweiterung","Hängt von Marked 2 für die Dateivorschau ab","Begrenzt auf aktive Änderungen, ausschließlich der bereits archivierten"],"pt":["Exige instalação da extensão do VS Code","Depende do Marked 2 para visualização de arquivos","Limitado a alterações ativas, excluindo as já arquivadas"],"ru":["Требует установки расширения VS Code","Зависит от Marked 2 для предпросмотра файлов","Ограничен активными изменениями, исключая уже архивированные"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت ملحق VS Code","يعتمد على Marked 2 لمعاينة الملفات","محدود بالتغييرات النشطة، باستثناء تلك المأرشفة بالفعل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gamingopgamingop/sarthak-skill-forge/bicep-diagrams', 'community', 'gamingopgamingop', 'sarthak-skill-forge', 'gamingopgamingop/sarthak-skill-forge', 'bicep-diagrams', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z', '2026-02-18T11:49:45.948Z', NULL, '{"id":"gamingopgamingop/sarthak-skill-forge/bicep-diagrams","name":"bicep-diagrams","description":{"zh":"BicepBicep","ja":"BicepAzureBicep","ko":"BicepBicep","es":"El generador de diagramas Bicep crea representaciones visuales de la infraestructura de Azure a partir de archivos Bicep.","fr":"Le générateur de diagrammes Bicep crée des représentations visuelles de l''infrastructure Azure à partir de fichiers Bicep.","de":"Der Bicep-Diagramm-Generator erstellt visuelle Darstellungen der Azure-Infrastruktur aus Bicep-Dateien.","pt":"O Gerador de Diagramas Bicep gera diagramas de arquitetura diretamente de arquivos Bicep do Azure.","ru":"Генератор диаграмм Bicep генерирует диаграммы архитектуры trực из файлов Azure Bicep.","ar":"مُولِد رسومات Bicep يُنشئ مخططات بنية تحتية مباشرة من ملفات Bicep لشركة Azure.","en":"sarthakdev.me"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Bicep ","ja":"Bicep","ko":"Bicep ","es":"Generador de diagramas Bicep para Azure","fr":"Générateur de diagrammes Bicep pour Azure","de":"Bicep-Diagramm-Generator für Azure","pt":"Gerador de Diagramas Bicep - Visualize Infraestrutura Azure","ru":"Генератор диаграмм Bicep - Визуализируйте инфраструктуру ...","ar":"مُولِد رسومات Bicep - قم بتصوير البنية التحتية لشركة Azure","en":"bicep-diagrams"},"description":{"zh":"BicepBicep","ja":"BicepAzureBicep","ko":"BicepBicep","es":"El generador de diagramas Bicep crea representaciones visuales de la infraestructura de Azure a partir de archivos Bicep.","fr":"Le générateur de diagrammes Bicep crée des représentations visuelles de l''infrastructure Azure à partir de fichiers Bicep.","de":"Der Bicep-Diagramm-Generator erstellt visuelle Darstellungen der Azure-Infrastruktur aus Bicep-Dateien.","pt":"O Gerador de Diagramas Bicep gera diagramas de arquitetura diretamente de arquivos Bicep do Azure.","ru":"Генератор диаграмм Bicep генерирует диаграммы архитектуры trực из файлов Azure Bicep.","ar":"مُولِد رسومات Bicep يُنشئ مخططات بنية تحتية مباشرة من ملفات Bicep لشركة Azure.","en":"sarthakdev.me"},"definition":{"en":"sarthakdev.me"},"features":{"zh":["Bicep","Azure","Bicep","Bicep","Bicep"],"ja":["Bicep","Azure","Bicep","Bicep","Bicep"],"ko":["Bicep","Azure","Bicep","Bicep","Bicep"],"es":["Generación de diagramas de arquitectura directamente desde archivos Bicep","Visualización de la infraestructura de Azure","Compatibilidad con archivos Bicep (.bicep)","Generación automática de diagramas","Mejora de la comprensión de la infraestructura en la nube"],"fr":["Génération de diagrammes d''architecture directement à partir de fichiers Bicep","Visualisation de l''infrastructure Azure","Compatibilité avec les fichiers Bicep (.bicep)","Génération automatique de diagrammes","Amélioration de la compréhension de l''infrastructure cloud"],"de":["Erstellung von Architekturdiagrammen direkt aus Bicep-Dateien","Visualisierung der Azure-Infrastruktur","Kompatibilität mit Bicep-Dateien (.bicep)","Automatische Generierung von Diagrammen","Verbesserung des Verständnisses der Cloud-Infrastruktur"],"pt":["Geração de diagramas de arquitetura diretamente de arquivos Bicep","Visualização da infraestrutura do Azure","Suporte a arquivos Bicep (.bicep)","Integração com o Azure","Geração automática de diagramas","Simplificação da visualização da infraestrutura"],"ru":["Генерация диаграмм архитектуры прям из файлов Bicep","Визуализация инфраструктуры Azure","Поддержка файлов Bicep (.bicep)","Интеграция с Azure","Автоматическая генерация диаграмм","Упрощение визуализации инфраструктуры"],"ar":["إنشاء مخططات بنية تحتية مباشرة من ملفات Bicep","تصوير البنية التحتية لشركة Azure","دعم ملفات Bicep (.bicep)","التكامل مع شركة Azure","إنشاء مخططات تلقائي","تبسيط عملية تصور البنية التحتية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Bicep","Azure Bicep","Bicep","Bicep","Azure","Bicep DSL"],"ja":["Bicep","Azure Bicep","Bicep","Bicep","Azure","Bicep DSL"],"ko":["Bicep","Azure Bicep","Bicep","Bicep","Azure","Bicep DSL"],"es":["Bicep","Azure","diagramas de arquitectura","infraestructura en la nube","generador de diagramas","visualización de infraestructura","Bicep files","Azure Bicep"],"fr":["Bicep","Azure","diagrammes d''architecture","infrastructure cloud","générateur de diagrammes","visualisation d''infrastructure","fichiers Bicep","Azure Bicep"],"de":["Bicep","Azure","Architekturdiagramme","Cloud-Infrastruktur","Diagramm-Generator","Visualisierung von Infrastruktur","Bicep-Dateien","Azure Bicep"],"pt":["Bicep","Azure","Diagramas de arquitetura","Infraestrutura","Desenvolvimento de software","Linguagem de domínio específico","Implantação de recursos","Visualização de infraestrutura","Gerador de diagramas"],"ru":["Bicep","Azure","Диаграммы архитектуры","Инфраструктура","Разработка программного обеспечения","Язык домена específico","Развертывание ресурсов","Визуализация инфраструктуры","Генератор диаграмм"],"ar":["Bicep","Azure","مخططات بنية تحتية","البنية التحتية","تطوير البرمجيات","لغة محددة للنطاق","تنصيب موارد","تصوير البنية التحتية","مُولِد رسومات"]}},"owner":"gamingopgamingop","repo":"sarthak-skill-forge","repoPath":"gamingopgamingop/sarthak-skill-forge","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bicep-diagrams","description":"Generates architecture diagrams from Azure Bicep files. Use when user has .bicep files or asks to visualize Bicep infrastructure.","version":"1.0.0","tags":"bicep, azure, diagram, infrastructure, iac, azure-resources","bodyPreview":"# Bicep Diagram Generator\n\nGenerates architecture diagrams directly from Azure Bicep files. Bicep is a domain-specific language (DSL) for deploying Azure resources declaratively.\n\n## When to Use\n\nActivate this skill when:\n\n- User has Bicep files (`.bicep`) and wants to visualize the infrastructure\n- User asks to \"diagram my Bicep\" or \"visualize this Bicep infrastructure\"\n- User mentions Bicep or Azure Bicep\n- User wants to see the architecture of their Bicep-deployed resources\n\n## How It Works","body":"# Bicep Diagram Generator\n\nGenerates architecture diagrams directly from Azure Bicep files. Bicep is a domain-specific language (DSL) for deploying Azure resources declaratively.\n\n## When to Use\n\nActivate this skill when:\n\n- User has Bicep files (`.bicep`) and wants to visualize the infrastructure\n- User asks to \"diagram my Bicep\" or \"visualize this Bicep infrastructure\"\n- User mentions Bicep or Azure Bicep\n- User wants to see the architecture of their Bicep-deployed resources\n\n## How It Works\n\nThis skill generates Bicep-specific diagrams by parsing Bicep code and calling the Eraser API directly:\n\n1. **Parse Bicep Files**: Identify resource declarations, modules, parameters, and outputs\n2. **Extract Relationships**: Map dependencies, resource references, and module hierarchies\n3. **Generate Eraser DSL**: Create Eraser DSL code from Bicep resources\n4. **Call Eraser API**: Use `/api/render/elements` with `diagramType: \"cloud-architecture-diagram\"`\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen the user provides Bicep code:\n\n1. **Parse the Bicep**\n\n   - Identify all `resource` declarations (Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines, etc.)\n   - Extract `module` declarations and their configurations\n   - Note `param` and `output` definitions\n   - Identify `var` variables and their usage\n\n2. **Map Relationships**\n\n   - Track resource dependencies (e.g., `dependsOn` or implicit dependencies)\n   - Group resources by type (compute, networking, storage, etc.)\n   - Identify VNets as containers for subnets and resources\n   - Note Network Security Groups, Key Vaults, and other security resources\n\n3. **Generate Eraser DSL** Convert Bicep resources to Eraser DSL:\n\n   - **CRITICAL: Label Formatting Rules**\n     - Labels MUST be on a single line - NEVER use newlines inside label attributes\n     - Keep labels simple and readable - prefer separate labels over concatenating too much metadata\n     - Format DSL with proper line breaks (one node/group per line, but labels stay on single lines)\n     - If including metadata like CIDR blocks or VM sizes, include them in the same quoted label string: `[label: \"VNet 10.0.0.0/16\"]`\n\n   Example:\n\n   ```\n   myVNet [label: \"VNet 10.0.0.0/16\"] {\n     subnet1 [label: \"Subnet 1\"] {\n       myVM [icon: azure-vm, label: \"Virtual Machine\"]\n       gateway [icon: azure-app-gateway]\n     }\n     subnet2 [label: \"Subnet 2\"] {\n       database [icon: azure-sql]\n     }\n   }\n   storage [icon: azure-storage]\n   myVNet -> myVM\n   myVM -> database\n   ```\n\n4. **Make the HTTP Request**\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: You MUST execute this curl command after generating the DSL. Never stop after generating DSL without making the API call.\n\n   **CRITICAL**: In the `X-Skill-Source` header below, you MUST replace the value with your AI agent name:\n   - If you are Claude (Anthropic), use: `claude`\n   - If you are running in Cursor, use: `cursor`\n   - If you are ChatGPT (OpenAI), use: `chatgpt`\n   - If you are Gemini (Google), use: `gemini`\n   - Otherwise, use your model/agent name in lowercase\n\n   ```bash\n   curl -X POST https://app.eraser.io/api/render/elements \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -H \"X-Skill-Source: eraser-skill\" \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${ERASER_API_KEY}\" \\\n     -d ''{\n       \"elements\": [{\n         \"type\": \"diagram\",\n         \"id\": \"diagram-1\",\n         \"code\": \"<your generated DSL>\",\n         \"diagramType\": \"cloud-architecture-diagram\"\n       }],\n       \"scale\": 2,\n       \"theme\": \"${ERASER_THEME:-dark}\",\n       \"background\": true\n     }''\n   ```\n\n5. **Track Sources During Analysis**\n\n   As you analyze Bicep files and resources to generate the diagram, track:\n\n   - **Internal files**: Record each Bicep file path you read and what resources were extracted (e.g., `infra/main.bicep` - VNet and subnet definitions, `infra/sql.bicep` - SQL Database configuration)\n   - **External references**: Note any documentation, examples, or URLs consulted (e.g., Azure Bicep documentation, Azure architecture best practices)\n   - **Annotations**: For each source, note what it contributed to the diagram\n\n6. **Handle the Response**\n\n   **CRITICAL: Minimal Output Format**\n\n   Your response MUST always include these elements with clear headers:\n\n   1. **Diagram Preview**: Display with a header\n      ```\n      ## Diagram\n      ![{Title}]({imageUrl})\n      ```\n      Use the ACTUAL `imageUrl` from the API response.\n\n   2. **Editor Link**: Display with a header\n      ```\n      ## Open in Eraser\n      [Edit this diagram in the Eraser editor]({createEraserFileUrl})\n      ```\n      Use the ACTUAL URL from the API response.\n\n   3. **Sources section**: Brief list of files/resources analyzed (if applicable)\n      ```\n      ## Sources\n      - `path/to/file` - What was extracted\n      ```\n\n   4. **Diagram Code section**: The Eraser DSL in a code block with `eraser` language tag\n      ```\n      ## Diagram Code\n      ```eraser\n      {DSL code here}\n      ```\n      ```\n\n   5. **Learn More link**: `You can learn more about Eraser at https://docs.eraser.io/docs/using-ai-agent-integrations`\n\n   **Additional content rules:**\n   - If the user ONLY asked for a diagram, include NOTHING beyond the 5 elements above\n   - If the user explicitly asked for more (e.g., \"explain the architecture\", \"suggest improvements\"), you may include that additional content\n   - Never add unrequested sections like Overview, Security Considerations, Testing, etc.\n\n   The default output should be SHORT. The diagram image speaks for itself.\n\n7. **Handle Modules**\n   - If modules are used, show module boundaries\n   - Include module parameters and outputs\n   - Show how modules connect to main resources\n\n## Bicep-Specific Tips\n\n- **Show Resource Groups**: Bicep deployments target resource groups\n- **VNets as Containers**: Show VNets containing subnets and resources\n- **Include Dependencies**: Show `dependsOn` relationships\n- **Module Structure**: If modules are used, show their boundaries\n- **Parameters**: Note key parameters that affect resource configuration\n- **Use Azure Icons**: Request Azure-specific styling\n\n## Example: Bicep with Parameters and Modules\n\n### User Input\n\n```bicep\n@description(''The name of the Virtual Network'')\nparam vnetName string = ''myVNet''\n@description(''The address prefix for the VNet'')\nparam vnetAddressPrefix string = ''10.0.0.0/16''\n@description(''The address prefix for the subnet'')\nparam subnetAddressPrefix string = ''10.0.1.0/24''\n@description(''VM size'')\nparam vmSize string = ''Standard_B1s''\n\n// Main VNet resource\nresource virtualNetwork ''Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks@2021-05-01'' = {\n  name: vnetName\n  location: resourceGroup().location\n  properties: {\n    addressSpace: {\n      addressPrefixes: [vnetAddressPrefix]\n    }\n    subnets: [\n      {\n        name: ''subnet1''\n        properties: {\n          addressPrefix: subnetAddressPrefix\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\n// VM resource with dependsOn\nresource virtualMachine ''Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines@2021-11-01'' = {\n  name: ''myVM''\n  location: resourceGroup().location\n  properties: {\n    hardwareProfile: {\n      vmSize: vmSize\n    }\n  }\n  dependsOn: [virtualNetwork]\n}\n\n// Module usage\nmodule storageModule ''./modules/storage.bicep'' = {\n  name: ''storage''\n  params: {\n    location: resourceGroup().location\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\n1. Parses Bicep:\n\n   - **Parameters**: vnetName, vnetAddressPrefix, subnetAddressPrefix, vmSize\n   - **Resources**: VNet with subnet, VM with dependsOn relationship\n   - **Module**: Storage module with parameters\n\n2. Generates DSL showing Bicep-specific features:\n\n   ```\n   myVNet [label: \"VNet 10.0.0.0/16\"] {\n     subnet1 [label: \"Subnet 1 10.0.1.0/24\"] {\n       myVM [icon: azure-vm, label: \"VM Standard_B1s\"]\n     }\n   }\n\n   storage-module [label: \"Storage Module\"] {\n     storage-account [icon: azure-storage]\n   }\n\n   myVNet -> myVM\n   ```\n\n   **Important**: All label text must be on a single line within quotes. Bicep-specific: Show modules as containers, include `dependsOn` relationships, note parameter usage in resource configuration.\n\n3. Calls `/api/render/elements` with `diagramType: \"cloud-architecture-diagram\"`\n\n4. Calls `/api/render/elements` with `diagramType: \"cloud-architecture-diagram\"`\n\n### Result\n\nUser receives a diagram showing:\n\n- VNet as a container\n- Subnet nested inside VNet\n- VM in the subnet\n- Dependency relationship shown\n- Proper Azure styling\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:49:45.948Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cloud Infrastructure Agents needing Azure Bicep visualization capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要 Azure Bicep 可视化能力的云基础设施代理。","ja":"Azure Bicep の視覚化機能を必要とするクラウドインフラストラクチャエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Azure Bicep 시각화 기능이 필요한 클라우드 인프라 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Infraestructura en la Nube que necesitan capacidades de visualización de Azure Bicep.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''infrastructure cloud ayant besoin de capacités de visualisation Azure Bicep.","de":"Perfekt für Cloud-Infrastruktur-Agents, die Azure Bicep-Visualisierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Infraestrutura em Nuvem que precisam de capacidades de visualização do Azure Bicep.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов инфраструктуры облака, которым необходимы возможности визуализации Azure Bicep.","ar":"مثالي لعميل بروتوكول إنترنت سحابي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات تمثيل Azure Bicep."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate architecture diagrams directly from Azure Bicep files (.bicep) using a domain-specific language (DSL) for deploying Azure resources declaratively, providing a clear visualization of the infrastructure.","zh":"赋予代理直接从 Azure Bicep 文件 (.bicep) 生成架构图的能力，使用特定领域语言 (DSL) 声明性地部署 Azure 资源，提供基础设施的清晰可视化。","ja":"エージェントに Azure Bicep ファイル (.bicep) から直接アーキテクチャ ダイアグラムを生成する機能を提供します。Azure リソースを宣言的にデプロイするためのドメイン固有言語 (DSL) を使用し、インフラストラクチャの明確な視覚化を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 Azure Bicep 파일 (.bicep)에서 직접 아키텍처 다이어그램을 생성할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다. Azure 리소스를 선언적으로 배포하기 위한 특정 도메인 언어 (DSL)를 사용하여 인프라의 명확한 시각화를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar diagramas de arquitectura directamente desde archivos Azure Bicep (.bicep) utilizando un lenguaje específico de dominio (DSL) para implementar recursos de Azure de forma declarativa, proporcionando una visualización clara de la infraestructura.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des diagrammes d''architecture directement à partir de fichiers Azure Bicep (.bicep) en utilisant un langage spécifique de domaine (DSL) pour déployer des ressources Azure de manière déclarative, fournissant une visualisation claire de l''infrastructure.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Architekturdiagramme direkt aus Azure Bicep-Dateien (.bicep) zu generieren, indem sie eine domänen-spezifische Sprache (DSL) zur deklarativen Bereitstellung von Azure-Ressourcen verwenden, wodurch eine klare Visualisierung der Infrastruktur bereitgestellt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar diagramas de arquitetura diretamente a partir de arquivos Azure Bicep (.bicep) usando uma linguagem específica de domínio (DSL) para implantar recursos do Azure de forma declarativa, fornecendo uma visualização clara da infraestrutura.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать диаграммы архитектуры напрямую из файлов Azure Bicep (.bicep) с использованием языка, специфичного для области (DSL), для развертывания ресурсов Azure декларативно, обеспечивая четкую визуализацию инфраструктуры.","ar":"تمكّن العميل من توليد رسومات بنية مباشرة من ملفات Azure Bicep (.bicep) باستخدام لغة محددة للنطاق (DSL) لتحويل موارد Azure تعريفيا، مما يوفر تمثيلا واضحا للبنية التحتية."},"useCases":{"en":["Visualizing Bicep infrastructure","Generating diagrams from .bicep files","Debugging Azure resource deployments"],"zh":["可视化 Bicep 基础设施","从 .bicep 文件生成图表","调试 Azure 资源部署"],"ja":["Bicep インフラストラクチャの視覚化",".bicep ファイルからダイアグラムを生成","Azure リソースのデプロイのデバッグ"],"ko":["Bicep 인프라 시각화",".bicep 파일에서 다이어그램 생성","Azure 리소스 배포 디버깅"],"es":["Visualización de infraestructura Bicep","Generación de diagramas a partir de archivos .bicep","Depuración de implementaciones de recursos de Azure"],"fr":["Visualisation d''infrastructure Bicep","Génération de diagrammes à partir de fichiers .bicep","Débogage des déploiements de ressources Azure"],"de":["Visualisierung von Bicep-Infrastruktur","Generierung von Diagrammen aus .bicep-Dateien","Fehlerbehebung bei der Bereitstellung von Azure-Ressourcen"],"pt":["Visualizar infraestrutura Bicep","Gerar diagramas a partir de arquivos .bicep","Depurar implantações de recursos do Azure"],"ru":["Визуализация инфраструктуры Bicep","Генерация диаграмм из файлов .bicep","Отладка развертывания ресурсов Azure"],"ar":["تمثيل بنية Bicep","توليد الرسومات من ملفات .bicep","تصحيح أخطاء عمليات نشر مورد Azure"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Azure Bicep files (.bicep)","Azure-specific functionality"],"zh":["需要 Azure Bicep 文件 (.bicep)","Azure 特定功能"],"ja":["Azure Bicep ファイル (.bicep) が必要","Azure 特有の機能"],"ko":["Azure Bicep 파일 (.bicep) 필요","Azure 전용 기능"],"es":["Requiere archivos Azure Bicep (.bicep)","Funcionalidad específica de Azure"],"fr":["Nécessite des fichiers Azure Bicep (.bicep)","Fonctionnalité spécifique à Azure"],"de":["Benötigt Azure Bicep-Dateien (.bicep)","Azure-spezifische Funktionalität"],"pt":["Requer arquivos Azure Bicep (.bicep)","Funcionalidade específica do Azure"],"ru":["Требует файлов Azure Bicep (.bicep)","Функциональность, специфичная для Azure"],"ar":["يتطلب ملفات Azure Bicep (.bicep)","وظائف محددة لبروتوكول إنترنت Azure"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2/openspec-continue-change', 'community', 'gAmUssA', 'vscode-open-in-marked2', 'gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2', 'openspec-continue-change', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z', '2026-02-18T11:49:24.291Z', NULL, '{"id":"gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2/openspec-continue-change","name":"openspec-continue-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change VS Code , Marked 2.","ja":"openspec-continue-change VS Code Marked 2.","ko":"openspec-continue-change VS Code Marked 2.","es":"La extensión openspec-continue-change de VS Code permite abrir archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc en Marked 2 para continuar trabajando en un cambio.","fr":"L''extension openspec-continue-change de VS Code permet d''ouvrir des fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc dans Marked 2 pour continuer à travailler sur un changement.","de":"Die VS Code-Erweiterung openspec-continue-change ermöglicht das Öffnen von Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien in Marked 2, um an einer Änderung weiterzuarbeiten.","pt":"A extensão openspec-continue-change para VS Code permite abrir arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc no Marked 2","ru":"Расширение openspec-continue-change для VS Code позволяет открывать файлы Markdown и AsciiDoc в Marked 2","ar":"يمكّن mởension openspec-continue-change لكود من فتح ملفات ماركداون وآسكيدوك في ماركد 2","en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change VS Code ","ja":"openspec-continue-change VS Code","ko":"openspec-continue-change VS Code","es":"Extensión de VS Code para abrir Markdown y AsciiDoc","fr":"Extension VS Code pour ouvrir Markdown et AsciiDoc","de":"VS Code-Erweiterung zum Öffnen von Markdown und AsciiDoc","pt":"Extensão VS Code openspec-continue-change para Markdown","ru":"Расширение VS Code openspec-continue-change для Markdown","ar":"توسيع كود openspec-continue-change لملفات ماركداون","en":"openspec-continue-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change VS Code , Marked 2.","ja":"openspec-continue-change VS Code Marked 2.","ko":"openspec-continue-change VS Code Marked 2.","es":"La extensión openspec-continue-change de VS Code permite abrir archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc en Marked 2 para continuar trabajando en un cambio.","fr":"L''extension openspec-continue-change de VS Code permet d''ouvrir des fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc dans Marked 2 pour continuer à travailler sur un changement.","de":"Die VS Code-Erweiterung openspec-continue-change ermöglicht das Öffnen von Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien in Marked 2, um an einer Änderung weiterzuarbeiten.","pt":"A extensão openspec-continue-change para VS Code permite abrir arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc no Marked 2","ru":"Расширение openspec-continue-change для VS Code позволяет открывать файлы Markdown и AsciiDoc в Marked 2","ar":"يمكّن mởension openspec-continue-change لكود من فتح ملفات ماركداون وآسكيدوك في ماركد 2","en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"definition":{"en":"VS Code extension to open Markdown and AsciiDoc files in Marked 2"},"features":{"zh":["VS Code","Marked 2","openspec list --json","AskUserQuestion","JSON"],"ja":["VS Code","Marked 2","openspec list --json","AskUserQuestion","JSON"],"ko":["VS Code","Marked 2","openspec list --json","AskUserQuestion","JSON"],"es":["Abre archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc en Marked 2","Permite continuar trabajando en un cambio","Lista los cambios disponibles ordenados por fecha de modificación","Permite seleccionar el cambio en el que se desea trabajar","Utiliza la herramienta AskUserQuestion para seleccionar el cambio","Ejecuta el comando openspec list --json para obtener los cambios disponibles"],"fr":["Ouvre des fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc dans Marked 2","Permet de continuer à travailler sur un changement","Liste les changements disponibles classés par date de modification","Permet de sélectionner le changement sur lequel travailler","Utilise l''outil AskUserQuestion pour sélectionner le changement","Exécute la commande openspec list --json pour obtenir les changements disponibles"],"de":["Öffnet Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien in Marked 2","Ermöglicht die Fortsetzung der Arbeit an einer Änderung","Listet die verfügbaren Änderungen nach dem Datum der letzten Änderung","Ermöglicht die Auswahl der Änderung, an der gearbeitet werden soll","Verwendet das Tool AskUserQuestion zur Auswahl der Änderung","Führt den Befehl openspec list --json aus, um die verfügbaren Änderungen zu erhalten"],"pt":["Abre arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc no Marked 2","Permite continuar trabalhando em uma alteração criando o próximo artifact","Fornece uma lista de alterações disponíveis","Permite ao usuário selecionar qual alteração trabalhar","Executa o comando openspec list --json para obter alterações","Utiliza a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para perguntas ao usuário"],"ru":["Открывает файлы Markdown и AsciiDoc в Marked 2","Позволяет продолжить работу над изменением, создавая следующий артефакт","Предоставляет список доступных изменений","Позволяет пользователю выбрать, над какой изменением работать","Выполняет команду openspec list --json для получения изменений","Использует инструмент AskUserQuestion для вопросов пользователю"],"ar":["يفتح ملفات ماركداون وآسكيدوك في ماركد 2","يمكّن من الاستمرار في العمل على التعديل من خلال إنشاء الملف التالي","يقدم قائمة بالتعديلات المتاحة","يسمح للمستخدم باختيار التعديل الذي يعمل عليه","ينفذ الأمر openspec list --json للحصول على التعديلات","يستخدم أداة AskUserQuestion لطرح الأسئلة على المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["VS Code","Marked 2","openspec-continue-change","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","JSON"],"ja":["VS Code","Marked 2","openspec-continue-change","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","JSON"],"ko":["VS Code","Marked 2","openspec-continue-change","VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","JSON"],"es":["VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","openspec-continue-change","extensión de VS Code","trabajo con cambios","edición de Markdown","edición de AsciiDoc"],"fr":["VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","openspec-continue-change","extension de VS Code","travail avec des changements","édition de Markdown","édition de AsciiDoc"],"de":["VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","openspec-continue-change","VS Code-Erweiterung","Arbeit mit Änderungen","Bearbeitung von Markdown","Bearbeitung von AsciiDoc"],"pt":["VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","openspec-continue-change","extensão","desenvolvimento","programação","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["VS Code","Markdown","AsciiDoc","Marked 2","openspec-continue-change","расширение","разработка","программирование","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["كود","ماركداون","آسكيدوك","ماركد 2","openspec-continue-change","مởension","التطوير","البرمجة","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"gAmUssA","repo":"vscode-open-in-marked2","repoPath":"gAmUssA/vscode-open-in-marked2","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-continue-change","description":"Continue working on an OpenSpec change by creating the next artifact. Use when the user wants to progress their change, create the next artifact, or continue their workflow.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-","body":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-4 most recently modified changes as options, showing:\n   - Change name\n   - Schema (from `schema` field if present, otherwise \"spec-driven\")\n   - Status (e.g., \"0/5 tasks\", \"complete\", \"no tasks\")\n   - How recently it was modified (from `lastModified` field)\n\n   Mark the most recently modified change as \"(Recommended)\" since it''s likely what the user wants to continue.\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check current status**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand current state. The response includes:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow schema being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - `artifacts`: Array of artifacts with their status (\"done\", \"ready\", \"blocked\")\n   - `isComplete`: Boolean indicating if all artifacts are complete\n\n3. **Act based on status**:\n\n   ---\n\n   **If all artifacts are complete (`isComplete: true`)**:\n   - Congratulate the user\n   - Show final status including the schema used\n   - Suggest: \"All artifacts created! You can now implement this change or archive it.\"\n   - STOP\n\n   ---\n\n   **If artifacts are ready to create** (status shows artifacts with `status: \"ready\"`):\n   - Pick the FIRST artifact with `status: \"ready\"` from the status output\n   - Get its instructions:\n     ```bash\n     openspec instructions <artifact-id> --change \"<name>\" --json\n     ```\n   - Parse the JSON. The key fields are:\n     - `context`: Project background (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `rules`: Artifact-specific rules (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `template`: The structure to use for your output file\n     - `instruction`: Schema-specific guidance\n     - `outputPath`: Where to write the artifact\n     - `dependencies`: Completed artifacts to read for context\n   - **Create the artifact file**:\n     - Read any completed dependency files for context\n     - Use `template` as the structure - fill in its sections\n     - Apply `context` and `rules` as constraints when writing - but do NOT copy them into the file\n     - Write to the output path specified in instructions\n   - Show what was created and what''s now unlocked\n   - STOP after creating ONE artifact\n\n   ---\n\n   **If no artifacts are ready (all blocked)**:\n   - This shouldn''t happen with a valid schema\n   - Show status and suggest checking for issues\n\n4. **After creating an artifact, show progress**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n\n**Output**\n\nAfter each invocation, show:\n- Which artifact was created\n- Schema workflow being used\n- Current progress (N/M complete)\n- What artifacts are now unlocked\n- Prompt: \"Want to continue? Just ask me to continue or tell me what to do next.\"\n\n**Artifact Creation Guidelines**\n\nThe artifact types and their purpose depend on the schema. Use the `instruction` field from the instructions output to understand what to create.\n\nCommon artifact patterns:\n\n**spec-driven schema** (proposal → specs → design → tasks):\n- **proposal.md**: Ask user about the change if not clear. Fill in Why, What Changes, Capabilities, Impact.\n  - The Capabilities section is critical - each capability listed will need a spec file.\n- **specs/<capability>/spec.md**: Create one spec per capability listed in the proposal''s Capabilities section (use the capability name, not the change name).\n- **design.md**: Document technical decisions, architecture, and implementation approach.\n- **tasks.md**: Break down implementation into checkboxed tasks.\n\nFor other schemas, follow the `instruction` field from the CLI output.\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Create ONE artifact per invocation\n- Always read dependency artifacts before creating a new one\n- Never skip artifacts or create out of order\n- If context is unclear, ask the user before creating\n- Verify the artifact file exists after writing before marking progress\n- Use the schema''s artifact sequence, don''t assume specific artifact names\n- **IMPORTANT**: `context` and `rules` are constraints for YOU, not content for the file\n  - Do NOT copy `<context>`, `<rules>`, `<project_context>` blocks into the artifact\n  - These guide what you write, but should never appear in the output\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:49:24.291Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing seamless integration with VS Code and Marked 2 for Markdown and AsciiDoc file management.","zh":"非常适合需要与 VS Code 和 Marked 2 无缝集成的开发代理，用于管理 Markdown 和 AsciiDoc 文件。","ja":"VS Code および Marked 2 とのシームレスな統合が必要な開発エージェントに最適です。Markdown および AsciiDoc ファイルの管理に使用されます。","ko":"VS Code와 Marked 2와의无缝한統合이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 마크다운 및 AsciiDoc 파일 관리에 사용됩니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una integración sin problemas con VS Code y Marked 2 para la gestión de archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une intégration transparente avec VS Code et Marked 2 pour la gestion de fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine nahtlose Integration mit VS Code und Marked 2 für die Verwaltung von Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de integração perfeita com o VS Code e o Marked 2 para gerenciamento de arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходима бесшовная интеграция с VS Code и Marked 2 для управления файлами Markdown и AsciiDoc.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يحتاج إلى تكامل بدون مشاكل مع VS Code و Marked 2 لإدارة ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to continue working on changes by creating the next artifact, utilizing the `openspec list --json` command for available changes and the AskUserQuestion tool for user selection, all while handling Markdown and AsciiDoc files.","zh":"使代理能够继续处理更改，通过创建下一个工件，利用 `openspec list --json` 命令获取可用更改，并使用 AskUserQuestion 工具进行用户选择，同时处理 Markdown 和 AsciiDoc 文件。","ja":"エージェントが次のアーティファクトを作成して変更を続行できるようにし、`openspec list --json` コマンドを使用して利用可能な変更を取得し、AskUserQuestion ツールを使用してユーザー選択を行い、同時に Markdown および AsciiDoc ファイルを処理します。","ko":"에이전트가 다음 아티팩트를 생성하여 변경을 계속할 수 있도록 하며, `openspec list --json` 명령을 사용하여 사용 가능한 변경을 가져오고, AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자 선택을 수행하며,同時に 마크다운 및 AsciiDoc 파일을 처리합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes continuar trabajando en los cambios creando el siguiente artefacto, utilizando el comando `openspec list --json` para los cambios disponibles y la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la selección del usuario, todo mientras se manejan archivos Markdown y AsciiDoc.","fr":"Permet aux agents de continuer à travailler sur les modifications en créant le prochain artefact, en utilisant la commande `openspec list --json` pour les modifications disponibles et l''outil AskUserQuestion pour la sélection de l''utilisateur, le tout en gérant les fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, an den Änderungen weiterzuarbeiten, indem sie das nächste Artefakt erstellen, wobei sie den Befehl `openspec list --json` für verfügbare Änderungen und das Tool AskUserQuestion für die Benutzerauswahl verwenden, während sie gleichzeitig Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateien verwalten.","pt":"Permite que os agentes continuem trabalhando nas alterações criando o próximo artefato, utilizando o comando `openspec list --json` para alterações disponíveis e a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para seleção do usuário, manipulando arquivos Markdown e AsciiDoc.","ru":"Позволяет агентам продолжать работу над изменениями, создавая следующий артефакт, используя команду `openspec list --json` для доступных изменений и инструмент AskUserQuestion для выбора пользователя, при этом обрабатывая файлы Markdown и AsciiDoc.","ar":"يمكن للعميل الاستمرار في العمل على التغييرات من خلال إنشاء الملف التالي، باستخدام الأمر `openspec list --json` للتحديثات المتاحة وأداة AskUserQuestion لاختيار المستخدم، مع معالجة ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc."},"useCases":{"en":["Continuing unfinished changes","Managing Markdown files with Marked 2","Automating AsciiDoc file workflows"],"zh":["继续未完成的更改","使用 Marked 2 管理 Markdown 文件","自动化 AsciiDoc 文件工作流"],"ja":["未完了の変更の続行","Marked 2 を使用した Markdown ファイルの管理","AsciiDoc ファイルのワークフローの自動化"],"ko":["미완료 변경을 계속함","Marked 2를 사용한 마크다운 파일 관리","AsciiDoc 파일 워크플로 자동화"],"es":["Continuar cambios sin terminar","Gestionar archivos Markdown con Marked 2","Automatizar flujos de trabajo de archivos AsciiDoc"],"fr":["Continuer les modifications non terminées","Gérer les fichiers Markdown avec Marked 2","Automatiser les flux de travail de fichiers AsciiDoc"],"de":["Unvollendete Änderungen fortsetzen","Markdown-Dateien mit Marked 2 verwalten","Arbeitsabläufe für AsciiDoc-Dateien automatisieren"],"pt":["Continuar alterações incompletas","Gerenciar arquivos Markdown com o Marked 2","Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de arquivos AsciiDoc"],"ru":["Продолжить незавершенные изменения","Управлять файлами Markdown с помощью Marked 2","Автоматизировать рабочие процессы файлов AsciiDoc"],"ar":["استكمال التغييرات غير المكتملة","إدارة ملفات Markdown مع Marked 2","توفير سير عمل ملفات AsciiDoc"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires VS Code extension installation","Limited to Markdown and AsciiDoc file formats","Needs conversation context or user input for change name inference"],"zh":["需要安装 VS Code 扩展","仅限 Markdown 和 AsciiDoc 文件格式","需要对话上下文或用户输入来推断更改名称"],"ja":["VS Code 拡張機能のインストールが必要","Markdown および AsciiDoc ファイル形式のみ","変更名の推論には会話のコンテキストまたはユーザー入力が必要"],"ko":["VS Code 확장 프로그램 설치가 필요함","마크다운 및 AsciiDoc 파일 형식만 해당","변경 이름 추론을 위해 대화 문脈 또는 사용자 입력이 필요"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de la extensión de VS Code","Limitado a formatos de archivo Markdown y AsciiDoc","Necesita contexto de conversación o entrada de usuario para inferir el nombre del cambio"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de l''extension VS Code","Limité aux formats de fichiers Markdown et AsciiDoc","Nécessite un contexte de conversation ou une entrée utilisateur pour inférer le nom de la modification"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation der VS Code-Erweiterung","Begrenzt auf Markdown- und AsciiDoc-Dateiformate","Benötigt Konversationskontext oder Benutzereingabe zur Ableitung des Änderungsnamens"],"pt":["Requer instalação da extensão do VS Code","Limitado a formatos de arquivo Markdown e AsciiDoc","Necessita de contexto de conversa ou entrada do usuário para inferência de nome de alteração"],"ru":["Требует установки расширения VS Code","Ограничен форматами файлов Markdown и AsciiDoc","Требует контекста разговора или ввода пользователя для вывода имени изменений"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت ملحقات VS Code","محدود بصيغ ملفات Markdown و AsciiDoc","يحتاج إلى سياق محادثة أو إدخال المستخدم لاستنتاج اسم التغيير"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
