","Verwendung von Audio in Remotion","Detaillierte Codebeispiele"],"pt":["Crie conteúdo 3D com Three.js e React Three Fiber","Desenvolva habilidades fundamentais de animação","Importe imagens, vídeos, áudio e fontes","Aprenda a usar áudio em Remotion","Obtenha conhecimento específico do domínio"],"ru":["Создавайте 3D-контент с помощью Three.js и React Three Fiber","Разрабатывайте фундаментальные навыки анимации","Импортируйте изображения, видео, аудио и шрифты","Узнайте, как использовать аудио в Remotion","Получите домен-специфические знания"],"ar":["انشئ محتوى 3D باستخدام Three.js و React Three Fiber","طور مهارات أساسية للرسوم المتحركة","استورد الصور و الفيديوهات و الصوت و الخطوط","تعرف على كيفية استخدام الصوت في Remotion","احصل على معرفة محددة بال領域"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Remotion最佳实践","Remotion开发","Remotion代码质量","Remotion开发效率","3D内容","动画技能","音频处理","Three.js","React Three Fiber"],"ja":["Remotionベストプラクティス","Remotion開発","Remotionコードの品質","Remotion開発効率","3Dコンテンツ","アニメーションスキル","オーディオ処理","Three.js","React Three Fiber"],"ko":["Remotion 최적화 방법","Remotion 개발","Remotion 코드 품질","Remotion 개발 효율성","3D 콘텐츠","애니메이션 스킬","오디오 처리","Three.js","React Three Fiber"],"es":["Remotion","mejores prácticas","desarrollo de video","contenido personalizado","Three.js","React Three Fiber","animación","importación de activos"],"fr":["Remotion","bonnes pratiques","développement de vidéo","contenu personnalisé","Three.js","React Three Fiber","animation","importation de ressources"],"de":["Remotion","Best Practices","Videoentwicklung","personalisierter Inhalt","Three.js","React Three Fiber","Animation","Import von Ressourcen"],"pt":["Remotion","Melhores práticas","Desenvolvimento de vídeo","Three.js","React Three Fiber","Animação","Áudio","Imagens","Vídeos"],"ru":["Remotion","Лучшие практики","Разработка видео","Three.js","React Three Fiber","Анимация","Аудио","Изображения","Видео"],"ar":["Remotion","أفضل الممارسات","تطوير الفيديو","Three.js","React Three Fiber","الرسوم المتحركة","الصوت","الصور","الفيديوهات"]}},"owner":"fazlurr","repo":"video-editor","repoPath":"fazlurr/video-editor","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"remotion-best-practices","description":"Best practices for Remotion - Video creation in React","tags":"remotion, video, react, animation, composition","bodyPreview":"## When to use\n\nUse this skills whenever you are dealing with Remotion code to obtain the domain-specific knowledge.\n\n## How to use\n\nRead individual rule files for detailed explanations and code examples:\n\n- [rules/3d.md](rules/3d.md) - 3D content in Remotion using Three.js and React Three Fiber\n- [rules/animations.md](rules/animations.md) - Fundamental animation skills for Remotion\n- [rules/assets.md](rules/assets.md) - Importing images, videos, audio, and fonts into Remotion\n- [rules/audio.md]","body":"## When to use\n\nUse this skills whenever you are dealing with Remotion code to obtain the domain-specific knowledge.\n\n## How to use\n\nRead individual rule files for detailed explanations and code examples:\n\n- [rules/3d.md](rules/3d.md) - 3D content in Remotion using Three.js and React Three Fiber\n- [rules/animations.md](rules/animations.md) - Fundamental animation skills for Remotion\n- [rules/assets.md](rules/assets.md) - Importing images, videos, audio, and fonts into Remotion\n- [rules/audio.md](rules/audio.md) - Using audio and sound in Remotion - importing, trimming, volume, speed, pitch\n- [rules/calculate-metadata.md](rules/calculate-metadata.md) - Dynamically set composition duration, dimensions, and props\n- [rules/can-decode.md](rules/can-decode.md) - Check if a video can be decoded by the browser using Mediabunny\n- [rules/charts.md](rules/charts.md) - Chart and data visualization patterns for Remotion\n- [rules/compositions.md](rules/compositions.md) - Defining compositions, stills, folders, default props and dynamic metadata\n- [rules/display-captions.md](rules/display-captions.md) - Displaying captions in Remotion with TikTok-style pages and word highlighting\n- [rules/extract-frames.md](rules/extract-frames.md) - Extract frames from videos at specific timestamps using Mediabunny\n- [rules/fonts.md](rules/fonts.md) - Loading Google Fonts and local fonts in Remotion\n- [rules/get-audio-duration.md](rules/get-audio-duration.md) - Getting the duration of an audio file in seconds with Mediabunny\n- [rules/get-video-dimensions.md](rules/get-video-dimensions.md) - Getting the width and height of a video file with Mediabunny\n- [rules/get-video-duration.md](rules/get-video-duration.md) - Getting the duration of a video file in seconds with Mediabunny\n- [rules/gifs.md](rules/gifs.md) - Displaying GIFs synchronized with Remotion''s timeline\n- [rules/images.md](rules/images.md) - Embedding images in Remotion using the Img component\n- [rules/import-srt-captions.md](rules/import-srt-captions.md) - Importing .srt subtitle files into Remotion using @remotion/captions\n- [rules/lottie.md](rules/lottie.md) - Embedding Lottie animations in Remotion\n- [rules/measuring-dom-nodes.md](rules/measuring-dom-nodes.md) - Measuring DOM element dimensions in Remotion\n- [rules/measuring-text.md](rules/measuring-text.md) - Measuring text dimensions, fitting text to containers, and checking overflow\n- [rules/sequencing.md](rules/sequencing.md) - Sequencing patterns for Remotion - delay, trim, limit duration of items\n- [rules/tailwind.md](rules/tailwind.md) - Using TailwindCSS in Remotion\n- [rules/text-animations.md](rules/text-animations.md) - Typography and text animation patterns for Remotion\n- [rules/timing.md](rules/timing.md) - Interpolation curves in Remotion - linear, easing, spring animations\n- [rules/transcribe-captions.md](rules/transcribe-captions.md) - Transcribing audio to generate captions in Remotion\n- [rules/transitions.md](rules/transitions.md) - Scene transition patterns for Remotion\n- [rules/transparent-videos.md](rules/transparent-videos.md) - Rendering out a video with transparency\n- [rules/trimming.md](rules/trimming.md) - Trimming patterns for Remotion - cut the beginning or end of animations\n- [rules/videos.md](rules/videos.md) - Embedding videos in Remotion - trimming, volume, speed, looping, pitch\n- [rules/parameters.md](rules/parameters.md) - Make a video parametrizable by adding a Zod schema\n- [rules/maps.md](rules/maps.md) - Add a map using Mapbox and animate it\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:52:12.942Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Video Generation Agents needing advanced animation and 3D rendering capabilities with Remotion","zh":"非常适合需要使用 Remotion 的高级动画和 3D 渲染功能的视频生成代理","ja":"Remotion を使用した高度なアニメーションと 3D レンダリング機能を必要とするビデオ生成エージェントに最適","ko":"Remotion을 사용하는 고급 애니메이션 및 3D 렌더링 기능이 필요한 비디오 생성 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de generación de video que necesitan capacidades de animación avanzada y renderizado 3D con Remotion","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de génération de vidéo nécessitant des capacités d''animation avancée et de rendu 3D avec Remotion","de":"Perfekt für Video-Generierungsagenten, die erweiterte Animations- und 3D-Rendering-Funktionen mit Remotion benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Geração de Vídeo que precisam de capacidades avançadas de animação e renderização 3D com Remotion","ru":"Идеально для агентов генерации видео, требующих продвинутых возможностей анимации и рендеринга 3D с Remotion","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة للرسوم المتحركة وتجسيد 3D مع Remotion"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create complex animations using Three.js and React Three Fiber, import various media assets such as images, videos, and audio, and leverage domain-specific knowledge for Remotion code optimization","zh":"使代理能够使用 Three.js 和 React Three Fiber 创建复杂的动画，导入各种媒体资产，如图像、视频和音频，并利用特定领域的知识优化 Remotion 代码","ja":"Three.js と React Three Fiber を使用して複雑なアニメーションを作成し、画像、ビデオ、オーディオなどのさまざまなメディア資産をインポートし、Remotion コードの最適化のためにドメイン固有の知識を利用できるようにエージェントをEmpowerする","ko":"에이전트가 Three.js 및 React Three Fiber를 사용하여 복잡한 애니메이션을 생성하고 이미지, 비디오, 오디오 등의 다양한 미디어 자산을 가져오고 Remotion 코드 최적화를 위한 도메인 특정 지식을 활용할 수 있도록 하는 것","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear animaciones complejas utilizando Three.js y React Three Fiber, importar varios activos multimedia como imágenes, videos y audio, y aprovechar el conocimiento específico del dominio para la optimización del código Remotion","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des animations complexes en utilisant Three.js et React Three Fiber, d''importer divers actifs multimédias tels que des images, des vidéos et des fichiers audio, et de tirer parti des connaissances spécifiques au domaine pour l''optimisation du code Remotion","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, komplexe Animationen mit Three.js und React Three Fiber zu erstellen, verschiedene Medienassets wie Bilder, Videos und Audio zu importieren und domänen-spezifisches Wissen für die Optimierung des Remotion-Codes zu nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar animações complexas usando Three.js e React Three Fiber, importar vários ativos de mídia, como imagens, vídeos e áudio, e aproveitar conhecimentos específicos de domínio para otimização de código Remotion","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать сложные анимации с использованием Three.js и React Three Fiber, импортировать различные медиа-активы, такие как изображения, видео и аудио, и использовать специфические знания области для оптимизации кода Remotion","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية إنشاء رسوم متحركة معقدة باستخدام Three.js و React Three Fiber، واستيراد مختلف资产 الوسائط مثل الصور والفيديوهات والصوت، وتحقيق المعرفة المحددة للنطاق لتحسين код Remotion"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating 3D content for explainer videos","Creating smooth animations for social media clips","Importing and utilizing audio files for video soundtracks"],"zh":["为解释性视频生成 3D 内容","为社交媒体剪辑创建平滑的动画","导入和利用音频文件用于视频音轨"],"ja":["解説動画の 3D コンテンツを生成する","ソーシャルメディアクリップのスムーズなアニメーションを作成する","ビデオサウンドトラック用のオーディオファイルをインポートして利用する"],"ko":["설명 비디오를 위한 3D 콘텐츠 생성","소셜 미디어 클립을 위한 매끄러운 애니메이션 생성","비디오 사운드트랙을 위한 오디오 파일 가져오기 및 활용"],"es":["Generación de contenido 3D para videos explicativos","Creación de animaciones suaves para clips de redes sociales","Importación y utilización de archivos de audio para bandas sonoras de video"],"fr":["Génération de contenu 3D pour des vidéos explicatives","Création d''animations fluides pour des extraits de réseaux sociaux","Importation et utilisation de fichiers audio pour des bandes sonores de vidéo"],"de":["Erstellung von 3D-Inhalten für Erklärungsvideos","Erstellung von flüssigen Animationen für Social-Media-Clips","Import und Nutzung von Audio-Dateien für Video-Soundtracks"],"pt":["Geração de conteúdo 3D para vídeos explicativos","Criação de animações suaves para clipes de mídia social","Importação e utilização de arquivos de áudio para trilhas sonoras de vídeo"],"ru":["Генерация 3D-контента для объяснительных видео","Создание плавных анимаций для социальных медиа-клипов","Импорт и использование аудиофайлов для видеозаписей"],"ar":["توليد محتوى 3D لفيديوهات توضيحية","إنشاء رسوم متحركة ناعمة لمقاطع فيديو الوسائط الاجتماعية","استيراد واستخدام ملفات الصوت لتسجيلات الفيديو"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Remotion codebase access","Familiarity with Three.js and React Three Fiber necessary"],"zh":["需要访问 Remotion 代码库","需要熟悉 Three.js 和 React Three Fiber"],"ja":["Remotion コードベースへのアクセスが必要","Three.js と React Three Fiber に対する熟悉度が必要"],"ko":["Remotion 코드베이스에 대한 액세스가 필요","Three.js 및 React Three Fiber에 대한熟悉도가必要"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la base de código Remotion","Familiaridad con Three.js y React Three Fiber necesaria"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la base de code Remotion","Connaissance de Three.js et React Three Fiber nécessaire"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Remotion-Codebasis","Vertrautheit mit Three.js und React Three Fiber erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso à base de código Remotion","Familiaridade com Three.js e React Three Fiber necessária"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к базе кода Remotion","Необходимо знание Three.js и React Three Fiber"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة رمز Remotion","الضرورة لمعرفة Three.js و React Three Fiber"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('karstenheld3/SharePoint-GPT-Middleware/session-management', 'community', 'karstenheld3', 'SharePoint-GPT-Middleware', 'karstenheld3/SharePoint-GPT-Middleware', 'session-management', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z', '2026-02-18T11:52:04.142Z', NULL, '{"id":"karstenheld3/SharePoint-GPT-Middleware/session-management","name":"session-management","description":{"zh":"Azure Web App 会话管理是一种 Python 应用，用于爬取 SharePoint 站点内容到 OpenAI Vector Stores。它实现了会话跟踪和阶段管理","ja":"Azure Web App セッション管理は、SharePoint サイトのコンテンツを OpenAI Vector Stores にクロールする Python アプリケーションです。セッション追跡とフェーズ管理を実現します","ko":"Azure Web App 세션 관리는 SharePoint 사이트의 내용을 OpenAI Vector Stores로 크롤링하는 Python 애플리케이션입니다. 세션 추적 및 단계 관리를 구현합니다","es":"La gestión de sesiones es crucial para Azure Web App en Python, permitiendo el seguimiento de fases y la administración de contenido de SharePoint","fr":"La gestion de sessions est essentielle pour Azure Web App en Python, permettant le suivi de phases et la gestion de contenu de SharePoint","de":"Die Sitzungsverwaltung ist für Azure Web App in Python von entscheidender Bedeutung, um Phasen zu verfolgen und SharePoint-Inhalte zu verwalten","pt":"O gerenciamento de sessão é uma técnica para rastrear fases de EDIRD em um aplicativo web Azure em Python","ru":"Управление сессиями - это техника для отслеживания фаз EDIRD в веб-приложении Azure на Python","ar":"إدارة الجلسات هي تقنية لتتبع مراحل EDIRD في تطبيق ويب Azure باستخدام Python","en":"An Azure Web App in Python to crawl the content of SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Azure Web App 会话管理","ja":"Azure Web App セッション管理","ko":"Azure Web App 세션 관리","es":"Gestión de Sesiones para Azure Web App en Python","fr":"Gestion de Sessions pour Azure Web App en Python","de":"Sitzungsverwaltung für Azure Web App in Python","pt":"Gerenciamento de Sessão em Azure com Python","ru":"Управление сессиями в Azure с помощью Python","ar":"إدارة الجلسات في Azure باستخدام Python","en":"session-management"},"description":{"zh":"Azure Web App 会话管理是一种 Python 应用，用于爬取 SharePoint 站点内容到 OpenAI Vector Stores。它实现了会话跟踪和阶段管理","ja":"Azure Web App セッション管理は、SharePoint サイトのコンテンツを OpenAI Vector Stores にクロールする Python アプリケーションです。セッション追跡とフェーズ管理を実現します","ko":"Azure Web App 세션 관리는 SharePoint 사이트의 내용을 OpenAI Vector Stores로 크롤링하는 Python 애플리케이션입니다. 세션 추적 및 단계 관리를 구현합니다","es":"La gestión de sesiones es crucial para Azure Web App en Python, permitiendo el seguimiento de fases y la administración de contenido de SharePoint","fr":"La gestion de sessions est essentielle pour Azure Web App en Python, permettant le suivi de phases et la gestion de contenu de SharePoint","de":"Die Sitzungsverwaltung ist für Azure Web App in Python von entscheidender Bedeutung, um Phasen zu verfolgen und SharePoint-Inhalte zu verwalten","pt":"O gerenciamento de sessão é uma técnica para rastrear fases de EDIRD em um aplicativo web Azure em Python","ru":"Управление сессиями - это техника для отслеживания фаз EDIRD в веб-приложении Azure на Python","ar":"إدارة الجلسات هي تقنية لتتبع مراحل EDIRD في تطبيق ويب Azure باستخدام Python","en":"An Azure Web App in Python to crawl the content of SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores"},"definition":{"en":"An Azure Web App in Python to crawl the content of SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores"},"features":{"zh":["会话跟踪","阶段管理","SharePoint 站点内容爬取","OpenAI Vector Stores 集成","Python 应用"],"ja":["セッション追跡","フェーズ管理","SharePoint サイトのコンテンツクロール","OpenAI Vector Stores 統合","Python アプリケーション"],"ko":["세션 추적","단계 관리","SharePoint 사이트의 내용 크롤링","OpenAI Vector Stores 통합","Python 애플리케이션"],"es":["Seguimiento de fases de procesos","Administración de contenido de SharePoint","Integración con OpenAI Vector Stores","Gestión de carpetas de sesiones","Rastreo de progreso y estado de las sesiones"],"fr":["Suivi de phases de processus","Gestion de contenu de SharePoint","Intégration avec OpenAI Vector Stores","Gestion de dossiers de sessions","Rastreage de progrès et d''état des sessions"],"de":["Verfolgung von Phasen von Prozessen","Verwaltung von SharePoint-Inhalten","Integration mit OpenAI Vector Stores","Verwaltung von Sitzungsordnern","Verfolgung von Fortschritt und Status von Sitzungen"],"pt":["Rastreamento de fases de EDIRD","Gerenciamento de pastas de sessão","Criação de arquivos NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md e PROGRESS.md","Suporte a override de pastas de sessão","Integração com lojas de vetores OpenAI"],"ru":["Отслеживание фаз EDIRD","Управление папками сессий","Создание файлов NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md и PROGRESS.md","Поддержка переопределения папок сессий","Интеграция с хранилищами векторов OpenAI"],"ar":["تتبع مراحل EDIRD","إدارة مجلدات الجلسات","إنشاء ملفات NOTES.md و PROBLEMS.md و PROGRESS.md","دعم إعادة تعريف مجلدات الجلسات","التكامل مع مخازن متجهات OpenAI"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Azure Web App","会话管理","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","Python 应用","会话跟踪","阶段管理"],"ja":["Azure Web App","セッション管理","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","Python アプリケーション","セッション追跡","フェーズ管理"],"ko":["Azure Web App","세션 관리","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","Python 애플리케이션","세션 추적","단계 관리"],"es":["gestión de sesiones","Azure Web App","Python","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","desarrollo web","administración de contenido"],"fr":["gestion de sessions","Azure Web App","Python","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","développement web","gestion de contenu"],"de":["Sitzungsverwaltung","Azure Web App","Python","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","Webentwicklung","Inhaltsverwaltung"],"pt":["gerenciamento de sessão","Azure Web App","Python","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","EDIRD","rastreamento de fases"],"ru":["управление сессиями","Azure Web App","Python","SharePoint","Хранилища векторов OpenAI","EDIRD","отслеживание фаз"],"ar":["إدارة الجلسات","تطبيق ويب Azure","Python","SharePoint","مخازن متجهات OpenAI","EDIRD","تتبع المراحل"]}},"owner":"karstenheld3","repo":"SharePoint-GPT-Middleware","repoPath":"karstenheld3/SharePoint-GPT-Middleware","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"session-management","description":"Apply when initializing, saving, resuming, or closing a work session","bodyPreview":"# Session Management Guide\n\n## Phase Tracking\n\nSessions track EDIRD phases:\n- NOTES.md: \"Current Phase\" section with phase, last verb, gate status\n- PROGRESS.md: \"Phase Plan\" section with 5 phases and status\n\n## MUST-NOT-FORGET\n\n- Session folder location: `[DEFAULT_SESSIONS_FOLDER]/_YYYY-MM-DD_[SessionTopicCamelCase]/`\n- Default: `[DEFAULT_SESSIONS_FOLDER]` = `[WORKSPACE_FOLDER]` (override in `!NOTES.md`)\n- Required files: NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md\n- Lifecycle: Init → Work → Save → Resu","body":"# Session Management Guide\n\n## Phase Tracking\n\nSessions track EDIRD phases:\n- NOTES.md: \"Current Phase\" section with phase, last verb, gate status\n- PROGRESS.md: \"Phase Plan\" section with 5 phases and status\n\n## MUST-NOT-FORGET\n\n- Session folder location: `[DEFAULT_SESSIONS_FOLDER]/_YYYY-MM-DD_[SessionTopicCamelCase]/`\n- Default: `[DEFAULT_SESSIONS_FOLDER]` = `[WORKSPACE_FOLDER]` (override in `!NOTES.md`)\n- Required files: NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md\n- Lifecycle: Init → Work → Save → Resume → Finalize → Archive\n- Sync session PROBLEMS.md to project on /session-finalize\n- Phase tracking: NOTES.md has current phase, PROGRESS.md has full phase plan\n- **STOP after session init**: After creating session files, STOP and wait for user review. Do NOT implement session goal until explicitly requested. User must review and refine goals before work begins.\n\n## Session Lifecycle\n\n1. **Init** (`/session-new`): Create session folder with tracking files\n2. **Work**: Create specs, plans, implement, track progress\n3. **Save** (`/session-save`): Document findings, commit changes\n4. **Resume** (`/session-load`): Re-read session documents, continue work\n5. **Finalize** (`/session-finalize`): Sync findings to project files, prepare for archive\n\n## Session Folder Location\n\n**Base:** `[DEFAULT_SESSIONS_FOLDER]` (default: `[WORKSPACE_FOLDER]`, can be overridden in `!NOTES.md`)\n\n**Format:** `[DEFAULT_SESSIONS_FOLDER]/_YYYY-MM-DD_[SessionTopicCamelCase]/`\n\n**Example:** `_PrivateSessions/_2026-01-12_FixAuthenticationBug/`\n\n## Required Session Files\n\nUse templates from this skill folder:\n\n- **NOTES.md** (`NOTES_TEMPLATE.md`): Key information, agent instructions, working patterns, large initial prompts (>120 tokens)\n- **PROBLEMS.md** (`PROBLEMS_TEMPLATE.md`): All problems to be addressed - initial prompts, questions, feature requests, bugs, strange behavior, investigation topics. Each problem gets a unique ID and tracks status (Open/Resolved/Deferred)\n- **PROGRESS.md** (`PROGRESS_TEMPLATE.md`): Task execution tracking - to-do list, done items, tried-but-not-used approaches\n\n**Key distinction:**\n- **NOTES.md** = Context and reference information (static knowledge)\n- **PROBLEMS.md** = All topics requiring attention (dynamic problem list with IDs)\n- **PROGRESS.md** = Task execution status (what''s being worked on)\n\n## Assumed Workflow\n\n```\n1. INIT: User initializes session (`/session-new`)\n   └── Session folder, NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md created\n\n2. PREPARE (one of):\n   A) User prepares work manually\n      └── Creates INFO / SPEC / IMPL documents, tracks progress\n   B) User explains problem, agent assists\n      └── Updates Problems, Progress, Notes → researches → creates documents\n\n3. WORK: User or agent implements\n   └── Makes decisions, creates tests, implements, verifies\n   └── Progress and findings tracked continuously\n\n4. SAVE: User saves session for later (`/session-save`)\n   └── Everything updated and committed\n\n5. RESUME: User resumes session (`/session-load`)\n   └── Agent primes from session files, executes workflows in Notes\n   └── Continue with steps 2-3\n\n6. FINALIZE: User finalizes session (`/session-finalize`)\n   └── Everything updated, committed, synced to project/workspace\n\n7. ARCHIVE: User archives session\n   └── Session folder moved to _Archive/\n```\n\n## ID System\n\nSee `[AGENT_FOLDER]/rules/devsystem-ids.md` rule (always-on) for complete ID system.\n\n**Quick Reference:**\n- Document: `[TOPIC]-[DOC][NN]` (IN, SP, IP, TP)\n  - Example: `CRWL-SP01`, `AUTH-IP01`\n- Tracking: `[TOPIC]-[TYPE]-[NNN]` (BG = Bug, FT = Feature, PR = Problem, FX = Fix, TK = Task)\n  - Example: `SAP-BG-001`, `UI-PR-003`, `GLOB-TK-015`\n- Topic Registry: Maintained in project NOTES.md\n\n## Session Init Template\n\n### NOTES.md\n```markdown\n# Session Notes\n\n## Session Info\n- **Started**: [DATE]\n- **Goal**: [Brief description]\n\n## Key Decisions\n\n## Important Findings\n\n## Workflows to Run on Resume\n```\n\n### PROBLEMS.md\n```markdown\n# Session Problems\n\n## Open\n\n## Resolved\n\n## Deferred\n```\n\n### PROGRESS.md\n```markdown\n# Session Progress\n\n## To Do\n\n## In Progress\n\n## Done\n\n## Tried But Not Used\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:52:04.142Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Azure-focused AI Agents requiring advanced SharePoint content crawling and OpenAI Vector Store integration","zh":"Ideal for Azure-focused AI Agents requiring advanced SharePoint content crawling and OpenAI Vector Store integration","ja":"Ideal for Azure-focused AI Agents requiring advanced SharePoint content crawling and OpenAI Vector Store integration","ko":"Ideal for Azure-focused AI Agents requiring advanced SharePoint content crawling and OpenAI Vector Store integration","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial centrados en Azure que requieren un rastreo avanzado de contenido de SharePoint y una integración con OpenAI Vector Store","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle axés sur Azure nécessitant un crawling avancé de contenu SharePoint et une intégration avec OpenAI Vector Store","de":"Ideal für Azure-fokussierte KI-Agents, die ein erweitertes SharePoint-Inhalts-Crawling und eine OpenAI Vector Store-Integration erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA focados no Azure que requerem crawling de conteúdo avançado do SharePoint e integração com o OpenAI Vector Store","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на Azure, требующих продвинутого поиска контента SharePoint и интеграции с OpenAI Vector Store","ar":"مثالية لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يركز على Azure والذي يتطلب تبويب محتوى متقدم من SharePoint وتكامل مع مخزن OpenAI Vector"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to efficiently track EDIRD phases, manage session folders, and crawl SharePoint site content into OpenAI Vector Stores using Python, leveraging phase tracking and lifecycle management through NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, and PROGRESS.md files","zh":"Empowers agents to efficiently track EDIRD phases, manage session folders, and crawl SharePoint site content into OpenAI Vector Stores using Python, leveraging phase tracking and lifecycle management through NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, and PROGRESS.md files","ja":"Empowers agents to efficiently track EDIRD phases, manage session folders, and crawl SharePoint site content into OpenAI Vector Stores using Python, leveraging phase tracking and lifecycle management through NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, and PROGRESS.md files","ko":"Empowers agents to efficiently track EDIRD phases, manage session folders, and crawl SharePoint site content into OpenAI Vector Stores using Python, leveraging phase tracking and lifecycle management through NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, and PROGRESS.md files","es":"Permite a los agentes realizar un seguimiento eficiente de las fases de EDIRD, gestionar carpetas de sesión y rastrear el contenido del sitio de SharePoint en OpenAI Vector Stores mediante Python, aprovechando el seguimiento de fases y la gestión del ciclo de vida a través de archivos NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md y PROGRESS.md","fr":"Permet aux agents de suivre efficacement les phases EDIRD, de gérer les dossiers de session et de crawler le contenu du site SharePoint dans OpenAI Vector Stores à l''aide de Python, en exploitant le suivi des phases et la gestion du cycle de vie via les fichiers NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md et PROGRESS.md","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, EDIRD-Phasen effizient zu verfolgen, Sitzungsordner zu verwalten und SharePoint-Site-Inhalte in OpenAI Vector Stores mithilfe von Python zu crawlen, indem Phasenverfolgung und Lebenszyklusverwaltung durch NOTES.md-, PROBLEMS.md- und PROGRESS.md-Dateien genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a acompanharem de forma eficiente as fases do EDIRD, gerenciar pastas de sessão e fazer crawling de conteúdo do site do SharePoint para lojas de vetores OpenAI usando Python, aproveitando o acompanhamento de fases e gerenciamento de ciclo de vida por meio de arquivos NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md e PROGRESS.md","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью эффективно отслеживать фазы EDIRD, управлять папками сеанса и выполнять поиск контента сайта SharePoint в хранилища векторов OpenAI с помощью Python, используя отслеживание фаз и управление жизненным циклом через файлы NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md и PROGRESS.md","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تتبع مراحل EDIRD بفعالية، وإدارة مجلدات الجلسة، وتبويب محتوى موقع SharePoint إلى مخازن OpenAI Vector باستخدام Python، واستخدام تتبع المراحل وإدارة دورة الحياة من خلال ملفات NOTES.md و PROBLEMS.md و PROGRESS.md"},"useCases":{"en":["Tracking EDIRD phases for optimized workflow","Crawling SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores for enhanced data analysis","Managing session folders with automated lifecycle support"],"zh":["Tracking EDIRD phases for optimized workflow","Crawling SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores for enhanced data analysis","Managing session folders with automated lifecycle support"],"ja":["Tracking EDIRD phases for optimized workflow","Crawling SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores for enhanced data analysis","Managing session folders with automated lifecycle support"],"ko":["Tracking EDIRD phases for optimized workflow","Crawling SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores for enhanced data analysis","Managing session folders with automated lifecycle support"],"es":["Seguimiento de fases de EDIRD para un flujo de trabajo optimizado","Crawling de sitios de SharePoint en OpenAI Vector Stores para un análisis de datos mejorado","Gestión de carpetas de sesión con soporte de ciclo de vida automatizado"],"fr":["Suivi des phases EDIRD pour un workflow optimisé","Crawling de sites SharePoint dans OpenAI Vector Stores pour une analyse de données améliorée","Gestion des dossiers de session avec un support de cycle de vie automatisé"],"de":["Verfolgung von EDIRD-Phasen für einen optimierten Workflow","Crawling von SharePoint-Sites in OpenAI Vector Stores für eine verbesserte Datenanalyse","Verwaltung von Sitzungsordnern mit automatisiertem Lebenszyklus-Unterstützung"],"pt":["Acompanhamento de fases do EDIRD para fluxo de trabalho otimizado","Crawling de sites do SharePoint para lojas de vetores OpenAI para análise de dados aprimorada","Gerenciamento de pastas de sessão com suporte de ciclo de vida automatizado"],"ru":["Отслеживание фаз EDIRD для оптимизированного потока работы","Поиск контента сайта SharePoint в хранилища векторов OpenAI для улучшенного анализа данных","Управление папками сеанса с автоматизированной поддержкой жизненного цикла"],"ar":["تتبع مراحل EDIRD من أجل تحسين تدفق العمل","تبويب محتوى موقع SharePoint إلى مخازن OpenAI Vector لتحليل بيانات محسّن","إدارة مجلدات الجلسة مع دعم دورة الحياة التلقائي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Azure Web App setup","Dependent on OpenAI Vector Stores integration","Specific file structure and naming conventions mandatory (NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md)"],"zh":["Requires Azure Web App setup","Dependent on OpenAI Vector Stores integration","Specific file structure and naming conventions mandatory (NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md)"],"ja":["Requires Azure Web App setup","Dependent on OpenAI Vector Stores integration","Specific file structure and naming conventions mandatory (NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md)"],"ko":["Requires Azure Web App setup","Dependent on OpenAI Vector Stores integration","Specific file structure and naming conventions mandatory (NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md)"],"es":["Requiere configuración de Azure Web App","Dependiente de la integración con OpenAI Vector Stores","Estructura de archivo y convenciones de nomenclatura específicas obligatorias (NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md)"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration d''Azure Web App","Dépendante de l''intégration avec OpenAI Vector Stores","Structure de fichier et conventions de nommage spécifiques obligatoires (NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md)"],"de":["Erfordert Azure Web App-Setup","Abhängig von der OpenAI Vector Stores-Integration","Spezifische Dateistruktur und Benennungskonventionen obligatorisch (NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md)"],"pt":["Requer configuração do Azure Web App","Dependente da integração com lojas de vetores OpenAI","Estrutura de arquivo e convenções de nomenclatura específicas são obrigatórias (NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md)"],"ru":["Требуется настройка веб-приложения Azure","Зависит от интеграции с хранилищами векторов OpenAI","Конкретная структура файла и соглашения об именовании являются обязательными (NOTES.md, PROBLEMS.md, PROGRESS.md)"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد تطبيق الويب في Azure","يعتمد على تكامل مخازن OpenAI Vector","بناء ملف معين وتوافق اسمي إلزامية (NOTES.md و PROBLEMS.md و PROGRESS.md)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('congwa/embedease-ai/image-compress', 'community', 'congwa', 'embedease-ai', 'congwa/embedease-ai', 'image-compress', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z', '2026-02-18T11:52:06.037Z', NULL, '{"id":"congwa/embedease-ai/image-compress","name":"image-compress","description":{"zh":"图像压缩工具是一个帮助开发者优化图片文件大小的工具，支持多种图片格式。通过压缩图片文件，可以提高网页加载速度和用户体验","ja":"画像圧縮ツールは、開発者が画像ファイルのサイズを最適化するのを助けるツールで、複数の画像形式をサポートしています。画像ファイルを圧縮することで、Webページの読み込み速度とユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させることができます","ko":"이미지 압축 도구는 개발자가 이미지 파일 크기를 최적화하는 것을 도와주는 도구로, 여러 가지 이미지 형식을 지원합니다. 이미지 파일을 압축함으로써 웹 페이지 로딩 속도와 사용자 경험을 개선할 수 있습니다","es":"Nuestra herramienta de compresión de imágenes utiliza inteligencia artificial para reducir el tamaño de las imágenes sin perder calidad.","fr":"Notre outil de compression d''images utilise l''intelligence artificielle pour réduire la taille des images sans perdre de qualité.","de":"Unser Bildkomprimierungstool verwendet künstliche Intelligenz, um die Größe von Bildern zu reduzieren, ohne die Qualität zu beeinträchtigen.","pt":"A compressão de imagem é uma técnica para reduzir o tamanho dos arquivos de imagem, melhorando a velocidade do site e a experiência do usuário.","ru":"Сжатие изображений - это техника для уменьшения размера файлов изображений, улучшающая скорость сайта и пользовательский опыт.","ar":"ضغط الصور هو تقنية لتقليل حجم ملفات الصور، مما يحسن سرعة الموقع وتجربة المستخدم.","en":"一款开箱即用的 AI 智能客服系统，人工客服，客户转化"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"图像压缩工具 - 优化图片文件大小","ja":"画像圧縮ツール - 画像ファイルのサイズを最適化","ko":"이미지 압축 도구 - 이미지 파일 크기 최적화","es":"Comprimir imágenes con inteligencia artificial","fr":"Compresser des images avec l''intelligence artificielle","de":"Bildkomprimierung mit künstlicher Intelligenz","pt":"Compressão de Imagem para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Сжатие изображений для разработчиков","ar":"ضغط الصور للمطورين","en":"image-compress"},"description":{"zh":"图像压缩工具是一个帮助开发者优化图片文件大小的工具，支持多种图片格式。通过压缩图片文件，可以提高网页加载速度和用户体验","ja":"画像圧縮ツールは、開発者が画像ファイルのサイズを最適化するのを助けるツールで、複数の画像形式をサポートしています。画像ファイルを圧縮することで、Webページの読み込み速度とユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させることができます","ko":"이미지 압축 도구는 개발자가 이미지 파일 크기를 최적화하는 것을 도와주는 도구로, 여러 가지 이미지 형식을 지원합니다. 이미지 파일을 압축함으로써 웹 페이지 로딩 속도와 사용자 경험을 개선할 수 있습니다","es":"Nuestra herramienta de compresión de imágenes utiliza inteligencia artificial para reducir el tamaño de las imágenes sin perder calidad.","fr":"Notre outil de compression d''images utilise l''intelligence artificielle pour réduire la taille des images sans perdre de qualité.","de":"Unser Bildkomprimierungstool verwendet künstliche Intelligenz, um die Größe von Bildern zu reduzieren, ohne die Qualität zu beeinträchtigen.","pt":"A compressão de imagem é uma técnica para reduzir o tamanho dos arquivos de imagem, melhorando a velocidade do site e a experiência do usuário.","ru":"Сжатие изображений - это техника для уменьшения размера файлов изображений, улучшающая скорость сайта и пользовательский опыт.","ar":"ضغط الصور هو تقنية لتقليل حجم ملفات الصور، مما يحسن سرعة الموقع وتجربة المستخدم.","en":"一款开箱即用的 AI 智能客服系统，人工客服，客户转化"},"definition":{"en":"一款开箱即用的 AI 智能客服系统，人工客服，客户转化"},"features":{"zh":["支持avif、webp、png、jpg等图片格式","自动检测和压缩超过100KB的图片文件","推荐格式优先级：avif > webp > png > jpg","macOS内置sips工具支持","命令行工具支持"],"ja":["avif、webp、png、jpgなどの画像形式をサポート","100KBを超える画像ファイルを自動で検出して圧縮","形式の優先順位：avif > webp > png > jpg","macOS内蔵のsipsツールをサポート","コマンドラインツールをサポート"],"ko":["avif, webp, png, jpg 등 이미지 형식 지원","100KB 이상의 이미지 파일 자동检测 및 압축","형식 우선 순위：avif > webp > png > jpg","macOS 내장 sips 도구 지원","명령줄 도구 지원"],"es":["Compresión de imágenes sin pérdida de calidad","Soporte para múltiples formatos de imagen","Optimización para web y dispositivos móviles","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo","Análisis de imágenes y recomendaciones de compresión"],"fr":["Compression d''images sans perte de qualité","Prise en charge de plusieurs formats d''image","Optimisation pour le web et les appareils mobiles","Intégration avec des outils de développement","Analyse d''images et recommandations de compression"],"de":["Bildkomprimierung ohne Qualitätsverlust","Unterstützung für mehrere Bildformate","Optimierung für Web und mobile Geräte","Integration mit Entwicklungstools","Bildanalyse und Komprimierungsempfehlungen"],"pt":["Reduz o tamanho dos arquivos de imagem","Melhora a velocidade do site","Otimiza a experiência do usuário","Suporta formatos de imagem como avif, webp, png e jpg","Fornece comando para verificar imagens com tamanho superior a 100KB"],"ru":["Уменьшает размер файлов изображений","Улучшает скорость сайта","Оптимизирует пользовательский опыт","Поддерживает форматы изображений như avif, webp, png и jpg","Предоставляет команду для проверки изображений с размером больше 100КБ"],"ar":["يقلل من حجم ملفات الصور","يحسن سرعة الموقع","يحسن تجربة المستخدم","يدعم صيغ الصور مثل avif و webp و png و jpg","يوفر أمرًا للتحقق من الصور بأحجام أكبر من 100KB"]},"keywords":{"zh":["图像压缩","图片优化","网页加载速度","用户体验","avif","webp","png","jpg"],"ja":["画像圧縮","画像最適化","Webページ読み込み速度","ユーザーエクスペリエンス","avif","webp","png","jpg"],"ko":["이미지 압축","이미지 최적화","웹 페이지 로딩 속도","사용자 경험","avif","webp","png","jpg"],"es":["compresión de imágenes","inteligencia artificial","optimización de imágenes","desarrollo web","diseño gráfico","formatos de imagen","calidad de imagen","tamaño de archivo"],"fr":["compression d''images","intelligence artificielle","optimisation d''images","développement web","conception graphique","formats d''image","qualité d''image","taille de fichier"],"de":["Bildkomprimierung","künstliche Intelligenz","Bildoptimierung","Webentwicklung","Grafikdesign","Bildformate","Bildqualität","Dateigröße"],"pt":["compressão de imagem","otimização de imagem","velocidade do site","experiência do usuário","formatos de imagem","avif","webp","png","jpg"],"ru":["сжатие изображений","оптимизация изображений","скорость сайта","пользовательский опыт","форматы изображений","avif","webp","png","jpg"],"ar":["ضغط الصور","تحسين الصور","سرعة الموقع","تجربة المستخدم","صيغ الصور","avif","webp","png","jpg"]}},"owner":"congwa","repo":"embedease-ai","repoPath":"congwa/embedease-ai","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"image-compress","description":"图片压缩检查规则。当添加或修改 README 引用的图片时自动触发。检查图片是否超过 100KB，超出则压缩。推荐使用 avif/webp 格式。触发场景：添加新图片到仓库、更新 README 中的截图、发版前检查。","bodyPreview":"# Image Compress\n\nREADME 引用的图片不得超过 **100KB**。\n\n## 检查规则\n\n1. 扫描 README.md 中所有 `![](path)` 引用的图片文件\n2. 检查每个文件大小，超过 100KB 的必须压缩\n3. 推荐格式优先级：**avif > webp > png > jpg**\n\n## 检查命令\n\n```bash\n# 查找 docs/ 和 images/ 下超过 100KB 的图片\nfind docs/ images/ -type f \\( -name \"*.png\" -o -name \"*.jpg\" -o -name \"*.jpeg\" -o -name \"*.webp\" -o -name \"*.avif\" -o -name \"*.gif\" \\) -size +100k\n```\n\n## 压缩方式\n\n### macOS 内置 sips（png/jpg）\n\n```bash\n# 缩小尺寸（保持宽度 1200px 以内）\nsips --resampleWidth 1200 image.png\n\n# 转为 jpg 并降低质量\nsips -s forma","body":"# Image Compress\n\nREADME 引用的图片不得超过 **100KB**。\n\n## 检查规则\n\n1. 扫描 README.md 中所有 `![](path)` 引用的图片文件\n2. 检查每个文件大小，超过 100KB 的必须压缩\n3. 推荐格式优先级：**avif > webp > png > jpg**\n\n## 检查命令\n\n```bash\n# 查找 docs/ 和 images/ 下超过 100KB 的图片\nfind docs/ images/ -type f \\( -name \"*.png\" -o -name \"*.jpg\" -o -name \"*.jpeg\" -o -name \"*.webp\" -o -name \"*.avif\" -o -name \"*.gif\" \\) -size +100k\n```\n\n## 压缩方式\n\n### macOS 内置 sips（png/jpg）\n\n```bash\n# 缩小尺寸（保持宽度 1200px 以内）\nsips --resampleWidth 1200 image.png\n\n# 转为 jpg 并降低质量\nsips -s format jpeg -s formatOptions 80 image.png --out image.jpg\n```\n\n### ffmpeg（推荐，支持 avif/webp）\n\n```bash\n# png → avif（推荐，体积最小）\nffmpeg -i input.png -c:v libaom-av1 -crf 30 -still-picture 1 output.avif\n\n# png → webp\nffmpeg -i input.png -quality 80 output.webp\n\n# 批量转换\nfor f in docs/screenshots/*.png; do\n  ffmpeg -i \"$f\" -c:v libaom-av1 -crf 30 -still-picture 1 \"${f%.png}.avif\"\ndone\n```\n\n### 使用 scripts/check_compress.sh\n\n```bash\nbash .windsurf/skills/image-compress/scripts/check_compress.sh\n```\n\n## 压缩后\n\n1. 更新 README.md 中的图片路径（扩展名可能变化）\n2. 删除旧的大图片文件\n3. 确认所有图片 < 100KB\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:52:06.037Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing optimized image compression for web deployment, such as Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code.","zh":"适合需要优化图像压缩以部署到网络的AI代理，例如Cursor、Windsurf或Claude Code。","ja":"Webへのデプロイのために最適化された画像圧縮が必要なAIエージェント、たとえばCursor、Windsurf、またはClaude Codeに適しています。","ko":"웹 배포를 위한 최적화된 이미지 압축이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. 예를 들어 Cursor, Windsurf 또는 Claude Code와 같은 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan una compresión de imagen optimizada para la implementación web, como Cursor, Windsurf o Claude Code.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA qui nécessitent une compression d''image optimisée pour le déploiement web, tels que Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die eine optimierte Bildkomprimierung für die Webbereitstellung benötigen, wie z. B. Cursor, Windsurf oder Claude Code.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de compressão de imagem otimizada para implantação na web, como Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым требуется оптимизированная сжатие изображений для веб-развертывания, таких как Cursor, Windsurf или Claude Code.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى ضغط صورة محسّن لتنفيذ الويب، مثل Cursor أو Windsurf أو Claude Code."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to compress images using avif, webp, png, and jpg formats, ensuring files are under 100KB for efficient web loading, utilizing tools like sips for macOS and command-line scripts for file size checks.","zh":"使代理能够使用avif、webp、png和jpg格式压缩图像，确保文件大小在100KB以下，以实现高效的Web加载，利用macOS上的sips工具和命令行脚本进行文件大小检查。","ja":"エージェントがavif、webp、png、jpg形式で画像を圧縮することを可能にし、ファイルサイズが100KB以下になるようにして効率的なWebロードを実現します。macOSのsipsツールやファイルサイズのチェック用のコマンドラインスクリプトなどを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 avif, webp, png, jpg 형식으로 이미지를 압축할 수 있도록 하여 파일 크기가 100KB 이하로 유지되어 웹 로딩이 효율적으로 수행되도록 합니다. macOS의 sips 도구 및 파일 크기 체크를 위한 명령줄 스크립트等을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a comprimir imágenes utilizando formatos avif, webp, png y jpg, asegurando que los archivos tengan un tamaño inferior a 100KB para una carga web eficiente, utilizando herramientas como sips para macOS y scripts de línea de comandos para comprobar el tamaño de archivo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de compresser les images en utilisant les formats avif, webp, png et jpg, en garantissant que les fichiers sont inférieurs à 100 Ko pour un chargement web efficace, en utilisant des outils comme sips pour macOS et des scripts de ligne de commande pour vérifier la taille des fichiers.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Bilder mithilfe der Formate avif, webp, png und jpg zu komprimieren, wodurch sichergestellt wird, dass Dateien kleiner als 100 KB für eine effiziente Webladung sind, unter Verwendung von Tools wie sips für macOS und Befehlszeilen-Skripten für Dateigrößenprüfungen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a comprimir imagens usando formatos avif, webp, png e jpg, garantindo que os arquivos estejam abaixo de 100KB para carregamento eficiente na web, utilizando ferramentas como sips para macOS e scripts de linha de comando para verificações de tamanho de arquivo.","ru":"Позволяет агентам сжимать изображения с использованием форматов avif, webp, png и jpg, гарантируя, что файлы находятся ниже 100 КБ для эффективной загрузки веб-страниц, используя инструменты như sips для macOS и командные сценарии для проверки размера файла.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من ضغط الصور باستخدام صيغ avif و webp و png و jpg، مما يضمن أن تكون الملفات أقل من 100KB للتحميل الفعال على الويب، باستخدام أدوات مثل sips لنظام macOS وبرامج سطر الأوامر لفحص حجم الملف."},"useCases":{"en":["Compressing README images for GitHub repositories","Optimizing website images for faster page loading","Converting image formats for web compatibility"],"zh":["压缩GitHub仓库的README图像","优化网站图像以加快页面加载","转换图像格式以实现Web兼容性"],"ja":["GitHubリポジトリのREADME画像を圧縮する","Webサイトの画像を最適化してページロードを高速化する","Webとの互換性を確保するために画像形式を変換する"],"ko":["GitHub 저장소의 README 이미지 압축","웹 사이트 이미지 최적화하여 페이지 로딩 속도提高","웹 호환성을 위해 이미지 형식 변환"],"es":["Comprimir imágenes de README para repositorios de GitHub","Optimizar imágenes de sitios web para una carga de páginas más rápida","Convertir formatos de imagen para la compatibilidad web"],"fr":["Compresser les images de README pour les référentiels GitHub","Optimiser les images de sites web pour un chargement de pages plus rapide","Convertir les formats d''image pour la compatibilité web"],"de":["Komprimieren von README-Bildern für GitHub-Repositorys","Optimieren von Website-Bildern für ein schnelleres Seitenladen","Umwandeln von Bildformaten für die Webkompatibilität"],"pt":["Comprimir imagens de README para repositórios GitHub","Otimizar imagens de sites para carregamento de página mais rápido","Converter formatos de imagem para compatibilidade com a web"],"ru":["Сжатие изображений README для репозиториев GitHub","Оптимизация изображений сайта для более быстрой загрузки страниц","Преобразование форматов изображений для веб-совместимости"],"ar":["ضغط صور README لمخازن GitHub","تحسين صور الموقع للتحميل السريع للصفحة","تحويل صيغ الصورة للتوافق مع الويب"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires macOS for sips command","Limited to specific image formats (avif, webp, png, jpg, gif)","File size limit of 100KB"],"zh":["需要macOS来运行sips命令","仅限于特定的图像格式（avif、webp、png、jpg、gif）","文件大小限制为100KB"],"ja":["sipsコマンドを実行するにはmacOSが必要","特定の画像形式（avif、webp、png、jpg、gif）のみに対応","ファイルサイズの制限は100KB"],"ko":["sips 명령을 실행하기 위해 macOS가 필요","특정 이미지 형식(avif, webp, png, jpg, gif)만 지원","파일 크기 제한은 100KB"],"es":["Requiere macOS para el comando sips","Limitado a formatos de imagen específicos (avif, webp, png, jpg, gif)","Límite de tamaño de archivo de 100KB"],"fr":["Nécessite macOS pour la commande sips","Limité à des formats d''image spécifiques (avif, webp, png, jpg, gif)","Limite de taille de fichier de 100 Ko"],"de":["Benötigt macOS für den sips-Befehl","Begrenzt auf bestimmte Bildformate (avif, webp, png, jpg, gif)","Dateigrößenbegrenzung von 100 KB"],"pt":["Requer macOS para comando sips","Limitado a formatos de imagem específicos (avif, webp, png, jpg, gif)","Limite de tamanho de arquivo de 100KB"],"ru":["Требуется macOS для команды sips","Ограничен до определенных форматов изображений (avif, webp, png, jpg, gif)","Ограничение размера файла 100 КБ"],"ar":["يتطلب نظام macOS للأمر sips","محدود لصيغ الصورة المحددة (avif و webp و png و jpg و gif)","حجم ملف محدود ب 100KB"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ollieb89/ml_challenges/postgresql-table-design', 'community', 'ollieb89', 'ml_challenges', 'ollieb89/ml_challenges', 'postgresql-table-design', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z', '2026-02-18T11:52:04.815Z', NULL, '{"id":"ollieb89/ml_challenges/postgresql-table-design","name":"postgresql-table-design","description":{"zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计是数据库性能优化的关键。通过定义主键、规范化和反规范化等最佳实践，开发人员可以设计出高效的表结构","ja":"PostgreSQL テーブル設計はデータベースのパフォーマンスを最適化するための重要な要素です。開発者はベストプラクティスに従って効率的なテーブルを設計できます","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 디자인은 데이터베이스 성능 최적화를 위한 핵심 요소입니다. 개발자는 기본 키 정의, 정규화 및 반정규화 등 최선의 방법을 따라 효율적인 테이블을 디자인할 수 있습니다","es":"El diseño de tablas en PostgreSQL requiere una comprensión profunda de las reglas de normalización y denormalización para optimizar el rendimiento","fr":"La conception de tableaux en PostgreSQL nécessite une compréhension approfondie des règles de normalisation et de dénormalisation pour optimiser les performances","de":"Das Tabellendesign in PostgreSQL erfordert ein tiefes Verständnis der Normalisierungs- und Denormalisierungsregeln zur Optimierung der Leistung","pt":"O projeto de tabela PostgreSQL envolve a definição de chaves primárias e a normalização de dados para garantir a eficiência.","ru":"Проектирование таблиц PostgreSQL включает определение первичных ключей и нормализацию данных для обеспечения эффективности.","ar":"يتضمن تصميم جدول PostgreSQL تعريف المفاتيح الرئيسية وتنظيم البيانات لضمان الفعالية.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计最佳实践","ja":"PostgreSQL テーブル設計のベストプラクティス","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 디자인 가이드","es":"Diseño de Tablas PostgreSQL: Mejores Prácticas","fr":"Conception de Tableaux PostgreSQL: Règles de Base","de":"PostgreSQL-Tabellendesign: Kernregeln","pt":"Projeto de Tabela PostgreSQL: Melhores Práticas","ru":"Проектирование таблиц PostgreSQL: лучшие практики","ar":"تصميم جدول PostgreSQL: أفضل الممارسات","en":"postgresql-table-design"},"description":{"zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计是数据库性能优化的关键。通过定义主键、规范化和反规范化等最佳实践，开发人员可以设计出高效的表结构","ja":"PostgreSQL テーブル設計はデータベースのパフォーマンスを最適化するための重要な要素です。開発者はベストプラクティスに従って効率的なテーブルを設計できます","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 디자인은 데이터베이스 성능 최적화를 위한 핵심 요소입니다. 개발자는 기본 키 정의, 정규화 및 반정규화 등 최선의 방법을 따라 효율적인 테이블을 디자인할 수 있습니다","es":"El diseño de tablas en PostgreSQL requiere una comprensión profunda de las reglas de normalización y denormalización para optimizar el rendimiento","fr":"La conception de tableaux en PostgreSQL nécessite une compréhension approfondie des règles de normalisation et de dénormalisation pour optimiser les performa...","de":"Das Tabellendesign in PostgreSQL erfordert ein tiefes Verständnis der Normalisierungs- und Denormalisierungsregeln zur Optimierung der Leistung","pt":"O projeto de tabela PostgreSQL envolve a definição de chaves primárias e a normalização de dados para garantir a eficiência.","ru":"Проектирование таблиц PostgreSQL включает определение первичных ключей и нормализацию данных для обеспечения эффективности.","ar":"يتضمن تصميم جدول PostgreSQL تعريف المفاتيح الرئيسية وتنظيم البيانات لضمان الفعالية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["定义主键","规范化和反规范化","使用 BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","使用 UUID 保证全局唯一性","优化数据读取性能"],"ja":["プライマリーキーを定義する","正規化と反正規化","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY を使用する","UUID を使用してグローバル一意性を保証する","データ読み取りパフォーマンスを最適化する"],"ko":["기본 키 정의","정규화 및 반정규화","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY 사용","UUID 사용하여 글로벌 고유성 보장","데이터 읽기 성능 최적화"],"es":["Definir claves primarias para tablas de referencia","Normalizar datos para eliminar redundancias","Denormalizar datos para mejorar el rendimiento de lectura","Utilizar BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY para claves primarias","Utilizar UUID para garantizar la unicidad global"],"fr":["Définir des clés primaires pour les tableaux de référence","Normaliser les données pour éliminer les redondances","Dénormaliser les données pour améliorer les performances de lecture","Utiliser BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY pour les clés primaires","Utiliser UUID pour garantir l''unicité globale"],"de":["Definieren von Primärschlüsseln für Referenztabelle","Normalisieren von Daten zur Beseitigung von Redundanz","Denormalisieren von Daten zur Verbesserung der Leseleistung","Verwenden von BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY für Primärschlüssel","Verwenden von UUID zur Gewährleistung der globalen Eindeutigkeit"],"pt":["Definição de chaves primárias","Normalização de dados","Denormalização para melhor desempenho","Uso de BIGINT e UUID","Otimização de consultas","Melhores práticas para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Определение первичных ключей","Нормализация данных","Денормализация для лучшей производительности","Использование BIGINT и UUID","Оптимизация запросов","Лучшие практики для разработчиков"],"ar":["تعريف المفاتيح الرئيسية","تنظيم البيانات","التنظيم غير الطبيعي لتحسين الأداء","استخدام BIGINT و UUID","تحسين الاستفسارات","أفضل الممارسات للمطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PostgreSQL 表设计","数据库性能优化","主键定义","规范化","反规范化","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID"],"ja":["PostgreSQL テーブル設計","データベースパフォーマンス最適化","プライマリーキー定義","正規化","反正規化","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID"],"ko":["PostgreSQL 테이블 디자인","데이터베이스 성능 최적화","기본 키 정의","정규화","반정규화","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID"],"es":["diseño de tablas postgresql","normalización de datos","denormalización de datos","claves primarias","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","optimización de rendimiento"],"fr":["conception de tableaux postgresql","normalisation de données","dénormalisation de données","clés primaires","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","optimisation des performances"],"de":["Tabellendesign postgresql","Normalisierung von Daten","Denormalisierung von Daten","Primärschlüssel","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","Leistungsoptimierung"],"pt":["projeto de tabela postgresql","desenvolvimento de banco de dados","normalização de dados","denormalização","chaves primárias","BIGINT","UUID","otimização de consultas"],"ru":["проектирование таблиц postgresql","разработка базы данных","нормализация данных","денормализация","первичные ключи","BIGINT","UUID","оптимизация запросов"],"ar":["تصميم جدول postgresql","تطوير قاعدة البيانات","تنظيم البيانات","التنظيم غير الطبيعي","المفاتيح الرئيسية","BIGINT","UUID","تحسين الاستفسارات"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"ml_challenges","repoPath":"ollieb89/ml_challenges","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"postgresql-table-design","description":"Design a PostgreSQL-specific schema. Covers best-practices, data types, indexing, constraints, performance patterns, and advanced features","bodyPreview":"# PostgreSQL Table Design \n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Define a **PRIMARY KEY** for reference tables (users, orders, etc.). Not always needed for time-series/event/log data. When used, prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`; use `UUID` only when global uniqueness/opacity is needed.\n- **Normalize first (to 3NF)** to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies; denormalize **only** for measured, high-ROI reads where join performance is proven problematic. Premature denormalization creates maintenan","body":"# PostgreSQL Table Design \n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Define a **PRIMARY KEY** for reference tables (users, orders, etc.). Not always needed for time-series/event/log data. When used, prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`; use `UUID` only when global uniqueness/opacity is needed.\n- **Normalize first (to 3NF)** to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies; denormalize **only** for measured, high-ROI reads where join performance is proven problematic. Premature denormalization creates maintenance burden.\n- Add **NOT NULL** everywhere it’s semantically required; use **DEFAULT**s for common values.\n- Create **indexes for access paths you actually query**: PK/unique (auto), **FK columns (manual!)**, frequent filters/sorts, and join keys.\n- Prefer **TIMESTAMPTZ** for event time; **NUMERIC** for money; **TEXT** for strings; **BIGINT** for integer values, **DOUBLE PRECISION** for floats (or `NUMERIC` for exact decimal arithmetic).\n\n## PostgreSQL “Gotchas”\n\n- **Identifiers**: unquoted → lowercased. Avoid quoted/mixed-case names. Convention: use `snake_case` for table/column names.\n- **Unique + NULLs**: UNIQUE allows multiple NULLs. Use `UNIQUE (...) NULLS NOT DISTINCT` (PG15+) to restrict to one NULL.\n- **FK indexes**: PostgreSQL **does not** auto-index FK columns. Add them.\n- **No silent coercions**: length/precision overflows error out (no truncation). Example: inserting 999 into `NUMERIC(2,0)` fails with error, unlike some databases that silently truncate or round.\n- **Sequences/identity have gaps** (normal; don''t \"fix\"). Rollbacks, crashes, and concurrent transactions create gaps in ID sequences (1, 2, 5, 6...). This is expected behavior—don''t try to make IDs consecutive.\n- **Heap storage**: no clustered PK by default (unlike SQL Server/MySQL InnoDB); `CLUSTER` is one-off reorganization, not maintained on subsequent inserts. Row order on disk is insertion order unless explicitly clustered.\n- **MVCC**: updates/deletes leave dead tuples; vacuum handles them—design to avoid hot wide-row churn.\n\n## Data Types\n\n- **IDs**: `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY` preferred (`GENERATED BY DEFAULT` also fine); `UUID` when merging/federating/used in a distributed system or for opaque IDs. Generate with `uuidv7()` (preferred if using PG18+) or `gen_random_uuid()` (if using an older PG version).\n- **Integers**: prefer `BIGINT` unless storage space is critical; `INTEGER` for smaller ranges; avoid `SMALLINT` unless constrained.\n- **Floats**: prefer `DOUBLE PRECISION` over `REAL` unless storage space is critical. Use `NUMERIC` for exact decimal arithmetic.\n- **Strings**: prefer `TEXT`; if length limits needed, use `CHECK (LENGTH(col) <= n)` instead of `VARCHAR(n)`; avoid `CHAR(n)`. Use `BYTEA` for binary data. Large strings/binary (>2KB default threshold) automatically stored in TOAST with compression. TOAST storage: `PLAIN` (no TOAST), `EXTENDED` (compress + out-of-line), `EXTERNAL` (out-of-line, no compress), `MAIN` (compress, keep in-line if possible). Default `EXTENDED` usually optimal. Control with `ALTER TABLE tbl ALTER COLUMN col SET STORAGE strategy` and `ALTER TABLE tbl SET (toast_tuple_target = 4096)` for threshold. Case-insensitive: for locale/accent handling use non-deterministic collations; for plain ASCII use expression indexes on `LOWER(col)` (preferred unless column needs case-insensitive PK/FK/UNIQUE) or `CITEXT`.\n- **Money**: `NUMERIC(p,s)` (never float).\n- **Time**: `TIMESTAMPTZ` for timestamps; `DATE` for date-only; `INTERVAL` for durations. Avoid `TIMESTAMP` (without timezone). Use `now()` for transaction start time, `clock_timestamp()` for current wall-clock time.\n- **Booleans**: `BOOLEAN` with `NOT NULL` constraint unless tri-state values are required.\n- **Enums**: `CREATE TYPE ... AS ENUM` for small, stable sets (e.g. US states, days of week). For business-logic-driven and evolving values (e.g. order statuses) → use TEXT (or INT) + CHECK or lookup table.\n- **Arrays**: `TEXT[]`, `INTEGER[]`, etc. Use for ordered lists where you query elements. Index with **GIN** for containment (`@>`, `<@`) and overlap (`&&`) queries. Access: `arr[1]` (1-indexed), `arr[1:3]` (slicing). Good for tags, categories; avoid for relations—use junction tables instead. Literal syntax: `''{val1,val2}''` or `ARRAY[val1,val2]`.\n- **Range types**: `daterange`, `numrange`, `tstzrange` for intervals. Support overlap (`&&`), containment (`@>`), operators. Index with **GiST**. Good for scheduling, versioning, numeric ranges. Pick a bounds scheme and use it consistently; prefer `[)` (inclusive/exclusive) by default.\n- **Network types**: `INET` for IP addresses, `CIDR` for network ranges, `MACADDR` for MAC addresses. Support network operators (`<<`, `>>`, `&&`).\n- **Geometric types**: `POINT`, `LINE`, `POLYGON`, `CIRCLE` for 2D spatial data. Index with **GiST**. Consider **PostGIS** for advanced spatial features.\n- **Text search**: `TSVECTOR` for full-text search documents, `TSQUERY` for search queries. Index `tsvector` with **GIN**. Always specify language: `to_tsvector(''english'', col)` and `to_tsquery(''english'', ''query'')`. Never use single-argument versions. This applies to both index expressions and queries.\n- **Domain types**: `CREATE DOMAIN email AS TEXT CHECK (VALUE ~ ''^[^@]+@[^@]+$'')` for reusable custom types with validation. Enforces constraints across tables.\n- **Composite types**: `CREATE TYPE address AS (street TEXT, city TEXT, zip TEXT)` for structured data within columns. Access with `(col).field` syntax.\n- **JSONB**: preferred over JSON; index with **GIN**. Use only for optional/semi-structured attrs. ONLY use JSON if the original ordering of the contents MUST be preserved.\n- **Vector types**: `vector` type by `pgvector` for vector similarity search for embeddings.\n\n\n### Do not use the following data types\n- DO NOT use `timestamp` (without time zone); DO use `timestamptz` instead.\n- DO NOT use `char(n)` or `varchar(n)`; DO use `text` instead.\n- DO NOT use `money` type; DO use `numeric` instead.\n- DO NOT use `timetz` type; DO use `timestamptz` instead.\n- DO NOT use `timestamptz(0)` or any other precision specification; DO use `timestamptz` instead\n- DO NOT use `serial` type; DO use `generated always as identity` instead.\n\n\n## Table Types\n\n- **Regular**: default; fully durable, logged.\n- **TEMPORARY**: session-scoped, auto-dropped, not logged. Faster for scratch work.\n- **UNLOGGED**: persistent but not crash-safe. Faster writes; good for caches/staging.\n\n## Row-Level Security\n\nEnable with `ALTER TABLE tbl ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`. Create policies: `CREATE POLICY user_access ON orders FOR SELECT TO app_users USING (user_id = current_user_id())`. Built-in user-based access control at the row level.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **PK**: implicit UNIQUE + NOT NULL; creates a B-tree index.\n- **FK**: specify `ON DELETE/UPDATE` action (`CASCADE`, `RESTRICT`, `SET NULL`, `SET DEFAULT`). Add explicit index on referencing column—speeds up joins and prevents locking issues on parent deletes/updates. Use `DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED` for circular FK dependencies checked at transaction end.\n- **UNIQUE**: creates a B-tree index; allows multiple NULLs unless `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` (PG15+). Standard behavior: `(1, NULL)` and `(1, NULL)` are allowed. With `NULLS NOT DISTINCT`: only one `(1, NULL)` allowed. Prefer `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` unless you specifically need duplicate NULLs.\n- **CHECK**: row-local constraints; NULL values pass the check (three-valued logic). Example: `CHECK (price > 0)` allows NULL prices. Combine with `NOT NULL` to enforce: `price NUMERIC NOT NULL CHECK (price > 0)`.\n- **EXCLUDE**: prevents overlapping values using operators. `EXCLUDE USING gist (room_id WITH =, booking_period WITH &&)` prevents double-booking rooms. Requires appropriate index type (often GiST).\n\n## Indexing\n\n- **B-tree**: default for equality/range queries (`=`, `<`, `>`, `BETWEEN`, `ORDER BY`)\n- **Composite**: order matters—index used if equality on leftmost prefix (`WHERE a = ? AND b > ?` uses index on `(a,b)`, but `WHERE b = ?` does not). Put most selective/frequently filtered columns first.\n- **Covering**: `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (id) INCLUDE (name, email)` - includes non-key columns for index-only scans without visiting table.\n- **Partial**: for hot subsets (`WHERE status = ''active''` → `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (user_id) WHERE status = ''active''`). Any query with `status = ''active''` can use this index.\n- **Expression**: for computed search keys (`CREATE INDEX ON tbl (LOWER(email))`). Expression must match exactly in WHERE clause: `WHERE LOWER(email) = ''user@example.com''`.\n- **GIN**: JSONB containment/existence, arrays (`@>`, `?`), full-text search (`@@`)\n- **GiST**: ranges, geometry, exclusion constraints\n- **BRIN**: very large, naturally ordered data (time-series)—minimal storage overhead. Effective when row order on disk correlates with indexed column (insertion order or after `CLUSTER`).\n\n## Partitioning\n\n- Use for very large tables (>100M rows) where queries consistently filter on partition key (often time/date).\n- Alternate use: use for tables where data maintenance tasks dictates e.g. data pruned or bulk replaced periodically\n- **RANGE**: common for time-series (`PARTITION BY RANGE (created_at)`). Create partitions: `CREATE TABLE logs_2024_01 PARTITION OF logs FOR VALUES FROM (''2024-01-01'') TO (''2024-02-01'')`. **TimescaleDB** automates time-based or ID-based partitioning with retention policies and compression.\n- **LIST**: for discrete values (`PARTITION BY LIST (region)`). Example: `FOR VALUES IN (''us-east'', ''us-west'')`.\n- **HASH**: for even distribution when no natural key (`PARTITION BY HASH (user_id)`). Creates N partitions with modulus.\n- **Constraint exclusion**: requires `CHECK` constraints on partitions for query planner to prune. Auto-created for declarative partitioning (PG10+).\n- Prefer declarative partitioning or hypertables. Do NOT use table inheritance.\n- **Limitations**: no global UNIQUE constraints—include partition key in PK/UNIQUE. FKs from partitioned tables not supported; use triggers.\n\n## Special Considerations\n\n### Update-Heavy Tables\n\n- **Separate hot/cold columns**—put frequently updated columns in separate table to minimize bloat.\n- **Use `fillfactor=90`** to leave space for HOT updates that avoid index maintenance.\n- **Avoid updating indexed columns**—prevents beneficial HOT updates.\n- **Partition by update patterns**—separate frequently updated rows in a different partition from stable data.\n\n### Insert-Heavy Workloads\n\n- **Minimize indexes**—only create what you query; every index slows inserts.\n- **Use `COPY` or multi-row `INSERT`** instead of single-row inserts.\n- **UNLOGGED tables** for rebuildable staging data—much faster writes.\n- **Defer index creation** for bulk loads—>drop index, load data, recreate indexes.\n- **Partition by time/hash** to distribute load. **TimescaleDB** automates partitioning and compression of insert-heavy data.\n- **Use a natural key for primary key** such as a (timestamp, device_id) if enforcing global uniqueness is important many insert-heavy tables don''t need a primary key at all.\n- If you do need a surrogate key, **Prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY` over `UUID`**.\n\n### Upsert-Friendly Design\n\n- **Requires UNIQUE index** on conflict target columns—`ON CONFLICT (col1, col2)` needs exact matching unique index (partial indexes don''t work).\n- **Use `EXCLUDED.column`** to reference would-be-inserted values; only update columns that actually changed to reduce write overhead.\n- **`DO NOTHING` faster** than `DO UPDATE` when no actual update needed.\n\n### Safe Schema Evolution\n\n- **Transactional DDL**: most DDL operations can run in transactions and be rolled back—`BEGIN; ALTER TABLE...; ROLLBACK;` for safe testing.\n- **Concurrent index creation**: `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` avoids blocking writes but can''t run in transactions.\n- **Volatile defaults cause rewrites**: adding `NOT NULL` columns with volatile defaults (e.g., `now()`, `gen_random_uuid()`) rewrites entire table. Non-volatile defaults are fast.\n- **Drop constraints before columns**: `ALTER TABLE DROP CONSTRAINT` then `DROP COLUMN` to avoid dependency issues.\n- **Function signature changes**: `CREATE OR REPLACE` with different arguments creates overloads, not replacements. DROP old version if no overload desired.\n\n## Generated Columns\n\n- `... GENERATED ALWAYS AS (<expr>) STORED` for computed, indexable fields. PG18+ adds `VIRTUAL` columns (computed on read, not stored).\n\n## Extensions\n\n- **`pgcrypto`**: `crypt()` for password hashing.\n- **`uuid-ossp`**: alternative UUID functions; prefer `pgcrypto` for new projects.\n- **`pg_trgm`**: fuzzy text search with `%` operator, `similarity()` function. Index with GIN for `LIKE ''%pattern%''` acceleration.\n- **`citext`**: case-insensitive text type. Prefer expression indexes on `LOWER(col)` unless you need case-insensitive constraints.\n- **`btree_gin`/`btree_gist`**: enable mixed-type indexes (e.g., GIN index on both JSONB and text columns).\n- **`hstore`**: key-value pairs; mostly superseded by JSONB but useful for simple string mappings.\n- **`timescaledb`**: essential for time-series—automated partitioning, retention, compression, continuous aggregates.\n- **`postgis`**: comprehensive geospatial support beyond basic geometric types—essential for location-based applications.\n- **`pgvector`**: vector similarity search for embeddings.\n- **`pgaudit`**: audit logging for all database activity.\n\n## JSONB Guidance\n\n- Prefer `JSONB` with **GIN** index.\n- Default: `CREATE INDEX ON tbl USING GIN (jsonb_col);` → accelerates:\n  - **Containment** `jsonb_col @> ''{\"k\":\"v\"}''`\n  - **Key existence** `jsonb_col ? ''k''`, **any/all keys** `?\\|`, `?&`\n  - **Path containment** on nested docs\n  - **Disjunction** `jsonb_col @> ANY(ARRAY[''{\"status\":\"active\"}'', ''{\"status\":\"pending\"}''])`\n- Heavy `@>` workloads: consider opclass `jsonb_path_ops` for smaller/faster containment-only indexes:\n  - `CREATE INDEX ON tbl USING GIN (jsonb_col jsonb_path_ops);`\n  - **Trade-off**: loses support for key existence (`?`, `?|`, `?&`) queries—only supports containment (`@>`)\n- Equality/range on a specific scalar field: extract and index with B-tree (generated column or expression):\n  - `ALTER TABLE tbl ADD COLUMN price INT GENERATED ALWAYS AS ((jsonb_col->>''price'')::INT) STORED;`\n  - `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (price);`\n  - Prefer queries like `WHERE price BETWEEN 100 AND 500` (uses B-tree) over `WHERE (jsonb_col->>''price'')::INT BETWEEN 100 AND 500` without index.\n- Arrays inside JSONB: use GIN + `@>` for containment (e.g., tags). Consider `jsonb_path_ops` if only doing containment.\n- Keep core relations in tables; use JSONB for optional/variable attributes.\n- Use constraints to limit allowed JSONB values in a column e.g. `config JSONB NOT NULL CHECK(jsonb_typeof(config) = ''object'')`\n\n\n## Examples\n\n### Users\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  user_id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,\n  email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX ON users (LOWER(email));\nCREATE INDEX ON users (created_at);\n```\n\n### Orders\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  order_id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,\n  user_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(user_id),\n  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''PENDING'' CHECK (status IN (''PENDING'',''PAID'',''CANCELED'')),\n  total NUMERIC(10,2) NOT NULL CHECK (total > 0),\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX ON orders (user_id);\nCREATE INDEX ON orders (created_at);\n```\n\n### JSONB\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE profiles (\n  user_id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES users(user_id),\n  attrs JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT ''{}'',\n  theme TEXT GENERATED ALWAYS AS (attrs->>''theme'') STORED\n);\nCREATE INDEX profiles_attrs_gin ON profiles USING GIN (attrs);\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:52:04.815Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Database Administration Agents needing advanced PostgreSQL table design capabilities.","zh":"适合需要高级PostgreSQL表设计能力的数据库管理代理。","ja":"PostgreSQLの高度なテーブル設計機能を必要とするデータベース管理エージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 PostgreSQL 테이블 설계 기능이 필요한 데이터베이스 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Administración de Base de Datos que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de diseño de tablas de PostgreSQL.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Administration de Base de Données ayant besoin de capacités avancées de conception de tableaux PostgreSQL.","de":"Perfekt für Datenbank-Administrations-Agents, die erweiterte PostgreSQL-Tabellendesignfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Administração de Banco de Dados que precisam de capacidades avançadas de design de tabelas PostgreSQL.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов администрирования баз данных, которым требуются расширенные возможности проектирования таблиц PostgreSQL.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل إدارة قاعدة البيانات التي تحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتصميم جداول PostgreSQL."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define efficient PRIMARY KEYs using BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, normalize tables to 3NF, and denormalize for high-ROI reads, all while leveraging PostgreSQL''s UUID for global uniqueness when necessary.","zh":"赋予代理定义使用BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY的高效主键、将表规范化为3NF以及针对高投资回报率读取进行反规范化的能力，同时在必要时利用PostgreSQL的UUID实现全局唯一性。","ja":"エージェントがBIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITYを使用した効率的な主キーを定義し、テーブルを3NFに正規化し、高投資回報率の読み取りのために反正規化することを可能にし、必要に応じてPostgreSQLのUUIDを使用して世界的に一意の識別子を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY를 사용하여 효율적인 기본 키를 정의하고, 테이블을 3NF로 정규화하고, 높은 투자 수익률의 읽기 위해 비정규화를 수행하며, 필요에 따라 PostgreSQL의 UUID를 사용하여 전역 고유성을 보장하는 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a definir PRIMARY KEYs eficientes utilizando BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, normalizar tablas a 3NF y desnormalizar para lecturas de alta rentabilidad, todo mientras aprovecha el UUID de PostgreSQL para la unicidad global cuando sea necesario.","fr":"Permet aux agents de définir des PRIMARY KEYs efficaces en utilisant BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, normaliser les tableaux à 3NF et dénormaliser pour des lectures à rendement élevé, le tout en exploitant l''UUID de PostgreSQL pour l''unicité globale lorsque nécessaire.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, effiziente PRIMARY KEYs mithilfe von BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY zu definieren, Tabellen auf 3NF zu normalisieren und für hochrentable Lesevorgänge zu denormalisieren, und zwar unter Ausnutzung der UUID von PostgreSQL für globale Eindeutigkeit wenn notwendig.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a definirem chaves primárias eficientes usando BIGINT GERADO SEMPRE COMO IDENTIDADE, normalizar tabelas para 3NF e desnormalizar para leituras de alto ROI, tudo isso aproveitando o UUID do PostgreSQL para unicidade global quando necessário.","ru":"Позволяет агентам определять эффективные первичные ключи с использованием BIGINT СГЕНЕРИРОВАННОГО ВСЕГДА КАК ИДЕНТИЧНОСТЬ, нормализовать таблицы до 3НФ и денормализовать для чтений с высокой отдачей от инвестиций, все это при использовании UUID PostgreSQL для глобальной уникальности при необходимости.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تعريف المفاتيح الرئيسية الفعالة باستخدام BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY، وتنظيم الجداول إلى 3NF، وتنظيم غير عادي للقراءات عالية العائد على الاستثمار، مع استخدام UUID من PostgreSQL للفردية العالمية عند الحاجة."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing normalized tables to eliminate data redundancy","Denormalizing tables for measured, high-ROI reads","Defining PRIMARY KEYs for reference tables using BIGINT or UUID"],"zh":["为消除数据冗余而设计规范化表","为了获得测量的高投资回报率读取而反规范化表","使用BIGINT或UUID为引用表定义主键"],"ja":["データの冗長性を排除するために正規化されたテーブルを設計する","測定された高投資回報率の読み取りのために反正規化されたテーブルを設計する","BIGINTまたはUUIDを使用して参照テーブルの主キーを定義する"],"ko":["데이터 중복을 제거하기 위해 정규화된 테이블을 설계하는 것","측정된 높은 투자 수익률의 읽기 위해 비정규화된 테이블을 설계하는 것","BIGINT 또는 UUID를 사용하여 참조 테이블의 기본 키를 정의하는 것"],"es":["Diseñar tablas normalizadas para eliminar la redundancia de datos","Desnormalizar tablas para lecturas de alta rentabilidad medidas","Definir PRIMARY KEYs para tablas de referencia utilizando BIGINT o UUID"],"fr":["Concevoir des tableaux normalisés pour éliminer la redondance des données","Dénormaliser les tableaux pour des lectures à rendement élevé mesurées","Définir des PRIMARY KEYs pour les tableaux de référence en utilisant BIGINT ou UUID"],"de":["Entwerfen normalisierter Tabellen, um Datenredundanz zu eliminieren","Denormalisieren von Tabellen für gemessene, hochrentable Lesevorgänge","Definieren von PRIMARY KEYs für Referenztabelle mit BIGINT oder UUID"],"pt":["Projetar tabelas normalizadas para eliminar a redundância de dados","Desnormalizar tabelas para leituras medidas de alto ROI","Definir chaves primárias para tabelas de referência usando BIGINT ou UUID"],"ru":["Проектировать нормализованные таблицы для устранения избыточности данных","Денормализовать таблицы для измеренных чтений с высокой отдачей от инвестиций","Определить первичные ключи для таблиц ссылок, используя BIGINT или UUID"],"ar":["تصميم جداول منضبطة لإزالة التكرار البيانات","التنظيم غير العادي للجداول للقراءات المقاسة عالية العائد على الاستثمار","تحديد المفاتيح الرئيسية للجداول المرجعية باستخدام BIGINT أو UUID"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of database normalization and denormalization trade-offs","PostgreSQL-specific syntax and features"],"zh":["需要理解数据库规范化和反规范化的权衡","PostgreSQL特有的语法和功能"],"ja":["データベースの正規化と反正規化のトレードオフを理解する必要がある","PostgreSQL固有の構文と機能"],"ko":["데이터베이스 정규화와 비정규화의 트레이드 오프를 이해해야 함","PostgreSQL 고유의 구문과 기능"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los trade-offs de normalización y desnormalización de bases de datos","Sintaxis y características específicas de PostgreSQL"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des compromis entre normalisation et dénormalisation des bases de données","Syntaxe et fonctionnalités spécifiques à PostgreSQL"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für Kompromisse bei Datenbanknormalisierung und -denormalisierung","PostgreSQL-spezifische Syntax und Funktionen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das compensações da normalização e desnormalização de banco de dados","Sintaxe e recursos específicos do PostgreSQL"],"ru":["Требует понимания компромиссов между нормализацией и денормализацией базы данных","Синтаксис и функции, специфичные для PostgreSQL"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم التضحيات بين التنظيم والتنظيم غير العادي لقاعدة البيانات","بناء الجملة والميزات الخاصة ببرنامج PostgreSQL"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
