 de desempenho para vídeos personalizados","Melhores práticas para desenvolvedores Remotion"],"ru":["Создание 3D-контента с помощью Three.js и React Three Fiber","Основные анимации для Remotion","Импорт изображений, видео, аудио и шрифтов","Оптимизация производительности для персонализированных видеороликов","Лучшие практики для разработчиков Remotion"],"ar":["إنشاء محتوى 3D باستخدام Three.js و React Three Fiber","الرسوم المتحركة الأساسية لبرموشن","استيراد الصور والفيديو والصوت والخطوط","تحسين الأداء لمقاطع الفيديو المخصصة","أفضل الممارسات للمطورين برموشن"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Remotion","Remotion最佳实践","3D内容","动画","资产处理","音频处理","代码优化"],"ja":["Remotion","Remotionベストプラクティス","3Dコンテンツ","アニメーション","資産処理","オーディオ処理","コード最適化"],"ko":["Remotion","Remotion 최적화 방법","3D 콘텐츠","애니메이션","자산 처리","오디오 처리","코드 최적화"],"es":["Remotion","mejores prácticas","desarrollo de video","Three.js","React Three Fiber","animaciones","importación de assets","audio en Remotion"],"fr":["Remotion","meilleures pratiques","développement de vidéos","Three.js","React Three Fiber","animations","importation de ressources","audio dans Remotion"],"de":["Remotion","Best Practices","Videentwicklung","Three.js","React Three Fiber","Animationen","Importieren von Ressourcen","Audio in Remotion"],"pt":["Remotion","Melhores práticas","Desenvolvimento de vídeos","3D","Animações","Importação de ativos","Otimização de desempenho","Vídeos personalizados"],"ru":["Remotion","Лучшие практики","Разработка видеороликов","3D","Анимации","Импорт активов","Оптимизация производительности","Персонализированные видеоролики"],"ar":["Remotion","أفضل الممارسات","تطوير مقاطع الفيديو","3D","الرسوم المتحركة","استيراد الأصول","تحسين الأداء","مقاطع الفيديو المخصصة"]}},"owner":"a-billet","repo":"oslo-remotion","repoPath":"a-billet/oslo-remotion","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"remotion-best-practices","description":"Best practices for Remotion - Video creation in React","tags":"remotion, video, react, animation, composition","bodyPreview":"## When to use\n\nUse this skills whenever you are dealing with Remotion code to obtain the domain-specific knowledge.\n\n## How to use\n\nRead individual rule files for detailed explanations and code examples:\n\n- [rules/3d.md](rules/3d.md) - 3D content in Remotion using Three.js and React Three Fiber\n- [rules/animations.md](rules/animations.md) - Fundamental animation skills for Remotion\n- [rules/assets.md](rules/assets.md) - Importing images, videos, audio, and fonts into Remotion\n- [rules/audio.md]","body":"## When to use\n\nUse this skills whenever you are dealing with Remotion code to obtain the domain-specific knowledge.\n\n## How to use\n\nRead individual rule files for detailed explanations and code examples:\n\n- [rules/3d.md](rules/3d.md) - 3D content in Remotion using Three.js and React Three Fiber\n- [rules/animations.md](rules/animations.md) - Fundamental animation skills for Remotion\n- [rules/assets.md](rules/assets.md) - Importing images, videos, audio, and fonts into Remotion\n- [rules/audio.md](rules/audio.md) - Using audio and sound in Remotion - importing, trimming, volume, speed, pitch\n- [rules/calculate-metadata.md](rules/calculate-metadata.md) - Dynamically set composition duration, dimensions, and props\n- [rules/can-decode.md](rules/can-decode.md) - Check if a video can be decoded by the browser using Mediabunny\n- [rules/charts.md](rules/charts.md) - Chart and data visualization patterns for Remotion\n- [rules/compositions.md](rules/compositions.md) - Defining compositions, stills, folders, default props and dynamic metadata\n- [rules/display-captions.md](rules/display-captions.md) - Displaying captions in Remotion with TikTok-style pages and word highlighting\n- [rules/extract-frames.md](rules/extract-frames.md) - Extract frames from videos at specific timestamps using Mediabunny\n- [rules/fonts.md](rules/fonts.md) - Loading Google Fonts and local fonts in Remotion\n- [rules/get-audio-duration.md](rules/get-audio-duration.md) - Getting the duration of an audio file in seconds with Mediabunny\n- [rules/get-video-dimensions.md](rules/get-video-dimensions.md) - Getting the width and height of a video file with Mediabunny\n- [rules/get-video-duration.md](rules/get-video-duration.md) - Getting the duration of a video file in seconds with Mediabunny\n- [rules/gifs.md](rules/gifs.md) - Displaying GIFs synchronized with Remotion''s timeline\n- [rules/images.md](rules/images.md) - Embedding images in Remotion using the Img component\n- [rules/import-srt-captions.md](rules/import-srt-captions.md) - Importing .srt subtitle files into Remotion using @remotion/captions\n- [rules/lottie.md](rules/lottie.md) - Embedding Lottie animations in Remotion\n- [rules/measuring-dom-nodes.md](rules/measuring-dom-nodes.md) - Measuring DOM element dimensions in Remotion\n- [rules/measuring-text.md](rules/measuring-text.md) - Measuring text dimensions, fitting text to containers, and checking overflow\n- [rules/sequencing.md](rules/sequencing.md) - Sequencing patterns for Remotion - delay, trim, limit duration of items\n- [rules/tailwind.md](rules/tailwind.md) - Using TailwindCSS in Remotion\n- [rules/text-animations.md](rules/text-animations.md) - Typography and text animation patterns for Remotion\n- [rules/timing.md](rules/timing.md) - Interpolation curves in Remotion - linear, easing, spring animations\n- [rules/transcribe-captions.md](rules/transcribe-captions.md) - Transcribing audio to generate captions in Remotion\n- [rules/transitions.md](rules/transitions.md) - Scene transition patterns for Remotion\n- [rules/transparent-videos.md](rules/transparent-videos.md) - Rendering out a video with transparency\n- [rules/trimming.md](rules/trimming.md) - Trimming patterns for Remotion - cut the beginning or end of animations\n- [rules/videos.md](rules/videos.md) - Embedding videos in Remotion - trimming, volume, speed, looping, pitch\n- [rules/parameters.md](rules/parameters.md) - Make a video parametrizable by adding a Zod schema\n- [rules/maps.md](rules/maps.md) - Add a map using Mapbox and animate it\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:52:24.956Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents specializing in programmatic video generation and motion graphics workflows.","zh":"非常适合专门从事程序化视频生成和运动图形工作流的AI代理。","ja":"プログラムによるビデオ生成とモーショングラフィックスのワークフローに特化したAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"프로그램 방식의 비디오 생성 및 모션 그래픽스 워크플로우를専門으로하는 AI 에이전트에게 최적입니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que se especializan en la generación de video programático y flujos de trabajo de gráficos en movimiento.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA spécialisés dans la génération de vidéos programmées et les flux de travail de graphiques animés.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die auf die programmatische Videogenerierung und Motion-Graphics-Workflows spezialisiert sind.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA especializados em geração de vídeo programática e fluxos de trabalho de gráficos em movimento.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, специализирующихся на программной генерации видео и рабочих процессах графики в движении.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يتخصصون في توليد الفيديو البرمجي وعمليات الرسومات المتحركة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents with Remotion-specific domain knowledge for creating dynamic video content using React components, including Three.js integration for 3D scenes, optimized asset handling for images and audio, and professional animation techniques through React Spring and Framer Motion. Provides structured best practices for component composition, timeline management, and rendering optimization specific to the Remotion framework.","zh":"赋予代理Remotion特定的领域知识，用于使用React组件创建动态视频内容，包括使用Three.js进行3D场景集成、优化图像和音频的资产处理，以及通过React Spring和Framer Motion实现专业的动画技术。为组件组合、时间线管理和渲染优化提供了结构化的最佳实践，具体针对Remotion框架。","ja":"エージェントにRemotion特有のドメイン知識を提供し、Reactコンポーネントを使用して動的なビデオコンテンツを作成します。Three.jsを使用した3Dシーン統合、画像およびオーディオの最適化されたアセット処理、およびReact SpringおよびFramer Motionを使用したプロフェッショナルなアニメーション技術が含まれます。Remotionフレームワークに特有のコンポーネント構成、タイムライン管理、レンダリング最適化の構造化されたベストプラクティスを提供します。","ko":"에이전트에게 Remotion 특정 도메인 지식을 제공하여 React 컴포넌트를 사용하여 동적 비디오 콘텐츠를 생성한다. Three.js를 사용한 3D 시각화 통합, 이미지 및 오디오의 최적화된 자산 처리 및 React Spring 및 Framer Motion을 사용한 전문 애니메이션 기술을 포함한다. Remotion 프레임워크에 특정한 컴포넌트 구성, 타임 라인 관리 및 렌더링 최적화에 대한 구조화된 모범 사례를 제공한다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes con conocimientos específicos del dominio de Remotion para crear contenido de video dinámico utilizando componentes de React, incluida la integración de Three.js para escenas 3D, el manejo optimizado de activos para imágenes y audio, y técnicas de animación profesionales a través de React Spring y Framer Motion. Proporciona prácticas recomendadas estructuradas para la composición de componentes, la gestión de la línea de tiempo y la optimización del renderizado específicas del marco de Remotion.","fr":"Équipe les agents avec des connaissances spécifiques au domaine de Remotion pour créer du contenu vidéo dynamique en utilisant des composants React, y compris l''intégration de Three.js pour les scènes 3D, la gestion optimisée des ressources pour les images et l''audio, et des techniques d''animation professionnelles via React Spring et Framer Motion. Fournit des meilleures pratiques structurées pour la composition de composants, la gestion de la timeline et l''optimisation du rendu spécifiques au cadre de Remotion.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents mit Remotion-spezifischem Domänenwissen, dynamisches Videoinhalte mithilfe von React-Komponenten zu erstellen, einschließlich Three.js-Integration für 3D-Szenen, optimiertes Asset-Handling für Bilder und Audio sowie professionelle Animationsverfahren über React Spring und Framer Motion. Bietet strukturierte Best Practices für die Komposition von Komponenten, die Zeitachsenverwaltung und die Renderoptimierung, die speziell auf das Remotion-Framework zugeschnitten sind.","pt":"Habilita os agentes com conhecimento de domínio específico do Remotion para criar conteúdo de vídeo dinâmico usando componentes React, incluindo integração do Three.js para cenas 3D, manipulação de ativos otimizada para imagens e áudio, e técnicas de animação profissionais por meio do React Spring e Framer Motion. Fornece práticas recomendadas estruturadas para composição de componentes, gerenciamento de linha do tempo e otimização de renderização específica do framework Remotion.","ru":"Наделяет агентов знаниями в области Remotion для создания динамического видеоконтента с использованием компонентов React, включая интеграцию Three.js для 3D-сцен, оптимизированную обработку активов для изображений и аудио, а также профессиональные техники анимации с помощью React Spring и Framer Motion. Предоставляет структурированные рекомендации для составления компонентов, управления временной шкалой и оптимизации рендеринга, специфичные для фреймворка Remotion.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء بمعرفة النطاق الخاصة ب Remotion لإنشاء محتوى فيديو ديناميكي باستخدام مكونات React، بما في ذلك دمج Three.js للرسومات ثلاثية الأبعاد، ومعالجة الأصول المُحسّنة للصور والصوت، وتقنيات الرسوم المتحركة الاحترافية من خلال React Spring و Framer Motion. يوفر أفضل الممارسات المهيكلة لتركيب المكونات وإدارة الجدول الزمني وتحسين العرض المحدد لإطار Remotion."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating programmatic video sequences from data inputs","Implementing 3D visualizations using React Three Fiber components","Optimizing media asset loading and composition for render performance","Creating complex animation sequences with timeline precision"],"zh":["从数据输入生成程序化视频序列","使用React Three Fiber组件实现3D可视化","优化媒体资产加载和组合以提高渲染性能","使用时间线精度创建复杂的动画序列"],"ja":["データ入力からプログラムによるビデオシーケンスを生成する","React Three Fiberコンポーネントを使用した3Dビジュアライゼーションの実装","レンダリング性能の向上のためのメディアアセットのロードとコンポジションの最適化","タイムライン精度で複雑なアニメーションシーケンスを作成する"],"ko":["데이터 입력에서 프로그래밍 방식 비디오 시퀀스를 생성한다","React Three Fiber 컴포넌트를 사용한 3D 시각화 구현","렌더링 성능 향상을 위한 미디어 자산 로딩 및 구성 최적화","타임 라인 精度로 복잡한 애니메이션 시퀀스를 생성한다"],"es":["Generar secuencias de video programáticas a partir de entradas de datos","Implementar visualizaciones 3D utilizando componentes de React Three Fiber","Optimizar la carga y composición de activos multimedia para el rendimiento de renderizado","Crear secuencias de animación complejas con precisión de línea de tiempo"],"fr":["Générer des séquences de vidéo programmées à partir d''entrées de données","Mettre en œuvre des visualisations 3D en utilisant des composants React Three Fiber","Optimiser le chargement et la composition des ressources multimédias pour les performances de rendu","Créer des séquences d''animation complexes avec une précision de la timeline"],"de":["Programmatische Videosequenzen aus Dateninputs generieren","3D-Visualisierungen mithilfe von React Three Fiber-Komponenten implementieren","Medien-Asset-Ladung und -Zusammensetzung für Renderleistung optimieren","Komplexe Animationssequenzen mit Zeitachsenpräzision erstellen"],"pt":["Gerar sequências de vídeo programáticas a partir de entradas de dados","Implementar visualizações 3D usando componentes React Three Fiber","Otimizar o carregamento e composição de ativos de mídia para desempenho de renderização","Criar sequências de animação complexas com precisão de linha do tempo"],"ru":["Генерировать программные видеопоследовательности из входных данных","Реализовывать 3D-визуализации с использованием компонентов React Three Fiber","Оптимизировать загрузку и составление мультимедийных активов для рендеринга","Создавать сложные анимационные последовательности с точностью временной шкалы"],"ar":["توليد تسلسلات فيديو برمجية من مدخلات البيانات","تنفيذ التصورات ثلاثية الأبعاد باستخدام مكونات React Three Fiber","تحسين تحميل وتأليف أصول الوسائط المتعددة لأداء العرض","إنشاء تسلسلات رسوم متحركة معقدة بدقة جدول زمني"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires existing Remotion project structure","Assumes React component knowledge","Limited to Remotion-specific APIs and patterns"],"zh":["需要现有的Remotion项目结构","假设React组件知识","仅限Remotion特定的API和模式"],"ja":["既存のRemotionプロジェクト構造が必要","Reactコンポーネント知識が前提","Remotion特有のAPIとパターンに限定"],"ko":["기존의 Remotion 프로젝트 구조가 필요하다","React 컴포넌트 지식이 가정된다","Remotion 특정 API 및 패턴으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere estructura de proyecto Remotion existente","Supone conocimiento de componentes de React","Limitado a APIs y patrones específicos de Remotion"],"fr":["Nécessite une structure de projet Remotion existante","Suppose des connaissances en composants React","Limité aux API et modèles spécifiques de Remotion"],"de":["Erfordert bestehende Remotion-Projektstruktur","Gibt voraus, dass React-Komponentenkenntnisse vorhanden sind","Begrenzt auf Remotion-spezifische APIs und Muster"],"pt":["Exige estrutura de projeto Remotion existente","Pressupõe conhecimento de componentes React","Limitado a APIs e padrões específicos do Remotion"],"ru":["Требует существующей структуры проекта Remotion","Предполагает знание компонентов React","Ограничен API и шаблонами, специфичными для Remotion"],"ar":["يتطلب هيكلاً مشروعًا موجودًا ل Remotion","يفترض معرفة مكونات React","محدود بالواجهات البرمجية وأنماط Remotion المحددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Ejyke90/kudegowo/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'Ejyke90', 'kudegowo', 'Ejyke90/kudegowo', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z', '2026-02-18T11:52:53.221Z', NULL, '{"id":"Ejyke90/kudegowo/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南，引导用户完成首个工作流程循环，包括初始化、工作流管理等","ja":"OpenSpec 入門ガイドは、ユーザーを最初のワークフロー循環に導き、初期化、ワークフローの管理などを含みます","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기는 사용자를 첫 번째 워크플로우 사이클에導き, 초기화, 워크플로우 관리 등을 포함합니다","es":"OpenSpec Onboard es una guía que te lleva a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo de OpenSpec. Aprende a configurar y ejecutar OpenSpec en tu código","fr":"OpenSpec Onboard est un guide qui vous accompagne dans votre premier cycle de travail OpenSpec. Apprenez à configurer et exécuter OpenSpec dans votre code","de":"OpenSpec Onboard ist eine Anleitung, die Sie durch Ihren ersten OpenSpec-Arbeitszyklus führt. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie OpenSpec in Ihrem Code konfigurieren und ausführen","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que ajuda os desenvolvedores a configurar o OpenSpec em seus projetos","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это руководство, которое помогает разработчикам настроить OpenSpec в своих проектах","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يساعد المطورين على تشغيل OpenSpec في مشاريعهم","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南","ja":"OpenSpec 入門ガイド","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기","es":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guía de inicio","fr":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guide de démarrage","de":"OpenSpec Onboard: Einstiegshilfe","pt":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guia de Inicialização","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard: Руководство по настройке","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard: دليل الإعداد","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南，引导用户完成首个工作流程循环，包括初始化、工作流管理等","ja":"OpenSpec 入門ガイドは、ユーザーを最初のワークフロー循環に導き、初期化、ワークフローの管理などを含みます","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기는 사용자를 첫 번째 워크플로우 사이클에導き, 초기화, 워크플로우 관리 등을 포함합니다","es":"OpenSpec Onboard es una guía que te lleva a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo de OpenSpec. Aprende a configurar y ejecutar OpenSpec en tu código","fr":"OpenSpec Onboard est un guide qui vous accompagne dans votre premier cycle de travail OpenSpec. Apprenez à configurer et exécuter OpenSpec dans votre code","de":"OpenSpec Onboard ist eine Anleitung, die Sie durch Ihren ersten OpenSpec-Arbeitszyklus führt. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie OpenSpec in Ihrem Code konfigurieren und ...","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que ajuda os desenvolvedores a configurar o OpenSpec em seus projetos","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это руководство, которое помогает разработчикам настроить OpenSpec в своих проектах","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يساعد المطورين على تشغيل OpenSpec في مشاريعهم","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["代码库初始化","工作流管理","实时反馈","可扩展性","高效开发"],"ja":["コードベースの初期化","ワークフローの管理","リアルタイムのフィードバック","拡張性","効率的な開発"],"ko":["코드베이스 초기화","워크플로우 관리","실시간 피드백","확장성","효율적인 개발"],"es":["Configuración de OpenSpec","Ejecución del primer flujo de trabajo","Guía paso a paso","Verificación del estado de OpenSpec","Inicialización de OpenSpec"],"fr":["Configuration d''OpenSpec","Exécution du premier workflow","Guide étape par étape","Vérification de l''état d''OpenSpec","Initialisation d''OpenSpec"],"de":["Konfiguration von OpenSpec","Ausführung des ersten Workflows","Schritt-für-Schritt-Anleitung","Überprüfung des OpenSpec-Status","Initialisierung von OpenSpec"],"pt":["Configuração do OpenSpec","Ciclo de trabalho completo","Explicação passo a passo","Trabalho real no código","Verificação de inicialização"],"ru":["Настройка OpenSpec","Полный цикл работы","Пошаговое объяснение","Реальная работа над кодом","Проверка инициализации"],"ar":["إعداد OpenSpec","دورة عمل كاملة","توضيح خطوة بخطوة","عمل حقيقي على الرمز","فحص التشغيل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","工作流管理","代码库初始化","开发工具","效率开发","实时反馈"],"ja":["OpenSpec","ワークフローの管理","コードベースの初期化","開発ツール","効率的な開発","リアルタイムのフィードバック"],"ko":["OpenSpec","워크플로우 관리","코드베이스 초기화","개발 도구","효율적인 개발","실시간 피드백"],"es":["OpenSpec","Onboard","Guía de inicio","Configuración de OpenSpec","Flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec","Desarrollo de software","Herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["OpenSpec","Onboard","Guide de démarrage","Configuration d''OpenSpec","Workflow OpenSpec","Développement de logiciels","Outils de développement"],"de":["OpenSpec","Onboard","Einstiegshilfe","Konfiguration von OpenSpec","OpenSpec-Workflow","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklertools"],"pt":["OpenSpec","configuração","desenvolvimento","código","guia","onboard","inicialização"],"ru":["OpenSpec","настройка","разработка","код","руководство","onboard","инициализация"],"ar":["OpenSpec","إعداد","تطوير","رمز","دليل","onboard","تشغيل"]}},"owner":"Ejyke90","repo":"kudegowo","repoPath":"Ejyke90/kudegowo","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:52:53.221Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing guided OpenSpec workflow integration.","zh":"非常适合需要指导的 OpenSpec 工作流集成的开发代理。","ja":"OpenSpec ワークフロー統合のガイダンスが必要な開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"가이드가 필요한 OpenSpec 워크플ロー 통합을 필요로 하는 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo que necesitan una integración guiada de flujos de trabajo OpenSpec.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Développement ayant besoin d''une intégration guidée de workflows OpenSpec.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungs-Agenten, die eine geführte Integration von OpenSpec-Workflows benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de integração de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec orientada.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходима управляемая интеграция рабочего процесса OpenSpec.","ar":"مثالي لوسائل تطوير الحاجة إلى تكامل تدفق العمل الموجه OpenSpec."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to initiate and complete OpenSpec workflow cycles, utilizing `openspec init` and `openspec status` commands for project setup and validation, while explaining each step in a teaching experience.","zh":"赋予代理初始化和完成 OpenSpec 工作流周期的能力，利用 `openspec init` 和 `openspec status` 命令进行项目设置和验证，同时解释每一步骤的教学经验。","ja":"エージェントに OpenSpec ワークフロー周期を開始して完了する能力を与え、プロジェクトの設定と検証のために `openspec init` と `openspec status` コマンドを使用し、同時に各ステップの教える体験を提供する。","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 워크플ロー 사이클을 초기화하고 완료할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 프로젝트 설정 및 검증을 위해 `openspec init` 및 `openspec status` 명령을 사용하고,同時에 각 단계의 교육 경험을 설명합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes iniciar y completar ciclos de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec, utilizando los comandos `openspec init` y `openspec status` para la configuración y validación del proyecto, mientras explica cada paso en una experiencia educativa.","fr":"Permet aux agents de lancer et de terminer des cycles de workflow OpenSpec, en utilisant les commandes `openspec init` et `openspec status` pour la configuration et la validation du projet, tout en expliquant chaque étape dans une expérience pédagogique.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklen zu starten und abzuschließen, indem sie die Befehle `openspec init` und `openspec status` für die Projekteinrichtung und -validierung nutzen, wobei jeder Schritt in einer lehrreichen Erfahrung erklärt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a iniciar e concluir ciclos de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec, utilizando os comandos `openspec init` e `openspec status` para configuração e validação do projeto, explicando cada etapa em uma experiência de ensino.","ru":"Направляет агентов на начало и завершение циклов рабочего процесса OpenSpec, используя команды `openspec init` и `openspec status` для настройки и проверки проекта, объясняя каждую ступень в процессе обучения.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من開始 واكمال دورات تدفق العمل OpenSpec، باستخدام أوامر `openspec init` و `openspec status` لإعداد وتأكيد المشروع، وشرح كل خطوة في تجربة تعليمية."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through their first OpenSpec workflow cycle","Validating OpenSpec project setup using JSON output"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化 OpenSpec","指导用户完成第一个 OpenSpec 工作流周期","使用 JSON 输出验证 OpenSpec 项目设置"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトで OpenSpec を初期化する","ユーザーが最初の OpenSpec ワークフロー周期を完了するためのガイダンス","JSON 出力で OpenSpec プロジェクト設定を検証する"],"ko":["새 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자가 첫 번째 OpenSpec 워크플ロー 사이클을 완료하도록 안내","JSON 출력을 사용하여 OpenSpec 프로젝트 설정을 검증"],"es":["Inicializar OpenSpec en proyectos nuevos","Guiar a los usuarios a través de su primer ciclo de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec","Validar la configuración del proyecto OpenSpec utilizando salida JSON"],"fr":["Initialiser OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guider les utilisateurs lors de leur premier cycle de workflow OpenSpec","Valider la configuration du projet OpenSpec en utilisant la sortie JSON"],"de":["Initialisierung von OpenSpec in neuen Projekten","Benutzer durch ihren ersten OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklus führen","Validierung der OpenSpec-Projekteinrichtung unter Verwendung der JSON-Ausgabe"],"pt":["Inicializar OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientar usuários ao longo de seu primeiro ciclo de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec","Validar configuração do projeto OpenSpec usando saída JSON"],"ru":["Инициализировать OpenSpec в новых проектах","Направлять пользователей через их первый цикл рабочего процесса OpenSpec","Проверить настройку проекта OpenSpec с использованием вывода JSON"],"ar":["تشغيل OpenSpec في المشاريع الجديدة","توجيه المستخدمين خلال دورة تدفق العمل OpenSpec الأولى","تحقق من إعداد مشروع OpenSpec باستخدام إخراج JSON"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec installation","Project must be properly set up for OpenSpec initialization"],"zh":["需要 OpenSpec 安装","项目必须正确设置以便于 OpenSpec 初始化"],"ja":["OpenSpec のインストールが必要","OpenSpec 初期化のためにプロジェクトが正しく設定されている必要がある"],"ko":["OpenSpec 설치가 필요","프로젝트가 OpenSpec 초기화를 위해 올바르게 설정되어 있어야 함"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de OpenSpec","El proyecto debe estar configurado correctamente para la inicialización de OpenSpec"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation d''OpenSpec","Le projet doit être correctement configuré pour l''initialisation d''OpenSpec"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation von OpenSpec","Das Projekt muss für die OpenSpec-Initialisierung korrekt eingerichtet sein"],"pt":["Requer instalação do OpenSpec","O projeto deve estar configurado corretamente para inicialização do OpenSpec"],"ru":["Требуется установка OpenSpec","Проект должен быть правильно настроен для инициализации OpenSpec"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت OpenSpec","يجب أن يكون المشروع محددًا بشكل صحيح لتشغيل OpenSpec"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
