e l''efficacité de l''agent","Flexibilité dans la création de compétences"],"de":["Erstellung benutzerdefinierter Fähigkeiten","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude","Spezialisiertes Wissen und Arbeitsabläufe","Verbesserung der Effizienz des Agents","Flexibilität bei der Erstellung von Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades personalizadas","Extensões modulares para tarefas específicas","Desenvolvimento de workflows especializados","Integração com Claude"],"ru":["Создание персонализированных навыков","Модульные расширения для конкретных задач","Разработка специализированных рабочих процессов","Интеграция с Claude"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات مخصصة","امتدادات قابلة للتحديث لعمليات معينة","تطوير سير عمل متخصصة","التكامل مع برنامج Claude"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创建器","Claude能力扩展","专业化工作流","模块化知识","任务自动化","工作效率提升"],"ja":["スキルクリエイター","Claudeの機能拡張","専門化ワークフロー","モジュール化知識","タスク自動化","作業効率向上"],"ko":["스킬 생성기","클라우드 능력 확장","전문적인 워크플로우","모듈화된 지식","태스크 자동화","작업 효율 향상"],"es":["creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","Claude","agentes de inteligencia artificial","habilidades personalizadas","eficiencia del agente"],"fr":["créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","Claude","agents d''intelligence artificielle","compétences personnalisées","efficacité de l''agent"],"de":["Fähigkeitscreator","Erstellung von Fähigkeiten","Claude","Künstliche Intelligenz-Agenten","benutzerdefinierte Fähigkeiten","Effizienz des Agents"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de habilidades","extensões personalizadas","workflows especializados","integração com Claude","criação de habilidades","desenvolvimento de skills"],"ru":["разработка навыков","персонализированные расширения","специализированные рабочие процессы","интеграция с Claude","создание навыков","разработка навыков для Claude"],"ar":["تطوير المهارات","امتدادات مخصصة","سير عمل متخصصة","التكامل مع برنامج Claude","إنشاء مهارات","تطوير مهارات لبرنامج Claude"]}},"owner":"HarshalPatel1972","repo":"flow","repoPath":"HarshalPatel1972/flow","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields. These are the only fields that Claude reads to determine when the skill gets used, thus it is very important to be clear and comprehensive in describing what the skill is, and when it should be used.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:52:58.414Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing to extend their capabilities with specialized knowledge and workflows.","zh":"非常适合需要使用专门知识和工作流来扩展其功能的AI代理。","ja":"特化された知識とワークフローで機能を拡張する必要があるAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"전문 지식과 워크플로를 사용하여 기능을 확장해야 하는 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan ampliar sus capacidades con conocimientos y flujos de trabajo especializados.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA qui ont besoin d''étendre leurs capacités avec des connaissances et des flux de travail spécialisés.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agenten, die ihre Fähigkeiten mit speziellen Kenntnissen und Workflows erweitern müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que precisam estender suas capacidades com conhecimento especializado e fluxos de trabalho.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым необходимо расширить свои возможности с помощью специализированных знаний и рабочих процессов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكيين الذين يحتاجون إلى توسيع قدراتهم بالمعرفة المتخصصة والتدفقات العمل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create modular, self-contained packages that provide specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools, effectively transforming them into specialized agents equipped with procedural knowledge using multi-step workflows.","zh":"赋予代理创建模块化、自包含的软件包的能力，这些软件包提供专门的知识、工作流和工具，从而将代理转化为使用多步骤工作流的程序化知识的专门代理。","ja":"エージェントがモジュール化された、自己完結したパッケージを作成できるようにし、これらのパッケージは専門の知識、ワークフロー、およびツールを提供し、エージェントを複数のステップで構成されるワークフローを使用する専門のエージェントに変換します。","ko":"에이전트가 모듈화된 자체 포함된 패키지를 만들 수 있도록 하여 이들 패키지는 전문 지식, 워크플로 및 도구를 제공하고 에이전트를 다단계 워크플로를 사용하는 전문 에이전트로 변환합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que proporcionan conocimientos especializados, flujos de trabajo y herramientas, transformándolos efectivamente en agentes especializados equipados con conocimientos procedimentales que utilizan flujos de trabajo multietapa.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des packages modulaires et autocontenus qui fournissent des connaissances spécialisées, des flux de travail et des outils, les transformant effectivement en agents spécialisés équipés de connaissances procédurales utilisant des flux de travail multietapes.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, modulare, selbstenthaltene Pakete zu erstellen, die spezielle Kenntnisse, Workflows und Tools bereitstellen und sie damit effektiv in spezialisierte Agenten mit prozeduralen Kenntnissen umwandeln, die Multi-Schritt-Workflows verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar pacotes modulares, autocontidos que fornecem conhecimento especializado, fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas, transformando-os efetivamente em agentes especializados equipados com conhecimento procedural usando fluxos de trabalho em várias etapas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать модульные, самодостаточные пакеты, которые предоставляют специализированные знания, рабочие процессы и инструменты, эффективно превращая их в специализированных агентов, оснащенных процедурными знаниями с использованием многоступенчатых рабочих процессов.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء حزم متواصلة وتوفر المعرفة المتخصصة والتدفقات العمل والأدوات، مما يجعلهم وكلاء متخصصين يمتلكون المعرفة الإجرائية باستخدام سلاسل عمل متعددة"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating onboarding guides for specific domains","Developing specialized workflows for tasks","Extending agent capabilities with procedural knowledge"],"zh":["为特定领域创建入门指南","为任务开发专门的工作流","使用程序化知识扩展代理功能"],"ja":["特定ドメインのガイドを作成する","タスク用の専門のワークフローを開発する","エージェントの機能を手順化された知識で拡張する"],"ko":["특정 도메인에 대한 온보딩 가이드 만들기","작업을 위한 전문 워크플로 개발","프로그램화된 지식을 사용하여 에이전트 기능 확장"],"es":["Crear guías de incorporación para dominios específicos","Desarrollar flujos de trabajo especializados para tareas","Ampliar las capacidades de los agentes con conocimientos procedimentales"],"fr":["Créer des guides d''intégration pour des domaines spécifiques","Développer des flux de travail spécialisés pour les tâches","Étendre les capacités des agents avec des connaissances procédurales"],"de":["Erstellen von Onboarding-Leitfäden für bestimmte Bereiche","Entwickeln von spezialisierten Workflows für Aufgaben","Erweitern der Agentenfähigkeiten mit prozeduralen Kenntnissen"],"pt":["Criar guias de integração para domínios específicos","Desenvolver fluxos de trabalho especializados para tarefas","Estender as capacidades dos agentes com conhecimento procedural"],"ru":["Создание руководств по интеграции для конкретных доменов","Разработка специализированных рабочих процессов для задач","Расширение возможностей агентов с помощью процедурных знаний"],"ar":["إنشاء أدلة إعداد للنطاقات المحددة","تطوير سلاسل عمل متخصصة للمهام","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء بالمعرفة الإجرائية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Claude''s capabilities and limitations","Limited to creating skills within Claude''s ecosystem"],"zh":["需要了解Claude的功能和局限性","仅限于在Claude的生态系统内创建技能"],"ja":["Claudeの機能と限界を理解する必要がある","Claudeのエコシステム内でのみスキルを作成できる"],"ko":["Claude의 기능과 제한을 이해해야 함","Claude의 생태계 내에서만 스킬을 만들 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de las capacidades y limitaciones de Claude","Limitado a la creación de habilidades dentro del ecosistema de Claude"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des capacités et des limites de Claude","Limité à la création de compétences au sein de l''écosystème de Claude"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für die Fähigkeiten und Einschränkungen von Claude","Begrenzt auf die Erstellung von Fähigkeiten innerhalb des Claude-Ökosystems"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das capacidades e limitações do Claude","Limitado à criação de habilidades dentro do ecossistema do Claude"],"ru":["Требует понимания возможностей и ограничений Claude","Ограничен созданием навыков внутри экосистемы Claude"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم قدرات كلود وقيودها","محدود بالقدرة على إنشاء المهارات داخل نظام كلود"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('faint45/zhewei-ai-chat-01/skill-creator', 'community', 'faint45', 'zhewei-ai-chat-01', 'faint45/zhewei-ai-chat-01', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z', '2026-02-18T11:52:27.428Z', NULL, '{"id":"faint45/zhewei-ai-chat-01/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"本技能提供创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展 Claude 的能力，并将其转变为专用代理","ja":"このスキルは、開発者が Claude の能力を拡張し、専用エージェントに変えるための有効なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供します","ko":"이 스킬은 개발자가 클라우드의 능력을 확장하고 전문 에이전트로 변환하는 효율적인 스킬을 생성하는 데 도움을 주는 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es una herramienta para desarrolladores que permite crear paquetes modulares y personalizados para Claude.","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un outil pour les développeurs qui permet de créer des paquets modulaires et personnalisés pour Claude.","de":"Der Fähigkeitscreator ist ein Tool für Entwickler, mit dem Sie modulare und benutzerdefinierte Pakete für Claude erstellen können.","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendem as capacidades de Claude","ru":"Skill Creator предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude","ar":"يوفر Skill Creator إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة لتوسيع قدرات برنامج Claude","en":"築未科技 AI 對話窗口 - GitHub Pages 部署"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI 技能创建指南 - 构建高效技能","ja":"AI スキル作成ガイド - 有効なスキルの構築","ko":"AI 스킬 생성 가이드 - 효율적인 스킬 구축","es":"Creador de habilidades para desarrolladores","fr":"Créateur de compétences pour les développeurs","de":"Fähigkeitscreator für Entwickler","pt":"Crie Habilidades Personalizadas com Skill Creator","ru":"Создание индивидуальных навыков с Skill Creator","ar":"إنشاء مهارات مخصصة باستخدام Skill Creator","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"本技能提供创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展 Claude 的能力，并将其转变为专用代理","ja":"このスキルは、開発者が Claude の能力を拡張し、専用エージェントに変えるための有効なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供します","ko":"이 스킬은 개발자가 클라우드의 능력을 확장하고 전문 에이전트로 변환하는 효율적인 스킬을 생성하는 데 도움을 주는 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"El creador de habilidades es una herramienta para desarrolladores que permite crear paquetes modulares y personalizados para Claude.","fr":"Le créateur de compétences est un outil pour les développeurs qui permet de créer des paquets modulaires et personnalisés pour Claude.","de":"Der Fähigkeitscreator ist ein Tool für Entwickler, mit dem Sie modulare und benutzerdefinierte Pakete für Claude erstellen können.","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendem as capacidades de Claude","ru":"Skill Creator предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude","ar":"يوفر Skill Creator إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة لتوسيع قدرات برنامج Claude","en":"築未科技 AI 對話窗口 - GitHub Pages 部署"},"definition":{"en":"築未科技 AI 對話窗口 - GitHub Pages 部署"},"features":{"zh":["提供专门的工作流","扩展 Claude 的能力","将 Claude 转变为专用代理","提供专门的知识和工具","支持多种任务和领域"],"ja":["専門のワークフローを提供","Claude の能力を拡張","Claude を専用エージェントに変える","専門の知識とツールを提供","多種多様なタスクとドメインをサポート"],"ko":["전문적인 워크플ロー 제공","클라우드의 능력 확장","클라우드를 전문 에이전트로 변환","전문 지식과 툴 제공","다양한 태스크와 도메인 지원"],"es":["Flujos de trabajo especializados","Conocimiento procedural","Herramientas de desarrollo","Paquetes modulares","Personalización de Claude"],"fr":["Flux de travail spécialisés","Connaissances procédurales","Outils de développement","Paquets modulaires","Personnalisation de Claude"],"de":["Spezialisierte Workflows","Prozedurales Wissen","Entwicklungstools","Modulare Pakete","Anpassung von Claude"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades personalizadas","Extensão das capacidades de Claude","Fluxos de trabalho especializados","Ferramentas e conhecimentos procedurais"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных навыков","Расширение возможностей Claude","Специализированные рабочие процессы","Инструменты и процедурные знания"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات مخصصة","توسيع قدرات برنامج Claude","عمليات عمل مخصصة","أدوات ومعارف إجرائية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 技能","技能创建","Claude","专用代理","模块化软件","自包含软件","专门知识","工作流","工具"],"ja":["AI スキル","スキル作成","Claude","専用エージェント","モジュール化ソフトウェア","自包含ソフトウェア","専門知識","ワークフロー","ツール"],"ko":["AI 스킬","스킬 생성","클라우드","전문 에이전트","모듈화 소프트웨어","자체 포함 소프트웨어","전문 지식","워크플로","툴"],"es":["creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","Claude","conocimiento especializado","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","paquetes modulares","personalización de IA"],"fr":["créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","Claude","connaissances spécialisées","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","paquets modulaires","personnalisation de l''IA"],"de":["Fähigkeitscreator","Fähigkeitsentwicklung","Claude","spezialisiertes Wissen","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools","modulare Pakete","Anpassung von KI"],"pt":["Skill Creator","habilidades personalizadas","Claude","desenvolvimento de habilidades","IA","aprendizado de máquina","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Skill Creator","индивидуальные навыки","Claude","разработка навыков","ИИ","машинное обучение","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["Skill Creator","مهارات مخصصة","برنامج Claude","تطوير المهارات","الذكاء الاصطناعي","تعلم الآلة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"faint45","repo":"zhewei-ai-chat-01","repoPath":"faint45/zhewei-ai-chat-01","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields. These are the only fields that Claude reads to determine when the skill gets used, thus it is very important to be clear and comprehensive in describing what the skill is, and when it should be used.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:52:27.428Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing to extend their capabilities with modular, self-contained knowledge packages.","zh":"非常适合需要使用模块化、自包含的知识包来扩展其能力的AI代理。","ja":"モジュラーでセルフコンテイナ化された知識パッケージを使用して能力を拡張する必要があるAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"모듈화되고 자체적으로 포함된 지식 패키지를 사용하여 능력을 확장해야 하는 AI 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan ampliar sus capacidades con paquetes de conocimiento modulares y autocontenidos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA qui ont besoin d''étendre leurs capacités avec des packages de connaissances modulaires et autonomes.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die ihre Fähigkeiten mit modularen, selbstenthaltenen Wissenspaketen erweitern müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que precisam estender suas capacidades com pacotes de conhecimento modulares e autocontidos.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым необходимо расширить свои возможности с помощью модульных, самодостаточных пакетов знаний.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى توسيع قدراتهم مع حزم معرفة متواصلة وذاتية الحوض"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized agents equipped with procedural knowledge, providing specialized workflows and tools, and leveraging GitHub Pages for deployment.","zh":"使代理能够转变为配备了程序化知识的专业代理，提供专业的工作流程和工具，并利用GitHub Pages进行部署。","ja":"エージェントを手順化された知識を備えた専門エージェントに変えることができ、専門のワークフローとツールを提供し、GitHub Pagesを使用してデプロイできます。","ko":"에이전트를 절차적 지식을 갖춘 전문 에이전트로 변환할 수 있으며, 전문 워크플로우와 도구를 제공하고 GitHub Pages를 사용하여 배포할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformarse en agentes especializados equipados con conocimiento procedural, proporcionando flujos de trabajo y herramientas especializados, y aprovechando GitHub Pages para la implementación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en agents spécialisés équipés de connaissances procédurales, fournissant des flux de travail et des outils spécialisés, et exploitant GitHub Pages pour le déploiement.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, sich in spezialisierte Agents mit prozeduralem Wissen zu verwandeln, spezialisierte Arbeitsabläufe und Tools bereitzustellen und GitHub Pages für die Bereitstellung zu nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se transformarem em agentes especializados equipados com conhecimento procedural, fornecendo fluxos de trabalho especializados e ferramentas, e aproveitando o GitHub Pages para implantação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью превратиться в специализированных агентов, оснащенных процедурными знаниями, обеспечивающих специализированные рабочие процессы и инструменты, и использующих GitHub Pages для развертывания.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من التحول إلى وكلاء متخصصين مجهزين بمعرفة إجرائية، وتوفير سير عمل متخصصة وأدوات، واستخدام صفحات GitHub لنشرها."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating modular skills for specific domains","Extending agent capabilities with procedural knowledge","Deploying skills on GitHub Pages"],"zh":["为特定领域创建模块化技能","使用程序化知识扩展代理能力","在GitHub Pages上部署技能"],"ja":["特定ドメインのモジュラーなスキルを作成する","手順化された知識を使用してエージェントの機能を拡張する","GitHub Pagesにスキルをデプロイする"],"ko":["특정 도메인에 대한 모듈화된 스킬을 생성하는 것","절차적 지식을 사용하여 에이전트의 능력을 확장하는 것","GitHub Pages에 스킬을 배포하는 것"],"es":["Crear habilidades modulares para dominios específicos","Ampliar las capacidades de los agentes con conocimiento procedural","Implementar habilidades en GitHub Pages"],"fr":["Créer des compétences modulaires pour des domaines spécifiques","Étendre les capacités des agents avec des connaissances procédurales","Déployer des compétences sur GitHub Pages"],"de":["Modulare Fähigkeiten für spezifische Domänen erstellen","Die Fähigkeiten von Agents mit prozeduralem Wissen erweitern","Fähigkeiten auf GitHub Pages bereitstellen"],"pt":["Criar habilidades modulares para domínios específicos","Estender as capacidades dos agentes com conhecimento procedural","Implantar habilidades no GitHub Pages"],"ru":["Создание модульных навыков для конкретных областей","Расширение возможностей агентов с помощью проце