، Git 연산, 커밋 기록 탐색 및 파일 복구","es":"Nuestra guía de Git te enseña a navegar por el historial de commits y recuperar archivos eliminados de manera efectiva","fr":"Notre guide Git vous apprend à naviguer dans l''historique des commits et à récupérer des fichiers supprimés de manière efficace","de":"Unsere Git-Anleitung zeigt Ihnen, wie Sie den Commit-Verlauf navigieren und gelöschte Dateien effektiv wiederherstellen","pt":"O Git é uma coleção de ferramentas para testar, operar e manter backends OpenAI, com foco em navegação de histórico de commits e recuperação de arquivos","ru":"Git - это коллекция инструментов для тестирования, эксплуатации и обслуживания бэкендов OpenAI, с фокусом на навигации по истории коммитов и восстановлении ф...","ar":"Git هو مجموعة من الأدوات لاختبار وتشغيل وصيانة الخوادم الخلفية لشركة OpenAI، مع التركيز على التنقل في سجل التعديلات واستعادة الملفات","en":"A collection of tools to test, operate and maintain OpenAI backends (OpenAI and AzureOpenAI)"},"definition":{"en":"A collection of tools to test, operate and maintain OpenAI backends (OpenAI and AzureOpenAI)"},"features":{"zh":["Git 操作","提交历史导航","文件恢复","仓库根目录验证","Reflog 复原"],"ja":["Git 操作","コミット履歴のナビゲーション","ファイルの復元","リポジトリルートディレクトリの検証","Reflog を使用した復元"],"ko":["Git 연산","커밋 기록 탐색","파일 복구","仓库 根 디렉토리 검증","Reflog 복구"],"es":["Navegación de historial de commits","Recuperación de archivos eliminados","Verificación de la raíz del repositorio","Uso de --name-status para ver cambios","Uso de reflog para recuperación"],"fr":["Navigation de l''historique des commits","Récupération de fichiers supprimés","Vérification de la racine du référentiel","Utilisation de --name-status pour voir les modifications","Utilisation de reflog pour la récupération"],"de":["Navigation von Commit-Verlaufs","Wiederherstellung von gelöschten Dateien","Überprüfung der Repository-Wurzel","Verwendung von --name-status zum Anzeigen von Änderungen","Verwendung von Reflog zur Wiederherstellung"],"pt":["Navegação de histórico de commits","Recuperação de arquivos","Verificação da raiz do repositório","Uso de reflog para recuperação","Instalação personalizada"],"ru":["Навигация по истории коммитов","Восстановление файлов","Проверка корня репозитория","Использование reflog для восстановления","Пользовательская установка"],"ar":["تنقل في سجل التعديلات","استعادة الملفات","التحقق من الجذر للمستودع","استخدام Reflog لاستعادة","التثبيت المخصص"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git 技术","版本控制","提交历史","文件恢复","仓库管理","Reflog","Git 操作"],"ja":["Git スキル","バージョン管理","コミット履歴","ファイルの復元","リポジトリ管理","Reflog","Git 操作"],"ko":["Git 기술","버전 제어","커밋 기록","파일 복구","倉庫 관리","Reflog","Git 연산"],"es":["git","operaciones avanzadas","navegación de historial de commits","recuperación de archivos","OpenAI","desarrollo de software","control de versiones"],"fr":["git","opérations avancées","navigation de l''historique des commits","récupération de fichiers","OpenAI","développement de logiciels","contrôle de versions"],"de":["git","erweiterte Operationen","Navigation von Commit-Verlaufs","Wiederherstellung von Dateien","OpenAI","Software-Entwicklung","Versionskontrolle"],"pt":["Git","controle de versão","navegação de histórico de commits","recuperação de arquivos","OpenAI","AzureOpenAI","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Git","контроль версий","навигация по истории коммитов","восстановление файлов","OpenAI","AzureOpenAI","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["Git","مراقبة الإصدار","تنقل في سجل التعديلات","استعادة الملفات","OpenAI","AzureOpenAI","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"karstenheld3","repo":"OpenAI-BackendTools","repoPath":"karstenheld3/OpenAI-BackendTools","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"git","description":"Apply when working with Git repositories, commit history, or recovering files from previous commits","bodyPreview":"# Git Skill\n\nGit operations with focus on commit history navigation and file recovery.\n\n## MUST-NOT-FORGET\n\n- Always verify repository root before operations: `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`\n- Use `--name-status` to see A/M/D (Added/Modified/Deleted) per commit\n- To recover deleted file: checkout from commit BEFORE deletion (use `^` suffix)\n- Reflog survives even after reset/rebase - use it for recovery\n\n## Setup\n\nFor installation, see `SETUP.md` in this skill folder.\n\n## Commit History Navigati","body":"# Git Skill\n\nGit operations with focus on commit history navigation and file recovery.\n\n## MUST-NOT-FORGET\n\n- Always verify repository root before operations: `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`\n- Use `--name-status` to see A/M/D (Added/Modified/Deleted) per commit\n- To recover deleted file: checkout from commit BEFORE deletion (use `^` suffix)\n- Reflog survives even after reset/rebase - use it for recovery\n\n## Setup\n\nFor installation, see `SETUP.md` in this skill folder.\n\n## Commit History Navigation\n\n### View Recent Commits\n\n```powershell\n# Last 10 commits, one line each\ngit log --oneline -10\n\n# With file changes summary\ngit log --oneline --name-status -10\n\n# With date and author\ngit log --format=\"%h %ad %an: %s\" --date=short -10\n```\n\n### View Files Changed in Specific Commit\n\n```powershell\n# Show files with status (A=added, M=modified, D=deleted)\ngit show --name-status <commit_hash>\n\n# Just the file list\ngit show --name-only <commit_hash>\n\n# Full diff\ngit show <commit_hash>\n```\n\n### Navigate Commits Step by Step\n\n```powershell\n# Show current HEAD\ngit log --oneline -1\n\n# Show parent of HEAD\ngit log --oneline HEAD^ -1\n\n# Show N commits back\ngit log --oneline HEAD~5 -1\n\n# Compare two commits\ngit diff <commit1> <commit2> --name-status\n```\n\n### Interactive Walkback (Step Through History)\n\nTo investigate commits one-by-one, walking backwards:\n\n```powershell\n# Step 1: Start at HEAD, show what changed\ngit log --oneline -1\ngit show --name-status HEAD\n\n# Step 2: Move back one commit, show changes\ngit log --oneline HEAD^ -1\ngit show --name-status HEAD^\n\n# Step 3: Continue back (use ~2, ~3, etc.)\ngit log --oneline HEAD~2 -1\ngit show --name-status HEAD~2\n\n# Pattern: HEAD~N where N = steps back from current\n```\n\n**Tip:** Your current position is always HEAD. Use `git log --oneline -1` to confirm where you are.\n\n## File Recovery\n\n### Find When File Was Deleted\n\n```powershell\n# List all deleted files across history\ngit log --diff-filter=D --summary\n\n# Find specific file deletion\ngit log --diff-filter=D --summary -- \"**/filename.ext\"\n\n# Find EXACTLY which commit deleted a specific file (one-liner)\ngit log --diff-filter=D -1 -- path/to/file.ext\n\n# With paths\ngit log --diff-filter=D --name-only --format=\"%H %s\"\n```\n\n### Find Last Commit Where File Existed\n\n```powershell\n# Shows commits that touched the file (including deletion)\ngit log --all -- path/to/deleted/file.ext\n\n# The first result is the deletion commit\n# Use its parent (^) to get the version before deletion\n```\n\n### Recover Deleted File\n\n```powershell\n# From commit that deleted it (^ = parent commit)\ngit checkout <deletion_commit>^ -- path/to/file.ext\n\n# From known good commit\ngit checkout <good_commit> -- path/to/file.ext\n\n# Alternative (Git 2.23+): git restore --source=<commit> -- path/to/file\n\n# Using show (outputs to stdout, redirect to file)\ngit show <commit>:path/to/file.ext > recovered_file.ext\n```\n\n### Recover File from Reflog\n\n```powershell\n# View reflog\ngit reflog\n\n# Recover from specific reflog entry\ngit checkout HEAD@{n} -- path/to/file.ext\n```\n\n## Guided Recovery Workflow\n\nWhen user needs to recover accidentally deleted files:\n\n### Step 1: Identify Deletion\n\n```powershell\n# Find recent deletions\ngit log --diff-filter=D --name-only --format=\"=== %H %s ===\" -5\n```\n\n**Note:** If file was renamed (not deleted), use `git log --follow -- oldname` to track renames.\n\n### Step 2: Confirm Deletion Commit\n\n```powershell\n# Show what was deleted in that commit\ngit show --name-status <commit_hash>\n```\n\n### Step 3: Verify File Existed Before\n\n```powershell\n# Check file in parent commit\ngit show <commit_hash>^:<path/to/file>\n```\n\n### Step 4: Recover\n\n```powershell\n# Restore the file\ngit checkout <commit_hash>^ -- path/to/file\n```\n\n### Step 5: Verify Recovery\n\n```powershell\n# Check file exists\nGet-Item path/to/file\n\n# Check status\ngit status\n```\n\n## Batch Operations\n\n### List All Files Deleted in Last N Commits\n\n```powershell\ngit log --diff-filter=D --name-only --format=\"\" -n 20 | Where-Object { $_ -ne \"\" } | Sort-Object -Unique\n```\n\n### Recover Multiple Files from Same Commit\n\n```powershell\n# List files first\ngit show --name-only <commit>^\n\n# Recover specific files\ngit checkout <commit>^ -- file1.ext file2.ext file3.ext\n\n# Recover entire directory\ngit checkout <commit>^ -- path/to/directory/\n```\n\n## Comparing Versions\n\n### Compare File Across Commits\n\n```powershell\n# Between two commits\ngit diff <commit1> <commit2> -- path/to/file\n\n# Between commit and working directory\ngit diff <commit> -- path/to/file\n\n# Between commit and staged\ngit diff --cached <commit> -- path/to/file\n```\n\n### Show File Content at Specific Commit\n\n```powershell\ngit show <commit>:path/to/file\n```\n\n## Undo Operations\n\n### Undo Last Commit (Keep Changes)\n\n```powershell\ngit reset --soft HEAD^\n```\n\n### Undo Last Commit (Discard Changes)\n\n```powershell\ngit reset --hard HEAD^\n```\n\n### Restore File to Last Committed Version\n\n```powershell\ngit checkout HEAD -- path/to/file\n```\n\n### Unstage File\n\n```powershell\ngit reset HEAD -- path/to/file\n```\n\n## Status and Inspection\n\n### Repository Status\n\n```powershell\ngit status\ngit status --short\n```\n\n### Show Staged Changes\n\n```powershell\ngit diff --cached\ngit diff --cached --name-status\n```\n\n### Show Unstaged Changes\n\n```powershell\ngit diff\ngit diff --name-status\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Investigate Accidental Deletion\n\n```powershell\n# 1. Find what was deleted recently\ngit log --diff-filter=D --name-only -5\n\n# 2. Identify the commit\ngit show <commit> --name-status\n\n# 3. Recover\ngit checkout <commit>^ -- <file>\n```\n\n### Recover Workflow File Deleted by Commit Workflow\n\nWhen `/commit` accidentally deletes a file:\n\n```powershell\n# 1. Check last few commits for deletions\ngit log --diff-filter=D --name-status -3\n\n# 2. Find the workflow file\ngit log --diff-filter=D -- \"**/*.md\" --name-only -5\n\n# 3. Recover from parent of deletion commit\ngit checkout <commit>^ -- .windsurf/workflows/filename.md\n```\n\n### Compare What Changed Between Sessions\n\n```powershell\n# Find commits from today\ngit log --since=\"today\" --oneline\n\n# Compare start to end\ngit diff <first_commit> <last_commit> --name-status\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:54:08.591Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing advanced Git commit history navigation and file recovery capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级 Git 提交历史导航和文件恢复功能的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが高度な Git コミット履歴のナビゲーションとファイルの回復機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 고급 Git 커밋 기록 탐색 및 파일 복구 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una navegación avanzada del historial de commits de Git y capacidades de recuperación de archivos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une navigation avancée de l''historique des commits Git et de capacités de récupération de fichiers.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine erweiterte Navigation im Git-Commit-Historie und Dateiwiederherstellungs-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de navegação avançada de histórico de commits do Git e capacidades de recuperação de arquivos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым требуются продвинутые возможности навигации по истории коммитов Git и восстановления файлов.","ar":"مثالي لعملاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى مهارات متقدمة في التنقل في تاريخ الإلتزامات Git وقدرات استعادة الملفات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to navigate commit history using `git rev-parse` and recover deleted files via reflog, utilizing `--name-status` for detailed change tracking and `^` suffix for file recovery from previous commits.","zh":"赋予代理使用 `git rev-parse` 导航提交历史和通过 reflog 恢复删除的文件的能力，利用 `--name-status` 进行详细的更改跟踪，并使用 `^` 后缀从以前的提交中恢复文件。","ja":"エージェントが `git rev-parse` を使用してコミット履歴をナビゲートし、reflog を使用して削除されたファイルを回復する機能を提供し、`--name-status` を使用して詳細な変更を追跡し、`^` サフィックスを使用して前のコミットからのファイルの回復を行う。","ko":"에이전트가 `git rev-parse`를 사용하여 커밋 기록을 탐색하고 reflog를 사용하여 삭제된 파일을 복구할 수 있는 기능을 제공하며, `--name-status`를 사용하여 자세한 변경 사항을 추적하고 `^` 접미사를 사용하여 이전 커밋에서 파일을 복구합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a navegar por el historial de commits utilizando `git rev-parse` y a recuperar archivos eliminados a través de reflog, utilizando `--name-status` para un seguimiento detallado de cambios y el sufijo `^` para la recuperación de archivos de commits anteriores.","fr":"Permet aux agents de naviguer dans l''historique des commits à l''aide de `git rev-parse` et de récupérer des fichiers supprimés via reflog, en utilisant `--name-status` pour un suivi détaillé des modifications et le suffixe `^` pour la récupération de fichiers à partir de commits précédents.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Mitteln, die Commit-Historie mit `git rev-parse` zu navigieren und gelöschte Dateien über reflog wiederherzustellen, wobei `--name-status` für eine detaillierte Änderungsverfolgung und das Suffix `^` für die Dateiwiederherstellung aus vorherigen Commits verwendet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a navegar pelo histórico de commits usando `git rev-parse` e recuperar arquivos excluídos via reflog, utilizando `--name-status` para rastreamento detalhado de alterações e sufixo `^` para recuperação de arquivos de commits anteriores.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью навигации по истории коммитов с помощью `git rev-parse` и восстановления удаленных файлов через reflog, используя `--name-status` для подробного отслеживания изменений и суффикса `^` для восстановления файлов из предыдущих коммитов.","ar":"يمنح العملاء القدرة على التنقل في تاريخ الإلتزامات باستخدام `git rev-parse` واستعادة الملفات المحذوفة عبر سجل الإشارات، باستخدام `--name-status` لتتبع التغييرات بالتفصيل وإضافة `^` لاستعادة الملفات من الإلتزامات السابقة."},"useCases":{"en":["Navigating commit history with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`","Recovering deleted files using reflog and checkout","Analyzing commit changes with `--name-status`"],"zh":["使用 `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` 导航提交历史","使用 reflog 和 checkout 恢复删除的文件","使用 `--name-status` 分析提交更改"],"ja":["コミット履歴のナビゲーションに `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` を使用する","reflog と checkout を使用して削除されたファイルを回復する","コミットの変更を分析するために `--name-status` を使用する"],"ko":["커밋 기록 탐색에 `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` 사용","reflog와 checkout을 사용하여 삭제된 파일을 복구","커밋 변경 분석에 `--name-status` 사용"],"es":["Navegar por el historial de commits con `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`","Recuperar archivos eliminados utilizando reflog y checkout","Analizar los cambios de los commits con `--name-status`"],"fr":["Naviguer dans l''historique des commits avec `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`","Récupérer des fichiers supprimés en utilisant reflog et checkout","Analyser les modifications des commits avec `--name-status`"],"de":["Durch die Commit-Historie navigieren mit `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`","Gelöschte Dateien mit reflog und checkout wiederherstellen","Commit-Änderungen mit `--name-status` analysieren"],"pt":["Navegar pelo histórico de commits com `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`","Recuperar arquivos excluídos usando reflog e checkout","Analizar alterações de commits com `--name-status`"],"ru":["Навигация по истории коммитов с помощью `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`","Восстановление удаленных файлов с помощью reflog и checkout","Анализ изменений коммитов с помощью `--name-status`"],"ar":["التنقل في تاريخ الإلتزامات باستخدام `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`","استعادة الملفات المحذوفة باستخدام سجل الإشارات والتحقق","تحليل التغييرات في الإلتزامات باستخدام `--name-status`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation","Limited to Git-based version control systems"],"zh":["需要 Git 安装","仅限 Git 基础的版本控制系统"],"ja":["Git のインストールが必要","Git ベースのバージョン管理システムのみ"],"ko":["Git 설치가 필요","Git 기반 버전 관리 시스템만 해당"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de Git","Limitado a sistemas de control de versiones basados en Git"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Git","Limité aux systèmes de contrôle de version basés sur Git"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von Git","Begrenzt auf Git-basierte Versionskontrollsysteme"],"pt":["Requer instalação do Git","Limitado a sistemas de controle de versão baseados em Git"],"ru":["Требуется установка Git","Ограничен системами контроля версий на основе Git"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Git","محدود بنظم التحكم في الإصدارات التي تعتمد على Git"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Intelligent-Data-Design-Inc/NEP/netcdf-architecture', 'community', 'Intelligent-Data-Design-Inc', 'NEP', 'Intelligent-Data-Design-Inc/NEP', 'netcdf-architecture', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z', '2026-02-18T11:54:33.430Z', NULL, '{"id":"Intelligent-Data-Design-Inc/NEP/netcdf-architecture","name":"netcdf-architecture","description":{"zh":"NetCDF-C 是一个多格式 I/O 库，采用.dispatch 表架构，提供统一的 API","ja":"NetCDF-C は、dispatch テーブル アーキテクチャを採用した多形式 I/O ライブラリで、統一された API を提供","ko":"NetCDF-C 는 dispatch 테이블 아키텍처를採用한 다중 형식 I/O 라이브러리로서, 통일된 API 를 제공","es":"La arquitectura NetCDF-C es una biblioteca de E/S multi-formato que proporciona una API unificada para varios formatos de almacenamiento","fr":"L''architecture NetCDF-C est une bibliothèque de E/S multi-format qui fournit une API unifiée pour plusieurs formats de stockage","de":"Die NetCDF-C-Architektur ist eine Multi-Format-E/A-Bibliothek, die eine einheitliche API für verschiedene Speicherformate bietet","pt":"A arquitetura NetCDF-C é uma biblioteca de E/S multi-formato que fornece uma API unificada para vários formatos de armazenamento.","ru":"Архитектура NetCDF-C - это библиотека многоформатного ввода/вывода, обеспечивающая унифицированный API для нескольких форматов хранения.","ar":"هندسة NetCDF-C هي مكتبة إدخال/إخراج متعددة التنسيقات توفر واجهة برمجة تطبيقات موحدة للعديد من تنسيقات التخزين.","en":"NetCDF Expansion Pack"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"NetCDF-C 架构技能","ja":"NetCDF-C アーキテクチャ スキル","ko":"NetCDF-C 아키텍처 스킬","es":"Arquitectura NetCDF-C: Guía para desarrolladores","fr":"Architecture NetCDF-C : Guide pour les développeurs","de":"NetCDF-C-Architektur: Entwicklerleitfaden","pt":"Arquitetura NetCDF-C: Guia para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Архитектура NetCDF-C: Руководство для Разработчиков","ar":"هندسة NetCDF-C: دليل للمطورين","en":"netcdf-architecture"},"description":{"zh":"NetCDF-C 是一个多格式 I/O 库，采用.dispatch 表架构，提供统一的 API","ja":"NetCDF-C は、dispatch テーブル アーキテクチャを採用した多形式 I/O ライブラリで、統一された API を提供","ko":"NetCDF-C 는 dispatch 테이블 아키텍처를採用한 다중 형식 I/O 라이브러리로서, 통일된 API 를 제공","es":"La arquitectura NetCDF-C es una biblioteca de E/S multi-formato que proporciona una API unificada para varios formatos de almacenamiento","fr":"L''architecture NetCDF-C est une bibliothèque de E/S multi-format qui fournit une API unifiée pour plusieurs formats de stockage","de":"Die NetCDF-C-Architektur ist eine Multi-Format-E/A-Bibliothek, die eine einheitliche API für verschiedene Speicherformate bietet","pt":"A arquitetura NetCDF-C é uma biblioteca de E/S multi-formato que fornece uma API unificada para vários formatos de armazenamento.","ru":"Архитектура NetCDF-C - это библиотека многоформатного ввода/вывода, обеспечивающая унифицированный API для нескольких форматов хранения.","ar":"هندسة NetCDF-C هي مكتبة إدخال/إخراج متعددة التنسيقات توفر واجهة برمجة تطبيقات موحدة للعديد من تنسيقات التخزين.","en":"NetCDF Expansion Pack"},"definition":{"en":"NetCDF Expansion Pack"},"features":{"zh":["dispatch 表架构","多格式 I/O","统一的 API","10 个用户定义格式插槽","函数指针表"],"ja":["dispatch テーブル アーキテクチャ","多形式 I/O","統一された API","10 個のユーザー定義形式スロット","関数ポインタ テーブル"],"ko":["dispatch 테이블 아키텍처","다중 형식 I/O","통일된 API","10 개의 사용자 정의 형식 슬롯","함수 포인터 테이블"],"es":["Arquitectura de tabla de despacho","API unificada para varios formatos de almacenamiento","Soporte para 7+ formatos de almacenamiento integrados","10 ranuras para formatos de usuario definidos","Diseño de patrón de función de puntero"],"fr":["Architecture de table de dispatch","API unifiée pour plusieurs formats de stockage","Prise en charge de 7+ formats de stockage intégrés","10 emplacements pour les formats définis par l''utilisateur","Conception de modèle de fonction de pointeur"],"de":["Dispatch-Tabelle-Architektur","Einheitliche API für verschiedene Speicherformate","Unterstützung für 7+ integrierte Speicherformate","10 Schlitze für benutzerdefinierte Formate","Funktionstyp-Muster-Design"],"pt":["Arquitetura de dispatch table","API unificada para vários formatos de armazenamento","10 slots de formato de usuário definido (UDF)","7 formatos de armazenamento internos","Funcionalidade de ponteiro de função para implementações específicas de formato"],"ru":["Архитектура диспетчерской таблицы","Унифицированный API для нескольких форматов хранения","10 слотов формата пользователя (UDF)","7 встроенных форматов хранения","Функциональность указателя функции для реализаций, специфичных для формата"],"ar":["هندسة جدول التوجيه","واجهة برمجة تطبيقات موحدة للعديد من تنسيقات التخزين","10 فتحات تنسيق المستخدم المحدد (UDF)","7 تنسيقات تخزين مدمجة","وظيفة مؤشر الدالة لتنفيذ تنسيق محدد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["NetCDF-C","dispatch 表","多格式 I/O","统一的 API","用户定义格式","函数指针表","NetCDF-C 库","NetCDF-C 架构"],"ja":["NetCDF-C","dispatch テーブル","多形式 I/O","統一された API","ユーザー定義形式","関数ポインタ テーブル","NetCDF-C ライブラリ","NetCDF-C アーキテクチャ"],"ko":["NetCDF-C","dispatch 테이블","다중 형식 I/O","통일된 API","사용자 정의 형식","함수 포인터 테이블","NetCDF-C 라이브러리","NetCDF-C 아키텍처"],"es":["NetCDF-C","arquitectura de biblioteca","E/S multi-formato","API unificada","tabla de despacho","formatos de almacenamiento","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["NetCDF-C","architecture de bibliothèque","E/S multi-format","API unifiée","table de dispatch","formats de stockage","développement de logiciel"],"de":["NetCDF-C","Bibliotheksarchitektur","Multi-Format-E/A","Einheitliche API","Dispatch-Tabelle","Speicherformate","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["NetCDF-C","arquitetura de dispatch table","API unificada","formatos de armazenamento","desenvolvimento de software","biblioteca de E/S"],"ru":["NetCDF-C","архитектура диспетчерской таблицы","унифицированный API","форматы хранения","разработка программного обеспечения","библиотека ввода/вывода"],"ar":["NetCDF-C","هندسة جدول التوجيه","واجهة برمجة تطبيقات موحدة","تنسيقات التخزين","تطوير البرمجيات","مكتبة إدخال/إخراج"]}},"owner":"Intelligent-Data-Design-Inc","repo":"NEP","repoPath":"Intelligent-Data-Design-Inc/NEP","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"netcdf-architecture","description":"Understanding the NetCDF-C library architecture including dispatch tables, format implementations (NetCDF-3, HDF5, Zarr, DAP), I/O layers, and metadata structures. Use when working on NetCDF-C codebase, debugging format issues, adding new features, or understanding how different storage backends interact.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# NetCDF-C Architecture Skill\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive knowledge of the NetCDF-C library architecture to help you navigate, understand, and modify the codebase effectively.\n\n## Overview\n\nNetCDF-C is a multi-format I/O library built on a **dispatch table architecture** that provides a unified API across 7+ built-in storage formats plus 10 user-defined format (UDF) slots. The core design pattern uses function pointer tables to route operations to format-specific implementations.\n\n**Built","body":"# NetCDF-C Architecture Skill\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive knowledge of the NetCDF-C library architecture to help you navigate, understand, and modify the codebase effectively.\n\n## Overview\n\nNetCDF-C is a multi-format I/O library built on a **dispatch table architecture** that provides a unified API across 7+ built-in storage formats plus 10 user-defined format (UDF) slots. The core design pattern uses function pointer tables to route operations to format-specific implementations.\n\n**Built-in formats**: NetCDF-3 (CDF-1/2/5), NetCDF-4/HDF5, Zarr, DAP2, DAP4\n**User-defined formats**: UDF0-UDF9 slots for custom format plugins\n\n## Core Architecture Pattern\n\n### Dispatch Table Design\n\nEvery file format implements the same `NC_Dispatch` interface containing ~70 function pointers:\n\n```c\nstruct NC_Dispatch {\n    int model;                    // Format identifier\n    int dispatch_version;         // Compatibility version\n    \n    // File operations\n    int (*create)(...);\n    int (*open)(...);\n    int (*close)(...);\n    \n    // Variable I/O\n    int (*get_vara)(...);\n    int (*put_vara)(...);\n    \n    // Metadata operations\n    int (*def_dim)(...);\n    int (*def_var)(...);\n    int (*put_att)(...);\n    \n    // ... ~60 more function pointers\n};\n```\n\n**Location**: `include/netcdf_dispatch.h`\n\n### Common File Handle (NC Structure)\n\nEvery open file is represented by an `NC` struct:\n\n```c\ntypedef struct NC {\n    int ext_ncid;              // External ID (user-visible)\n    int int_ncid;              // Internal ID (format-specific)\n    const NC_Dispatch* dispatch;  // Function pointer table\n    void* dispatchdata;        // Format-specific metadata\n    char* path;                // File path\n    int mode;                  // Open mode flags\n} NC;\n```\n\n**Location**: `include/nc.h`\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n### Primary Libraries\n\n- **`libdispatch/`** - Central routing layer, API entry points, utilities, UDF plugin loading\n- **`libsrc/`** - Classic NetCDF-3 implementation (CDF-1, CDF-2, CDF-5)\n- **`libsrc4/`** - NetCDF-4 enhanced model coordination\n- **`libhdf5/`** - HDF5 storage backend\n- **`libnczarr/`** - Zarr cloud-native storage\n- **`libdap2/`** + **`oc2/`** - OPeNDAP DAP2 client\n- **`libdap4/`** - OPeNDAP DAP4 client\n- **`libhdf4/`** - HDF4 file access (optional)\n- **User plugins** - External shared libraries for UDF0-UDF9 slots\n\n### Support Libraries\n\n- **`include/`** - Public API headers and internal interfaces\n- **`libncpoco/`** - Portable components\n- **`libncxml/`** - XML parsing for DAP4\n- **`liblib/`** - Additional utilities\n\n## Key Components by Library\n\n### libdispatch/ - The Routing Layer\n\n**Purpose**: Provides unified API facade and routes calls to appropriate format implementations.\n\n**Critical Files**:\n- `ddispatch.c` - Dispatch initialization, global state management\n- `dfile.c` - File open/create orchestration, format detection\n- `dvarget.c`, `dvarput.c` - Variable I/O entry points\n- `dvar.c`, `datt.c`, `ddim.c` - Metadata operation entry points\n- `dinfermodel.c` - Format detection (magic numbers, URLs)\n\n**Format Detection Logic**:\n1. Check magic number (first 8 bytes) - includes user-defined magic numbers\n2. Parse URL scheme (http://, s3://, file://)\n3. Analyze mode flags (NC_NETCDF4, NC_CLASSIC_MODEL, NC_UDF0-NC_UDF9, etc.)\n4. Select appropriate dispatch table (built-in or user-defined)\n\n**Utilities**:\n- `ncjson.c` - JSON parsing\n- `ncuri.c` - URI parsing\n- `dauth.c` - Authentication (includes RC file parsing for UDF configuration)\n- `dhttp.c` - HTTP operations\n- `ds3util.c` - S3/cloud utilities\n- `drc.c` - RC file parsing for UDF plugin configuration\n- `dutil.c` - Plugin loading (dlopen/LoadLibrary)\n\n### libsrc/ - Classic NetCDF-3\n\n**Purpose**: Implements traditional binary NetCDF formats.\n\n**Dispatch Table**: `NC3_dispatcher` in `nc3dispatch.c`\n\n**Metadata Structure**: `NC3_INFO` - Simple arrays with hashmaps\n\n**Critical Files**:\n- `nc3dispatch.c` (517 lines) - Dispatch table implementation\n- `nc3internal.c` - Metadata management\n- `ncx.c` (743KB) - XDR-like encoding/decoding for all data types\n- `putget.c` (353KB) - Variable I/O operations\n- `attr.c` (47KB) - Attribute operations\n- `var.c`, `dim.c` - Variable and dimension management\n\n**I/O Abstraction (ncio layer)**:\n- `posixio.c` - Standard POSIX file I/O\n- `memio.c` - In-memory files\n- `httpio.c` - HTTP byte-range access\n- `s3io.c` - S3 object storage\n\n**Data Structures**:\n```c\ntypedef struct NC3_INFO {\n    NC_dimarray dims;      // Dimensions\n    NC_attrarray attrs;    // Global attributes\n    NC_vararray vars;      // Variables\n    size_t xsz;           // External size\n    size_t begin_var;     // Offset to variables\n    size_t begin_rec;     // Offset to record data\n    size_t recsize;       // Record size\n    // ... more fields\n} NC3_INFO;\n```\n\n### libsrc4/ - NetCDF-4 Coordination\n\n**Purpose**: Thin coordination layer for NetCDF-4 enhanced features (groups, user-defined types).\n\n**Note**: This is NOT a complete implementation - it delegates to HDF5 or Zarr backends.\n\n**Files**:\n- `nc4dispatch.c` - Minimal initialization\n- `nc4attr.c`, `nc4dim.c`, `nc4var.c` - Enhanced metadata operations\n- `nc4grp.c` - Group operations\n- `nc4type.c` - User-defined type operations\n- `nc4internal.c` - Common infrastructure\n\n### libhdf5/ - HDF5 Storage Backend\n\n**Purpose**: Implements NetCDF-4 using HDF5 as the storage format.\n\n**Dispatch Table**: `HDF5_dispatcher` in `hdf5dispatch.c`\n\n**Metadata Structure**: `NC_FILE_INFO_T` with hierarchical groups\n\n**Critical Files**:\n- `hdf5dispatch.c` (152 lines) - Dispatch table\n- `nc4hdf.c` (87KB) - Core HDF5 integration\n- `hdf5open.c` (99KB) - File opening, metadata reading from HDF5\n- `hdf5var.c` (85KB) - Variable I/O with chunking, compression, filters\n- `hdf5attr.c` (28KB) - Attribute operations\n- `hdf5filter.c` - Filter/compression plugin management\n- `H5FDhttp.c` - HTTP virtual file driver for byte-range access\n\n**Key Data Structures**:\n```c\ntypedef struct NC_FILE_INFO_T {\n    NC_GRP_INFO_T* root_grp;    // Root group\n    int no_write;                // Read-only flag\n    void* format_file_info;      // HDF5-specific data\n    // ... more fields\n} NC_FILE_INFO_T;\n\ntypedef struct NC_VAR_INFO_T {\n    NC_OBJ hdr;                  // Name and ID\n    NC_GRP_INFO_T* container;    // Parent group\n    size_t ndims;                // Number of dimensions\n    int* dimids;                 // Dimension IDs\n    size_t* chunksizes;          // Chunk sizes\n    int storage;                 // Chunked/contiguous/compact\n    int endianness;              // Byte order\n    void* filters;               // Compression filters\n    // ... more fields\n} NC_VAR_INFO_T;\n```\n\n**Delegates to**: HDF5 library → HDF5 VFD layer → actual storage\n\n### libnczarr/ - Zarr Storage\n\n**Purpose**: Cloud-native storage using Zarr format specification.\n\n**Dispatch Table**: `NCZ_dispatcher` in `zdispatch.c`\n\n**Metadata Structure**: `NC_FILE_INFO_T` (same as HDF5)\n\n**Critical Files**:\n- `zdispatch.c` (323 lines) - Dispatch table\n- `zarr.c` - Main Zarr implementation\n- `zsync.c` (84KB) - Data synchronization, chunk management\n- `zvar.c` (76KB) - Variable operations\n- `zfilter.c` - Codec pipeline (compression, filters)\n- `zxcache.c` - Chunk caching\n\n**Storage Abstraction (zmap)**:\n- `zmap.c` - Abstract storage interface\n- `zmap_file.c` - Filesystem backend\n- `zmap_s3sdk.c` - AWS S3 backend\n- `zmap_zip.c` - ZIP archive backend\n\n**Key Feature**: JSON metadata (.zarray, .zgroup, .zattrs files)\n\n### libdap2/ + oc2/ - OPeNDAP DAP2 Client\n\n**Purpose**: Access remote OPeNDAP servers using DAP2 protocol.\n\n**Dispatch Table**: `NCD2_dispatcher` in `ncd2dispatch.c`\n\n**Components**:\n- `ncd2dispatch.c` (85KB) - Dispatch implementation\n- `getvara.c` (44KB) - Maps NetCDF API to DAP requests\n- `constraints.c` - DAP constraint expression handling\n- `cache.c` - Response caching\n\n**OC2 Library** (OPeNDAP Client in `oc2/`):\n- `oc.c` (62KB) - Main client implementation\n- `dapparse.c`, `daplex.c` - DDS/DAS parsing\n- `ocdata.c` - Data retrieval and decoding\n- `occurlfunctions.c` - HTTP/libcurl integration\n\n### libdap4/ - OPeNDAP DAP4 Client\n\n**Purpose**: Access remote DAP4 servers (newer protocol).\n\n**Dispatch Table**: `NCD4_dispatcher` in `ncd4dispatch.c`\n\n**Critical Files**:\n- `ncd4dispatch.c` (24KB) - Dispatch table\n- `d4parser.c` (49KB) - DMR (Dataset Metadata Response) parsing\n- `d4data.c` - Binary data handling\n- `d4chunk.c` - Chunked response processing\n- `d4meta.c` (34KB) - Metadata translation to NetCDF model\n- `d4curlfunctions.c` - HTTP operations\n\n### User-Defined Formats (UDFs)\n\n**Purpose**: Extensible plugin system for custom file formats and storage backends.\n\n**Available Slots**: UDF0 through UDF9 (10 independent format slots)\n\n**Dispatch Tables**: Registered via `nc_def_user_format()` or RC file configuration\n\n**Key Features**:\n- **Plugin loading**: Automatic loading from RC files during `nc_initialize()`\n- **Magic number detection**: Optional automatic format detection\n- **Shared libraries**: .so (Unix) or .dll (Windows) plugins\n- **Full API support**: Plugins implement complete `NC_Dispatch` interface\n\n**Plugin Architecture**:\n\n1. **Dispatch Table**: Plugin provides `NC_Dispatch` structure with function pointers\n2. **Initialization Function**: Exported function called during plugin load\n3. **Format-Specific Code**: Custom implementation of file I/O and data operations\n\n**Registration Methods**:\n\n**Programmatic Registration**:\n```c\n// Register UDF in slot 0 with magic number\nnc_def_user_format(NC_UDF0 | NC_NETCDF4, &my_dispatcher, \"MYFORMAT\");\n\n// Query registered UDF\nNC_Dispatch *disp;\nnc_inq_user_format(NC_UDF0, &disp, magic_buffer);\n```\n\n**RC File Configuration** (`.ncrc`):\n```ini\nNETCDF.UDF0.LIBRARY=/usr/local/lib/libmyformat.so\nNETCDF.UDF0.INIT=myformat_init\nNETCDF.UDF0.MAGIC=MYFORMAT\n```\n\n**Plugin Loading Process**:\n1. RC files parsed during `nc_initialize()`\n2. Library loaded via `dlopen()` (Unix) or `LoadLibrary()` (Windows)\n3. Init function located via `dlsym()` or `GetProcAddress()`\n4. Init function calls `nc_def_user_format()` to register dispatch table\n5. Dispatch table ABI version verified (`NC_DISPATCH_VERSION`)\n6. Plugin remains loaded for process lifetime\n\n**RC File Search Order**:\n1. `$HOME/.ncrc`\n2. `$HOME/.daprc`\n3. `$HOME/.dodsrc`\n4. `$CWD/.ncrc`\n5. `$CWD/.daprc`\n6. `$CWD/.dodsrc`\n\n**UDF Slot Modes**:\n- **UDF0, UDF1**: Original slots, mode flags in lower 16 bits\n- **UDF2-UDF9**: Extended slots, mode flags in upper 16 bits\n\n**Pre-defined Dispatch Functions** (for plugin use):\n- `NC_RO_*` - Read-only stubs (return `NC_EPERM`)\n- `NC_NOTNC4_*` - Not-NetCDF-4 stubs (return `NC_ENOTNC4`)\n- `NC_NOTNC3_*` - Not-NetCDF-3 stubs (return `NC_ENOTNC3`)\n- `NC_NOOP_*` - No-operation stubs (return `NC_NOERR`)\n- `NCDEFAULT_*` - Generic implementations\n- `NC4_*` - NetCDF-4 inquiry functions using internal metadata model\n\n**Critical Files**:\n- `libdispatch/dfile.c` - UDF dispatch table storage (`UDF0_dispatch_table`, etc.)\n- `libdispatch/ddispatch.c` - `nc_def_user_format()`, `nc_inq_user_format()`\n- `libdispatch/drc.c` - RC file parsing for UDF configuration\n- `libdispatch/dutil.c` - Plugin library loading\n- `include/netcdf_dispatch.h` - `NC_Dispatch` structure definition\n- `libdispatch/dreadonly.c` - Pre-defined read-only stubs\n- `libdispatch/dnotnc*.c` - Pre-defined not-supported stubs\n\n**Example Plugin Structure**:\n```c\n#include \"netcdf_dispatch.h\"\n\nstatic NC_Dispatch my_dispatcher = {\n    NC_FORMATX_UDF0,        // Use UDF slot 0\n    NC_DISPATCH_VERSION,    // Current ABI version\n    \n    NC_RO_create,           // Read-only: use predefined function\n    my_open,                // Custom open function\n    my_close,               // Custom close function\n    NC4_inq,                // Use NC4 inquiry defaults\n    // ... ~70 function pointers total\n};\n\n// Initialization function - must be exported\nint my_plugin_init(void) {\n    return nc_def_user_format(NC_UDF0 | NC_NETCDF4, \n                              &my_dispatcher, \n                              \"MYFMT\");\n}\n```\n\n**Security Considerations**:\n- RC files must specify absolute library paths\n- Plugins execute arbitrary code in process space\n- Only load trusted libraries\n- Library verifies dispatch table ABI version\n\n**Common Use Cases**:\n- Proprietary or specialized file formats\n- Custom storage backends\n- Format translation layers\n- Domain-specific data formats\n- Integration with legacy systems\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### 1. API Call Flow\n\n```\nUser calls nc_get_vara(ncid, varid, start, count, data)\n    ↓\nlibdispatch/dvarget.c\n    ↓\nLookup NC* from ncid → get dispatch table\n    ↓\ndispatch->get_vara(...)\n    ↓\nFormat-specific implementation:\n    • NC3_get_vara() → ncx.c XDR decode → ncio read\n    • NC4_get_vara() → HDF5 API → chunk cache → decompress\n    • NCZ_get_vara() → zmap retrieve → codec pipeline\n    • NCD2_get_vara() → HTTP request → parse DDS/DAS\n```\n\n### 2. File Opening\n\n```\nnc_open(path, mode, &ncid)\n    ↓\nlibdispatch/dfile.c: NC_open()\n    ↓\ndinfermodel.c: Detect format\n    • Check magic number\n    • Parse URL scheme\n    • Analyze mode flags\n    ↓\nSelect dispatch table\n    ↓\ndispatch->open(path, mode, ...)\n    ↓\nFormat-specific open implementation\n    ↓\nReturn ncid to user\n```\n\n### 3. Metadata Access\n\nAll formats use indexed structures for fast lookup:\n- **NC3**: Arrays with `NC_hashmap`\n- **NC4/HDF5/Zarr**: `NCindex` (hash-based index)\n\n## Important Headers\n\n### Public API\n- `netcdf.h` - Main public API\n- `netcdf_par.h` - Parallel I/O extensions\n- `netcdf_filter.h` - Filter API\n- `netcdf_mem.h` - In-memory file API\n\n### Internal Interfaces\n- `ncdispatch.h` - Dispatch layer interfaces\n- `netcdf_dispatch.h` - NC_Dispatch structure definition\n- `nc.h` - NC structure and common functions\n- `nc3internal.h` - NetCDF-3 internal structures\n- `nc4internal.h` - NetCDF-4 internal structures\n- `nc3dispatch.h`, `nc4dispatch.h`, `hdf5dispatch.h` - Format-specific dispatch headers\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n- **Adding new features** to NetCDF-C\n- **Debugging format-specific issues** (e.g., HDF5 vs Zarr differences)\n- **Understanding data flow** through the library\n- **Implementing new dispatch tables** or storage backends\n- **Developing UDF plugins** for custom file formats\n- **Modifying I/O operations** (chunking, compression, filters)\n- **Working with metadata structures** (groups, types, dimensions)\n- **Investigating performance issues** (caching, I/O patterns)\n- **Integrating new protocols** (new remote access methods)\n- **Extending NetCDF-C** with proprietary or domain-specific formats\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Find the Right File\n\n**For API entry points**: Look in `libdispatch/d*.c`\n**For NetCDF-3 operations**: Look in `libsrc/`\n**For HDF5 operations**: Look in `libhdf5/`\n**For Zarr operations**: Look in `libnczarr/`\n**For remote access**: Look in `libdap2/` or `libdap4/`\n**For data encoding**: Look in `libsrc/ncx.c`\n**For I/O backends**: Look in `libsrc/*io.c` or `libnczarr/zmap*.c`\n\n### Common Tasks\n\n**Adding a new API function**:\n1. Add to `include/netcdf.h`\n2. Add entry point in `libdispatch/`\n3. Add to `NC_Dispatch` structure\n4. Implement in each format''s dispatch table\n\n**Adding a new format**:\n1. Create new library directory\n2. Implement `NC_Dispatch` table\n3. Register in `libdispatch/ddispatch.c`\n4. Add format detection logic\n\n**Debugging I/O issues**:\n1. Enable logging: `export NETCDF_LOG_LEVEL=5`\n2. Check dispatch table selection\n3. Trace through format-specific implementation\n4. Check I/O layer (ncio, HDF5 VFD, zmap)\n\n## Additional Resources\n\nSee [references/COMPONENTS.md](references/COMPONENTS.md) for detailed component descriptions.\n\nSee [references/DATA-STRUCTURES.md](references/DATA-STRUCTURES.md) for complete data structure documentation.\n\nSee [references/DISPATCH-TABLES.md](references/DISPATCH-TABLES.md) for all dispatch table implementations.\n\nSee [references/UDF-PLUGINS.md](references/UDF-PLUGINS.md) for comprehensive UDF plugin development guide.\n\nSee [references/EXAMPLES.md](references/EXAMPLES.md) for programming examples and common patterns.\n\nSee [references/FORTRAN-INTERFACE.md](references/FORTRAN-INTERFACE.md) for NetCDF Fortran 90 API documentation and usage patterns.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:54:33.430Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing to navigate and modify NetCDF file formats with advanced dispatch table architecture","zh":"非常适合需要导航和修改NetCDF文件格式的数据分析代理，具有高级的调度表架构","ja":"NetCDFファイル形式をナビゲートおよび修正する必要があるデータ分析エージェントに最適です。高度なディスパッチテーブルアーキテクチャを備えています","ko":"NetCDF 파일 형식을 탐색하고 수정해야 하는 데이터 분석 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 고급 디스패치 테이블 아키텍처가 있습니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan navegar y modificar formatos de archivos NetCDF con arquitectura de tabla de despacho avanzada","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse de Données ayant besoin de naviguer et de modifier les formats de fichiers NetCDF avec une architecture de table de dispatch avancée","de":"Perfekt für Data Analysis Agents, die NetCDF-Dateiformate mit erweiterter Dispatch-Tabelle-Architektur navigieren und modifizieren müssen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que precisam navegar e modificar formatos de arquivos NetCDF com arquitetura de tabela de despacho avançada","ru":"Идеально для Агентов Анализа Данных, которым необходимо ориентироваться и изменять форматы файлов NetCDF с помощью продвинутой архитектуры диспетчерской таблицы","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء تحليل البيانات الذين يحتاجون إلى التنقل وتعديل تنسيقات الملفات NetCDF مع هندسة جدول التوجيه المتقدمة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to unify APIs across multiple storage formats, utilizing function pointer tables to route operations to format-specific implementations, and leveraging the NetCDF-C library for efficient data I/O operations","zh":"使代理能够统一多个存储格式的API，利用函数指针表将操作路由到格式特定的实现，并利用NetCDF-C库进行高效的数据I/O操作","ja":"エージェントが複数のストレージ形式のAPIを統一し、関数ポインタテーブルを使用して操作を形式ごとの実装にルーティングし、NetCDF-Cライブラリを使用して効率的なデータI/O操作を実現できるようにします","ko":"에이전트가 여러 저장소 형식의 API를 통일하고 함수 포인터 테이블을 사용하여 작업을 형식별 구현으로 라우팅하며 NetCDF-C 라이브러리를 사용하여 효율적인 데이터 I/O 작업을 수행할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a unificar las API en varios formatos de almacenamiento, utilizando tablas de punteros a funciones para enrutrar operaciones a implementaciones específicas de formato, y aprovechando la biblioteca NetCDF-C para operaciones de E/S de datos eficientes","fr":"Permet aux agents d''unifier les API sur plusieurs formats de stockage, en utilisant des tables de pointeurs de fonctions pour acheminer les opérations vers des implémentations spécifiques au format, et en exploitant la bibliothèque NetCDF-C pour des opérations de E/S de données efficaces","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, APIs über mehrere Speicherformate zu vereinheitlichen, indem Funktionstabelle-Zeiger verwendet werden, um Operationen an formatsspezifische Implementierungen zu übergeben, und die NetCDF-C-Bibliothek für effiziente Daten-E/A-Operationen nutzt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a unificar APIs em vários formatos de armazenamento, utilizando tabelas de ponteiros de função para encaminhar operações para implementações específicas de formato, e aproveitando a biblioteca NetCDF-C para operações de E/S de dados eficientes","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью унифицировать API в нескольких форматах хранения, используя таблицы указателей функций для маршрутизации операций к реализациям, специфичным для формата, и используя библиотеку NetCDF-C для эффективных операций ввода/вывода данных","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من توحيد واجهات برمجة التطبيقات عبر عدة تنسيقات تخزين، باستخدام جداول مؤشرات الدالة لتنفيذ العمليات إلى تنفيذات محددة بالتنسيق، وتحقيق бібліoteca NetCDF-C لعمليات الإدخال والإخراج الفعالة للبيانات"},"useCases":{"en":["Navigating NetCDF file structures with built-in storage formats","Modifying user-defined format slots for custom data storage","Optimizing data I/O operations with dispatch table architecture"],"zh":["带有内置存储格式的NetCDF文件结构导航","用于自定义数据存储的用户定义格式槽修改","使用调度表架构优化数据I/O操作"],"ja":["内蔵ストレージ形式を備えたNetCDFファイル構造のナビゲート","カスタムデータストレージ用のユーザー定義形式スロットの修正","ディスパッチテーブルアーキテクチャを使用したデータI/O操作の最適化"],"ko":["내장 저장소 형식을 갖춘 NetCDF 파일 구조 탐색","사용자 정의 형식 슬롯 수정을 위한 사용자 정의 데이터 저장","디스패치 테이블 아키텍처를 사용한 데이터 I/O 작업 최적화"],"es":["Navegar estructuras de archivos NetCDF con formatos de almacenamiento integrados","Modificar ranuras de formato definidas por el usuario para el almacenamiento de datos personalizados","Optimizar operaciones de E/S de datos con arquitectura de tabla de despacho"],"fr":["Naviguer dans les structures de fichiers NetCDF avec des formats de stockage intégrés","Modifier les emplacements de format définis par l''utilisateur pour un stockage de données personnalisé","Optimiser les opérations de E/S de données avec une architecture de table de dispatch"],"de":["NetCDF-Dateistrukturen mit integrierten Speicherformaten navigieren","Benutzerdefinierte Format-Schlitze für benutzerdefinierten Datenspeicher modifizieren","Daten-E/A-Operationen mit Dispatch-Tabelle-Architektur optimieren"],"pt":["Navegando estruturas de arquivos NetCDF com formatos de armazenamento integrados","Modificando slots de formato definidos pelo usuário para armazenamento de dados personalizado","Otimizando operações de E/S de dados com arquitetura de tabela de despacho"],"ru":["Ориентирование в структурах файлов NetCDF с встроенными форматами хранения","Изменение слотов формата, определенных пользователем, для индивидуального хранения данных","Оптимизация операций ввода/вывода данных с помощью архитектуры диспетчерской таблицы"],"ar":["ملاحة هياكل ملفات NetCDF مع تنسيقات تخزين مدمجة","تعديل فتحات التنسيق المحددة من قبل المستخدم لتخزين البيانات المخصص","تحسين عمليات الإدخال والإخراج للبيانات مع هندسة جدول التوجيه"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of NetCDF-C library architecture","Limited to NetCDF file formats","Dependent on function pointer table implementations"],"zh":["需要了解NetCDF-C库架构","仅限NetCDF文件格式","依赖于函数指针表实现"],"ja":["NetCDF-Cライブラリアーキテクチャの理解が必要","NetCDFファイル形式に限定される","関数ポインタテーブル実装に依存する"],"ko":["NetCDF-C 라이브러리 아키텍처를 이해해야 함","NetCDF 파일 형식으로만 제한","함수 포인터 테이블 구현에 의존"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la arquitectura de la biblioteca NetCDF-C","Limitado a formatos de archivos NetCDF","Dependiente de implementaciones de tablas de punteros a funciones"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de l''architecture de la bibliothèque NetCDF-C","Limité aux formats de fichiers NetCDF","Dépendant des implémentations 