回帰検出","プロダクションシステムの構築","ベースラインの確立と進度の追跡"],"ko":["자동화된 지표","인간 평가","A/B 테스트","성능 회귀 감지","생산 시스템 구축","기준 설정 및 진행 상황 추적"],"es":["Estrategias de evaluación automatizadas","Prueba A/B para comparar modelos","Detección de regresiones de rendimiento","Validación de mejoras en los prompts","Creación de líneas de base y seguimiento del progreso","Depuración de comportamientos inesperados del modelo"],"fr":["Stratégies d''évaluation automatisées","Test A/B pour comparer les modèles","Détection de régressions de performances","Validation des améliorations des invites","Création de lignes de base et suivi des progrès","Débogage de comportements inattendus du modèle"],"de":["Automatisierte Bewertungsstrategien","A/B-Testing zum Vergleich von Modellen","Erkennung von Leistungsregressionen","Validierung von Verbesserungen bei Prompts","Erstellung von Basislinien und Verfolgung des Fortschritts","Fehlerbehebung bei unerwartetem Modellverhalten"],"pt":["Treinamento distribuído","Inferência avançada","Otimização de sistemas de computação","Avaliação de desempenho de aplicações LLM","Detecção de regressões de desempenho","Validação de melhorias de prompt"],"ru":["Распределенное обучение","Продвинутый вывод","Оптимизация систем вычислений","Оценка производительности приложений LLM","Обнаружение регрессий производительности","Проверка улучшений промпта"],"ar":["تدريب موزع","استدلال متقدم","تحسين أنظمة الحوسبة","تقييم أداء تطبيقات LLM","كشف انحدارات الأداء","تحقق التحسينات من التلميح"]},"keywords":{"zh":["LLM 评估","大型语言模型","自动化指标","人工评估","A/B 测试","性能优化","生产系统"],"ja":["LLM 評価","大規模言語モデル","自動化メトリック","人工評価","A/B テスト","パフォーマンス最適化","プロダクションシステム"],"ko":["LLM 평가","대규모 언어 모델","자동화된 지표","인간 평가","A/B 테스트","성능 최적화","생산 시스템"],"es":["evaluación de LLM","desarrollo de aplicaciones de inteligencia artificial","estrategias de evaluación","prueba A/B","mejora del rendimiento","depuración de modelos","líneas de base","seguimiento del progreso"],"fr":["évaluation de LLM","développement d''applications d''intelligence artificielle","stratégies d''évaluation","test A/B","amélioration des performances","débogage de modèles","lignes de base","suivi des progrès"],"de":["Bewertung von LLM","Entwicklung von KI-Anwendungen","Bewertungsstrategien","A/B-Testing","Leistungsverbesserung","Fehlerbehebung bei Modellen","Basislinien","Verfolgung des Fortschritts"],"pt":["avaliação de LLM","treinamento distribuído","inferência avançada","otimização de sistemas de computação","desempenho de aplicações LLM","regressões de desempenho","melhorias de prompt","sistemas de computação de alta potência"],"ru":["оценка LLM","распределенное обучение","продвинутый вывод","оптимизация систем вычислений","производительность приложений LLM","регрессии производительности","улучшения промпта","системы вычислений высокопроизводительные"],"ar":["تقييم LLM","تدريب موزع","استدلال متقدم","تحسين أنظمة الحوسبة","أداء تطبيقات LLM","انحدارات الأداء","تحسينات التلميح","نظم الحوسبة عالية الأداء"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"ugro","repoPath":"ollieb89/ugro","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.505Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"llm-evaluation","description":"Implement comprehensive evaluation strategies for LLM applications using automated metrics, human feedback, and benchmarking. Use when testing LLM performance, measuring AI application quality, or establishing evaluation frameworks.","bodyPreview":"# LLM Evaluation\n\nMaster comprehensive evaluation strategies for LLM applications, from automated metrics to human evaluation and A/B testing.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Measuring LLM application performance systematically\n- Comparing different models or prompts\n- Detecting performance regressions before deployment\n- Validating improvements from prompt changes\n- Building confidence in production systems\n- Establishing baselines and tracking progress over time\n- Debugging unexpected model beha","body":"# LLM Evaluation\n\nMaster comprehensive evaluation strategies for LLM applications, from automated metrics to human evaluation and A/B testing.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Measuring LLM application performance systematically\n- Comparing different models or prompts\n- Detecting performance regressions before deployment\n- Validating improvements from prompt changes\n- Building confidence in production systems\n- Establishing baselines and tracking progress over time\n- Debugging unexpected model behavior\n\n## Core Evaluation Types\n\n### 1. Automated Metrics\nFast, repeatable, scalable evaluation using computed scores.\n\n**Text Generation:**\n- **BLEU**: N-gram overlap (translation)\n- **ROUGE**: Recall-oriented (summarization)\n- **METEOR**: Semantic similarity\n- **BERTScore**: Embedding-based similarity\n- **Perplexity**: Language model confidence\n\n**Classification:**\n- **Accuracy**: Percentage correct\n- **Precision/Recall/F1**: Class-specific performance\n- **Confusion Matrix**: Error patterns\n- **AUC-ROC**: Ranking quality\n\n**Retrieval (RAG):**\n- **MRR**: Mean Reciprocal Rank\n- **NDCG**: Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain\n- **Precision@K**: Relevant in top K\n- **Recall@K**: Coverage in top K\n\n### 2. Human Evaluation\nManual assessment for quality aspects difficult to automate.\n\n**Dimensions:**\n- **Accuracy**: Factual correctness\n- **Coherence**: Logical flow\n- **Relevance**: Answers the question\n- **Fluency**: Natural language quality\n- **Safety**: No harmful content\n- **Helpfulness**: Useful to the user\n\n### 3. LLM-as-Judge\nUse stronger LLMs to evaluate weaker model outputs.\n\n**Approaches:**\n- **Pointwise**: Score individual responses\n- **Pairwise**: Compare two responses\n- **Reference-based**: Compare to gold standard\n- **Reference-free**: Judge without ground truth\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```python\nfrom llm_eval import EvaluationSuite, Metric\n\n# Define evaluation suite\nsuite = EvaluationSuite([\n    Metric.accuracy(),\n    Metric.bleu(),\n    Metric.bertscore(),\n    Metric.custom(name=\"groundedness\", fn=check_groundedness)\n])\n\n# Prepare test cases\ntest_cases = [\n    {\n        \"input\": \"What is the capital of France?\",\n        \"expected\": \"Paris\",\n        \"context\": \"France is a country in Europe. Paris is its capital.\"\n    },\n    # ... more test cases\n]\n\n# Run evaluation\nresults = suite.evaluate(\n    model=your_model,\n    test_cases=test_cases\n)\n\nprint(f\"Overall Accuracy: {results.metrics[''accuracy'']}\")\nprint(f\"BLEU Score: {results.metrics[''bleu'']}\")\n```\n\n## Automated Metrics Implementation\n\n### BLEU Score\n```python\nfrom nltk.translate.bleu_score import sentence_bleu, SmoothingFunction\n\ndef calculate_bleu(reference, hypothesis):\n    \"\"\"Calculate BLEU score between reference and hypothesis.\"\"\"\n    smoothie = SmoothingFunction().method4\n\n    return sentence_bleu(\n        [reference.split()],\n        hypothesis.split(),\n        smoothing_function=smoothie\n    )\n\n# Usage\nbleu = calculate_bleu(\n    reference=\"The cat sat on the mat\",\n    hypothesis=\"A cat is sitting on the mat\"\n)\n```\n\n### ROUGE Score\n```python\nfrom rouge_score import rouge_scorer\n\ndef calculate_rouge(reference, hypothesis):\n    \"\"\"Calculate ROUGE scores.\"\"\"\n    scorer = rouge_scorer.RougeScorer([''rouge1'', ''rouge2'', ''rougeL''], use_stemmer=True)\n    scores = scorer.score(reference, hypothesis)\n\n    return {\n        ''rouge1'': scores[''rouge1''].fmeasure,\n        ''rouge2'': scores[''rouge2''].fmeasure,\n        ''rougeL'': scores[''rougeL''].fmeasure\n    }\n```\n\n### BERTScore\n```python\nfrom bert_score import score\n\ndef calculate_bertscore(references, hypotheses):\n    \"\"\"Calculate BERTScore using pre-trained BERT.\"\"\"\n    P, R, F1 = score(\n        hypotheses,\n        references,\n        lang=''en'',\n        model_type=''microsoft/deberta-xlarge-mnli''\n    )\n\n    return {\n        ''precision'': P.mean().item(),\n        ''recall'': R.mean().item(),\n        ''f1'': F1.mean().item()\n    }\n```\n\n### Custom Metrics\n```python\ndef calculate_groundedness(response, context):\n    \"\"\"Check if response is grounded in provided context.\"\"\"\n    # Use NLI model to check entailment\n    from transformers import pipeline\n\n    nli = pipeline(\"text-classification\", model=\"microsoft/deberta-large-mnli\")\n\n    result = nli(f\"{context} [SEP] {response}\")[0]\n\n    # Return confidence that response is entailed by context\n    return result[''score''] if result[''label''] == ''ENTAILMENT'' else 0.0\n\ndef calculate_toxicity(text):\n    \"\"\"Measure toxicity in generated text.\"\"\"\n    from detoxify import Detoxify\n\n    results = Detoxify(''original'').predict(text)\n    return max(results.values())  # Return highest toxicity score\n\ndef calculate_factuality(claim, knowledge_base):\n    \"\"\"Verify factual claims against knowledge base.\"\"\"\n    # Implementation depends on your knowledge base\n    # Could use retrieval + NLI, or fact-checking API\n    pass\n```\n\n## LLM-as-Judge Patterns\n\n### Single Output Evaluation\n```python\ndef llm_judge_quality(response, question):\n    \"\"\"Use GPT-5 to judge response quality.\"\"\"\n    prompt = f\"\"\"Rate the following response on a scale of 1-10 for:\n1. Accuracy (factually correct)\n2. Helpfulness (answers the question)\n3. Clarity (well-written and understandable)\n\nQuestion: {question}\nResponse: {response}\n\nProvide ratings in JSON format:\n{{\n  \"accuracy\": <1-10>,\n  \"helpfulness\": <1-10>,\n  \"clarity\": <1-10>,\n  \"reasoning\": \"<brief explanation>\"\n}}\n\"\"\"\n\n    result = openai.ChatCompletion.create(\n        model=\"gpt-5\",\n        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n        temperature=0\n    )\n\n    return json.loads(result.choices[0].message.content)\n```\n\n### Pairwise Comparison\n```python\ndef compare_responses(question, response_a, response_b):\n    \"\"\"Compare two responses using LLM judge.\"\"\"\n    prompt = f\"\"\"Compare these two responses to the question and determine which is better.\n\nQuestion: {question}\n\nResponse A: {response_a}\n\nResponse B: {response_b}\n\nWhich response is better and why? Consider accuracy, helpfulness, and clarity.\n\nAnswer with JSON:\n{{\n  \"winner\": \"A\" or \"B\" or \"tie\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"<explanation>\",\n  \"confidence\": <1-10>\n}}\n\"\"\"\n\n    result = openai.ChatCompletion.create(\n        model=\"gpt-5\",\n        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n        temperature=0\n    )\n\n    return json.loads(result.choices[0].message.content)\n```\n\n## Human Evaluation Frameworks\n\n### Annotation Guidelines\n```python\nclass AnnotationTask:\n    \"\"\"Structure for human annotation task.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, response, question, context=None):\n        self.response = response\n        self.question = question\n        self.context = context\n\n    def get_annotation_form(self):\n        return {\n            \"question\": self.question,\n            \"context\": self.context,\n            \"response\": self.response,\n            \"ratings\": {\n                \"accuracy\": {\n                    \"scale\": \"1-5\",\n                    \"description\": \"Is the response factually correct?\"\n                },\n                \"relevance\": {\n                    \"scale\": \"1-5\",\n                    \"description\": \"Does it answer the question?\"\n                },\n                \"coherence\": {\n                    \"scale\": \"1-5\",\n                    \"description\": \"Is it logically consistent?\"\n                }\n            },\n            \"issues\": {\n                \"factual_error\": False,\n                \"hallucination\": False,\n                \"off_topic\": False,\n                \"unsafe_content\": False\n            },\n            \"feedback\": \"\"\n        }\n```\n\n### Inter-Rater Agreement\n```python\nfrom sklearn.metrics import cohen_kappa_score\n\ndef calculate_agreement(rater1_scores, rater2_scores):\n    \"\"\"Calculate inter-rater agreement.\"\"\"\n    kappa = cohen_kappa_score(rater1_scores, rater2_scores)\n\n    interpretation = {\n        kappa < 0: \"Poor\",\n        kappa < 0.2: \"Slight\",\n        kappa < 0.4: \"Fair\",\n        kappa < 0.6: \"Moderate\",\n        kappa < 0.8: \"Substantial\",\n        kappa <= 1.0: \"Almost Perfect\"\n    }\n\n    return {\n        \"kappa\": kappa,\n        \"interpretation\": interpretation[True]\n    }\n```\n\n## A/B Testing\n\n### Statistical Testing Framework\n```python\nfrom scipy import stats\nimport numpy as np\n\nclass ABTest:\n    def __init__(self, variant_a_name=\"A\", variant_b_name=\"B\"):\n        self.variant_a = {\"name\": variant_a_name, \"scores\": []}\n        self.variant_b = {\"name\": variant_b_name, \"scores\": []}\n\n    def add_result(self, variant, score):\n        \"\"\"Add evaluation result for a variant.\"\"\"\n        if variant == \"A\":\n            self.variant_a[\"scores\"].append(score)\n        else:\n            self.variant_b[\"scores\"].append(score)\n\n    def analyze(self, alpha=0.05):\n        \"\"\"Perform statistical analysis.\"\"\"\n        a_scores = self.variant_a[\"scores\"]\n        b_scores = self.variant_b[\"scores\"]\n\n        # T-test\n        t_stat, p_value = stats.ttest_ind(a_scores, b_scores)\n\n        # Effect size (Cohen''s d)\n        pooled_std = np.sqrt((np.std(a_scores)**2 + np.std(b_scores)**2) / 2)\n        cohens_d = (np.mean(b_scores) - np.mean(a_scores)) / pooled_std\n\n        return {\n            \"variant_a_mean\": np.mean(a_scores),\n            \"variant_b_mean\": np.mean(b_scores),\n            \"difference\": np.mean(b_scores) - np.mean(a_scores),\n            \"relative_improvement\": (np.mean(b_scores) - np.mean(a_scores)) / np.mean(a_scores),\n            \"p_value\": p_value,\n            \"statistically_significant\": p_value < alpha,\n            \"cohens_d\": cohens_d,\n            \"effect_size\": self.interpret_cohens_d(cohens_d),\n            \"winner\": \"B\" if np.mean(b_scores) > np.mean(a_scores) else \"A\"\n        }\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def interpret_cohens_d(d):\n        \"\"\"Interpret Cohen''s d effect size.\"\"\"\n        abs_d = abs(d)\n        if abs_d < 0.2:\n            return \"negligible\"\n        elif abs_d < 0.5:\n            return \"small\"\n        elif abs_d < 0.8:\n            return \"medium\"\n        else:\n            return \"large\"\n```\n\n## Regression Testing\n\n### Regression Detection\n```python\nclass RegressionDetector:\n    def __init__(self, baseline_results, threshold=0.05):\n        self.baseline = baseline_results\n        self.threshold = threshold\n\n    def check_for_regression(self, new_results):\n        \"\"\"Detect if new results show regression.\"\"\"\n        regressions = []\n\n        for metric in self.baseline.keys():\n            baseline_score = self.baseline[metric]\n            new_score = new_results.get(metric)\n\n            if new_score is None:\n                continue\n\n            # Calculate relative change\n            relative_change = (new_score - baseline_score) / baseline_score\n\n            # Flag if significant decrease\n            if relative_change < -self.threshold:\n                regressions.append({\n                    \"metric\": metric,\n                    \"baseline\": baseline_score,\n                    \"current\": new_score,\n                    \"change\": relative_change\n                })\n\n        return {\n            \"has_regression\": len(regressions) > 0,\n            \"regressions\": regressions\n        }\n```\n\n## Benchmarking\n\n### Running Benchmarks\n```python\nclass BenchmarkRunner:\n    def __init__(self, benchmark_dataset):\n        self.dataset = benchmark_dataset\n\n    def run_benchmark(self, model, metrics):\n        \"\"\"Run model on benchmark and calculate metrics.\"\"\"\n        results = {metric.name: [] for metric in metrics}\n\n        for example in self.dataset:\n            # Generate prediction\n            prediction = model.predict(example[\"input\"])\n\n            # Calculate each metric\n            for metric in metrics:\n                score = metric.calculate(\n                    prediction=prediction,\n                    reference=example[\"reference\"],\n                    context=example.get(\"context\")\n                )\n                results[metric.name].append(score)\n\n        # Aggregate results\n        return {\n            metric: {\n                \"mean\": np.mean(scores),\n                \"std\": np.std(scores),\n                \"min\": min(scores),\n                \"max\": max(scores)\n            }\n            for metric, scores in results.items()\n        }\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/metrics.md**: Comprehensive metric guide\n- **references/human-evaluation.md**: Annotation best practices\n- **references/benchmarking.md**: Standard benchmarks\n- **references/a-b-testing.md**: Statistical testing guide\n- **references/regression-testing.md**: CI/CD integration\n- **assets/evaluation-framework.py**: Complete evaluation harness\n- **assets/benchmark-dataset.jsonl**: Example datasets\n- **scripts/evaluate-model.py**: Automated evaluation runner\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Multiple Metrics**: Use diverse metrics for comprehensive view\n2. **Representative Data**: Test on real-world, diverse examples\n3. **Baselines**: Always compare against baseline performance\n4. **Statistical Rigor**: Use proper statistical tests for comparisons\n5. **Continuous Evaluation**: Integrate into CI/CD pipeline\n6. **Human Validation**: Combine automated metrics with human judgment\n7. **Error Analysis**: Investigate failures to understand weaknesses\n8. **Version Control**: Track evaluation results over time\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Single Metric Obsession**: Optimizing for one metric at the expense of others\n- **Small Sample Size**: Drawing conclusions from too few examples\n- **Data Contamination**: Testing on training data\n- **Ignoring Variance**: Not accounting for statistical uncertainty\n- **Metric Mismatch**: Using metrics not aligned with business goals\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:55:05.574Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, and Claude Code needing comprehensive LLM evaluation strategies for automated metrics, human evaluation, and A/B testing.","zh":"非常适合需要全面LLM评估策略的AI智能体，如Cursor、Windsurf和Claude Code，适用于自动化指标评估、人工评估和A/B测试。","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、Claude CodeなどのAIエージェントに最適です。自動化メトリクス、人的評価、A/Bテストを含む総合的なLLM評価戦略を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트에 완벽하게 적합합니다. 자동화된 메트릭, 인간 평가 및 A/B 테스트를 위한 포괄적인 LLM 평가 전략이 필요합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf y Claude Code que necesitan estrategias de evaluación de LLM integrales para métricas automatizadas, evaluación humana y pruebas A/B.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf et Claude Code ayant besoin de stratégies d''évaluation de LLM complètes pour des métriques automatisées, une évaluation humaine et des tests A/B.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf und Claude Code, die umfassende LLM-Evaluierungsstrategien für automatisierte Metriken, humane Bewertung und A/B-Testing benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf e Claude Code que necessitam de estratégias de avaliação de LLM abrangentes para métricas automatizadas, avaliação humana e testes A/B.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf и Claude Code, которым требуются комплексные стратегии оценки LLM для автоматизированных метрик, оценки человека и тестирования А/Б.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و Windsurf و Claude Code الذين يحتاجون إلى استراتيجيات تقييم LLM شاملة لأدوات قياس آليّة وتقييم بشري واختبار أ/ب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically measure LLM application performance, compare different models or prompts, and detect performance regressions using advanced inference and distributed training capabilities, while establishing baselines and tracking progress over time with human evaluation and A/B testing protocols.","zh":"赋能智能体系统化地衡量LLM应用性能，利用先进的推理和分布式训练能力比较不同模型或提示词，并检测性能回归，同时通过人工评估和A/B测试协议建立基线并跟踪随时间推移的进展。","ja":"先進的な推論と分散トレーニング機能を活用して、エージェントがLLMアプリケーションのパフォーマンスを体系的に測定し、さまざまなモデルやプロンプトを比較し、パフォーマンスの退行を検出することを可能にします。同時に、人的評価とA/Bテストプロトコルを通じてベースラインを確立し、時間の経過に伴う進捗を追跡します。","ko":"고급 추론 및 분산 훈련 기능을 사용하여 에이전트가 LLM 애플리케이션 성능을 체계적으로 측정하고, 다양한 모델이나 프롬프트를 비교하며, 성능 회귀를 감지할 수 있도록 합니다. 동시에 인간 평가 및 A/B 테스트 프로토콜을 통해 기준선을 설정하고 시간 경과에 따른 진행 상황을 추적합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes medir sistemáticamente el rendimiento de la aplicación LLM, comparar diferentes modelos o instrucciones y detectar regresiones de rendimiento utilizando capacidades de inferencia avanzadas y entrenamiento distribuido, al mismo tiempo que establece líneas base y realiza un seguimiento del progreso con el tiempo mediante protocolos de evaluación humana y pruebas A/B.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mesurer systématiquement les performances de l''application LLM, de comparer différents modèles ou invites et de détecter les régressions de performances en utilisant des capacités d''inférence avancées et un entraînement distribué, tout en établissant des références et en suivant les progrès dans le temps avec des protocoles d''évaluation humaine et de tests A/B.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, das LLM-Anwendungsleistungsvermögen systematisch zu messen, verschiedene Modelle oder Prompts für optimale Ergebnisse zu vergleichen und Leistungsregressionen vor der Bereitstellung zu erkennen, indem es erweiterte Inferenz- und verteilte Trainingsfunktionen nutzt, während es gleichzeitig Baselines festlegt und den Fortschritt über die Zeit mit humaner Bewertung und A/B-Testprotokollen verfolgt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a medir sistematicamente o desempenho da aplicação LLM, comparar diferentes modelos ou prompts e detectar regressões de desempenho usando capacidades de inferência avançadas e treinamento distribuído, ao mesmo tempo em que estabelece referenciais e acompanha o progresso ao longo do tempo com protocolos de avaliação humana e testes A/B.","ru":"Позволяет агентам систематически измерять производительность приложения LLM, сравнивать разные модели или подсказки и обнаруживать регрессии производительности с помощью продвинутых возможностей вывода и распределенной тренировки, а также устанавливать базовые показатели и отслеживать прогресс с течением времени с помощью протоколов оценки человека и тестирования А/Б.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء قياس أداء تطبيق LLM بشكل منهجي ومقارنة نماذج أو تلميحات مختلفة وكشف انحدارات الأداء باستخدام قدرات استدلال متقدمة وتدريب موزّع، مع تحديد نقاط مرجعية وتتبع التقدم بمرور الوقت باستخدام بروتوكولات تقييم بشري واختبار أ/ب."},"useCases":{"en":["Measuring LLM application performance systematically","Comparing different models or prompts for optimal results","Detecting performance regressions before deployment to ensure reliability"],"zh":["系统化地衡量LLM应用性能","比较不同模型或提示词以获得最佳结果","在部署前检测性能回归以确保可靠性"],"ja":["LLMアプリケーションのパフォーマンスを体系的に測定する","最適な結果を得るためにさまざまなモデルやプロンプトを比較する","信頼性を確保するためにデプロイ前にパフォーマンスの退行を検出する"],"ko":["LLM 애플리케이션 성능을 체계적으로 측정","최적의 결과를 위해 다양한 모델이나 프롬프트 비교","신뢰성을 보장하기 위해 배포 전 성능 회귀 감지"],"es":["Medir sistemáticamente el rendimiento de la aplicación LLM","Comparar diferentes modelos o instrucciones para obtener resultados óptimos","Detectar regresiones de rendimiento antes de la implementación para garantizar la confiabilidad"],"fr":["Mesurer systématiquement les performances de l''application LLM","Comparer différents modèles ou invites pour obtenir des résultats optimaux","Détecter les régressions de performances avant le déploiement pour assurer la fiabilité"],"de":["Das LLM-Anwendungsleistungsvermögen systematisch messen","Verschiedene Modelle oder Prompts für optimale Ergebnisse vergleichen","Leistungsregressionen vor der Bereitstellung erkennen, um die Zuverlässigkeit zu gewährleisten"],"pt":["Medir o desempenho da aplicação LLM de forma sistemática","Comparar diferentes modelos ou prompts para obter resultados ótimos","Detectar regressões de desempenho antes da implantação para garantir a confiabilidade"],"ru":["Систематически измерять производительность приложения LLM","Сравнивать разные модели или подсказки для получения оптимальных результатов","Обнаруживать регрессии производительности до развертывания для обеспечения надежности"],"ar":["قياس أداء تطبيق LLM بشكل منهجي","مقارنة نماذج أو تلميحات مختلفة لتحقيق نتائج مثالية","كشف انحدارات الأداء قبل النشر لضمان الموثوقية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires a single, cohesive, high-power compute system for distributed training and advanced inference","Needs human evaluation and A/B testing for comprehensive assessment"],"zh":["需要单一、 cohesive 的高性能计算系统来支持分布式训练和高级推理","需要人工评估和A/B测试以进行全面评估"],"ja":["分散トレーニングと高度な推論のために、単一の結束力のある高性能コンピューティングシステムが必要","総合的な評価には人的評価とA/Bテストが必要"],"ko":["분산 훈련 및 고급 추론을 위해 단일적이고 응집력 있는 고성능 컴퓨팅 시스템 필요","포괄적인 평가를 위해 인간 평가 및 A/B 테스트 필요"],"es":["Requiere un solo sistema de cómputo cohesivo y de alta potencia para el entrenamiento distribuido y la inferencia avanzada","Necesita evaluación humana y pruebas A/B para una evaluación integral"],"fr":["Nécessite un système de calcul cohérent et puissant unique pour la formation distribuée et l''inférence avancée","A besoin d''une évaluation humaine et de tests A/B pour une évaluation complète"],"de":["Benötigt ein einzelnes, kohärentes Hochleistungsrechnersystem für verteiltes Training und erweiterte Inferenz","Benötigt humane Bewertung und A/B-Testing für eine umfassende Bewertung"],"pt":["Exige um sistema de computação único e coeso de alta potência para treinamento distribuído e inferência avançada","Necessita de avaliação humana e testes A/B para avaliação abrangente"],"ru":["Требует единой, сплоченной, высокомощной вычислительной системы для распределенной тренировки и продвинутого вывода","Требует оценки человека и тестирования А/Б для всесторонней оценки"],"ar":["يتطلب نظام حسابي موحّد ومتكامل ذو قدرة عالية للتدريب الموزّع والاستدلال المتقدم","يحتاج إلى تقييم بشري واختبار أ/ب لتقييم شامل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
