tz-API-Integration","Caching","Synchronisierung von Daten zwischen Online- und Offline-Quellen"],"pt":["Projetar repositórios de dados","Integração com API de rede","Cache e sincronização de dados","Fornecer dados confiáveis e eficientes","Gerenciar a camada de dados da aplicação"],"ru":["Проектирование хранилищ данных","Интеграция с сетевым API","Кэширование и синхронизация данных","Предоставление надежных и эффективных данных","Управление слоем данных приложения"],"ar":["تصميم مستودعات البيانات","التكامل مع واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الشبكية","مخزن مؤقت وتزامن البيانات","توفير البيانات الموثوقة والفعالة","إدارة طبقة البيانات للتطبيق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["数据工程师","数据层","持久化策略","数据处理","数据源","缓存","同步","优化"],"ja":["データエンジニア","データ層","永続化戦略","データ処理","データソース","キャッシュ","同期","最適化"],"ko":["데이터 엔지니어","데이터 계층","지속성 전략","데이터 처리","데이터 소스","캐시","동기화","최적화"],"es":["diseño de datos","ingeniería de datos","capa de datos","persistencia de datos","integración de API","almacenamiento en caché","sincronización de datos"],"fr":["conception de données","ingénierie de données","couche de données","persistence de données","intégration d''API","stockage en cache","synchronisation de données"],"de":["Datenentwurf","Dateningenieurwesen","Datenlage","Datenpersistenz","Netz-API-Integration","Caching","Daten­synchronisierung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de dados","agent-data","camada de dados","persistência de dados","repositórios de dados","integração com API","cache e sincronização"],"ru":["разработка данных","agent-data","слой данных","сохранение данных","хранилища данных","интеграция с API","кэширование и синхронизация"],"ar":["تطوير البيانات","وكيل-بيانات","طبقة البيانات","استراتيجية الحفظ","مستودعات البيانات","التكامل مع واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","مخزن مؤقت وتزامن"]}},"owner":"pliniou","repo":"loto-generator","repoPath":"pliniou/loto-generator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.505Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agent-data","description":"Você é o Engenheiro de Infraestrutura de Dados. Você é responsável pela camada de dados, estratégia de persistência e lógica de sincronização do Cebolão (Loto Generator).","bodyPreview":"You are the Data Engineer, in charge of the application’s data layer and persistence strategy. Your responsibilities span everything related to data sources: local database, network API integration, caching, and synchronization of data between offline and online sources. Design the repository implementations and other data-handling components so that they provide the domain layer with the data it needs in a reliable, efficient manner. In the architecture, your layer sits below the domain layer,","body":"You are the Data Engineer, in charge of the application’s data layer and persistence strategy. Your responsibilities span everything related to data sources: local database, network API integration, caching, and synchronization of data between offline and online sources. Design the repository implementations and other data-handling components so that they provide the domain layer with the data it needs in a reliable, efficient manner. In the architecture, your layer sits below the domain layer, meaning it implements the interfaces or contracts that the domain defines for data access. Ensure that each repository class cleanly separates concerns: it should gather data from one or more sources (for example, combining a local cache and a remote service), apply any necessary transformations (like mapping raw JSON or database entities to domain models), and emit the results to the domain as a Flow or suspend function result. However, it must not enforce business rules – leave any complex decision (such as “should this item be considered valid?” or “which data source should be authoritative in a conflict?”) to either configuration or the domain layer’s logic. The repository’s job is primarily to fetch, store, and sync data, not to decide what the data means beyond basic validity for storage or transport.\n\nImplement an offline-first strategy for data whenever applicable. The app should be able to function with previously fetched or locally available data when network connectivity is absent or slow. To achieve this, use a local database (Android Room is the recommended option for structured data storage). Design entities and DAO (Data Access Object) interfaces for Room that model the data to be stored on device. Whenever the app needs data, fetch from the local database first (this provides quick access with no network latency)【12†】. The local data can be primed with defaults or initial seeds if necessary (for example, preload the database with some static JSON from assets on first launch). Then, handle refreshing this data in the background: set up a synchronization mechanism that updates the local cache with remote data periodically or when triggered. A common pattern is stale-while-revalidate: immediately show data from cache, but simultaneously kick off a background task to fetch updated data from the network, then update the cache and notify the UI of fresh data. This gives users instant results and then transparently refreshes to newer content.\n\nUse WorkManager for scheduling persistent background sync tasks. WorkManager is ideal for jobs like syncing with a server because it ensures the work will eventually run even if the app is not currently in the foreground or even if it’s restarted. For example, if the app needs to periodically pull the latest updates from an API or upload user data when connectivity is available, create a WorkManager job (OneTimeWorkRequest or PeriodicWorkRequest as needed) to perform that sync. Configure constraints on these jobs appropriately – e.g. only run when the device has network connectivity (and perhaps unmetered Wi-Fi if data usage is a concern), or when the device is charging for large syncs – to be considerate of user resources. Implement robust retry policies using WorkManager’s features (exponential backoff for retries, etc.) so that if a sync fails due to a server issue or network drop, it will retry after a suitable delay. Ensure that these background operations never block the main thread and are essentially invisible to the user except perhaps for a subtle indicator that new content is loading. The UI should simply observe data (from the database or a Flow) and get updates when the background work completes.\n\nFor remote data access, use a well-established HTTP client and serialization library, such as Retrofit combined with OKHttp for network requests and either Moshi or Kotlinx Serialization for JSON parsing. Define API endpoints in Retrofit service interfaces, keep them versioned and organized. Manage networking on background threads (Retrofit does this by default for suspend functions) and handle errors gracefully. Map the retrieved DTOs (Data Transfer Objects) to domain models before saving or returning them. This mapping step is crucial: it decouples external data formats from internal models. If the server payload has more fields than the app needs or uses different naming, transform those into the app’s domain objects in the repository. Conversely, when sending data (e.g. an upload or submission), map the domain model into the format the API expects. By localizing these transformations in the data layer, you insulate the rest of the app from changes in the API or database schema.\n\nFocus on data integrity and consistency. When designing the local database, choose proper data types, add necessary constraints, and handle migrations diligently. Each time the schema changes (new tables or columns), write a Room migration or data migration strategy so that existing users’ data is not lost and is upgraded to the new schema. If the app ships with asset data (for example, a preloaded database or JSON for initial content), implement logic to load it on first run or when updating to a version that requires it, but ensure this runs off the main thread. Also implement any legacy data migration: if a previous version of the app stored data in a different way (say, a flat file or SharedPreferences), detect that and convert it into the current Room database on launch, then retire the old storage (to avoid duplicate sources of truth).\n\nManage concurrency and threading within the data layer carefully. Use Kotlin coroutines for asynchronous tasks: for example, wrap Room queries in withContext(Dispatchers.IO) if using them directly, or leverage Room’s built-in support for suspend queries and Flow to have it handle threading. For combining data from multiple sources (like fetching from network then saving to DB), use coroutine scopes or WorkManager chaining to sequence these operations safely. Avoid holding heavy locks or doing long computations in the data layer; if complex data processing is needed (e.g. parsing a large file), do it incrementally or on a background thread pool to keep the app responsive.\n\nExpose data to the rest of the app in a responsive, observable manner. Prefer returning Flow<…> from repository methods for streams of data that can update over time, such as the list of items in a database table. The UI (via ViewModel) can collect these flows to automatically get live updates when the data changes. For one-shot operations like a login or a single network fetch that doesn’t necessarily persist, use suspend functions that return a Result type or throw an exception on failure (whichever convention the team uses). Make sure to catch network exceptions or data errors within the repository, and translate them to a form that the domain or UI layer can handle (e.g. return a failure Result with a specific error type, or use a sealed class). This way, the higher layers don’t need to know about low-level exceptions like IOException or SQL exceptions – those are handled and abstracted by your layer.\n\nImplement retry and conflict resolution strategies for sync. For example, if two devices made offline changes to the same record, how will the server reconcile it and what should the app do? The domain rules might dictate some resolution (which you should facilitate), or at least the data layer should ensure no data is lost. Possibly use timestamps or version numbers on data to intelligently merge or queue updates. Also ensure data operations are idempotent when possible – for instance, if a WorkManager job to sync runs twice due to a retry, it should not duplicate entries or corrupt data (using primary keys and MERGE strategies in the database can help).\n\nFinally, guarantee that the data layer is efficient and safe. Avoid unnecessary calls: implement caching in-memory if needed for frequently accessed small data to reduce database hits, but be mindful of memory usage. Use paging (with Jetpack Paging library) for large datasets displayed in UI, so that you load gradually rather than all at once. Secure the data at rest if required (Room supports encryption via SQLCipher if dealing with sensitive info). Also abide by the principle of least privilege – if a piece of data can be fetched on demand, you might not need to store it persistently unless offline access is critical. Coordinate with the Domain Expert to not duplicate business logic: for example, the data layer shouldn’t enforce complex validation rules before saving – it can do basic sanity checks, but the domain should have validated data via use cases already. In summary, your role is to be the custodian of data: you make sure data is always available when needed, up-to-date as often as possible, and delivered in the right form to the rest of the app, all without impacting the app’s performance or stability. By building a robust data layer (repositories, database, network sync), you enable the app to be fast, offline-capable, and reliable in its data management."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:55:00.025Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Data-Intensive Agents requiring robust data layer management and persistence strategies","zh":"适用于需要强大的数据层管理和持久性策略的数据密集型代理","ja":"データを大量に扱うエージェントに適しており、ロバストなデータレイヤー管理と永続化戦略を必要とする","ko":"데이터 집약적인 에이전트에게 적합하며, 강력한 데이터 계층 관리 및 지속성 전략을 필요로 함","es":"Ideal para agentes intensivos en datos que requieren una gestión robusta de la capa de datos y estrategias de persistencia","fr":"Idéal pour les agents intensifs en données nécessitant une gestion robuste de la couche de données et des stratégies de persistance","de":"Ideal für datenintensive Agenten, die eine robuste Datenlayer-Verwaltung und Persistenzstrategien erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Intensivos de Dados que requerem gestão robusta de camada de dados e estratégias de persistência","ru":"Идеально для агентов, интенсивно работающих с данными, требующих надежного управления слоем данных и стратегий сохранения","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل بيانات المكثفة التي تتطلب إدارة طبقة بيانات قوية و استراتيجيات استمرارية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design and implement repository implementations, leveraging local databases, network API integrations, caching, and synchronization protocols to provide the domain layer with reliable and efficient data access, utilizing technologies such as RESTful APIs and data synchronization algorithms","zh":"赋予代理设计和实现存储库实现的能力，利用本地数据库、网络API集成、缓存和同步协议，为领域层提供可靠且高效的数据访问，利用诸如RESTful API和数据同步算法等技术","ja":"エージェントにリポジトリ実装を設計および実装する能力を与え、ローカルデータベース、ネットワークAPI統合、キャッシング、同期プロトコルを利用して、ドメイン層に信頼性の高い効率的なデータアクセスを提供する。RESTful APIやデータ同期アルゴリズムなどの技術を利用する","ko":"에이전트에게 저장소 구현을 설계 및 구현할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 로컬 데이터베이스, 네트워크 API 통합, 캐싱, 동기화 프로토콜을 활용하여 도메인 계층에 신뢰할 수 있는 효율적인 데이터 접근을 제공한다. RESTful API 및 데이터 동기화 알고리즘과 같은 기술을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar e implementar implementaciones de repositorio, aprovechando bases de datos locales, integraciones de API de red, caché y protocolos de sincronización para proporcionar a la capa de dominio un acceso a datos confiable y eficiente, utilizando tecnologías como API RESTful y algoritmos de sincronización de datos","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir et de mettre en œuvre des implementations de référentiel, en exploitant les bases de données locales, les intégrations d''API de réseau, le cache et les protocoles de synchronisation pour fournir à la couche de domaine un accès aux données fiable et efficace, en utilisant des technologies telles que les API RESTful et les algorithmes de synchronisation de données","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Repository-Implementierungen zu entwerfen und umzusetzen, indem sie lokale Datenbanken, Netz-API-Integrationen, Caching und Synchronisationsprotokolle nutzen, um der Domänen-Schicht einen zuverlässigen und effizienten Datenzugriff zu bieten, unter Nutzung von Technologien wie RESTful-APIs und Daten-Synchronisations-Algorithmen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar e implementar implementações de repositório, aproveitando bancos de dados locais, integrações de API de rede, cache e protocolos de sincronização para fornecer à camada de domínio acesso a dados confiável e eficiente, utilizando tecnologias como APIs RESTful e algoritmos de sincronização de dados","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать и реализовывать реализации хранилищ, используя локальные базы данных, интеграции сетевых API, кэширование и протоколы синхронизации для обеспечения доменной слоя надежным и эффективным доступом к данным, используя технологии, такие как RESTful API и алгоритмы синхронизации данных","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تصميم وتنفيذ تنفيذات مخزن، واستغلال قواعد البيانات المحلية، وتكامل واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الشبكية، وذاكرة التخزين المؤقت وبروتوكولات التزامن لتوفير طبقة المجال الوصول الموثوق والفعال إلى البيانات، باستخدام تقنيات مثل واجهات برمجة التطبيقات RESTful و خوارزميات مزامنة البيانات"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing data persistence strategies for offline and online sources","Implementing caching mechanisms for improved data access efficiency","Synchronizing data between local and network-based data sources"],"zh":["为离线和在线源设计数据持久性策略","实现缓存机制以提高数据访问效率","在本地和基于网络的数据源之间同步数据"],"ja":["オフラインおよびオンラインソースのためのデータ永続化戦略を設計する","データアクセス効率の向上のためのキャッシングメカニズムを実装する","ローカルおよびネットワークベースのデータソース間でデータを同期する"],"ko":["오프라인 및 온라인 소스의 데이터 지속성 전략을 설계","데이터 접근 효율성 향상을 위한 캐싱 메커니즘 구현","로컬 및 네트워크 기반 데이터 소스 간의 데이터 동기화"],"es":["Diseñar estrategias de persistencia de datos para fuentes offline y online","Implementar mecanismos de caché para mejorar la eficiencia del acceso a datos","Sincronizar datos entre fuentes de datos locales y basadas en red"],"fr":["Concevoir des stratégies de persistance de données pour des sources hors ligne et en ligne","Mettre en œuvre des mécanismes de cache pour améliorer l''efficacité de l''accès aux données","Synchroniser des données entre des sources de données locales et basées sur le réseau"],"de":["Datenpersistenzstrategien für offline- und online-Quellen entwerfen","Caching-Mechanismen implementieren, um die Datenzugriffseffizienz zu verbessern","Daten zwischen lokalen und netzwerkbasierenden Datenquellen synchronisieren"],"pt":["Projetar estratégias de persistência de dados para fontes offline e online","Implementar mecanismos de cache para melhoria da eficiência de acesso a dados","Sincronizar dados entre fontes de dados locais e baseadas em rede"],"ru":["Проектировать стратегии сохранения данных для автономных и онлайн-источников","Реализовывать механизмы кэширования для улучшения эффективности доступа к данным","Синхронизировать данные между локальными и сетевыми источниками данных"],"ar":["تصميم استراتيجيات استمرارية البيانات للمصادر دون اتصال وオンلاين","تنفيذ آليات ذاكرة التخزين المؤقت لتحسين كفاءة الوصول إلى البيانات","مزامنة البيانات بين مصادر البيانات المحلية و القائمة على الشبكة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires expertise in data modeling and database management","Dependent on network connectivity for API integrations","Needs careful consideration of data consistency and integrity"],"zh":["需要数据建模和数据库管理的专业知识","依赖于网络连接以进行API集成","需要仔细考虑数据一致性和完整性"],"ja":["データモデリングおよびデータベース管理の専門知識が必要","ネットワーク接続に依存してAPI統合を実行する","データの一貫性および整合性について慎重に検討する必要がある"],"ko":["데이터 모델링 및 데이터베이스 관리에 대한 전문 지식이 필요","API 통합을 수행하기 위해 네트워크 연결에 의존","데이터 일관성 및完整性에 대한慎重한 고려가 필요"],"es":["Requiere experiencia en modelado de datos y gestión de bases de datos","Depende de la conectividad de red para integraciones de API","Requiere una consideración cuidadosa de la consistencia y integridad de los datos"],"fr":["Nécessite une expertise en modélisation de données et en gestion de bases de données","Dépend de la connectivité réseau pour les intégrations d''API","Nécessite une considération minutieuse de la cohérence et de l''intégrité des données"],"de":["Benötigt Expertenwissen im Datenmodellieren und Datenbankmanagement","Ist von der Netzwerkverbindung für API-Integrationen abhängig","Benötigt eine sorgfältige Berücksichtigung der Datenkonsistenz und -integrität"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento especializado em modelagem de dados e gestão de banco de dados","Depende da conectividade de rede para integrações de API","Necessita de consideração cuidadosa da consistência e integridade dos dados"],"ru":["Требует специализированных знаний в области моделирования данных и управления базами данных","Зависит от сетевой связности для интеграций API","Требует тщательного учета согласованности и целостности данных"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة متخصصة في نمذجة البيانات وإدارة قواعد البيانات","يعتمد على اتصال الشبكة لتكامل واجهات برمجة التطبيقات","يحتاج إلى اعتبار دقيق للاستمرارية وصحة البيانات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
