","OAuth","Magische Links","Passkeys"],"pt":["autenticação","segurança","framework","Better Auth","desenvolvimento web","plugins","OAuth","email/senha"],"ru":["аутентификация","безопасность","фреймворк","Better Auth","веб-разработка","плагины","OAuth","электронная почта/пароль"],"ar":["توثيق","أمان","إطار عمل","Better Auth","تطوير الويب","الإضافات","OAuth","البريد الإلكتروني / كلمة المرور"]}},"owner":"ThinkEx-OSS","repo":"thinkex","repoPath":"ThinkEx-OSS/thinkex","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.505Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"better-auth-best-practices","description":"Skill for integrating Better Auth - the comprehensive TypeScript authentication framework.","bodyPreview":"# Better Auth Integration Guide\n\n**Always consult [better-auth.com/docs](https://better-auth.com/docs) for code examples and latest API.**\n\nBetter Auth is a TypeScript-first, framework-agnostic auth framework supporting email/password, OAuth, magic links, passkeys, and more via plugins.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Environment Variables\n- `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` - Encryption secret (min 32 chars). Generate: `openssl rand -base64 32`\n- `BETTER_AUTH_URL` - Base URL (e.g., `https://example.com`)\n\nOnl","body":"# Better Auth Integration Guide\n\n**Always consult [better-auth.com/docs](https://better-auth.com/docs) for code examples and latest API.**\n\nBetter Auth is a TypeScript-first, framework-agnostic auth framework supporting email/password, OAuth, magic links, passkeys, and more via plugins.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Environment Variables\n- `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` - Encryption secret (min 32 chars). Generate: `openssl rand -base64 32`\n- `BETTER_AUTH_URL` - Base URL (e.g., `https://example.com`)\n\nOnly define `baseURL`/`secret` in config if env vars are NOT set.\n\n### File Location\nCLI looks for `auth.ts` in: `./`, `./lib`, `./utils`, or under `./src`. Use `--config` for custom path.\n\n### CLI Commands\n- `npx @better-auth/cli@latest migrate` - Apply schema (built-in adapter)\n- `npx @better-auth/cli@latest generate` - Generate schema for Prisma/Drizzle\n- `npx @better-auth/cli mcp --cursor` - Add MCP to AI tools\n\n**Re-run after adding/changing plugins.**\n\n---\n\n## Core Config Options\n\n| Option | Notes |\n|--------|-------|\n| `appName` | Optional display name |\n| `baseURL` | Only if `BETTER_AUTH_URL` not set |\n| `basePath` | Default `/api/auth`. Set `/` for root. |\n| `secret` | Only if `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` not set |\n| `database` | Required for most features. See adapters docs. |\n| `secondaryStorage` | Redis/KV for sessions & rate limits |\n| `emailAndPassword` | `{ enabled: true }` to activate |\n| `socialProviders` | `{ google: { clientId, clientSecret }, ... }` |\n| `plugins` | Array of plugins |\n| `trustedOrigins` | CSRF whitelist |\n\n---\n\n## Database\n\n**Direct connections:** Pass `pg.Pool`, `mysql2` pool, `better-sqlite3`, or `bun:sqlite` instance.\n\n**ORM adapters:** Import from `better-auth/adapters/drizzle`, `better-auth/adapters/prisma`, `better-auth/adapters/mongodb`.\n\n**Critical:** Better Auth uses adapter model names, NOT underlying table names. If Prisma model is `User` mapping to table `users`, use `modelName: \"user\"` (Prisma reference), not `\"users\"`.\n\n---\n\n## Session Management\n\n**Storage priority:**\n1. If `secondaryStorage` defined → sessions go there (not DB)\n2. Set `session.storeSessionInDatabase: true` to also persist to DB\n3. No database + `cookieCache` → fully stateless mode\n\n**Cookie cache strategies:**\n- `compact` (default) - Base64url + HMAC. Smallest.\n- `jwt` - Standard JWT. Readable but signed.\n- `jwe` - Encrypted. Maximum security.\n\n**Key options:** `session.expiresIn` (default 7 days), `session.updateAge` (refresh interval), `session.cookieCache.maxAge`, `session.cookieCache.version` (change to invalidate all sessions).\n\n---\n\n## User & Account Config\n\n**User:** `user.modelName`, `user.fields` (column mapping), `user.additionalFields`, `user.changeEmail.enabled` (disabled by default), `user.deleteUser.enabled` (disabled by default).\n\n**Account:** `account.modelName`, `account.accountLinking.enabled`, `account.storeAccountCookie` (for stateless OAuth).\n\n**Required for registration:** `email` and `name` fields.\n\n---\n\n## Email Flows\n\n- `emailVerification.sendVerificationEmail` - Must be defined for verification to work\n- `emailVerification.sendOnSignUp` / `sendOnSignIn` - Auto-send triggers\n- `emailAndPassword.sendResetPassword` - Password reset email handler\n\n---\n\n## Security\n\n**In `advanced`:**\n- `useSecureCookies` - Force HTTPS cookies\n- `disableCSRFCheck` - ⚠️ Security risk\n- `disableOriginCheck` - ⚠️ Security risk  \n- `crossSubDomainCookies.enabled` - Share cookies across subdomains\n- `ipAddress.ipAddressHeaders` - Custom IP headers for proxies\n- `database.generateId` - Custom ID generation or `\"serial\"`/`\"uuid\"`/`false`\n\n**Rate limiting:** `rateLimit.enabled`, `rateLimit.window`, `rateLimit.max`, `rateLimit.storage` (\"memory\" | \"database\" | \"secondary-storage\").\n\n---\n\n## Hooks\n\n**Endpoint hooks:** `hooks.before` / `hooks.after` - Array of `{ matcher, handler }`. Use `createAuthMiddleware`. Access `ctx.path`, `ctx.context.returned` (after), `ctx.context.session`.\n\n**Database hooks:** `databaseHooks.user.create.before/after`, same for `session`, `account`. Useful for adding default values or post-creation actions.\n\n**Hook context (`ctx.context`):** `session`, `secret`, `authCookies`, `password.hash()`/`verify()`, `adapter`, `internalAdapter`, `generateId()`, `tables`, `baseURL`.\n\n---\n\n## Plugins\n\n**Import from dedicated paths for tree-shaking:**\n```\nimport { twoFactor } from \"better-auth/plugins/two-factor\"\n```\nNOT `from \"better-auth/plugins\"`.\n\n**Popular plugins:** `twoFactor`, `organization`, `passkey`, `magicLink`, `emailOtp`, `username`, `phoneNumber`, `admin`, `apiKey`, `bearer`, `jwt`, `multiSession`, `sso`, `oauthProvider`, `oidcProvider`, `openAPI`, `genericOAuth`.\n\nClient plugins go in `createAuthClient({ plugins: [...] })`.\n\n---\n\n## Client\n\nImport from: `better-auth/client` (vanilla), `better-auth/react`, `better-auth/vue`, `better-auth/svelte`, `better-auth/solid`.\n\nKey methods: `signUp.email()`, `signIn.email()`, `signIn.social()`, `signOut()`, `useSession()`, `getSession()`, `revokeSession()`, `revokeSessions()`.\n\n---\n\n## Type Safety\n\nInfer types: `typeof auth.$Infer.Session`, `typeof auth.$Infer.Session.user`.\n\nFor separate client/server projects: `createAuthClient<typeof auth>()`.\n\n---\n\n## Common Gotchas\n\n1. **Model vs table name** - Config uses ORM model name, not DB table name\n2. **Plugin schema** - Re-run CLI after adding plugins\n3. **Secondary storage** - Sessions go there by default, not DB\n4. **Cookie cache** - Custom session fields NOT cached, always re-fetched\n5. **Stateless mode** - No DB = session in cookie only, logout on cache expiry\n6. **Change email flow** - Sends to current email first, then new email\n\n---\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Docs](https://better-auth.com/docs)\n- [Options Reference](https://better-auth.com/docs/reference/options)\n- [LLMs.txt](https://better-auth.com/llms.txt)\n- [GitHub](https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth)\n- [Init Options Source](https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/blob/main/packages/core/src/types/init-options.ts)"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:58:41.484Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Authentication Agents needing advanced auth framework integration with support for email/password, OAuth, and passkeys via plugins.","zh":"非常适合需要高级认证框架集成的身份验证代理，支持通过插件实现的电子邮件/密码、OAuth 和密钥认证。","ja":"高度な認証フレームワークの統合が必要な認証エージェントに最適です。プラグインを介した電子メール/パスワード、OAuth、およびパスキーのサポートを提供します。","ko":"고급 인증 프레임워크 통합이 필요한 인증 에이전트에 적합합니다. 플러그인을 통해 이메일/암호, OAuth 및 패스키를 지원합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Autenticación que necesitan una integración avanzada del marco de autenticación con soporte para correo electrónico/contraseña, OAuth y passkeys a través de plugins.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Authentification ayant besoin d''une intégration avancée du cadre d''authentification avec prise en charge de l''e-mail/mot de passe, OAuth et des passkeys via des plugins.","de":"Perfekt für Authentifizierungsagenten, die eine erweiterte Authentifizierungsframework-Integration mit Unterstützung für E-Mail/Kennwort, OAuth und Passkeys über Plugins benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Autenticação que necessitam de uma integração avançada do framework de autenticação com suporte a email/senha, OAuth e passkeys via plugins.","ru":"Идеально для агентов аутентификации, которым требуется продвинутая интеграция с фреймворком аутентификации с поддержкой электронной почты/пароля, OAuth и ключей через плагины.","ar":" مثالي للوكلاء المسؤولين عن التحقق من الهوية الذين يحتاجون إلى دمج إطار تحقق متقدم مع دعم البريد الإلكتروني / كلمة المرور و OAuth و Passkeys عبر الإضافات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to securely manage user authentication using Better Auth''s TypeScript-first, framework-agnostic approach, leveraging environment variables like BETTER_AUTH_SECRET and BETTER_AUTH_URL for seamless integration.","zh":"通过 Better Auth 的 TypeScript 首先、框架无关的方法，利用环境变量（如 BETTER_AUTH_SECRET 和 BETTER_AUTH_URL）实现无缝集成，从而使代理能够安全地管理用户身份验证。","ja":"Better Auth の TypeScript 最初、フレームワーク非依存のアプローチを使用して、環境変数（BETTER_AUTH_SECRET および BETTER_AUTH_URL など）を活用し、エージェントがユーザーの認証を安全に管理できるようにします。","ko":"Better Auth의 TypeScript 우선, 프레임워크 독립적 접근 방식을 사용하여 환경 변수(BETTER_AUTH_SECRET 및 BETTER_AUTH_URL 등)를 활용하여 에이전트가 사용자 인증을 안전하게 관리할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar de forma segura la autenticación de usuarios utilizando el enfoque de Better Auth de TypeScript, agnóstico al marco, aprovechando variables de entorno como BETTER_AUTH_SECRET y BETTER_AUTH_URL para una integración sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer de manière sécurisée l''authentification des utilisateurs en utilisant l''approche de Better Auth de premier plan TypeScript, agnostique au cadre, en exploitant des variables d''environnement comme BETTER_AUTH_SECRET et BETTER_AUTH_URL pour une intégration transparente.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Benutzerauthentifizierung mithilfe des typsicheren, framework-agnostischen Ansatzes von Better Auth sicher zu verwalten, indem Umgebungsvariablen wie BETTER_AUTH_SECRET und BETTER_AUTH_URL für eine nahtlose Integration genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar a autenticação do usuário de forma segura usando a abordagem TypeScript-first e framework-agnostic da Better Auth, aproveitando variáveis de ambiente como BETTER_AUTH_SECRET e BETTER_AUTH_URL para uma integração perfeita.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью безопасно управлять аутентификацией пользователей, используя подход Better Auth, основанный на TypeScript и независимый от фреймворка, используя переменные среды, такие как BETTER_AUTH_SECRET и BETTER_AUTH_URL, для бесшовной интеграции.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة التحقق من الهوية للمستخدمين بشكل آمن باستخدام نهج Better Auth القائم على TypeScript ومدمج مع الإطار، باستخدام متغيرات البيئة مثل BETTER_AUTH_SECRET و BETTER_AUTH_URL من أجل التكامل السلس."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing email/password authentication with encryption","Configuring OAuth and magic links for enhanced security","Generating and managing passkeys for passwordless login"],"zh":["实现电子邮件/密码认证并加密","配置 OAuth 和魔术链接以增强安全性","生成和管理密钥以实现无密码登录"],"ja":["暗号化を伴う電子メール/パスワード認証の実装","セキュリティの向上のための OAuth およびマジックリンクの構成","パスワードレスログインのためのパスキーの生成および管理"],"ko":["암호화된 이메일/암호 인증 구현","보안 강화를 위한 OAuth 및 매직 링크 구성","패스워드 없는 로그인 위한 패스키 생성 및 관리"],"es":["Implementar la autenticación por correo electrónico/contraseña con cifrado","Configurar OAuth y enlaces mágicos para una mayor seguridad","Generar y gestionar passkeys para el inicio de sesión sin contraseña"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre l''authentification par e-mail/mot de passe avec chiffrement","Configurer OAuth et les liens magiques pour une sécurité renforcée","Générer et gérer des passkeys pour la connexion sans mot de passe"],"de":["Implementierung der E-Mail/Kennwort-Authentifizierung mit Verschlüsselung","Konfiguration von OAuth und Magischen Links für erhöhte Sicherheit","Generieren und Verwalten von Passkeys für den passwortlosen Login"],"pt":["Implementar autenticação por email/senha com criptografia","Configurar OAuth e links mágicos para segurança reforçada","Gerar e gerenciar passkeys para login sem senha"],"ru":["Реализовать аутентификацию по электронной почте/паролю с шифрованием","Настроить OAuth и магические ссылки для повышения безопасности","Создавать и управлять ключами для входа без пароля"],"ar":["تنفيذ التحقق من الهوية بواسطة البريد الإلكتروني / كلمة المرور مع التشفير","تكوين OAuth والروابط السحرية لتعزيز الأمان","إنشاء وإدارة المفاتيح للوصول بدون كلمة مرور"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires BETTER_AUTH_SECRET environment variable with a minimum of 32 characters","Needs BETTER_AUTH_URL environment variable set to the base URL","Dependent on the Better Auth API and documentation at better-auth.com/docs"],"zh":["需要至少 32 个字符的 BETTER_AUTH_SECRET 环境变量","需要将 BETTER_AUTH_URL 环境变量设置为基本 URL","依赖于 Better Auth API 和 better-auth.com/docs 中的文档"],"ja":["少なくとも 32 文字の BETTER_AUTH_SECRET 環境変数が必要","BETTER_AUTH_URL 環境変数を基本 URL に設定する必要がある","Better Auth API および better-auth.com/docs に記載されたドキュメントに依存する"],"ko":["최소 32개의 문자가 있는 BETTER_AUTH_SECRET 환경 변수가 필요","BETTER_AUTH_URL 환경 변수를 기본 URL로 설정해야 함","Better Auth API 및 better-auth.com/docs에 문서화된 내용에 의존"],"es":["Requiere la variable de entorno BETTER_AUTH_SECRET con un mínimo de 32 caracteres","Necesita la variable de entorno BETTER_AUTH_URL establecida en la URL base","Dependiente de la API de Better Auth y la documentación en better-auth.com/docs"],"fr":["Nécessite la variable d''environnement BETTER_AUTH_SECRET avec un minimum de 32 caractères","A besoin de la variable d''environnement BETTER_AUTH_URL définie sur l''URL de base","Dépend de l''API Better Auth et de la documentation sur better-auth.com/docs"],"de":["Benötigt die Umgebungsvariable BETTER_AUTH_SECRET mit einem Minimum von 32 Zeichen","Benötigt die Umgebungsvariable BETTER_AUTH_URL auf der Basis-URL","Abhängig von der Better Auth-API und der Dokumentation unter better-auth.com/docs"],"pt":["Exige variável de ambiente BETTER_AUTH_SECRET com no mínimo 32 caracteres","Necessita variável de ambiente BETTER_AUTH_URL definida para a URL base","Depende da API Better Auth e da documentação em better-auth.com/docs"],"ru":["Требует переменной среды BETTER_AUTH_SECRET с минимум 32 символами","Требует переменной среды BETTER_AUTH_URL, установленной для базового URL","Зависит от API Better Auth и документации на better-auth.com/docs"],"ar":["يتطلب متغير بيئة BETTER_AUTH_SECRET مع حد أدنى 32 حرفًا","يحتاج إلى متغير بيئة BETTER_AUTH_URL معين لعنوان URL الأساسي","يعتمد على وثائق واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Better Auth على better-auth.com/docs"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/opennote-vault', 'community', 'Paxeer-Network', 'Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'opennote-vault', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.505Z', '2026-02-18T11:58:55.811Z', NULL, '{"id":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/opennote-vault","name":"opennote-vault","description":{"zh":"OpenNotes Vault 是一个支持 RWA 资产、加密货币、股票和指数的合成永续期货协议，提供高达 1000 倍的杠杆","ja":"OpenNotes Vault は、RWA アセット、暗号資産、株式、指数をサポートする合成永続先物プロトコルで、最大 1000 倍のレバレッジを提供します","ko":"OpenNotes Vault는 RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식 및 지수를 지원하는 합성 영속 선물 프로토콜로, 최대 1000배의 레버리지 제공","es":"OpenNote Vault es un protocolo de futuros perpetuos sintéticos que admite activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices.","fr":"OpenNote Vault est un protocole de futures perpétuels synthétiques qui prend en charge les actifs RWA, les crypto-monnaies, les actions et les indices.","de":"OpenNote Vault ist ein Protokoll für synthetische Perpetual Futures, das RWA-Vermögenswerte, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes unterstützt.","pt":"O opennote-vault é um protocolo de futuros sintéticos que permite aos traders abrir posições alavancadas longas/curtas com até 1000x de alavanco.","ru":"opennote-vault - это синтетический протокол фьючерсов, который позволяет трейдерам открывать левериджные длинные/короткие позиции с коэффициентом до 1000х.","ar":"opennote-vault هو بروتوكول مستقبلات اصطناعي يسمح للمتداولين بفتح مراكز طويلة / قصيرة بمعدل تداول يصل إلى 1000 مرة.","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a cus..."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenNotes Vault 协议：合成永续期货","ja":"OpenNotes Vault プロトコル：合成永続先物","ko":"OpenNotes Vault 프로토콜: 합성 영속 선물","es":"OpenNote Vault: Protocolo de Futuros Perpetuos","fr":"OpenNote Vault: Protocole de Futures Perpétuels","de":"OpenNote Vault: Perpetual Futures Protokoll","pt":"opennote-vault: Protocolo de Futuros Sintéticos","ru":"opennote-vault: Синтетический Протокол Фьючерсов","ar":"opennote-vault: بروتوكول مستقبلات اصطناعي","en":"opennote-vault"},"description":{"zh":"OpenNotes Vault 是一个支持 RWA 资产、加密货币、股票和指数的合成永续期货协议，提供高达 1000 倍的杠杆","ja":"OpenNotes Vault は、RWA アセット、暗号資産、株式、指数をサポートする合成永続先物プロトコルで、最大 1000 倍のレバレッジを提供します","ko":"OpenNotes Vault는 RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식 및 지수를 지원하는 합성 영속 선물 프로토콜로, 최대 1000배의 레버리지 제공","es":"OpenNote Vault es un protocolo de futuros perpetuos sintéticos que admite activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices.","fr":"OpenNote Vault est un protocole de futures perpétuels synthétiques qui prend en charge les actifs RWA, les crypto-monnaies, les actions et les indices.","de":"OpenNote Vault ist ein Protokoll für synthetische Perpetual Futures, das RWA-Vermögenswerte, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes unterstützt.","pt":"O opennote-vault é um protocolo de futuros sintéticos que permite aos traders abrir posições alavancadas longas/curtas com até 1000x de alavanco.","ru":"opennote-vault - это синтетический протокол фьючерсов, который позволяет трейдерам открывать левериджные длинные/короткие позиции с коэффициентом до 1000х.","ar":"opennote-vault هو بروتوكول مستقبلات اصطناعي يسمح للمتداولين بفتح مراكز طويلة / قصيرة بمعدل تداول يصل إلى 1000 مرة.","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collater..."},"definition":{"en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"zh":["支持 RWA 资产、加密货币、股票和指数","提供高达 1000 倍的杠杆","使用稳定币作为抵押品","自定义 oracle 和虚拟 AMM","TWAP 平滑价格"],"ja":["RWA アセット、暗号資産、株式、指数をサポート","最大 1000 倍のレバレッジを提供","安定したコインを担保として使用","カスタム オラクルと仮想 AMM","TWAP スムージング価格"],"ko":["RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식 및 지수를 지원","최대 1000배의 레버리지 제공","안정된 코인을 담보로 사용","사용자 정의 오라클 및 가상 AMM","TWAP 스무딩 가격"],"es":["Soporte para activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices","Posiciones apalancadas con hasta 1000 veces de apalancamiento","Bóveda de liquidez centralizada como contraparte para todos los trades","Precios que combinan un oráculo personalizado, un AMM virtual y suavizado de TWAP"],"fr":["Prise en charge des actifs RWA, des crypto-monnaies, des actions et des indices","Positions à effet de levier avec jusqu''à 1000 fois de levier","Chambre de liquidité centralisée en tant que contrepartie pour tous les trades","Prix qui combinent un oracle personnalisé, un AMM virtuel et un lissage de TWAP"],"de":["Unterstützung für RWA-Vermögenswerte, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes","Hebelgeschäfte mit bis zu 1000-fachem Hebel","Zentralisierte Liquiditätsbörse als Kontrahent für alle Trades","Preise, die einen benutzerdefinierten Oracle, ein virtuelles AMM und TWAP-Glättung kombinieren"],"pt":["Suporte a ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices","Posições alavancadas longas/curtas com até 1000x de alavanco","Cofre de liquidez centralizado","Preços combinados com oráculo personalizado, AMM virtual e suavização TWAP"],"ru":["Поддержка активов RWA, криптовалют, акций и индексов","Левериджные длинные/короткие позиции с коэффициентом до 1000х","Центральный кофр ликвидности","Цены, объединенные с индивидуальным оракулом, виртуальным AMM и сглаживанием TWAP"],"ar":["دعم أصول RWA وأسهم و Criptomoedas والفهارس","مراكز طويلة / قصيرة بمعدل تداول يصل إلى 1000 مرة","خزنة سيولة مركزية","أسعار مجتمعة مع بريدج مخصص و AMM افتراضي ومعالجة TWAP"]},"keywords":{"zh":["合成永续期货","RWA 资产","加密货币","股票","指数","杠杆","稳定币","oracle","AMM","TWAP"],"ja":["合成永続先物","RWA アセット","暗号資産","株式","指数","レバレッジ","安定したコイン","オラクル","AMM","TWAP"],"ko":["합성 영속 선물","RWA 자산","암호화폐","주식","지수","레버리지","안정된 코인","오라클","AMM","TWAP"],"es":["OpenNote Vault","futuros perpetuos","activos RWA","criptomonedas","acciones","índices","posiciones apalancadas","bóveda de liquidez"],"fr":["OpenNote Vault","futures perpétuels","actifs RWA","crypto-monnaies","actions","indices","positions à effet de levier","chambre de liquidité"],"de":["OpenNote Vault","Perpetual Futures","RWA-Vermögenswerte","Kryptowährungen","Aktien","Indizes","Hebelgeschäfte","Liquiditätsbörse"],"pt":["opennote-vault","protocolo de futuros sintéticos","ativos RWA","criptomoedas","ações","índices","posições alavancadas","cofre de liquidez centralizado"],"ru":["opennote-vault","синтетический протокол фьючерсов","активы RWA","криптовалюты","акции","индексы","левериджные позиции","центральный кофр ликвидности"],"ar":["opennote-vault","بروتوكول مستقبلات اصطناعي","أصول RWA","Criptomoedas","أَسهم","الفهارس","مراكز طويلة / قصيرة","خزنة سيولة مركزية"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.505Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"opennote-vault","description":"Use when managing markdown-based notes with SQL queries, creating notebooks with frontmatter metadata, searching notes by content or relationships, or executing reusable query views - handles note organization, DuckDB-powered search, and link analysis","bodyPreview":"# OpenNotes Vault Management\n\n## Overview\n\nOpenNotes manages markdown notes in notebooks with DuckDB-powered SQL queries. Create notes with frontmatter metadata, search by content or links, and execute reusable query views.\n\n**Core principle:** Notes are markdown files + metadata searchable via SQL queries.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Create or manage notebooks of markdown notes\n- Add notes with frontmatter metadata (tags, author, status, etc.)\n- Search notes by content,","body":"# OpenNotes Vault Management\n\n## Overview\n\nOpenNotes manages markdown notes in notebooks with DuckDB-powered SQL queries. Create notes with frontmatter metadata, search by content or links, and execute reusable query views.\n\n**Core principle:** Notes are markdown files + metadata searchable via SQL queries.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Create or manage notebooks of markdown notes\n- Add notes with frontmatter metadata (tags, author, status, etc.)\n- Search notes by content, metadata, or relationships\n- Execute SQL queries against note collections\n- Find broken links or orphaned notes\n- Create reusable query views\n\nDon''t use for:\n- Simple file-based note taking (just use mkdir/touch)\n- Binary attachments or non-markdown content\n- Real-time collaborative editing\n- Version control (use git separately)\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Essential Commands\n\n| Task | Command | Example |\n|------|---------|---------|\n| **Setup** | `opennotes init` | One-time initialization |\n| **Create notebook** | `opennotes notebook create --name <name>` | `opennotes notebook create --name \"work\"` |\n| **Add simple note** | `opennotes notes add \"<title>\"` | `opennotes notes add \"Meeting Notes\"` |\n| **Add with metadata** | `opennotes notes add \"<title>\" --data k=v` | `opennotes notes add \"Sprint\" --data tag=urgent` |\n| **List notes** | `opennotes notes list` | Shows all notes in current notebook |\n| **Search text** | `opennotes notes search \"<query>\"` | `opennotes notes search \"deadline\"` |\n| **Boolean query** | `opennotes notes search query --and <field>=<val>` | `opennotes notes search query --and data.tag=meeting` |\n| **SQL query** | `opennotes notes search --sql \"<query>\"` | `opennotes notes search --sql \"SELECT * FROM ...\"` |\n| **Execute view** | `opennotes notes view <name>` | `opennotes notes view today` |\n| **List views** | `opennotes notes view` | Shows all available views |\n\n### Feature Detection\n\nAlways check `--help` to determine available features, as version numbers may vary in dev builds.\n\n```bash\n# Check for metadata support\nopennotes notes add --help | grep -- ''--data'' && echo \"Metadata supported\"\n\n# Check for boolean query support\nopennotes notes search query --help && echo \"Boolean queries supported\"\n```\n\n## Notebook Management\n\n### Creating Notebooks\n\n```bash\n# Create new notebook in current directory\nopennotes notebook create --name \"project-notes\"\n# Creates: .opennotes.json in current directory\n# Notes are stored in current directory (root: \".\")\n\n# To create notebook in a new subdirectory:\nmkdir project-notes && cd project-notes\nopennotes notebook create --name \"project-notes\"\n\n# View notebook info\nopennotes notebook\n```\n\n### Notebook Auto-Discovery\n\nOpenNotes finds notebooks automatically:\n\n1. Searches current directory for `.opennotes.json`\n2. Walks up parent directories until found\n3. Falls back to registered notebooks in global config\n4. Override with `--notebook <path>` flag\n\n```bash\n# Work from anywhere in notebook tree\ncd project-notes/2026/january\nopennotes notes list  # Auto-discovers notebook\n\n# Use specific notebook\nopennotes notes list --notebook ~/work-notes\n```\n\n### Managing Multiple Notebooks\n\n```bash\n# List all registered notebooks\nopennotes notebook list\n\n# Register existing notebook\nopennotes notebook register ~/existing-notes\n\n# Add context path (for auto-discovery)\nopennotes notebook add-context /path/to/workspace\n```\n\n## Note Creation\n\n### Basic Note Creation\n\n```bash\n# Simple note (filename auto-slugified)\nopennotes notes add \"My First Note\"\n# Creates: my-first-note.md\n\n# Title with special characters\nopennotes notes add \"2026-01-24: Daily Log\"\n# Creates: 2026-01-24-daily-log.md\n\n# Using deprecated --title flag (still works)\nopennotes notes add --title \"Meeting Notes\"\n```\n\n### With Metadata (v0.0.3+)\n\n```bash\n# Single metadata field\nopennotes notes add \"Team Standup\" --data author=\"John Doe\"\n\n# Multiple fields\nopennotes notes add \"API Review\" \\\n  --data author=\"Engineering Team\" \\\n  --data priority=high \\\n  --data status=draft\n\n# Array values (repeated fields)\nopennotes notes add \"Sprint Planning\" \\\n  --data tag=meeting \\\n  --data tag=urgent \\\n  --data tag=sprint\n\n# Result in frontmatter:\n# ---\n# author: John Doe\n# priority: high\n# tag:\n#   - meeting\n#   - urgent\n# ---\n```\n\n### Path Options\n\n```bash\n# Create in subfolder\nopennotes notes add \"Project Plan\" projects/\n# Creates: projects/project-plan.md\n\n# Specify exact filename\nopennotes notes add \"Changelog\" CHANGELOG\n# Creates: CHANGELOG.md\n\n# Full path with extension\nopennotes notes add \"README\" docs/README.md\n# Creates: docs/README.md\n```\n\n### Content Priority\n\nNotes are populated in this order:\n\n1. **Stdin** (piped content)\n2. **Template** (`--template` flag)\n3. **Default** (simple `# Title\\n\\n`)\n\n```bash\n# From stdin\necho \"# Meeting Notes\\n\\n- Point 1\" | opennotes notes add \"Meeting\"\n\n# From template\nopennotes notes add \"Standup\" --template daily-standup\n\n# Default (just title)\nopennotes notes add \"Quick Note\"\n```\n\n## Searching Notes\n\n### Text Search (v0.0.2+)\n\n```bash\n# Search all fields (content, title, filename)\nopennotes notes search \"deadline\"\n\n# Case-insensitive, partial matches\nopennotes notes search \"meet\"  # Finds \"Meeting\", \"meet\", \"meetings\"\n\n# No results\nopennotes notes search \"nonexistent\"\n# Output: No notes found matching ''nonexistent''\n```\n\n### Fuzzy Search (v0.0.3+)\n\n```bash\n# Typo-tolerant search\nopennotes notes search --fuzzy \"meetng\"  # Finds \"meeting\"\n\n# Ranked by relevance\nopennotes notes search --fuzzy \"project\"\n# Title matches ranked higher than body matches\n```\n\n### Boolean Queries (v0.0.3+)\n\n```bash\n# Single condition (AND)\nopennotes notes search query --and data.priority=high\n\n# Multiple AND conditions\nopennotes notes search query --and data.status=active --and data.priority=high\n\n# OR conditions\nopennotes notes search query --or data.priority=high --or data.priority=critical\n\n# NOT conditions\nopennotes notes search query --and data.type=task --not data.status=archived\n\n# Path glob patterns\nopennotes notes search query --and \"path=projects/**/*.md\"\n\n# Complex queries (mix AND/OR)\nopennotes notes search query \\\n  --and \"data.type=task\" \\\n  --and \"data.status=active\" \\\n  --or \"data.priority=high\" \\\n  --or \"data.priority=critical\"\n```\n\n**Supported Fields**:\n- `data.*` (any metadata field, use for scalar values)\n- `path` (file path with glob support)\n- `title` (note title from frontmatter or filename)\n- `links-to` (outgoing links)\n- `linked-by` (incoming links)\n\n**Operators**:\n- `--and` (all must match)\n- `--or` (any must match)\n- `--not` (exclude matches)\n\n**⚠️ Limitation:** Boolean queries work best with scalar metadata values (strings, numbers). For array fields (created with repeated `--data` flags), use SQL queries instead.\n\n### Link Queries (v0.0.3+)\n\n```bash\n# Find notes linking to specific note\nopennotes notes search query --and \"links-to=README.md\"\n\n# With glob patterns\nopennotes notes search query --and \"links-to=docs/*.md\"\n\n# Find notes linked by specific note\nopennotes notes search query --and \"linked-by=index.md\"\n\n# Combined with other conditions\nopennotes notes search query --and \"links-to=*.md\" --and \"data.status=reference\"\n```\n\n### Querying Array Metadata\n\nArray metadata fields (created with repeated `--data` flags) are stored correctly in YAML but have limitations in boolean query interface. Use these approaches:\n\n```bash\n# Text search works for array content\nopennotes notes search \"meeting\"  # Finds notes with ''meeting'' in any array field\n\n# SQL query for precise array membership\nopennotes notes search --sql \\\n  \"SELECT * FROM read_markdown(''**/*.md'') \n   WHERE content LIKE ''%- meeting%''\"  # Search in YAML array format\n\n# Alternative: Use scalar metadata for queryable fields\n# Instead of: opennotes notes add \"Note\" --data tag=meeting --data tag=important\n# Consider: opennotes notes add \"Note\" --data status=draft --data category=meeting\n# Then query with: opennotes notes search query --and data.category=meeting\n```\n\n### SQL Queries (v0.0.3+)\n\n```bash\n# Direct SQL query (uses glob pattern from config)\nopennotes notes search --sql \"SELECT * FROM read_markdown(''**/*.md'')\"\n\n# With WHERE clause for scalar fields\nopennotes notes search --sql \\\n  \"SELECT file_path, metadata FROM read_markdown(''**/*.md'') \n   WHERE metadata[''status''] = ''active''\"\n\n# Query array fields (better for tag fields)\nopennotes notes search --sql \\\n  \"SELECT file_path, metadata FROM read_markdown(''**/*.md'')\n   WHERE array_contains(metadata[''tag''], ''meeting'')\"\n\n# Complex aggregations\nopennotes notes search --sql \\\n  \"WITH tagged AS (\n     SELECT file_path, metadata[''tag''] as tag\n     FROM read_markdown(''**/*.md'')\n   )\n   SELECT tag, COUNT(*) as count\n   FROM tagged\n   WHERE tag IS NOT NULL\n   GROUP BY tag\n   ORDER BY count DESC\"\n```\n\n**Safety**:\n- Only `SELECT` and `WITH` queries allowed\n- `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `DROP` blocked\n- Parameterized queries prevent SQL injection\n\n**Pattern Notes**:\n- Use glob patterns matching your `groups[].globs` config\n- Metadata is stored as a struct/object - access fields with `metadata[''field_name'']`\n- Array fields use `array_contains()` function for membership testing\n- Date comparisons use ISO 8601 format (e.g., `''2026-01-20''`)\n\n## Views System (v0.0.3+)\n\n### Built-in Views\n\n```bash\n# List all available views\nopennotes notes view\n\n# Execute built-in view\nopennotes notes view today        # Notes created/updated today\nopennotes notes view recent       # Last 30 days\nopennotes notes view untagged     # Notes without tags\nopennotes notes view orphans      # Notes with no incoming links\nopennotes notes view broken-links # Notes with broken links\n\n# Parameterized view\nopennotes notes view kanban --param status=in-progress\n```\n\n### Custom Views\n\nDefine in notebook''s `.opennotes.json` or global `~/.config/opennotes/config.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"views\": {\n    \"active-tasks\": {\n      \"description\": \"All active tasks\",\n      \"conditions\": [\n        {\"field\": \"tag\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": \"task\"},\n        {\"field\": \"status\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": \"active\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    \"recent-meetings\": {\n      \"description\": \"Meetings in last 7 days\",\n      \"conditions\": [\n        {\"field\": \"tag\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": \"meeting\"},\n        {\"field\": \"created\", \"operator\": \">=\", \"value\": \"{{7_days_ago}}\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**View Precedence**:\n1. Notebook config (`.opennotes.json`)\n2. Global config (`~/.config/opennotes/config.json`)\n3. Built-in views\n\n### Template Variables\n\nUse in view definitions:\n\n- `{{today}}` - Today''s date (YYYY-MM-DD)\n- `{{yesterday}}` - Yesterday''s date\n- `{{this_week}}` - Start of current week\n- `{{this_month}}` - Start of current month\n- `{{7_days_ago}}` - Date 7 days ago\n- `{{30_days_ago}}` - Date 30 days ago\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n### Daily Note Workflow\n\n```bash\n# Create today''s note\nopennotes notes add \"$(date +%Y-%m-%d): Daily Log\" \\\n  --data type=daily \\\n  --data date=\"$(date +%Y-%m-%d)\"\n\n# View today''s notes\nopennotes notes view today\n\n# Search recent dailies (SQL for date range)\nopennotes notes search --sql \"SELECT * FROM read_markdown(''.notes/**/*.md'') WHERE metadata[''type''] = ''daily'' AND created >= ''2026-01-20''\"\n```\n\n### Project Management\n\n```bash\n# Create project epic\nopennotes notes add \"Q1 2026 Goals\" projects/ \\\n  --data tag=epic \\\n  --data status=planning \\\n  --data priority=high\n\n# Create tasks\nopennotes notes add \"Implement Feature X\" tasks/ \\\n  --data tag=task \\\n  --data epic=q1-2026-goals \\\n  --data status=todo\n\n# View active tasks\nopennotes notes search query --and \"data.tag=task\" --and \"data.status=todo\"\n\n# Kanban board\nopennotes notes view kanban --param status=in-progress\n```\n\n### Knowledge Base\n\n```bash\n# Create reference note\nopennotes notes add \"Git Cheatsheet\" reference/ \\\n  --data tag=reference \\\n  --data tag=git \\\n  --data category=tools\n\n# Link analysis\nopennotes notes view orphans        # Unconnected notes\nopennotes notes view broken-links   # Fix broken links\n\n# Find related notes\nopennotes notes search query --and \"data.tag=git\"\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n### ❌ Using --title instead of positional argument\n\n```bash\n# Don''t (deprecated flag)\nopennotes notes add --title \"My Note\"\n\n# Do (positional argument)\nopennotes notes add \"My Note\"\n```\n\n### ❌ Forgetting flags for boolean queries\n\n```bash\n# Don''t (missing flags)\nopennotes notes search query tag=urgent status=active\n\n# Do (use explicit flags and data prefix)\nopennotes notes search query --and data.status=active --and data.priority=high\n```\n\n### ❌ Using boolean queries for array fields\n\n```bash\n# Don''t (arrays not queryable via boolean interface)\nopennotes notes search query --and data.tag=meeting  # Won''t work reliably\n\n# Do (use SQL for array fields)\nopennotes notes search --sql \"SELECT * FROM read_markdown(''**/*.md'') WHERE array_contains(metadata[''tag''], ''meeting'')\"\n```\n\n### ❌ Using --data on old version\n\n```bash\n# Check version first\nopennotes notes add --help | grep -q -- ''--data'' || echo \"Upgrade needed\"\n\n# On v0.0.2: Edit frontmatter manually after creation\nopennotes notes add \"My Note\"\nvim my-note.md  # Add frontmatter manually\n```\n\n### ❌ Assuming case-sensitive search\n\n```bash\n# Search is case-INsensitive\nopennotes notes search \"MEETING\"  # Finds \"meeting\", \"Meeting\", etc.\n```\n\n### ❌ Forgetting notebook auto-discovery\n\n```bash\n# Don''t (unnecessary --notebook flag)\ncd ~/my-notes\nopennotes notes list --notebook ~/my-notes\n\n# Do (auto-discovery from current directory)\ncd ~/my-notes\nopennotes notes list\n```\n\n### ❌ Looking for notes in .notes/ directory\n\n```bash\n# Don''t (notes are stored in notebook root by default)\nls .notes/  # Directory doesn''t exist\n\n# Do (check notebook root)\nls *.md     # Notes stored here\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### No notebook found\n\n```bash\n# Error: No notebook found\n# Solution 1: Create notebook\nopennotes notebook create --name \"my-notes\"\n\n# Solution 2: Register existing\nopennotes notebook register ~/existing-notes\n\n# Solution 3: Specify explicitly\nopennotes notes list --notebook ~/my-notes\n```\n\n### Metadata not showing in frontmatter\n\n```bash\n# Check version supports --data\nopennotes notes add --help | grep -- ''--data''\n\n# Verify format: field=value (no spaces around =)\nopennotes notes add \"Note\" --data \"tag = value\"  # ❌ Wrong\nopennotes notes add \"Note\" --data \"tag=value\"    # ✅ Correct\n\n# Check created file (notes stored in notebook root by default)\ncat note.md\n```\n\n### Search returns no results\n\n```bash\n# Verify notebook has notes\nopennotes notes list\n\n# Check search is case-insensitive\nopennotes notes search \"KEYWORD\"\n\n# Try broader search\nopennotes notes search \"\"  # List all notes\n\n# Use SQL for debugging\nopennotes notes search --sql \"SELECT * FROM read_markdown(''.notes/**/*.md'')\"\n```\n\n## Configuration Files\n\n### Global Config\n\n`~/.config/opennotes/config.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"notebooks\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"work\",\n      \"path\": \"/home/user/work-notes\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"views\": {\n    \"my-custom-view\": {\n      \"description\": \"Custom view\",\n      \"conditions\": []\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Notebook Config\n\n`.opennotes.json` in notebook root:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"root\": \".\",\n  \"name\": \"My Notebook\",\n  \"contexts\": [\n    \"/path/to/workspace\"\n  ],\n  \"groups\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Default\",\n      \"globs\": [\n        \"**/*.md\"\n      ],\n      \"metadata\": {}\n    }\n  ],\n  \"views\": {\n    \"project-active\": {\n      \"description\": \"Active project tasks\",\n      \"conditions\": [\n        {\"field\": \"tag\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": \"project\"},\n        {\"field\": \"status\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": \"active\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Configuration Fields**:\n- `root`: Base directory for notes (typically `\".\"` for notebook root)\n- `name`: Notebook display name\n- `contexts`: Paths for auto-discovery\n- `groups`: Array of note groups with glob patterns for discovery\n- `views`: Custom view definitions (optional)\n\n## Environment Variables\n\n```bash\n# Override config path\nexport OPENNOTES_CONFIG=\"~/.config/opennotes/custom.json\"\n\n# Enable debug logging\nexport DEBUG=1\nexport LOG_LEVEL=debug\n\n# In scripts\nOPENNOTES_CONFIG=/tmp/test-config.json opennotes notes list\n```\n\n## Integration Examples\n\n### With Git\n\n```bash\n# Initialize notebook with git\nmkdir wiki && cd wiki\nopennotes notebook create --name \"wiki\"\ngit init\necho \".DS_Store\" > .gitignore\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit\"\n\n# Commit after note creation\nopennotes notes add \"New Feature Spec\" --data status=draft\ngit add new-feature-spec.md  # Notes in notebook root by default\ngit commit -m \"Add feature spec\"\n```\n\n### With Obsidian\n\nOpenNotes notebooks are compatible with Obsidian:\n\n1. Create OpenNotes notebook: `mkdir obsidian-vault && cd obsidian-vault && opennotes notebook create --name \"obsidian-vault\"`\n2. Open in Obsidian: Point to notebook directory\n3. Use OpenNotes for CLI operations, Obsidian for GUI editing\n4. Frontmatter metadata is shared between both tools\n5. Notes are stored in notebook root by default (same directory as `.opennotes.json`)\n\n### With Scripts\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# daily-note.sh - Create daily note with template\n\nDATE=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)\nTITLE=\"$DATE: Daily Log\"\n\nopennotes notes add \"$TITLE\" \\\n  --data type=daily \\\n  --data date=\"$DATE\" \\\n  --template daily-standup\n\n# Open in editor (notes stored in notebook root by default)\n$EDITOR *${DATE}*.md\n```\n\n## Performance Characteristics\n\n### Scalability\n\n- **Small notebooks** (< 100 notes): Instant operations\n- **Medium notebooks** (100-1000 notes): ~100ms search latency\n- **Large notebooks** (1000+ notes): ~1s search latency (1147 ops/sec tested)\n\n### Memory Usage\n\n- **Per note**: ~4KB memory footprint at scale\n- **1000 notes**: ~4MB total memory usage\n- **Search**: Memory-efficient streaming queries\n\n### Concurrency\n\n- **Thread-safe**: Safe for concurrent operations\n- **Connection pooling**: DuckDB handles locking\n- **File operations**: Uses atomic writes where possible\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\n### Use Cases\n\n1. **Personal Knowledge Base**: 500+ reference notes, full-text search, link analysis\n2. **Project Management**: Task tracking with metadata, kanban views, status queries\n3. **Meeting Notes**: Daily logs, searchable archive, template-based creation\n4. **Documentation**: Technical specs, API docs, cross-referenced with link queries\n\n### Advantages Over Alternatives\n\n**vs Plain Markdown + grep**:\n- Structured metadata queries (not just text search)\n- Link analysis and relationship tracking\n- Reusable views with parameters\n- SQL query power\n\n**vs Obsidian**:\n- CLI automation and scripting\n- SSH/remote access friendly\n- Version control friendly (plain text)\n- SQL query interface\n\n**vs Notion/Roam**:\n- Local-first, no cloud dependency\n- Plain markdown files (portability)\n- Git-friendly for version control\n- Open source, extensible\n\n## Further Reading\n\n- **Note Creation Guide**: `docs/note-creation-guide.md` (471 lines)\n- **Search Guide**: `docs/commands/notes-search.md` (407 lines)\n- **Views Guide**: `docs/views-guide.md` (880 lines)\n- **Views API**: `docs/views-api.md` (805 lines)\n- **Views Examples**: `docs/views-examples.md` (812 lines)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T11:58:55.811Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Knowledge Management Agents needing advanced markdown note organization and SQL query capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级markdown笔记组织和SQL查询功能的知识管理代理。","ja":"高度なMarkdownノートの整理とSQLクエリ機能が必要なナレッジマネジメントエージェントに最適。","ko":"고급 마크다운 노트 조직 및 SQL 쿼리 기능이 필요한 지식 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfect for Knowledge Management Agents needing advanced markdown note organization and SQL query capabilities.","fr":"Perfect for Knowledge Management Agents needing advanced markdown note organization and SQL query capabilities.","de":"Perfect for Knowledge Management Agents needing advanced markdown note organization and SQL query capabilities.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Conhecimento que necessitam de organização avançada de notas em markdown e capacidades de consulta SQL.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов управления знаниями, которым необходима расширенная организация заметок в формате markdown и возможности запросов SQL.","ar":"مثالي لعميل إدارة المعرفة الذي يحتاج إلى تنظيم متقدم للملاحظات بأسلوب Markdown وقدرات استعلام SQL."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage notebooks of markdown notes with DuckDB-powered SQL queries, enabling efficient note creation, searching, and querying via reusable query views, utilizing frontmatter metadata and markdown file formats.","zh":"赋予代理管理带有自定义元数据的markdown笔记本的能力，使用DuckDB驱动的SQL查询，实现高效的笔记创建、搜索和查询，通过可重用的查询视图，利用前置元数据和markdown文件格式。","ja":"DuckDBを利用したSQLクエリでノートブックの作成、検索、クエリを効率的に行えるようにエージェントをEmpowerし、再利用可能なクエリビューを使用してメタデータとMarkdownファイル形式を活用する。","ko":"DuckDB를 활용한 SQL 쿼리를 사용하여 노트북의 생성, 검색, 쿼리를 효율적으로 수행할 수 있도록 에이전트를 강화하고, 재사용 가능한 쿼리 뷰를 사용하여 메타데이터와 마크다운 파일 형식을 활용합니다.","es":"Empowers agents to manage notebooks of markdown notes with DuckDB-powered SQL queries, enabling efficient note creation, searching, and querying via reusable query views, utilizing frontmatter metadata and markdown file formats.","fr":"Empowers agents to manage notebooks of markdown notes with DuckDB-powered SQL queries, enabling efficient note creation, searching, and querying via reusable query views, utilizing frontmatter metadata and markdown file formats.","de":"Empowers agents to manage notebooks of markdown notes with DuckDB-powered SQL queries, enabling efficient note creation, searching, and querying via reusable query views, utilizing frontmatter metadata and markdown file formats.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar notebooks de notas em markdown com consultas SQL com suporte do DuckDB, permitindo a criação eficiente de notas, busca e consulta por meio de visualizações de consulta reutilizáveis, utilizando metadados de frontmatter e formatos de arquivo markdown.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять блокнотами заметок в формате markdown с помощью запросов SQL, поддерживаемых DuckDB, что позволяет эффективно создавать заметки, искать и запрашивать их через многоразовые представления запросов, используя метаданные frontmatter и форматы файлов markdown.","ar":"يُضفي على العميل القدرة على إدارة دفاتر ملاحظات بأسلوب Markdown باستخدام استعلامات SQL مدعومة من DuckDB، مما يسمح بإنشاء ملاحظات فعالة، البحث عنها والاستعلام عنها من خلال مناظير استعلام قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام، باستخدام بيانات تعريف المستند والتنسيقات الملفية بأسلوب Markdown."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating and managing notebooks of markdown notes with custom metadata","Searching notes by content or links using SQL queries","Executing reusable query views for efficient note retrieval"],"zh":["创建和管理带有自定义元数据的markdown笔记本","使用SQL查询按内容或链接搜索笔记","执行可重用的查询视图以实现高效的笔记检索"],"ja":["カスタムメタデータを含むMarkdownノートブックの作成と管理","SQLクエリを使用してコンテンツまたはリンクでノートを検索する","効率的なノートの取得を実現するための再利用可能なクエリビューの実行"],"ko":["커스텀 메타데이터를 포함한 마크다운 노트북의 생성 및 관리","SQL 쿼리를 사용하여 내용 또는 링크로 노트를 검색","효율적인 노트 검색을实现하기 위한 재사용 가능한 쿼리 뷰의 실행"],"es":["Creating and managing notebooks of markdown notes with custom metadata","Searching notes by content or links using SQL queries","Executing reusable query views for efficient note retrieval"],"fr":["Creating and managing notebooks of markdown notes with custom metadata","Searching notes by content or links using SQL queries","Executing reusable query views for efficient note retrieval"],"de":["Creating and managing notebooks of markdown notes with custom metadata","Searching notes by content or links using SQL queries","Executing reusable query views for efficient note retrieval"],"pt":["Criando e gerenciando notebooks de notas em markdown com metadados personalizados","Pesquisando notas por conteúdo ou links usando consultas SQL","Executando visualizações de consulta reutilizáveis para recuperação eficiente de notas"],"ru":["Создание и управление блокнотами заметок в формате markdown с пользовательскими метаданными","Поиск заметок по содержанию или ссылкам с помощью запросов SQL","Выполнение многоразовых представлений запросов для эффективного извлечения заметок"],"ar":["إنشاء وإدارة دفاتر ملاحظات بأسلوب Markdown مع بيانات تعريف مخصصة","البحث عن الملاحظات من خلال المحتوى أو الروابط باستخدام استعلامات SQL","تنفيذ مناظير استعلام قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام لاسترجاع الملاحظات بفعالية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires DuckDB for SQL query functionality","Limited to markdown file format for notes"],"zh":["需要DuckDB来实现SQL查询功能","仅限于markdown文件格式的笔记"],"ja":["SQLクエリ機能を実現するためにDuckDBが必要","ノートはMarkdownファイル形式のみ"],"ko":["SQL 쿼리 기능을 구현하기 위해 DuckDB가 필요","노트는 마크다운 파일 형식만"],"es":["Requires DuckDB for SQL query functionality","Limited to markdown file format for notes"],"fr":["Requires DuckDB for SQL query functionality","Limited to markdown file format for notes"],"de":["Requires DuckDB for SQL query functionality","Limited to markdown file format for notes"],"pt":["Requer DuckDB para funcionalidade de consulta SQL","Limitado ao formato de arquivo markdown para notas"],"ru":["Требует DuckDB для функциональности запросов SQL","Ограничен форматом файла markdown для заметок"],"ar":["يتطلب DuckDB للوظيفة استعلام SQL","محدود بتنسيق الملف بأسلوب Markdown للملاحظات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
