مستخدم الأمامية"]}},"owner":"congwa","repo":"wdm","repoPath":"congwa/wdm","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.505Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend-component-design","description":"前端组件设计规范与最佳实践。在编写任何前端代码（React/Next.js 组件、页面、hooks）时自动触发。确保代码复用性、封装性、单一职责原则。触发场景包括创建新的前端组件或页面、重构现有前端代码、添加新功能到前端、任何涉及 frontend 目录的代码修改。此技能始终生效。","bodyPreview":"# 前端组件设计规范\n\n确保前端代码的复用性、封装性和可维护性。\n\n## 核心原则\n\n### 1. 单一职责原则\n- 每个文件只包含一个组件\n- 每个组件只负责一个业务功能\n- 组件代码不超过 **500 行**，超过则拆分\n\n### 2. 组件拆分规则\n\n```\n# 拆分时机判断\nif 组件 > 500 行:\n    拆分为子组件\nif 相同代码出现 >= 2 次:\n    抽取为公共组件\nif 业务逻辑复杂:\n    抽取为 hooks\nif 配置数据多:\n    抽取为配置文件\n```\n\n### 3. 目录结构规范\n\n```\nfrontend/\n├── components/           # 公共组件\n│   ├── ui/              # shadcn 基础组件\n│   └── admin/           # 业务公共组件\n├── app/                 # 页面\n│   └── admin/\n│       └── [feature]/\n│           ├── page.tsx         # 主页面（协调逻辑）\n│","body":"# 前端组件设计规范\n\n确保前端代码的复用性、封装性和可维护性。\n\n## 核心原则\n\n### 1. 单一职责原则\n- 每个文件只包含一个组件\n- 每个组件只负责一个业务功能\n- 组件代码不超过 **500 行**，超过则拆分\n\n### 2. 组件拆分规则\n\n```\n# 拆分时机判断\nif 组件 > 500 行:\n    拆分为子组件\nif 相同代码出现 >= 2 次:\n    抽取为公共组件\nif 业务逻辑复杂:\n    抽取为 hooks\nif 配置数据多:\n    抽取为配置文件\n```\n\n### 3. 目录结构规范\n\n```\nfrontend/\n├── components/           # 公共组件\n│   ├── ui/              # shadcn 基础组件\n│   └── admin/           # 业务公共组件\n├── app/                 # 页面\n│   └── admin/\n│       └── [feature]/\n│           ├── page.tsx         # 主页面（协调逻辑）\n│           └── components/      # 页面私有组件（可选）\n├── lib/\n│   ├── api/             # API 请求函数\n│   ├── config/          # 配置和映射\n│   └── hooks/           # 公共 hooks\n├── hooks/               # 全局 hooks\n└── types/               # 类型定义\n```\n\n### 4. 配置外置原则\n\n将以下内容抽取到 `lib/config/` 目录：\n- **标签映射** → `labels.ts` (英文→中文)\n- **枚举常量** → `constants.ts`\n- **表单配置** → `forms.ts`\n- **主题配置** → `theme.ts`\n\n示例：\n```typescript\n// lib/config/labels.ts\nexport const MIDDLEWARE_LABELS = {\n  MemoryOrchestration: { label: \"记忆编排\", desc: \"...\" },\n  // ...\n};\nexport function getMiddlewareLabel(name: string) {\n  return MIDDLEWARE_LABELS[name] || { label: name, desc: \"\" };\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Hooks 抽取规则\n\n抽取为 hook 的时机：\n- 状态逻辑复杂（>5 个 useState）\n- 数据获取逻辑\n- 副作用逻辑复杂\n- 相同逻辑在多处使用\n\n命名规范：`use[业务名][动作]`\n```typescript\n// lib/hooks/use-agents.ts\nexport function useAgentDetail({ agentId }: { agentId: string }) {\n  const [agent, setAgent] = useState<Agent | null>(null);\n  // ...\n  return { agent, isLoading, error, refresh };\n}\n```\n\n### 6. 导入路径规范\n\n始终使用 `@/` 别名，避免相对路径：\n```typescript\n// ✅ 正确\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\nimport { getAgentEffectiveConfig } from \"@/lib/api/agents\";\n\n// ❌ 错误\nimport { Button } from \"../../components/ui/button\";\n```\n\n## 编码前规划清单\n\n编写前端代码前，必须回答：\n\n1. **组件边界**：这个组件的职责是什么？是否单一？\n2. **复用性**：是否有已存在的类似组件可复用？\n3. **配置外置**：是否有硬编码的中文/配置需要抽取？\n4. **文件大小**：预估代码行数，是否需要拆分？\n5. **命名规范**：组件/文件命名是否清晰表达业务含义？\n\n## 代码审查要点\n\n完成编码后，检查：\n\n- [ ] 单文件不超过 500 行\n- [ ] 无重复代码（相同代码不超过 2 处）\n- [ ] 所有中文标签来自配置文件\n- [ ] 使用 `@/` 路径别名\n- [ ] 组件职责单一\n- [ ] 复杂逻辑已抽取为 hooks\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:00:29.214Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Windsurf AI and other modern frontend development agents needing structured component design and management capabilities.","zh":"Perfect for Windsurf AI and other modern frontend development agents needing structured component design and management capabilities.","ja":"Perfect for Windsurf AI and other modern frontend development agents needing structured component design and management capabilities.","ko":"Perfect for Windsurf AI and other modern frontend development agents needing structured component design and management capabilities.","es":"Perfecto para Windsurf AI y otros agentes de desarrollo de frontend modernos que necesitan diseño y capacidades de gestión de componentes estructurados.","fr":"Parfait pour Windsurf AI et d''autres agents de développement de frontend modernes ayant besoin d''une conception et de capacités de gestion de composants structurées.","de":"Perfekt für Windsurf AI und andere moderne Frontend-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine strukturierte Komponenten-Design- und Managementfunktion benötigen.","pt":"Perfect for Windsurf AI and other modern frontend development agents needing structured component design and management capabilities.","ru":"Perfect for Windsurf AI and other modern frontend development agents needing structured component design and management capabilities.","ar":"Perfect for Windsurf AI and other modern frontend development agents needing structured component design and management capabilities."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce single responsibility principle, implement efficient component splitting rules, and maintain organized directory structures using TypeScript and React, while ensuring code reusability, encapsulation, and maintainability through standards like 500-line component limits and hooks for complex business logic.","zh":"Empowers agents to enforce single responsibility principle, implement efficient component splitting rules, and maintain organized directory structures using TypeScript and React, while ensuring code reusability, encapsulation, and maintainability through standards like 500-line component limits and hooks for complex business logic.","ja":"Empowers agents to enforce single responsibility principle, implement efficient component splitting rules, and maintain organized directory structures using TypeScript and React, while ensuring code reusability, encapsulation, and maintainability through standards like 500-line component limits and hooks for complex business logic.","ko":"Empowers agents to enforce single responsibility principle, implement efficient component splitting rules, and maintain organized directory structures using TypeScript and React, while ensuring code reusability, encapsulation, and maintainability through standards like 500-line component limits and hooks for complex business logic.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar el principio de responsabilidad única, implementar reglas de división de componentes eficientes y mantener estructuras de directorios organizadas utilizando TypeScript y React, garantizando al mismo tiempo la reutilización del código, el encapsulamiento y la mantenibilidad a través de estándares como límites de componentes de 500 líneas y ganchos para lógica de negocio compleja.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer le principe de responsabilité unique, de mettre en œuvre des règles de division de composants efficaces et de maintenir des structures de répertoires organisées en utilisant TypeScript et React, tout en garantissant la réutilisation du code, l''encapsulation et la maintenabilité grâce à des normes telles que des limites de composant de 500 lignes et des crochets pour une logique métier complexe.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, das Prinzip der einzelnen Verantwortung durchzusetzen, effiziente Komponenten-Splitting-Regeln umzusetzen und organisierte Verzeichnisstrukturen mithilfe von TypeScript und React zu pflegen, während gleichzeitig die Code-Wiederverwendbarkeit, die Kapselung und die Wartbarkeit durch Standards wie 500-Zeilen-Komponentenlimits und Haken für komplexe Geschäftlogik sichergestellt werden.","pt":"Empowers agents to enforce single responsibility principle, implement efficient component splitting rules, and maintain organized directory structures using TypeScript and React, while ensuring code reusability, encapsulation, and maintainability through standards like 500-line component limits and hooks for complex business logic.","ru":"Empowers agents to enforce single responsibility principle, implement efficient component splitting rules, and maintain organized directory structures using TypeScript and React, while ensuring code reusability, encapsulation, and maintainability through standards like 500-line component limits and hooks for complex business logic.","ar":"Empowers agents to enforce single responsibility principle, implement efficient component splitting rules, and maintain organized directory structures using TypeScript and React, while ensuring code reusability, encapsulation, and maintainability through standards like 500-line component limits and hooks for complex business logic."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing modular and scalable frontend architectures","Implementing automated component splitting based on code complexity","Enforcing coding standards across large frontend codebases"],"zh":["Designing modular and scalable frontend architectures","Implementing automated component splitting based on code complexity","Enforcing coding standards across large frontend codebases"],"ja":["Designing modular and scalable frontend architectures","Implementing automated component splitting based on code complexity","Enforcing coding standards across large frontend codebases"],"ko":["Designing modular and scalable frontend architectures","Implementing automated component splitting based on code complexity","Enforcing coding standards across large frontend codebases"],"es":["Diseñar arquitecturas de frontend modulares y escalables","Implementar una división automática de componentes basada en la complejidad del código","Aplicar normas de codificación en grandes bases de código de frontend"],"fr":["Concevoir des architectures de frontend modulaires et évolutives","Mettre en œuvre une division automatique de composants basée sur la complexité du code","Faire respecter les normes de codage dans de grandes bases de code de frontend"],"de":["Entwicklung modularer und skalierbarer Frontend-Architekturen","Implementierung automatisierter Komponenten-Splitting basierend auf Code-Komplexität","Durchsetzung von Codierungsstandards in großen Frontend-Codebasen"],"pt":["Designing modular and scalable frontend architectures","Implementing automated component splitting based on code complexity","Enforcing coding standards across large frontend codebases"],"ru":["Designing modular and scalable frontend architectures","Implementing automated component splitting based on code complexity","Enforcing coding standards across large frontend codebases"],"ar":["Designing modular and scalable frontend architectures","Implementing automated component splitting based on code complexity","Enforcing coding standards across large frontend codebases"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires TypeScript and React familiarity","Limited to frontend development contexts","Enforces specific coding standards which may not be compatible with all project requirements"],"zh":["Requires TypeScript and React familiarity","Limited to frontend development contexts","Enforces specific coding standards which may not be compatible with all project requirements"],"ja":["Requires TypeScript and React familiarity","Limited to frontend development contexts","Enforces specific coding standards which may not be compatible with all project requirements"],"ko":["Requires TypeScript and React familiarity","Limited to frontend development contexts","Enforces specific coding standards which may not be compatible with all project requirements"],"es":["Requiere conocimientos de TypeScript y React","Limitado a contextos de desarrollo de frontend","Aplica normas de codificación específicas que pueden no ser compatibles con todos los requisitos del proyecto"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en TypeScript et React","Limité aux contextes de développement de frontend","Impose des normes de codage spécifiques qui peuvent ne pas être compatibles avec tous les besoins du projet"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse in TypeScript und React","Begrenzt auf Frontend-Entwicklungskontexte","Zwingt spezifische Codierungsstandards auf, die möglicherweise nicht mit allen Projektanforderungen kompatibel sind"],"pt":["Requires TypeScript and React familiarity","Limited to frontend development contexts","Enforces specific coding standards which may not be compatible with all project requirements