ntend","ru":"Разработка фронтенд-компонентов","ar":"تصميم مكونات واجهة المستخدم الأمامية","en":"frontend-component-design"},"description":{"zh":"前端组件设计规范是为了确保代码的复用性、封装性和可维护性，提供了单一职责原则、组件拆分规则和目录结构规范等","ja":"フロントエンドコンポーネント設計規約は、コードの再利用性、カプセル化、メンテナンス性を確保するために、シングルレスポンス原則、コンポーネント分割規則、ディレクトリ構造規約などを提供する","ko":"프론트엔드 컴포넌트 디자인 규칙은 코드의 재사용성, 캡슐화, 유지보수성을 đảm보하기 위해 단일 책임 원칙, 컴포넌트 분리 규칙, 디렉토리 구조 규칙 등을 제공한다","es":"El diseño de componentes frontend es fundamental para la reutilización y mantenimiento del código. Nuestros principios y reglas de diseño te ayudarán a mejor...","fr":"La conception de composants frontend est essentielle pour la réutilisation et la maintenance du code. Nos principes et règles de conception vous aideront à a...","de":"Das Design von Frontend-Componenten ist entscheidend für die Wiederverwendbarkeit und Wartung des Codes. Unsere Designprinzipien und -regeln helfen Ihnen, di...","pt":"O desenvolvimento de componentes frontend envolve a criação de códigos reutilizáveis e escaláveis.","ru":"Разработка фронтенд-компонентов предполагает создание повторно используемого и масштабируемого кода.","ar":"يتضمن تطوير مكونات واجهة المستخدم الأمامية إنشاء رموز قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام والتحجيم.","en":"一款开箱即用的 AI 智能客服系统，人工客服，客户转化"},"definition":{"en":"一款开箱即用的 AI 智能客服系统，人工客服，客户转化"},"features":{"zh":["单一职责原则","组件拆分规则","目录结构规范","提高代码复用性","提高代码可维护性"],"ja":["シングルレスポンス原則","コンポーネント分割規則","ディレクトリ構造規約","コードの再利用性の向上","コードのメンテナンス性の向上"],"ko":["단일 책임 원칙","컴포넌트 분리 규칙","디렉토리 구조 규칙","코드 재사용성 향상","코드 유지보수성 향상"],"es":["Principio de responsabilidad única","Reglas de división de componentes","Estructura de directorios normalizada","Código mantenible y reutilizable","Mejora de la calidad del código"],"fr":["Principe de responsabilité unique","Règles de division de composants","Structure de répertoires normalisée","Code maintenable et réutilisable","Amélioration de la qualité du code"],"de":["Prinzip der eindeutigen Verantwortung","Regeln für die Aufteilung von Componenten","Normierte Verzeichnisstruktur","Wartbarer und wiederverwendbarer Code","Verbesserung der Codequalität"],"pt":["Princípios de design de componentes","Reutilização de código","Escalabilidade","Separação de preocupações","Manutenção de código"],"ru":["Принципы проектирования компонентов","Повторное использование кода","Масштабируемость","Разделение проблем","Техническое обслуживание кода"],"ar":["مبادئ تصميم المكونات","إعادة استخدام الرمز","القدرة على التحجيم","فصل المشاكل","صيانة الرمز"]},"keywords":{"zh":["前端组件设计","前端开发规范","代码复用性","代码封装性","代码可维护性","单一职责原则","组件拆分规则","目录结构规范"],"ja":["フロントエンドコンポーネント設計","フロントエンド開発規約","コードの再利用性","コードのカプセル化","コードのメンテナンス性","シングルレスポンス原則","コンポーネント分割規則","ディレクトリ構造規約"],"ko":["프론트엔드 컴포넌트 디자인","프론트엔드 개발 규칙","코드 재사용성","코드 캡슐화","코드 유지보수성","단일 책임 원칙","컴포넌트 분리 규칙","디렉토리 구조 규칙"],"es":["diseño de componentes frontend","desarrollo web","reutilización de código","mantenimiento de código","principios de diseño","reglas de diseño","estructura de directorios"],"fr":["conception de composants frontend","développement web","réutilisation de code","maintenance de code","principes de conception","règles de conception","structure de répertoires"],"de":["Frontend-Component-Design","Webentwicklung","Code-Wiederverwendbarkeit","Code-Wartung","Designprinzipien","Designregeln","Verzeichnisstruktur"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de componentes frontend","design de componentes","reutilização de código","escalabilidade","separação de preocupações","manutenção de código","frontend development"],"ru":["разработка фронтенд-компонентов","проектирование компонентов","повторное использование кода","масштабируемость","разделение проблем","техническое обслуживание кода","фронтенд разработка"],"ar":["تطوير مكونات واجهة المستخدم الأمامية","تصميم المكونات","إعادة استخدام الرمز","القدرة على التحجيم","فصل المشاكل","صيانة الرمز","تطوير واجهة المستخدم الأمامية"]}},"owner":"congwa","repo":"embedease-ai","repoPath":"congwa/embedease-ai","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.506Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend-component-design","description":"前端组件设计规范与最佳实践。在编写任何前端代码（React/Next.js 组件、页面、hooks）时自动触发。确保代码复用性、封装性、单一职责原则。触发场景包括创建新的前端组件或页面、重构现有前端代码、添加新功能到前端、任何涉及 frontend 目录的代码修改。此技能始终生效。","bodyPreview":"# 前端组件设计规范\n\n确保前端代码的复用性、封装性和可维护性。\n\n## 核心原则\n\n### 1. 单一职责原则\n- 每个文件只包含一个组件\n- 每个组件只负责一个业务功能\n- 组件代码不超过 **500 行**，超过则拆分\n\n### 2. 组件拆分规则\n\n```\n# 拆分时机判断\nif 组件 > 500 行:\n    拆分为子组件\nif 相同代码出现 >= 2 次:\n    抽取为公共组件\nif 业务逻辑复杂:\n    抽取为 hooks\nif 配置数据多:\n    抽取为配置文件\n```\n\n### 3. 目录结构规范\n\n```\nfrontend/\n├── components/           # 公共组件\n│   ├── ui/              # shadcn 基础组件\n│   └── admin/           # 业务公共组件\n├── app/                 # 页面\n│   └── admin/\n│       └── [feature]/\n│           ├── page.tsx         # 主页面（协调逻辑）\n│","body":"# 前端组件设计规范\n\n确保前端代码的复用性、封装性和可维护性。\n\n## 核心原则\n\n### 1. 单一职责原则\n- 每个文件只包含一个组件\n- 每个组件只负责一个业务功能\n- 组件代码不超过 **500 行**，超过则拆分\n\n### 2. 组件拆分规则\n\n```\n# 拆分时机判断\nif 组件 > 500 行:\n    拆分为子组件\nif 相同代码出现 >= 2 次:\n    抽取为公共组件\nif 业务逻辑复杂:\n    抽取为 hooks\nif 配置数据多:\n    抽取为配置文件\n```\n\n### 3. 目录结构规范\n\n```\nfrontend/\n├── components/           # 公共组件\n│   ├── ui/              # shadcn 基础组件\n│   └── admin/           # 业务公共组件\n├── app/                 # 页面\n│   └── admin/\n│       └── [feature]/\n│           ├── page.tsx         # 主页面（协调逻辑）\n│           └── components/      # 页面私有组件（可选）\n├── lib/\n│   ├── api/             # API 请求函数\n│   ├── config/          # 配置和映射\n│   └── hooks/           # 公共 hooks\n├── hooks/               # 全局 hooks\n└── types/               # 类型定义\n```\n\n### 4. 配置外置原则\n\n将以下内容抽取到 `lib/config/` 目录：\n- **标签映射** → `labels.ts` (英文→中文)\n- **枚举常量** → `constants.ts`\n- **表单配置** → `forms.ts`\n- **主题配置** → `theme.ts`\n\n示例：\n```typescript\n// lib/config/labels.ts\nexport const MIDDLEWARE_LABELS = {\n  MemoryOrchestration: { label: \"记忆编排\", desc: \"...\" },\n  // ...\n};\nexport function getMiddlewareLabel(name: string) {\n  return MIDDLEWARE_LABELS[name] || { label: name, desc: \"\" };\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Hooks 抽取规则\n\n抽取为 hook 的时机：\n- 状态逻辑复杂（>5 个 useState）\n- 数据获取逻辑\n- 副作用逻辑复杂\n- 相同逻辑在多处使用\n\n命名规范：`use[业务名][动作]`\n```typescript\n// lib/hooks/use-agents.ts\nexport function useAgentDetail({ agentId }: { agentId: string }) {\n  const [agent, setAgent] = useState<Agent | null>(null);\n  // ...\n  return { agent, isLoading, error, refresh };\n}\n```\n\n### 6. 导入路径规范\n\n始终使用 `@/` 别名，避免相对路径：\n```typescript\n// ✅ 正确\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\nimport { getAgentEffectiveConfig } from \"@/lib/api/agents\";\n\n// ❌ 错误\nimport { Button } from \"../../components/ui/button\";\n```\n\n## 编码前规划清单\n\n编写前端代码前，必须回答：\n\n1. **组件边界**：这个组件的职责是什么？是否单一？\n2. **复用性**：是否有已存在的类似组件可复用？\n3. **配置外置**：是否有硬编码的中文/配置需要抽取？\n4. **文件大小**：预估代码行数，是否需要拆分？\n5. **命名规范**：组件/文件命名是否清晰表达业务含义？\n\n## 代码审查要点\n\n完成编码后，检查：\n\n- [ ] 单文件不超过 500 行\n- [ ] 无重复代码（相同代码不超过 2 处）\n- [ ] 所有中文标签来自配置文件\n- [ ] 使用 `@/` 路径别名\n- [ ] 组件职责单一\n- [ ] 复杂逻辑已抽取为 hooks\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:05:02.585Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing scalable and maintainable frontend component architecture.","zh":"非常适合需要可扩展和可维护的前端组件架构的全栈代理。","ja":"スケーラブルでメンテナンス可能なフロントエンドコンポーネントアーキテクチャを必要とするフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"확장 가능하고 유지 보수가 가능한 프론트엔드 컴포넌트 아키텍처가 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Full Stack que necesitan una arquitectura de componentes de frontend escalable y mantenible.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack ayant besoin d''une architecture de composants frontend évolutives et maintenables.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die eine skalierbare und wartbare Frontend-Komponenten-Architektur benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que precisam de uma arquitetura de componentes frontend escalável e mantida.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Full Stack, которым необходима масштабируемая и поддерживаемая архитектура компонентов frontend.","ar":"مثالي لوجوهات العميل الكاملة التي تحتاج إلى بنية مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للتمكين والصيانة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design reusable and modular frontend components using single responsibility principle, component splitting rules, and standardized directory structures, ensuring efficient code management and scalability with libraries like React and TypeScript.","zh":"赋予代理设计可重用和模块化的前端组件的能力，使用单一职责原则、组件拆分规则和标准化的目录结构，确保使用React和TypeScript等库的高效代码管理和可扩展性。","ja":"シングルレスポンシビリティプリンシプル、コンポーネント分割ルール、および標準化されたディレクトリ構造を使用して、再利用可能でモジュラーなフロントエンドコンポーネントを設計するエージェントをEmpowerし、ReactおよびTypeScriptなどのライブラリを使用した効率的なコード管理およびスケーラビリティを確保します。","ko":"단일 책임 원칙, 컴포넌트 분할 규칙 및 표준화된 디렉토리 구조를 사용하여 재사용 가능하고 모듈화된 프론트엔드 컴포넌트를 설계할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하여 React 및 TypeScript와 같은 라이브러리를 사용한 효율적인 코드 관리 및 확장성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar componentes de frontend reutilizables y modulares utilizando el principio de responsabilidad única, reglas de división de componentes y estructuras de directorios estandarizadas, lo que garantiza una gestión de código eficiente y escalabilidad con bibliotecas como React y TypeScript.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des composants frontend réutilisables et modulaires en utilisant le principe de responsabilité unique, les règles de division de composants et les structures de répertoires standardisées, garantissant ainsi une gestion de code efficace et une évolutivité avec des bibliothèques comme React et TypeScript.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, wiederverwendbare und modulare Frontend-Komponenten unter Verwendung des Single-Responsibility-Prinzips, Komponenten-Split-Regeln und standardisierter Verzeichnisstrukturen zu entwerfen, was eine effiziente Codeverwaltung und Skalierbarkeit mit Bibliotheken wie React und TypeScript gewährleistet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetarem componentes frontend reutilizáveis e modulares utilizando o princípio da responsabilidade única, regras de divisão de componentes e estruturas de diretório padronizadas, garantindo uma gestão de código eficiente e escalabilidade com bibliotecas como React e TypeScript.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать многократно используемые и модульные компоненты frontend с использованием принципа единой ответственности, правил разделения компонентов и стандартизированных структур директорий, обеспечивая эффективное управление кодом и масштабируемость с библиотеками zoals React и TypeScript.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تصميم مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة لإعادة الاستخدام والمتوافقة باستخدام مبدأ المسؤولية الواحدة وقواعد تقسيم المكونات والهياكل الموجهة المعيارية، مما يضمن إدارة شفرة فعالة وقابلية التوسع باستخدام مكتبات مثل React وTypeScript."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing modular and reusable UI components","Implementing single responsibility principle for better code maintainability","Optimizing component code by splitting large components into smaller ones"],"zh":["设计模块化和可重用的UI组件","实现单一职责原则以提高代码维护性","通过将大型组件分割为较小的组件来优化组件代码"],"ja":["モジュラーで再利用可能なUIコンポーネントを設計する","単一レスポンシビリティプリンシプルを実装してコードのメンテナンス性を向上させる","大きなコンポーネントを小さなコンポーネントに分割してコンポーネントコードを最適化する"],"ko":["모듈화되고 재사용 가능한 UI 컴포넌트를 설계한다","단일 책임 원칙을 구현하여 코드 유지 보수성을 향상시키다","큰 컴포넌트를 작은 컴포넌트로 분할하여 컴포넌트 코드를 최적화한다"],"es":["Diseñar componentes de UI modulares y reutilizables","Implementar el principio de responsabilidad única para una mejor mantenibilidad del código","Optimizar el código de componentes dividiendo componentes grandes en más pequeños"],"fr":["Concevoir des composants UI modulaires et réutilisables","Mettre en œuvre le principe de responsabilité unique pour une meilleure maintenabilité du code","Optimiser le code de composants en divisant les composants importants en plus petits"],"de":["Entwerfen modulare und wiederverwendbare Benutzeroberflächen-Komponenten","Implementieren des Single-Responsibility-Prinzips für eine bessere Wartbarkeit des Codes","Optimieren des Komponenten-Codes, indem große Komponenten in kleinere aufgeteilt werden"],"pt":["Projetar componentes de UI modulares e reutilizáveis","Implementar o princípio da responsabilidade única para uma melhor manutenção de código","Otimizar o código de componentes dividindo componentes grandes em menores"],"ru":["Проектировать модульные и многократно используемые компоненты пользовательского интерфейса","Реализовывать принцип единой ответственности для лучшей поддержки кода","Оптимизировать код компонентов, разделяя большие компоненты на меньшие"],"ar":["تصميم مكونات واجهة المستخدم المتوافقة والقابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","تنفيذ مبدأ المسؤولية الواحدة من أجل صيانة أفضل للشفرة","تحسين شفرة المكونات عن طريق تقسيم المكونات الكبيرة إلى مكونات أصغر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to specific coding standards and directory structures","Component code should not exceed 500 lines for optimal maintainability"],"zh":["需要遵守特定的编码标准和目录结构","组件代码不应超过500行以确保最佳维护性"],"ja":["特定のコーディング規格とディレクトリ構造に従う必要がある","コンポーネントコードはメンテナンス性を確保するために500行を超えてはなりません"],"ko":["특정 코딩 표준 및 디렉토리 구조를 따라야 함","컴포넌트 코드는 유지 보수성을 보장하기 위해 500줄을 초과해서는 안 됨"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a estándares de codificación y estructuras de directorios específicos","El código de componentes no debe exceder los 500 líneas para una mantenibilidad óptima"],"fr":["Nécessite d''adhérer à des normes de codage et des structures de répertoires spécifiques","Le code de composant ne doit pas dépasser 500 lignes pour une maintenabilité optimale"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung spezifischer Codierungsstandards und Verzeichnisstrukturen","Der Komponenten-Code sollte nicht mehr als 500 Zeilen umfassen, um eine optimale Wartbarkeit zu gewährleisten"],"pt":["Exige aderência a padrões de codificação específicos e estruturas de diretório","O código de componente não deve exceder 500 linhas para manutenção ótima"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения определенных стандартов кодирования и структур директорий","Код компонента не должен превышать 500 строк для оптимальной поддержки"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بمعايير الترميز المحددة والهياكل الموجهة","لا ينبغي أن يتجاوز код المكون 500 سطرًا من أجل الصيانة المثلى"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ollieb89/orchestrator/debugging-strategies', 'community', 'ollieb89', 'orchestrator', 'ollieb89/orchestrator', 'debugging-strategies', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.506Z', '2026-02-18T12:05:53.114Z', NULL, '{"id":"ollieb89/orchestrator/debugging-strategies","name":"debugging-strategies","description":{"zh":"调试策略是指将调试从令人沮丧的猜测变为系统化的问题解决","ja":"デバッグ戦略とは、デバッグをフラストレーションを伴う猜測から体系的な問題解決に変えること","ko":"디버깅 전략은 디버깅을 좌절을 동반하는 추측에서 체계적인 문제 해결로 변환하는 것을 말합니다","es":"Estrategias de depuración para transformar la búsqueda de errores en un proceso sistemático y eficiente","fr":"Stratégies de débogage pour transformer la recherche d''erreurs en un processus systématique et efficace","de":"Debugging-Strategien, um die Fehlerbehebung in einen systematischen und effizienten Prozess zu verwandeln","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"调试策略与技巧","ja":"デバッグ戦略とテクニック","ko":"디버깅 전략 및 기술","es":"Estrategias de depuración efectivas","fr":"Stratégies de débogage efficaces","de":"Effektive Debugging-Strategien","en":"debugging-strategies"},"description":{"zh":"调试策略是指将调试从令人沮丧的猜测变为系统化的问题解决","ja":"デバッグ戦略とは、デバッグをフラストレーションを伴う猜測から体系的な問題解決に変えること","ko":"디버깅 전략은 디버깅을 좌절을 동반하는 추측에서 체계적인 문제 해결로 변환하는 것을 말합니다","es":"Estrategias de depuración para transformar la búsqueda de errores en un proceso sistemático y eficiente","fr":"Stratégies de débogage pour transformer la recherche d''erreurs en un processus systématique et efficace","de":"Debugging-Strategien, um die Fehlerbehebung in einen systematischen und effizienten Prozess zu verwandeln","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["系统化的问题解决","强大的调试工具","方法论的调试方法","性能优化","内存泄漏检测"],"ja":["体系的な問題解決","強力なデバッグツール","方法論的なデバッグ方法","パフォーマンス最適化","メモリーリーク検出"],"ko":["체계적인 문제 해결","강력한 디버깅 도구","방법론적인 디버깅 방법","성능 최적화","메모리 누수 검출"],"es":["Identificación de errores elusivos","Análisis de problemas de rendimiento","Depuración de código desconocido","Análisis de volcados de memoria y trazas de pila","Perfilar el rendimiento de la aplicación","Investigar pérdidas de memoria"],"fr":["Identification d''erreurs évasives","Analyse de problèmes de performances","Débogage de code inconnu","Analyse de dumps de mémoire et de traces de pile","Profiler les performances de l''application","Enquêter sur les fuites de mémoire"],"de":["Identifizierung von schwer zu findenden Fehlern","Analyse von Leistungsproblemen","Debugging von unbekanntem Code","Analyse von Speicherausgaben und Stack-Traces","Leistungsbewertung der Anwendung","Ermittlung von Speicherlecks"]},"keywords":{"zh":["调试策略","系统化调试","性能优化","内存泄漏检测","代码调试","程序调试"],"ja":["デバッグ戦略","体系的なデバッグ","パフォーマンス最適化","メモリーリーク検出","コードデバッグ","プログラムデバッグ"],"ko":["디버깅 전략","체계적인 디버깅","성능 최적화","메모리 누수 검출","코드 디버깅","프로그램 디버깅"],"es":["depuración de código","estrategias de depuración","herramientas de depuración","análisis de errores","solución de problemas","optimización de rendimiento"],"fr":["débogage de code","stratégies de débogage","outils de débogage","analyse d''erreurs","résolution de problèmes","optimisation des performances"],"de":["Code-Debugging","Debugging-Strategien","Debugging-Tools","Fehleranalyse","Problembehebung","Leistungsoptimierung"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"orchestrator","repoPath":"ollieb89/orchestrator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.506Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"debugging-strategies","description":"Master systematic debugging techniques, profiling tools, and root cause analysis to efficiently track down bugs across any codebase or technology stack. Use when investigating bugs, performance issues, or unexpected behavior.","bodyPreview":"# Debugging Strategies\n\nTransform debugging from frustrating guesswork into systematic problem-solving with proven strategies, powerful tools, and methodical approaches.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Tracking down elusive bugs\n- Investigating performance issues\n- Understanding unfamiliar codebases\n- Debugging production issues\n- Analyzing crash dumps and stack traces\n- Profiling application performance\n- Investigating memory leaks\n- Debugging distributed systems\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. The S","body":"# Debugging Strategies\n\nTransform debugging from frustrating guesswork into systematic problem-solving with proven strategies, powerful tools, and methodical approaches.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Tracking down elusive bugs\n- Investigating performance issues\n- Understanding unfamiliar codebases\n- Debugging production issues\n- Analyzing crash dumps and stack traces\n- Profiling application performance\n- Investigating memory leaks\n- Debugging distributed systems\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. The Scientific Method\n\n**1. Observe**: What''s the actual behavior?\n**2. Hypothesize**: What could be causing it?\n**3. Experiment**: Test your hypothesis\n**4. Analyze**: Did it prove/disprove your theory?\n**5. Repeat**: Until you find the root cause\n\n### 2. Debugging Mindset\n\n**Don''t Assume:**\n- \"It can''t be X\" - Yes it can\n- \"I didn''t change Y\" - Check anyway\n- \"It works on my machine\" - Find out why\n\n**Do:**\n- Reproduce consistently\n- Isolate the problem\n- Keep detailed notes\n- Question everything\n- Take breaks when stuck\n\n### 3. Rubber Duck Debugging\n\nExplain your code and problem out loud (to a rubber duck, colleague, or yourself). Often reveals the issue.\n\n## Systematic Debugging Process\n\n### Phase 1: Reproduce\n\n```markdown\n## Reproduction Checklist\n\n1. **Can you reproduce it?**\n   - Always? Sometimes? Randomly?\n   - Specific conditions needed?\n   - Can others reproduce it?\n\n2. **Create minimal reproduction**\n   - Simplify to smallest example\n   - Remove unrelated code\n   - Isolate the problem\n\n3. **Document steps**\n   - Write down exact steps\n   - Note environment details\n   - Capture error messages\n```\n\n### Phase 2: Gather Information\n\n```markdown\n## Information Collection\n\n1. **Error Messages**\n   - Full stack trace\n   - Error codes\n   - Console/log output\n\n2. **Environment**\n   - OS version\n   - Language/runtime version\n   - Dependencies versions\n   - Environment variables\n\n3. **Recent Changes**\n   - Git history\n   - Deployment timeline\n   - Configuration changes\n\n4. **Scope**\n   - Affects all users or specific ones?\n   - All browsers or specific ones?\n   - Production only or also dev?\n```\n\n### Phase 3: Form Hypothesis\n\n```markdown\n## Hypothesis Formation\n\nBased on gathered info, ask:\n\n1. **What changed?**\n   - Recent code changes\n   - Dependency updates\n   - Infrastructure changes\n\n2. **What''s different?**\n   - Working vs broken environment\n   - Working vs broken user\n   - Before vs after\n\n3. **Where could this fail?**\n   - Input validation\n   - Business logic\n   - Data layer\n   - External services\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Test & Verify\n\n```markdown\n## Testing Strategies\n\n1. **Binary Search**\n   - Comment out half the code\n   - Narrow down problematic section\n   - Repeat until found\n\n2. **Add Logging**\n   - Strategic console.log/print\n   - Track variable values\n   - Trace execution flow\n\n3. **Isolate Components**\n   - Test each piece separately\n   - Mock dependencies\n   - Remove complexity\n\n4. **Compare Working vs Broken**\n   - Diff configurations\n   - Diff environments\n   - Diff data\n```\n\n## Debugging Tools\n\n### JavaScript/TypeScript Debugging\n\n```typescript\n// Chrome DevTools Debugger\nfunction processOrder(order: Order) {\n    debugger;  // Execution pauses here\n\n    const total = calculateTotal(order);\n    console.log(''Total:'', total);\n\n    // Conditional breakpoint\n    if (order.items.length > 10) {\n        debugger;  // Only breaks if condition true\n    }\n\n    return total;\n}\n\n// Console debugging techniques\nconsole.log(''Value:'', value);                    // Basic\nconsole.table(arrayOfObjects);                   // Table format\nconsole.time(''operation''); /* code */ console.timeEnd(''operation'');  // Timing\nconsole.trace();                                 // Stack trace\nconsole.assert(value > 0, ''Value must be positive'');  // Assertion\n\n// Performance profiling\nperformance.mark(''start-operation'');\n// ... operation code\nperformance.mark(''end-operation'');\nperformance.measure(''operation'', ''start-operation'', ''end-operation'');\nconsole.log(performance.getEntriesByType(''measure''));\n```\n\n**VS Code Debugger Configuration:**\n```json\n// .vscode/launch.json\n{\n    \"version\": \"0.2.0\",\n    \"configurations\": [\n        {\n            \"type\": \"node\",\n            \"request\": \"launch\",\n            \"name\": \"Debug Program\",\n            \"program\": \"${workspaceFolder}/src/index.ts\",\n            \"preLaunchTask\": \"tsc: build - tsconfig.json\",\n            \"outFiles\": [\"${workspaceFolder}/dist/**/*.js\"],\n            \"skipFiles\": [\"<node_internals>/**\"]\n        },\n        {\n            \"type\": \"node\",\n            \"request\": \"launch\",\n            \"name\": \"Debug Tests\",\n            \"program\": \"${workspaceFolder}/node_modules/jest/bin/jest\",\n            \"args\": [\"--runInBand\", \"--no-cache\"],\n            \"console\": \"integratedTerminal\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n### Python Debugging\n\n```python\n# Built-in debugger (pdb)\nimport pdb\n\ndef calculate_total(items):\n    total = 0\n    pdb.set_trace()  # Debugger starts here\n\n    for item in items:\n        total += item.price * item.quantity\n\n    return total\n\n# Breakpoint (Python 3.7+)\ndef process_order(order):\n    breakpoint()  # More convenient than pdb.set_trace()\n    # ... code\n\n# Post-mortem debugging\ntry:\n    risky_operation()\nexcept Exception:\n    import pdb\n    pdb.post_mortem()  # Debug at exception point\n\n# IPython debugging (ipdb)\nfrom ipdb import set_trace\nset_trace()  # Better interface than pdb\n\n# Logging for debugging\nimport logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef fetch_user(user_id):\n    logger.debug(f''Fetching user: {user_id}'')\n    user = db.query(User).get(user_id)\n    logger.debug(f''Found user: {user}'')\n    return user\n\n# Profile performance\nimport cProfile\nimport pstats\n\ncProfile.run(''slow_function()'', ''profile_stats'')\nstats = pstats.Stats(''profile_stats'')\nstats.sort_stats(''cumulative'')\nstats.print_stats(10)  # Top 10 slowest\n```\n\n### Go Debugging\n\n```go\n// Delve debugger\n// Install: go install github.com/go-delve/delve/cmd/dlv@latest\n// Run: dlv debug main.go\n\nimport (\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"runtime\"\n    \"runtime/debug\"\n)\n\n// Print stack trace\nfunc debugStack() {\n    debug.PrintStack()\n}\n\n// Panic recovery with debugging\nfunc processRequest() {\n    defer func() {\n        if r := recover(); r != nil {\n            fmt.Println(\"Panic:\", r)\n            debug.PrintStack()\n        }\n    }()\n\n    // ... code that might panic\n}\n\n// Memory profiling\nimport _ \"net/http/pprof\"\n// Visit http://localhost:6060/debug/pprof/\n\n// CPU profiling\nimport (\n    \"os\"\n    \"runtime/pprof\"\n)\n\nf, _ := os.Create(\"cpu.prof\")\npprof.StartCPUProfile(f)\ndefer pprof.StopCPUProfile()\n// ... code to profile\n```\n\n## Advanced Debugging Techniques\n\n### Technique 1: Binary Search Debugging\n\n```bash\n# Git bisect for finding regression\ngit bisect start\ngit bisect bad                    # Current commit is bad\ngit bisect good v1.0.0            # v1.0.0 was good\n\n# Git checks out middle commit\n# Test it, then:\ngit bisect good   # if it works\ngit bisect bad    # if it''s broken\n\n# Continue until bug found\ngit bisect reset  # when done\n```\n\n### Technique 2: Differential Debugging\n\nCompare working vs broken:\n\n```markdown\n## What''s Different?\n\n| Aspect       | Working         | Broken          |\n|--------------|-----------------|-----------------|\n| Environment  | Development     | Production      |\n| Node version | 18.16.0         | 18.15.0         |\n| Data         | Empty DB        | 1M records      |\n| User         | Admin           | Regular user    |\n| Browser      | Chrome          | Safari          |\n| Time         | During day      | After midnight  |\n\nHypothesis: Time-based issue? Check timezone handling.\n```\n\n### Technique 3: Trace Debugging\n\n```typescript\n// Function call tracing\nfunction trace(target: any, propertyKey: string, descriptor: PropertyDescriptor) {\n    const originalMethod = descriptor.value;\n\n    descriptor.value = function(...args: any[]) {\n        console.log(`Calling ${propertyKey} with args:`, args);\n        const result = originalMethod.apply(this, args);\n        console.log(`${propertyKey} returned:`, result);\n        return result;\n    };\n\n    return descriptor;\n}\n\nclass OrderService {\n    @trace\n    calculateTotal(items: Item[]): number {\n        return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Technique 4: Memory Leak Detection\n\n```typescript\n// Chrome DevTools Memory Profiler\n// 1. Take heap snapshot\n// 2. Perform action\n// 3. Take another snapshot\n// 4. Compare snapshots\n\n// Node.js memory debugging\nif (process.memoryUsage().heapUsed > 500 * 1024 * 1024) {\n    console.warn(''High memory usage:'', process.memoryUsage());\n\n    // Generate heap dump\n    require(''v8'').writeHeapSnapshot();\n}\n\n// Find memory leaks in tests\nlet beforeMemory: number;\n\nbeforeEach(() => {\n    beforeMemory = process.memoryUsage().heapUsed;\n});\n\nafterEach(() => {\n    const afterMemory = process.memoryUsage().heapUsed;\n    const diff = afterMemory - beforeMemory;\n\n    if (diff > 10 * 1024 * 1024) {  // 10MB threshold\n        console.warn(`Possible memory leak: ${diff / 1024 / 1024}MB`);\n    }\n});\n```\n\n## Debugging Patterns by Issue Type\n\n### Pattern 1: Intermittent Bugs\n\n```markdown\n## Strategies for Flaky Bugs\n\n1. **Add extensive logging**\n   - Log timing information\n   - Log all state transitions\n   - Log external interactions\n\n2. **Look for race conditions**\n   - Concurrent access to shared state\n   - Async operations completing out of order\n   - Missing synchronization\n\n3. **Check timing dependencies**\n   - setTimeout/setInterval\n   - Promise resolution order\n   - Animation frame timing\n\n4. **Stress test**\n   - Run many times\n   - Vary timing\n   - Simulate load\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Performance Issues\n\n```markdown\n## Performance Debugging\n\n1. **Profile first**\n   - Don''t optimize blindly\n   - Measure before and after\n   - Find bottlenecks\n\n2. **Common culprits**\n   - N+1 queries\n   - Unnecessary re-renders\n   - Large data processing\n   - Synchronous I/O\n\n3. **Tools**\n   - Browser DevTools Performance tab\n   - Lighthouse\n   - Python: cProfile, line_profiler\n   - Node: clinic.js, 0x\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Production Bugs\n\n```markdown\n## Production Debugging\n\n1. **Gather evidence**\n   - Error tracking (Sentry, Bugsnag)\n   - Application logs\n   - User reports\n   - Metrics/monitoring\n\n2. **Reproduce locally**\n   - Use production data (anonymized)\n   - Match environment\n   - Follow exact steps\n\n3. **Safe investigation**\n   - Don''t change production\n   - Use feature flags\n   - Add monitoring/logging\n   - Test fixes in staging\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Reproduce First**: Can''t fix what you can''t reproduce\n2. **Isolate the Problem**: Remove complexity until minimal case\n3. **Read Error Messages**: They''re usually helpful\n4. **Check Recent Changes**: Most bugs are recent\n5. **Use Version Control**: Git bisect, blame, history\n6. **Take Breaks**: Fresh eyes see better\n7. **Document Findings**: Help future you\n8. **Fix Root Cause**: Not just symptoms\n\n## Common Debugging Mistakes\n\n- **Making Multiple Changes**: Change one thing at a time\n- **Not Reading Error Messages**: Read the full stack trace\n- **Assuming It''s Complex**: Often it''s simple\n- **Debug Logging in Prod**: Remove before shipping\n- **Not Using Debugger**: console.log isn''t always best\n- **Giving Up Too Soon**: Persistence pays off\n- **Not Testing the Fix**: Verify it actually works\n\n## Quick Debugging Checklist\n\n```markdown\n## When Stuck, Check:\n\n- [ ] Spelling errors (typos in variable names)\n- [ ] Case sensitivity (fileName vs filename)\n- [ ] Null/undefined values\n- [ ] Array index off-by-one\n- [ ] Async timing (race conditions)\n- [ ] Scope issues (closure, hoisting)\n- [ ] Type mismatches\n- [ ] Missing dependencies\n- [ ] Environment variables\n- [ ] File paths (absolute vs relative)\n- [ ] Cache issues (clear cache)\n- [ ] Stale data (refresh database)\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/debugging-tools-guide.md**: Comprehensive tool documentation\n- **references/performance-profiling.md**: Performance debugging guide\n- **references/production-debugging.md**: Debugging live systems\n- **assets/debugging-checklist.md**: Quick reference checklist\n- **assets/common-bugs.md**: Common bug patterns\n- **scripts/debug-helper.ts**: Debugging utility functions\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:05:53.114Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing systematic debugging capabilities for tracking down elusive bugs and investigating performance issues","zh":"非常适合需要系统化调试能力以追踪难以发现的错误并调查性能问题的代码分析智能体","ja":"捉えにくいバグの追跡やパフォーマンス問題の調査のために体系的なデバッグ機能を必要とするコード分析エージェントに最適","ko":"파악하기 어려운 버그를 추적하고 성능 문제를 조사하기 위해 체계적인 디버깅 기능이 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de código que necesitan capacidades de depuración sistemática para rastrear errores elusivos e investigar problemas de rendimiento","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de code ayant besoin de capacités de débogage systématiques pour traquer les bogues insidieux et enquêter sur les problèmes de performance","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agents, die systematische Debugging-Fähigkeiten zur Nachverfolgung von schwer fassbaren Fehlern und zur Untersuchung von Leistungsproblemen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que necessitam de capacidades de depuração sistemática para rastrear bugs difíceis de encontrar e investigar problemas de desempenho","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа кода, которым требуются системные возможности отладки для отслеживания неуловимых ошибок и расследования проблем производительности","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات فحص منهجية لتعقب الأخطاء الخفية وتحقيق مشاكل الأداء"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform debugging into systematic problem-solving using proven strategies, powerful tools, and methodical approaches, including analyzing crash dumps and stack traces, profiling application performance, and investigating memory leaks","zh":"使智能体能够利用经过验证的策略、强大工具和系统方法将调试转化为系统化问题解决，包括分析崩溃转储和堆栈跟踪、分析应用程序性能以及调查内存泄漏","ja":"実証済みの戦略、強力なツール、体系的なアプローチ（クラッシュダンプやスタックトレースの分析、アプリケーションパフォーマンスのプロファイリング、メモリリークの調査など）を使用して、デバッグを体系的な問題解決に変えることをエージェントに可能にする","ko":"입증된 전략, 강력한 도구 및 체계적인 접근법(크래시 덤프 및 스택 트레이스 분석, 애플리케이션 성능 프로파일링, 메모리 누수 조사 포함)을 사용하여 디버깅을 체계적인 문제 해결로 전환하는 것을 에이전트에 부여함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar la depuración en resolución sistemática de problemas utilizando estrategias probadas, herramientas poderosas y enfoques metódicos, incluyendo el análisis de volcados de memoria y seguimientos de pila, la creación de perfiles de rendimiento de aplicaciones y la investigación de fugas de memoria","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer le débogage en résolution systématique de problèmes en utilisant des stratégies éprouvées, des outils puissants et des approches méthodiques, notamment l''analyse des dumps de crash et des traces de pile, le profilage des performances des applications et l''enquête sur les fuites de mémoire","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, das Debugging in eine systematische Problemlösung umzuwandeln, indem sie bew