,"fr":"Modèle de frontend avec Vite, GraphQL et Typescript","de":"Frontend-Boilerplate mit Vite, GraphQL und Typescript","pt":"Boilerplate Vite + GraphQL + Typescript","ru":"Шаблон Vite + GraphQL + Typescript","ar":"قالب بدئي Vite + GraphQL + Typescript","en":"openspec-continue-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change是一个Vite + GraphQL + Typescript前端开发模板，采用Feature-Sliced Design作为项目架构方法","ja":"openspec-continue-changeはVite + GraphQL + Typescriptフロントエンドボイラープレートで、Feature-Sliced Designをプロジェクトアーキテクチャ方法として採用","ko":"openspec-continue-change는 Vite + GraphQL + Typescript 프론트엔드 개발 보일러플레이트로 Feature-Sliced Design를 프로젝트 아키텍처 방법으로 사용","es":"Nuestra plantilla de frontend utiliza Vite, GraphQL y Typescript, con una arquitectura de diseño basada en Feature-Sliced Design","fr":"Notre modèle de frontend utilise Vite, GraphQL et Typescript, avec une architecture de conception basée sur Feature-Sliced Design","de":"Unser Frontend-Boilerplate verwendet Vite, GraphQL und Typescript, mit einer Architektur basierend auf Feature-Sliced Design","pt":"O boilerplate openspec-continue-change é uma solução de frontend que combina Vite, GraphQL e Typescript com Feature-Sliced Design","ru":"Шаблон openspec-continue-change является решением для frontend, сочетающим Vite, GraphQL и Typescript с Feature-Sliced Design","ar":"قالب openspec-continue-change هو حل لمشاريع frontend يجمع بين Vite و GraphQL و Typescript مع Feature-Sliced Design","en":"A Vite + GraphQL + Typescript frontend boilerplate using Feature-Sliced Design as project architecture methodology"},"definition":{"en":"A Vite + GraphQL + Typescript frontend boilerplate using Feature-Sliced Design as project architecture methodology"},"features":{"zh":["Vite + GraphQL + Typescript","Feature-Sliced Design项目架构","快速创建下一个工件","支持多种开发环境","高效的开发流程"],"ja":["Vite + GraphQL + Typescript","Feature-Sliced Designプロジェクトアーキテクチャ","次のアーティファクトの迅速な作成","複数の開発環境のサポート","効率的な開発フロー"],"ko":["Vite + GraphQL + Typescript","Feature-Sliced Design 프로젝트 아키텍처","다음 아티팩트의 빠른 생성","다양한 개발 환경 지원","효율적인 개발 프로세스"],"es":["Plantilla de frontend con Vite","Integración con GraphQL","Soporte para Typescript","Arquitectura de diseño basada en Feature-Sliced Design","Escalabilidad y mantenibilidad"],"fr":["Modèle de frontend avec Vite","Intégration avec GraphQL","Prise en charge de Typescript","Architecture de conception basée sur Feature-Sliced Design","Évolutivité et maintenabilité"],"de":["Frontend-Boilerplate mit Vite","Integration mit GraphQL","Unterstützung für Typescript","Architektur basierend auf Feature-Sliced Design","Skalierbarkeit und Wartbarkeit"],"pt":["Vite como ferramenta de build","GraphQL para gerenciamento de dados","Typescript para tipagem estática","Feature-Sliced Design como metodologia de arquitetura","Suporte a criação de artefatos","Integração com o tool AskUserQuestion"],"ru":["Vite в качестве инструмента сборки","GraphQL для управления данными","Typescript для статической типизации","Feature-Sliced Design в качестве методологии архитектуры","Поддержка создания артефактов","Интеграция с инструментом AskUserQuestion"],"ar":["Vite كأداة بناء","GraphQL لإدارة البيانات","Typescript للتحقق من الأنواع الثابتة","Feature-Sliced Design ك منهجية لتصميم الهندسة المعمارية","دعم إنشاء الملفات","التكامل مع أداة AskUserQuestion"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Vite","GraphQL","Typescript","前端开发","Feature-Sliced Design","快速开发","高效开发"],"ja":["Vite","GraphQL","Typescript","フロントエンド開発","Feature-Sliced Design","迅速な開発","効率的な開発"],"ko":["Vite","GraphQL","Typescript","프론트엔드 개발","Feature-Sliced Design","빠른 개발","효율적인 개발"],"es":["plantilla de frontend","Vite","GraphQL","Typescript","Feature-Sliced Design","desarrollo de aplicaciones","escalabilidad","mantenimiento"],"fr":["modèle de frontend","Vite","GraphQL","Typescript","Feature-Sliced Design","développement d''applications","évolutivité","maintenabilité"],"de":["Frontend-Boilerplate","Vite","GraphQL","Typescript","Feature-Sliced Design","Anwendungsentwicklung","Skalierbarkeit","Wartbarkeit"],"pt":["Vite","GraphQL","Typescript","Feature-Sliced Design","boilerplate frontend","desenvolvimento frontend","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","metodologias de arquitetura","gerenciamento de dados"],"ru":["Vite","GraphQL","Typescript","Feature-Sliced Design","шаблон frontend","разработка frontend","инструменты разработки","методологии архитектуры","управление данными"],"ar":["Vite","GraphQL","Typescript","Feature-Sliced Design","قالب بدئي لمشاريع frontend","تطوير frontend","أدوات التطوير","منهجيات تصميم الهندسة المعمارية","إدارة البيانات"]}},"owner":"uxname","repo":"litefront","repoPath":"uxname/litefront","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.507Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-continue-change","description":"Continue working on an OpenSpec change by creating the next artifact. Use when the user wants to progress their change, create the next artifact, or continue their workflow.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-","body":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-4 most recently modified changes as options, showing:\n   - Change name\n   - Schema (from `schema` field if present, otherwise \"spec-driven\")\n   - Status (e.g., \"0/5 tasks\", \"complete\", \"no tasks\")\n   - How recently it was modified (from `lastModified` field)\n\n   Mark the most recently modified change as \"(Recommended)\" since it''s likely what the user wants to continue.\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check current status**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand current state. The response includes:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow schema being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - `artifacts`: Array of artifacts with their status (\"done\", \"ready\", \"blocked\")\n   - `isComplete`: Boolean indicating if all artifacts are complete\n\n3. **Act based on status**:\n\n   ---\n\n   **If all artifacts are complete (`isComplete: true`)**:\n   - Congratulate the user\n   - Show final status including the schema used\n   - Suggest: \"All artifacts created! You can now implement this change or archive it.\"\n   - STOP\n\n   ---\n\n   **If artifacts are ready to create** (status shows artifacts with `status: \"ready\"`):\n   - Pick the FIRST artifact with `status: \"ready\"` from the status output\n   - Get its instructions:\n     ```bash\n     openspec instructions <artifact-id> --change \"<name>\" --json\n     ```\n   - Parse the JSON. The key fields are:\n     - `context`: Project background (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `rules`: Artifact-specific rules (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `template`: The structure to use for your output file\n     - `instruction`: Schema-specific guidance\n     - `outputPath`: Where to write the artifact\n     - `dependencies`: Completed artifacts to read for context\n   - **Create the artifact file**:\n     - Read any completed dependency files for context\n     - Use `template` as the structure - fill in its sections\n     - Apply `context` and `rules` as constraints when writing - but do NOT copy them into the file\n     - Write to the output path specified in instructions\n   - Show what was created and what''s now unlocked\n   - STOP after creating ONE artifact\n\n   ---\n\n   **If no artifacts are ready (all blocked)**:\n   - This shouldn''t happen with a valid schema\n   - Show status and suggest checking for issues\n\n4. **After creating an artifact, show progress**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n\n**Output**\n\nAfter each invocation, show:\n- Which artifact was created\n- Schema workflow being used\n- Current progress (N/M complete)\n- What artifacts are now unlocked\n- Prompt: \"Want to continue? Just ask me to continue or tell me what to do next.\"\n\n**Artifact Creation Guidelines**\n\nThe artifact types and their purpose depend on the schema. Use the `instruction` field from the instructions output to understand what to create.\n\nCommon artifact patterns:\n\n**spec-driven schema** (proposal → specs → design → tasks):\n- **proposal.md**: Ask user about the change if not clear. Fill in Why, What Changes, Capabilities, Impact.\n  - The Capabilities section is critical - each capability listed will need a spec file.\n- **specs/<capability>/spec.md**: Create one spec per capability listed in the proposal''s Capabilities section (use the capability name, not the change name).\n- **design.md**: Document technical decisions, architecture, and implementation approach.\n- **tasks.md**: Break down implementation into checkboxed tasks.\n\nFor other schemas, follow the `instruction` field from the CLI output.\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Create ONE artifact per invocation\n- Always read dependency artifacts before creating a new one\n- Never skip artifacts or create out of order\n- If context is unclear, ask the user before creating\n- Verify the artifact file exists after writing before marking progress\n- Use the schema''s artifact sequence, don''t assume specific artifact names\n- **IMPORTANT**: `context` and `rules` are constraints for YOU, not content for the file\n  - Do NOT copy `<context>`, `<rules>`, `<project_context>` blocks into the artifact\n  - These guide what you write, but should never appear in the output\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:11:34.235Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Development Agents requiring streamlined project architecture and efficient change management using Vite, GraphQL, and Typescript","zh":"适用于需要简化项目架构和使用 Vite、GraphQL 和 Typescript 进行高效变更管理的前端开发代理","ja":"Vite、GraphQL、TypeScriptを使用してプロジェクトアーキテクチャを簡素化し、変更管理を効率化するフロントエンド開発エージェントに最適","ko":"Vite, GraphQL, TypeScript를 사용하여 프로젝트 아키텍처를 간소화하고 변경 관리를 효율적으로 수행하는 프론트엔드 개발 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo frontend que requieren una arquitectura de proyecto optimizada y un cambio de gestión eficiente utilizando Vite, GraphQL y Typescript","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement frontend nécessitant une architecture de projet rationalisée et une gestion de changement efficace utilisant Vite, GraphQL et Typescript","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine optimierte Projektarchitektur und ein effizientes Änderungsmanagement mit Vite, GraphQL und Typescript erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Frontend que exigem arquitetura de projeto simplificada e gerenciamento de alterações eficiente usando Vite, GraphQL e Typescript","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки фронтенда, требующих оптимизированной архитектуры проекта и эффективного управления изменениями с помощью Vite, GraphQL и Typescript","ar":"مثالي لعميلاء تطوير الواجهة الأمامية الذين يتطلبون هيكلة مشروع مبسطة وإدارة تغييرات فعالة باستخدام Vite و GraphQL و Typescript"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to seamlessly continue working on changes by leveraging Feature-Sliced Design, utilizing `openspec list --json` for retrieving available changes, and integrating the AskUserQuestion tool for user selection, all while managing project complexity with GraphQL and Typescript","zh":"使代理能够通过利用特性分片设计、使用 `openspec list --json` 检索可用更改并集成 AskUserQuestion 工具进行用户选择来无缝地继续处理更改，同时使用 GraphQL 和 TypeScript 管理项目复杂性","ja":"Feature-Sliced Designを利用し、`openspec list --json`で利用可能な変更を取得し、AskUserQuestionツールを使用してユーザー選択を実施し、GraphQLとTypeScriptを使用してプロジェクトの複雑さを管理することで、エージェントが変更を無停滞で継続して作業できるようにする","ko":"기능 분할 설계를 활용하고 `openspec list --json`을 사용하여 사용 가능한 변경 사항을 검색하며 AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자 선택을 통합하여 변경 사항을 처리할 수 있게 하며,同時に GraphQL 및 TypeScript를 사용하여 프로젝트 복잡성을 관리","es":"Permite a los agentes seguir trabajando en los cambios de manera fluida mediante el uso de Feature-Sliced Design, utilizando `openspec list --json` para recuperar los cambios disponibles y integrando la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la selección del usuario, todo mientras se gestiona la complejidad del proyecto con GraphQL y Typescript","fr":"Permet aux agents de continuer à travailler sur les changements de manière fluide en exploitant Feature-Sliced Design, en utilisant `openspec list --json` pour récupérer les changements disponibles et en intégrant l''outil AskUserQuestion pour la sélection de l''utilisateur, le tout en gérant la complexité du projet avec GraphQL et Typescript","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, nahtlos an den Änderungen weiterzuarbeiten, indem Feature-Sliced Design genutzt wird, `openspec list --json` für die Abrufung der verfügbaren Änderungen verwendet wird und das Tool AskUserQuestion für die Benutzerauswahl integriert wird, während die Projektkomplexität mit GraphQL und Typescript gemanagt wird","pt":"Permite que os agentes continuem trabalhando em alterações de forma sem interrupções, aproveitando o Design por Fatias de Recursos, utilizando `openspec list --json` para recuperar alterações disponíveis e integrando a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para seleção de usuário, tudo isso enquanto gerencia a complexidade do projeto com GraphQL e Typescript","ru":"Позволяет агентам беспрепятственно продолжать работу над изменениями, используя дизайн, разбитый на фичи, используя `openspec list --json` для получения доступных изменений и интегрируя инструмент AskUserQuestion для выбора пользователя, все это при управлении сложностью проекта с помощью GraphQL и Typescript","ar":"يسمح للعميلاء الاستمرار في العمل على التغييرات دون انقطاع، من خلال استخدام تصميم مقطع حسب الميزة، واستخدام `openspec list --json` لاسترجاع التغييرات المتاحة وتكامل أداة AskUserQuestion للتحديد المستخدم، مع إدارة تعقيد المشروع باستخدام GraphQL و Typescript"},"useCases":{"en":["Continuing development on recently modified changes with ease","Efficiently managing multiple changes through the `openspec list` command","Streamlining project architecture with Feature-Sliced Design methodology"],"zh":["轻松继续开发最近修改的更改","通过 `openspec list` 命令高效地管理多个更改","使用特性分片设计方法简化项目架构"],"ja":["最近変更された変更を容易に継続して開発","`openspec list`コマンドを使用して複数の変更を効率的に管理","Feature-Sliced Design方法を使用してプロジェクトアーキテクチャを簡素化"],"ko":["최근 수정된 변경 사항을 쉽게 계속 개발","`openspec list` 명령을 사용하여 여러 변경 사항을 효율적으로 관리","기능 분할 설계 방법을 사용하여 프로젝트 아키텍처를 간소화"],"es":["Seguir desarrollando con facilidad los cambios modificados recientemente","Gestionar de manera eficiente múltiples cambios a través del comando `openspec list`","Optimizar la arquitectura del proyecto con la metodología Feature-Sliced Design"],"fr":["Poursuivre le développement des changements modifiés récemment avec facilité","Gérer de manière efficace plusieurs changements via la commande `openspec list`","Rationaliser l''architecture du projet avec la méthodologie Feature-Sliced Design"],"de":["Weiterentwicklung der kürzlich geänderten Änderungen mit Leichtigkeit","Effizientes Management mehrerer Änderungen über den Befehl `openspec list`","Optimierung der Projektarchitektur mit der Feature-Sliced Design-Methode"],"pt":["Continuar desenvolvimento em alterações recentemente modificadas com facilidade","Gerenciar alterações múltiplas de forma eficiente por meio do comando `openspec list`","Simplificar a arquitetura do projeto com a metodologia de Design por Fatias de Recursos"],"ru":["Продолжать разработку недавно измененных изменений с легкостью","Эффективно управлять несколькими изменениями с помощью команды `openspec list`","Упрощать архитектуру проекта с помощью методологии дизайна, разбитого на фичи"],"ar":["الاستمرار في التطوير على التغييرات المعدلة حديثًا بسهولة","إدارة التغييرات المتعددة بفعالية من خلال الأمر `openspec list`","تبسيط هيكلة المشروع باستخدام منهجية تصميم مقطع حسب الميزة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Vite and GraphQL setup","Dependent on Typescript for project development","Needs user input for change selection when not specified"],"zh":["需要 Vite 和 GraphQL 设置","依赖于 TypeScript 进行项目开发","当未指定时需要用户输入来选择更改"],"ja":["ViteとGraphQLの設定が必要","プロジェクト開発にTypeScriptに依存","指定されていない場合は変更の選択にユーザー入力が必要"],"ko":["Vite 및 GraphQL 설정이 필요","프로젝트 개발에 TypeScript에 의존","지정되지 않은 경우 변경 선택에 사용자 입력이 필요"],"es":["Requiere configuración de Vite y GraphQL","Depende de Typescript para el desarrollo del proyecto","Necesita la entrada del usuario para la selección de cambios cuando no se especifica"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de Vite et GraphQL","Dépend de Typescript pour le développement du projet","Nécessite une entrée de l''utilisateur pour la sélection des changements lorsqu''elle n''est pas spécifiée"],"de":["Benötigt Vite- und GraphQL-Setup","Hängt von Typescript für die Projektentwicklung ab","Benötigt Benutzereingabe für die Änderungsauswahl, wenn nicht angegeben"],"pt":["Exige configuração do Vite e GraphQL","Depende do Typescript para desenvolvimento do projeto","Necessita de entrada do usuário para seleção de alterações quando não especificado"],"ru":["Требует настройки Vite и GraphQL","Зависит от Typescript для разработки проекта","Требует ввода пользователя для выбора изменений, когда не указано"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد Vite و GraphQL","يعتمد على Typescript من أجل تطوير المشروع","يحتاج إلى إدخال المستخدم لتحديد التغييرات عندما لم يتم تحديدها"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
