래","RWA 자산","암호화폐","주식","지수","레버리지 거래"],"es":["futuros sintéticos","protocolo de futuros","trading con apalancamiento","activos RWA","criptomonedas","acciones","índices","desarrollo de monorepo"],"fr":["futures synthétiques","protocole de futures","trading avec effet de levier","actifs RWA","crypto-monnaies","actions","indices","développement de monorepo"],"de":["synthetische Futures","Futures-Protokoll","Trading mit Hebelwirkung","RWA-Vermögenswerte","Kryptowährungen","Aktien","Indizes","Monorepo-Entwicklung"],"pt":["arquitetura de protocolo de futuros sintéticos","ativos RWA","criptomoedas","ações","índices","alavancagem","cofre de liquidez centralizado","preços combinados"],"ru":["архитектура синтетического перпетуального фьючерсного протокола","активы RWA","криптовалюты","акции","индексы","леверидж","централизованный ликвидный кошелек","цены, объединенные"],"ar":["هندسة بروتوكول المستقبلات الاصطناعية الدائمة","الأصول RWA","العملات المشفرة","الأسهم","المؤشرات","مضاعف","خزنة سيولة مركزية","أسعار مجتمعة"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"architecture","description":"Monorepo architecture and code organization. Use when understanding project structure, package relationships, import rules, or component organization. Triggers on architecture, structure, packages, imports, hierarchy, dependencies, monorepo, organization.","bodyPreview":"# Monorepo Architecture Overview\n\n## Platform Structure (Example)\n- **`apps/desktop/`** - Electron desktop app (Windows, macOS, Linux)\n- **`apps/mobile/`** - React Native mobile app (iOS, Android)\n- **`apps/ext/`** - Browser extension (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Brave)\n- **`apps/web/`** - Progressive web application\n- **`apps/web-embed/`** - Embeddable components\n\n## Core Packages (Example)\n- **`packages/core/`** - Core business logic, cryptography, protocol implementations\n- **`packages/kit/`** - A","body":"# Monorepo Architecture Overview\n\n## Platform Structure (Example)\n- **`apps/desktop/`** - Electron desktop app (Windows, macOS, Linux)\n- **`apps/mobile/`** - React Native mobile app (iOS, Android)\n- **`apps/ext/`** - Browser extension (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Brave)\n- **`apps/web/`** - Progressive web application\n- **`apps/web-embed/`** - Embeddable components\n\n## Core Packages (Example)\n- **`packages/core/`** - Core business logic, cryptography, protocol implementations\n- **`packages/kit/`** - Application logic, state management, API integrations\n- **`packages/kit-bg/`** - Background services and workers\n- **`packages/components/`** - Cross-platform UI components\n- **`packages/shared/`** - Platform abstractions, utilities, build configurations\n\n## Key Architectural Patterns\n- **Cross-platform UI**: Universal components with platform-specific adaptations\n- **Platform-specific files**: Use `.native.ts`, `.desktop.ts`, `.web.ts`, `.ext.ts` suffixes\n- **State management**: Atomic state management (e.g., Jotai, Zustand)\n- **Package isolation**: Clear boundaries between packages\n\n## Code Organization\n\n### File Naming Conventions\n- Platform-specific implementations use suffixes: `.native.ts`, `.web.ts`, `.desktop.ts`, `.ext.ts`\n- Component files use PascalCase: `ComponentName.tsx`\n- Hook files use camelCase with `use` prefix: `useHookName.ts`\n- Utility files use camelCase: `utilityName.ts`\n\n### Import Patterns\n- Use workspace references: `@{scope}/components`, `@{scope}/core`, `@{scope}/kit`\n- Platform detection via shared utilities\n- Conditional imports based on platform capabilities\n\n### Import Hierarchy Rules - STRICTLY ENFORCED\n\n**CRITICAL**: Violating these rules WILL break the build and cause circular dependencies.\n\n**HIERARCHY (NEVER violate this order):**\n- `@{scope}/shared` - **FORBIDDEN** to import from any other internal packages\n- `@{scope}/components` - **ONLY** allowed to import from `shared`\n- `@{scope}/kit-bg` - **ONLY** allowed to import from `shared` and `core` (NEVER `components` or `kit`)\n- `@{scope}/kit` - Can import from `shared`, `components`, and `kit-bg`\n- Apps (desktop/mobile/ext/web) - Can import from all packages\n\n**BEFORE ADDING ANY IMPORT:**\n1. Verify the import respects the hierarchy above\n2. Check if the import creates a circular dependency\n3. Run type check to validate no circular dependency introduced\n4. If unsure, find an alternative approach that respects the hierarchy\n\n**COMMON VIOLATIONS TO AVOID:**\n- ❌ Importing from `kit` in `components`\n- ❌ Importing from `components` in `kit-bg`\n- ❌ Importing from `kit` in `core`\n- ❌ Any \"upward\" imports in the hierarchy\n\n### Component Structure\n- UI components in `packages/components/src/`\n- Business logic in `packages/kit/src/`\n- Domain-specific code in `packages/core/src/`\n\n## Deep Analysis & Architecture Consistency Framework\n\n### Pre-Modification Analysis Protocol\n\n**MANDATORY ANALYSIS STEPS** (Execute BEFORE any code changes):\n\n1. **Scope Impact Assessment**\n   - Identify ALL packages/apps affected by the change\n   - Map dependencies that will be impacted (use `yarn why <package>` if needed)\n   - Evaluate cross-platform implications (desktop/mobile/web/extension)\n   - Assess backward compatibility requirements\n\n2. **Pattern Consistency Verification**\n   - Examine existing similar implementations in the codebase\n   - Identify established patterns and conventions used\n   - Verify new code follows identical patterns\n   - Check naming conventions align with existing code\n\n3. **Architecture Integrity Check**\n   - Validate against monorepo import hierarchy rules\n   - Ensure separation of concerns is maintained\n   - Verify platform-specific code uses correct file extensions\n   - Check that business logic stays in appropriate packages\n\n4. **Performance Impact Evaluation**\n   - Consider bundle size implications (especially for web/extension)\n   - Evaluate runtime performance effects\n   - Assess memory usage implications\n   - Consider impact on application startup time\n\n### Code Pattern Recognition Framework\n\n**WHEN ADDING NEW FUNCTIONALITY:**\n1. **Find Similar Examples**: Search codebase for similar implementations\n2. **Extract Patterns**: Identify common approaches, naming, structure\n3. **Follow Conventions**: Mirror existing patterns exactly\n4. **Validate Consistency**: Ensure new code looks like existing code\n\n**WHEN MODIFYING EXISTING CODE:**\n1. **Understand Context**: Read surrounding code and imports\n2. **Preserve Patterns**: Maintain existing architectural decisions\n3. **Consistent Style**: Match existing code style and structure\n4. **Validate Integration**: Ensure changes integrate seamlessly\n\n### Architecture Validation Checklist\n\n**BEFORE COMMITTING ANY CHANGES:**\n- [ ] Import hierarchy rules respected (no upward imports)\n- [ ] Platform-specific files use correct extensions\n- [ ] Security patterns maintained\n- [ ] Error handling follows established patterns\n- [ ] State management patterns consistently applied\n- [ ] UI component patterns followed\n- [ ] Translation patterns properly implemented (if applicable)\n- [ ] Testing patterns maintained and extended\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:14:20.971Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents specializing in Monorepo Architecture, such as those utilizing Electron, React Native, and Progressive Web Applications.","zh":"适合专攻 Monorepo 架构的 AI 代理，例如使用 Electron、React Native 和渐进式 Web 应用程序的代理。","ja":"モノレポアーキテクチャに特化したAIエージェントに適しています。たとえば、Electron、React Native、プログレッシブWebアプリケーションを使用するエージェントなどです。","ko":"모노레포 아키텍처에 특화된 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 예를 들어, Electron, React Native 및 프로그레시브 웹 애플리케이션을 사용하는 에이전트입니다.","es":"Ideal for AI Agents specializing in Monorepo Architecture, such as those utilizing Electron, React Native, and Progressive Web Applications.","fr":"Ideal for AI Agents specializing in Monorepo Architecture, such as those utilizing Electron, React Native, and Progressive Web Applications.","de":"Ideal for AI Agents specializing in Monorepo Architecture, such as those utilizing Electron, React Native, and Progressive Web Applications.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA especializados em Arquitetura Monorepo, como aqueles que utilizam Electron, React Native e Aplicativos Web Progressivos.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, специализирующихся на архитектуре Monorepo, таких как те, которые используют Electron, React Native и прогрессивные веб-приложения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المتخصص في هندسة مونوريبو، مثل تلك التي تستخدم إلكترون ورياكت نيتيف وتطبيقات الويب التقدمية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design and implement scalable monorepo structures, leveraging core packages like cryptography and protocol implementations, while managing multiple apps including desktop, mobile, and web applications through centralized vaults and counterparty trade management.","zh":"赋予代理设计和实施可扩展的 monorepo 结构的能力，利用核心包如密码学和协议实现，同时通过集中式金库和对手方交易管理管理多个应用程序，包括桌面、移动和网络应用程序。","ja":"エージェントがスケーラブルなモノレポ構造を設計して実装する能力を付与します。コアパッケージとして、暗号化とプロトコル実装を利用し、デスクトップ、アプリケーション、ウェブアプリケーションを含む複数のアプリケーションを、集中型の金庫と取引先の取引管理を通じて管理します。","ko":"에이전트가 확장 가능한 모노레포 구조를 설계하고 구현할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 핵심 패키지로서 암호학 및 프로토콜 구현을 활용하며, 데스크톱, 모바일, 웹 애플리케이션을 포함한 여러 애플리케이션을 중앙 집중식 금고 및 거래 상대방 거래 관리를 통해 관리합니다.","es":"Empowers agents to design and implement scalable monorepo structures, leveraging core packages like cryptography and protocol implementations, while managing multiple apps including desktop, mobile, and web applications through centralized vaults and counterparty trade management.","fr":"Empowers agents to design and implement scalable monorepo structures, leveraging core packages like cryptography and protocol implementations, while managing multiple apps including desktop, mobile, and web applications through centralized vaults and counterparty trade management.","de":"Empowers agents to design and implement scalable monorepo structures, leveraging core packages like cryptography and protocol implementations, while managing multiple apps including desktop, mobile, and web applications through centralized vaults and counterparty trade management.","pt":"Habilita agentes a projetar e implementar estruturas monorepo escaláveis, aproveitando pacotes principais como criptografia e implementações de protocolo, enquanto gerencia vários aplicativos, incluindo aplicativos de desktop, móveis e web, por meio de cofres centralizados e gerenciamento de comércio de contrapartes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать и реализовывать масштабируемые структуры monorepo, используя основные пакеты, такие как криптография и реализации протоколов, а также управлять несколькими приложениями, включая настольные, мобильные и веб-приложения, посредством централизованных хранилищ и системы управления торговлей с контрагентами.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية تصميم وتنفيذ هيكل مونوريبو قابل للتوسيع، واستخدام الحزم الأساسية مثل التشفير وتنفيذ البروتوكول، في حين إدارة التطبيقات المتعددة، بما في ذلك تطبيقات سطح المكتب والأجهزة المحمولة وتطبيقات الويب، من خلال الخزائن المركزية وإدارة التبادل مع الشركاء."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing modular monorepo architectures for multi-platform applications","Implementing core business logic and cryptography in protocol implementations","Managing trades and liquidity through central vaults and counterparty systems"],"zh":["为多平台应用程序设计模块化的 monorepo 架构","在协议实现中实施核心业务逻辑和密码学","通过集中式金库和对手方系统管理交易和流动性"],"ja":["マルチプラットフォームアプリケーションのモジュラーなモノレポアーキテクチャを設計する","プロトコル実装でコアビジネスロジックと暗号化を実装する","集中型の金庫と取引先システムを通じて取引と流動性を管理する"],"ko":["멀티 플랫폼 애플리케이션을 위한 모듈화된 모노레포 아키텍처를 설계하는 것","프로토콜 구현에서 핵심 비즈니스 논리 및 암호학을 구현하는 것","중앙 집중식 금고 및 거래 상대방 시스템을 통해 거래 및 유동성을 관리하는 것"],"es":["Designing modular monorepo architectures for multi-platform applications","Implementing core business logic and cryptography in protocol implementations","Managing trades and liquidity through central vaults and counterparty systems"],"fr":["Designing modular monorepo architectures for multi-platform applications","Implementing core business logic and cryptography in protocol implementations","Managing trades and liquidity through central vaults and counterparty systems"],"de":["Designing modular monorepo architectures for multi-platform applications","Implementing core business logic and cryptography in protocol implementations","Managing trades and liquidity through central vaults and counterparty systems"],"pt":["Projetar arquiteturas monorepo modulares para aplicativos multiplataforma","Implementar lógica comercial core e criptografia em implementações de protocolo","Gerenciar comércio e liquidez por meio de cofres centrais e sistemas de contrapartes"],"ru":["Проектировать модульные архитектуры monorepo для мультиплатформенных приложений","Реализовывать основную бизнес-логику и криптографию в реализациях протоколов","Управлять торговлей и ликвидностью посредством централизованных хранилищ и систем контрагентов"],"ar":["تصميم هيكل مونوريبو قابل للتوسيع للتطبيقات متعددة المنصات","تنفيذ المنطق التجاري الأساسي والتشفير في تنفيذ البروتوكول","إدارة التبادل والسيولة من خلال الخزائن المركزية ونظام الشركاء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of monorepo architecture and its components","Dependent on specific technologies like Electron and React Native","Limited to applications with on-chain vaults and stablecoin collateralization"],"zh":["需要了解 monorepo 架构及其组件","依赖于特定的技术，如 Electron 和 React Native","仅限于具有链上金库和稳定币担保的应用程序"],"ja":["モノレポアーキテクチャとそのコンポーネントを理解する必要がある","ElectronやReact Nativeなどの特定の技術に依存する","オンチェーン金庫とステーブルコイン担保を備えたアプリケーションに限定される"],"ko":["모노레포 아키텍처 및その 구성 요소를 이해해야 함","Electron 및 React Native와 같은 특정 기술에 의존함","체인상 금고 및 스테이블코인 담보를 갖춘 애플리케이션으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requires understanding of monorepo architecture and its components","Dependent on specific technologies like Electron and React Native","Limited to applications with on-chain vaults and stablecoin collateralization"],"fr":["Requires understanding of monorepo architecture and its components","Dependent on specific technologies like Electron and React Native","Limited to applications with on-chain vaults and stablecoin collateralization"],"de":["Requires understanding of monorepo architecture and its components","Dependent on specific technologies like Electron and React Native","Limited to applications with on-chain vaults and stablecoin collateralization"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da arquitetura monorepo e seus componentes","Dependente de tecnologias específicas como Electron e React Native","Limitado a aplicações com cofres em cadeia e garantia de stablecoin"],"ru":["Требует понимания архитектуры monorepo и ее компонентов","Зависит от конкретных технологий, таких как Electron и React Native","Ограничен для приложений с хранилищами в цепи и стейблкоин-коллатерализацией"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم هندسة مونوريبو ومكوناتها","يعتمد على تقنيات محددة مثل إلكترون ورياكت نيتيف","محدود للتطبيقات التي تحتوي على خزائن سلاسل وضمانات ستايبل كوين"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ollieb89/orchestrator/behavioral-modes', 'community', 'ollieb89', 'orchestrator', 'ollieb89/orchestrator', 'behavioral-modes', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:14:31.019Z', NULL, '{"id":"ollieb89/orchestrator/behavioral-modes","name":"behavioral-modes","description":{"zh":"行为模式定义了多种AI操作模式，优化AI性能以适应特定任务","ja":"行動モードは、特定のタスクに最適化されたAIのパフォーマンスを定義する","ko":"행동 모드는 특정 작업을 위해 최적화된 AI 성능을 정의합니다","es":"Los modos de comportamiento adaptativos permiten a la IA ajustar su enfoque para tareas específicas, mejorando su rendimiento","fr":"Les modes de comportement adaptatifs permettent à l''IA d''ajuster son approche pour des tâches spécifiques, améliorant ainsi ses performances","de":"Die adaptiven Verhaltensmodi ermöglichen es der KI, ihren Ansatz für spezifische Aufgaben anzupassen und ihre Leistung zu verbessern","pt":"Os modos comportamentais definem abordagens distintas para otimizar o desempenho de IA. Isso muda como o IA aborda problemas e se comunica.","ru":"Поведенческие режимы определяют различные подходы для оптимизации производительности ИИ. Это меняет то, как ИИ подходит к проблемам и общается.","ar":"تُحدِّد أوضاع السلوكية نهجًا متميزًا لتحسين أداء الذكاء الاصطناعي. هذا يغيِّر كيفية подход الذكاء الاصطناعي للمشكلات والاتصال.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"行为模式 - 适应性AI操作模式","ja":"行動モード - 適応性AIオペレーティングモード","ko":"행동 모드 - 적응형 AI 운영 모드","es":"Modos de comportamiento adaptativos para AI","fr":"Modes de comportement adaptatifs pour l''IA","de":"Adaptive Verhaltensmodi für KI","pt":"Modos Comportamentais: Otimização de Desempenho de IA","ru":"Поведенческие Режимы: Адаптивные Режимы Работы ИИ","ar":"أوضاع السلوكية: أوضاع تشغيل ذكاء اصطناعي متكيف","en":"behavioral-modes"},"description":{"zh":"行为模式定义了多种AI操作模式，优化AI性能以适应特定任务","ja":"行動モードは、特定のタスクに最適化されたAIのパフォーマンスを定義する","ko":"행동 모드는 특정 작업을 위해 최적화된 AI 성능을 정의합니다","es":"Los modos de comportamiento adaptativos permiten a la IA ajustar su enfoque para tareas específicas, mejorando su rendimiento","fr":"Les modes de comportement adaptatifs permettent à l''IA d''ajuster son approche pour des tâches spécifiques, améliorant ainsi ses performances","de":"Die adaptiven Verhaltensmodi ermöglichen es der KI, ihren Ansatz für spezifische Aufgaben anzupassen und ihre Leistung zu verbessern","pt":"Os modos comportamentais definem abordagens distintas para otimizar o desempenho de IA. Isso muda como o IA aborda problemas e se comunica.","ru":"Поведенческие режимы определяют различные подходы для оптимизации производительности ИИ. Это меняет то, как ИИ подходит к проблемам и общается.","ar":"تُحدِّد أوضاع السلوكية نهجًا متميزًا لتحسين أداء الذكاء الاصطناعي. هذا يغيِّر كيفية подход الذكاء الاصطناعي للمشكلات والاتصال.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["多种操作模式","任务特定优化","提高AI性能"," BRAINSTORM 模式","适应性操作"],"ja":["複数の操作モード","タスク特定の最適化","AIのパフォーマンスの向上","BRAINSTORM モード","適応性操作"],"ko":["여러 운영 모드","작업 특정 최적화","AI 성능 향상","BRAINSTORM 모드","적응형 운영"],"es":["Modos de comportamiento personalizables","Optimización del rendimiento de la IA","Enfoque adaptativo para tareas específicas","Mejora de la toma de decisiones","Flexibilidad en la resolución de problemas"],"fr":["Modes de comportement personnalisables","Optimisation des performances de l''IA","Approche adaptative pour des tâches spécifiques","Amélioration de la prise de décision","Flexibilité dans la résolution de problèmes"],"de":["Anpassbare Verhaltensmodi","Optimierung der KI-Leistung","Adaptiver Ansatz für spezifische Aufgaben","Verbesserung der Entscheidungsfindung","Flexibilität bei der Problemlösung"],"pt":["Modos de operação adaptáveis","Otimização de desempenho para tarefas específicas","Mudanças na abordagem do problema","Comunicação personalizada","Exploração de alternativas"],"ru":["Адаптивные режимы работы","Оптимизация производительности для конкретных задач","Изменения в подходе к проблеме","Персонализированная коммуникация","Изучение альтернатив"],"ar":["أوضاع تشغيل متكيفة","تحسين الأداء لمهام محددة","تغييرات في نهج المشكلة","اتصال مُخصَّص","استكشاف البدائل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["行为模式","AI操作模式","任务特定优化","AI性能优化","BRAINSTORM模式","适应性AI"],"ja":["行動モード","AIオペレーティングモード","タスク特定の最適化","AIのパフォーマンス最適化","BRAINSTORMモード","適応性AI"],"ko":["행동 모드","AI 운영 모드","작업 특정 최적화","AI 성능 최적화","BRAINSTORM 모드","적응형 AI"],"es":["modos de comportamiento adaptativos","IA adaptativa","optimización del rendimiento","tareas específicas","desarrollo de IA","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["modes de comportement adaptatifs","IA adaptative","optimisation des performances","tâches spécifiques","développement d''IA","ingénierie logicielle"],"de":["adaptive Verhaltensmodi","KI-Adaptivität","Leistungsoptimierung","spezifische Aufgaben","KI-Entwicklung","Software-Engineering"],"pt":["modos comportamentais","otimização de desempenho de IA","desenvolvimento de IA","inteligência artificial","aprendizado de máquina","desempenho de IA"],"ru":["поведенческие режимы","оптимизация производительности ИИ","разработка ИИ","искусственный интеллект","обучение машин","производительность ИИ"],"ar":["أوضاع السلوكية","تحسين أداء الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","الذكاء الاصطناعي","التعلم الآلي","أداء الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"orchestrator","repoPath":"ollieb89/orchestrator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"behavioral-modes","description":"AI operational modes (brainstorm, implement, debug, review, teach, ship, orchestrate). Use to adapt behavior based on task type.","bodyPreview":"# Behavioral Modes - Adaptive AI Operating Modes\n\n## Purpose\nThis skill defines distinct behavioral modes that optimize AI performance for specific tasks. Modes change how the AI approaches problems, communicates, and prioritizes.\n\n---\n\n## Available Modes\n\n### 1. 🧠 BRAINSTORM Mode\n\n**When to use:** Early project planning, feature ideation, architecture decisions\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Ask clarifying questions before assumptions\n- Offer multiple alternatives (at least 3)\n- Think divergently - explore","body":"# Behavioral Modes - Adaptive AI Operating Modes\n\n## Purpose\nThis skill defines distinct behavioral modes that optimize AI performance for specific tasks. Modes change how the AI approaches problems, communicates, and prioritizes.\n\n---\n\n## Available Modes\n\n### 1. 🧠 BRAINSTORM Mode\n\n**When to use:** Early project planning, feature ideation, architecture decisions\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Ask clarifying questions before assumptions\n- Offer multiple alternatives (at least 3)\n- Think divergently - explore unconventional solutions\n- No code yet - focus on ideas and options\n- Use visual diagrams (mermaid) to explain concepts\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n\"Let''s explore this together. Here are some approaches:\n\nOption A: [description]\n  ✅ Pros: ...\n  ❌ Cons: ...\n\nOption B: [description]\n  ✅ Pros: ...\n  ❌ Cons: ...\n\nWhat resonates with you? Or should we explore a different direction?\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. ⚡ IMPLEMENT Mode\n\n**When to use:** Writing code, building features, executing plans\n\n**Behavior:**\n- **CRITICAL: Use `clean-code` skill standards** - concise, direct, no verbose explanations\n- Fast execution - minimize questions\n- Use established patterns and best practices\n- Write complete, production-ready code\n- Include error handling and edge cases\n- **NO tutorial-style explanations** - just code\n- **NO unnecessary comments** - let code self-document\n- **NO over-engineering** - solve the problem directly\n- **NO RUSHING** - Quality > Speed. Read ALL references before coding.\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n[Code block]\n\n[Brief summary, max 1-2 sentences]\n```\n\n**NOT:**\n```\n\"Building [feature]...\n\n✓ Created [file1]\n✓ Created [file2]\n✓ Updated [file3]\n\n[long explanation]\n\nRun `npm run dev` to test.\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. 🔍 DEBUG Mode\n\n**When to use:** Fixing bugs, troubleshooting errors, investigating issues\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Ask for error messages and reproduction steps\n- Think systematically - check logs, trace data flow\n- Form hypothesis → test → verify\n- Explain the root cause, not just the fix\n- Prevent future occurrences\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n\"Investigating...\n\n🔍 Symptom: [what''s happening]\n🎯 Root cause: [why it''s happening]\n✅ Fix: [the solution]\n🛡️ Prevention: [how to avoid in future]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. 📋 REVIEW Mode\n\n**When to use:** Code review, architecture review, security audit\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Be thorough but constructive\n- Categorize by severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low)\n- Explain the \"why\" behind suggestions\n- Offer improved code examples\n- Acknowledge what''s done well\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n## Code Review: [file/feature]\n\n### 🔴 Critical\n- [issue with explanation]\n\n### 🟠 Improvements\n- [suggestion with example]\n\n### 🟢 Good\n- [positive observation]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. 📚 TEACH Mode\n\n**When to use:** Explaining concepts, documentation, onboarding\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Explain from fundamentals\n- Use analogies and examples\n- Progress from simple to complex\n- Include practical exercises\n- Check understanding\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n## Understanding [Concept]\n\n### What is it?\n[Simple explanation with analogy]\n\n### How it works\n[Technical explanation with diagram]\n\n### Example\n[Code example with comments]\n\n### Try it yourself\n[Exercise or task]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. 🚀 SHIP Mode\n\n**When to use:** Production deployment, final polish, release preparation\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Focus on stability over features\n- Check for missing error handling\n- Verify environment configs\n- Run all tests\n- Create deployment checklist\n\n**Output style:**\n```\n## Pre-Ship Checklist\n\n### ✅ Code Quality\n- [ ] No TypeScript errors\n- [ ] ESLint passing\n- [ ] All tests passing\n\n### ✅ Security\n- [ ] No exposed secrets\n- [ ] Input validation complete\n\n### ✅ Performance\n- [ ] Bundle size acceptable\n- [ ] No console.logs\n\n### 🚀 Ready to deploy\n```\n\n---\n\n## Mode Detection\n\nThe AI should automatically detect the appropriate mode based on:\n\n| Trigger | Mode |\n|---------|------|\n| \"what if\", \"ideas\", \"options\" | BRAINSTORM |\n| \"build\", \"create\", \"add\" | IMPLEMENT |\n| \"not working\", \"error\", \"bug\" | DEBUG |\n| \"review\", \"check\", \"audit\" | REVIEW |\n| \"explain\", \"how does\", \"learn\" | TEACH |\n| \"deploy\", \"release\", \"production\" | SHIP |\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Agent Collaboration Patterns (2025)\n\nModern architectures optimized for agent-to-agent collaboration:\n\n### 1. 🔭 EXPLORE Mode\n**Role:** Discovery and Analysis (Explorer Agent)\n**Behavior:** Socratic questioning, deep-dive code reading, dependency mapping.\n**Output:** `discovery-report.json`, architectural visualization.\n\n### 2. 🗺️ PLAN-EXECUTE-CRITIC (PEC)\nCyclic mode transitions for high-complexity tasks:\n1. **Planner:** Decomposes the task into atomic steps (`task.md`).\n2. **Executor:** Performs the actual coding (`IMPLEMENT`).\n3. **Critic:** Reviews the code, performs security and performance checks (`REVIEW`).\n\n### 3. 🧠 MENTAL MODEL SYNC\nBehavior for creating and loading \"Mental Model\" summaries to preserve context between sessions.\n\n---\n\n## Combining Modes\n\n---\n\n## Manual Mode Switching\n\nUsers can explicitly request a mode:\n\n```\n/brainstorm new feature ideas\n/implement the user profile page\n/debug why login fails\n/review this pull request\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:14:31.019Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversational Agents requiring adaptive problem-solving and communication strategies, such as Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code.","zh":"适合需要自适应问题解决和通信策略的对话式代理，例如Cursor、Windsurf或Claude Code。","ja":"アダプティブな問題解決とコミュニケーション戦略を必要とする会話エージェント、たとえばCursor、Windsurf、またはClaude Codeに適しています。","ko":"적응형 문제 해결 및 통신 전략이 필요한 대화형 에이전트에 적합합니다. 예를 들어 Cursor, Windsurf 또는 Claude Code와 같은 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de conversación que requieren estrategias de resolución de problemas y comunicación adaptativas, como Cursor, Windsurf o Claude Code.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de conversation nécessitant des stratégies de résolution de problèmes et de communication adaptatives, tels que Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code.","de":"Ideal für Conversational Agents, die adaptive Problemlösungs- und Kommunikationsstrategien erfordern, wie z. B. Cursor, Windsurf oder Claude Code.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Conversação que exigem resolução de problemas adaptativa e estratégias de comunicação, como Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-конверсантов, требующих адаптивных стратегий решения проблем и коммуникации, таких как Cursor, Windsurf или Claude Code.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المحادثين الذين يحتاجون إلى استراتيجيات حل المشكلات التكيفية والاتصالات، مثل Cursor أو Windsurf أو Claude Code."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to switch between distinct behavioral modes, including BRAINSTORM mode for divergent thinking, using clarifying questions, and offering multiple alternatives, thus enhancing their ability to approach problems and prioritize tasks effectively, leveraging protocols like dialogue management and natural language processing.","zh":"赋予代理切换不同行为模式的能力，包括BRAINSTORM模式，用于发散性思维，使用澄清问题，并提供多种替代方案，从而增强其解决问题和有效优先处理任务的能力，利用对话管理和自然语言处理等协议。","ja":"エージェントに異なる動作モードを切り替える能力を与え、BRAINSTORMモードを使用して発散的思考を行い、明確化の質問を使用し、複数の代替案を提供し、対話管理や自然言語処理などのプロトコルを利用して、問題に取り組み、タスクを効果的に優先順位付けする能力を高めます。","ko":"에이전트가 다른 행동 모드를 전환할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 BRAINSTORM 모드를 사용하여 발산적思考을 수행하고, 명확화 질문을 사용하며, 여러 대안을 제공하여, 에이전트가 문제에 접근하고 작업을 효과적으로 우선순위에 따라 처리할 수 있는 능력을 향상시킵니다. 이것은 대화 관리 및 자연어 처리와 같은 프로토콜을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes cambiar entre diferentes modos de comportamiento, incluyendo el modo BRAINSTORM para pensamiento divergente, utilizando preguntas clarificadoras y ofreciendo múltiples alternativas, lo que mejora su capacidad para abordar problemas y priorizar tareas de manera efectiva, aprovechando protocolos como la gestión de diálogos y el procesamiento de lenguaje natural.","fr":"Permet aux agents de basculer entre des modes de comportement distincts, notamment le mode BRAINSTORM pour la pensée divergente, en utilisant des questions clarificatrices et en proposant plusieurs alternatives, ce qui améliore leur capacité à aborder les problèmes et à prioriser les tâches de manière efficace, en exploitant des protocoles tels que la gestion de dialogue et le traitement automatique des langues.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, zwischen verschiedenen Verhaltensmodi zu wechseln, einschließlich des BRAINSTORM-Modus für divergentes Denken, unter Verwendung von Klarstellungsfragen und Angebot von mehreren Alternativen, wodurch ihre Fähigkeit, Probleme anzugehen und Aufgaben effektiv zu priorisieren, verbessert wird, indem Protokolle wie Dialogverwaltung und natürliche Sprachverarbeitung genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a mudar entre modos comportamentais distintos, incluindo o modo BRAINSTORM para pensamento divergente, utilizando perguntas esclarecedoras e oferecendo múltiplas alternativas, melhorando assim sua capacidade de abordar problemas e priorizar tarefas de forma eficaz, aproveitando protocolos como gerenciamento de diálogo e processamento de linguagem natural.","ru":"Позволяет агентам переключаться между различными поведенческими режимами, включая режим BRAINSTORM для дивергентного мышления, используя вопросы-разъяснения и предлагая несколько альтернатив, тем самым повышая их способность подходить к проблемам и расставлять приоритеты задач эффективно, используя протоколы, такие как управление диалогом и обработка естественного языка.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من التبديل بين أوضاع سلوكية متميزة، بما في ذلك وضع BRAINSTORM للتفكير المتنوع، باستخدام أسئلة توضيحية وطرح بدائل متعددة، وبالتالي تحسين قدرتهم على التعامل مع المشكلات وتحديد أولويات المهام بشكل فعال، و利用 بروتوكولات مثل إدارة الحوار والمعالجة اللغوية الطبيعية."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating project planning with BRAINSTORM mode for feature ideation and architecture decisions","Generating multiple solutions to complex problems using divergent thinking","Adapting communication strategies based on the task at hand, such as prioritizing clarity in explanations"],"zh":["使用BRAINSTORM模式自动执行项目规划，用于特性创意和架构决策","使用发散性思维生成复杂问题的多种解决方案","根据任务需求调整通信策略，例如在解释中优先考虑清晰度"],"ja":["BRAINSTORMモードを使用してプロジェクト計画を自動化し、機能アイデアとアーキテクチャの決定を行う","発散的思考を使用して複雑な問題の複数の解決策を生成する","タスクの要求に応じてコミュニケーション戦略を調整する、たとえば説明の明確性を優先する"],"ko":["BRAINSTORM 모드를 사용하여 프로젝트 계획을 자동화하고, 기능 아이디어 및 아키텍처 결정에 사용됩니다.","발산적思考을 사용하여 복잡한 문제의 여러 가지 해결책을 생성합니다.","작업의需求에 따라 통신 전략을 조정하여, 예를 들어 설명의 명확성을 우선합니다."],"es":["Automatización de la planificación de proyectos con el modo BRAINSTORM para la ideación de características y decisiones de arquitectura","Generación de múltiples soluciones a problemas complejos utilizando el pensamiento divergente","Adaptación de las estrategias de comunicación en función de la tarea en cuestión, como priorizar la claridad en las explicaciones"],"fr":["Automatisation de la planification de projet avec le mode BRAINSTORM pour l''idéation de fonctionnalités et les décisions d''architecture","Génération de plusieurs solutions à des problèmes complexes en utilisant la pensée divergente","Adaptation des stratégies de communication en fonction de la tâche en question, comme prioriser la clarté dans les explications"],"de":["Automatisierung der Projektplanung mit dem BRAINSTORM-Modus für die Ideenfindung von Funktionen und Architekturentscheidungen","Erzeugung mehrerer Lösungen für komplexe Probleme unter Verwendung von divergentem Denken","Anpassung der Kommunikationsstrategien anhand der jeweiligen Aufgabe, wie z. B. Priorisierung von Klarheit in Erklärungen"],"pt":["Automatizar a planejamento de projetos com o modo BRAINSTORM para ideação de recursos e decisões de arquitetura","Gerar múltiplas soluções para problemas complexos usando pensamento divergente","Adaptar estratégias de comunicação com base na tarefa em questão, como priorizar a clareza nas explicações"],"ru":["Автоматизировать планирование проектов с режимом BRAINSTORM для генерации идей и принятия решений по архитектуре","Генерировать несколько решений для сложных проблем, используя дивергентное мышление","Адаптировать стратегии коммуникации в зависимости от задачи, например, отдавать приоритет ясности в объяснениях"],"ar":["تحسين تخطيط المشروع باستخدام وضع BRAINSTORM لفكرة الميزات وتصميم القرارات","توليد حلول متعددة للمشكلات المعقدة باستخدام التفكير المتنوع","تعديل استراتيجيات الاتصال بناءً على المهمة المعنية، مثل تحديد الأولوية للوضوح في التوضيحات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with the agent''s core decision-making and communication systems","Modes may need customization to fit specific task requirements, such as adjusting the number of alternatives offered"],"zh":["需要与代理的核心决策和通信系统集成","模式可能需要自定义以适应特定的任务需求，例如调整提供的替代方案的数量"],"ja":["エージェントのコアの意思決定とコミュニケーションシステムとの統合が必要","モードは、特定のタスク要件に合わせてカスタマイズする必要がある場合があります。たとえば、提供される代替案の数を調整する"],"ko":["에이전트의 핵심 결정 및 통신 시스템과 통합이 필요합니다.","모드는 특정 작업 요구 사항에 맞게 사용자 지정할 필요가 있습니다. 예를 들어, 제공되는 대체 솔루션의 수를 조정합니다."],"es":["Requiere integración con los sistemas de toma de decisiones y comunicación principales del agente","Los modos pueden necesitar personalización para adaptarse a requisitos de tarea específicos, como ajustar el número de alternativas ofrecidas"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec les systèmes de prise de décision et de communication principaux de l''agent","Les modes peuvent nécessiter une personnalisation pour s''adapter à des exigences de tâche spécifiques, comme ajuster le nombre d''alternatives proposées"],"de":["Erfordert Integration mit den Haupt-Entscheidungs- und Kommunikationssystemen des Agents","Die Modi können eine Anpassung benötigen, um spezifischen Aufgabenanforderungen zu entsprechen, wie z. B. Anpassen der Anzahl der angebotenen Alternativen"],"pt":["Exige integração com os sistemas de tomada de decisão e comunicação centrais do agente","Os modos podem precisar de personalização para atender a requisitos de tarefas específicas, como ajustar o número de alternativas oferecidas"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с основными системами принятия решений и коммуникации агента","Режимы могут потребовать настройки для соответствия конкретным требованиям задач, например, корректировки количества предлагаемых альтернатив"],"ar":["يتطلب التكامل مع أنظمة اتخاذ القرارات والاتصالات الأساسية للوكيل","يمكن أن تحتاج أوضاع إلى تخصيص لتناسب متطلبات مهمة محددة، مثل تعديل عدد البدائل المقترحة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/new-skill', 'community', 'Paxeer-Network', 'Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'new-skill', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:14:01.994Z', NULL, '{"id":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/new-skill","name":"new-skill","description":{"zh":"新技能是一个合成永续期货协议，支持RWA资产、加密货币、股票和指数，允许交易者开设高达1000倍的杠杆多头空头仓位","ja":"新スキルは、RWAアセット、暗号資産、株式、指数をサポートする合成永続先物プロトコルで、トレーダーは最大1000倍のレバレッジでのロング/ショートポジションを開設できます","ko":"새로운 기술은 RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식 및 지수를 지원하는 합성 영속적 선물 프로토콜로, 거래자는 최대 1000배의 레버리지로 롱/숏 포지션을 개설할 수 있습니다","es":"El protocolo de futuros sintéticos perpetuos es una plataforma que admite activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices con apalancamiento de hasta 1000x. Los traders pueden abrir posiciones largas/cortas con garantía de stablecoins en bóvedas en cadena por usuario.","fr":"Le protocole de futures perpétuels synthétiques est une plate-forme qui prend en charge les actifs RWA, les crypto-monnaies, les actions et les indices avec un effet de levier allant jusqu''à 1000x. Les traders peuvent ouvrir des positions longues/courtes avec une garantie de stablecoins dans des ...","de":"Das synthetische Perpetual-Futures-Protokoll ist eine Plattform, die RWA-Assets, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes mit bis zu 1000x Hebelwirkung unterstützt. Trader können lange/kurze Positionen mit einer Garantie von Stablecoins in benutzerdefinierten Vaulten in der Blockchain eröffnen.","pt":"O novo skill é um protocolo de futuros sintéticos perpétuos que suporta ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices. Os traders podem abrir posições long/short com alavancagem de até 1000x.","ru":"Новый навык представляет собой синтетический протокол вечных фьючерсов, поддерживающий активы RWA, криптовалюты, акции и индексы. Трейдеры могут открывать длинные/короткие позиции с левериджем до 1000х.","ar":"المهارة الجديدة هي بروتوكول العقود الآجلة الاصطناعية الدائمة التي تدعم الأصول RWA والعملات المشفرة والأوراق المالية والأسواق. يمكن للمتداولين فتح مراكز طويلة/قصيرة مع رافعة مالية تصل إلى 1000 مرة","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a cus..."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"新技能：合成永续期货协议","ja":"新スキル：合成永続先物プロトコル","ko":"새로운 기술: 합성 영속적 선물 프로토콜","es":"Protocolo de Futuros Sintéticos Perpetuos","fr":"Protocole de Futures Perpétuels Synthétiques","de":"Synthetisches Perpetual-Futures-Protokoll","pt":"Protocolo de Futuros Sintéticos Perpétuos","ru":"Синтетический Протокол Вечных Фьючерсов","ar":"بروتوكول العقود الآجلة الاصطناعية الدائمة","en":"new-skill"},"description":{"zh":"新技能是一个合成永续期货协议，支持RWA资产、加密货币、股票和指数，允许交易者开设高达1000倍的杠杆多头空头仓位","ja":"新スキルは、RWAアセット、暗号資産、株式、指数をサポートする合成永続先物プロトコルで、トレーダーは最大1000倍のレバレッジでのロング/ショートポジションを開設できます","ko":"새로운 기술은 RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식 및 지수를 지원하는 합성 영속적 선물 프로토콜로, 거래자는 최대 1000배의 레버리지로 롱/숏 포지션을 개설할 수 있습니다","es":"El protocolo de futuros sintéticos perpetuos es una plataforma que admite activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices con apalancamiento de hasta 1000x. L...","fr":"Le protocole de futures perpétuels synthétiques est une plate-forme qui prend en charge les actifs RWA, les crypto-monnaies, les actions et les indices avec ...","de":"Das synthetische Perpetual-Futures-Protokoll ist eine Plattform, die RWA-Assets, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes mit bis zu 1000x Hebelwirkung unterstütz...","pt":"O novo skill é um protocolo de futuros sintéticos perpétuos que suporta ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices. Os traders podem abrir posições long/short...","ru":"Новый навык представляет собой синтетический протокол вечных фьючерсов, поддерживающий активы RWA, криптовалюты, акции и индексы. Трейдеры могут открывать дл...","ar":"المهارة الجديدة هي بروتوكول العقود الآجلة الاصطناعية الدائمة التي تدعم الأصول RWA والعملات المشفرة والأوراق المالية والأسواق. يمكن للمتداولين فتح مراكز طويلة...","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collater..."},"definition":{"en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"zh":["支持RWA资产、加密货币、股票和指数","高达1000倍的杠杆","使用稳定币作为抵押品","自定义oracle、虚拟AMM和TWAP平滑定价","中央流动性金库作为所有交易的对手方"],"ja":["RWAアセット、暗号資産、株式、指数のサポート","最大1000倍のレバレッジ","スターブルコインを担保として使用","カスタムオラクル、仮想AMM、TWAPスムージングによる価格設定","中央流動性金庫がすべての取引の対手方となる"],"ko":["RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식 및 지수의 지원","최대 1000배의 레버리지","스테이블코인을 담보로 사용","사용자 정의 오라클, 가상 AMM 및 TWAP 스무딩 가격 설정","중앙 유동성 금고가 모든 거래의 대응자로 작용"],"es":["Soporte para activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices","Apalancamiento de hasta 1000x","Bóvedas en cadena por usuario para garantizar stablecoins","Pricing combinado con un oráculo personalizado, un AMM virtual y suavizado TWAP","Posiciones largas/cortas con garantía de stablecoins","Vault de liquidez centralizado como contraparte para todos los trades"],"fr":["Prise en charge des actifs RWA, des crypto-monnaies, des actions et des indices","Effet de levier allant jusqu''à 1000x","Vaults en chaîne par utilisateur pour garantir les stablecoins","Pricing combiné avec un oracle personnalisé, un AMM virtuel et un lissage TWAP","Positions longues/courtes avec une garantie de stablecoins","Vault de liquidité centralisé en tant que contrepartie pour tous les trades"],"de":["Unterstützung für RWA-Assets, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes","Hebelwirkung von bis zu 1000x","Benutzerdefinierte Vaulten in der Blockchain zur Garantie von Stablecoins","Kombinierter Pricing mit einem benutzerdefinierten Oracle, einem virtuellen AMM und einem TWAP-Glättung","Lange/kurze Positionen mit einer Garantie von Stablecoins","Zentraler Liquiditäts-Vault als Kontrahent für alle Trades"],"pt":["Suporte a ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices","Posições long/short com alavancagem de até 1000x","Caixa de liquidez centralizada","Preços combinados com oracle personalizado, Virtual AMM e suavização TWAP"],"ru":["Поддержка активов RWA, криптовалют, акций и индексов","Длинные/короткие позиции с левериджем до 1000х","Централизованная ликвидационная коробка","Цены, объединенные с настраиваемым оракулом, виртуальной AMM и сглаживанием TWAP"],"ar":["دعم الأصول RWA والعملات المشفرة والأوراق المالية والأسواق","مراكز طويلة/قصيرة مع رافعة مالية تصل إلى 1000 مرة","صندوق سيولة مركزي","أسعار مجتمعة مع أوراكل مخصص و AMM افتراضي وتنعيم TWAP"]},"keywords":{"zh":["合成永续期货","RWA资产","加密货币","股票","指数","杠杆交易","稳定币","自定义oracle","虚拟AMM","TWAP平滑"],"ja":["合成永続先物","RWAアセット","暗号資産","株式","指数","レバレッジトレード","スターブルコイン","カスタムオラクル","仮想AMM","TWAPスムージング"],"ko":["합성 영속적 선물","RWA 자산","암호화폐","주식","지수","레버리지 거래","스테이블코인","사용자 정의 오라클","가상 AMM","TWAP 스무딩"],"es":["futuros sintéticos perpetuos","RWA assets","criptomonedas","acciones","índices","apalancamiento","stablecoins","bóvedas en cadena","oráculo personalizado","AMM virtual","TWAP suavizado"],"fr":["futures perpétuels synthétiques","actifs RWA","crypto-monnaies","actions","indices","effet de levier","stablecoins","vaults en chaîne","orácle personnalisé","AMM virtuel","lissage TWAP"],"de":["synthetische Perpetual-Futures","RWA-Assets","Kryptowährungen","Aktien","Indizes","Hebelwirkung","Stablecoins","benutzerdefinierte Vaulten","benutzerdefiniertes Oracle","virtueller AMM","TWAP-Glättung"],"pt":["protocolo de futuros sintéticos perpétuos","futuros sintéticos","posições long/short","alavancagem","ativos RWA","criptomoedas","ações","índices"],"ru":["синтетический протокол вечных фьючерсов","синтетические фьючерсы","длинные/короткие позиции","леверидж","активы RWA","криптовалюты","акции","индексы"],"ar":["بروتوكول العقود الآجلة الاصطناعية الدائمة","العقود الآجلة الاصطناعية","مراكز طويلة/قصيرة","رافعة مالية","الأصول RWA","العملات المشفرة","الأوراق المالية","الأسواق"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"new-skill","description":"Creates a new Claude Code Skill following best practices. Use when the user wants to create a new skill, add a skill, or asks about writing skills for Claude Code. Fetches latest documentation before generating skill content. New skill. Create a skill.","bodyPreview":"# Creating a New Skill\n\nFollow this workflow when creating a new Claude Code Skill.\n\n## 0) Fetch latest best practices (REQUIRED)\n\nBefore writing any skill content, you MUST fetch and read the latest documentation:\n\n1. **Skills overview**: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills\n2. **Best practices**: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/best-practices\n\nUse WebFetch to retrieve these pages and extract key guidelines before proceeding.\n\n## 1) Check if skill should merg","body":"# Creating a New Skill\n\nFollow this workflow when creating a new Claude Code Skill.\n\n## 0) Fetch latest best practices (REQUIRED)\n\nBefore writing any skill content, you MUST fetch and read the latest documentation:\n\n1. **Skills overview**: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills\n2. **Best practices**: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/best-practices\n\nUse WebFetch to retrieve these pages and extract key guidelines before proceeding.\n\n## 1) Check if skill should merge into existing skill (REQUIRED)\n\n**Before creating a new skill, first check if the content belongs in an existing skill.**\n\n### Review existing skills\n```bash\nls -la .claude/skills/\n```\n\n### Decision criteria for merging\n\n**MERGE into existing skill as a rule if:**\n- Topic is closely related to an existing skill''s domain\n- Content would be a sub-topic of an existing skill\n- Similar workflows or patterns already exist\n- Adding as a rule keeps related knowledge together\n\n**CREATE new skill if:**\n- Topic is distinct and doesn''t fit any existing category\n- Content is substantial enough to warrant standalone skill\n- Different trigger keywords and use cases\n- Would make existing skill too large or unfocused\n\n### Token optimization considerations\n\n**When to split existing skills:**\n\nSkills should be split when they become too large, causing unnecessary token consumption on every load. Use these criteria:\n\n**🚨 SPLIT if any of these apply:**\n- **File size**: Reference file >10 KB or >1000 lines\n- **Usage frequency mismatch**: Topics used in very different scenarios\n- **Independent workflows**: Topics don''t share common patterns\n- **Specific trigger words**: Topic has distinct keywords that rarely overlap\n\n**✅ KEEP TOGETHER if:**\n- **High correlation**: Topics frequently used together (>50% overlap)\n- **Shared concepts**: Common patterns, terminology, or workflows\n- **Small files**: All reference files <5 KB each\n- **Natural grouping**: User thinks of topics as related\n\n**Token savings formula:**\n\n```\nToken Savings = (Skill_Size × Probability_Not_Needed) - Split_Overhead\n\nWhere:\n- Skill_Size: Total tokens in skill (SKILL.md + all references)\n- Probability_Not_Needed: % of tasks that don''t need this topic\n- Split_Overhead: ~500-1000 tokens (new SKILL.md + metadata)\n```\n\n**Real-world examples from our codebase:**\n\n| Original | Size | Split Into | Token Savings |\n|----------|------|------------|---------------|\n| `1k-coding-patterns` | 15 KB (9 files) | 6 focused skills | 47-53% in 90% cases |\n| `1k-dev-workflows` | 43 KB (3 files) | 3 focused skills | 80% when not doing Sentry |\n\n**Splitting strategies:**\n\n1. **Conservative split** (safe, minimal disruption):\n   - Split only the largest, most independent file\n   - Keep related topics together\n   - Example: Split 34 KB Sentry analysis from 43 KB workflows\n\n2. **Moderate split** (balanced):\n   - Split 3-5 distinct topics into separate skills\n   - Keep core patterns together\n   - Example: Split date, i18n, error-handling, cross-platform, code-quality\n\n3. **Aggressive split** (maximum optimization):\n   - Each major topic becomes its own skill\n   - Only keep truly inseparable content together\n   - Use when: Very large skill (>50 KB), low topic correlation\n\n### Example Skill Categories\n\n| Category | Skill | Merge candidates |\n|----------|-------|------------------|\n| Code quality | `code-quality` | Lint fixes, pre-commit tasks, documentation |\n| Sentry analysis | `sentry-analysis` | Crash reports, AppHang, ANR fixes |\n| Native module patches | `patching-native-modules` | iOS/Android crash fixes, native code patches |\n| Error monitoring | `sentry` | Error filtering, crash configuration |\n| Architecture | `architecture` | Project structure, import rules |\n| Coding patterns | `coding-patterns` | React patterns, TypeScript conventions |\n| Performance | `performance` | Optimization, concurrent requests, memoization |\n| Error handling | `error-handling` | Try/catch, error boundaries, user-facing errors |\n| State management | `state-management` | State atoms, global state |\n| Cross-platform | `cross-platform` | Platform-specific code |\n| Date formatting | `date-formatting` | Date/time display, locale formatting |\n| i18n | `i18n` | Translations, locales |\n| Git workflow | `git-workflow` | Branching, commits, PRs |\n| Dev commands | `dev-commands` | Build, test, lint commands |\n\n### Merging workflow\n\nIf merging into existing skill:\n\n1. **Add as a rule file:**\n   ```\n   .claude/skills/<existing-skill>/\n   ├── SKILL.md                          # Update quick reference\n   └── references/rules/\n       └── <new-topic>.md                # Add detailed content here\n   ```\n\n2. **Update the main SKILL.md:**\n   - Add entry to quick reference table\n   - Add brief summary section\n   - Link to the new rule file\n\n3. **Example merge:**\n   ```markdown\n   ## Quick Reference\n\n   | Feature | Guide | Key Files |\n   |---------|-------|-----------|\n   | Existing topic | [existing.md](references/rules/existing.md) | `path/to/files` |\n   | **New topic** | [new-topic.md](references/rules/new-topic.md) | `path/to/files` |  <!-- Add this -->\n   ```\n\n### Splitting workflow\n\nIf splitting an existing skill:\n\n1. **Analyze current skill:**\n   ```bash\n   # Check file sizes\n   ls -lh .claude/skills/<skill-name>/references/rules/\n   wc -l .claude/skills/<skill-name>/references/rules/*.md\n   ```\n\n2. **Identify split candidates:**\n   - Files >10 KB or >1000 lines\n   - Topics with distinct trigger words\n   - Workflows used independently\n\n3. **Create new skill directories:**\n   ```bash\n   mkdir -p .claude/skills/<new-skill-1>/references/rules\n   mkdir -p .claude/skills/<new-skill-2>/references/rules\n   ```\n\n4. **Move files (git tracks as rename):**\n   ```bash\n   mv .claude/skills/<old-skill>/references/rules/<topic>.md \\\n      .claude/skills/<new-skill>/references/rules/\n   ```\n\n5. **Create SKILL.md for each new skill:**\n   - Write focused description with specific trigger words\n   - Add Quick Reference section\n   - Include Related Skills section\n\n6. **Update original skill SKILL.md:**\n   - Remove split topics from Quick Reference\n   - Update Related Skills to point to new skills\n\n7. **Update cross-references:**\n   ```bash\n   # Find all skills that reference the old skill\n   grep -r \"old-skill\" .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md\n\n   # Update each reference to point to appropriate new skill\n   ```\n\n8. **Commit with clear message:**\n   ```bash\n   git add -A .claude/skills/\n   git commit -m \"refactor: split <old-skill> into focused skills\"\n   ```\n\n## 2) Gather requirements (for new skills)\n\nIf creating a new skill, ask the user:\n- What task should this skill automate?\n- What triggers should activate this skill? (keywords, file types, contexts)\n- Should it be project-scoped (`.claude/skills/`) or personal (`~/.claude/skills/`)?\n- What tools does it need? (Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, WebFetch, Write, etc.)\n\n## 3) Create skill structure\n\n### Standard structure (recommended)\n\n```\n.claude/skills/<skill-name>/\n├── SKILL.md                    # Main entry with quick reference (required)\n└── references/\n    └── rules/\n        ├── topic-1.md          # Detailed guide for topic 1\n        ├── topic-2.md          # Detailed guide for topic 2\n        └── topic-3.md          # Detailed guide for topic 3\n```\n\n### Simple structure (for single-topic skills)\n\n```\n.claude/skills/<skill-name>/\n└── SKILL.md                    # All content in one file\n```\n\n### SKILL.md template\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: skill-name\ndescription: Brief description of what this Skill does and when to use it. Include specific trigger keywords.\nallowed-tools: Read, Grep, Glob  # Optional: restrict tool access\n---\n\n# Skill Title\n\nBrief overview.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Topic | Guide | Key Files |\n|-------|-------|-----------|\n| Topic 1 | [topic-1.md](references/rules/topic-1.md) | `path/to/files` |\n| Topic 2 | [topic-2.md](references/rules/topic-2.md) | `path/to/files` |\n\n## Topic 1 Summary\n\nSee: [references/rules/topic-1.md](references/rules/topic-1.md)\n\n**Key points:**\n- Point 1\n- Point 2\n\n## Topic 2 Summary\n\nSee: [references/rules/topic-2.md](references/rules/topic-2.md)\n\n**Key points:**\n- Point 1\n- Point 2\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- `/related-skill-1` - Description\n- `/related-skill-2` - Description\n```\n\n## 4) Apply best practices checklist\n\n### Naming\n- [ ] Use descriptive names: `feature-guides`, `dev-workflows`, `sentry`\n- [ ] Max 64 chars, lowercase letters/numbers/hyphens only\n- [ ] No reserved words: \"anthropic\", \"claude\"\n- [ ] Consider project-specific prefix if needed for organization\n\n### Description\n- [ ] Write in third person (\"Processes...\", not \"I can help...\")\n- [ ] Include what it does AND when to use it\n- [ ] Include specific trigger keywords users would say\n- [ ] Max 1024 chars\n\n### Content structure\n- [ ] Main SKILL.md has quick reference table linking to rules\n- [ ] Detailed content goes in `references/rules/*.md`\n- [ ] Each rule file is self-contained and focused\n- [ ] Keep SKILL.md body under 500 lines\n- [ ] Use Unix-style paths (forward slashes)\n\n### Organization\n- [ ] Group related topics into one skill with multiple rules\n- [ ] Use consistent formatting across all rules\n- [ ] Include \"Related Skills\" section for cross-references\n- [ ] Add checklist for complex workflows\n\n## 5) Output the skill\n\nAfter gathering requirements and applying best practices:\n1. Create the skill directory with `references/rules/` structure\n2. Write SKILL.md with quick reference table\n3. Add rule files for each topic\n4. Summarize what was created\n5. **Run token analysis to verify optimization** (REQUIRED)\n\n### Token Analysis (Self-Check)\n\n**ALWAYS run after creating or modifying skills:**\n\n```bash\n# Run token analysis\npython3 development/skills-analysis/analyze-skills-tokens.py --sort-by-size\n\n# Check your new skill''s token count\npython3 development/skills-analysis/analyze-skills-tokens.py --detailed | grep -A 5 \"your-skill-name\"\n```\n\n**Verification checklist:**\n- [ ] New skill is <5,000 tokens (ideal)\n- [ ] If >5,000 tokens: Topics are highly correlated (>50% usage together)\n- [ ] If >10,000 tokens: Plan immediate split\n- [ ] SKILL.md has Quick Reference (avoid forcing full file load)\n- [ ] No duplicate content across skills\n\n**Action based on results:**\n\n| Token Count | Action |\n|-------------|--------|\n| < 2,000 | ✅ Excellent - proceed |\n| 2,000 - 5,000 | ✅ Good - proceed, monitor growth |\n| 5,000 - 10,000 | ⚠️ Review: Can topics be split? If highly correlated, proceed with Quick Reference |\n| > 10,000 | 🚨 Split before committing |\n\nSee [development/skills-analysis/SKILLS-TOKEN-MONITORING.md](../../../development/skills-analysis/SKILLS-TOKEN-MONITORING.md) for detailed guidance.\n\n## Example: Skill with multiple rules\n\n```\n.claude/skills/feature-guides/\n├── SKILL.md\n└── references/rules/\n    ├── adding-features.md\n    ├── adding-events.md\n    ├── notification-system.md\n    └── page-and-route.md\n```\n\n**SKILL.md content:**\n```yaml\n---\nname: feature-guides\ndescription: Feature development guides. Use when adding new features, events, notifications, pages, or routes.\n---\n\n# Feature Development Guides\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Feature | Guide | Key Files |\n|---------|-------|-----------|\n| Add new feature | [adding-features.md](references/rules/adding-features.md) | `packages/core/src/features/` |\n| Add events | [adding-events.md](references/rules/adding-events.md) | `packages/shared/types/events.ts` |\n\n## Adding New Features\n\nSee: [references/rules/adding-features.md](references/rules/adding-features.md)\n\n**Key steps:**\n1. Implement core logic\n2. Add configuration\n3. Update UI components\n```\n\n## Anti-patterns to avoid\n\n### Structure & Organization\n- ❌ Creating new skill when content fits existing category\n- ❌ Putting all content in SKILL.md (use references/rules for detail)\n- ❌ Deeply nested file references (keep one level deep)\n\n### Content Quality\n- ❌ Vague descriptions like \"Helps with documents\"\n- ❌ Multiple approaches without clear defaults\n- ❌ Over-explaining what Claude already knows\n- ❌ Missing trigger keywords in description\n\n### Token Optimization Anti-patterns\n- ❌ **Keeping bloated skills**: Not splitting when files exceed 10 KB\n- ❌ **Over-splitting**: Creating separate skills for highly correlated topics\n- ❌ **Ignoring usage patterns**: Not considering which topics are used together\n- ❌ **Vague trigger words**: Using generic triggers that cause unnecessary loading\n- ❌ **No Quick Reference**: Forcing full file load instead of showing summary first\n- ❌ **Duplicate content**: Copying content across skills instead of cross-referencing\n\n### Examples of Good vs Bad Splitting\n\n**❌ BAD: Over-splitting**\n```\ndate-format-display\ndate-format-parse\ndate-format-locale\n```\n*Problem: These are always used together, split overhead > savings*\n\n**✅ GOOD: Focused skill**\n```\ndate-formatting\n├── SKILL.md (Quick Reference)\n└── references/rules/date-formatting.md\n```\n\n**❌ BAD: Keeping bloated**\n```\ncoding-patterns (15 KB, 9 unrelated files)\n```\n*Problem: Loading all patterns even when only need one*\n\n**✅ GOOD: Split by independence**\n```\ncoding-patterns (core patterns only)\ndate-formatting (independent utility)\ni18n (independent utility)\nerror-handling (independent patterns)\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:14:01.994Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Financial Analysis Agents needing advanced trading capabilities with perpetual futures protocols and support for RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes.","zh":"非常适合需要高级交易功能的金融分析代理，包括永续期货协议和对RWA资产、加密货币、股票和指数的支持。","ja":"高度な取引機能を必要とする金融分析エージェントに最適で、永続的な先物取引プロトコルとRWAアセット、暗号通貨、株式、指数に対するサポートを提供します。","ko":"고급 거래 기능이 필요한 금융 분석 에이전트에게 적합하며, 영구적 선물 프로토콜 및 RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식, 지수를 지원합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis Financiero que necesitan capacidades de trading avanzadas con protocolos de futuros perpetuos y soporte para activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse Financière ayant besoin de capacités de trading avancées avec des protocoles de futures perpétuels et un support pour les actifs RWA, les crypto-monnaies, les actions et les indices.","de":"Perfekt für Finanzanalyse-Agenten, die erweiterte Handelsfunktionen mit Perpetual-Futures-Protokollen und Unterstützung für RWA-Vermögenswerte, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise Financeira que necessitam de capacidades de negociação avançadas com protocolos de futuros perpétuos e suporte a ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices.","ru":"Идеально подходит для финансовых аналитических агентов, которым необходимы продвинутые торговые возможности с протоколами вечных фьючерсов и поддержкой активов RWA, криптовалют, акций и индексов.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل مالية تتطلب قدرات تداول متقدمة مع بروتوكولات المستقبل الدائم ودعم لأصول RWA والعملات المشفرة والأوراق المالية والمؤشرات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to facilitate leveraged long/short positions with up to 1000x collateralization, utilizing stablecoins and a central liquidity vault, while combining custom pricing mechanisms.","zh":"赋予代理人以最高1000倍的抵押能力，利用稳定币和集中流动性金库，同时结合自定义价格机制，实现杠杆长短仓位。","ja":"エージェントは、最大1000倍の担保能力でレバレッジの長短ポジションを実行できます。スターブルコインと集中式流動性金庫を利用し、カスタム価格メカニズムを組み合わせます。","ko":"에이전트에게 최대 1000배의 담보 능력을 제공하여 레버리지 롱/숏 포지션을 가능하게 하며, 스테이블코인과 集中적인 유동성 금고를 활용하여 커스텀 가격 메커니즘을 결합합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a facilitar posiciones largas/cortas apalancadas con hasta 1000 veces de colateralización, utilizando establescoins y un vault de liquidez central, mientras combina mecanismos de precios personalizados.","fr":"Permet aux agents de faciliter des positions longues/courtes à effet de levier avec jusqu''à 1000 fois de collateralisation, en utilisant des stablecoins et un vault de liquidité central, tout en combinant des mécanismes de tarification personnalisés.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, gehebelte Long-/Short-Positionen mit bis zu 1000-facher Collateralisierung zu ermöglichen, indem sie Stablecoins und einen zentralen Liquiditäts-Vault nutzen, während sie benutzerdefinierte Preisbildungsmechanismen kombinieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a facilitar posições longas/curtas alavancadas com até 1000x de collateralização, utilizando stablecoins e um cofre de liquidez central, combinando mecanismos de precificação personalizados.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью облегчать левериджные длинные/короткие позиции с до 1000-кратной залоговой стоимостью, используя стейблкоины и центральный хранилище ликвидности, объединяя пользовательские механизмы ценообразования.","ar":"تمكّن الوكالات من تسهيل مراكز طويلة/قصيرة معززة بحد أقصى 1000 ضعف الرهون، باستخدام العملات المستقرة وخزنة السيولة المركزية، مع دمج آليات تسعير مخصصة."},"useCases":{"en":["Executing high-leverage trades with stablecoin collateralization","Analyzing market trends for RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes","Optimizing trading strategies with custom pricing mechanisms"],"zh":["使用稳定币抵押执行高杠杆交易","分析RWA资产、加密货币、股票和指数的市场趋势","使用自定义价格机制优化交易策略"],"ja":["スターブルコイン担保による高レバレッジ取引の実行","RWAアセット、暗号通貨、株式、指数の市場動向分析","カスタム価格メカニズムを使用した取引戦略の最適化"],"ko":["스테이블코인 담보를 사용한 고레버리지 거래 실행","RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식, 지수의 시장 동향 분석","커스텀 가격 메커니즘을 사용한 거래 전략 최적화"],"es":["Ejecutar operaciones de trading de alto apalancamiento con colateralización de establescoins","Analizar tendencias del mercado para activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices","Optimizar estrategias de trading con mecanismos de precios personalizados"],"fr":["Exécuter des opérations de trading à effet de levier élevé avec une collateralisation de stablecoins","Analyser les tendances du marché pour les actifs RWA, les crypto-monnaies, les actions et les indices","Optimiser les stratégies de trading avec des mécanismes de tarification personnalisés"],"de":["Durchführen von Handelsgeschäften mit hohem Hebel mit Stablecoin-Besicherung","Analysieren von Markttrends für RWA-Vermögenswerte, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes","Optimieren von Handelsstrategien mit benutzerdefinierten Preisbildungsmechanismen"],"pt":["Executando operações de negociação com alavancagem alta com garantia de stablecoin","Analisando tendências de mercado para ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices","Otimizando estratégias de negociação com mecanismos de precificação personalizados"],"ru":["Выполнение операций с высоким левериджем с обеспечением стейблкоинов","Анализ тенденций рынка для активов RWA, криптовалют, акций и индексов","Оптимизация торговых стратегий с помощью пользовательских механизмов ценообразования"],"ar":["تنفيذ معاملات تداول عالية الرافعة المالية مع ضمان العملات المستقرة","تحليل اتجاهات السوق لأصول RWA والعملات المشفرة والأوراق المالية والمؤشرات","تحسين استراتيجيات التداول باستخدام آليات التسعير المخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires on-chain vault infrastructure","Limited to supported assets (RWA, crypto, stocks, indexes)","Dependent on central liquidity vault as counterparty"],"zh":["需要链上金库基础设施","仅限支持的资产（RWA、加密货币、股票、指数）","依赖于集中式流动性金库作为对手方"],"ja":["オンチェーン金庫インフラストラクチャが必要","サポートされているアセット（RWA、暗号通貨、株式、指数）に限定される","集中式流動性金庫を相手先として依存する"],"ko":["체인상 금고 인프라가 필요함","지원하는 자산(RWA, 암호화폐, 주식, 지수)로 제한됨","집중적인 유동성 금고를 상대방으로 의존함"],"es":["Requiere infraestructura de vault en cadena","Limitado a activos admitidos (RWA, criptomonedas, acciones, índices)","Dependiente del vault de liquidez central como contraparte"],"fr":["Nécessite une infrastructure de vault en chaîne","Limité aux actifs pris en charge (RWA, crypto-monnaies, actions, indices)","Dépendant du vault de liquidité central en tant que contrepartie"],"de":["Benötigt eine On-Chain-Vault-Infrastruktur","Begrenzt auf unterstützte Vermögenswerte (RWA, Kryptowährungen, Aktien, Indizes)","Abhängig vom zentralen Liquiditäts-Vault als Kontrahent"],"pt":["Exige infraestrutura de cofre em cadeia","Limitado a ativos suportados (RWA, criptomoedas, ações, índices)","Dependente do cofre de liquidez central como contraparte"],"ru":["Требует инфраструктуры хранилища в цепи","Ограничен поддерживаемыми активами (RWA, криптовалютами, акциями, индексами)","Зависит от центрального хранилища ликвидности как контрагента"],"ar":["يتطلب بنية تحتية لخزنة في سلسلة","محدود بأصول داعمة (RWA، العملات المشفرة، الأوراق المالية، المؤشرات)","يعتمد على خزنة السيولة المركزية كطرف مقابل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
