ons (up to 1000x) collater..."},"definition":{"en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"zh":["持久的代码理解","快速开发辅助","代码库模式学习","智能代码分析","开发支援"],"ja":["コードベースの理解を永続的に提供","迅速な開発支援","コードベースのパターンを学習","智能なコード分析","開発支援"],"ko":["코드베이스의 지속적인 이해"," 빠른 개발 지원","コードベース의 패턴을 학습","지능형 코드 분석","개발 지원"],"es":["Soporte para activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices","Posiciones largas/cortas apalancadas hasta 1000x","Oráculo personalizado para la fijación de precios","AMM virtual para la liquidación de trades","Suavizado TWAP para reducir la volatilidad"],"fr":["Prise en charge des actifs RWA, des cryptomonnaies, des actions et des indices","Positions longues/courtes avec effet de levier jusqu''à 1000x","Oracle personnalisé pour la fixation des prix","AMM virtuelle pour la liquidation des trades","Lissage TWAP pour réduire la volatilité"],"de":["Unterstützung für RWA-Assets, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes","Lang/kurze Positionen mit Hebelwirkung bis zu 1000x","Benutzerdefiniertes Orakel für die Preisfestlegung","Virtuelle AMM für die Liquidation von Trades","TWAP-Glättung zur Reduzierung der Volatilität"],"pt":["Suporte a ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices","Posições long/short alavancadas com até 1000x","Collateralização por stablecoins","Oráculo personalizado e AMM virtual","Suavização TWAP para preços estáveis"],"ru":["Поддержка активов RWA, криптовалют, акций и индексов","Левериджные длинные/короткие позиции с левериджем до 1000х","Обеспечение стейблкоинами","Индивидуальный оракул и виртуальный AMM","Сглаживание TWAP для стабильных цен"],"ar":["دعم أصول RWA والعملات المشفرة والأسهم والمؤشرات","مراكز طويلة/قصيرة مرفوعة مع رافعة مالية تصل إلى 1000 مرة","ضمانات من Stablecoins","أوراكل مخصص و AMM افتراضي","تسوية TWAP لأسعار مستقرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码库智能","持久代码理解","快速开发","代码分析","开发辅助","代码库模式学习"],"ja":["コードベースインテリジェンス","コードベースの理解を永続的に提供","迅速な開発","コード分析","開発支援","コードベースのパターンを学習"],"ko":["코드베이스 인텔리전스","코드베이스의 지속적인 이해","빠른 개발","코드 분석","개발 지원","코드베이스의 패턴을 학습"],"es":["inmemoria","futuros sintéticos","activos RWA","criptomonedas","acciones","índices","posiciones apalancadas","oráculo personalizado","AMM virtual","suavizado TWAP"],"fr":["inmemoria","futurs synthétiques","actifs RWA","cryptomonnaies","actions","indices","positions avec effet de levier","oracle personnalisé","AMM virtuelle","lissage TWAP"],"de":["inmemoria","synthetische Futures","RWA-Assets","Kryptowährungen","Aktien","Indizes","Positionen mit Hebelwirkung","benutzerdefiniertes Orakel","virtuelle AMM","TWAP-Glättung"],"pt":["futuros perpétuos","protocolo de futuros","ativos RWA","criptomoedas","ações","índices","alavancagem","stablecoins"],"ru":["вечные фьючерсы","протокол фьючерсов","активы RWA","криптовалюты","акции","индексы","леверидж","стейблкоины"],"ar":["مستقبلات دائمة","بروتوكول مستقبلات","أصول RWA","العملات المشفرة","الأسهم","المؤشرات","رافعة مالية","Stablecoins"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"inmemoria","description":"Use when building persistent codebase intelligence for AI agents or integrating knowledge systems via MCP","bodyPreview":"# In Memoria: Persistent Codebase Intelligence\n\n**In Memoria** is an MCP server that learns your codebase patterns once, then exposes that intelligence to AI agents persistently. Instead of re-analyzing code on every interaction, it maintains a semantic understanding of your architecture, conventions, and decisions.\n\n## Core Concept\n\nSetup → Learn → Verify → Serve. After that, AI agents query persistent intelligence without repeated parsing.\n\n## Quick Start (5 minutes)\n\n```bash\n# 1. Configure fo","body":"# In Memoria: Persistent Codebase Intelligence\n\n**In Memoria** is an MCP server that learns your codebase patterns once, then exposes that intelligence to AI agents persistently. Instead of re-analyzing code on every interaction, it maintains a semantic understanding of your architecture, conventions, and decisions.\n\n## Core Concept\n\nSetup → Learn → Verify → Serve. After that, AI agents query persistent intelligence without repeated parsing.\n\n## Quick Start (5 minutes)\n\n```bash\n# 1. Configure for your project\nnpx in-memoria setup --interactive\n\n# 2. Build intelligence database\nnpx in-memoria learn ./src\n\n# 3. Verify it worked\nnpx in-memoria check ./src --verbose\n\n# 4. Keep it fresh (optional but recommended)\nnpx in-memoria watch ./src\n\n# 5. Expose to agents via MCP\nnpx in-memoria server\n```\n\n## When to Use\n\n✅ **Use In Memoria:**\n- Building long-lived AI agent partnerships (Claude, Copilot, etc.)\n- Projects where consistency across sessions matters\n- Teams wanting shared codebase intelligence\n\n❌ **Skip it:**\n- One-off analysis (use `npx in-memoria analyze [path]` directly)\n- Simple projects agents can read directly\n\n## The 5 Core Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose | When |\n|---------|---------|------|\n| `setup --interactive` | Configure exclusions, paths, preferences | First time only |\n| `learn [path]` | Build/rebuild intelligence database | After setup, major refactors |\n| `check [path]` | Validate intelligence layer | After learn, before server |\n| `watch [path]` | Auto-update intelligence on code changes | During development (optional) |\n| `server` | Start MCP server for agent queries | After check passes |\n\n**Key difference:** `learn` builds persistent knowledge. `analyze` is one-time reporting only.\n\n## What Agents See\n\nWhen connected, agents can query:\n- **Project structure** - Tech stack, entry points, architecture\n- **Code patterns** - Your naming conventions, error handling, patterns used\n- **Smart routing** - \"Add password reset\" → suggests `src/auth/password-reset.ts`\n- **Semantic search** - Find code by meaning, not keywords\n- **Work context** - Track decisions, tasks, approach consistency\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n| Issue | Fix |\n|-------|-----|\n| Learn fails | Verify path is correct; check file permissions |\n| Check reports missing intelligence | Run `learn [path]` again |\n| Agent doesn''t see new code | Is `watch` running? Start it: `npx in-memoria watch ./src` |\n| Server won''t start | Run `check --verbose` first; if issues, rebuild: `rm .in-memoria/*.db && npx in-memoria learn ./src` |\n| Multiple projects conflict | Use `server --port 3001` (or different port per project) |\n\n## Performance Notes\n\n- **Small projects** (<1K files): 5-15s to learn\n- **Medium** (1K-10K files): 30-60s\n- **Large** (10K+ files): 2-5min\n\nIf learning stalls (>10min), verify you''re not indexing `node_modules/`, `dist/`, or build artifacts—use setup''s exclusion patterns.\n\n## Key Principles\n\n1. **Local-first** - Everything stays on your machine; no telemetry\n2. **Persistent** - One learning pass; intelligence updates incrementally with `watch`\n3. **Agent-native** - Designed for MCP; works with Claude, Copilot, and any MCP-compatible tool\n4. **Pattern-based** - Learns from your actual code, not rules you define\n\n## Deployment Pattern (3 terminals)\n\n```bash\n# Terminal 1: One-time setup\nnpx in-memoria setup --interactive\nnpx in-memoria learn ./src\nnpx in-memoria check ./src --verbose\n\n# Terminal 2: Keep intelligence fresh\nnpx in-memoria watch ./src\n\n# Terminal 3: Expose to agents\nnpx in-memoria server\n\n# Now agents (Claude, Copilot, etc.) have persistent codebase context\n```\n\nSee [GitHub](https://github.com/pi22by7/In-Memoria) for full API docs and agent integration examples.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:15:38.010Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing persistent semantic understanding of complex codebases.","zh":"非常适合需要对复杂代码库进行持久性语义理解的代码分析代理。","ja":"複雑なコードベースの永続的な意味的理解が必要なコード分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"복잡한 코드베이스에 대한 지속적인 의미적 이해가 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis de Código que necesitan una comprensión semántica persistente de bases de código complejas.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents d''Analyse de Code nécessitant une compréhension sémantique persistante de bases de code complexes.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die ein persistentes semantisches Verständnis komplexer Codebasen benötigen.","pt":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing persistent semantic understanding of complex codebases.","ru":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing persistent semantic understanding of complex codebases.","ar":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing persistent semantic understanding of complex codebases."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to query persistent architectural intelligence without repeated code parsing. The MCP server learns codebase patterns once through Setup → Learn → Verify → Serve workflow, then exposes semantic understanding of architecture, conventions, and decisions to AI agents.","zh":"使代理能够在无需重复代码解析的情况下查询持久的架构智能。MCP服务器通过设置→学习→验证→服务工作流一次学习代码库模式，然后向AI代理暴露对架构、约定和决策的语义理解。","ja":"エージェントが繰り返しのコード解析を必要とせずに永続的なアーキテクチャの知識にアクセスできるようにします。MCPサーバーはSetup → Learn → Verify → Serveワークフローを通じてコードベースのパターンを一度学習し、その後アーキテクチャ、約束、決定についての语义的理解をAIエージェントに公開します。","ko":"에이전트가 반복적인 코드 파싱 없이 지속적인 아키텍처 지능에 질의할 수 있도록 합니다. MCP 서버는 설정 → 학습 → 검증 → 제공 워크플로를 통해 코드베이스 패턴을一度 학습한 후 아키텍처, 규약 및 결정에 대한 의미적 이해를 AI 에이전트에 노출합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes consultar inteligencia arquitectónica persistente sin necesidad de analizar el código repetidamente. El servidor MCP aprende los patrones de la base de código una vez mediante el flujo de trabajo Configurar → Aprender → Verificar → Servir, y luego expone la comprensión semántica de la arquitectura, convenciones y decisiones a los agentes de IA.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''interroger une intelligence architecturale persistante sans avoir à analyser le code de manière répétée. Le serveur MCP apprend les modèles de la base de code une fois via le workflow Configurer → Apprendre → Vérifier → Servir, puis expose la compréhension sémantique de l''architecture, des conventions et des décisions aux agents IA.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, persistente architektonische Intelligenz abzufragen, ohne den Code wiederholt parsen zu müssen. Der MCP-Server lernt die Codebase-Muster einmal durch den Setup → Learn → Verify → Serve-Workflow und macht dann das semantische Verständnis von Architektur, Konventionen und Entscheidungen für KI-Agents zugänglich.","pt":"Enables agents to query persistent architectural intelligence without repeated code parsing. The MCP server learns codebase patterns once through Setup → Learn → Verify → Serve workflow, then exposes semantic understanding of architecture, conventions, and decisions to AI agents.","ru":"Enables agents to query persistent architectural intelligence without repeated code parsing. The MCP server learns codebase patterns once through Setup → Learn → Verify → Serve workflow, then exposes semantic understanding of architecture, conventions, and decisions to AI agents.","ar":"Enables agents to query persistent architectural intelligence without repeated code parsing. The MCP server learns codebase patterns once through Setup → Learn → Verify → Serve workflow, then exposes semantic understanding of architecture, conventions, and decisions to AI agents."},"useCases":{"en":["Accelerating codebase onboarding for new agents","Maintaining architectural consistency across multiple sessions","Providing persistent context for refactoring decisions","Semantic code search across learned patterns"],"zh":["加速新代理的代码库入门","在多个会话中保持架构的一致性","为重构决策提供持久的上下文","在学习的模式中进行语义代码搜索"],"ja":["新しいエージェントのコードベースのオンボーディングを加速する","複数のセッションでアーキテクチャの一貫性を維持する","リファクタリングの決定に持続的なコンテキストを提供する","学習したパターンで语义的コード検索を行う"],"ko":["새 에이전트의 코드베이스 온보딩을 가속화하는 것","여러 세션에서 아키텍처 일관성을 유지하는 것","리팩토링 결정에 대한 지속적인 contexto를 제공하는 것","학습된 패턴에서 의미 코드 검색을 수행하는 것"],"es":["Acelerar la incorporación de nuevas bases de código para nuevos agentes","Mantener la coherencia arquitectónica en múltiples sesiones","Proporcionar contexto persistente para decisiones de refactorización","Búsqueda de código semántica en patrones aprendidos"],"fr":["Accélérer l''intégration à la base de code pour les nouveaux agents","Maintenir la cohérence architecturale sur plusieurs sessions","Fournir un contexte persistant pour les décisions de refactorisation","Recherche sémantique de code parmi les modèles appris"],"de":["Beschleunigung des Onboardings für neue Codebasen bei neuen Agents","Aufrechterhaltung der architektonischen Konsistenz über mehrere Sitzungen hinweg","Bereitstellung eines persistenten Kontexts für Refactoring-Entscheidungen","Semantische Codesuche über gelernte Muster"],"pt":["Accelerating codebase onboarding for new agents","Maintaining architectural consistency across multiple sessions","Providing persistent context for refactoring decisions","Semantic code search across learned patterns"],"ru":["Accelerating codebase onboarding for new agents","Maintaining architectural consistency across multiple sessions","Providing persistent context for refactoring decisions","Semantic code search across learned patterns"],"ar":["Accelerating codebase onboarding for new agents","Maintaining architectural consistency across multiple sessions","Providing persistent context for refactoring decisions","Semantic code search across learned patterns"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires initial setup and learning phase","Dependent on MCP server architecture","Needs codebase access for initial learning"],"zh":["需要初始设置和学习阶段","依赖于MCP服务器架构","需要代码库访问以进行初始学习"],"ja":["初期設定と学習段階が必要","MCPサーバーのアーキテクチャに依存する","初期学習のためのコードベースへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["초기 설정 및 학습 단계가 필요함","MCP 서버 아키텍처에 의존함","초기 학습을 위한 코드베이스 접근이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere una fase inicial de configuración y aprendizaje","Depende de la arquitectura del servidor MCP","Necesita acceso a la base de código para el aprendizaje inicial"],"fr":["Nécessite une phase initiale de configuration et d''apprentissage","Dépend de l''architecture du serveur MCP","Nécessite un accès à la base de code pour l''apprentissage initial"],"de":["Erfordert eine anfängliche Setup- und Lernphase","Abhängig von der MCP-Server-Architektur","Benötigt Codebase-Zugriff für das anfängliche Lernen"],"pt":["Requires initial setup and learning phase","Dependent on MCP server architecture","Needs codebase access for initial learning"],"ru":["Requires initial setup and learning phase","Dependent on MCP server architecture","Needs codebase access for initial learning"],"ar":["Requires initial setup and learning phase","Dependent on MCP server architecture","Needs codebase access for initial learning"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ollieb89/ugro/workflow-orchestration-patterns', 'community', 'ollieb89', 'ugro', 'ollieb89/ugro', 'workflow-orchestration-patterns', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:15:32.122Z', NULL, '{"id":"ollieb89/ugro/workflow-orchestration-patterns","name":"workflow-orchestration-patterns","description":{"zh":"工作流编排模式是用于构建可靠分布式系统的技术，包括基础设计决策、弹性模式和最佳实践","ja":"ワークフロー オーケストレーション パターンは、信頼性の高い分散システムを構築するための技術であり、基本的な設計決定、リサイタンス パターン、ベスト プラクティスを含む","ko":"워크플로우 오케스트레이션 패턴은 안정적인 분산 시스템을 구축하기 위한 기술로, 기본 설계 결정, 복원力 패턴 및 최선의 관행을 포함","es":"El proyecto de patrones de orquestación de flujo de trabajo permite transformar máquinas GPU independientes en un sistema de cómputo de alto rendimiento","fr":"Le projet de modèles d''orchestration de flux de travail permet de transformer des machines GPU indépendantes en un système de calcul haute performance","de":"Das Projekt für die Orchestrierung von Workflows ermöglicht es, unabhängige GPU-Maschinen in ein Hochleistungsrechnersystem zu verwandeln","pt":"Este projeto ensina arquitetura de orquestração de workflows usando Temporal. Abrange decisões de design fundamentais, padrões de resiliência e melhores práticas para construir sistemas distribuídos confiáveis para treinamento e inferência.","ru":"Этот проект обучает архитектуре оркестрации рабочих процессов с использованием Temporal. Рассматривает ключевые архитектурные решения, паттерны отказоустойчивости и лучшие практики для создания надежных распределенных систем.","ar":"يهدف هذا المشروع إلى تعليم هندسة أوركسترة سير العمل باستخدام Temporal. يغطي قرارات التصميم الأساسية، أنماط المرونة، وأفضل الممارسات لبناء أنظمة موزعة موثوقة.","en":"This project aims to transform a small set of independently managed GPU machines into a **single, cohesive, high-power compute system** that can be dynamically orchestrated for **distributed training**, **advanced inference**, and **developer workflows**."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"工作流编排模式","ja":"ワークフロー オーケストレーション パターン","ko":"워크플로우 오케스트레이션 패턴","es":"Patrones de Orquestación de Flujo de Trabajo","fr":"Modèles d''Orchestration de Flux de Travail","de":"Muster für die Orchestrierung von Workflows","pt":"Padrões de Orquestração de Workflow com Temporal para Devs","ru":"Паттерны Оркестрации Рабочих Процессов с Temporal для Раз...","ar":"أنماط أوركسترة سير العمل باستخدام Temporal للمطورين","en":"workflow-orchestration-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"工作流编排模式是用于构建可靠分布式系统的技术，包括基础设计决策、弹性模式和最佳实践","ja":"ワークフロー オーケストレーション パターンは、信頼性の高い分散システムを構築するための技術であり、基本的な設計決定、リサイタンス パターン、ベスト プラクティスを含む","ko":"워크플로우 오케스트레이션 패턴은 안정적인 분산 시스템을 구축하기 위한 기술로, 기본 설계 결정, 복원力 패턴 및 최선의 관행을 포함","es":"El proyecto de patrones de orquestación de flujo de trabajo permite transformar máquinas GPU independientes en un sistema de cómputo de alto rendimiento","fr":"Le projet de modèles d''orchestration de flux de travail permet de transformer des machines GPU indépendantes en un système de calcul haute performance","de":"Das Projekt für die Orchestrierung von Workflows ermöglicht es, unabhängige GPU-Maschinen in ein Hochleistungsrechnersystem zu verwandeln","pt":"Este projeto ensina arquitetura de orquestração de workflows usando Temporal. Abrange decisões de design fundamentais, padrões de resiliência e melhores prát...","ru":"Этот проект обучает архитектуре оркестрации рабочих процессов с использованием Temporal. Рассматривает ключевые архитектурные решения, паттерны отказоустойчи...","ar":"يهدف هذا المشروع إلى تعليم هندسة أوركسترة سير العمل باستخدام Temporal. يغطي قرارات التصميم الأساسية، أنماط المرونة، وأفضل الممارسات لبناء أنظمة موزعة موثوقة.","en":"This project aims to transform a small set of independently managed GPU machines into a **single, cohesive, high-power compute system** that can be dynamical..."},"definition":{"en":"This project aims to transform a small set of independently managed GPU machines into a **single, cohesive, high-power compute system** that can be dynamically orchestrated for **distributed training**, **advanced inference**, and **developer workflows**."},"features":{"zh":["支持分布式训练","支持高级推理","支持开发者工作流","提供弹性模式","提供最佳实践","支持多步骤过程"],"ja":["分散トレーニングのサポート","高度な推論のサポート","開発者ワークフローのサポート","リサイタンス パターンの提供","ベスト プラクティスの提供","マルチステップ プロセスのサポート"],"ko":["분산 트레이닝 지원","고급 추론 지원","개발자 워크플로우 지원","복원력 패턴 제공","최선의 관행 제공","멀티스텝 프로세스 지원"],"es":["Diseño de arquitectura de orquestación de flujo de trabajo","Patrones de resiliencia para sistemas distribuidos","Mejoras para la creación de sistemas de cómputo de alto rendimiento","Orquestación dinámica para entrenamiento distribuido y inferencia avanzada","Integración con Temporal para una orquestación de flujo de trabajo eficiente"],"fr":["Conception d''architecture d''orchestration de flux de travail","Modèles de résilience pour les systèmes distribués","Améliorations pour la création de systèmes de calcul haute performance","Orchestration dynamique pour la formation distribuée et l''inférence avancée","Intégration avec Temporal pour une orchestration de flux de travail efficace"],"de":["Entwurf einer Orchestrierungsarchitektur für Workflows","Muster für die Resilienz in verteilten Systemen","Verbesserungen für die Erstellung von Hochleistungsrechnersystemen","Dynamische Orchestrierung für verteiltes Training und fortschrittliche Inferenz","Integration mit Temporal für eine effiziente Workflows-Orchestrierung"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de processos de múltiplas etapas","Suporte a transações distribuídas (semântica all-or-nothing)","Workflows de longa duração (horas a anos)","Persistência automática de estado","Padrões de resiliência e recuperação de falhas","Arquitetura para sistemas distribuídos confiáveis"],"ru":["Управление многоэтапными процессами","Поддержка распределенных транзакций (семантика \"все или ничего\")","Долгосрочные рабочие процессы (часы至годы)","Автоматическое сохранение состояния","Паттерны отказоустойчивости и восстановления","Архитектура надежных распределенных систем"],"ar":["إدارة العمليات متعددة المراحل","دعم المعاملات الموزعة (دلالات الكل أو لا شيء)","سير عمل طويلة الأمد (ساعات إلى سنوات)","استمرارية الحالة التلقائية","أنماط المرونة واستعادة الأخطاء","هندسة لأنظمة موزعة موثوقة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["工作流编排","分布式系统","弹性模式","最佳实践","分布式训练","高级推理","开发者工作流"],"ja":["ワークフロー オーケストレーション","分散システム","リサイタンス パターン","ベスト プラクティス","分散トレーニング","高度な推論","開発者ワークフロー"],"ko":["워크플로우 오케스트레이션","분산 시스템","복원력 패턴","최선의 관행","분산 트레이닝","고급 추론","개발자 워크플로우"],"es":["orquestación de flujo de trabajo","sistemas distribuidos","Temporal","diseño de arquitectura","patrones de resiliencia","entrenamiento distribuido","inferencia avanzada"],"fr":["orchestration de flux de travail","systèmes distribués","Temporal","conception d''architecture","modèles de résilience","formation distribuée","inférence avancée"],"de":["Orchestrierung von Workflows","verteilte Systeme","Temporal","Entwurf einer Architektur","Muster für die Resilienz","verteiltes Training","fortschrittliche Inferenz"],"pt":["orquestração de workflow temporal","sistemas distribuídos confiáveis","transações distribuídas","workflow de longa duração","padrões de resiliência","temporal io","arquitetura de orquestração","processos multi-step"],"ru":["оркестрация рабочих процессов temporal","надежные распределенные системы","распределенные транзакции","долгосрочные рабочие процессы","паттерны отказоустойчивости","temporal io","архитектура оркестрации","многоэтапные процессы"],"ar":["أوركسترة سير العمل temporal","أنظمة موزعة موثوقة","معاملات موزعة","سير عمل طويلة الأمد","أنماط المرونة","temporal io","هندسة الأوركسترة","عمليات متعددة المراحل"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"ugro","repoPath":"ollieb89/ugro","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"workflow-orchestration-patterns","description":"Design durable workflows with Temporal for distributed systems. Covers workflow vs activity separation, saga patterns, state management, and determinism constraints. Use when building long-running processes, distributed transactions, or microservice orchestration.","bodyPreview":"# Workflow Orchestration Patterns\n\nMaster workflow orchestration architecture with Temporal, covering fundamental design decisions, resilience patterns, and best practices for building reliable distributed systems.\n\n## When to Use Workflow Orchestration\n\n### Ideal Use Cases (Source: docs.temporal.io)\n\n- **Multi-step processes** spanning machines/services/databases\n- **Distributed transactions** requiring all-or-nothing semantics\n- **Long-running workflows** (hours to years) with automatic state","body":"# Workflow Orchestration Patterns\n\nMaster workflow orchestration architecture with Temporal, covering fundamental design decisions, resilience patterns, and best practices for building reliable distributed systems.\n\n## When to Use Workflow Orchestration\n\n### Ideal Use Cases (Source: docs.temporal.io)\n\n- **Multi-step processes** spanning machines/services/databases\n- **Distributed transactions** requiring all-or-nothing semantics\n- **Long-running workflows** (hours to years) with automatic state persistence\n- **Failure recovery** that must resume from last successful step\n- **Business processes**: bookings, orders, campaigns, approvals\n- **Entity lifecycle management**: inventory tracking, account management, cart workflows\n- **Infrastructure automation**: CI/CD pipelines, provisioning, deployments\n- **Human-in-the-loop** systems requiring timeouts and escalations\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n- Simple CRUD operations (use direct API calls)\n- Pure data processing pipelines (use Airflow, batch processing)\n- Stateless request/response (use standard APIs)\n- Real-time streaming (use Kafka, event processors)\n\n## Critical Design Decision: Workflows vs Activities\n\n**The Fundamental Rule** (Source: temporal.io/blog/workflow-engine-principles):\n- **Workflows** = Orchestration logic and decision-making\n- **Activities** = External interactions (APIs, databases, network calls)\n\n### Workflows (Orchestration)\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- Contain business logic and coordination\n- **MUST be deterministic** (same inputs → same outputs)\n- **Cannot** perform direct external calls\n- State automatically preserved across failures\n- Can run for years despite infrastructure failures\n\n**Example workflow tasks:**\n- Decide which steps to execute\n- Handle compensation logic\n- Manage timeouts and retries\n- Coordinate child workflows\n\n### Activities (External Interactions)\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- Handle all external system interactions\n- Can be non-deterministic (API calls, DB writes)\n- Include built-in timeouts and retry logic\n- **Must be idempotent** (calling N times = calling once)\n- Short-lived (seconds to minutes typically)\n\n**Example activity tasks:**\n- Call payment gateway API\n- Write to database\n- Send emails or notifications\n- Query external services\n\n### Design Decision Framework\n\n```\nDoes it touch external systems? → Activity\nIs it orchestration/decision logic? → Workflow\n```\n\n## Core Workflow Patterns\n\n### 1. Saga Pattern with Compensation\n\n**Purpose**: Implement distributed transactions with rollback capability\n\n**Pattern** (Source: temporal.io/blog/compensating-actions-part-of-a-complete-breakfast-with-sagas):\n\n```\nFor each step:\n  1. Register compensation BEFORE executing\n  2. Execute the step (via activity)\n  3. On failure, run all compensations in reverse order (LIFO)\n```\n\n**Example: Payment Workflow**\n1. Reserve inventory (compensation: release inventory)\n2. Charge payment (compensation: refund payment)\n3. Fulfill order (compensation: cancel fulfillment)\n\n**Critical Requirements:**\n- Compensations must be idempotent\n- Register compensation BEFORE executing step\n- Run compensations in reverse order\n- Handle partial failures gracefully\n\n### 2. Entity Workflows (Actor Model)\n\n**Purpose**: Long-lived workflow representing single entity instance\n\n**Pattern** (Source: docs.temporal.io/evaluate/use-cases-design-patterns):\n- One workflow execution = one entity (cart, account, inventory item)\n- Workflow persists for entity lifetime\n- Receives signals for state changes\n- Supports queries for current state\n\n**Example Use Cases:**\n- Shopping cart (add items, checkout, expiration)\n- Bank account (deposits, withdrawals, balance checks)\n- Product inventory (stock updates, reservations)\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Encapsulates entity behavior\n- Guarantees consistency per entity\n- Natural event sourcing\n\n### 3. Fan-Out/Fan-In (Parallel Execution)\n\n**Purpose**: Execute multiple tasks in parallel, aggregate results\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Spawn child workflows or parallel activities\n- Wait for all to complete\n- Aggregate results\n- Handle partial failures\n\n**Scaling Rule** (Source: temporal.io/blog/workflow-engine-principles):\n- Don''t scale individual workflows\n- For 1M tasks: spawn 1K child workflows × 1K tasks each\n- Keep each workflow bounded\n\n### 4. Async Callback Pattern\n\n**Purpose**: Wait for external event or human approval\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Workflow sends request and waits for signal\n- External system processes asynchronously\n- Sends signal to resume workflow\n- Workflow continues with response\n\n**Use Cases:**\n- Human approval workflows\n- Webhook callbacks\n- Long-running external processes\n\n## State Management and Determinism\n\n### Automatic State Preservation\n\n**How Temporal Works** (Source: docs.temporal.io/workflows):\n- Complete program state preserved automatically\n- Event History records every command and event\n- Seamless recovery from crashes\n- Applications restore pre-failure state\n\n### Determinism Constraints\n\n**Workflows Execute as State Machines**:\n- Replay behavior must be consistent\n- Same inputs → identical outputs every time\n\n**Prohibited in Workflows** (Source: docs.temporal.io/workflows):\n- ❌ Threading, locks, synchronization primitives\n- ❌ Random number generation (`random()`)\n- ❌ Global state or static variables\n- ❌ System time (`datetime.now()`)\n- ❌ Direct file I/O or network calls\n- ❌ Non-deterministic libraries\n\n**Allowed in Workflows**:\n- ✅ `workflow.now()` (deterministic time)\n- ✅ `workflow.random()` (deterministic random)\n- ✅ Pure functions and calculations\n- ✅ Calling activities (non-deterministic operations)\n\n### Versioning Strategies\n\n**Challenge**: Changing workflow code while old executions still running\n\n**Solutions**:\n1. **Versioning API**: Use `workflow.get_version()` for safe changes\n2. **New Workflow Type**: Create new workflow, route new executions to it\n3. **Backward Compatibility**: Ensure old events replay correctly\n\n## Resilience and Error Handling\n\n### Retry Policies\n\n**Default Behavior**: Temporal retries activities forever\n\n**Configure Retry**:\n- Initial retry interval\n- Backoff coefficient (exponential backoff)\n- Maximum interval (cap retry delay)\n- Maximum attempts (eventually fail)\n\n**Non-Retryable Errors**:\n- Invalid input (validation failures)\n- Business rule violations\n- Permanent failures (resource not found)\n\n### Idempotency Requirements\n\n**Why Critical** (Source: docs.temporal.io/activities):\n- Activities may execute multiple times\n- Network failures trigger retries\n- Duplicate execution must be safe\n\n**Implementation Strategies**:\n- Idempotency keys (deduplication)\n- Check-then-act with unique constraints\n- Upsert operations instead of insert\n- Track processed request IDs\n\n### Activity Heartbeats\n\n**Purpose**: Detect stalled long-running activities\n\n**Pattern**:\n- Activity sends periodic heartbeat\n- Includes progress information\n- Timeout if no heartbeat received\n- Enables progress-based retry\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Workflow Design\n\n1. **Keep workflows focused** - Single responsibility per workflow\n2. **Small workflows** - Use child workflows for scalability\n3. **Clear boundaries** - Workflow orchestrates, activities execute\n4. **Test locally** - Use time-skipping test environment\n\n### Activity Design\n\n1. **Idempotent operations** - Safe to retry\n2. **Short-lived** - Seconds to minutes, not hours\n3. **Timeout configuration** - Always set timeouts\n4. **Heartbeat for long tasks** - Report progress\n5. **Error handling** - Distinguish retryable vs non-retryable\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n\n**Workflow Violations**:\n- Using `datetime.now()` instead of `workflow.now()`\n- Threading or async operations in workflow code\n- Calling external APIs directly from workflow\n- Non-deterministic logic in workflows\n\n**Activity Mistakes**:\n- Non-idempotent operations (can''t handle retries)\n- Missing timeouts (activities run forever)\n- No error classification (retry validation errors)\n- Ignoring payload limits (2MB per argument)\n\n### Operational Considerations\n\n**Monitoring**:\n- Workflow execution duration\n- Activity failure rates\n- Retry attempts and backoff\n- Pending workflow counts\n\n**Scalability**:\n- Horizontal scaling with workers\n- Task queue partitioning\n- Child workflow decomposition\n- Activity batching when appropriate\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n**Official Documentation**:\n- Temporal Core Concepts: docs.temporal.io/workflows\n- Workflow Patterns: docs.temporal.io/evaluate/use-cases-design-patterns\n- Best Practices: docs.temporal.io/develop/best-practices\n- Saga Pattern: temporal.io/blog/saga-pattern-made-easy\n\n**Key Principles**:\n1. Workflows = orchestration, Activities = external calls\n2. Determinism is non-negotiable for workflows\n3. Idempotency is critical for activities\n4. State preservation is automatic\n5. Design for failure and recovery\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:15:32.122Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Distributed System Agents requiring advanced workflow orchestration and Temporal architecture expertise.","zh":"非常适合需要高级工作流编排和 Temporal 架构专业知识的分布式系统代理。","ja":"高度なワークフローオーケストレーションとTemporalアーキテクチャの専門知識を必要とする分散システムエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 워크플로 오케스트레이션 및 Temporal 아키텍처 전문 지식이 필요한 분산 시스템 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de sistemas distribuidos que requieren orquestación avanzada de flujos de trabajo y experiencia en arquitectura Temporal.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de systèmes distribués nécessitant une orchestration avancée de flux de travail et une expertise en architecture Temporal.","de":"Ideal für Agenten in verteilten Systemen, die eine erweiterte Workflow-Orchestrierung und Expertise in der Temporal-Architektur erfordern.","pt":"Ideal for Distributed System Agents requiring advanced workflow orchestration and Temporal architecture expertise.","ru":"Ideal for Distributed System Agents requiring advanced workflow orchestration and Temporal architecture expertise.","ar":"Ideal for Distributed System Agents requiring advanced workflow orchestration and Temporal architecture expertise."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to master workflow orchestration patterns using Temporal, enabling the design of resilient distributed systems with multi-step processes, distributed transactions, and long-running workflows, all while leveraging best practices for reliability and scalability.","zh":"使代理能够掌握使用 Temporal 的工作流编排模式，从而设计具有多步骤流程、分布式事务和长时间运行工作流的弹性分布式系统，同时利用可靠性和可扩展性的最佳实践。","ja":"Temporalを使用したワークフローオーケストレーションパターンを習得することで、マルチステッププロセス、分散トランザクション、長時間実行ワークフローを備えた回復力のある分散システムを設計できるようになり、信頼性と拡張性のベストプラクティスをすべて活用できます。","ko":"Temporal을 사용한 워크플로 오케스트레이션 패턴을 숙달하여 다단계 프로세스, 분산 트랜잭션 및 장기 실행 워크플로를 갖춘 복원력 있는 분산 시스템을 설계할 수 있도록 하며, 신뢰성과 확장성에 대한 모범 사례를 모두 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes dominar los patrones de orquestación de flujos de trabajo utilizando Temporal, facilitando el diseño de sistemas distribuidos resilientes con procesos de múltiples pasos, transacciones distribuidas y flujos de trabajo de larga duración, todo ello aprovechando las mejores prácticas para la confiabilidad y la escalabilidad.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maîtriser les modèles d''orchestration de flux de travail en utilisant Temporal, permettant la conception de systèmes distribués résilients avec des processus à plusieurs étapes, des transactions distribuées et des flux de travail de longue durée, le tout en tirant parti des meilleures pratiques pour la fiabilité et l''évolutivité.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Workflow-Orchestrierungsmuster mit Temporal zu beherrschen, was den Entwurf robuster verteilter Systeme mit mehrstufigen Prozessen, verteilten Transaktionen und langlaufenden Workflows ermöglicht, unter gleichzeitiger Nutzung von Best Practices für Zuverlässigkeit und Skalierbarkeit.","pt":"Empowers agents to master workflow orchestration patterns using Temporal, enabling the design of resilient distributed systems with multi-step processes, distributed transactions, and long-running workflows, all while leveraging best practices for reliability and scalability.","ru":"Empowers agents to master workflow orchestration patterns using Temporal, enabling the design of resilient distributed systems with multi-step processes, distributed transactions, and long-running workflows, all while leveraging best practices for reliability and scalability.","ar":"Empowers agents to master workflow orchestration patterns using Temporal, enabling the design of resilient distributed systems with multi-step processes, distributed transactions, and long-running workflows, all while leveraging best practices for reliability and scalability."},"useCases":{"en":["Orchestrating distributed training workflows across multiple GPU machines","Managing advanced inference pipelines with automatic state handling","Implementing reliable developer workflows with all-or-nothing semantics"],"zh":["跨多个 GPU 机器编排分布式训练工作流","通过自动状态处理管理高级推理管道","使用全有或全无语义实现可靠的开发人员工作流"],"ja":["複数のGPUマシンにわたる分散トレーニングワークフローのオーケストレーション","自動状態処理による高度な推論パイプラインの管理","オールオアナッシングセマンティクスによる信頼性の高い開発者ワークフローの実装"],"ko":["다중 GPU 머신에서 분산 학습 워크플로 오케스트레이션","자동 상태 처리로 고급 추론 파이프라인 관리","전부 혹은 전무(all-or-nothing) 의미론으로 신뢰할 수 있는 개발자 워크플로 구현"],"es":["Orquestación de flujos de trabajo de entrenamiento distribuido en múltiples máquinas con GPU","Gestión de pipelines de inferencia avanzada con manejo automático del estado","Implementación de flujos de trabajo confiables para desarrolladores con semántica de todo o nada"],"fr":["Orchestration de flux de travail de formation distribuée sur plusieurs machines GPU","Gestion de pipelines d''inférence avancés avec gestion automatique de l''état","Mise en œuvre de flux de travail de développement fiables avec sémantique de tout ou rien"],"de":["Orchestrierung verteilter Trainings-Workflows über mehrere GPU-Maschinen hinweg","Verwaltung erweiterter Inferenz-Pipelines mit automatischer Zustandsverwaltung","Implementierung zuverlässiger Entwickler-Workflows mit Alles-oder-Nichts-Semantik"],"pt":["Orchestrating distributed training workflows across multiple GPU machines","Managing advanced inference pipelines with automatic state handling","Implementing reliable developer workflows with all-or-nothing semantics"],"ru":["Orchestrating distributed training workflows across multiple GPU machines","Managing advanced inference pipelines with automatic state handling","Implementing reliable developer workflows with all-or-nothing semantics"],"ar":["Orchestrating distributed training workflows across multiple GPU machines","Managing advanced inference pipelines with automatic state handling","Implementing reliable developer workflows with all-or-nothing semantics"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Temporal workflow orchestration architecture","Designed for distributed systems and may not be suitable for single-machine workflows"],"zh":["需要 Temporal 工作流编排架构","专为分布式系统设计，可能不适用于单机工作流"],"ja":["Temporalワークフローオーケストレーションアーキテクチャが必要","分散システム向けに設計されており、単一マシンのワークフローには適さない可能性がある"],"ko":["Temporal 워크플로 오케스트레이션 아키텍처 필요","분산 시스템용으로 설계되어 단일 머신 워크플로에는 적합하지 않을 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere una arquitectura de orquestación de flujos de trabajo Temporal","Diseñado para sistemas distribuidos y puede no ser adecuado para flujos de trabajo de máquina única"],"fr":["Nécessite une architecture d''orchestration de flux de travail Temporal","Conçu pour les systèmes distribués et peut ne pas convenir aux flux de travail sur machine unique"],"de":["Erfordert eine Temporal-Workflow-Orchestrierungsarchitektur","Für verteilte Systeme konzipiert und möglicherweise nicht für Single-Machine-Workflows geeignet"],"pt":["Requires Temporal workflow orchestration architecture","Designed for distributed systems and may not be suitable for single-machine workflows"],"ru":["Requires Temporal workflow orchestration architecture","Designed for distributed systems and may not be suitable for single-machine workflows"],"ar":["Requires Temporal workflow orchestration architecture","Designed for distributed systems and may not be suitable for single-machine workflows"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
