time","Compatibilité avec AG-UI","Accès à des ressources techniques et des guides","Support pour la configuration personnalisée"],"de":["Konfiguration von AI SDK v6","Konfiguration von LangGraph","Verwendung von useLocalRuntime und useExternalStoreRuntime","Kompatibilität mit AG-UI","Zugriff auf technische Ressourcen und Anleitungen","Unterstützung für die benutzerdefinierte Konfiguration"],"pt":["Configuração de API","Integração com AI SDK v6","Suporte a LangGraph","Opção de uso de backend personalizado","Compatibilidade com AG-UI"],"ru":["Настройка API","Интеграция с AI SDK v6","Поддержка LangGraph","Возможность использования собственного бэкенда","Совместимость с AG-UI"],"ar":["إعداد API","دمج مع AI SDK v6","دعم LangGraph","خيار استخدام خلفية مخصصة","توافق مع AG-UI"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI Setup","AI 代理","AI SDK","LangGraph","自定义后端","AG-UI","人工智能","AI 开发"],"ja":["AI セットアップ","AI エージェント","AI SDK","LangGraph","カスタム バックエンド","AG-UI","人工知能","AI 開発"],"ko":["AI 설정","AI 에이전트","AI SDK","LangGraph","사용자 정의 백엔드","AG-UI","인공 지능","AI 개발"],"es":["setup para desarrolladores","configuración de AI SDK","LangGraph","useLocalRuntime","useExternalStoreRuntime","AG-UI","desarrollo de aplicaciones","configuración de sistemas"],"fr":["setup pour développeurs","configuration de l''AI SDK","LangGraph","useLocalRuntime","useExternalStoreRuntime","AG-UI","développement d''applications","configuration de systèmes"],"de":["Setup-Konfiguration für Entwickler","Konfiguration von AI SDK","LangGraph","useLocalRuntime","useExternalStoreRuntime","AG-UI","Anwendungsentwicklung","Systemkonfiguration"],"pt":["setup para desenvolvedores","configuração de API","integração de AI","desenvolvimento de projetos","tecnologias de inteligência artificial","AI SDK v6","LangGraph","backend personalizado"],"ru":["настройка setup для разработчиков","конфигурация API","интеграция ИИ","разработка проектов","технологии искусственного интеллекта","AI SDK v6","LangGraph","собственный бэкенд"],"ar":["إعداد Setup للمطورين","إعداد API","دمج الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير المشاريع","تقنيات الذكاء الاصطناعي","AI SDK v6","LangGraph","خلفية مخصصة"]}},"owner":"yashness","repo":"yash-full-stack-personal","repoPath":"yashness/yash-full-stack-personal","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"setup","description":"Setup and configure assistant-ui in a project. Use when installing packages, configuring runtimes, or troubleshooting setup issues.","version":"0.0.1","bodyPreview":"# assistant-ui Setup\n\n**Always consult [assistant-ui.com/llms.txt](https://assistant-ui.com/llms.txt) for latest API.**\n\n## References\n\n- [./references/ai-sdk.md](./references/ai-sdk.md) -- AI SDK v6 setup (recommended)\n- [./references/langgraph.md](./references/langgraph.md) -- LangGraph agent setup\n- [./references/custom-backend.md](./references/custom-backend.md) -- useLocalRuntime / useExternalStoreRuntime\n- [./references/ag-ui.md](./references/ag-ui.md) -- AG-UI protocol\n- [./references/a2a","body":"# assistant-ui Setup\n\n**Always consult [assistant-ui.com/llms.txt](https://assistant-ui.com/llms.txt) for latest API.**\n\n## References\n\n- [./references/ai-sdk.md](./references/ai-sdk.md) -- AI SDK v6 setup (recommended)\n- [./references/langgraph.md](./references/langgraph.md) -- LangGraph agent setup\n- [./references/custom-backend.md](./references/custom-backend.md) -- useLocalRuntime / useExternalStoreRuntime\n- [./references/ag-ui.md](./references/ag-ui.md) -- AG-UI protocol\n- [./references/a2a.md](./references/a2a.md) -- A2A protocol\n- [./references/styling.md](./references/styling.md) -- Styling options\n- [./references/tanstack.md](./references/tanstack.md) -- TanStack Router\n\n## Pick Your Setup\n\n```\nUsing Vercel AI SDK?\n├─ Yes → useChatRuntime (recommended)\n└─ No\n   ├─ LangGraph agents? → useLangGraphRuntime\n   ├─ AG-UI protocol? → useAgUiRuntime\n   ├─ A2A protocol? → useA2ARuntime\n   ├─ External state (Redux/Zustand)? → useExternalStoreRuntime\n   └─ Custom API → useLocalRuntime\n```\n\n## Quick Start (AI SDK)\n\n```bash\nnpm install @assistant-ui/react @assistant-ui/react-ai-sdk @ai-sdk/react ai @ai-sdk/openai\n```\n\n```tsx\n// app/page.tsx\n\"use client\";\nimport { AssistantRuntimeProvider, Thread } from \"@assistant-ui/react\";\nimport { useChatRuntime, AssistantChatTransport } from \"@assistant-ui/react-ai-sdk\";\n\nexport default function Chat() {\n  const runtime = useChatRuntime({\n    transport: new AssistantChatTransport({ api: \"/api/chat\" }),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <AssistantRuntimeProvider runtime={runtime}>\n      <Thread />\n    </AssistantRuntimeProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n```ts\n// app/api/chat/route.ts\nimport { openai } from \"@ai-sdk/openai\";\nimport { streamText } from \"ai\";\n\nexport async function POST(req: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await req.json();\n  const result = streamText({ model: openai(\"gpt-4o\"), messages });\n  return result.toUIMessageStreamResponse();\n}\n```\n\n## Styling\n\n```tsx\n// Option 1: Pre-built CSS\nimport \"@assistant-ui/styles/default.css\";\n\n// Option 2: Tailwind (add to tailwind.config.js)\ncontent: [\"./node_modules/@assistant-ui/react/dist/**/*.js\"]\n```\n\n## Environment Variables\n\n```env\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...\nNEXT_PUBLIC_ASSISTANT_BASE_URL=https://api.assistant-ui.com  # For cloud\n```\n\n## Common Gotchas\n\n**\"Cannot find module @ai-sdk/react\"**\n```bash\nnpm install @ai-sdk/react\n```\n\n**Styles not applied**\n- Import CSS at root level or configure Tailwind content paths\n\n**Streaming not working**\n- Use `toUIMessageStreamResponse()` in API route\n- Check for CORS errors in console\n\n**\"runtime is undefined\"**\n- Call `useChatRuntime` inside a component, not at module level\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:17:54.139Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents requiring customized runtime environments and API integrations for advanced language model interactions.","zh":"适用于需要自定义运行时环境和API集成的AI代理，以实现高级语言模型交互。","ja":"カスタマイズされたランタイム環境とAPI統合を必要とするAIエージェントに適しています。これにより、高度な言語モデルインタラクションが可能になります。","ko":"고급 언어 모델 상호 작용을 위한 사용자 정의 런타임 환경 및 API 통합이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que requieren entornos de ejecución personalizados y integraciones de API para interacciones avanzadas con modelos de lenguaje.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA nécessitant des environnements d''exécution personnalisés et des intégrations d''API pour des interactions avancées avec les modèles de langage.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die benutzerdefinierte Laufzeitumgebungen und API-Integrationen für erweiterte Sprachmodell-Interaktionen erfordern.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que exigem ambientes de tempo de execução personalizados e integrações de API para interações avançadas de modelos de linguagem.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, требующих настраиваемых сред выполнения и интеграций API для продвинутых взаимодействий языковых моделей.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي التي تتطلب بيئات زمن تشغيل مخصصة وتكاملات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات لتفاعلات متقدمة لنموذج اللغة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to integrate with various AI SDKs, such as AI SDK v6 and LangGraph, and utilize protocols like AG-UI, enabling seamless interactions with local runtime and external stores using useLocalRuntime and useExternalStoreRuntime.","zh":"赋予代理集成各种AI SDK（如AI SDK v6和LangGraph）和利用协议（如AG-UI）的能力，从而能够使用useLocalRuntime和useExternalStoreRuntime实现与本地运行时和外部存储的无缝交互。","ja":"AI SDK v6やLangGraphなどのさまざまなAI SDK、およびAG-UIなどのプロトコルと統合する能力をエージェントに与え、useLocalRuntimeおよびuseExternalStoreRuntimeを使用してローカルランタイムおよび外部ストアとのシームレスな相互作用を可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 다양한 AI SDK(AI SDK v6 및 LangGraph 등)와 프로토콜(AG-UI 등)을 통합할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 useLocalRuntime 및 useExternalStoreRuntime을 사용하여 로컬 런타임 및 외부 스토어와의无缝 상호 작용을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a integrarse con varios SDK de IA, como AI SDK v6 y LangGraph, y a utilizar protocolos como AG-UI, lo que permite interacciones sin problemas con el entorno de ejecución local y las tiendas externas utilizando useLocalRuntime y useExternalStoreRuntime.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''intégrer avec différents SDK d''IA, tels que AI SDK v6 et LangGraph, et d''utiliser des protocoles tels que AG-UI, permettant ainsi des interactions sans accroc avec l''exécution locale et les magasins externes en utilisant useLocalRuntime et useExternalStoreRuntime.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, sich mit verschiedenen KI-SDKs wie AI SDK v6 und LangGraph zu integrieren und Protokolle wie AG-UI zu nutzen, wodurch eine nahtlose Interaktion mit der lokalen Laufzeitumgebung und externen Stores mithilfe von useLocalRuntime und useExternalStoreRuntime ermöglicht wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se integrarem a vários SDKs de IA, como o SDK de IA v6 e LangGraph, e a utilizarem protocolos como AG-UI, permitindo interações sem problemas com o tempo de execução local e lojas externas usando useLocalRuntime e useExternalStoreRuntime.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью интегрироваться с различными SDK ИИ, такими как ИИ SDK v6 и LangGraph, и использовать протоколы, такие как AG-UI, обеспечивая бесшовное взаимодействие с локальной средой выполнения и внешними хранилищами с помощью useLocalRuntime и useExternalStoreRuntime.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من التكامل مع SDKs الذكاء الاصطناعي المختلفة مثل SDK الذكاء الاصطناعي v6 و LangGraph واستخدام بروتوكولات مثل AG-UI، وتمكين التفاعلات السلسة مع زمن التشغيل المحلي والمخازن الخارجية باستخدام useLocalRuntime و useExternalStoreRuntime."},"useCases":{"en":["Configuring AI SDK v6 for optimized language model performance","Setting up LangGraph agents for advanced natural language processing tasks","Implementing custom backends using useLocalRuntime and useExternalStoreRuntime for enhanced flexibility"],"zh":["为AI SDK v6配置优化的语言模型性能","为高级自然语言处理任务设置LangGraph代理","使用useLocalRuntime和useExternalStoreRuntime实现自定义后端以增强灵活性"],"ja":["AI SDK v6の最適化された言語モデルパフォーマンスの構成","高度な自然言語処理タスクのためのLangGraphエージェントの設定","useLocalRuntimeおよびuseExternalStoreRuntimeを使用したカスタムバックエンドの実装による柔軟性の向上"],"ko":["AI SDK v6의 최적화된 언어 모델 성능 구성","고급 자연어 처리 작업을 위한 LangGraph 에이전트 설정","useLocalRuntime 및 useExternalStoreRuntime을 사용한 사용자 정의 백엔드 구현으로 유연성을 향상"],"es":["Configuración de AI SDK v6 para un rendimiento óptimo del modelo de lenguaje","Configuración de agentes LangGraph para tareas avanzadas de procesamiento de lenguaje natural","Implementación de backends personalizados utilizando useLocalRuntime y useExternalStoreRuntime para una mayor flexibilidad"],"fr":["Configuration de AI SDK v6 pour des performances optimales du modèle de langage","Configuration des agents LangGraph pour des tâches avancées de traitement du langage naturel","Mise en œuvre de backends personnalisés en utilisant useLocalRuntime et useExternalStoreRuntime pour une flexibilité accrue"],"de":["Konfiguration von AI SDK v6 für ein optimales Sprachmodell-Performance","Einrichtung von LangGraph-Agents für erweiterte Aufgaben des natürlichen Sprachverarbeitung","Implementierung von benutzerdefinierten Backends unter Verwendung von useLocalRuntime und useExternalStoreRuntime für eine erhöhte Flexibilität"],"pt":["Configurando o SDK de IA v6 para desempenho de modelo de linguagem otimizado","Configurando agentes LangGraph para tarefas avançadas de processamento de linguagem natural","Implementando backends personalizados usando useLocalRuntime e useExternalStoreRuntime para flexibilidade aprimorada"],"ru":["Настройка ИИ SDK v6 для оптимизированной производительности языковой модели","Настройка агентов LangGraph для продвинутых задач обработки естественного языка","Реализация пользовательских бэкендов с помощью useLocalRuntime и useExternalStoreRuntime для повышения гибкости"],"ar":["تهيئة SDK الذكاء الاصطناعي v6 لأداء نموذج اللغة الأمثل","تهيئة وكلاء LangGraph لمهام متقدمة لمعالجة اللغة الطبيعية","تنفيذ الخوادم الخلفية المخصصة باستخدام useLocalRuntime و useExternalStoreRuntime لتعزيز المرونة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires consultation of the latest API documentation at assistant-ui.com/llms.txt","Dependent on specific AI SDK and protocol versions, such as AI SDK v6 and AG-UI"],"zh":["需要咨询assistant-ui.com/llms.txt上的最新API文档","依赖于特定的AI SDK和协议版本，例如AI SDK v6和AG-UI"],"ja":["最新のAPIドキュメント（assistant-ui.com/llms.txt）を参照する必要がある","特定のAI SDKおよびプロトコルバージョン（例：AI SDK v6およびAG-UI）に依存する"],"ko":["最新 API 문서(assistant-ui.com/llms.txt)를 참조해야 함","특정 AI SDK 및 프로토콜 버전(AI SDK v6 및 AG-UI 등)에 종속"],"es":["Requiere la consulta de la última documentación de la API en assistant-ui.com/llms.txt","Dependiente de versiones específicas de SDK de IA y protocolos, como AI SDK v6 y AG-UI"],"fr":["Nécessite la consultation de la dernière documentation de l''API sur assistant-ui.com/llms.txt","Dépendante de versions spécifiques de SDK d''IA et de protocoles, tels que AI SDK v6 et AG-UI"],"de":["Erfordert die Konsultation der neuesten API-Dokumentation unter assistant-ui.com/llms.txt","Abhängig von spezifischen Versionen von KI-SDKs und Protokollen, wie AI SDK v6 und AG-UI"],"pt":["Exige a consulta da documentação da API mais recente em assistant-ui.com/llms.txt","Depende de versões específicas do SDK de IA e protocolo, como o SDK de IA v6 e AG-UI"],"ru":["Требует консультации самой актуальной документации API на сайте assistant-ui.com/llms.txt","Зависит от конкретных версий ИИ SDK и протокола, таких как ИИ SDK v6 и AG-UI"],"ar":["يتطلب استشارة أحدث توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات على الموقع assistant-ui.com/llms.txt","يعتمد على إصدارات محددة من SDK الذكاء الاصطناعي وبروتوكول مثل SDK الذكاء الاصطناعي v6 و AG-UI"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('uxname/liteend/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'uxname', 'liteend', 'uxname/liteend', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:18:33.481Z', NULL, '{"id":"uxname/liteend/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"openspec-onboard 是一个轻量级的 GraphQL 和 Prisma.io Node.js 后端，用于指导用户完成第一个完整的 OpenSpec 工作流程周期","ja":"openspec-onboard は軽量級の GraphQL と Prisma.io Node.js バックエンドであり、ユーザーが最初の OpenSpec ワークフローサイクルを完了するためのガイドです","ko":"openspec-onboard는 경량급 GraphQL 및 Prisma.io Node.js 백엔드로서 사용자가 첫 번째 완전한 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 완료하도록 도와줍니다","es":"OpenSpec-onboard es un skill que guía a los desarrolladores en la configuración inicial y primer ciclo de trabajo de un backend Node.js con GraphQL y Prisma.io. Proporciona verificación de estado e inicialización del proyecto.","fr":"OpenSpec-onboard est un skill qui guide les développeurs dans la configuration initiale et le premier cycle de travail d''un backend Node.js avec GraphQL et Prisma.io. Il fournit une vérification d''état et une initialisation du projet.","de":"OpenSpec-onboard ist ein Skill, der Entwickler durch die Erstkonfiguration und den ersten Arbeitszyklus eines Node.js-Backends mit GraphQL und Prisma.io führt. Es bietet Statusüberprüfung und Projektinitialisierung.","en":"Lightweight GraphQL & Prisma.io node.js backend"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-onboard 技术指南","ja":"openspec-onboard 技術ガイド","ko":"openspec-onboard 기술 가이드","es":"Guía de Onboarding de OpenSpec: GraphQL y Prisma Backend","fr":"Guide d''Onboarding OpenSpec : Backend GraphQL et Prisma","de":"OpenSpec Onboarding-Guide: GraphQL & Prisma Backend","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-onboard 是一个轻量级的 GraphQL 和 Prisma.io Node.js 后端，用于指导用户完成第一个完整的 OpenSpec 工作流程周期","ja":"openspec-onboard は軽量級の GraphQL と Prisma.io Node.js バックエンドであり、ユーザーが最初の OpenSpec ワークフローサイクルを完了するためのガイドです","ko":"openspec-onboard는 경량급 GraphQL 및 Prisma.io Node.js 백엔드로서 사용자가 첫 번째 완전한 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 완료하도록 도와줍니다","es":"OpenSpec-onboard es un skill que guía a los desarrolladores en la configuración inicial y primer ciclo de trabajo de un backend Node.js con GraphQL y Prisma....","fr":"OpenSpec-onboard est un skill qui guide les développeurs dans la configuration initiale et le premier cycle de travail d''un backend Node.js avec GraphQL et P...","de":"OpenSpec-onboard ist ein Skill, der Entwickler durch die Erstkonfiguration und den ersten Arbeitszyklus eines Node.js-Backends mit GraphQL und Prisma.io führ...","en":"Lightweight GraphQL & Prisma.io node.js backend"},"definition":{"en":"Lightweight GraphQL & Prisma.io node.js backend"},"features":{"zh":["轻量级 GraphQL","Prisma.io Node.js 后端","OpenSpec 工作流程周期","初始化检查","工作流程指导"],"ja":["軽量級 GraphQL","Prisma.io Node.js バックエンド","OpenSpec ワークフローサイクル","初期化チェック","ワークフローガイド"],"ko":["경량급 GraphQL","Prisma.io Node.js 백엔드","OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클","초기화 확인","워크플로우 가이드"],"es":["Verificación del estado de inicialización de OpenSpec","Guía interactiva para el primer ciclo de trabajo completo","Comandos prácticos de terminal para configuración","Integración con GraphQL y Prisma.io","Proceso de onboarding automatizado para desarrolladores","Verificación JSON del estado del proyecto"],"fr":["Vérification de l''état d''initialisation d''OpenSpec","Guide interactif pour le premier cycle de travail complet","Commandes pratiques de terminal pour la configuration","Intégration avec GraphQL et Prisma.io","Processus d''onboarding automatisé pour développeurs","Vérification JSON de l''état du projet"],"de":["Überprüfung des Initialisierungsstatus von OpenSpec","Interaktive Anleitung für den ersten vollständigen Arbeitszyklus","Praktische Terminalbefehle für die Einrichtung","Integration mit GraphQL und Prisma.io","Automatisierter Onboarding-Prozess für Entwickler","JSON-Statusüberprüfung des Projekts"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-onboard","GraphQL","Prisma.io","Node.js","后端开发","OpenSpec"],"ja":["openspec-onboard","GraphQL","Prisma.io","Node.js","バックエンド開発","OpenSpec"],"ko":["openspec-onboard","GraphQL","Prisma.io","Node.js","백엔드 개발","OpenSpec"],"es":["openspec onboarding","graphql prisma backend","nodejs inicialización openspec","guía configuración openspec","openspec status verificación","prisma.io nodejs","backend ligero graphql","comandos terminal openspec"],"fr":["onboarding openspec","backend graphql prisma","initialisation nodejs openspec","guide configuration openspec","vérification status openspec","prisma.io nodejs","backend léger graphql","commandes terminal openspec"],"de":["openspec onboarding","graphql prisma backend","nodejs initialisierung openspec","einrichtungsguide openspec","statusprüfung openspec","prisma.io nodejs","leichtes graphql backend","terminalbefehle openspec"]}},"owner":"uxname","repo":"liteend","repoPath":"uxname/liteend","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:18:33.481Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Node.js Agents needing lightweight GraphQL and Prisma.io backend integration.","zh":"非常适合需要轻量级GraphQL和Prisma.io后端集成的Node.js代理。","ja":"Node.jsエージェントが軽量のGraphQLおよびPrisma.ioバックエンド統合を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"노드.js 에이전트가 가벼운 GraphQL 및 Prisma.io 백엔드 통합을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Node.js que necesitan una integración ligera de GraphQL y Prisma.io","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Node.js ayant besoin d''une intégration légère de GraphQL et Prisma.io","de":"Perfekt für Node.js-Agents, die eine leichte GraphQL- und Prisma.io-Backend-Integration benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Node.js que precisam de integração de backend leve com GraphQL e Prisma.io.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Node.js, которым необходима легкая интеграция с GraphQL и Prisma.io на стороне бэкенда.","ar":"مثالي لعميل Node.js الذي يحتاج إلى دمج خلفي خفيف مع GraphQL و Prisma.io."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage OpenSpec workflows, utilizing GraphQL for flexible querying and Prisma.io for robust database management, all within a node.js environment.","zh":"赋予代理管理OpenSpec工作流的能力，利用GraphQL进行灵活的查询和Prisma.io进行强大的数据库管理，全都在node.js环境中。","ja":"エージェントがOpenSpecワークフローを管理する能力を提供し、GraphQLを使用して柔軟なクエリとPrisma.ioを使用して堅牢なデータベース管理を実現し、すべてnode.js環境内で実行されます。","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 워크플ロー를 관리할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, GraphQL을 사용하여 유연한 쿼리와 Prisma.io를 사용하여 강력한 데이터베이스 관리를 모두 노드.js 환경에서 수행할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar flujos de trabajo de OpenSpec, utilizando GraphQL para consultas flexibles y Prisma.io para una gestión robusta de bases de datos, todo dentro de un entorno node.js","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les flux de travail OpenSpec, en utilisant GraphQL pour des requêtes flexibles et Prisma.io pour une gestion robuste de bases de données, le tout dans un environnement node.js","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, OpenSpec-Workflows zu verwalten, indem GraphQL für flexible Abfragen und Prisma.io für robuste Datenbankverwaltung verwendet wird, alles innerhalb einer node.js-Umgebung","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar fluxos de trabalho OpenSpec, utilizando GraphQL para consultas flexíveis e Prisma.io para gerenciamento robusto de banco de dados, tudo dentro de um ambiente node.js.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять рабочими процессами OpenSpec, используя GraphQL для гибкого запроса и Prisma.io для надежного управления базой данных, все в среде node.js.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة عمليات العمل المفتوحة، باستخدام GraphQL للاستفسار المرن و Prisma.io لإدارة قواعد البيانات القوية، كل ذلك في بيئة node.js."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through complete OpenSpec workflow cycles","Debugging OpenSpec initialization issues"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化OpenSpec","引导用户完成OpenSpec工作流程周期","调试OpenSpec初始化问题"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトでOpenSpecを初期化する","ユーザーがOpenSpecワークフロー周期を完了するように導く","OpenSpec初期化の問題をデバッグする"],"ko":["새로운 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자가 OpenSpec 워크플로우 주기를 완료하도록 안내","OpenSpec 초기화 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Inicializar OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Guiar a los usuarios a través de ciclos de flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec completos","Depurar problemas de inicialización de OpenSpec"],"fr":["Initialiser OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guider les utilisateurs à travers des cycles de flux de travail OpenSpec complets","Déboguer les problèmes d''initialisation d''OpenSpec"],"de":["OpenSpec in neuen Projekten initialisieren","Benutzer durch vollständige OpenSpec-Workflusszyklen führen","OpenSpec-Initialisierungsprobleme debuggen"],"pt":["Inicializar OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientar usuários por meio de ciclos de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec completos","Depurar problemas de inicialização OpenSpec"],"ru":["Инициализировать OpenSpec в новых проектах","Направлять пользователей через полные циклы рабочих процессов OpenSpec","Отлаживать проблемы инициализации OpenSpec"],"ar":["تشغيل OpenSpec في مشاريع جديدة","توجيه المستخدمين من خلال دورات كاملة من عمليات العمل المفتوحة","تصحيح أخطاء بدء تشغيل OpenSpec"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires node.js environment","OpenSpec must be initialized before use","Dependent on Prisma.io and GraphQL"],"zh":["需要node.js环境","OpenSpec必须在使用前初始化","依赖于Prisma.io和GraphQL"],"ja":["node.js環境が必要","OpenSpecは使用前に初期化する必要がある","Prisma.ioとGraphQLに依存する"],"ko":["노드.js 환경이 필요","OpenSpec는 사용 전에 초기화해야 함","Prisma.io 및 GraphQL에 의존"],"es":["Requiere un entorno node.js","OpenSpec debe estar inicializado antes de su uso","Dependiente de Prisma.io y GraphQL"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement node.js","OpenSpec doit être initialisé avant son utilisation","Dépendant de Prisma.io et GraphQL"],"de":["Benötigt eine node.js-Umgebung","OpenSpec muss vor der Verwendung initialisiert werden","Von Prisma.io und GraphQL abhängig"],"pt":["Requer ambiente node.js","OpenSpec deve ser inicializado antes do uso","Dependente de Prisma.io e GraphQL"],"ru":["Требуется среда node.js","OpenSpec должен быть инициализирован перед использованием","Зависит от Prisma.io и GraphQL"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة node.js","يجب تشغيل OpenSpec قبل الاستخدام","يعتمد على Prisma.io و GraphQL"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'gAmUssA', 'ai-assisted-engineering', 'gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:18:11.061Z', NULL, '{"id":"gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门指南，引导用户完成首个OpenSpec工作流程周期，包括初始化和运行","ja":"OpenSpecを始めるためのガイド、最初のOpenSpecワークフロー周期を通じて、初期化と実行方法を学ぶ","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기 위한 가이드, 첫 번째 OpenSpec 워크플로우 사이클을 통해 초기화 및 실행 방법을 배우는 것","es":"Esta guía te llevará a través del primer ciclo de trabajo completo de OpenSpec, explicando cada paso del proceso.","fr":"Cette guide vous accompagnera tout au long du premier cycle de travail complet d''OpenSpec, en expliquant chaque étape du processus.","de":"Diese Anleitung führt Sie durch den ersten vollständigen OpenSpec-Arbeitszyklus, wobei jeder Schritt des Prozesses erklärt wird.","pt":"O openspec-onboard é um guia que leva o usuário por seu primeiro ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec completo.","ru":"OpenSpec-онбординг - это гид, который проводит пользователя через его первый полный цикл работы OpenSpec.","ar":"openspec-onboard هو مرشد يقود المستخدم خلال دورة عمل OpenSpec الكاملة الأولى","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门指南","ja":"OpenSpecを始める","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기","es":"Guía de inicio de OpenSpec","fr":"Guide de démarrage OpenSpec","de":"OpenSpec-Einführungsleitfaden","pt":"Onboard OpenSpec: Guia de Inicialização","ru":"OpenSpec Онбординг: Руководство по запуску","ar":"تاهيل OpenSpec: دليل الإعداد","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门指南，引导用户完成首个OpenSpec工作流程周期，包括初始化和运行","ja":"OpenSpecを始めるためのガイド、最初のOpenSpecワークフロー周期を通じて、初期化と実行方法を学ぶ","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기 위한 가이드, 첫 번째 OpenSpec 워크플로우 사이클을 통해 초기화 및 실행 방법을 배우는 것","es":"Esta guía te llevará a través del primer ciclo de trabajo completo de OpenSpec, explicando cada paso del proceso.","fr":"Cette guide vous accompagnera tout au long du premier cycle de travail complet d''OpenSpec, en expliquant chaque étape du processus.","de":"Diese Anleitung führt Sie durch den ersten vollständigen OpenSpec-Arbeitszyklus, wobei jeder Schritt des Prozesses erklärt wird.","pt":"O openspec-onboard é um guia que leva o usuário por seu primeiro ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec completo.","ru":"OpenSpec-онбординг - это гид, который проводит пользователя через его первый полный цикл работы OpenSpec.","ar":"openspec-onboard هو مرشد يقود المستخدم خلال دورة عمل OpenSpec الكاملة الأولى","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["初始化OpenSpec","运行OpenSpec工作流程","检查OpenSpec状态","实时代码编辑","工作流程可视化"],"ja":["OpenSpecの初期化","OpenSpecワークフローの実行","OpenSpecのステータス確認","リアルタイムコード編集","ワークフローの可視化"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화","OpenSpec 워크플로우 실행","OpenSpec 상태 확인","실시간 코드 편집","워크플로우 시각화"],"es":["Configuración inicial de OpenSpec","Ciclo de trabajo completo","Explicación paso a paso","Integración con el código del proyecto","Verificación del estado de OpenSpec","Guía para principiantes"],"fr":["Configuration initiale d''OpenSpec","Cycle de travail complet","Explication étape par étape","Intégration avec le code du projet","Vérification de l''état d''OpenSpec","Guide pour les débutants"],"de":["Erstkonfiguration von OpenSpec","Vollständiger Arbeitszyklus","Schritt-für-Schritt-Erklärung","Integration mit dem Projektcode","Überprüfung des OpenSpec-Status","Anleitung für Anfänger"],"pt":["Guia passo a passo para inicialização","Verificação de status de inicialização","Iniciação do fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec","Explicação de cada etapa do processo","Trabalho real no codebase do usuário"],"ru":["Пошаговое руководство по запуску","Проверка статуса инициализации","Запуск рабочего процесса OpenSpec","Объяснение каждого этапа процесса","Реальная работа в кодовой базе пользователя"],"ar":["دليل خطوة بخطوة للإعداد","فحص حالة الإعداد","تشغيل دورة عمل OpenSpec","شرح كل خطوة في العملية","العمل الفعلي في قاعدة الشفرة للمستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","开发工具","工作流程","初始化","运行","代码编辑","可视化"],"ja":["OpenSpec","開発ツール","ワークフロー","初期化","実行","コード編集","可視化"],"ko":["OpenSpec","개발 도구","워크플로우","초기화","실행","코드 편집","시각화"],"es":["OpenSpec","guía de inicio","configuración de OpenSpec","ciclo de trabajo","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","integración con código"],"fr":["OpenSpec","guide de démarrage","configuration d''OpenSpec","cycle de travail","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","intégration avec code"],"de":["OpenSpec","Einführungsleitfaden","Konfiguration von OpenSpec","Arbeitszyklus","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklertools","Integration mit Code"],"pt":["OpenSpec","onboard","inicialização","guia","fluxo de trabalho","codebase","desenvolvedor","programador"],"ru":["OpenSpec","онбординг","запуск","руководство","рабочий процесс","кодовая база","разработчик","программист"],"ar":["OpenSpec","تاهيل","إعداد","دليل","دورة عمل","قاعدة الشفرة","مطور","مبرمج"]}},"owner":"gAmUssA","repo":"ai-assisted-engineering","repoPath":"gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:18:11.061Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing guided workflow integration and initialization with OpenSpec.","zh":"非常适合需要使用OpenSpec进行指导工作流集成和初始化的开发代理","ja":"OpenSpecを使用したガイド付きワークフロー統合および初期化を必要とする開発エージェントに最適","ko":"OpenSpec를 사용한 가이드 워크플로 통합 및 초기화를 필요로 하는 개발 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan integración de flujo de trabajo guiada e inicialización con OpenSpec.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une intégration de flux de travail guidée et d''initialisation avec OpenSpec.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine guidierte Workflow-Integration und Initialisierung mit OpenSpec benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de integração de fluxo de trabalho orientada e inicialização com OpenSpec.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым требуется управляемая интеграция рабочего процесса и инициализация с OpenSpec.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى تكامل تدفق العمل الموجه والتهيئة مع OpenSpec."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to initialize and guide users through complete OpenSpec workflow cycles, utilizing JSON output and command-line interactions with openspec status and init commands.","zh":"赋予代理初始化和指导用户完成OpenSpec工作流周期的能力，利用JSON输出和命令行交互以openspec状态和初始化命令","ja":"エージェントにOpenSpecワークフローサイクルを初期化およびユーザーに案内する能力を付与し、JSON出力とコマンドラインでのopenspecステータスおよび初期化コマンドとの相互作用を利用","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 초기화하고 사용자를 안내할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, JSON 출력과 명령행 상의 openspec 상태 및 초기화 명령어와의 상호작용을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a inicializar y guiar a los usuarios a través de ciclos de flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec completos, utilizando la salida JSON y las interacciones de línea de comandos con los comandos openspec status e init.","fr":"Habilite les agents à initialiser et à guider les utilisateurs à travers des cycles de workflow OpenSpec complets, en utilisant la sortie JSON et les interactions de ligne de commande avec les commandes openspec status et init.","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, Benutzer durch vollständige OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklen zu führen und zu initialisieren, unter Verwendung von JSON-Ausgaben und Kommandozeilen-Interaktionen mit openspec-Status- und init-Befehlen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a inicializar e orientar os usuários por meio de ciclos de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec completos, utilizando saída JSON e interações de linha de comando com os comandos openspec status e init.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью инициализировать и направлять пользователей через полные циклы рабочего процесса OpenSpec, используя вывод JSON и взаимодействие с командной строкой с помощью команд openspec status и init.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تهيئة وتوجيه المستخدمين من خلال دورات كاملة من تدفق عمل OpenSpec، باستخدام الإخراج JSON وتواصل سطر الأوامر مع أوامر openspec status و init."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through first-time OpenSpec workflow cycles","Validating OpenSpec initialization status via JSON output"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化OpenSpec","指导用户完成首次OpenSpec工作流周期","通过JSON输出验证OpenSpec初始化状态"],"ja":["新規プロジェクトでOpenSpecを初期化","ユーザーが最初のOpenSpecワークフローサイクルを完了するのを支援","JSON出力によってOpenSpec初期化状態を検証"],"ko":["새 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자가 첫 번째 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 완료하도록 안내","JSON 출력을 통해 OpenSpec 초기화 상태를 검증"],"es":["Inicialización de OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Guía de los usuarios a través de los primeros ciclos de flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec","Validación del estado de inicialización de OpenSpec a través de la salida JSON"],"fr":["Initialisation d''OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guidage des utilisateurs à travers les premiers cycles de flux de travail OpenSpec","Validation de l''état d''initialisation d''OpenSpec via la sortie JSON"],"de":["Initialisierung von OpenSpec in neuen Projekten","Führung von Benutzern durch die ersten OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklen","Validierung des OpenSpec-Initialisierungsstatus über die JSON-Ausgabe"],"pt":["Inicializar OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientar os usuários por meio de ciclos de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec pela primeira vez","Validar o status de inicialização do OpenSpec via saída JSON"],"ru":["Инициализировать OpenSpec в новых проектах","Направлять пользователей через циклы рабочего процесса OpenSpec впервые","Проверять статус инициализации OpenSpec через вывод JSON"],"ar":["تهيئة OpenSpec في مشاريع جديدة","توجيه المستخدمين من خلال دورات تدفق عمل OpenSpec لأول مرة","تحقق من حالة تهيئة OpenSpec من خلال الإخراج JSON"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires openspec command-line tool installed","Must be run in a project directory"],"zh":["需要安装openspec命令行工具","必须在项目目录中运行"],"ja":["openspecコマンドラインツールをインストールする必要がある","プロジェクトディレクトリ内で実行する必要がある"],"ko":["openspec 명령행 도구를 설치해야 함","프로젝트 디렉토리에서 실행해야 함"],"es":["Requiere la herramienta de línea de comandos openspec instalada","Debe ejecutarse en un directorio de proyecto"],"fr":["Nécessite l''outil de ligne de commande openspec installé","Doit être exécuté dans un répertoire de projet"],"de":["Benötigt das installierte openspec-Kommandozeilen-Tool","Muss in einem Projektverzeichnis ausgeführt werden"],"pt":["Requer a ferramenta de linha de comando openspec instalada","Deve ser executado em um diretório de projeto"],"ru":["Требует установленного инструмента командной строки openspec","Должно быть запущено в директории проекта"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت أداة سطر الأوامر openspec","يجب تشغيله في دليل مشروع"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('beyildirim/tracehound/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'beyildirim', 'tracehound', 'beyildirim/tracehound', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:18:12.181Z', NULL, '{"id":"beyildirim/tracehound/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"本指南将指导用户完成OpenSpec的整个工作流程循环，包括初始化和运行","ja":"OpenSpecのワークフローを実行するためのガイド","ko":"OpenSpec의 워크플로우를 통해 프로젝트를 설정하고 실행하는 방법을紹介","es":"Esta guía te llevará a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec, explicando cada paso","fr":"Cette guide vous accompagnera tout au long de votre premier cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec, en expliquant chaque étape","de":"Diese Anleitung führt Sie durch Ihren ersten kompletten OpenSpec-Arbeitszyklus, indem jeder Schritt erklärt wird","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que leva você pelo seu primeiro ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec. Ele explica cada etapa e executa trabalho real no seu código.","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это гид, который ведет вас через ваш первый цикл работы OpenSpec. Он объясняет каждую ступень и выполняет реальную работу в вашем коде.","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يرشدك خلال دورة عمل OpenSpec الأولى. يشرح كل خطوة ويعمل على kodك الفعلي","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门指南","ja":"OpenSpecのガイド","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기","es":"Onboarding de OpenSpec: Guía para desarrolladores","fr":"Onboarding OpenSpec: Guide pour les développeurs","de":"OpenSpec-Onboarding: Anleitung für Entwickler","pt":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guia de Início Rápido","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard: Быстрый Старт","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard: إرشادات البداية","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"本指南将指导用户完成OpenSpec的整个工作流程循环，包括初始化和运行","ja":"OpenSpecのワークフローを実行するためのガイド","ko":"OpenSpec의 워크플로우를 통해 프로젝트를 설정하고 실행하는 방법을紹介","es":"Esta guía te llevará a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec, explicando cada paso","fr":"Cette guide vous accompagnera tout au long de votre premier cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec, en expliquant chaque étape","de":"Diese Anleitung führt Sie durch Ihren ersten kompletten OpenSpec-Arbeitszyklus, indem jeder Schritt erklärt wird","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que leva você pelo seu primeiro ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec. Ele explica cada etapa e executa trabalho real no seu código.","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это гид, который ведет вас через ваш первый цикл работы OpenSpec. Он объясняет каждую ступень и выполняет реальную работу в вашем коде.","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يرشدك خلال دورة عمل OpenSpec الأولى. يشرح كل خطوة ويعمل على kodك الفعلي","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["初始化OpenSpec","运行OpenSpec工作流程","代码检查","项目设置"],"ja":["OpenSpecの初期化","OpenSpecのワークフローを実行","コードチェック","プロジェクト設定"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화","OpenSpec 워크플로우 실행","코드 검사","프로젝트 설정"],"es":["Configuración inicial de OpenSpec","Ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec","Explicación detallada de cada paso","Trabajo práctico en el código del proyecto","Verificación del estado de OpenSpec","Inicialización de OpenSpec si es necesario"],"fr":["Configuration initiale d''OpenSpec","Cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec","Explication détaillée de chaque étape","Travail pratique sur le code du projet","Vérification de l''état d''OpenSpec","Initialisation d''OpenSpec si nécessaire"],"de":["Initiale Konfiguration von OpenSpec","Kompletter Arbeitszyklus mit OpenSpec","Detaillierte Erklärung jeder Phase","Praktische Arbeit am Projektcode","Überprüfung des OpenSpec-Status","Initialisierung von OpenSpec wenn erforderlich"],"pt":["Guia de início rápido para OpenSpec","Configuração e execução do primeiro ciclo de trabalho","Explicação de cada etapa do processo","Trabalho real no código do usuário","Verificação de inicialização de OpenSpec"],"ru":["Быстрый старт для OpenSpec","Настройка и выполнение первого цикла работы","Объяснение каждой ступени процесса","Реальная работа в коде пользователя","Проверка инициализации OpenSpec"],"ar":["دليل سريع للبداية مع OpenSpec","تكوين وتنفيذ دورة العمل الأولى","شرح كل خطوة في العملية","العمل الفعلي على kod المستخدم","فحص تشغيل OpenSpec"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","开源项目管理","代码检查","项目设置","工作流程","初始化"],"ja":["OpenSpec","オープンソースプロジェクト管理","コードチェック","プロジェクト設定","ワークフロー","初期化"],"ko":["OpenSpec","오픈소스 프로젝트 관리","코드 검사","프로젝트 설정","워크플로우","초기화"],"es":["OpenSpec","onboarding","desarrollo de software","herramientas de código","configuración inicial","ciclo de trabajo","trabajo práctico","verificación de estado"],"fr":["OpenSpec","onboarding","développement de logiciels","outils de code","configuration initiale","cycle de travail","travail pratique","vérification d''état"],"de":["OpenSpec","Onboarding","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Werkzeuge","initiale Konfiguration","Arbeitszyklus","praktische Arbeit","Status-Überprüfung"],"pt":["OpenSpec","Guia de início rápido","Configuração OpenSpec","Ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec","Desenvolvimento de software","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["OpenSpec","Быстрый старт","Настройка OpenSpec","Цикл работы OpenSpec","Разработка программного обеспечения","Инструменты разработки"],"ar":["OpenSpec","دليل سريع للبداية","تكوين OpenSpec","دورة العمل OpenSpec","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"beyildirim","repo":"tracehound","repoPath":"beyildirim/tracehound","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:18:12.181Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents requiring guided workflow cycles and codebase interaction.","zh":"非常适合需要引导工作流循环和代码库交互的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが導かれたワークフロー サイクルとコードベースの相互作用を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"가이드된 워크플로 사이클과 코드베이스 상호작용이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que requieren ciclos de flujo de trabajo guiados y interacción con el código base.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant des cycles de workflow guidés et une interaction avec la base de code.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die einen geleiteten Workflow-Zyklus und Codebasis-Interaktion erfordern.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que exigem ciclos de fluxo de trabalho guiados e interação com o código-fonte.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих руководства по циклам рабочих процессов и взаимодействия с кодовой базой.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تطوير الوكلاء التي تتطلب دورات عمل توجيهية وتفاعل مع قاعدة الشفرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to facilitate complete OpenSpec workflow cycles, utilizing JSON output and command-line interactions like `openspec status` and `openspec init`, to streamline project setup and initialization.","zh":"赋予代理人完成 OpenSpec 工作流循环的能力，利用 JSON 输出和命令行交互（如 `openspec status` 和 `openspec init`），以简化项目设置和初始化。","ja":"エージェントが OpenSpec ワークフロー サイクルを完了できるようにし、JSON 出力とコマンドラインのやり取り（例： `openspec status` と `openspec init`）を使用してプロジェクトの設定と初期化を簡素化します。","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 완료할 수 있도록하며 JSON 출력 및 명령줄 상호작용(예: `openspec status` 및 `openspec init`)을 사용하여 프로젝트 설정 및 초기화를 간소화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a facilitar ciclos de flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec completos, utilizando la salida JSON y las interacciones de línea de comandos como `openspec status` y `openspec init`, para agilizar la configuración y la inicialización del proyecto.","fr":"Permet aux agents de faciliter des cycles de workflow OpenSpec complets, en utilisant la sortie JSON et les interactions de ligne de commande comme `openspec status` et `openspec init`, pour rationaliser la configuration et l''initialisation du projet.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, komplette OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklen zu erleichtern, indem JSON-Ausgabe und Befehlszeilen-Interaktionen wie `openspec status` und `openspec init` verwendet werden, um die Projekt-Konfiguration und Initialisierung zu rationalisieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a facilitar ciclos de trabalho OpenSpec completos, utilizando saída JSON e interações de linha de comando como `openspec status` e `openspec init`, para otimizar a configuração e inicialização do projeto.","ru":"Позволяет агентам облегчить выполнение полных циклов рабочих процессов OpenSpec, используя выходные данные JSON и взаимодействия с командной строкой, такие как `openspec status` и `openspec init`, для оптимизации настройки и инициализации проекта.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تسهيل دورات عمل OpenSpec الكاملة، باستخدام إخراج JSON وتفاعلات سطر الأوامر مثل `openspec status` و `openspec init`، لتحسين إعداد وتشغيل المشروع."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through workflow cycles","Debugging OpenSpec initialization issues"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化 OpenSpec","引导用户完成工作流循环","调试 OpenSpec 初始化问题"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトで OpenSpec を初期化する","ユーザーをワークフロー サイクルに沿って導く","OpenSpec 初期化の問題をデバッグする"],"ko":["새로운 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자를 워크플로 사이클로 안내","OpenSpec 초기화 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Inicializar OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Guiar a los usuarios a través de los ciclos de flujo de trabajo","Depurar problemas de inicialización de OpenSpec"],"fr":["Initialiser OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guider les utilisateurs à travers les cycles de workflow","Déboguer les problèmes d''initialisation d''OpenSpec"],"de":["OpenSpec in neuen Projekten initialisieren","Benutzer durch Workflow-Zyklen führen","OpenSpec-Initialisierungsprobleme debuggen"],"pt":["Inicializar OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientar usuários por meio de ciclos de fluxo de trabalho","Depurar problemas de inicialização do OpenSpec"],"ru":["Инициализировать OpenSpec в новых проектах","Направлять пользователей через циклы рабочих процессов","Отладить проблемы инициализации OpenSpec"],"ar":["تشغيل OpenSpec في مشاريع جديدة","توجيه المستخدمين من خلال دورات عمل","تصحيح مشاكل بدء تشغيل OpenSpec"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec installation","Needs command-line access","Must be run in a project directory"],"zh":["需要 OpenSpec 安装","需要命令行访问","必须在项目目录中运行"],"ja":["OpenSpec のインストールが必要","コマンドラインへのアクセスが必要","プロジェクト ディレクトリ内で実行する必要がある"],"ko":["OpenSpec 설치가 필요","명령줄 액세스가 필요","프로젝트 디렉토리에서 실행해야 함"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de OpenSpec","Necesita acceso a la línea de comandos","Debe ejecutarse en un directorio de proyecto"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation d''OpenSpec","A besoin d''un accès à la ligne de commande","Doit être exécuté dans un répertoire de projet"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von OpenSpec","Benötigt Zugriff auf die Befehlszeile","Muss in einem Projekt-Verzeichnis ausgeführt werden"],"pt":["Exige instalação do OpenSpec","Necessita acesso à linha de comando","Deve ser executado em um diretório de projeto"],"ru":["Требует установки OpenSpec","Требует доступа к командной строке","Должен быть запущен в каталоге проекта"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت OpenSpec","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى سطر الأوامر","يجب تشغيله في دليل المشروع"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Ejyke90/kudegowo/openspec-continue-change', 'community', 'Ejyke90', 'kudegowo', 'Ejyke90/kudegowo', 'openspec-continue-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:18:18.931Z', NULL, '{"id":"Ejyke90/kudegowo/openspec-continue-change","name":"openspec-continue-change","description":{"zh":"Openspec Continue Change 是用于继续处理更改的技术，通过创建下一个构件来实现","ja":"Openspec Continue Change は、次のアーティファクトを作成して変更を続行する技術です","ko":"Openspec Continue Change는 다음 아티팩트를 생성하여 변경을 계속 처리하는 기술입니다","es":"La habilidad openspec-continue-change permite continuar trabajando en un cambio creando el próximo artefacto, seleccionando el cambio correcto desde la conversación.","fr":"La compétence openspec-continue-change permet de continuer à travailler sur un changement en créant le prochain artefact, en sélectionnant le changement approprié à partir de la conversation.","de":"Die Fähigkeit openspec-continue-change ermöglicht es, eine Änderung fortzusetzen, indem der nächste Artefakt erstellt und die richtige Änderung aus der Konversation ausgewählt wird.","pt":"O OpenSpec permite continuar trabalhando em uma alteração, criando o próximo artefato e melhorando a produtividade. Saiba mais sobre como usar essa ferramenta","ru":"OpenSpec позволяет продолжить работу над изменением, создавая следующий артефакт и повышая производительность. Узнайте больше о том, как использовать эту функцию","ar":"يسمح OpenSpec بمواصلة العمل على تغيير، من خلال إنشاء الملف التالي وتحسين الإنتاجية. تعلم المزيد حول كيفية استخدام هذه الأداة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Openspec Continue Change 技术","ja":"Openspec Continue Change 技術","ko":"Openspec Continue Change 기능","es":"Continuar cambio con openspec","fr":"Continuer un changement avec openspec","de":"Änderung mit openspec fortsetzen","pt":"Continue Change com OpenSpec","ru":"Продолжить изменение с OpenSpec","ar":"استمرار التغيير مع OpenSpec","en":"openspec-continue-change"},"description":{"zh":"Openspec Continue Change 是用于继续处理更改的技术，通过创建下一个构件来实现","ja":"Openspec Continue Change は、次のアーティファクトを作成して変更を続行する技術です","ko":"Openspec Continue Change는 다음 아티팩트를 생성하여 변경을 계속 처리하는 기술입니다","es":"La habilidad openspec-continue-change permite continuar trabajando en un cambio creando el próximo artefacto, seleccionando el cambio correcto desde la conve...","fr":"La compétence openspec-continue-change permet de continuer à travailler sur un changement en créant le prochain artefact, en sélectionnant le changement appr...","de":"Die Fähigkeit openspec-continue-change ermöglicht es, eine Änderung fortzusetzen, indem der nächste Artefakt erstellt und die richtige Änderung aus der Konve...","pt":"O OpenSpec permite continuar trabalhando em uma alteração, criando o próximo artefato e melhorando a produtividade. Saiba mais sobre como usar essa ferramenta","ru":"OpenSpec позволяет продолжить работу над изменением, создавая следующий артефакт и повышая производительность. Узнайте больше о том, как использовать эту фун...","ar":"يسمح OpenSpec بمواصلة العمل على تغيير، من خلال إنشاء الملف التالي وتحسين الإنتاجية. تعلم المزيد حول كيفية استخدام هذه الأداة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持创建下一个构件","可选指定更改名称","如果省略，更改名称可以从对话上下文中推断","如果不明确或模糊，必须提示用户选择可用的更改","使用 AskUserQuestion 工具让用户选择要处理的更改","运行 openspec list --json 获取可用的更改，按最近修改时间排序"],"ja":["次のアーティファクトを作成する機能","変更名の指定が可能","省略した場合、会話のコンテキストから変更名を推測する","不明確または曖昧な場合、利用可能な変更を選択するようにユーザーに促す","AskUserQuestion ツールを使用して、ユーザーが処理する変更を選択する","openspec list --json を実行して、利用可能な変更を最新の変更日時順に取得する"],"ko":["다음 아티팩트를 생성하는 기능","변경 이름을 지정할 수 있음"," 省略한 경우, 대화의 contexto에서 변경 이름을 추론함","불분명 또는 모호한 경우, 사용 가능한 변경을 선택하도록 사용자에게提示","AskUserQuestion 툴을 사용하여 사용자가 처리할 변경을 선택","openspec list --json을 실행하여 사용 가능한 변경을 최근 수정 시간 순으로 가져옴"],"es":["Continuar trabajando en un cambio","Crear el próximo artefacto","Seleccionar el cambio correcto desde la conversación","Utilizar la herramienta AskUserQuestion","Ejecutar openspec list --json","Presentar los cambios más recientemente modificados"],"fr":["Continuer à travailler sur un changement","Créer le prochain artefact","Sélectionner le changement approprié à partir de la conversation","Utiliser l''outil AskUserQuestion","Exécuter openspec list --json","Présenter les changements les plus récemment modifiés"],"de":["Eine Änderung fortsetzen","Den nächsten Artefakt erstellen","Die richtige Änderung aus der Konversation auswählen","Das Tool AskUserQuestion verwenden","Openspec list --json ausführen","Die zuletzt geänderten Änderungen anzeigen"],"pt":["Continuar trabalhando em uma alteração","Criar o próximo artefato","Melhorar a produtividade","Selecionar alterações disponíveis","Usar a ferramenta AskUserQuestion"],"ru":["Продолжить работу над изменением","Создать следующий артефакт","Повысить производительность","Выбрать доступные изменения","Использовать инструмент AskUserQuestion"],"ar":["استمرار العمل على تغيير","إنشاء الملف التالي","تحسين الإنتاجية","اختيار التغييرات المتاحة","استخدام أداة AskUserQuestion"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Openspec Continue Change","开发过程","更改处理","构件创建","AskUserQuestion","openspec list"],"ja":["Openspec Continue Change","開発プロセス","変更処理","アーティファクトの作成","AskUserQuestion","openspec list"],"ko":["Openspec Continue Change","개발 프로세스","변경 처리","아티팩트 생성","AskUserQuestion","openspec list"],"es":["openspec","cambios","artefactos","conversación","AskUserQuestion","desarrollo de software","control de versiones"],"fr":["openspec","changement","artefacts","conversation","AskUserQuestion","développement de logiciels","contrôle de version"],"de":["openspec","Änderungen","Artefakte","Konversation","AskUserQuestion","Softwareentwicklung","Versionskontrolle"],"pt":["OpenSpec","continuar alteração","criar artefato","melhorar produtividade","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["OpenSpec","продолжить изменение","создать артефакт","повысить производительность","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["OpenSpec","استمرار التغيير","إنشاء الملف","تحسين الإنتاجية","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"Ejyke90","repo":"kudegowo","repoPath":"Ejyke90/kudegowo","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-continue-change","description":"Continue working on an OpenSpec change by creating the next artifact. Use when the user wants to progress their change, create the next artifact, or continue their workflow.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-","body":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-4 most recently modified changes as options, showing:\n   - Change name\n   - Schema (from `schema` field if present, otherwise \"spec-driven\")\n   - Status (e.g., \"0/5 tasks\", \"complete\", \"no tasks\")\n   - How recently it was modified (from `lastModified` field)\n\n   Mark the most recently modified change as \"(Recommended)\" since it''s likely what the user wants to continue.\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check current status**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand current state. The response includes:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow schema being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - `artifacts`: Array of artifacts with their status (\"done\", \"ready\", \"blocked\")\n   - `isComplete`: Boolean indicating if all artifacts are complete\n\n3. **Act based on status**:\n\n   ---\n\n   **If all artifacts are complete (`isComplete: true`)**:\n   - Congratulate the user\n   - Show final status including the schema used\n   - Suggest: \"All artifacts created! You can now implement this change or archive it.\"\n   - STOP\n\n   ---\n\n   **If artifacts are ready to create** (status shows artifacts with `status: \"ready\"`):\n   - Pick the FIRST artifact with `status: \"ready\"` from the status output\n   - Get its instructions:\n     ```bash\n     openspec instructions <artifact-id> --change \"<name>\" --json\n     ```\n   - Parse the JSON. The key fields are:\n     - `context`: Project background (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `rules`: Artifact-specific rules (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `template`: The structure to use for your output file\n     - `instruction`: Schema-specific guidance\n     - `outputPath`: Where to write the artifact\n     - `dependencies`: Completed artifacts to read for context\n   - **Create the artifact file**:\n     - Read any completed dependency files for context\n     - Use `template` as the structure - fill in its sections\n     - Apply `context` and `rules` as constraints when writing - but do NOT copy them into the file\n     - Write to the output path specified in instructions\n   - Show what was created and what''s now unlocked\n   - STOP after creating ONE artifact\n\n   ---\n\n   **If no artifacts are ready (all blocked)**:\n   - This shouldn''t happen with a valid schema\n   - Show status and suggest checking for issues\n\n4. **After creating an artifact, show progress**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n\n**Output**\n\nAfter each invocation, show:\n- Which artifact was created\n- Schema workflow being used\n- Current progress (N/M complete)\n- What artifacts are now unlocked\n- Prompt: \"Want to continue? Just ask me to continue or tell me what to do next.\"\n\n**Artifact Creation Guidelines**\n\nThe artifact types and their purpose depend on the schema. Use the `instruction` field from the instructions output to understand what to create.\n\nCommon artifact patterns:\n\n**spec-driven schema** (proposal → specs → design → tasks):\n- **proposal.md**: Ask user about the change if not clear. Fill in Why, What Changes, Capabilities, Impact.\n  - The Capabilities section is critical - each capability listed will need a spec file.\n- **specs/*.md**: Create one spec per capability listed in the proposal.\n- **design.md**: Document technical decisions, architecture, and implementation approach.\n- **tasks.md**: Break down implementation into checkboxed tasks.\n\nFor other schemas, follow the `instruction` field from the CLI output.\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Create ONE artifact per invocation\n- Always read dependency artifacts before creating a new one\n- Never skip artifacts or create out of order\n- If context is unclear, ask the user before creating\n- Verify the artifact file exists after writing before marking progress\n- Use the schema''s artifact sequence, don''t assume specific artifact names\n- **IMPORTANT**: `context` and `rules` are constraints for YOU, not content for the file\n  - Do NOT copy `<context>`, `<rules>`, `<project_context>` blocks into the artifact\n  - These guide what you write, but should never appear in the output\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:18:18.931Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents needing to manage and continue working on multiple changes within the openspec ecosystem.","zh":"适合需要在openspec生态系统中管理和继续处理多个更改的开发代理。","ja":"openspecエコシステム内で複数の変更を管理し、続けて作業する必要がある開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"openspec 생태계 내에서 여러 변경 사항을 관리하고 계속 작업해야 하는 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan gestionar y continuar trabajando en múltiples cambios dentro del ecosistema openspec.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de gérer et de continuer à travailler sur plusieurs modifications au sein de l''écosystème openspec.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsagenten, die mehrere Änderungen innerhalb des openspec-Ökosystems verwalten und weiter daran arbeiten müssen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam gerenciar e continuar trabalhando em várias alterações dentro do ecossistema openspec.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходимо управлять и продолжать работать над несколькими изменениями в экосистеме openspec.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة الاستمرار في العمل على عدة تغييرات داخل منظومة openspec."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to seamlessly continue working on changes by creating the next artifact, utilizing the openspec list command and AskUserQuestion tool to handle change selection, and supporting JSON output for streamlined processing.","zh":"通过创建下一个工件、利用openspec列表命令和AskUserQuestion工具处理更改选择，并支持JSON输出以实现流畅的处理，从而使代理能够无缝地继续处理更改。","ja":"次のアーティファクトを作成し、openspecリストコマンドとAskUserQuestionツールを使用して変更の選択を処理し、JSON出力をサポートすることで、エージェントが変更をシームレスに続行できるようにします。","ko":"다음 아티팩트를 생성하고 openspec 목록 명령과 AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 변경 선택을 처리하며 JSON 출력을 지원함으로써 에이전트가 변경을 무중단으로 계속할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a continuar trabajando en cambios de forma fluida creando el siguiente artefacto, utilizando el comando de lista openspec y la herramienta AskUserQuestion para manejar la selección de cambios, y admitiendo la salida JSON para un procesamiento optimizado.","fr":"Permet aux agents de continuer à travailler sur les modifications de manière fluide en créant le prochain artefact, en utilisant la commande de liste openspec et l''outil AskUserQuestion pour gérer la sélection des modifications, et en prenant en charge la sortie JSON pour un traitement optimisé.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Änderungen nahtlos fortzusetzen, indem sie das nächste Artefakt erstellen, den openspec-Listenbefehl und das Tool AskUserQuestion zur Änderungsauswahl verwenden und JSON-Ausgaben für ein optimiertes Verarbeiten unterstützen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a continuar trabalhando sem interrupção nas alterações, criando o próximo artefato, utilizando o comando de lista openspec e a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para lidar com a seleção de alterações, e suportando saída JSON para processamento simplificado.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью бесшовно продолжать работу над изменениями, создавая следующий артефакт, используя команду списка openspec и инструмент AskUserQuestion для обработки выбора изменений, и поддерживая вывод JSON для упрощенной обработки.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من الاستمرار في العمل على التغييرات بشكل متواصل من خلال إنشاء الملف التالي، واستخدام أمر قائمة openspec وأداة AskUserQuestion لمعالجة اختيار التغييرات، ودعم الإخراج JSON لمعالجة مبسطة."},"useCases":{"en":["Continuing interrupted changes","Managing multiple concurrent changes","Automating change artifact creation"],"zh":["继续中断的更改","管理多个并发更改","自动化更改工件创建"],"ja":["中断された変更の続行","複数の並行変更の管理","変更アーティファクトの自動作成"],"ko":["중단된 변경의 계속","여러 개의 병렬 변경을 관리","변경 아티팩트의 자동 생성"],"es":["Continuar cambios interrumpidos","Gestionar múltiples cambios concurrentes","Automatizar la creación de artefactos de cambio"],"fr":["Continuer les modifications interrompues","Gérer plusieurs modifications concurrentes","Automatiser la création d''artefacts de modification"],"de":["Unterbrochene Änderungen fortsetzen","Mehrere gleichzeitige Änderungen verwalten","Erstellung von Änderungsartefakten automatisieren"],"pt":["Continuar alterações interrompidas","Gerenciar várias alterações concorrentes","Automatizar a criação de artefatos de alterações"],"ru":["Продолжить прерванные изменения","Управлять несколькими одновременными изменениями","Автоматизировать создание артефактов изменений"],"ar":["استمرار التغييرات المتوقفة","إدارة التغييرات المتزامنة المتعددة","تأطير إنشاء ملفات التغييرات تلقائيًا"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires openspec installation and configuration","Dependent on conversation context for change name inference","Limited to top 3 changes for selection prompt"],"zh":["需要openspec安装和配置","依赖于对话上下文来推断更改名称","仅限于前3个更改用于选择提示"],"ja":["openspecのインストールと設定が必要","変更名の推論に会話のコンテキストに依存","選択プロンプトには最初の3つの変更のみが対象"],"ko":["openspec 설치 및 구성 필요","변경 이름 추론에 대화 문맥에 의존","선택 프롬프트는 첫 3개의 변경만 해당"],"es":["Requiere la instalación y configuración de openspec","Depende del contexto de conversación para inferir el nombre del cambio","Limitado a los 3 primeros cambios para la invitación de selección"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration d''openspec","Dépend du contexte de conversation pour inférer le nom de la modification","Limité aux 3 premières modifications pour l''invite de sélection"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation und Konfiguration von openspec","Hängt vom Konversationskontext ab, um den Änderungsnamen abzuleiten","Begrenzt auf die ersten 3 Änderungen für den Auswahlhinweis"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do openspec","Dependente do contexto da conversa para inferência do nome da alteração","Limitado aos 3 principais alterações para prompt de seleção"],"ru":["Требует установки и конфигурации openspec","Зависит от контекста разговора для вывода имени изменения","Ограничен до 3 лучших изменений для подсказки выбора"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين openspec","يعتمد على سياق المحادثة لاستنتاج اسم التغيير","محدود بالتغييرات الثلاث الأولى لتحفيز اختيار"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ollieb89/ml_challenges/sql-optimization-patterns', 'community', 'ollieb89', 'ml_challenges', 'ollieb89/ml_challenges', 'sql-optimization-patterns', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:19:12.127Z', NULL, '{"id":"ollieb89/ml_challenges/sql-optimization-patterns","name":"sql-optimization-patterns","description":{"zh":"SQL 优化模式是通过系统优化、适当索引和查询计划分析来提高数据库查询效率的方法","ja":"SQL 最適化パターンは、システム最適化、適切なインデックス作成、クエリプラン分析によってデータベースクエリの効率を高める方法です","ko":"SQL 최적화 패턴은 시스템 최적화, 적절한 인덱싱 및 쿼리 계획 분석을 통해 데이터베이스 쿼리 효율을 높이는 방식입니다","es":"Los patrones de optimización SQL permiten transformar consultas lentas en operaciones rápidas y eficientes. Mejora el rendimiento de tus bases de datos","fr":"Les modèles d''optimisation SQL permettent de transformer des requêtes lentes en opérations rapides et efficaces. Améliorez les performances de vos bases de données","de":"Muster für SQL-Optimierung ermöglichen die Umwandlung von langsamen Abfragen in schnelle und effiziente Operationen. Verbessern Sie die Leistung Ihrer Datenbanken","pt":"Otimização de SQL para transformar consultas lentas em operações rápidas e eficientes","ru":"Оптимизация SQL для преобразования медленных запросов в быстрые и эффективные операции","ar":"تحسين قواعد البيانات لجعل الاستفسارات البطيئة عمليات سريعة وفعالة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"SQL 优化模式","ja":"SQL 最適化パターン","ko":"SQL 최적화 패턴","es":"Patrones de Optimización SQL para Consultas Rápidas","fr":"Modèles d''Optimisation SQL pour des Requêtes Rapides","de":"Muster für SQL-Optimierung für Schnelle Abfragen","pt":"Otimização de SQL: Padrões para Consultas Rápidas","ru":"Оптимизация SQL: Шаблоны для Быстрых Запросов","ar":"تحسين قواعد البيانات: أنماط لجعل الاستفسارات أسرع","en":"sql-optimization-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"SQL 优化模式是通过系统优化、适当索引和查询计划分析来提高数据库查询效率的方法","ja":"SQL 最適化パターンは、システム最適化、適切なインデックス作成、クエリプラン分析によってデータベースクエリの効率を高める方法です","ko":"SQL 최적화 패턴은 시스템 최적화, 적절한 인덱싱 및 쿼리 계획 분석을 통해 데이터베이스 쿼리 효율을 높이는 방식입니다","es":"Los patrones de optimización SQL permiten transformar consultas lentas en operaciones rápidas y eficientes. Mejora el rendimiento de tus bases de datos","fr":"Les modèles d''optimisation SQL permettent de transformer des requêtes lentes en opérations rapides et efficaces. Améliorez les performances de vos bases de d...","de":"Muster für SQL-Optimierung ermöglichen die Umwandlung von langsamen Abfragen in schnelle und effiziente Operationen. Verbessern Sie die Leistung Ihrer Datenb...","pt":"Otimização de SQL para transformar consultas lentas em operações rápidas e eficientes","ru":"Оптимизация SQL для преобразования медленных запросов в быстрые и эффективные операции","ar":"تحسين قواعد البيانات لجعل الاستفسارات البطيئة عمليات سريعة وفعالة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["系统优化","适当索引","查询计划分析","调试慢速查询","设计高性能数据库架构"],"ja":["システム最適化","適切なインデックス作成","クエリプラン分析","遅いクエリのデバッグ","高性能データベーススキーマの設計"],"ko":["시스템 최적화","적절한 인덱싱","쿼리 계획 분석","느린 쿼리 디버깅","고성능 데이터베이스 스키마 설계"],"es":["Análisis de planes de consulta","Implementación de índices eficientes","Resolución de problemas de consulta N+1","Diseño de esquemas de base de datos performantes","Optimización de tiempos de respuesta de aplicaciones","Reducción de la carga y los costos de la base de datos"],"fr":["Analyse de plans de requête","Mise en œuvre d''index efficaces","Résolution de problèmes de requête N+1","Conception de schémas de base de données performants","Optimisation des temps de réponse des applications","Réduction de la charge et des coûts de la base de données"],"de":["Abfrageplananalyse","Implementierung effizienter Indizes","Lösung von N+1-Abfrageproblemen","Entwurf von performanten Datenbankschemata","Optimierung der Antwortzeiten von Anwendungen","Reduzierung der Last und der Kosten der Datenbank"],"pt":["Otimização sistemática de consultas","Indexação adequada para melhor desempenho","Análise de planos de consulta para identificar gargalos","Resolução de problemas de consultas N+1","Melhoria da escalabilidade para conjuntos de dados em crescimento"],"ru":["Систематическая оптимизация запросов","Правильное индексирование для лучшей производительности","Анализ планов запросов для выявления узких мест","Решение проблем с запросами N+1","Улучшение масштабируемости для растущих наборов данных"],"ar":["تحسين منهجي للاستفسارات","فهرسة مناسبة لتحسين الأداء","تحليل خطط الاستفسار لتحديد نقاط الضعف","حل مشاكل الاستفسارات N+1","تحسين القدرة على التوسع ل مجموعات البيانات المتزايدة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SQL 优化","数据库查询优化","系统优化","索引优化","查询计划分析","数据库性能优化"],"ja":["SQL 最適化","データベースクエリ最適化","システム最適化","インデックス最適化","クエリプラン分析","データベースパフォーマンス最適化"],"ko":["SQL 최적화","데이터베이스 쿼리 최적화","시스템 최적화","인덱스 최적화","쿼리 계획 분석","데이터베이스 성능 최적화"],"es":["optimización sql","patrones de optimización","consultas rápidas","indexing","análisis de planes de consulta","diseño de bases de datos","tiempos de respuesta de aplicaciones","reducción de costos"],"fr":["optimisation sql","modèles d''optimisation","requêtes rapides","indexation","analyse de plans de requête","conception de bases de données","temps de réponse des applications","réduction de coûts"],"de":["sql-optimierung","muster für optimierung","schnelle abfragen","indexierung","abfrageplananalyse","entwurf von datenbanken","antwortzeiten von anwendungen","kostenreduzierung"],"pt":["otimização de sql","consultas de banco de dados","indexação","análise de planos de consulta","consultas n+1","escalabilidade de banco de dados"],"ru":["оптимизация sql","запросы базы данных","индексирование","анализ планов запросов","запросы n+1","масштабируемость базы данных"],"ar":["تحسين قواعد البيانات","استفسارات قواعد البيانات","فهرسة","تحليل خطط الاستفسار","استفسارات n+1","توسع قواعد البيانات"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"ml_challenges","repoPath":"ollieb89/ml_challenges","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"sql-optimization-patterns","description":"Master SQL query optimization, indexing strategies, and EXPLAIN analysis to dramatically improve database performance and eliminate slow queries. Use when debugging slow queries, designing database schemas, or optimizing application performance.","bodyPreview":"# SQL Optimization Patterns\n\nTransform slow database queries into lightning-fast operations through systematic optimization, proper indexing, and query plan analysis.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Debugging slow-running queries\n- Designing performant database schemas\n- Optimizing application response times\n- Reducing database load and costs\n- Improving scalability for growing datasets\n- Analyzing EXPLAIN query plans\n- Implementing efficient indexes\n- Resolving N+1 query problems\n\n## Core Concept","body":"# SQL Optimization Patterns\n\nTransform slow database queries into lightning-fast operations through systematic optimization, proper indexing, and query plan analysis.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Debugging slow-running queries\n- Designing performant database schemas\n- Optimizing application response times\n- Reducing database load and costs\n- Improving scalability for growing datasets\n- Analyzing EXPLAIN query plans\n- Implementing efficient indexes\n- Resolving N+1 query problems\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Query Execution Plans (EXPLAIN)\n\nUnderstanding EXPLAIN output is fundamental to optimization.\n\n**PostgreSQL EXPLAIN:**\n```sql\n-- Basic explain\nEXPLAIN SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ''user@example.com'';\n\n-- With actual execution stats\nEXPLAIN ANALYZE\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ''user@example.com'';\n\n-- Verbose output with more details\nEXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS, VERBOSE)\nSELECT u.*, o.order_total\nFROM users u\nJOIN orders o ON u.id = o.user_id\nWHERE u.created_at > NOW() - INTERVAL ''30 days'';\n```\n\n**Key Metrics to Watch:**\n- **Seq Scan**: Full table scan (usually slow for large tables)\n- **Index Scan**: Using index (good)\n- **Index Only Scan**: Using index without touching table (best)\n- **Nested Loop**: Join method (okay for small datasets)\n- **Hash Join**: Join method (good for larger datasets)\n- **Merge Join**: Join method (good for sorted data)\n- **Cost**: Estimated query cost (lower is better)\n- **Rows**: Estimated rows returned\n- **Actual Time**: Real execution time\n\n### 2. Index Strategies\n\nIndexes are the most powerful optimization tool.\n\n**Index Types:**\n- **B-Tree**: Default, good for equality and range queries\n- **Hash**: Only for equality (=) comparisons\n- **GIN**: Full-text search, array queries, JSONB\n- **GiST**: Geometric data, full-text search\n- **BRIN**: Block Range INdex for very large tables with correlation\n\n```sql\n-- Standard B-Tree index\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_email ON users(email);\n\n-- Composite index (order matters!)\nCREATE INDEX idx_orders_user_status ON orders(user_id, status);\n\n-- Partial index (index subset of rows)\nCREATE INDEX idx_active_users ON users(email)\nWHERE status = ''active'';\n\n-- Expression index\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_lower_email ON users(LOWER(email));\n\n-- Covering index (include additional columns)\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_email_covering ON users(email)\nINCLUDE (name, created_at);\n\n-- Full-text search index\nCREATE INDEX idx_posts_search ON posts\nUSING GIN(to_tsvector(''english'', title || '' '' || body));\n\n-- JSONB index\nCREATE INDEX idx_metadata ON events USING GIN(metadata);\n```\n\n### 3. Query Optimization Patterns\n\n**Avoid SELECT \\*:**\n```sql\n-- Bad: Fetches unnecessary columns\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE id = 123;\n\n-- Good: Fetch only what you need\nSELECT id, email, name FROM users WHERE id = 123;\n```\n\n**Use WHERE Clause Efficiently:**\n```sql\n-- Bad: Function prevents index usage\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE LOWER(email) = ''user@example.com'';\n\n-- Good: Create functional index or use exact match\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_email_lower ON users(LOWER(email));\n-- Then:\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE LOWER(email) = ''user@example.com'';\n\n-- Or store normalized data\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ''user@example.com'';\n```\n\n**Optimize JOINs:**\n```sql\n-- Bad: Cartesian product then filter\nSELECT u.name, o.total\nFROM users u, orders o\nWHERE u.id = o.user_id AND u.created_at > ''2024-01-01'';\n\n-- Good: Filter before join\nSELECT u.name, o.total\nFROM users u\nJOIN orders o ON u.id = o.user_id\nWHERE u.created_at > ''2024-01-01'';\n\n-- Better: Filter both tables\nSELECT u.name, o.total\nFROM (SELECT * FROM users WHERE created_at > ''2024-01-01'') u\nJOIN orders o ON u.id = o.user_id;\n```\n\n## Optimization Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Eliminate N+1 Queries\n\n**Problem: N+1 Query Anti-Pattern**\n```python\n# Bad: Executes N+1 queries\nusers = db.query(\"SELECT * FROM users LIMIT 10\")\nfor user in users:\n    orders = db.query(\"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE user_id = ?\", user.id)\n    # Process orders\n```\n\n**Solution: Use JOINs or Batch Loading**\n```sql\n-- Solution 1: JOIN\nSELECT\n    u.id, u.name,\n    o.id as order_id, o.total\nFROM users u\nLEFT JOIN orders o ON u.id = o.user_id\nWHERE u.id IN (1, 2, 3, 4, 5);\n\n-- Solution 2: Batch query\nSELECT * FROM orders\nWHERE user_id IN (1, 2, 3, 4, 5);\n```\n\n```python\n# Good: Single query with JOIN or batch load\n# Using JOIN\nresults = db.query(\"\"\"\n    SELECT u.id, u.name, o.id as order_id, o.total\n    FROM users u\n    LEFT JOIN orders o ON u.id = o.user_id\n    WHERE u.id IN (1, 2, 3, 4, 5)\n\"\"\")\n\n# Or batch load\nusers = db.query(\"SELECT * FROM users LIMIT 10\")\nuser_ids = [u.id for u in users]\norders = db.query(\n    \"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE user_id IN (?)\",\n    user_ids\n)\n# Group orders by user_id\norders_by_user = {}\nfor order in orders:\n    orders_by_user.setdefault(order.user_id, []).append(order)\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Optimize Pagination\n\n**Bad: OFFSET on Large Tables**\n```sql\n-- Slow for large offsets\nSELECT * FROM users\nORDER BY created_at DESC\nLIMIT 20 OFFSET 100000;  -- Very slow!\n```\n\n**Good: Cursor-Based Pagination**\n```sql\n-- Much faster: Use cursor (last seen ID)\nSELECT * FROM users\nWHERE created_at < ''2024-01-15 10:30:00''  -- Last cursor\nORDER BY created_at DESC\nLIMIT 20;\n\n-- With composite sorting\nSELECT * FROM users\nWHERE (created_at, id) < (''2024-01-15 10:30:00'', 12345)\nORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC\nLIMIT 20;\n\n-- Requires index\nCREATE INDEX idx_users_cursor ON users(created_at DESC, id DESC);\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Aggregate Efficiently\n\n**Optimize COUNT Queries:**\n```sql\n-- Bad: Counts all rows\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders;  -- Slow on large tables\n\n-- Good: Use estimates for approximate counts\nSELECT reltuples::bigint AS estimate\nFROM pg_class\nWHERE relname = ''orders'';\n\n-- Good: Filter before counting\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders\nWHERE created_at > NOW() - INTERVAL ''7 days'';\n\n-- Better: Use index-only scan\nCREATE INDEX idx_orders_created ON orders(created_at);\nSELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders\nWHERE created_at > NOW() - INTERVAL ''7 days'';\n```\n\n**Optimize GROUP BY:**\n```sql\n-- Bad: Group by then filter\nSELECT user_id, COUNT(*) as order_count\nFROM orders\nGROUP BY user_id\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 10;\n\n-- Better: Filter first, then group (if possible)\nSELECT user_id, COUNT(*) as order_count\nFROM orders\nWHERE status = ''completed''\nGROUP BY user_id\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 10;\n\n-- Best: Use covering index\nCREATE INDEX idx_orders_user_status ON orders(user_id, status);\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Subquery Optimization\n\n**Transform Correlated Subqueries:**\n```sql\n-- Bad: Correlated subquery (runs for each row)\nSELECT u.name, u.email,\n    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders o WHERE o.user_id = u.id) as order_count\nFROM users u;\n\n-- Good: JOIN with aggregation\nSELECT u.name, u.email, COUNT(o.id) as order_count\nFROM users u\nLEFT JOIN orders o ON o.user_id = u.id\nGROUP BY u.id, u.name, u.email;\n\n-- Better: Use window functions\nSELECT DISTINCT ON (u.id)\n    u.name, u.email,\n    COUNT(o.id) OVER (PARTITION BY u.id) as order_count\nFROM users u\nLEFT JOIN orders o ON o.user_id = u.id;\n```\n\n**Use CTEs for Clarity:**\n```sql\n-- Using Common Table Expressions\nWITH recent_users AS (\n    SELECT id, name, email\n    FROM users\n    WHERE created_at > NOW() - INTERVAL ''30 days''\n),\nuser_order_counts AS (\n    SELECT user_id, COUNT(*) as order_count\n    FROM orders\n    WHERE created_at > NOW() - INTERVAL ''30 days''\n    GROUP BY user_id\n)\nSELECT ru.name, ru.email, COALESCE(uoc.order_count, 0) as orders\nFROM recent_users ru\nLEFT JOIN user_order_counts uoc ON ru.id = uoc.user_id;\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Batch Operations\n\n**Batch INSERT:**\n```sql\n-- Bad: Multiple individual inserts\nINSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES (''Alice'', ''alice@example.com'');\nINSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES (''Bob'', ''bob@example.com'');\nINSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES (''Carol'', ''carol@example.com'');\n\n-- Good: Batch insert\nINSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES\n    (''Alice'', ''alice@example.com''),\n    (''Bob'', ''bob@example.com''),\n    (''Carol'', ''carol@example.com'');\n\n-- Better: Use COPY for bulk inserts (PostgreSQL)\nCOPY users (name, email) FROM ''/tmp/users.csv'' CSV HEADER;\n```\n\n**Batch UPDATE:**\n```sql\n-- Bad: Update in loop\nUPDATE users SET status = ''active'' WHERE id = 1;\nUPDATE users SET status = ''active'' WHERE id = 2;\n-- ... repeat for many IDs\n\n-- Good: Single UPDATE with IN clause\nUPDATE users\nSET status = ''active''\nWHERE id IN (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, ...);\n\n-- Better: Use temporary table for large batches\nCREATE TEMP TABLE temp_user_updates (id INT, new_status VARCHAR);\nINSERT INTO temp_user_updates VALUES (1, ''active''), (2, ''active''), ...;\n\nUPDATE users u\nSET status = t.new_status\nFROM temp_user_updates t\nWHERE u.id = t.id;\n```\n\n## Advanced Techniques\n\n### Materialized Views\n\nPre-compute expensive queries.\n\n```sql\n-- Create materialized view\nCREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW user_order_summary AS\nSELECT\n    u.id,\n    u.name,\n    COUNT(o.id) as total_orders,\n    SUM(o.total) as total_spent,\n    MAX(o.created_at) as last_order_date\nFROM users u\nLEFT JOIN orders o ON u.id = o.user_id\nGROUP BY u.id, u.name;\n\n-- Add index to materialized view\nCREATE INDEX idx_user_summary_spent ON user_order_summary(total_spent DESC);\n\n-- Refresh materialized view\nREFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW user_order_summary;\n\n-- Concurrent refresh (PostgreSQL)\nREFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY user_order_summary;\n\n-- Query materialized view (very fast)\nSELECT * FROM user_order_summary\nWHERE total_spent > 1000\nORDER BY total_spent DESC;\n```\n\n### Partitioning\n\nSplit large tables for better performance.\n\n```sql\n-- Range partitioning by date (PostgreSQL)\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n    id SERIAL,\n    user_id INT,\n    total DECIMAL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMP\n) PARTITION BY RANGE (created_at);\n\n-- Create partitions\nCREATE TABLE orders_2024_q1 PARTITION OF orders\n    FOR VALUES FROM (''2024-01-01'') TO (''2024-04-01'');\n\nCREATE TABLE orders_2024_q2 PARTITION OF orders\n    FOR VALUES FROM (''2024-04-01'') TO (''2024-07-01'');\n\n-- Queries automatically use appropriate partition\nSELECT * FROM orders\nWHERE created_at BETWEEN ''2024-02-01'' AND ''2024-02-28'';\n-- Only scans orders_2024_q1 partition\n```\n\n### Query Hints and Optimization\n\n```sql\n-- Force index usage (MySQL)\nSELECT * FROM users\nUSE INDEX (idx_users_email)\nWHERE email = ''user@example.com'';\n\n-- Parallel query (PostgreSQL)\nSET max_parallel_workers_per_gather = 4;\nSELECT * FROM large_table WHERE condition;\n\n-- Join hints (PostgreSQL)\nSET enable_nestloop = OFF;  -- Force hash or merge join\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Index Selectively**: Too many indexes slow down writes\n2. **Monitor Query Performance**: Use slow query logs\n3. **Keep Statistics Updated**: Run ANALYZE regularly\n4. **Use Appropriate Data Types**: Smaller types = better performance\n5. **Normalize Thoughtfully**: Balance normalization vs performance\n6. **Cache Frequently Accessed Data**: Use application-level caching\n7. **Connection Pooling**: Reuse database connections\n8. **Regular Maintenance**: VACUUM, ANALYZE, rebuild indexes\n\n```sql\n-- Update statistics\nANALYZE users;\nANALYZE VERBOSE orders;\n\n-- Vacuum (PostgreSQL)\nVACUUM ANALYZE users;\nVACUUM FULL users;  -- Reclaim space (locks table)\n\n-- Reindex\nREINDEX INDEX idx_users_email;\nREINDEX TABLE users;\n```\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Over-Indexing**: Each index slows down INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE\n- **Unused Indexes**: Waste space and slow writes\n- **Missing Indexes**: Slow queries, full table scans\n- **Implicit Type Conversion**: Prevents index usage\n- **OR Conditions**: Can''t use indexes efficiently\n- **LIKE with Leading Wildcard**: `LIKE ''%abc''` can''t use index\n- **Function in WHERE**: Prevents index usage unless functional index exists\n\n## Monitoring Queries\n\n```sql\n-- Find slow queries (PostgreSQL)\nSELECT query, calls, total_time, mean_time\nFROM pg_stat_statements\nORDER BY mean_time DESC\nLIMIT 10;\n\n-- Find missing indexes (PostgreSQL)\nSELECT\n    schemaname,\n    tablename,\n    seq_scan,\n    seq_tup_read,\n    idx_scan,\n    seq_tup_read / seq_scan AS avg_seq_tup_read\nFROM pg_stat_user_tables\nWHERE seq_scan > 0\nORDER BY seq_tup_read DESC\nLIMIT 10;\n\n-- Find unused indexes (PostgreSQL)\nSELECT\n    schemaname,\n    tablename,\n    indexname,\n    idx_scan,\n    idx_tup_read,\n    idx_tup_fetch\nFROM pg_stat_user_indexes\nWHERE idx_scan = 0\nORDER BY pg_relation_size(indexrelid) DESC;\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/postgres-optimization-guide.md**: PostgreSQL-specific optimization\n- **references/mysql-optimization-guide.md**: MySQL/MariaDB optimization\n- **references/query-plan-analysis.md**: Deep dive into EXPLAIN plans\n- **assets/index-strategy-checklist.md**: When and how to create indexes\n- **assets/query-optimization-checklist.md**: Step-by-step optimization guide\n- **scripts/analyze-slow-queries.sql**: Identify slow queries in your database\n- **scripts/index-recommendations.sql**: Generate index recommendations\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:19:12.127Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced SQL optimization capabilities for efficient database querying.","zh":"非常适合需要高级SQL优化功能以实现高效数据库查询的数据分析智能体。","ja":"効率的なデータベースクエリのための高度なSQL最適化機能を必要とするデータ分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"효율적인 데이터베이스 쿼리를 위해 고급 SQL 최적화 기능이 필요한 데이터 분석 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de datos que necesitan capacidades de optimización de SQL avanzadas para consultas de bases de datos eficientes.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données ayant besoin de capacités d''optimisation de SQL avancées pour des requêtes de base de données efficaces.","de":"Perfekt für Datenanalyseagenten, die erweiterte SQL-Optimierungsfunktionen für effiziente Datenbankabfragen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de otimização do SQL para consultas de banco de dados eficientes.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа данных, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности оптимизации SQL для эффективного запроса базы данных.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل البيانات التي تحتاج إلى возможности متقدمة لتحسين الاستعلامات المكتوبة بلغة SQL من أجل استعلام قواعد البيانات بكفاءة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform slow database queries into lightning-fast operations through systematic optimization, proper indexing, and query plan analysis using EXPLAIN query plans and efficient indexing techniques.","zh":"通过系统性优化、适当的索引以及使用EXPLAIN查询计划和高效索引技术进行查询计划分析，使智能体能够将缓慢的数据库查询转变为闪电般快速的操作。","ja":"体系的な最適化、適切なインデックス作成、EXPLAINクエリプランと効率的なインデックス技術を使用したクエリプラン分析を通じて、エージェントが低速なデータベースクエリを超高速な操作に変換することを可能にします。","ko":"체계적인 최적화, 적절한 인덱싱, EXPLAIN 쿼리 플랜 및 효율적인 인덱싱 기술을 사용한 쿼리 플랜 분석을 통해 에이전트가 느린 데이터베이스 쿼리를 매우 빠른 작업으로 변환할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes transformar consultas de base de datos lentas en operaciones de alta velocidad a través de la optimización sistemática, la indexación adecuada y el análisis de planes de consulta utilizando planes de consulta EXPLAIN y técnicas de indexación eficientes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer des requêtes de base de données lentes en opérations à haute vitesse grâce à l''optimisation systématique, à l''indexation appropriée et à l''analyse des plans de requête à l''aide de plans de requête EXPLAIN et de techniques d''indexation efficaces.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, langsame Datenbankabfragen in blitzschnelle Operationen durch systematische Optimierung, ordnungsgemäße Indexierung und Abfrageplananalyse unter Verwendung von EXPLAIN-Abfrageplänen und effizienten Indexierungstechniken umzuwandeln.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar consultas de banco de dados lentas em operações de alta velocidade por meio da otimização sistemática, indexação adequada e análise do plano de consulta usando planos de consulta EXPLAIN e técnicas de indexação eficientes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью превратить медленные запросы базы данных в молниеносные операции посредством систематической оптимизации, правильного индексирования и анализа плана запроса с использованием планов запросов EXPLAIN и эффективных методов индексирования.","ar":"تمكّن العميل من تحويل استعلامات قواعد البيانات البطيئة إلى عمليات سريعة جداً من خلال التحسين المنهجي والفهرسة المناسبة وتحليل خطة الاستعلام باستخدام خطط استعلام EXPLAIN وتقنيات الفهرسة الفعالة."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging slow-running queries to improve application response times","Designing performant database schemas for reduced database load and costs","Optimizing database queries to improve scalability for growing datasets"],"zh":["调试运行缓慢的查询以改善应用程序响应时间","设计高性能数据库模式以减少数据库负载和成本","优化数据库查询以提高不断增长的数据集的可扩展性"],"ja":["アプリケーションの応答時間を改善するための低速クエリのデバッグ","データベースの負荷とコストを削減するための高性能データベーススキーマの設計","成長するデータセットのスケーラビリティを向上させるためのデータベースクエリの最適化"],"ko":["애플리케이션 응답 시간을 개선하기 위해 실행 속도가 느린 쿼리 디버깅","데이터베이스 부하와 비용을 줄이기 위한 성능 중심 데이터베이스 스키마 설계","성장하는 데이터 세트의 확장성을 개선하기 위해 데이터베이스 쿼리 최적화"],"es":["Depuración de consultas de ejecución lenta para mejorar los tiempos de respuesta de la aplicación","Diseño de esquemas de base de datos de alto rendimiento para reducir la carga y los costos de la base de datos","Optimización de consultas de base de datos para mejorar la escalabilidad para conjuntos de datos en crecimiento"],"fr":["Débogage des requêtes à exécution lente pour améliorer les temps de réponse de l''application","Conception de schémas de base de données performants pour réduire la charge et les coûts de la base de données","Optimisation des requêtes de base de données pour améliorer la scalabilité pour les ensembles de données en croissance"],"de":["Debuggen langsam ablaufender Abfragen, um die Antwortzeiten der Anwendung zu verbessern","Entwurf von leistungsstarken Datenbankschemata, um die Datenbanklast und -kosten zu reduzieren","Optimierung von Datenbankabfragen, um die Skalierbarkeit für wachsende Datensätze zu verbessern"],"pt":["Depuração de consultas de execução lenta para melhorar os tempos de resposta do aplicativo","Projeto de esquemas de banco de dados performáticos para reduzir a carga e os custos do banco de dados","Otimização de consultas de banco de dados para melhorar a escalabilidade para conjuntos de dados em crescimento"],"ru":["Отладка медленных запросов для улучшения времени ответа приложения","Проектирование производительных схем базы данных для уменьшения нагрузки и затрат на базу данных","Оптимизация запросов базы данных для улучшения масштабируемости для растущих наборов данных"],"ar":["تصحيح الأعطال في الاستعلامات التي تعمل ببطء لتحسين أوقات الاستجابة للتطبيق","تصميم مخططات قواعد البيانات عالية الأداء لتقليل حمل قواعد البيانات والتكاليف","تحسين استعلامات قواعد البيانات لتحسين القدرة على التوسع لمجموعات البيان