Prisma.io node.js 백엔드","구현이 변경 문서와 일치하는지 검증","변경 이름 지정 지원","변경 이름이 지정되지 않은 경우 사용자에게 선택을 요청","AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자에게 선택을 요청","구현 작업이 있는 변경을 표시"],"es":["Verificación de cambios en la implementación","Uso de GraphQL y Prisma.io para nodos de JavaScript","Opción para especificar un nombre de cambio","Compatibilidad con la herramienta AskUserQuestion","Listado de cambios disponibles con la opción --json"],"fr":["Vérification de modifications dans l''implémentation","Utilisation de GraphQL et Prisma.io pour les nœuds JavaScript","Option pour spécifier un nom de modification","Compatibilité avec l''outil AskUserQuestion","Liste des modifications disponibles avec l''option --json"],"de":["Überprüfung von Änderungen in der Implementierung","Verwendung von GraphQL und Prisma.io für JavaScript-Knoten","Option zur Angabe eines Änderungsnamens","Kompatibilität mit dem Tool AskUserQuestion","Liste der verfügbaren Änderungen mit der Option --json"],"pt":["Verificação de alterações de especificação","Utiliza GraphQL e Prisma.io","Integração com o AskUserQuestion tool","Suporte à seleção de alterações","Executa o comando openspec list --json","Mostra alterações com tarefas de implementação"],"ru":["Проверка изменений спецификации","Использует GraphQL и Prisma.io","Интеграция с AskUserQuestion tool","Поддержка выбора изменений","Выполняет команду openspec list --json","Показывает изменения с задачами реализации"],"ar":["التحقق من التغييرات في المواصفات","يستخدم GraphQL و Prisma.io","التكامل مع أداة AskUserQuestion","دعم اختيار التغييرات","ينفذ الأمر openspec list --json","يعرض التغييرات ذات مهام التنفيذ"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-verify-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","node.js","后端","技术验证","变更文档","实现验证"],"ja":["openspec-verify-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","node.js","バックエンド","技術検証","変更ドキュメント","実装検証"],"ko":["openspec-verify-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","node.js","백엔드","기술 검증","변경 문서","구현 검증"],"es":["openspec","verificación de cambios","graphql","prisma.io","nodos de javascript","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","askuserquestion"],"fr":["openspec","vérification de modifications","graphql","prisma.io","nœuds javascript","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","askuserquestion"],"de":["openspec","änderungsüberprüfung","graphql","prisma.io","javascript-knoten","softwareentwicklung","entwicklungstools","askuserquestion"],"pt":["openspec-verify-change","verificação de alterações","GraphQL","Prisma.io","AskUserQuestion tool","seleção de alterações","comando openspec list --json","tarefas de implementação"],"ru":["openspec-verify-change","проверка изменений","GraphQL","Prisma.io","AskUserQuestion tool","выбор изменений","команда openspec list --json","задачи реализации"],"ar":["openspec-verify-change","التحقق من التغييرات","GraphQL","Prisma.io","أداة AskUserQuestion","اختيار التغييرات","الأمر openspec list --json","مهام التنفيذ"]}},"owner":"uxname","repo":"liteend","repoPath":"uxname/liteend","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-verify-change","description":"Verify implementation matches change artifacts. Use when the user wants to validate that implementation is complete, correct, and coherent before archiving.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifa","body":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifact exists).\n   Include the schema used for each change if available.\n   Mark changes with incomplete tasks as \"(In Progress)\".\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check status to understand the schema**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - Which artifacts exist for this change\n\n3. **Get the change directory and load artifacts**\n\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions apply --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n\n   This returns the change directory and context files. Read all available artifacts from `contextFiles`.\n\n4. **Initialize verification report structure**\n\n   Create a report structure with three dimensions:\n   - **Completeness**: Track tasks and spec coverage\n   - **Correctness**: Track requirement implementation and scenario coverage\n   - **Coherence**: Track design adherence and pattern consistency\n\n   Each dimension can have CRITICAL, WARNING, or SUGGESTION issues.\n\n5. **Verify Completeness**\n\n   **Task Completion**:\n   - If tasks.md exists in contextFiles, read it\n   - Parse checkboxes: `- [ ]` (incomplete) vs `- [x]` (complete)\n   - Count complete vs total tasks\n   - If incomplete tasks exist:\n     - Add CRITICAL issue for each incomplete task\n     - Recommendation: \"Complete task: <description>\" or \"Mark as done if already implemented\"\n\n   **Spec Coverage**:\n   - If delta specs exist in `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/`:\n     - Extract all requirements (marked with \"### Requirement:\")\n     - For each requirement:\n       - Search codebase for keywords related to the requirement\n       - Assess if implementation likely exists\n     - If requirements appear unimplemented:\n       - Add CRITICAL issue: \"Requirement not found: <requirement name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Implement requirement X: <description>\"\n\n6. **Verify Correctness**\n\n   **Requirement Implementation Mapping**:\n   - For each requirement from delta specs:\n     - Search codebase for implementation evidence\n     - If found, note file paths and line ranges\n     - Assess if implementation matches requirement intent\n     - If divergence detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Implementation may diverge from spec: <details>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Review <file>:<lines> against requirement X\"\n\n   **Scenario Coverage**:\n   - For each scenario in delta specs (marked with \"#### Scenario:\"):\n     - Check if conditions are handled in code\n     - Check if tests exist covering the scenario\n     - If scenario appears uncovered:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Scenario not covered: <scenario name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Add test or implementation for scenario: <description>\"\n\n7. **Verify Coherence**\n\n   **Design Adherence**:\n   - If design.md exists in contextFiles:\n     - Extract key decisions (look for sections like \"Decision:\", \"Approach:\", \"Architecture:\")\n     - Verify implementation follows those decisions\n     - If contradiction detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Design decision not followed: <decision>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Update implementation or revise design.md to match reality\"\n   - If no design.md: Skip design adherence check, note \"No design.md to verify against\"\n\n   **Code Pattern Consistency**:\n   - Review new code for consistency with project patterns\n   - Check file naming, directory structure, coding style\n   - If significant deviations found:\n     - Add SUGGESTION: \"Code pattern deviation: <details>\"\n     - Recommendation: \"Consider following project pattern: <example>\"\n\n8. **Generate Verification Report**\n\n   **Summary Scorecard**:\n   ```\n   ## Verification Report: <change-name>\n\n   ### Summary\n   | Dimension    | Status           |\n   |--------------|------------------|\n   | Completeness | X/Y tasks, N reqs|\n   | Correctness  | M/N reqs covered |\n   | Coherence    | Followed/Issues  |\n   ```\n\n   **Issues by Priority**:\n\n   1. **CRITICAL** (Must fix before archive):\n      - Incomplete tasks\n      - Missing requirement implementations\n      - Each with specific, actionable recommendation\n\n   2. **WARNING** (Should fix):\n      - Spec/design divergences\n      - Missing scenario coverage\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   3. **SUGGESTION** (Nice to fix):\n      - Pattern inconsistencies\n      - Minor improvements\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   **Final Assessment**:\n   - If CRITICAL issues: \"X critical issue(s) found. Fix before archiving.\"\n   - If only warnings: \"No critical issues. Y warning(s) to consider. Ready for archive (with noted improvements).\"\n   - If all clear: \"All checks passed. Ready for archive.\"\n\n**Verification Heuristics**\n\n- **Completeness**: Focus on objective checklist items (checkboxes, requirements list)\n- **Correctness**: Use keyword search, file path analysis, reasonable inference - don''t require perfect certainty\n- **Coherence**: Look for glaring inconsistencies, don''t nitpick style\n- **False Positives**: When uncertain, prefer SUGGESTION over WARNING, WARNING over CRITICAL\n- **Actionability**: Every issue must have a specific recommendation with file/line references where applicable\n\n**Graceful Degradation**\n\n- If only tasks.md exists: verify task completion only, skip spec/design checks\n- If tasks + specs exist: verify completeness and correctness, skip design\n- If full artifacts: verify all three dimensions\n- Always note which checks were skipped and why\n\n**Output Format**\n\nUse clear markdown with:\n- Table for summary scorecard\n- Grouped lists for issues (CRITICAL/WARNING/SUGGESTION)\n- Code references in format: `file.ts:123`\n- Specific, actionable recommendations\n- No vague suggestions like \"consider reviewing\"\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:20:28.482Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Node.js Agents requiring GraphQL and Prisma.io integration for change verification and implementation matching.","zh":"适用于需要GraphQL和Prisma.io集成以进行变更验证和实现匹配的Node.js代理。","ja":"GraphQLおよびPrisma.ioを使用した変更の検証と実装の一致を必要とするNode.jsエージェントに適しています。","ko":"GraphQL 및 Prisma.io 통합을 통해 변경 사항을 확인하고 구현을 일치시키는 Node.js 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de Node.js que requieren integración de GraphQL y Prisma.io para verificación de cambios y coincidencia de implementación.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Node.js nécessitant une intégration GraphQL et Prisma.io pour la vérification des modifications et la correspondance de la mise en œuvre.","de":"Ideal für Node.js-Agents, die eine GraphQL- und Prisma.io-Integration für Änderungsverifizierung und Implementierungsübereinstimmung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes Node.js que exigem integração do GraphQL e do Prisma.io para verificação de alterações e correspondência de implementação.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Node.js, требующих интеграции GraphQL и Prisma.io для проверки изменений и соответствия реализации.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء Node.js الذين يتطلبون دمج GraphQL و Prisma.io للتحقق من التغييرات وطابق التنفيذ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to verify implementation matches change artifacts using GraphQL and Prisma.io, providing a lightweight node.js backend for openspec verification, and leveraging the AskUserQuestion tool for user selection and conversation context inference.","zh":"赋予代理验证实现是否与变更文档匹配的能力，使用GraphQL和Prisma.io，提供轻量级的node.js后端用于openspec验证，并利用AskUserQuestion工具进行用户选择和会话上下文推理。","ja":"GraphQLおよびPrisma.ioを使用して、実装が変更成果物と一致することをエージェントが検証できるようにし、openspecの検証用に軽量なnode.jsバックエンドを提供し、AskUserQuestionツールを使用してユーザーの選択と会話のコンテキストの推論を行う。","ko":"에이전트가 구현이 변경 아티팩트와 일치하는지 확인할 수 있도록 하는 기능을 제공합니다. GraphQL 및 Prisma.io를 사용하여 openspec 검증을 위한 경량 node.js 백엔드를 제공하고 AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자 선택 및 대화 문脈 추론을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a verificar que la implementación coincide con los artefactos de cambio utilizando GraphQL y Prisma.io, proporcionando un backend de node.js ligero para la verificación de openspec y aprovechando la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la selección del usuario y la inferencia del contexto de conversación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier que la mise en œuvre correspond aux artefacts de modification à l''aide de GraphQL et Prisma.io, en fournissant un backend node.js léger pour la vérification openspec et en exploitant l''outil AskUserQuestion pour la sélection de l''utilisateur et l''inférence du contexte de conversation.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Implementierung mit Änderungsartefakten mithilfe von GraphQL und Prisma.io zu überprüfen, indem ein leichtes node.js-Backend für die Überprüfung von openspec bereitgestellt und das Tool AskUserQuestion für die Benutzerauswahl und die Inferenz des Konversationskontexts genutzt wird.","pt":"Permite que os agentes verifiquem se a implementação corresponde aos artefatos de alteração usando o GraphQL e o Prisma.io, fornecendo um backend leve do node.js para verificação do openspec e utilizando a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para seleção do usuário e inferência de contexto de conversa.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять соответствие реализации артефактам изменений с помощью GraphQL и Prisma.io, обеспечивая легкийbackend node.js для проверки openspec и использует инструмент AskUserQuestion для выбора пользователя и вывода контекста разговора.","ar":"يسمح للوكلاء بالتحقق من تطابق التنفيذ مع مقتطفات التغيير باستخدام GraphQL و Prisma.io، مع توفير خلفية خفيفة من node.js للتحقق من openspec، واستخدام أداة AskUserQuestion لتحديد المستخدم واستنتاج سياق المحادثة."},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying implementation against change specifications","Automating change artifact validation using openspec list and AskUserQuestion tools","Debugging implementation mismatches with inferred change names from conversation context"],"zh":["验证实现是否符合变更规格","使用openspec列表和AskUserQuestion工具自动验证变更成果物","使用对话上下文推理的变更名称调试实现不匹配"],"ja":["実装が変更の仕様と一致することを検証する","openspecリストとAskUserQuestionツールを使用して変更のアーティファクトを自動検証する","会話のコンテキストから推論された変更名を使用して実装の不一致をデバッグする"],"ko":["구현이 변경 사양과 일치하는지 확인","openspec 목록 및 AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 변경 아티팩트를 자동으로 검증","대화 문脈에서 추론한 변경 이름을 사용하여 구현 불일치를 디버깅"],"es":["Verificar la implementación frente a las especificaciones de cambio","Automatizar la validación de artefactos de cambio mediante las herramientas openspec y AskUserQuestion","Depurar las discrepancias de implementación con nombres de cambios inferidos del contexto de conversación"],"fr":["Vérifier la mise en œuvre par rapport aux spécifications de modification","Automatiser la validation des artefacts de modification à l''aide des outils openspec et AskUserQuestion","Déboguer les discordances de mise en œuvre avec des noms de modifications déduits du contexte de conversation"],"de":["Überprüfen der Implementierung gegenüber den Änderungsspezifikationen","Automatisieren der Überprüfung von Änderungsartefakten mithilfe der openspec- und AskUserQuestion-Tools","Fehlerbehebung bei Implementierungsunterschieden mit aus dem Konversationskontext abgeleiteten Änderungsnamen"],"pt":["Verificar a implementação contra especificações de alterações","Automatizar a validação de artefatos de alteração usando as ferramentas openspec list e AskUserQuestion","Depurar discrepâncias de implementação com nomes de alterações inferidos do contexto da conversa"],"ru":["Проверка реализации против спецификаций изменений","Автоматизация проверки артефактов изменений с помощью инструментов openspec list и AskUserQuestion","Отладка несоответствий реализации с именами изменений, выведенных из контекста разговора"],"ar":["التحقق من التنفيذ ضد مواصفات التغييرات","تأهيل التحقق من مقتطفات التغيير باستخدام أدوات openspec list و AskUserQuestion","تصحيح أخطاء التنفيذ مع أسماء التغييرات المستنبطة من سياق المحادثة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires node.js environment","Dependent on Prisma.io and GraphQL libraries","Needs access to conversation context for change name inference"],"zh":["需要node.js环境","依赖Prisma.io和GraphQL库","需要访问会话上下文以进行变更名称推理"],"ja":["node.js環境が必要","Prisma.ioとGraphQLライブラリに依存","変更名の推論のために会話のコンテキストへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["node.js 환경이 필요","Prisma.io 및 GraphQL 라이브러리에 의존","변경 이름 추론을 위해 대화 문脈에 액세스해야 함"],"es":["Requiere entorno de node.js","Dependiente de las bibliotecas Prisma.io y GraphQL","Necesita acceso al contexto de conversación para la inferencia del nombre del cambio"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement node.js","Dépend des bibliothèques Prisma.io et GraphQL","A besoin d''un accès au contexte de conversation pour l''inférence du nom de modification"],"de":["Benötigt eine node.js-Umgebung","Abhängig von den Bibliotheken Prisma.io und GraphQL","Benötigt Zugriff auf den Konversationskontext für die Ableitung des Änderungsnamens"],"pt":["Exige ambiente node.js","Depende das bibliotecas Prisma.io e GraphQL","Necessita acesso ao contexto da conversa para inferência do nome da alteração"],"ru":["Требует среды node.js","Зависит от библиотек Prisma.io и GraphQL","Требует доступа к контексту разговора для вывода имени изменения"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة node.js","يعتمد على مكتبات Prisma.io و GraphQL","يحتاج الوصول إلى سياق المحادثة لاستنتاج اسم التغيير"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('uxname/liteend/openspec-apply-change', 'community', 'uxname', 'liteend', 'uxname/liteend', 'openspec-apply-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:19:46.770Z', NULL, '{"id":"uxname/liteend/openspec-apply-change","name":"openspec-apply-change","description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 应用更改是一种轻量级的 GraphQL 和 Prisma.io 后端解决方案，用于实现 OpenSpec 更改。它可以自动选择更改或提示用户选择","ja":"OpenSpec 変更の適用は、OpenSpec の変更を実装するための軽量級の GraphQL と Prisma.io バックエンド ソリューションです。自動的に変更を選択するか、ユーザーに選択を求めます","ko":"OpenSpec 변경 적용은 OpenSpec 변경을 구현하기 위한 경량級 GraphQL 및 Prisma.io 백엔드 솔루션입니다. 자동으로 변경을 선택하거나 사용자에게 선택을 요청합니다","es":"El skill openspec-apply-change implementa tareas de OpenSpec con GraphQL y Prisma.io","fr":"La compétence openspec-apply-change met en œuvre des tâches OpenSpec avec GraphQL et Prisma.io","de":"Die Fähigkeit openspec-apply-change implementiert OpenSpec-Aufgaben mit GraphQL und Prisma.io","pt":"O openspec-apply-change é uma ferramenta para implementar tarefas do OpenSpec em um backend leve em GraphQL e Prisma.io.","ru":"Openspec-apply-change - это инструмент для реализации задач OpenSpec на легком бэкенде на GraphQL и Prisma.io.","ar":"openspec-apply-change هو أداة لتنفيذ مهام OpenSpec على خلفية خفيفة في GraphQL و Prisma.io","en":"Lightweight GraphQL & Prisma.io node.js backend"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec 应用更改 - 轻量级 GraphQL 和 Prisma.io 后端","ja":"OpenSpec 変更の適用 - 軽量級 GraphQL と Prisma.io バックエンド","ko":"OpenSpec 변경 적용 - 경량 GraphQL 및 Prisma.io 백엔드","es":"Aplicar cambios con OpenSpec y GraphQL","fr":"Appliquer des modifications avec OpenSpec et GraphQL","de":"Änderungen mit OpenSpec und GraphQL anwenden","pt":"Aplicar alterações com openspec-apply-change","ru":"Применение изменений с openspec-apply-change","ar":"تطبيق التغييرات مع openspec-apply-change","en":"openspec-apply-change"},"description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 应用更改是一种轻量级的 GraphQL 和 Prisma.io 后端解决方案，用于实现 OpenSpec 更改。它可以自动选择更改或提示用户选择","ja":"OpenSpec 変更の適用は、OpenSpec の変更を実装するための軽量級の GraphQL と Prisma.io バックエンド ソリューションです。自動的に変更を選択するか、ユーザーに選択を求めます","ko":"OpenSpec 변경 적용은 OpenSpec 변경을 구현하기 위한 경량級 GraphQL 및 Prisma.io 백엔드 솔루션입니다. 자동으로 변경을 선택하거나 사용자에게 선택을 요청합니다","es":"El skill openspec-apply-change implementa tareas de OpenSpec con GraphQL y Prisma.io","fr":"La compétence openspec-apply-change met en œuvre des tâches OpenSpec avec GraphQL et Prisma.io","de":"Die Fähigkeit openspec-apply-change implementiert OpenSpec-Aufgaben mit GraphQL und Prisma.io","pt":"O openspec-apply-change é uma ferramenta para implementar tarefas do OpenSpec em um backend leve em GraphQL e Prisma.io.","ru":"Openspec-apply-change - это инструмент для реализации задач OpenSpec на легком бэкенде на GraphQL и Prisma.io.","ar":"openspec-apply-change هو أداة لتنفيذ مهام OpenSpec على خلفية خفيفة في GraphQL و Prisma.io","en":"Lightweight GraphQL & Prisma.io node.js backend"},"definition":{"en":"Lightweight GraphQL & Prisma.io node.js backend"},"features":{"zh":["轻量级 GraphQL 和 Prisma.io 后端","自动选择更改或提示用户选择","支持 OpenSpec 更改","使用 openspec list 命令获取可用更改","支持对话上下文推断更改"],"ja":["軽量級の GraphQL と Prisma.io バックエンド","自動的に変更を選択するか、ユーザーに選択を求める","OpenSpec の変更をサポート","openspec list コマンドを使用して利用可能な変更を取得","会話のコンテキストから変更を推測する機能"],"ko":["경량級 GraphQL 및 Prisma.io 백엔드","자동으로 변경을 선택하거나 사용자에게 선택을 요청","OpenSpec 변경 지원","openspec list 명령을 사용하여 사용 가능한 변경을 가져옴","대화 상텍스트에서 변경을 추론하는 기능"],"es":["Implementación de tareas de OpenSpec","Uso de GraphQL y Prisma.io","Backend ligero en Node.js","Selección automática de cambios","Compatibilidad con inferencia de contexto de conversación"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre des tâches OpenSpec","Utilisation de GraphQL et Prisma.io","Backend léger sur Node.js","Sélection automatique des modifications","Compatibilité avec l''inférence du contexte de conversation"],"de":["Implementierung von OpenSpec-Aufgaben","Verwendung von GraphQL und Prisma.io","Leichtes Backend in Node.js","Automatische Auswahl von Änderungen","Kompatibilität mit Konversationskontextinferenz"],"pt":["Implementação de tarefas do OpenSpec","Backend leve em GraphQL","Integração com Prisma.io","Seleção automática de alterações","Suporte a inferência de contexto"],"ru":["Реализация задач OpenSpec","Легкий бэкенд на GraphQL","Интеграция с Prisma.io","Автоматический выбор изменений","Поддержка контекстного вывода"],"ar":["تنفيذ مهام OpenSpec","خلفية خفيفة في GraphQL","تكامل مع Prisma.io","اختيار تلقائي للتحديثات","دعم الاستدلال السياقي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","GraphQL","Prisma.io","后端","轻量级","自动选择","对话上下文"],"ja":["OpenSpec","GraphQL","Prisma.io","バックエンド","軽量級","自動選択","会話のコンテキスト"],"ko":["OpenSpec","GraphQL","Prisma.io","백엔드","경량级","자동 선택","대화 상텍스트"],"es":["OpenSpec","GraphQL","Prisma.io","Node.js","Backend ligero","Implementación de tareas","Selección automática de cambios"],"fr":["OpenSpec","GraphQL","Prisma.io","Node.js","Backend léger","Mise en œuvre des tâches","Sélection automatique des modifications"],"de":["OpenSpec","GraphQL","Prisma.io","Node.js","Leichtes Backend","Implementierung von Aufgaben","Automatische Auswahl von Änderungen"],"pt":["openspec-apply-change","OpenSpec","GraphQL","Prisma.io","backend leve","implementação de tarefas","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["openspec-apply-change","OpenSpec","GraphQL","Prisma.io","легкий бэкенд","реализация задач","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["openspec-apply-change","OpenSpec","GraphQL","Prisma.io","خلفية خفيفة","تنفيذ مهام","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"uxname","repo":"liteend","repoPath":"uxname/liteend","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-apply-change","description":"Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change. Use when the user wants to start implementing, continue implementation, or work through tasks.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Select the change**\n\n   If a name is provided, use it. Otherwise:\n   - Infer from conversation context if the user mentioned a change\n   - Auto-select if only one active change exists\n   - If ambiguous, run `openspec list --json` to get available changes and use the *","body":"Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Select the change**\n\n   If a name is provided, use it. Otherwise:\n   - Infer from conversation context if the user mentioned a change\n   - Auto-select if only one active change exists\n   - If ambiguous, run `openspec list --json` to get available changes and use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select\n\n   Always announce: \"Using change: <name>\" and how to override (e.g., `/opsx:apply <other>`).\n\n2. **Check status to understand the schema**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - Which artifact contains the tasks (typically \"tasks\" for spec-driven, check status for others)\n\n3. **Get apply instructions**\n\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions apply --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n\n   This returns:\n   - Context file paths (varies by schema - could be proposal/specs/design/tasks or spec/tests/implementation/docs)\n   - Progress (total, complete, remaining)\n   - Task list with status\n   - Dynamic instruction based on current state\n\n   **Handle states:**\n   - If `state: \"blocked\"` (missing artifacts): show message, suggest using openspec-continue-change\n   - If `state: \"all_done\"`: congratulate, suggest archive\n   - Otherwise: proceed to implementation\n\n4. **Read context files**\n\n   Read the files listed in `contextFiles` from the apply instructions output.\n   The files depend on the schema being used:\n   - **spec-driven**: proposal, specs, design, tasks\n   - Other schemas: follow the contextFiles from CLI output\n\n5. **Show current progress**\n\n   Display:\n   - Schema being used\n   - Progress: \"N/M tasks complete\"\n   - Remaining tasks overview\n   - Dynamic instruction from CLI\n\n6. **Implement tasks (loop until done or blocked)**\n\n   For each pending task:\n   - Show which task is being worked on\n   - Make the code changes required\n   - Keep changes minimal and focused\n   - Mark task complete in the tasks file: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n   - Continue to next task\n\n   **Pause if:**\n   - Task is unclear → ask for clarification\n   - Implementation reveals a design issue → suggest updating artifacts\n   - Error or blocker encountered → report and wait for guidance\n   - User interrupts\n\n7. **On completion or pause, show status**\n\n   Display:\n   - Tasks completed this session\n   - Overall progress: \"N/M tasks complete\"\n   - If all done: suggest archive\n   - If paused: explain why and wait for guidance\n\n**Output During Implementation**\n\n```\n## Implementing: <change-name> (schema: <schema-name>)\n\nWorking on task 3/7: <task description>\n[...implementation happening...]\n✓ Task complete\n\nWorking on task 4/7: <task description>\n[...implementation happening...]\n✓ Task complete\n```\n\n**Output On Completion**\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\n**Change:** <change-name>\n**Schema:** <schema-name>\n**Progress:** 7/7 tasks complete ✓\n\n### Completed This Session\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n...\n\nAll tasks complete! Ready to archive this change.\n```\n\n**Output On Pause (Issue Encountered)**\n\n```\n## Implementation Paused\n\n**Change:** <change-name>\n**Schema:** <schema-name>\n**Progress:** 4/7 tasks complete\n\n### Issue Encountered\n<description of the issue>\n\n**Options:**\n1. <option 1>\n2. <option 2>\n3. Other approach\n\nWhat would you like to do?\n```\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Keep going through tasks until done or blocked\n- Always read context files before starting (from the apply instructions output)\n- If task is ambiguous, pause and ask before implementing\n- If implementation reveals issues, pause and suggest artifact updates\n- Keep code changes minimal and scoped to each task\n- Update task checkbox immediately after completing each task\n- Pause on errors, blockers, or unclear requirements - don''t guess\n- Use contextFiles from CLI output, don''t assume specific file names\n\n**Fluid Workflow Integration**\n\nThis skill supports the \"actions on a change\" model:\n\n- **Can be invoked anytime**: Before all artifacts are done (if tasks exist), after partial implementation, interleaved with other actions\n- **Allows artifact updates**: If implementation reveals design issues, suggest updating artifacts - not phase-locked, work fluidly\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:19:46.770Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Infrastructure Agents managing GraphQL schema migrations and Prisma database changes.","zh":"适用于管理GraphQL schema迁移和Prisma数据库更改的基础设施代理。","ja":"GraphQLスキーマ移行とPrismaデータベースの変更を管理するインフラストラクチャエージェントに不可欠です。","ko":"GraphQL 스키마 마이그레이션 및 Prisma 데이터베이스 변경을 관리하는 인프라 에이전트에 필수입니다.","es":"Esencial para los agentes de infraestructura que administran las migraciones de esquemas GraphQL y los cambios en la base de datos Prisma.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents d''infrastructure gérant les migrations de schémas GraphQL et les modifications de base de données Prisma.","de":"Wesentlich für Infrastrukturagenten, die GraphQL-Schemamigrationen und Prisma-Datenbankänderungen verwalten.","pt":"Essencial para agentes de infraestrutura que gerenciam migrações de esquema GraphQL e alterações de banco de dados Prisma.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов инфраструктуры, которые управляют миграциями схемы GraphQL и изменениями базы данных Prisma.","ar":"ضروري لعمليات وكيل البنية التحتية لإدارة هجرات مخطط قاعدة البيانات GraphQL وتغييرات قاعدة بيانات Prisma."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables automated application of OpenSpec changes to GraphQL backends, providing direct integration with Prisma.io for database schema modifications. The skill intelligently handles change selection through context inference and fallback to `openspec list --json` command when ambiguous.","zh":"实现OpenSpec更改的自动应用于GraphQL后端，为Prisma.io提供直接集成以修改数据库模式。该技能通过上下文推理智能处理更改选择，当模糊时fallback到`openspec list --json`命令。","ja":"OpenSpecの変更をGraphQLバックエンドに自動適用する機能を提供し、Prisma.ioと直接統合してデータベーススキーマを変更します。このスキルは、コンテキスト推論を介して変更の選択をスマートに処理し、曖昧な場合は`openspec list --json`コマンドにfallbackします。","ko":"OpenSpec 변경 사항을 GraphQL 백엔드에 자동으로 적용하여 Prisma.io와 직접 통합하여 데이터베이스 스키마를 수정합니다. 이 스킬은 컨텍스트 추론을 통해 변경 사항을 선택하고 모호한 경우 `openspec list --json` 명령으로 fallback합니다.","es":"Permite la aplicación automatizada de cambios de OpenSpec a backends de GraphQL, proporcionando una integración directa con Prisma.io para la modificación de esquemas de base de datos. La habilidad maneja de forma inteligente la selección de cambios a través de la inferencia de contexto y vuelve a la orden `openspec list --json` cuando es ambiguo.","fr":"Permet l''application automatique des modifications OpenSpec aux backends GraphQL, offrant une intégration directe avec Prisma.io pour la modification des schémas de base de données. La compétence gère de manière intelligente la sélection des modifications via l''inférence de contexte et revient à la commande `openspec list --json` en cas d''ambiguïté.","de":"Ermöglicht die automatisierte Anwendung von OpenSpec-Änderungen an GraphQL-Backends, wodurch eine direkte Integration mit Prisma.io für Datenbankschemamodifikationen bereitgestellt wird. Die Fähigkeit verarbeitet die Änderungsauswahl intelligenterweise durch Kontextinferenz und fällt auf den Befehl `openspec list --json` zurück, wenn diese mehrdeutig ist.","pt":"Permite a aplicação automatizada de alterações OpenSpec em backends GraphQL, fornecendo integração direta com Prisma.io para modificações de esquema de banco de dados. A habilidade lida inteligentemente com a seleção de alterações por meio da inferência de contexto e fallback para o comando `openspec list --json` quando ambíguo.","ru":"Позволяет автоматически применять изменения OpenSpec к бэкендам GraphQL, обеспечивая прямую интеграцию с Prisma.io для изменений схемы базы данных. Этот навык интеллектуально обрабатывает выбор изменений посредством контекстного вывода и fallback к команде `openspec list --json` при неоднозначности.","ar":"تمكن من تطبيق تلقائي لتغييرات OpenSpec على خوادم GraphQL الخلفية، مع توفير تكامل مباشر مع Prisma.io لعملية تعديل مخطط قاعدة البيانات. يتعامل هذا الخبرة بذكاء مع اختيار التغييرات من خلال الاستدلال السياقي والعودة إلى أمر `openspec list --json` عند الغموض."},"useCases":{"en":["Applying database schema migrations","Automating GraphQL API updates","Managing Prisma.io backend changes","Resolving ambiguous change specifications"],"zh":["应用数据库模式迁移","自动化GraphQL API更新","管理Prisma.io后端更改","解析模糊的更改规格"],"ja":["データベーススキーマ移行の適用","GraphQL APIの自動更新","Prisma.ioバックエンドの変更の管理","曖昧な変更の仕様の解決"],"ko":["데이터베이스 스키마 마이그레이션 적용","GraphQL API 자동 업데이트","Prisma.io 백엔드 변경 관리","모호한 변경 명세 해석"],"es":["Aplicar migraciones de esquemas de base de datos","Automatizar actualizaciones de API de GraphQL","Administrar cambios en el backend de Prisma.io","Resolver especificaciones de cambios ambiguas"],"fr":["Appliquer les migrations de schémas de base de données","Automatiser les mises à jour des API GraphQL","Gérer les modifications du backend Prisma.io","Résoudre les spécifications de modifications ambiguës"],"de":["Anwenden von Datenbankschemamigrationen","Automatisieren von GraphQL-API-Updates","Verwalten von Änderungen am Prisma.io-Backend","Auflösen von mehrdeutigen Änderungsspezifikationen"],"pt":["Aplicar migrações de esquema de banco de dados","Automatizar atualizações de API GraphQL","Gerenciar alterações de backend Prisma.io","Resolver especificações de alteração ambíguas"],"ru":["Применять миграции схемы базы данных","Автоматизировать обновления API GraphQL","Управлять изменениями бэкенда Prisma.io","Разрешать неоднозначные спецификации изменений"],"ar":["تطبيق هجرات مخطط قاعدة البيانات","توفير تحديثات تلقائية لبروتوكول واجهة برمجة التطبيقات GraphQL","إدارة تغييرات الخادم الخلفي Prisma.io","حل تحديدات التغيير الغامضة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec change definitions","Needs access to openspec CLI commands","Depends on conversation context for inference"],"zh":["需要OpenSpec更改定义","需要访问openspec CLI命令","依赖对话上下文进行推理"],"ja":["OpenSpecの変更定義が必要","openspec CLIコマンドへのアクセスが必要","会話のコンテキストに依存して推論する"],"ko":["OpenSpec 변경 정의가 필요","openspec CLI 명령어에 접근이 필요","대화 문脈에 의존하여 추론"],"es":["Requiere definiciones de cambios de OpenSpec","Necesita acceso a los comandos de CLI de openspec","Depende del contexto de conversación para la inferencia"],"fr":["Nécessite des définitions de modifications OpenSpec","A besoin d''un accès aux commandes CLI d''openspec","Dépend du contexte de conversation pour l''inférence"],"de":["Benötigt OpenSpec-Änderungsdefinitionen","Benötigt Zugriff auf OpenSpec-CLI-Befehle","Hängt vom Konversationskontext für die Inferenz ab"],"pt":["Requer definições de alterações OpenSpec","Necessita acesso a comandos CLI openspec","Depende do contexto da conversa para inferência"],"ru":["Требует определений изменений OpenSpec","Требует доступа к командам CLI openspec","Зависит от контекста разговора для вывода"],"ar":["يتطلب تعريفات لتعديلات OpenSpec","يحتاج إلى وصول إلى أوامر سطر الأوامر openspec","يعتمد على سياق المحادثة للاستدلال"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering/openspec-verify-change', 'community', 'gAmUssA', 'ai-assisted-engineering', 'gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering', 'openspec-verify-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:20:26.680Z', NULL, '{"id":"gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering/openspec-verify-change","name":"openspec-verify-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-verify-change技能验证实现是否匹配变更Artifact，确保开发的一致性","ja":"openspec-verify-changeスキルは、実装が変更のArtifactと一致することを確認します","ko":"openspec-verify-change 스킬은 구현과 변경 사항이 일치하는지 확인하여 개발의 일관성을 제공합니다","es":"openspec-verify-change es una habilidad que verifica que una implementación se ajusta a los artefactos de cambio, como especificaciones, tareas y diseños.","fr":"openspec-verify-change est une compétence qui vérifie qu''une implémentation correspond aux artefacts de modification, tels que les spécifications, les tâches et les conceptions.","de":"openspec-verify-change ist eine Fähigkeit, die überprüft, ob eine Implementierung mit den Änderungsartefakten, wie Spezifikationen, Aufgaben und Designs, übereinstimmt.","pt":"O openspec-verify-change é uma ferramenta para verificar se uma implementação corresponde aos artefatos de alteração. Ele executa o comando openspec list --json para obter as alterações disponíveis.","ru":"Openspec-verify-change - это инструмент для проверки соответствия реализации артефактам изменения. Он запускает команду openspec list --json, чтобы получить доступные изменения.","ar":"openspec-verify-change هو أداة للتحقق من أن التنفيذ соответств لمواصفات التغيير. يقوم بتشغيل الأمر openspec list --json لاسترداد التغييرات المتاحة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-verify-change技能：验证实现与变更","ja":"openspec-verify-changeスキル：実装と変更のバリデーション","ko":"openspec-verify-change 스킬: 구현과 변경 사항 확인","es":"Verifica cambios en la implementación con openspec-verify...","fr":"Vérifiez les modifications d''implémentation avec openspec...","de":"Überprüfen Sie Implementierungsänderungen mit openspec-ve...","pt":"Verifique Alterações com openspec-verify-change","ru":"Проверьте изменения с openspec-verify-change","ar":"تحقق من التغييرات مع openspec-verify-change","en":"openspec-verify-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-verify-change技能验证实现是否匹配变更Artifact，确保开发的一致性","ja":"openspec-verify-changeスキルは、実装が変更のArtifactと一致することを確認します","ko":"openspec-verify-change 스킬은 구현과 변경 사항이 일치하는지 확인하여 개발의 일관성을 제공합니다","es":"openspec-verify-change es una habilidad que verifica que una implementación se ajusta a los artefactos de cambio, como especificaciones, tareas y diseños.","fr":"openspec-verify-change est une compétence qui vérifie qu''une implémentation correspond aux artefacts de modification, tels que les spécifications, les tâches...","de":"openspec-verify-change ist eine Fähigkeit, die überprüft, ob eine Implementierung mit den Änderungsartefakten, wie Spezifikationen, Aufgaben und Designs, übe...","pt":"O openspec-verify-change é uma ferramenta para verificar se uma implementação corresponde aos artefatos de alteração. Ele executa o comando openspec list --j...","ru":"Openspec-verify-change - это инструмент для проверки соответствия реализации артефактам изменения. Он запускает команду openspec list --json, чтобы получить ...","ar":"openspec-verify-change هو أداة للتحقق من أن التنفيذ соответств لمواصفات التغيير. يقوم بتشغيل الأمر openspec list --json لاسترداد التغييرات المتاحة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["验证实现与变更Artifact的一致性","支持选项指定变更名称","自动推断变更名称","用户交互式选择变更"],"ja":["実装と変更のArtifactの一致性を検証","変更名の指定をサポート","変更名の自動推測","ユーザーによる変更の選択"],"ko":["구현과 변경 사항의 일관성을 확인","변경 이름을 선택할 수 있는 옵션","변경 이름 자동 추론","사용자와의 상호작용을 통한 변경 선택"],"es":["Verificación de implementaciones","Coincidencia con artefactos de cambio","Soporte para tareas de implementación","Interacción con el usuario para selección de cambios","Uso de la herramienta AskUserQuestion","Ejecución de comandos openspec"],"fr":["Vérification des implémentations","Correspondance avec les artefacts de modification","Prise en charge des tâches d''implémentation","Interaction avec l''utilisateur pour la sélection des modifications","Utilisation de l''outil AskUserQuestion","Exécution de commandes openspec"],"de":["Überprüfung von Implementierungen","Übereinstimmung mit Änderungsartefakten","Unterstützung für Implementierungsaufgaben","Interaktion mit dem Benutzer zur Auswahl von Änderungen","Verwendung des Tools AskUserQuestion","Ausführung von openspec-Befehlen"],"pt":["Verificação de implementação","Obtenção de alterações disponíveis com openspec list --json","Seleção de alterações com o AskUserQuestion tool","Verificação de tarefas de implementação"],"ru":["Проверка реализации","Получение доступных изменений с помощью openspec list --json","Выбор изменений с помощью инструмента AskUserQuestion","Проверка задач реализации"],"ar":["التحقق من التنفيذ","استرجاع التغييرات المتاحة باستخدام openspec list --json","اختيار التغييرات باستخدام أداة AskUserQuestion","التحقق من مهام التنفيذ"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-verify-change","验证实现","变更Artifact","开发一致性","自动推断","用户交互"],"ja":["openspec-verify-change","実装の検証","変更のArtifact","開発の一致性","自動推測","ユーザーとの対話"],"ko":["openspec-verify-change","구현 확인","변경 사항","개발 일관성","자동 추론","사용자 상호작용"],"es":["openspec-verify-change","verificación de implementaciones","artefactos de cambio","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","AskUserQuestion","comandos openspec"],"fr":["openspec-verify-change","vérification des implémentations","artefacts de modification","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","AskUserQuestion","commandes openspec"],"de":["openspec-verify-change","Überprüfung von Implementierungen","Änderungsartefakte","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools","AskUserQuestion","openspec-Befehle"],"pt":["openspec-verify-change","verificação de implementação","artefatos de alteração","openspec list --json","AskUserQuestion tool","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["openspec-verify-change","проверка реализации","артефакты изменения","openspec list --json","инструмент AskUserQuestion","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["openspec-verify-change","التحقق من التنفيذ","مواصفات التغيير","openspec list --json","أداة AskUserQuestion","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"gAmUssA","repo":"ai-assisted-engineering","repoPath":"gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-verify-change","description":"Verify implementation matches change artifacts. Use when the user wants to validate that implementation is complete, correct, and coherent before archiving.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifa","body":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifact exists).\n   Include the schema used for each change if available.\n   Mark changes with incomplete tasks as \"(In Progress)\".\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check status to understand the schema**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - Which artifacts exist for this change\n\n3. **Get the change directory and load artifacts**\n\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions apply --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n\n   This returns the change directory and context files. Read all available artifacts from `contextFiles`.\n\n4. **Initialize verification report structure**\n\n   Create a report structure with three dimensions:\n   - **Completeness**: Track tasks and spec coverage\n   - **Correctness**: Track requirement implementation and scenario coverage\n   - **Coherence**: Track design adherence and pattern consistency\n\n   Each dimension can have CRITICAL, WARNING, or SUGGESTION issues.\n\n5. **Verify Completeness**\n\n   **Task Completion**:\n   - If tasks.md exists in contextFiles, read it\n   - Parse checkboxes: `- [ ]` (incomplete) vs `- [x]` (complete)\n   - Count complete vs total tasks\n   - If incomplete tasks exist:\n     - Add CRITICAL issue for each incomplete task\n     - Recommendation: \"Complete task: <description>\" or \"Mark as done if already implemented\"\n\n   **Spec Coverage**:\n   - If delta specs exist in `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/`:\n     - Extract all requirements (marked with \"### Requirement:\")\n     - For each requirement:\n       - Search codebase for keywords related to the requirement\n       - Assess if implementation likely exists\n     - If requirements appear unimplemented:\n       - Add CRITICAL issue: \"Requirement not found: <requirement name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Implement requirement X: <description>\"\n\n6. **Verify Correctness**\n\n   **Requirement Implementation Mapping**:\n   - For each requirement from delta specs:\n     - Search codebase for implementation evidence\n     - If found, note file paths and line ranges\n     - Assess if implementation matches requirement intent\n     - If divergence detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Implementation may diverge from spec: <details>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Review <file>:<lines> against requirement X\"\n\n   **Scenario Coverage**:\n   - For each scenario in delta specs (marked with \"#### Scenario:\"):\n     - Check if conditions are handled in code\n     - Check if tests exist covering the scenario\n     - If scenario appears uncovered:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Scenario not covered: <scenario name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Add test or implementation for scenario: <description>\"\n\n7. **Verify Coherence**\n\n   **Design Adherence**:\n   - If design.md exists in contextFiles:\n     - Extract key decisions (look for sections like \"Decision:\", \"Approach:\", \"Architecture:\")\n     - Verify implementation follows those decisions\n     - If contradiction detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Design decision not followed: <decision>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Update implementation or revise design.md to match reality\"\n   - If no design.md: Skip design adherence check, note \"No design.md to verify against\"\n\n   **Code Pattern Consistency**:\n   - Review new code for consistency with project patterns\n   - Check file naming, directory structure, coding style\n   - If significant deviations found:\n     - Add SUGGESTION: \"Code pattern deviation: <details>\"\n     - Recommendation: \"Consider following project pattern: <example>\"\n\n8. **Generate Verification Report**\n\n   **Summary Scorecard**:\n   ```\n   ## Verification Report: <change-name>\n\n   ### Summary\n   | Dimension    | Status           |\n   |--------------|------------------|\n   | Completeness | X/Y tasks, N reqs|\n   | Correctness  | M/N reqs covered |\n   | Coherence    | Followed/Issues  |\n   ```\n\n   **Issues by Priority**:\n\n   1. **CRITICAL** (Must fix before archive):\n      - Incomplete tasks\n      - Missing requirement implementations\n      - Each with specific, actionable recommendation\n\n   2. **WARNING** (Should fix):\n      - Spec/design divergences\n      - Missing scenario coverage\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   3. **SUGGESTION** (Nice to fix):\n      - Pattern inconsistencies\n      - Minor improvements\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   **Final Assessment**:\n   - If CRITICAL issues: \"X critical issue(s) found. Fix before archiving.\"\n   - If only warnings: \"No critical issues. Y warning(s) to consider. Ready for archive (with noted improvements).\"\n   - If all clear: \"All checks passed. Ready for archive.\"\n\n**Verification Heuristics**\n\n- **Completeness**: Focus on objective checklist items (checkboxes, requirements list)\n- **Correctness**: Use keyword search, file path analysis, reasonable inference - don''t require perfect certainty\n- **Coherence**: Look for glaring inconsistencies, don''t nitpick style\n- **False Positives**: When uncertain, prefer SUGGESTION over WARNING, WARNING over CRITICAL\n- **Actionability**: Every issue must have a specific recommendation with file/line references where applicable\n\n**Graceful Degradation**\n\n- If only tasks.md exists: verify task completion only, skip spec/design checks\n- If tasks + specs exist: verify completeness and correctness, skip design\n- If full artifacts: verify all three dimensions\n- Always note which checks were skipped and why\n\n**Output Format**\n\nUse clear markdown with:\n- Table for summary scorecard\n- Grouped lists for issues (CRITICAL/WARNING/SUGGESTION)\n- Code references in format: `file.ts:123`\n- Specific, actionable recommendations\n- No vague suggestions like \"consider reviewing\"\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:20:26.680Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring precise implementation verification against change artifacts and specs.","zh":"适用于需要对变更工件和规格进行精确实现验证的开发代理。","ja":"変更アーティファクトと仕様に対する正確な実装の検証を必要とする開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"변경 아티팩트 및 사양에 대한 정확한 구현 확인이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren una verificación de implementación precisa contra artefactos de cambio y especificaciones.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une vérification d''implémentation précise contre les artefacts de modification et les spécifications.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine präzise Implementierungsverifizierung gegen Änderungsartefakte und Spezifikationen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que requerem verificação de implementação precisa contra artefatos de alteração e especificações.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих точной проверки реализации изменений против артефактов и спецификаций.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الناشئين الذين يحتاجون إلى التحقق الدقيق لتطبيق التغييرات ضد مستندات التغيير والمتطلبات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to verify implementation changes against specs, tasks, and design using the openspec tool, ensuring consistency and accuracy in development workflows by running `openspec list --json` and utilizing the AskUserQuestion tool for user selection.","zh":"通过使用openspec工具、运行`openspec list --json`并利用AskUserQuestion工具进行用户选择，赋予代理验证实现更改与规格、任务和设计的一致性和准确性，在开发工作流中确保一致性和准确性。","ja":"openspecツールを使用し、`openspec list --json`を実行し、AskUserQuestionツールを使用してユーザー選択を行うことで、エージェントは実装の変更を仕様、タスク、設計と照合して一致性と正確性を確保できるようになり、開発ワークフローでの一貫性と正確性を確保します。","ko":"openspec 툴을 사용하고 `openspec list --json`을 실행하며 AskUserQuestion 툴을 사용하여 사용자 선택을 함으로써, 에이전트는 구현 변경 사항을 사양, 태스크 및 디자인과 비교하여 일관성과 정확성을 보장할 수 있으며, 개발 워크플ロー에서 일관성과 정확성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a verificar los cambios de implementación contra las especificaciones, tareas y diseño utilizando la herramienta openspec, garantizando la coherencia y la precisión en los flujos de trabajo de desarrollo al ejecutar `openspec list --json` y utilizar la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la selección de usuario.","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier les modifications d''implémentation contre les spécifications, les tâches et la conception en utilisant l''outil openspec, en garantissant la cohérence et la précision dans les flux de travail de développement en exécutant `openspec list --json` et en utilisant l''outil AskUserQuestion pour la sélection de l''utilisateur.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Implementierungsänderungen gegen Spezifikationen, Aufgaben und Design mit dem openspec-Tool zu überprüfen, wodurch Konsistenz und Genauigkeit in den Entwicklungswerkflüssen durch Ausführen von `openspec list --json` und Nutzung des AskUserQuestion-Tools für die Benutzerauswahl gewährleistet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a verificar as alterações de implementação contra especificações, tarefas e design usando a ferramenta openspec, garantindo a consistência e a precisão nos fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento executando `openspec list --json` e utilizando a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para seleção de usuário.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять изменения реализации против спецификаций, задач и дизайна с помощью инструмента openspec, обеспечивая последовательность и точность в рабочих процессах разработки путем выполнения `openspec list --json` и использования инструмента AskUserQuestion для выбора пользователя.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من التحقق من التغييرات في التطبيق ضد المواصفات والمهام والتصميم باستخدام أداة openspec، مما يضمن الاتساق والدقة في سير عمل التطوير من خلال تشغيل `openspec list --json` واستخدام أداة AskUserQuestion لتحديد المستخدم."},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying implementation matches against change artifacts","Automating spec validation for tasks and design","Debugging inconsistencies between implementation and specs"],"zh":["验证实现是否与变更工件匹配","自动化任务和设计的规格验证","调试实现和规格之间的不一致性"],"ja":["実装が変更アーティファクトと一致することを確認する","タスクと設計の仕様の検証を自動化する","実装と仕様の間の不一致をデバッグする"],"ko":["구현이 변경 아티팩트와 일치하는지 확인하기","태스크 및 디자인의 사양 검증 자동화","구현과 사양 간의 불일치 디버깅"],"es":["Verificar que la implementación coincide con los artefactos de cambio","Automatizar la validación de especificaciones para tareas y diseño","Depurar las inconsistencias entre la implementación y las especificaciones"],"fr":["Vérifier que l''implémentation correspond aux artefacts de modification","Automatiser la validation des spécifications pour les tâches et la conception","Déboguer les incohérences entre l''implémentation et les spécifications"],"de":["Überprüfen, ob die Implementierung mit den Änderungsartefakten übereinstimmt","Automatisieren der Spezifikationsvalidierung für Aufgaben und Design","Fehlerbehebung bei Inkonsistenzen zwischen Implementierung und Spezifikationen"],"pt":["Verificar se a implementação corresponde aos artefatos de alteração","Automatizar a validação de especificações para tarefas e design","Depurar inconsistências entre a implementação e as especificações"],"ru":["Проверка соответствия реализации артефактам изменений","Автоматизация проверки спецификаций для задач и дизайна","Отладка несоответствий между реализацией и спецификациями"],"ar":["التحقق من تطابق التطبيق مع مستندات التغيير","تحويل التحقق من المواصفات إلى تلقائي للمهام والتصميم","تصحيح أخطاء عدم التوافق بين التطبيق والمواصفات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires openspec tool installation","Needs access to conversation context for change name inference","Limited to changes with implementation tasks"],"zh":["需要openspec工具安装","需要访问对话上下文以进行更改名称推断","仅限于具有实现任务的更改"],"ja":["openspecツールのインストールが必要","会話のコンテキストへのアクセスが必要であるため、変更名の推論に限界がある","実装タスクを持つ変更のみに限定される"],"ko":["openspec 툴 설치가 필요함","대화 문脈에 접근할 수 있어야 하므로 변경 이름 추론에 제한이 있음","구현 태스크를 가진 변경만으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de la herramienta openspec","Necesita acceso al contexto de conversación para inferir el nombre del cambio","Limitado a cambios con tareas de implementación"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de l''outil openspec","A besoin d''un accès au contexte de conversation pour inférer le nom du changement","Limité aux modifications avec des tâches d''implémentation"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation des openspec-Tools","Benötigt Zugriff auf den Konversationskontext zur Ableitung des Änderungsnamens","Begrenzt auf Änderungen mit Implementierungsaufgaben"],"pt":["Requer instalação da ferramenta openspec","Necessita acesso ao contexto da conversa para inferência do nome da alteração","Limitado a alterações com tarefas de implementação"],"ru":["Требует установки инструмента openspec","Требует доступа к контексту разговора для вывода имени изменений","Ограничен изменениями с задачами реализации"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت أداة openspec","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى سياق المحادثة لاستنتاج اسم التغيير","محدود بالتغييرات التي تحتوي على مهام تطبيق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('HAI3org/HAI3/openspec-continue-change', 'community', 'HAI3org', 'HAI3', 'HAI3org/HAI3', 'openspec-continue-change', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:20:49.796Z', NULL, '{"id":"HAI3org/HAI3/openspec-continue-change","name":"openspec-continue-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change API, SaaS.","ja":"openspec-continue-change API, SaaS.","ko":"openspec-continue-change API, SaaS.","es":"El kit de desarrollo UI openspec-continue-change permite a los desarrolladores continuar trabajando en un cambio para aplicaciones SaaS modernas de manera eficiente.","fr":"Le kit de développement UI openspec-continue-change permet aux développeurs de continuer à travailler sur un changement pour les applications SaaS modernes de manière efficace.","de":"Das UI-Entwicklungskit openspec-continue-change ermöglicht es Entwicklern, an einem Change für moderne SaaS-Anwendungen effizient weiterzuarbeiten.","pt":"O openspec é um kit de desenvolvimento de UI para aplicações SaaS modernas, permitindo continuar trabalhando em uma alteração de forma eficiente.","ru":"Openspec - это набор инструментов для разработки пользовательского интерфейса для современных приложений SaaS, позволяющий продолжать работать над изменением эффективно.","ar":"openspec هو حزمة تطوير واجهة المستخدم لبرامج SaaS الحديثة، مما يسمح بالاستمرار في العمل على التغيير بفعالية.","en":"HAI3 - UI development kit for modern SaaS applications"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change API - SaaS ","ja":"openspec-continue-change API - SaaS","ko":"openspec-continue-change API - SaaS","es":"Kit de desarrollo UI para aplicaciones SaaS modernas","fr":"Kit de développement UI pour applications SaaS modernes","de":"UI-Entwicklungskit für moderne SaaS-Anwendungen","pt":"Continuar alteração com openspec","ru":"Продолжить изменение с openspec","ar":"استمرار التغيير مع openspec","en":"openspec-continue-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change API, SaaS.","ja":"openspec-continue-change API, SaaS.","ko":"openspec-continue-change API, SaaS.","es":"El kit de desarrollo UI openspec-continue-change permite a los desarrolladores continuar trabajando en un cambio para aplicaciones SaaS modernas de manera ef...","fr":"Le kit de développement UI openspec-continue-change permet aux développeurs de continuer à travailler sur un changement pour les applications SaaS modernes d...","de":"Das UI-Entwicklungskit openspec-continue-change ermöglicht es Entwicklern, an einem Change für moderne SaaS-Anwendungen effizient weiterzuarbeiten.","pt":"O openspec é um kit de desenvolvimento de UI para aplicações SaaS modernas, permitindo continuar trabalhando em uma alteração de forma eficiente.","ru":"Openspec - это набор инструментов для разработки пользовательского интерфейса для современных приложений SaaS, позволяющий продолжать работать над изменением...","ar":"openspec هو حزمة تطوير واجهة المستخدم لبرامج SaaS الحديثة، مما يسمح بالاستمرار في العمل على التغيير بفعالية.","en":"HAI3 - UI development kit for modern SaaS applications"},"definition":{"en":"HAI3 - UI development kit for modern SaaS applications"},"features":{"zh":["SaaS","API","UI","SaaS","openspec list --json","AskUserQuestion"],"ja":["SaaS","API","UI","SaaS","openspec list --json","AskUserQuestion"],"ko":["SaaS","API","UI","SaaS","openspec list --json","AskUserQuestion"],"es":["Permite a los desarrolladores continuar trabajando en un cambio","Incluye la herramienta AskUserQuestion para seleccionar cambios","Ejecuta el comando openspec list --json para obtener cambios disponibles","Presenta los 3 cambios más recientes","Permite la inferencia de cambios a partir del contexto de la conversación"],"fr":["Permet aux développeurs de continuer à travailler sur un changement","Inclut l''outil AskUserQuestion pour sélectionner des changements","Exécute la commande openspec list --json pour obtenir les changements disponibles","Présente les 3 changements les plus récents","Permet l''inférence des changements à partir du contexte de la conversation"],"de":["Ermöglicht es Entwicklern, an einem Change weiterzuarbeiten","Enthält das Tool AskUserQuestion zur Auswahl von Änderungen","Führt den Befehl openspec list --json aus, um verfügbare Änderungen zu erhalten","Präsentiert die 3 zuletzt geänderten Änderungen","Ermöglicht die Ableitung von Änderungen aus dem Konversationskontext"],"pt":["Criação do próximo artifact em uma alteração","Seleção de alterações disponíveis","Integração com o AskUserQuestion tool","Listagem de alterações por data de modificação","Suporte a desenvolvimento de UI para aplicações SaaS"],"ru":["Создание следующего артефакта в изменении","Выбор доступных изменений","Интеграция с инструментом AskUserQuestion","Список изменений по дате изменения","Поддержка разработки пользовательского интерфейса для приложений SaaS"],"ar":["إنشاء الملف التالي في تغيير","اختيار التغييرات المتاحة","التكامل مع أداة AskUserQuestion","قائمة التغييرات حسب تاريخ التعديل","دعم تطوير واجهة المستخدم لبرامج SaaS"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SaaS","API","UI","SaaS","openspec","HAI3","SaaS","SaaS API","SaaS UI"],"ja":["SaaS","API","UI","SaaS","openspec","HAI3","SaaS","SaaS API","SaaS UI"],"ko":["SaaS","API","UI","SaaS","openspec","HAI3","SaaS","SaaS API","SaaS UI"],"es":["desarrollo UI","aplicaciones SaaS modernas","kit de desarrollo","openspec-continue-change","herramienta AskUserQuestion","comando openspec list --json"],"fr":["développement UI","applications SaaS modernes","kit de développement","openspec-continue-change","outil AskUserQuestion","commande openspec list --json"],"de":["UI-Entwicklung","moderne SaaS-Anwendungen","Entwicklungskit","openspec-continue-change","Tool AskUserQuestion","Befehl openspec list --json"],"pt":["openspec","desenvolvimento de UI","aplicações SaaS","alterações","artefatos","AskUserQuestion","listagem de alterações"],"ru":["openspec","разработка пользовательского интерфейса","приложения SaaS","изменения","артефакты","AskUserQuestion","список изменений"],"ar":["openspec","تطوير واجهة المستخدم","برامج SaaS","التغييرات","الملفات","AskUserQuestion","قائمة التغييرات"]}},"owner":"HAI3org","repo":"HAI3","repoPath":"HAI3org/HAI3","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-continue-change","description":"Continue working on an OpenSpec change by creating the next artifact. Use when the user wants to progress their change, create the next artifact, or continue their workflow.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-","body":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-4 most recently modified changes as options, showing:\n   - Change name\n   - Schema (from `schema` field if present, otherwise \"spec-driven\")\n   - Status (e.g., \"0/5 tasks\", \"complete\", \"no tasks\")\n   - How recently it was modified (from `lastModified` field)\n\n   Mark the most recently modified change as \"(Recommended)\" since it''s likely what the user wants to continue.\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check current status**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand current state. The response includes:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow schema being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - `artifacts`: Array of artifacts with their status (\"done\", \"ready\", \"blocked\")\n   - `isComplete`: Boolean indicating if all artifacts are complete\n\n3. **Act based on status**:\n\n   ---\n\n   **If all artifacts are complete (`isComplete: true`)**:\n   - Congratulate the user\n   - Show final status including the schema used\n   - Suggest: \"All artifacts created! You can now implement this change or archive it.\"\n   - STOP\n\n   ---\n\n   **If artifacts are ready to create** (status shows artifacts with `status: \"ready\"`):\n   - Pick the FIRST artifact with `status: \"ready\"` from the status output\n   - Get its instructions:\n     ```bash\n     openspec instructions <artifact-id> --change \"<name>\" --json\n     ```\n   - Parse the JSON. The key fields are:\n     - `context`: Project background (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `rules`: Artifact-specific rules (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `template`: The structure to use for your output file\n     - `instruction`: Schema-specific guidance\n     - `outputPath`: Where to write the artifact\n     - `dependencies`: Completed artifacts to read for context\n   - **Create the artifact file**:\n     - Read any completed dependency files for context\n     - Use `template` as the structure - fill in its sections\n     - Apply `context` and `rules` as constraints when writing - but do NOT copy them into the file\n     - Write to the output path specified in instructions\n   - Show what was created and what''s now unlocked\n   - STOP after creating ONE artifact\n\n   ---\n\n   **If no artifacts are ready (all blocked)**:\n   - This shouldn''t happen with a valid schema\n   - Show status and suggest checking for issues\n\n4. **After creating an artifact, show progress**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n\n**Output**\n\nAfter each invocation, show:\n- Which artifact was created\n- Schema workflow being used\n- Current progress (N/M complete)\n- What artifacts are now unlocked\n- Prompt: \"Want to continue? Just ask me to continue or tell me what to do next.\"\n\n**Artifact Creation Guidelines**\n\nThe artifact types and their purpose depend on the schema. Use the `instruction` field from the instructions output to understand what to create.\n\nCommon artifact patterns:\n\n**spec-driven schema** (proposal → specs → design → tasks):\n- **proposal.md**: Ask user about the change if not clear. Fill in Why, What Changes, Capabilities, Impact.\n  - The Capabilities section is critical - each capability listed will need a spec file.\n- **specs/<capability>/spec.md**: Create one spec per capability listed in the proposal''s Capabilities section (use the capability name, not the change name).\n- **design.md**: Document technical decisions, architecture, and implementation approach.\n- **tasks.md**: Break down implementation into checkboxed tasks.\n\nFor other schemas, follow the `instruction` field from the CLI output.\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Create ONE artifact per invocation\n- Always read dependency artifacts before creating a new one\n- Never skip artifacts or create out of order\n- If context is unclear, ask the user before creating\n- Verify the artifact file exists after writing before marking progress\n- Use the schema''s artifact sequence, don''t assume specific artifact names\n- **IMPORTANT**: `context` and `rules` are constraints for YOU, not content for the file\n  - Do NOT copy `<context>`, `<rules>`, `<project_context>` blocks into the artifact\n  - These guide what you write, but should never appear in the output\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:20:49.796Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents utilizing HAI3 for modern SaaS applications, needing streamlined UI development kit integration.","zh":"适用于使用 HAI3 进行现代 SaaS 应用开发的开发代理，需要简化 UI 开发工具包集成。","ja":"HAI3 を使用して最新の SaaS アプリケーションを開発する開発エージェントに最適で、ストリーミング UI 開発キット統合が必要です。","ko":"HAI3를 사용하여 최신 SaaS 애플리케이션 개발에 적합하며, 개발자 에이전트가 스트림라인 UI 개발 키트 통합을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que utilizan HAI3 para aplicaciones SaaS modernas, que necesitan una integración de kit de desarrollo de UI optimizada.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement utilisant HAI3 pour les applications SaaS modernes, nécessitant une intégration de kit de développement d''interface utilisateur optimisée.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsmittel, die HAI3 für moderne SaaS-Anwendungen verwenden und eine optimierte Benutzeroberflächen-Entwicklungs-Kit-Integration benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que utilizam HAI3 para aplicações SaaS modernas, necessitando de integração de kit de desenvolvimento de UI simplificado.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, использующих HAI3 для современных приложений SaaS, требующих упрощенной интеграции набора инструментов для разработки пользовательского интерфейса.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذين يستخدمون HAI3 للتطبيقات السحابية الحديثة، والذين يحتاجون إلى إدماج حزمة تطوير واجهة المستخدم المتبسطة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to seamlessly continue working on changes by creating the next artifact, leveraging the `openspec list --json` command for available changes and the AskUserQuestion tool for user selection, utilizing JSON data formats and command-line interfaces.","zh":"使代理能够通过创建下一个构件来无缝地继续处理更改，利用 `openspec list --json` 命令获取可用更改，并使用 AskUserQuestion 工具进行用户选择，利用 JSON 数据格式和命令行接口。","ja":"エージェントが次のアーティファクトを作成することで変更を続けて作業できるようにし、利用可能な変更を取得するために `openspec list --json` コマンドと、ユーザー選択のために AskUserQuestion ツールを利用し、JSON データ形式とコマンドライン インターフェイスを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 다음 아티팩트를 생성하여 변경 사항을 계속 작업할 수 있도록 하며, 사용 가능한 변경 사항을 가져오기 위해 `openspec list --json` 명령과 사용자 선택을 위해 AskUserQuestion 툴을 사용하며, JSON 데이터 형식과 명령줄 인터페이스를 사용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes continuar trabajando en los cambios de manera fluida creando el próximo artefacto, aprovechando el comando `openspec list --json` para los cambios disponibles y la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la selección de usuario, utilizando formatos de datos JSON y interfaces de línea de comandos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de continuer à travailler sur les modifications de manière fluide en créant le prochain artefact, en exploitant la commande `openspec list --json` pour les modifications disponibles et l''outil AskUserQuestion pour la sélection de l''utilisateur, en utilisant des formats de données JSON et des interfaces de ligne de commande.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, nahtlos an den Änderungen weiterzuarbeiten, indem sie das nächste Artefakt erstellen, das `openspec list --json`-Kommando für verfügbare Änderungen und das AskUserQuestion-Tool für die Benutzerselektion nutzen, wobei JSON-Datenformate und Kommandozeileninterfaces verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a continuar trabalhando em alterações de forma contínua, criando o próximo artefato, utilizando o comando `openspec list --json` para alterações disponíveis e a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para seleção do usuário, utilizando formatos de dados JSON e interfaces de linha de comando.","ru":"Позволяет агентам беспрепятственно продолжать работу над изменениями, создавая следующий артефакт, используя команду `openspec list --json` для доступных изменений и инструмент AskUserQuestion для выбора пользователя, используя форматы данных JSON и командные интерфейсы.","ar":"تمكن العملاء من الاستمرار في العمل على التعديلات بشكل متواصل، من خلال إنشاء الملف التالي، واستخدام الأمر `openspec list --json` للتعديلات المتاحة وأداة AskUserQuestion لاختيار المستخدم، واستخدام صيغ بيانات JSON وواجهات سطر الأوامر."},"useCases":{"en":["Continuing development on recently modified changes","Selecting and working on specific changes using the AskUserQuestion tool","Streamlining UI development workflows with HAI3"],"zh":["继续开发最近修改的更改","使用 AskUserQuestion 工具选择并处理特定更改","使用 HAI3 简化 UI 开发工作流"],"ja":["最近変更された変更の開発を続ける","AskUserQuestion ツールを使用して特定の変更を選択して作業する","HAI3 を使用して UI 開発ワークフローをストリーミングする"],"ko":["최근 수정된 변경 사항에 대한 개발을 계속하는 것","AskUserQuestion 툴을 사용하여 특정 변경 사항을 선택하고 작업하는 것","HAI3를 사용하여 UI 개발 워크플ロー 스트림"],"es":["Continuar el desarrollo en los cambios modificados recientemente","Seleccionar y trabajar en cambios específicos utilizando la herramienta AskUserQuestion","Optimizar flujos de trabajo de desarrollo de UI con HAI3"],"fr":["Continuer le développement sur les modifications récemment modifiées","Sélectionner et travailler sur des modifications spécifiques à l''aide de l''outil AskUserQuestion","Optimiser les flux de travail de développement d''interface utilisateur avec HAI3"],"de":["Weiterentwicklung an kürzlich geänderten Änderungen","Auswählen und Arbeiten an bestimmten Änderungen mit dem AskUserQuestion-Tool","Optimieren von Benutzeroberflächen-Entwicklungsworkflows mit HAI3"],"pt":["Continuar desenvolvimento em alterações recentemente modificadas","Selecionar e trabalhar em alterações específicas usando a ferramenta AskUserQuestion","Simplificar fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento de UI com HAI3"],"ru":["Продолжать разработку недавно измененных изменений","Выбирать и работать над определенными изменениями, используя инструмент AskUserQuestion","Упрощать рабочие процессы разработки пользовательского интерфейса с помощью HAI3"],"ar":["استمرار التطوير في التعديلات المعدلة حديثًا","اختيار العمل على تعديلات محددة باستخدام أداة AskUserQuestion","تبسيط سير عمل تطوير واجهة المستخدم مع HAI3"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires HAI3 UI development kit installation","Needs access to conversation context for change inference","Limited to top 3 changes for user selection"],"zh":["需要 HAI3 UI 开发工具包安装","需要访问会话上下文以进行更改推理","用户选择仅限于前 3 个更改"],"ja":["HAI3 UI 開発キットのインストールが必要","変更の推論のために会話のコンテキストへのアクセスが必要","ユーザー選択は最初の 3 つの変更に限定される"],"ko":["HAI3 UI 개발 툴킷 설치가 필요하다.","변경 추론을 위해 대화 맥락에 대한 액세스가 필요하다.","사용자 선택은 최초 3개의 변경 사항으로 제한된다."],"es":["Requiere la instalación del kit de desarrollo de UI de HAI3","Necesita acceso al contexto de conversación para la inferencia de cambios","Limitado a los 3 primeros cambios para la selección de usuario"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation du kit de développement d''interface utilisateur HAI3","A besoin d''un accès au contexte de conversation pour l''inférence de modifications","Limité aux 3 premières modifications pour la sélection de l''utilisateur"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation des HAI3-Benutzeroberflächen-Entwicklungs-Kit","Benötigt Zugriff auf den Konversationskontext für die Änderungsinferenz","Begrenzt auf die ersten 3 Änderungen für die Benutzerselektion"],"pt":["Exige instalação do kit de desenvolvimento de UI HAI3","Necessita acesso ao contexto da conversa para inferência de alterações","Limitado às 3 principais alterações para seleção do usuário"],"ru":["Требует установки набора инструментов для разработки пользовательского интерфейса HAI3","Требует доступа к контексту разговора для вывода изменений","Ограничен до 3 лучших изменений для выбора пользователя"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت حزمة تطوير واجهة المستخدم HAI3","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى سياق المحادثة لاستدلال التعديلات","محدود بالتعديلات الثلاث الأولى لاختيار المستخدم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('beyildirim/tracehound/openspec-apply-change', 'community', 'beyildirim', 'tracehound', 'beyildirim/tracehound', 'openspec-apply-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:19:54.264Z', NULL, '{"id":"beyildirim/tracehound/openspec-apply-change","name":"openspec-apply-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-apply-change 技能用于实现 OpenSpec 中的任务更改，支持从会话上下文中推断更改名称","ja":"OpenSpec 変更適用スキルは、OpenSpec 内のタスク変更を実装し、会話のコンテキストから変更名を推測することをサポート","ko":"OpenSpec 변경 적용 기능은 OpenSpec 내의 작업 변경을 구현하며 대화의 맥락에서 변경 이름을 추론하는 것을 지원","es":"El skill openspec-apply-change permite implementar tareas desde un cambio OpenSpec de forma automática.","fr":"Le skill openspec-apply-change permet de mettre en œuvre des tâches à partir d''un changement OpenSpec de manière automatisée.","de":"Das Skill openspec-apply-change ermöglicht die Implementierung von Aufgaben aus einer OpenSpec-Änderung auf automatisierte Weise.","pt":"O openspec-apply-change é uma habilidade que implementa tarefas de mudança do OpenSpec. Ele seleciona a mudança com base no nome fornecido ou no contexto da conversa.","ru":"Openspec-apply-change - это навык, который реализует задачи изменений OpenSpec. Он выбирает изменение на основе предоставленного имени или контекста разговора.","ar":"openspec-apply-change هو مهارة ينفذ مهام تغيير مواصفات مفتوحة. يقوم باختيار التغيير على أساس الاسم المحدد أو سياق المحادثة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec 应用更改","ja":"OpenSpec 変更適用","ko":"OpenSpec 변경 적용","es":"Aplicar cambios con OpenSpec","fr":"Appliquer les modifications OpenSpec","de":"Änderungen mit OpenSpec anwenden","pt":"Aplicar Mudanças com OpenSpec","ru":"Применение изменений с OpenSpec","ar":"تطبيق التغييرات باستخدام OpenSpec","en":"openspec-apply-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-apply-change 技能用于实现 OpenSpec 中的任务更改，支持从会话上下文中推断更改名称","ja":"OpenSpec 変更適用スキルは、OpenSpec 内のタスク変更を実装し、会話のコンテキストから変更名を推測することをサポート","ko":"OpenSpec 변경 적용 기능은 OpenSpec 내의 작업 변경을 구현하며 대화의 맥락에서 변경 이름을 추론하는 것을 지원","es":"El skill openspec-apply-change permite implementar tareas desde un cambio OpenSpec de forma automática.","fr":"Le skill openspec-apply-change permet de mettre en œuvre des tâches à partir d''un changement OpenSpec de manière automatisée.","de":"Das Skill openspec-apply-change ermöglicht die Implementierung von Aufgaben aus einer OpenSpec-Änderung auf automatisierte Weise.","pt":"O openspec-apply-change é uma habilidade que implementa tarefas de mudança do OpenSpec. Ele seleciona a mudança com base no nome fornecido ou no contexto da ...","ru":"Openspec-apply-change - это навык, который реализует задачи изменений OpenSpec. Он выбирает изменение на основе предоставленного имени или контекста разговора.","ar":"openspec-apply-change هو مهارة ينفذ مهام تغيير مواصفات مفتوحة. يقوم باختيار التغيير على أساس الاسم المحدد أو سياق المحادثة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持从会话上下文中推断更改名称","自动选择唯一的活动更改","当更改名称不明确时，提示可用更改","运行 openspec list --json 获取可用更改","从 OpenSpec 实现任务更改"],"ja":["会話のコンテキストから変更名を推測することをサポート","唯一のアクティブな変更を自動選択","変更名が不明確な場合、利用可能な変更を提示","openspec list --json を実行して利用可能な変更を取得","OpenSpec からタスク変更を実装"],"ko":["대화의 맥락에서 변경 이름을 추론하는 것을 지원","唯一의 활성 변경을 자동 선택","변경 이름이 불분명할 때 사용 가능한 변경을 제안","openspec list --json을 실행하여 사용 가능한 변경을 가져옴","OpenSpec에서 작업 변경을 구현"],"es":["Selección automática de cambios","Inferencia de contexto de conversación","Compatibilidad con varios cambios","Prompt para cambios disponibles","Implementación de tareas de cambio"],"fr":["Sélection automatique de modifications","Inférence du contexte de conversation","Compatibilité avec plusieurs modifications","Invite pour les modifications disponibles","Mise en œuvre des tâches de modification"],"de":["Automatische Änderungsauswahl","Kontextschlussfolgerung","Unterstützung für mehrere Änderungen","Prompt für verfügbare Änderungen","Implementierung von Änderungsaufgaben"],"pt":["Implementação de tarefas de mudança do OpenSpec","Seleção de mudança com base no nome ou contexto","Suporte a inferência de mudança a partir do contexto","Capacidade de executar comandos do OpenSpec","Listagem de mudanças disponíveis"],"ru":["Реализация задач изменений OpenSpec","Выбор изменений на основе имени или контекста","Поддержка вывода изменений из контекста","Возможность выполнения команд OpenSpec","Список доступных изменений"],"ar":["تنفيذ مهام تغيير مواصفات مفتوحة","اختيار التغيير على أساس الاسم أو السياق","دعم استنتاج التغيير من السياق","قدرة على تشغيل أوامر مواصفات مفتوحة","قائمة التغييرات المتاحة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","openspec-apply-change","任务更改","会话上下文","自动选择","openspec list"],"ja":["OpenSpec","OpenSpec 変更適用","タスク変更","会話のコンテキスト","自動選択","openspec list"],"ko":["OpenSpec","OpenSpec 변경 적용","작업 변경","대화의 맥락","자동 선택","openspec list"],"es":["OpenSpec","cambios automatizados","implementación de tareas","desarrollo de software","automatización de flujo de trabajo","integración de cambios"],"fr":["OpenSpec","modifications automatisées","mise en œuvre de tâches","développement de logiciels","automatisation de flux de travail","intégration de modifications"],"de":["OpenSpec","automatisierte Änderungen","Implementierung von Aufgaben","Software-Entwicklung","Automatisierung von Workflows","Integration von Änderungen"],"pt":["openspec","mudança","tarefa","desenvolvimento","programação","automatização","OpenSpec","change","task","development"],"ru":["openspec","изменение","задача","разработка","программирование","автоматизация","OpenSpec","change","task","development"],"ar":["مواصفات مفتوحة","تغيير","مهام","تطوير","برمجة","أتمتة","OpenSpec","change","task","development"]}},"owner":"beyildirim","repo":"tracehound","repoPath":"beyildirim/tracehound","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-apply-change","description":"Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change. Use when the user wants to start implementing, continue implementation, or work through tasks.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Select the change**\n\n   If a name is provided, use it. Otherwise:\n   - Infer from conversation context if the user mentioned a change\n   - Auto-select if only one active change exists\n   - If ambiguous, run `openspec list --json` to get available changes and use the *","body":"Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Select the change**\n\n   If a name is provided, use it. Otherwise:\n   - Infer from conversation context if the user mentioned a change\n   - Auto-select if only one active change exists\n   - If ambiguous, run `openspec list --json` to get available changes and use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select\n\n   Always announce: \"Using change: <name>\" and how to override (e.g., `/opsx:apply <other>`).\n\n2. **Check status to understand the schema**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - Which artifact contains the tasks (typically \"tasks\" for spec-driven, check status for others)\n\n3. **Get apply instructions**\n\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions apply --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n\n   This returns:\n   - Context file paths (varies by schema - could be proposal/specs/design/tasks or spec/tests/implementation/docs)\n   - Progress (total, complete, remaining)\n   - Task list with status\n   - Dynamic instruction based on current state\n\n   **Handle states:**\n   - If `state: \"blocked\"` (missing artifacts): show message, suggest using openspec-continue-change\n   - If `state: \"all_done\"`: congratulate, suggest archive\n   - Otherwise: proceed to implementation\n\n4. **Read context files**\n\n   Read the files listed in `contextFiles` from the apply instructions output.\n   The files depend on the schema being used:\n   - **spec-driven**: proposal, specs, design, tasks\n   - Other schemas: follow the contextFiles from CLI output\n\n5. **Show current progress**\n\n   Display:\n   - Schema being used\n   - Progress: \"N/M tasks complete\"\n   - Remaining tasks overview\n   - Dynamic instruction from CLI\n\n6. **Implement tasks (loop until done or blocked)**\n\n   For each pending task:\n   - Show which task is being worked on\n   - Make the code changes required\n   - Keep changes minimal and focused\n   - Mark task complete in the tasks file: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n   - Continue to next task\n\n   **Pause if:**\n   - Task is unclear → ask for clarification\n   - Implementation reveals a design issue → suggest updating artifacts\n   - Error or blocker encountered → report and wait for guidance\n   - User interrupts\n\n7. **On completion or pause, show status**\n\n   Display:\n   - Tasks completed this session\n   - Overall progress: \"N/M tasks complete\"\n   - If all done: suggest archive\n   - If paused: explain why and wait for guidance\n\n**Output During Implementation**\n\n```\n## Implementing: <change-name> (schema: <schema-name>)\n\nWorking on task 3/7: <task description>\n[...implementation happening...]\n✓ Task complete\n\nWorking on task 4/7: <task description>\n[...implementation happening...]\n✓ Task complete\n```\n\n**Output On Completion**\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\n**Change:** <change-name>\n**Schema:** <schema-name>\n**Progress:** 7/7 tasks complete ✓\n\n### Completed This Session\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n...\n\nAll tasks complete! Ready to archive this change.\n```\n\n**Output On Pause (Issue Encountered)**\n\n```\n## Implementation Paused\n\n**Change:** <change-name>\n**Schema:** <schema-name>\n**Progress:** 4/7 tasks complete\n\n### Issue Encountered\n<description of the issue>\n\n**Options:**\n1. <option 1>\n2. <option 2>\n3. Other approach\n\nWhat would you like to do?\n```\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Keep going through tasks until done or blocked\n- Always read context files before starting (from the apply instructions output)\n- If task is ambiguous, pause and ask before implementing\n- If implementation reveals issues, pause and suggest artifact updates\n- Keep code changes minimal and scoped to each task\n- Update task checkbox immediately after completing each task\n- Pause on errors, blockers, or unclear requirements - don''t guess\n- Use contextFiles from CLI output, don''t assume specific file names\n\n**Fluid Workflow Integration**\n\nThis skill supports the \"actions on a change\" model:\n\n- **Can be invoked anytime**: Before all artifacts are done (if tasks exist), after partial implementation, interleaved with other actions\n- **Allows artifact updates**: If implementation reveals design issues, suggest updating artifacts - not phase-locked, work fluidly\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:19:54.264Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing automated OpenSpec change implementation and management.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化OpenSpec变更实现和管理的开发代理。","ja":"OpenSpecの変更の自動化された実装と管理が必要な開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"자동화된 OpenSpec 변경 구현 및 관리가 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan implementación y gestión automatizada de cambios de OpenSpec.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement qui ont besoin d''une mise en œuvre et d''une gestion automatiques des modifications OpenSpec.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsagenten, die eine automatisierte Implementierung und Verwaltung von OpenSpec-Änderungen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de implementação e gerenciamento automatizados de alterações do OpenSpec.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходима автоматизированная реализация и управление изменениями OpenSpec.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التطوير التي تحتاج إلى تنفيذ وتحكم آليين في تغييرات OpenSpec."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to seamlessly apply OpenSpec changes by inferring or selecting changes, utilizing the OpenSpec JSON output, and prompting users when necessary, all while handling ambiguous or vague change requests.","zh":"赋予代理以无缝应用OpenSpec更改的能力，通过推断或选择更改，利用OpenSpec JSON输出，并在必要时提示用户，同时处理模糊或不明确的更改请求。","ja":"OpenSpecの変更を無効的に適用する能力をエージェントに与え、変更の推論または選択、OpenSpec JSON出力の利用、および必要に応じたユーザーのプロンプトを行い、曖昧または不明確な変更リクエストを処理します。","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 변경을 무결점으로 적용할 수 있는 능력을 부여함으로써, 변경 사항을 추론하거나 선택하고, OpenSpec JSON 출력을 사용하며, 필요한 경우 사용자에게 프롬프트를 표시하고, 모호하거나 불분명한 변경 요청을 처리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar cambios de OpenSpec de forma transparente, infiriendo o seleccionando cambios, utilizando la salida JSON de OpenSpec y solicitando a los usuarios cuando sea necesario, todo mientras maneja solicitudes de cambio ambiguas o vagas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des modifications OpenSpec de manière transparente en déduisant ou en sélectionnant des modifications, en utilisant la sortie JSON OpenSpec et en sollicitant les utilisateurs lorsque nécessaire, le tout en gérant les demandes de modification ambigües ou vagues.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, OpenSpec-Änderungen nahtlos anzuwenden, indem Änderungen inferiert oder ausgewählt werden, die OpenSpec-JSON-Ausgabe verwendet wird und Benutzer bei Bedarf aufgefordert werden, während unklare oder vage Änderungsanfragen gehandhabt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar alterações do OpenSpec de forma transparente, inferindo ou selecionando alterações, utilizando a saída JSON do OpenSpec e solicitando aos usuários quando necessário, lidando com solicitações de alteração ambíguas ou vagas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью бесшовного применения изменений OpenSpec, выводя или выбирая изменения, используя выходные данные JSON OpenSpec и запрашивая у пользователей при необходимости, а также обрабатывая неоднозначные или расплывчатые запросы на изменение.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تطبيق تغييرات OpenSpec بسهولة، путем استنتاج أو اختيار التغييرات، وتحديد ناتج JSON الخاص بـ OpenSpec، والاستعلام عن المستخدمين عند الضرورة، مع التعامل مع طلبات التغيير الغامضة أو المبهمة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating OpenSpec change implementation","Selecting and applying specific changes","Inferring changes from conversation context"],"zh":["自动化OpenSpec变更实现","选择并应用特定更改","从对话上下文推断更改"],"ja":["OpenSpecの変更の自動化された実装","特定の変更の選択と適用","会話のコンテキストからの変更の推論"],"ko":["OpenSpec 변경 구현의 자동화","특정 변경의 선택 및 적용","대화 문脈에서 변경 사항을 추론"],"es":["Automatización de la implementación de cambios de OpenSpec","Selección y aplicación de cambios específicos","Inferencia de cambios desde el contexto de conversación"],"fr":["Automatisation de la mise en œuvre des modifications OpenSpec","Sélection et application de modifications spécifiques","Déduction de modifications à partir du contexte de conversation"],"de":["Automatisierung der Implementierung von OpenSpec-Änderungen","Auswahl und Anwendung spezifischer Änderungen","Ableitung von Änderungen aus dem Konversationskontext"],"pt":["Automatizar a implementação de alterações do OpenSpec","Selecionar e aplicar alterações específicas","Inferir alterações a partir do contexto da conversa"],"ru":["Автоматизация реализации изменений OpenSpec","Выбор и применение конкретных изменений","Вывод изменений из контекста разговора"],"ar":["تحسين تنفيذ تغييرات OpenSpec","اختيار وتطبيق تغييرات محددة","استنتاج التغييرات من سياق المحادثة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to OpenSpec changes","Needs conversation context or user input for change selection","Limited to handling available changes via ''openspec list --json'' command"],"zh":["需要访问OpenSpec更改","需要对话上下文或用户输入以选择更改","仅限通过''openspec list --json''命令处理可用更改"],"ja":["OpenSpecの変更へのアクセスが必要","変更の選択には会話のコンテキストまたはユーザー入力が必要","利用可能な変更の処理は ''openspec list --json'' コマンドを介してのみ"],"ko":["OpenSpec 변경에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다.","변경 선택에는 대화 문脈 또는 사용자 입력이 필요합니다.","사용 가능한 변경 사항의 처리는 ''openspec list --json'' 명령을 통해만 제한됩니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a los cambios de OpenSpec","Necesita contexto de conversación o entrada de usuario para la selección de cambios","Limitado a la gestión de cambios disponibles a través del comando ''openspec list --json''"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux modifications OpenSpec","Nécessite un contexte de conversation ou une entrée utilisateur pour la sélection de modifications","Limité à la gestion des modifications disponibles via la commande ''openspec list --json''"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf OpenSpec-Änderungen","Benötigt Konversationskontext oder Benutzereingabe für die Änderungsauswahl","Begrenzt auf die Verwaltung verfügbarer Änderungen über den Befehl ''openspec list --json''"],"pt":["Requer acesso às alterações do OpenSpec","Necessita de contexto de conversa ou entrada do usuário para seleção de alterações","Limitado ao tratamento de alterações disponíveis via comando ''openspec list --json''"],"ru":["Требует доступа к изменениям OpenSpec","Требует контекста разговора или ввода пользователя для выбора изменений","Ограничен обработкой доступных изменений через команду ''openspec list --json''"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى تغييرات OpenSpec","يحتاج إلى سياق المحادثة أو مدخلات المستخدم لاختيار التغييرات","محدود بالتعامل مع التغييرات المتاحة عبر أمر ''openspec list --json''"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('beyildirim/tracehound/openspec-verify-change', 'community', 'beyildirim', 'tracehound', 'beyildirim/tracehound', 'openspec-verify-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:20:40.072Z', NULL, '{"id":"beyildirim/tracehound/openspec-verify-change","name":"openspec-verify-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-verify-change 技术验证实现是否匹配变更工件，确保开发的一致性","ja":"openspec-verify-change 技術は、実装が変更アーティファクトと一致するかを検証します","ko":"openspec-verify-change 기술은 구현이 변경 아티팩트와 일치하는지 확인하여 개발의 일관성을 보장합니다","es":"OpenSpec es una herramienta que verifica que una implementación coincida con los artefactos de cambio. Ayuda a asegurar la consistencia entre el diseño y la implementación.","fr":"OpenSpec est un outil qui vérifie que une implémentation correspond aux artefacts de modification. Il aide à assurer la cohérence entre la conception et l''implémentation.","de":"OpenSpec ist ein Werkzeug, das überprüft, ob eine Implementierung mit den Änderungsartefakten übereinstimmt. Es hilft dabei, die Konsistenz zwischen Design und Implementierung sicherzustellen.","pt":"O openspec-verify-change é uma ferramenta que verifica se uma implementação corresponde aos artifacts de alteração, como specs, tarefas e design.","ru":"openspec-verify-change - это инструмент, который проверяет, соответствует ли реализация артефактам изменений, таким как спецификации, задачи и дизайн.","ar":"openspec-verify-change هو أداة تتحقق من تطابق التنفيذ مع مكونات التغيير، مثل المواصفات والمهام والتصميم.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-verify-change 技术验证","ja":"openspec-verify-change 技術検証","ko":"openspec-verify-change 기술 검증","es":"Verificar Cambios con OpenSpec","fr":"Vérifier les Modifications avec OpenSpec","de":"Änderungen mit OpenSpec Überprüfen","pt":"Verifique Alterações com openspec-verify-change","ru":"Проверьте изменения с openspec-verify-change","ar":"تحقق من التغييرات باستخدام openspec-verify-change","en":"openspec-verify-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-verify-change 技术验证实现是否匹配变更工件，确保开发的一致性","ja":"openspec-verify-change 技術は、実装が変更アーティファクトと一致するかを検証します","ko":"openspec-verify-change 기술은 구현이 변경 아티팩트와 일치하는지 확인하여 개발의 일관성을 보장합니다","es":"OpenSpec es una herramienta que verifica que una implementación coincida con los artefactos de cambio. Ayuda a asegurar la consistencia entre el diseño y la ...","fr":"OpenSpec est un outil qui vérifie que une implémentation correspond aux artefacts de modification. Il aide à assurer la cohérence entre la conception et l''im...","de":"OpenSpec ist ein Werkzeug, das überprüft, ob eine Implementierung mit den Änderungsartefakten übereinstimmt. Es hilft dabei, die Konsistenz zwischen Design u...","pt":"O openspec-verify-change é uma ferramenta que verifica se uma implementação corresponde aos artifacts de alteração, como specs, tarefas e design.","ru":"openspec-verify-change - это инструмент, который проверяет, соответствует ли реализация артефактам изменений, таким как спецификации, задачи и дизайн.","ar":"openspec-verify-change هو أداة تتحقق من تطابق التنفيذ مع مكونات التغيير، مثل المواصفات والمهام والتصميم.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["验证实现是否匹配变更工件","支持选项指定变更名称","可从对话上下文推断变更名称","当变更名称不明确时，提示用户选择","使用 AskUserQuestion 工具让用户选择变更","运行 openspec list --json 获取可用变更"],"ja":["実装が変更アーティファクトと一致するかを検証","変更名を指定するオプションをサポート","対話のコンテキストから変更名を推測","変更名が不明確な場合、ユーザーに選択を求める","AskUserQuestion ツールを使用してユーザーに選択を求める","openspec list --json を実行して利用可能な変更を取得"],"ko":["구현이 변경 아티팩트와 일치하는지 확인","변경 이름을 지정하는 옵션을 지원","대화의 문맥에서 변경 이름을 추론","변경 이름이 불분명한 경우 사용자에게 선택을 요청","AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자에게 선택을 요청","openspec list --json 을 실행하여 사용 가능한 변경을 가져옴"],"es":["Verificación automática de cambios","Integración con herramientas de diseño","Compatibilidad con múltiples formatos de archivo","Opción para seleccionar cambios específicos","Informes detallados de verificación"],"fr":["Vérification automatique des modifications","Intégration avec des outils de conception","Compatibilité avec plusieurs formats de fichiers","Option pour sélectionner des modifications spécifiques","Rapports détaillés de vérification"],"de":["Automatische Überprüfung von Änderungen","Integration mit Designwerkzeugen","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Dateiformaten","Option zur Auswahl spezifischer Änderungen","Detaillierte Prüfberichte"],"pt":["Verificação de implementação de alterações","Suporte a specs, tarefas e design","Integração com openspec list","Seleção de alterações via AskUserQuestion","Compatibilidade com vários ambientes de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Проверка реализации изменений","Поддержка спецификаций, задач и дизайна","Интеграция с openspec list","Выбор изменений через AskUserQuestion","Совместимость с разными средами разработки"],"ar":["التحقق من تنفيذ التغييرات","دعم المواصفات والمهام والتصميم","التكامل مع openspec list","اختيار التغييرات من خلال AskUserQuestion","التوافق مع بيئات تطوير متعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-verify-change","技术验证","变更工件","实现验证","开发一致性","AskUserQuestion","openspec list"],"ja":["openspec-verify-change","技術検証","変更アーティファクト","実装検証","開発一貫性","AskUserQuestion","openspec list"],"ko":["openspec-verify-change","기술 검증","변경 아티팩트","구현 검증","개발 일관성","AskUserQuestion","openspec list"],"es":["verificación de cambios","OpenSpec","diseño de implementación","herramientas de desarrollo","coherencia de diseño","automatización de pruebas"],"fr":["vérification des modifications","OpenSpec","conception d''implémentation","outils de développement","cohérence de conception","automatisation des tests"],"de":["Überprüfung von Änderungen","OpenSpec","Implementierungsdesign","Entwicklungstools","Designkonsistenz","Testautomatisierung"],"pt":["openspec-verify-change","verificação de implementação","alterações de software","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","openspec list","AskUserQuestion"],"ru":["openspec-verify-change","проверка реализации","изменения программного обеспечения","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки","openspec list","AskUserQuestion"],"ar":["openspec-verify-change","التحقق من التنفيذ","تغييرات البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","openspec list","AskUserQuestion"]}},"owner":"beyildirim","repo":"tracehound","repoPath":"beyildirim/tracehound","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-verify-change","description":"Verify implementation matches change artifacts. Use when the user wants to validate that implementation is complete, correct, and coherent before archiving.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifa","body":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifact exists).\n   Include the schema used for each change if available.\n   Mark changes with incomplete tasks as \"(In Progress)\".\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check status to understand the schema**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - Which artifacts exist for this change\n\n3. **Get the change directory and load artifacts**\n\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions apply --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n\n   This returns the change directory and context files. Read all available artifacts from `contextFiles`.\n\n4. **Initialize verification report structure**\n\n   Create a report structure with three dimensions:\n   - **Completeness**: Track tasks and spec coverage\n   - **Correctness**: Track requirement implementation and scenario coverage\n   - **Coherence**: Track design adherence and pattern consistency\n\n   Each dimension can have CRITICAL, WARNING, or SUGGESTION issues.\n\n5. **Verify Completeness**\n\n   **Task Completion**:\n   - If tasks.md exists in contextFiles, read it\n   - Parse checkboxes: `- [ ]` (incomplete) vs `- [x]` (complete)\n   - Count complete vs total tasks\n   - If incomplete tasks exist:\n     - Add CRITICAL issue for each incomplete task\n     - Recommendation: \"Complete task: <description>\" or \"Mark as done if already implemented\"\n\n   **Spec Coverage**:\n   - If delta specs exist in `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/`:\n     - Extract all requirements (marked with \"### Requirement:\")\n     - For each requirement:\n       - Search codebase for keywords related to the requirement\n       - Assess if implementation likely exists\n     - If requirements appear unimplemented:\n       - Add CRITICAL issue: \"Requirement not found: <requirement name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Implement requirement X: <description>\"\n\n6. **Verify Correctness**\n\n   **Requirement Implementation Mapping**:\n   - For each requirement from delta specs:\n     - Search codebase for implementation evidence\n     - If found, note file paths and line ranges\n     - Assess if implementation matches requirement intent\n     - If divergence detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Implementation may diverge from spec: <details>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Review <file>:<lines> against requirement X\"\n\n   **Scenario Coverage**:\n   - For each scenario in delta specs (marked with \"#### Scenario:\"):\n     - Check if conditions are handled in code\n     - Check if tests exist covering the scenario\n     - If scenario appears uncovered:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Scenario not covered: <scenario name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Add test or implementation for scenario: <description>\"\n\n7. **Verify Coherence**\n\n   **Design Adherence**:\n   - If design.md exists in contextFiles:\n     - Extract key decisions (look for sections like \"Decision:\", \"Approach:\", \"Architecture:\")\n     - Verify implementation follows those decisions\n     - If contradiction detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Design decision not followed: <decision>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Update implementation or revise design.md to match reality\"\n   - If no design.md: Skip design adherence check, note \"No design.md to verify against\"\n\n   **Code Pattern Consistency**:\n   - Review new code for consistency with project patterns\n   - Check file naming, directory structure, coding style\n   - If significant deviations found:\n     - Add SUGGESTION: \"Code pattern deviation: <details>\"\n     - Recommendation: \"Consider following project pattern: <example>\"\n\n8. **Generate Verification Report**\n\n   **Summary Scorecard**:\n   ```\n   ## Verification Report: <change-name>\n\n   ### Summary\n   | Dimension    | Status           |\n   |--------------|------------------|\n   | Completeness | X/Y tasks, N reqs|\n   | Correctness  | M/N reqs covered |\n   | Coherence    | Followed/Issues  |\n   ```\n\n   **Issues by Priority**:\n\n   1. **CRITICAL** (Must fix before archive):\n      - Incomplete tasks\n      - Missing requirement implementations\n      - Each with specific, actionable recommendation\n\n   2. **WARNING** (Should fix):\n      - Spec/design divergences\n      - Missing scenario coverage\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   3. **SUGGESTION** (Nice to fix):\n      - Pattern inconsistencies\n      - Minor improvements\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   **Final Assessment**:\n   - If CRITICAL issues: \"X critical issue(s) found. Fix before archiving.\"\n   - If only warnings: \"No critical issues. Y warning(s) to consider. Ready for archive (with noted improvements).\"\n   - If all clear: \"All checks passed. Ready for archive.\"\n\n**Verification Heuristics**\n\n- **Completeness**: Focus on objective checklist items (checkboxes, requirements list)\n- **Correctness**: Use keyword search, file path analysis, reasonable inference - don''t require perfect certainty\n- **Coherence**: Look for glaring inconsistencies, don''t nitpick style\n- **False Positives**: When uncertain, prefer SUGGESTION over WARNING, WARNING over CRITICAL\n- **Actionability**: Every issue must have a specific recommendation with file/line references where applicable\n\n**Graceful Degradation**\n\n- If only tasks.md exists: verify task completion only, skip spec/design checks\n- If tasks + specs exist: verify completeness and correctness, skip design\n- If full artifacts: verify all three dimensions\n- Always note which checks were skipped and why\n\n**Output Format**\n\nUse clear markdown with:\n- Table for summary scorecard\n- Grouped lists for issues (CRITICAL/WARNING/SUGGESTION)\n- Code references in format: `file.ts:123`\n- Specific, actionable recommendations\n- No vague suggestions like \"consider reviewing\"\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:20:40.072Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring precise change verification and implementation validation.","zh":"适用于需要精确变更验证和实现验证的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが正確な変更の検証と実装の検証を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"정확한 변경 검증과 구현 검증이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren una verificación de cambios precisa y una validación de implementación.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une vérification de changement précise et une validation d''implémentation.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine präzise Änderungsverifizierung und Implementierungsvalidierung benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que requerem verificação precisa de alterações e validação de implementação.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих точной верификации изменений и валидации реализации.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التطوير التي تتطلب التحقق الدقيق من التغييرات والتحقق من التنفيذ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to verify implementation matches against change artifacts using openspec, tasks, and design specs, ensuring accuracy and consistency through JSON output and AskUserQuestion tool integration.","zh":"赋予代理人使用openspec、任务和设计规格来验证实现与变更文档的匹配，通过JSON输出和AskUserQuestion工具集成确保准确性和一致性。","ja":"openspec、タスク、設計仕様を使用して実装が変更成果物と一致することを検証することで、エージェントに実力を与え、JSON出力とAskUserQuestionツールの統合を通じて正確性と一貫性を確保します。","ko":"오픈스펙, 태스크, 설계 사양을 사용하여 구현이 변경 아티팩트와 일치하는지 검증할 수 있도록 에이전트를 활성화하고, JSON 출력과 AskUserQuestion 툴 통합을 통해 정확성과 일관성을 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes verificar que la implementación coincida con los artefactos de cambio utilizando openspec, tareas y especificaciones de diseño, garantizando la precisión y la coherencia a través de la salida JSON y la integración de la herramienta AskUserQuestion.","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier que l''implémentation correspond aux artefacts de changement en utilisant openspec, les tâches et les spécifications de conception, en garantissant l''exactitude et la cohérence grâce à la sortie JSON et à l''intégration de l''outil AskUserQuestion.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die Implementierung gegen Änderungsartefakte unter Verwendung von openspec, Aufgaben und Designspezifikationen zu überprüfen, und stellt durch JSON-Ausgabe und die Integration des AskUserQuestion-Tools Genauigkeit und Konsistenz sicher.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a verificar se a implementação corresponde aos artefatos de alteração usando openspec, tarefas e especificações de design, garantindo precisão e consistência por meio da saída JSON e integração da ferramenta AskUserQuestion.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять соответствие реализации артефактам изменений с помощью openspec, задач и спецификаций дизайна, обеспечивая точность и последовательность посредством вывода JSON и интеграции инструмента AskUserQuestion.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من التحقق من مطابقة التنفيذ لعناصر التغيير باستخدام openspec والtasks ومواصفات التصميم، وضمان الدقة والاتساق من خلال إخراج JSON ودمج أداة AskUserQuestion."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating change implementations against design specifications","Automating verification of tasks and specs for consistency","Debugging implementation discrepancies using openspec list and JSON output"],"zh":["验证实现是否符合设计规格","自动验证任务和规格的一致性","使用openspec列表和JSON输出调试实现不一致性"],"ja":["設計仕様に対する実装の検証","タスクと仕様の一貫性の自動検証","openspecリストとJSON出力を使用した実装不一致のデバッグ"],"ko":["설계 사양에 대한 구현 검증","태스크와 사양의 일관성 자동 검증","오픈스펙 목록과 JSON 출력을 사용한 구현 불일치 디버깅"],"es":["Validar implementaciones de cambios contra especificaciones de diseño","Automatizar la verificación de tareas y especificaciones para garantizar la coherencia","Depurar discrepancias de implementación utilizando la lista openspec y la salida JSON"],"fr":["Valider les implémentations de changement contre les spécifications de conception","Automatiser la vérification des tâches et des spécifications pour assurer la cohérence","Déboguer les désaccords d''implémentation en utilisant la liste openspec et la sortie JSON"],"de":["Überprüfen der Implementierung von Änderungen gegen Designspezifikationen","Automatisieren der Überprüfung von Aufgaben und Spezifikationen zur Sicherstellung der Konsistenz","Fehlerbehebung bei Implementierungsunterschieden mithilfe der openspec-Liste und der JSON-Ausgabe"],"pt":["Validar implementações de alterações contra especificações de design","Automatizar verificação de tarefas e especificações para consistência","Depurar discrepâncias de implementação usando lista openspec e saída JSON"],"ru":["Проверка реализации изменений против спецификаций дизайна","Автоматизация проверки задач и спецификаций на последовательность","Отладка несоответствий реализации с помощью списка openspec и вывода JSON"],"ar":["التحقق من تنفيذ التغييرات مقابل مواصفات التصميم","تحسين التأكد التلقائي من المهام والمواصفات للاتساق","تصحيح أخطاء التنفيذ باستخدام قائمة openspec وإخراج JSON"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires openspec installation and configuration","Needs access to change artifacts and implementation details","May prompt for user input if change name is vague or ambiguous"],"zh":["需要openspec的安装和配置","需要访问变更文档和实现细节","如果变更名称不明确或模糊，可能会提示用户输入"],"ja":["openspecのインストールと構成が必要","変更成果物と実装詳細にアクセスする必要がある","変更名が不明確または曖昧な場合、ユーザー入力を求める場合がある"],"ko":["오픈스펙의 설치와 구성이 필요합니다","변경 아티팩트와 구현 세부 정보에 액세스할 수 있어야 합니다","변경 이름이 불명확하거나 모호한 경우 사용자 입력을 요청할 수 있습니다"],"es":["Requiere la instalación y configuración de openspec","Necesita acceso a artefactos de cambio y detalles de implementación","Puede solicitar la entrada del usuario si el nombre del cambio es vago o ambiguo"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration d''openspec","A besoin d''un accès aux artefacts de changement et aux détails d''implémentation","Peut demander une entrée utilisateur si le nom du changement est vague ou ambigu"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation und Konfiguration von openspec","Benötigt Zugriff auf Änderungsartefakte und Implementierungsdetails","Kann Benutzereingabe anfordern, wenn der Änderungsname vage oder mehrdeutig ist"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do openspec","Necessita acesso a artefatos de alteração e detalhes de implementação","Pode solicitar entrada do usuário se o nome da alteração for vago ou ambíguo"],"ru":["Требует установки и конфигурации openspec","Требует доступа к артефактам изменений и деталям реализации","Может запрашивать ввод пользователя, если имя изменения неоднозначно или двусмысленно"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين openspec","يتطلب الوصول إلى عناصر التغيير و تفاصيل التنفيذ","قد يطلب إدخال المستخدم إذا كان اسم التغيير غامض أو مزدوج"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('uxname/liteend/openspec-continue-change', 'community', 'uxname', 'liteend', 'uxname/liteend', 'openspec-continue-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:20:56.813Z', NULL, '{"id":"uxname/liteend/openspec-continue-change","name":"openspec-continue-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change 是一个轻量级的 GraphQL 和 Prisma.io 后端开发技术，用于继续工作中的更改","ja":"openspec-continue-change は軽量の GraphQL と Prisma.io バックエンド開発技術であり、作業中の変更を続けるために使用される","ko":"openspec-continue-change는 경량 GraphQL과 Prisma.io 백엔드 개발 기술로 작업 중인 변경을 계속할 때 사용된다","es":"Openspec-continue-change es una herramienta para continuar trabajando en un cambio creando el próximo artifact en un backend de node.js con GraphQL y Prisma.io.","fr":"Openspec-continue-change est un outil pour continuer à travailler sur un changement en créant le prochain artifact dans un backend node.js avec GraphQL et Prisma.io.","de":"Openspec-continue-change ist ein Tool, um an einer Änderung weiterzuarbeiten, indem das nächste Artifact in einem node.js-Backend mit GraphQL und Prisma.io erstellt wird.","pt":"O openspec-continue-change é uma ferramenta para continuar trabalhando em uma alteração, criando o próximo artefato em um projeto GraphQL e Prisma.io.","ru":"Openspec-continue-change - это инструмент для продолжения работы над изменением, создавая следующий артефакт в проекте GraphQL и Prisma.io.","ar":"openspec-continue-change هو أداة للاستمرار في العمل على تعديل، من خلال إنشاء الملف التالي في مشروع GraphQL و Prisma.io","en":"Lightweight GraphQL & Prisma.io node.js backend"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change 技术","ja":"openspec-continue-change 技術","ko":"openspec-continue-change 기술","es":"Continuar cambio con openspec-continue-change","fr":"Continuer un changement avec openspec-continue-change","de":"Änderung fortsetzen mit openspec-continue-change","pt":"Continuar Alterações com openspec-continue-change","ru":"Продолжить изменения с openspec-continue-change","ar":"استمرار التعديلات مع openspec-continue-change","en":"openspec-continue-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change 是一个轻量级的 GraphQL 和 Prisma.io 后端开发技术，用于继续工作中的更改","ja":"openspec-continue-change は軽量の GraphQL と Prisma.io バックエンド開発技術であり、作業中の変更を続けるために使用される","ko":"openspec-continue-change는 경량 GraphQL과 Prisma.io 백엔드 개발 기술로 작업 중인 변경을 계속할 때 사용된다","es":"Openspec-continue-change es una herramienta para continuar trabajando en un cambio creando el próximo artifact en un backend de node.js con GraphQL y Prisma.io.","fr":"Openspec-continue-change est un outil pour continuer à travailler sur un changement en créant le prochain artifact dans un backend node.js avec GraphQL et Pr...","de":"Openspec-continue-change ist ein Tool, um an einer Änderung weiterzuarbeiten, indem das nächste Artifact in einem node.js-Backend mit GraphQL und Prisma.io e...","pt":"O openspec-continue-change é uma ferramenta para continuar trabalhando em uma alteração, criando o próximo artefato em um projeto GraphQL e Prisma.io.","ru":"Openspec-continue-change - это инструмент для продолжения работы над изменением, создавая следующий артефакт в проекте GraphQL и Prisma.io.","ar":"openspec-continue-change هو أداة للاستمرار في العمل على تعديل، من خلال إنشاء الملف التالي في مشروع GraphQL و Prisma.io","en":"Lightweight GraphQL & Prisma.io node.js backend"},"definition":{"en":"Lightweight GraphQL & Prisma.io node.js backend"},"features":{"zh":["轻量级 GraphQL 后端开发","Prisma.io 集成","自动化工作流","支持多个开发环境","提高开发效率"],"ja":["軽量の GraphQL バックエンド開発","Prisma.io 統合","自動化されたワークフロー","複数の開発環境のサポート","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["경량 GraphQL 백엔드 개발","Prisma.io 통합","자동화된 워크플로","複数의 개발 환경 지원","개발 효율의 향상"],"es":["Creación de artifacts","Integración con GraphQL","Compatibilidad con Prisma.io","Selección de cambios","Uso de la herramienta AskUserQuestion"],"fr":["Création d''artefacts","Intégration avec GraphQL","Compatibilité avec Prisma.io","Sélection de changements","Utilisation de l''outil AskUserQuestion"],"de":["Erstellung von Artifacts","Integration mit GraphQL","Kompatibilität mit Prisma.io","Auswahl von Änderungen","Verwendung des Tools AskUserQuestion"],"pt":["Criação de artefatos em projetos GraphQL","Integração com Prisma.io","Seleção de alterações para continuar trabalhando","Uso da ferramenta AskUserQuestion para seleção de alterações","Listagem de alterações recentes com `openspec list --json`"],"ru":["Создание артефактов в проектах GraphQL","Интеграция с Prisma.io","Выбор изменений для продолжения работы","Использование инструмента AskUserQuestion для выбора изменений","Список最近них изменений с `openspec list --json`"],"ar":["إنشاء الملفات في مشاريع GraphQL","التكامل مع Prisma.io","اختيار التعديلات للاستمرار في العمل","استخدام أداة AskUserQuestion لاختيار التعديلات","قائمة التعديلات الأخيرة مع `openspec list --json`"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-continue-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","后端开发","自动化","开发效率","轻量级","Node.js"],"ja":["openspec-continue-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","バックエンド開発","自動化","開発効率","軽量","Node.js"],"ko":["openspec-continue-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","백엔드 개발","자동화","개발 효율","경량","Node.js"],"es":["openspec-continue-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","node.js","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","creación de artifacts","selección de cambios"],"fr":["openspec-continue-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","node.js","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","création d''artefacts","sélection de changements"],"de":["openspec-continue-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","node.js","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Erstellung von Artifacts","Auswahl von Änderungen"],"pt":["openspec-continue-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","alterações em projetos","criação de artefatos","integração com Prisma.io"],"ru":["openspec-continue-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки","изменения в проектах","создание артефактов","интеграция с Prisma.io"],"ar":["openspec-continue-change","GraphQL","Prisma.io","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","التعديلات على المشاريع","إنشاء الملفات","التكامل مع Prisma.io"]}},"owner":"uxname","repo":"liteend","repoPath":"uxname/liteend","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-continue-change","description":"Continue working on an OpenSpec change by creating the next artifact. Use when the user wants to progress their change, create the next artifact, or continue their workflow.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-","body":"Continue working on a change by creating the next artifact.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes sorted by most recently modified. Then use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select which change to work on.\n\n   Present the top 3-4 most recently modified changes as options, showing:\n   - Change name\n   - Schema (from `schema` field if present, otherwise \"spec-driven\")\n   - Status (e.g., \"0/5 tasks\", \"complete\", \"no tasks\")\n   - How recently it was modified (from `lastModified` field)\n\n   Mark the most recently modified change as \"(Recommended)\" since it''s likely what the user wants to continue.\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check current status**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand current state. The response includes:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow schema being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\")\n   - `artifacts`: Array of artifacts with their status (\"done\", \"ready\", \"blocked\")\n   - `isComplete`: Boolean indicating if all artifacts are complete\n\n3. **Act based on status**:\n\n   ---\n\n   **If all artifacts are complete (`isComplete: true`)**:\n   - Congratulate the user\n   - Show final status including the schema used\n   - Suggest: \"All artifacts created! You can now implement this change or archive it.\"\n   - STOP\n\n   ---\n\n   **If artifacts are ready to create** (status shows artifacts with `status: \"ready\"`):\n   - Pick the FIRST artifact with `status: \"ready\"` from the status output\n   - Get its instructions:\n     ```bash\n     openspec instructions <artifact-id> --change \"<name>\" --json\n     ```\n   - Parse the JSON. The key fields are:\n     - `context`: Project background (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `rules`: Artifact-specific rules (constraints for you - do NOT include in output)\n     - `template`: The structure to use for your output file\n     - `instruction`: Schema-specific guidance\n     - `outputPath`: Where to write the artifact\n     - `dependencies`: Completed artifacts to read for context\n   - **Create the artifact file**:\n     - Read any completed dependency files for context\n     - Use `template` as the structure - fill in its sections\n     - Apply `context` and `rules` as constraints when writing - but do NOT copy them into the file\n     - Write to the output path specified in instructions\n   - Show what was created and what''s now unlocked\n   - STOP after creating ONE artifact\n\n   ---\n\n   **If no artifacts are ready (all blocked)**:\n   - This shouldn''t happen with a valid schema\n   - Show status and suggest checking for issues\n\n4. **After creating an artifact, show progress**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n\n**Output**\n\nAfter each invocation, show:\n- Which artifact was created\n- Schema workflow being used\n- Current progress (N/M complete)\n- What artifacts are now unlocked\n- Prompt: \"Want to continue? Just ask me to continue or tell me what to do next.\"\n\n**Artifact Creation Guidelines**\n\nThe artifact types and their purpose depend on the schema. Use the `instruction` field from the instructions output to understand what to create.\n\nCommon artifact patterns:\n\n**spec-driven schema** (proposal → specs → design → tasks):\n- **proposal.md**: Ask user about the change if not clear. Fill in Why, What Changes, Capabilities, Impact.\n  - The Capabilities section is critical - each capability listed will need a spec file.\n- **specs/<capability>/spec.md**: Create one spec per capability listed in the proposal''s Capabilities section (use the capability name, not the change name).\n- **design.md**: Document technical decisions, architecture, and implementation approach.\n- **tasks.md**: Break down implementation into checkboxed tasks.\n\nFor other schemas, follow the `instruction` field from the CLI output.\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Create ONE artifact per invocation\n- Always read dependency artifacts before creating a new one\n- Never skip artifacts or create out of order\n- If context is unclear, ask the user before creating\n- Verify the artifact file exists after writing before marking progress\n- Use the schema''s artifact sequence, don''t assume specific artifact names\n- **IMPORTANT**: `context` and `rules` are constraints for YOU, not content for the file\n  - Do NOT copy `<context>`, `<rules>`, `<project_context>` blocks into the artifact\n  - These guide what you write, but should never appear in the output\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:20:56.813Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Node.js Agents needing seamless integration with GraphQL and Prisma.io for efficient backend development.","zh":"非常适合需要与 GraphQL 和 Prisma.io 无缝集成以实现高效后端开发的 Node.js 代理。","ja":"GraphQLおよびPrisma.ioとのシームレスな統合が必要なNode.jsエージェントのための最適な選択です。","ko":"GraphQL 및 Prisma.io와의 무리없는 통합을 필요로 하는 Node.js 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Node.js que necesitan una integración sin problemas con GraphQL y Prisma.io para un desarrollo de backend eficiente.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Node.js nécessitant une intégration transparente avec GraphQL et Prisma.io pour un développement de backend efficace.","de":"Perfekt für Node.js-Agents, die eine nahtlose Integration mit GraphQL und Prisma.io für eine effiziente Backend-Entwicklung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Node.js que necessitam de integração sem problemas com GraphQL e Prisma.io para desenvolvimento de backend eficiente.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Node.js, которым необходима бесшовная интеграция с GraphQL и Prisma.io для эффективного развития бэкенда.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء Node.js الذين يحتاجون إلى دمج متسلسلة مع GraphQL و Prisma.io من أجل تطوير خلفية فعال"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to continue working on changes by creating the next artifact, utilizing openspec and Prisma.io for robust backend management, and leveraging GraphQL for flexible data querying and manipulation.","zh":"使代理能够通过创建下一个工件、利用 openspec 和 Prisma.io 进行强大的后端管理以及利用 GraphQL 进行灵活的数据查询和操作来继续处理更改。","ja":"openspecとPrisma.ioを使用した強力なバックエンド管理、およびGraphQLを使用した柔軟なデータの問い合わせと操作により、エージェントが変更の作業を続けることができます。","ko":"openspec와 Prisma.io를 사용한 강력한 백엔드 관리 및 GraphQL을 사용한 유연한 데이터 쿼리 및 조작을 통해 에이전트가 변경 사항 작업을 계속할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a seguir trabajando en los cambios creando el próximo artefacto, utilizando openspec y Prisma.io para una gestión de backend robusta, y aprovechando GraphQL para consultas y manipulación de datos flexibles.","fr":"Permet aux agents de poursuivre leur travail sur les modifications en créant le prochain artefact, en utilisant openspec et Prisma.io pour une gestion de backend robuste, et en exploitant GraphQL pour des requêtes et une manipulation de données flexibles.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, ihre Arbeit an den Änderungen fortzusetzen, indem sie das nächste Artefakt erstellen, openspec und Prisma.io für eine robuste Backend-Verwaltung nutzen und GraphQL für flexible Datenabfragen und -manipulation ausnutzen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes continuem trabalhando nas alterações, criando o próximo artefato, utilizando openspec e Prisma.io para gerenciamento robusto de backend e aproveitando GraphQL para consulta e manipulação flexíveis de dados.","ru":"Позволяет агентам продолжать работать над изменениями, создавая следующий артефакт, используя openspec и Prisma.io для надежного управления бэкендом, и используя GraphQL для гибкого запроса и манипулирования данными.","ar":"يسمح للوكلاء بمواصلة العمل على التغييرات من خلال إنشاء الملف القادم، وتحقيق openspec و Prisma.io لإدارة خلفية قوية، وتفويض GraphQL للاستعلام عن البيانات والتلاعب بها بسهولة"},"useCases":{"en":["Continuing development on existing changes with openspec","Managing multiple changes with Prisma.io and GraphQL","Automating backend workflows with node.js and openspec"],"zh":["使用 openspec 继续现有更改的开发","使用 Prisma.io 和 GraphQL 管理多个更改","使用 node.js 和 openspec 自动化后端工作流"],"ja":["openspecを使用して既存の変更の開発を続ける","Prisma.ioとGraphQLを使用して複数の変更を管理する","node.jsとopenspecを使用してバックエンドのワークフローを自動化する"],"ko":["openspec를 사용하여 기존 변경 사항의 개발을 계속함","Prisma.io와 GraphQL을 사용하여 여러 변경 사항을 관리함","node.js와 openspec를 사용하여 백엔드 워크플로를 자동화함"],"es":["Continuar el desarrollo en los cambios existentes con openspec","Gestionar varios cambios con Prisma.io y GraphQL","Automatizar flujos de trabajo de backend con node.js y openspec"],"fr":["Poursuivre le développement sur les modifications existantes avec openspec","Gérer plusieurs modifications avec Prisma.io et GraphQL","Automatiser les flux de travail de backend avec node.js et openspec"],"de":["Weiterentwicklung an bestehenden Änderungen mit openspec","Verwalten mehrerer Änderungen mit Prisma.io und GraphQL","Automatisieren von Backend-Workflows mit node.js und openspec"],"pt":["Continuar desenvolvimento em alterações existentes com openspec","Gerenciar várias alterações com Prisma.io e GraphQL","Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de backend com node.js e openspec"],"ru":["Продолжить разработку на существующих изменениях с openspec","Управлять несколькими изменениями с Prisma.io и GraphQL","Автоматизировать рабочие процессы бэкенда с node.js и openspec"],"ar":["استمرار التطوير على التغييرات الحالية مع openspec","إدارة تغييرات متعددة مع Prisma.io و GraphQL","توفير تدفقات عمل خلفية مع node.js و openspec"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires node.js environment","Dependent on Prisma.io and GraphQL","Needs ''openspec list --json'' command for change selection"],"zh":["需要 node.js 环境","依赖于 Prisma.io 和 GraphQL","需要 ''openspec list --json'' 命令进行更改选择"],"ja":["node.js環境が必要","Prisma.ioとGraphQLに依存している","変更の選択には ''openspec list --json'' コマンドが必要"],"ko":["node.js 환경이 필요함","Prisma.io와 GraphQL에 의존함","변경 사항 선택에는 ''openspec list --json'' 명령어가 필요함"],"es":["Requiere entorno de node.js","Dependiente de Prisma.io y GraphQL","Necesita el comando ''openspec list --json'' para la selección de cambios"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement node.js","Dépendant de Prisma.io et GraphQL","Nécessite la commande ''openspec list --json'' pour la sélection des modifications"],"de":["Benötigt node.js-Umgebung","Abhängig von Prisma.io und GraphQL","Benötigt den Befehl ''openspec list --json'' für die Änderungsauswahl"],"pt":["Requer ambiente node.js","Dependente de Prisma.io e GraphQL","Necessita do comando ''openspec list --json'' para seleção de alterações"],"ru":["Требуется окружение node.js","Зависит от Prisma.io и GraphQL","Требуется команда ''openspec list --json'' для выбора изменений"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة node.js","يعتمد على Prisma.io و GraphQL","يحتاج إلى أمر ''openspec list --json'' لتحديد التغييرات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('eKoh951/hytale-gg/marketing-psychology', 'community', 'eKoh951', 'hytale-gg', 'eKoh951/hytale-gg', 'marketing-psychology', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:21:27.704Z', NULL, '{"id":"eKoh951/hytale-gg/marketing-psychology","name":"marketing-psychology","description":{"zh":"营销心理学和心智模型帮助您理解消费者行为，做出数据驱动的决策","ja":"マーケティング心理学とメンタルモデルは、消費者の行動を理解し、データ駆動の決定を下すのに役立ちます","ko":"마케팅 심리학 및 마음 모델은 소비자 행동을 이해하고 데이터 驱动의 결정에 도움을 줍니다","es":"La psicología de marketing se centra en aplicar principios psicológicos para entender por qué la gente compra y cómo influir en su comportamiento de manera ética","fr":"La psychologie de marketing vise à appliquer les principes psychologiques pour comprendre pourquoi les gens achètent et comment influencer leur comportement de manière éthique","de":"Die Marketing-Psychologie konzentriert sich auf die Anwendung psychologischer Prinzipien, um zu verstehen, warum Menschen kaufen und wie man ihr Verhalten ethisch beeinflussen kann","pt":"A psicologia de marketing ajuda a entender por que as pessoas compram e como influenciar comportamentos de compra de forma ética.","ru":"Маркетинг-психология помогает понять, почему люди покупают и как этично влиять на поведение покупателей.","ar":"علم نفس التسويق يساعد على فهم لماذا يشترون الناس وكيف يتأثر سلوك الشراء بطرق أخلاقية.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"营销心理学与心智模型","ja":"マーケティング心理学とメンタルモデル","ko":"마케팅 심리학 및 마음 모델","es":"Psicología de Marketing: Influencia Comportamientos","fr":"Psychologie de Marketing: Comprendre les Achats","de":"Marketing-Psychologie: Verhaltensweisen Beeinflussen","pt":"Psicologia de Marketing: Melhore Decisões de Compra","ru":"Маркетинг-Психология: Повышение Продаж","ar":"علم نفس التسويق: تحسين قرارات الشراء","en":"marketing-psychology"},"description":{"zh":"营销心理学和心智模型帮助您理解消费者行为，做出数据驱动的决策","ja":"マーケティング心理学とメンタルモデルは、消費者の行動を理解し、データ駆動の決定を下すのに役立ちます","ko":"마케팅 심리학 및 마음 모델은 소비자 행동을 이해하고 데이터 驱动의 결정에 도움을 줍니다","es":"La psicología de marketing se centra en aplicar principios psicológicos para entender por qué la gente compra y cómo influir en su comportamiento de manera é...","fr":"La psychologie de marketing vise à appliquer les principes psychologiques pour comprendre pourquoi les gens achètent et comment influencer leur comportement ...","de":"Die Marketing-Psychologie konzentriert sich auf die Anwendung psychologischer Prinzipien, um zu verstehen, warum Menschen kaufen und wie man ihr Verhalten et...","pt":"A psicologia de marketing ajuda a entender por que as pessoas compram e como influenciar comportamentos de compra de forma ética.","ru":"Маркетинг-психология помогает понять, почему люди покупают и как этично влиять на поведение покупателей.","ar":"علم نفس التسويق يساعد على فهم لماذا يشترون الناس وكيف يتأثر سلوك الشراء بطرق أخلاقية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["了解消费者行为","影响行为和决策","应用心理学原理","数据驱动的决策","提高营销效果"],"ja":["消費者の行動を理解する","行動と決定に影響を与える","心理学的原理を適用する","データ駆動の決定","マーケティングの効果を高める"],"ko":["소비자 행동 이해","행동과 결정에 영향을 미치기","심리학적 원리 적용","데이터 驱动의 결정","마케팅 효과 향상"],"es":["Aplicación de principios psicológicos en marketing","Influencia en el comportamiento de los consumidores","Mejora de las decisiones de marketing","Análisis de la psicología del consumidor","Desarrollo de estrategias de marketing efectivas"],"fr":["Application des principes psychologiques en marketing","Influence sur le comportement des consommateurs","Amélioration des décisions de marketing","Analyse de la psychologie du consommateur","Développement de stratégies de marketing efficaces"],"de":["Anwendung psychologischer Prinzipien im Marketing","Beeinflussung des Verhaltens der Konsumenten","Verbesserung der Marketingentscheidungen","Analyse der Konsumentenpsychologie","Entwicklung effektiver Marketingstrategien"],"pt":["Entenda por que as pessoas compram","Influencie comportamentos de compra de forma ética","Aplique modelos mentais para melhorar decisões de marketing","Desenvolva estratégias de marketing personalizadas","Análise de comportamento do consumidor"],"ru":["Понимайте, почему люди покупают","Этично влияйте на поведение покупателей","Применяйте ментальные модели для улучшения маркетинговых решений","Разрабатывайте персонализированные маркетинговые стратегии","Анализ поведения потребителей"],"ar":["فهم لماذا يشترون الناس","تأثير سلوك الشراء بطرق أخلاقية","تطبيق النماذج العقلية لتحسين قرارات التسويق","تطوير استراتيجيات تسويقية مخصصة","تحليل سلوك المستهلك"]},"keywords":{"zh":["营销心理学","心智模型","消费者行为","数据驱动","决策","行为影响","心理学原理"],"ja":["マーケティング心理学","メンタルモデル","消費者の行動","データ駆動","決定","行動への影響","心理学的原理"],"ko":["마케팅 심리학","마음 모델","소비자 행동","데이터 驱动","결정","행동에 영향을 미치기","심리학적 원리"],"es":["psicología de marketing","influencia en el comportamiento","marketing ético","decisiones de marketing","análisis de la psicología del consumidor","estrategias de marketing efectivas"],"fr":["psychologie de marketing","influence sur le comportement","marketing éthique","décisions de marketing","analyse de la psychologie du consommateur","stratégies de marketing efficaces"],"de":["Marketing-Psychologie","Beeinflussung des Verhaltens","ethisches Marketing","Marketingentscheidungen","Analyse der Konsumentenpsychologie","effektive Marketingstrategien"],"pt":["psicologia de marketing","comportamento de compra","modelos mentais","marketing ético","estratégias de marketing","análise de comportamento do consumidor"],"ru":["маркетинг-психология","поведение покупателей","ментальные модели","этический маркетинг","маркетинговые стратегии","анализ поведения потребителей"],"ar":["علم نفس التسويق","سلوك الشراء","نماذج عقلية","تسويق أخلاقي"," استراتيجيات تسويقية","تحليل سلوك المستهلك"]}},"owner":"eKoh951","repo":"hytale-gg","repoPath":"eKoh951/hytale-gg","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"marketing-psychology","description":"When the user wants to apply psychological principles, mental models, or behavioral science to marketing. Also use when the user mentions psychology, mental models, cognitive bias, persuasion, behavioral science, why people buy, decision-making, or consumer behavior. This skill provides 70+ mental models organized for marketing application.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Marketing Psychology & Mental Models\n\nYou are an expert in applying psychological principles and mental models to marketing. Your goal is to help users understand why people buy, how to influence behavior ethically, and how to make better marketing decisions.\n\n## How to Use This Skill\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before applying mental models. Use that context to tailor recommendations to the specific product and audi","body":"# Marketing Psychology & Mental Models\n\nYou are an expert in applying psychological principles and mental models to marketing. Your goal is to help users understand why people buy, how to influence behavior ethically, and how to make better marketing decisions.\n\n## How to Use This Skill\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before applying mental models. Use that context to tailor recommendations to the specific product and audience.\n\nMental models are thinking tools that help you make better decisions, understand customer behavior, and create more effective marketing. When helping users:\n\n1. Identify which mental models apply to their situation\n2. Explain the psychology behind the model\n3. Provide specific marketing applications\n4. Suggest how to implement ethically\n\n---\n\n## Foundational Thinking Models\n\nThese models sharpen your strategy and help you solve the right problems.\n\n### First Principles\nBreak problems down to basic truths and build solutions from there. Instead of copying competitors, ask \"why\" repeatedly to find root causes. Use the 5 Whys technique to tunnel down to what really matters.\n\n**Marketing application**: Don''t assume you need content marketing because competitors do. Ask why you need it, what problem it solves, and whether there''s a better solution.\n\n### Jobs to Be Done\nPeople don''t buy products—they \"hire\" them to get a job done. Focus on the outcome customers want, not features.\n\n**Marketing application**: A drill buyer doesn''t want a drill—they want a hole. Frame your product around the job it accomplishes, not its specifications.\n\n### Circle of Competence\nKnow what you''re good at and stay within it. Venture outside only with proper learning or expert help.\n\n**Marketing application**: Don''t chase every channel. Double down where you have genuine expertise and competitive advantage.\n\n### Inversion\nInstead of asking \"How do I succeed?\", ask \"What would guarantee failure?\" Then avoid those things.\n\n**Marketing application**: List everything that would make your campaign fail—confusing messaging, wrong audience, slow landing page—then systematically prevent each.\n\n### Occam''s Razor\nThe simplest explanation is usually correct. Avoid overcomplicating strategies or attributing results to complex causes when simple ones suffice.\n\n**Marketing application**: If conversions dropped, check the obvious first (broken form, page speed) before assuming complex attribution issues.\n\n### Pareto Principle (80/20 Rule)\nRoughly 80% of results come from 20% of efforts. Identify and focus on the vital few.\n\n**Marketing application**: Find the 20% of channels, customers, or content driving 80% of results. Cut or reduce the rest.\n\n### Local vs. Global Optima\nA local optimum is the best solution nearby, but a global optimum is the best overall. Don''t get stuck optimizing the wrong thing.\n\n**Marketing application**: Optimizing email subject lines (local) won''t help if email isn''t the right channel (global). Zoom out before zooming in.\n\n### Theory of Constraints\nEvery system has one bottleneck limiting throughput. Find and fix that constraint before optimizing elsewhere.\n\n**Marketing application**: If your funnel converts well but traffic is low, more conversion optimization won''t help. Fix the traffic bottleneck first.\n\n### Opportunity Cost\nEvery choice has a cost—what you give up by not choosing alternatives. Consider what you''re saying no to.\n\n**Marketing application**: Time spent on a low-ROI channel is time not spent on high-ROI activities. Always compare against alternatives.\n\n### Law of Diminishing Returns\nAfter a point, additional investment yields progressively smaller gains.\n\n**Marketing application**: The 10th blog post won''t have the same impact as the first. Know when to diversify rather than double down.\n\n### Second-Order Thinking\nConsider not just immediate effects, but the effects of those effects.\n\n**Marketing application**: A flash sale boosts revenue (first order) but may train customers to wait for discounts (second order).\n\n### Map ≠ Territory\nModels and data represent reality but aren''t reality itself. Don''t confuse your analytics dashboard with actual customer experience.\n\n**Marketing application**: Your customer persona is a useful model, but real customers are more complex. Stay in touch with actual users.\n\n### Probabilistic Thinking\nThink in probabilities, not certainties. Estimate likelihoods and plan for multiple outcomes.\n\n**Marketing application**: Don''t bet everything on one campaign. Spread risk and plan for scenarios where your primary strategy underperforms.\n\n### Barbell Strategy\nCombine extreme safety with small high-risk/high-reward bets. Avoid the mediocre middle.\n\n**Marketing application**: Put 80% of budget into proven channels, 20% into experimental bets. Avoid moderate-risk, moderate-reward middle.\n\n---\n\n## Understanding Buyers & Human Psychology\n\nThese models explain how customers think, decide, and behave.\n\n### Fundamental Attribution Error\nPeople attribute others'' behavior to character, not circumstances. \"They didn''t buy because they''re not serious\" vs. \"The checkout was confusing.\"\n\n**Marketing application**: When customers don''t convert, examine your process before blaming them. The problem is usually situational, not personal.\n\n### Mere Exposure Effect\nPeople prefer things they''ve seen before. Familiarity breeds liking.\n\n**Marketing application**: Consistent brand presence builds preference over time. Repetition across channels creates comfort and trust.\n\n### Availability Heuristic\nPeople judge likelihood by how easily examples come to mind. Recent or vivid events seem more common.\n\n**Marketing application**: Case studies and testimonials make success feel more achievable. Make positive outcomes easy to imagine.\n\n### Confirmation Bias\nPeople seek information confirming existing beliefs and ignore contradictory evidence.\n\n**Marketing application**: Understand what your audience already believes and align messaging accordingly. Fighting beliefs head-on rarely works.\n\n### The Lindy Effect\nThe longer something has survived, the longer it''s likely to continue. Old ideas often outlast new ones.\n\n**Marketing application**: Proven marketing principles (clear value props, social proof) outlast trendy tactics. Don''t abandon fundamentals for fads.\n\n### Mimetic Desire\nPeople want things because others want them. Desire is socially contagious.\n\n**Marketing application**: Show that desirable people want your product. Waitlists, exclusivity, and social proof trigger mimetic desire.\n\n### Sunk Cost Fallacy\nPeople continue investing in something because of past investment, even when it''s no longer rational.\n\n**Marketing application**: Know when to kill underperforming campaigns. Past spend shouldn''t justify future spend if results aren''t there.\n\n### Endowment Effect\nPeople value things more once they own them.\n\n**Marketing application**: Free trials, samples, and freemium models let customers \"own\" the product, making them reluctant to give it up.\n\n### IKEA Effect\nPeople value things more when they''ve put effort into creating them.\n\n**Marketing application**: Let customers customize, configure, or build something. Their investment increases perceived value and commitment.\n\n### Zero-Price Effect\nFree isn''t just a low price—it''s psychologically different. \"Free\" triggers irrational preference.\n\n**Marketing application**: Free tiers, free trials, and free shipping have disproportionate appeal. The jump from $1 to $0 is bigger than $2 to $1.\n\n### Hyperbolic Discounting / Present Bias\nPeople strongly prefer immediate rewards over future ones, even when waiting is more rational.\n\n**Marketing application**: Emphasize immediate benefits (\"Start saving time today\") over future ones (\"You''ll see ROI in 6 months\").\n\n### Status-Quo Bias\nPeople prefer the current state of affairs. Change requires effort and feels risky.\n\n**Marketing application**: Reduce friction to switch. Make the transition feel safe and easy. \"Import your data in one click.\"\n\n### Default Effect\nPeople tend to accept pre-selected options. Defaults are powerful.\n\n**Marketing application**: Pre-select the plan you want customers to choose. Opt-out beats opt-in for subscriptions (ethically applied).\n\n### Paradox of Choice\nToo many options overwhelm and paralyze. Fewer choices often lead to more decisions.\n\n**Marketing application**: Limit options. Three pricing tiers beat seven. Recommend a single \"best for most\" option.\n\n### Goal-Gradient Effect\nPeople accelerate effort as they approach a goal. Progress visualization motivates action.\n\n**Marketing application**: Show progress bars, completion percentages, and \"almost there\" messaging to drive completion.\n\n### Peak-End Rule\nPeople judge experiences by the peak (best or worst moment) and the end, not the average.\n\n**Marketing application**: Design memorable peaks (surprise upgrades, delightful moments) and strong endings (thank you pages, follow-up emails).\n\n### Zeigarnik Effect\nUnfinished tasks occupy the mind more than completed ones. Open loops create tension.\n\n**Marketing application**: \"You''re 80% done\" creates pull to finish. Incomplete profiles, abandoned carts, and cliffhangers leverage this.\n\n### Pratfall Effect\nCompetent people become more likable when they show a small flaw. Perfection is less relatable.\n\n**Marketing application**: Admitting a weakness (\"We''re not the cheapest, but...\") can increase trust and differentiation.\n\n### Curse of Knowledge\nOnce you know something, you can''t imagine not knowing it. Experts struggle to explain simply.\n\n**Marketing application**: Your product seems obvious to you but confusing to newcomers. Test copy with people unfamiliar with your space.\n\n### Mental Accounting\nPeople treat money differently based on its source or intended use, even though money is fungible.\n\n**Marketing application**: Frame costs in favorable mental accounts. \"$3/day\" feels different than \"$90/month\" even though it''s the same.\n\n### Regret Aversion\nPeople avoid actions that might cause regret, even if the expected outcome is positive.\n\n**Marketing application**: Address regret directly. Money-back guarantees, free trials, and \"no commitment\" messaging reduce regret fear.\n\n### Bandwagon Effect / Social Proof\nPeople follow what others are doing. Popularity signals quality and safety.\n\n**Marketing application**: Show customer counts, testimonials, logos, reviews, and \"trending\" indicators. Numbers create confidence.\n\n---\n\n## Influencing Behavior & Persuasion\n\nThese models help you ethically influence customer decisions.\n\n### Reciprocity Principle\nPeople feel obligated to return favors. Give first, and people want to give back.\n\n**Marketing application**: Free content, free tools, and generous free tiers create reciprocal obligation. Give value before asking for anything.\n\n### Commitment & Consistency\nOnce people commit to something, they want to stay consistent with that commitment.\n\n**Marketing application**: Get small commitments first (email signup, free trial). People who''ve taken one step are more likely to take the next.\n\n### Authority Bias\nPeople defer to experts and authority figures. Credentials and expertise create trust.\n\n**Marketing application**: Feature expert endorsements, certifications, \"featured in\" logos, and thought leadership content.\n\n### Liking / Similarity Bias\nPeople say yes to those they like and those similar to themselves.\n\n**Marketing application**: Use relatable spokespeople, founder stories, and community language. \"Built by marketers for marketers\" signals similarity.\n\n### Unity Principle\nShared identity drives influence. \"One of us\" is powerful.\n\n**Marketing application**: Position your brand as part of the customer''s tribe. Use insider language and shared values.\n\n### Scarcity / Urgency Heuristic\nLimited availability increases perceived value. Scarcity signals desirability.\n\n**Marketing application**: Limited-time offers, low-stock warnings, and exclusive access create urgency. Only use when genuine.\n\n### Foot-in-the-Door Technique\nStart with a small request, then escalate. Compliance with small requests leads to compliance with larger ones.\n\n**Marketing application**: Free trial → paid plan → annual plan → enterprise. Each step builds on the last.\n\n### Door-in-the-Face Technique\nStart with an unreasonably large request, then retreat to what you actually want. The contrast makes the second request seem reasonable.\n\n**Marketing application**: Show enterprise pricing first, then reveal the affordable starter plan. The contrast makes it feel like a deal.\n\n### Loss Aversion / Prospect Theory\nLosses feel roughly twice as painful as equivalent gains feel good. People will work harder to avoid losing than to gain.\n\n**Marketing application**: Frame in terms of what they''ll lose by not acting. \"Don''t miss out\" beats \"You could gain.\"\n\n### Anchoring Effect\nThe first number people see heavily influences subsequent judgments.\n\n**Marketing application**: Show the higher price first (original price, competitor price, enterprise tier) to anchor expectations.\n\n### Decoy Effect\nAdding a third, inferior option makes one of the original two look better.\n\n**Marketing application**: A \"decoy\" pricing tier that''s clearly worse value makes your preferred tier look like the obvious choice.\n\n### Framing Effect\nHow something is presented changes how it''s perceived. Same facts, different frames.\n\n**Marketing application**: \"90% success rate\" vs. \"10% failure rate\" are identical but feel different. Frame positively.\n\n### Contrast Effect\nThings seem different depending on what they''re compared to.\n\n**Marketing application**: Show the \"before\" state clearly. The contrast with your \"after\" makes improvements vivid.\n\n---\n\n## Pricing Psychology\n\nThese models specifically address how people perceive and respond to prices.\n\n### Charm Pricing / Left-Digit Effect\nPrices ending in 9 seem significantly lower than the next round number. $99 feels much cheaper than $100.\n\n**Marketing application**: Use .99 or .95 endings for value-focused products. The left digit dominates perception.\n\n### Rounded-Price (Fluency) Effect\nRound numbers feel premium and are easier to process. $100 signals quality; $99 signals value.\n\n**Marketing application**: Use round prices for premium products ($500/month), charm prices for value products ($497/month).\n\n### Rule of 100\nFor prices under $100, percentage discounts seem larger (\"20% off\"). For prices over $100, absolute discounts seem larger (\"$50 off\").\n\n**Marketing application**: $80 product: \"20% off\" beats \"$16 off.\" $500 product: \"$100 off\" beats \"20% off.\"\n\n### Price Relativity / Good-Better-Best\nPeople judge prices relative to options presented. A middle tier seems reasonable between cheap and expensive.\n\n**Marketing application**: Three tiers where the middle is your target. The expensive tier makes it look reasonable; the cheap tier provides an anchor.\n\n### Mental Accounting (Pricing)\nFraming the same price differently changes perception.\n\n**Marketing application**: \"$1/day\" feels cheaper than \"$30/month.\" \"Less than your morning coffee\" reframes the expense.\n\n---\n\n## Design & Delivery Models\n\nThese models help you design effective marketing systems.\n\n### Hick''s Law\nDecision time increases with the number and complexity of choices. More options = slower decisions = more abandonment.\n\n**Marketing application**: Simplify choices. One clear CTA beats three. Fewer form fields beat more.\n\n### AIDA Funnel\nAttention → Interest → Desire → Action. The classic customer journey model.\n\n**Marketing application**: Structure pages and campaigns to move through each stage. Capture attention before building desire.\n\n### Rule of 7\nProspects need roughly 7 touchpoints before converting. One ad rarely converts; sustained presence does.\n\n**Marketing application**: Build multi-touch campaigns across channels. Retargeting, email sequences, and consistent presence compound.\n\n### Nudge Theory / Choice Architecture\nSmall changes in how choices are presented significantly influence decisions.\n\n**Marketing application**: Default selections, strategic ordering, and friction reduction guide behavior without restricting choice.\n\n### BJ Fogg Behavior Model\nBehavior = Motivation × Ability × Prompt. All three must be present for action.\n\n**Marketing application**: High motivation but hard to do = won''t happen. Easy to do but no prompt = won''t happen. Design for all three.\n\n### EAST Framework\nMake desired behaviors: Easy, Attractive, Social, Timely.\n\n**Marketing application**: Reduce friction (easy), make it appealing (attractive), show others doing it (social), ask at the right moment (timely).\n\n### COM-B Model\nBehavior requires: Capability, Opportunity, Motivation.\n\n**Marketing application**: Can they do it (capability)? Is the path clear (opportunity)? Do they want to (motivation)? Address all three.\n\n### Activation Energy\nThe initial energy required to start something. High activation energy prevents action even if the task is easy overall.\n\n**Marketing application**: Reduce starting friction. Pre-fill forms, offer templates, show quick wins. Make the first step trivially easy.\n\n### North Star Metric\nOne metric that best captures the value you deliver to customers. Focus creates alignment.\n\n**Marketing application**: Identify your North Star (active users, completed projects, revenue per customer) and align all efforts toward it.\n\n### The Cobra Effect\nWhen incentives backfire and produce the opposite of intended results.\n\n**Marketing application**: Test incentive structures. A referral bonus might attract low-quality referrals gaming the system.\n\n---\n\n## Growth & Scaling Models\n\nThese models explain how marketing compounds and scales.\n\n### Feedback Loops\nOutput becomes input, creating cycles. Positive loops accelerate growth; negative loops create decline.\n\n**Marketing application**: Build virtuous cycles: more users → more content → better SEO → more users. Identify and strengthen positive loops.\n\n### Compounding\nSmall, consistent gains accumulate into large results over time. Early gains matter most.\n\n**Marketing application**: Consistent content, SEO, and brand building compound. Start early; benefits accumulate exponentially.\n\n### Network Effects\nA product becomes more valuable as more people use it.\n\n**Marketing application**: Design features that improve with more users: shared workspaces, integrations, marketplaces, communities.\n\n### Flywheel Effect\nSustained effort creates momentum that eventually maintains itself. Hard to start, easy to maintain.\n\n**Marketing application**: Content → traffic → leads → customers → case studies → more content. Each element powers the next.\n\n### Switching Costs\nThe price (time, money, effort, data) of changing to a competitor. High switching costs create retention.\n\n**Marketing application**: Increase switching costs ethically: integrations, data accumulation, workflow customization, team adoption.\n\n### Exploration vs. Exploitation\nBalance trying new things (exploration) with optimizing what works (exploitation).\n\n**Marketing application**: Don''t abandon working channels for shiny new ones, but allocate some budget to experiments.\n\n### Critical Mass / Tipping Point\nThe threshold after which growth becomes self-sustaining.\n\n**Marketing application**: Focus resources on reaching critical mass in one segment before expanding. Depth before breadth.\n\n### Survivorship Bias\nFocusing on successes while ignoring failures that aren''t visible.\n\n**Marketing application**: Study failed campaigns, not just successful ones. The viral hit you''re copying had 99 failures you didn''t see.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\nWhen facing a marketing challenge, consider:\n\n| Challenge | Relevant Models |\n|-----------|-----------------|\n| Low conversions | Hick''s Law, Activation Energy, BJ Fogg, Friction |\n| Price objections | Anchoring, Framing, Mental Accounting, Loss Aversion |\n| Building trust | Authority, Social Proof, Reciprocity, Pratfall Effect |\n| Increasing urgency | Scarcity, Loss Aversion, Zeigarnik Effect |\n| Retention/churn | Endowment Effect, Switching Costs, Status-Quo Bias |\n| Growth stalling | Theory of Constraints, Local vs Global Optima, Compounding |\n| Decision paralysis | Paradox of Choice, Default Effect, Nudge Theory |\n| Onboarding | Goal-Gradient, IKEA Effect, Commitment & Consistency |\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What specific behavior are you trying to influence?\n2. What does your customer believe before encountering your marketing?\n3. Where in the journey (awareness → consideration → decision) is this?\n4. What''s currently preventing the desired action?\n5. Have you tested this with real customers?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **page-cro**: Apply psychology to page optimization\n- **copywriting**: Write copy using psychological principles\n- **popup-cro**: Use triggers and psychology in popups\n- **pricing-page optimization**: See page-cro for pricing psychology\n- **ab-test-setup**: Test psychological hypotheses\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:21:27.704Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude or AutoGPT needing to apply psychological principles to influence consumer behavior and make data-driven marketing decisions.","zh":"适用于像 Claude 或 AutoGPT 这样的 AI 代理，需要应用心理学原理来影响消费者行为并做出数据驱动的营销决策。","ja":"Claude 或 AutoGPT などの AI エージェントが消費者行動に心理学的原則を適用してデータドリブンなマーケティングの決定を下すのに適しています。","ko":"Claude 또는 AutoGPT와 같은 AI 에이전트가 소비자 행동에 심리학적 원리를 적용하여 데이터 기반 마케팅 결정을 내리기에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude o AutoGPT que necesitan aplicar principios psicológicos para influir en el comportamiento del consumidor y tomar decisiones de marketing basadas en datos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude ou AutoGPT ayant besoin d''appliquer des principes psychologiques pour influencer le comportement du consommateur et prendre des décisions de marketing basées sur des données.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude oder AutoGPT, die psychologische Prinzipien anwenden müssen, um das Verbraucherverhalten zu beeinflussen und datengetriebene Marketingentscheidungen zu treffen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude ou AutoGPT que precisam aplicar princípios psicológicos para influenciar o comportamento do consumidor e tomar decisões de marketing baseadas em dados.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude или AutoGPT, которым необходимо применять психологические принципы для влияния на поведение потребителей и принятия решений по маркетингу на основе данных.","ar":"مثالية لعمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude أو AutoGPT التي تحتاج إلى تطبيق المبادئ النفسية لتأثير سلوك المستهلك واتخاذ قرارات التسويق القائمة على البيانات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage mental models and psychological principles, such as understanding why people buy and how to ethically influence behavior, to inform marketing strategies and optimize product marketing context using files like `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","zh":"赋予代理人利用心理模型和心理原则的能力，例如了解为什么人们购买以及如何以合乎道德的方式影响行为，以此来指导营销策略并使用诸如 `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` 之类的文件来优化产品营销背景。","ja":"エージェントが心理モデルや心理原則を利用できるようにし、たとえばなぜ人々が購入するのか、またどのように倫理的に行動を影響できるのかを理解し、これをもとにマーケティング戦略を立て、`.claude/product-marketing-context.md` などのファイルを使用して製品マーケティングのコンテキストを最適化する。","ko":"에이전트가 심리 모델과 심리학적 원리를 활용할 수 있도록 해주어 예를 들어 사람들이 왜 구매하는지, 그리고 어떻게 윤리적으로 행동에 영향을 줄 수 있는지 이해하여 이를 바탕으로 마케팅 전략을 수립하고 `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`와 같은 파일을 사용하여 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트를 최적화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar modelos mentales y principios psicológicos, como entender por qué la gente compra y cómo influir éticamente en el comportamiento, para informar estrategias de marketing y optimizar el contexto de marketing de productos utilizando archivos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter des modèles mentaux et des principes psychologiques, tels que la compréhension de pourquoi les gens achètent et de la manière d''influencer éthiquement le comportement, pour éclairer les stratégies de marketing et optimiser le contexte de marketing de produits en utilisant des fichiers comme `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, mentale Modelle und psychologische Prinzipien wie das Verständnis, warum Menschen kaufen und wie man das Verhalten ethisch beeinflusst, zu nutzen, um Marketingstrategien zu informieren und den Kontext des Produktmarketings mithilfe von Dateien wie `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` zu optimieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitarem modelos mentais e princípios psicológicos, como entender por que as pessoas compram e como influenciar eticamente o comportamento, para informar estratégias de marketing e otimizar o contexto de marketing de produtos usando arquivos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать психологические модели и принципы, такие как понимание причин покупки и этичного влияния на поведение, для разработки маркетинговых стратегий и оптимизации контекста маркетинга продукта с помощью файлов типа `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من استخدام النماذج العقلية والمبادئ النفسية، مثل فهم سبب شراء الناس وكيفية التأثير على السلوك بطريقة أخلاقية، لتحديد استراتيجيات التسويق وضبط سياق تسويق المنتج باستخدام ملفات مثل `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing consumer purchasing decisions","Developing targeted marketing campaigns","Optimizing product marketing context for better engagement"],"zh":["分析消费者购买决策","开发有针对性的营销活动","优化产品营销背景以提高参与度"],"ja":["消費者による購入決定を分析する","ターゲットを絞ったマーケティングキャンペーンを開発する","製品マーケティングのコンテキストを最適化してエンゲージメントを高める"],"ko":["소비자 구매 결정 분석","타겟 마케팅 캠페인 개발","제품 마케팅 컨텍스트 최적화하여 참여도 향상"],"es":["Análisis de las decisiones de compra de los consumidores","Desarrollo de campañas de marketing dirigidas","Optimización del contexto de marketing de productos para una mejor participación"],"fr":["Analyse des décisions d''achat des consommateurs","Développement de campagnes de marketing ciblées","Optimisation du contexte de marketing de produits pour une meilleure implication"],"de":["Analyse der Kaufentscheidungen der Verbraucher","Entwicklung gezielter Marketingkampagnen","Optimierung des Produktmarketing-Kontexts für eine bessere Einbindung"],"pt":["Analisar decisões de compra do consumidor","Desenvolver campanhas de marketing direcionadas","Otimizar o contexto de marketing de produtos para melhor engajamento"],"ru":["Анализ решений потребителей о покупке","Разработка целевых маркетинговых кампаний","Оптимизация контекста маркетинга продукта для лучшего взаимодействия"],"ar":["تحليل قرارات شراء المستهلك","تطوير حملات تسويقية مستهدفة","تحسين سياق تسويق المنتج من أجل التواصل الأفضل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires existence of `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` for tailored recommendations","Limited to ethical influence strategies"],"zh":["需要 `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` 文件的存在以提供个性化推荐","仅限于伦理影响策略"],"ja":["`.claude/product-marketing-context.md` ファイルの存在が必要で、カスタマイズされた推奨事項を提供する","倫理的な影響戦略に限定される"],"ko":["`.claude/product-marketing-context.md` 파일의 존재가 필요하여 맞춤형 추천을 제공","윤리적인 영향 전략에만 محدود"],"es":["Requiere la existencia de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para recomendaciones personalizadas","Limitado a estrategias de influencia ética"],"fr":["Nécessite l''existence de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` pour des recommandations personnalisées","Limité à des stratégies d''influence éthique"],"de":["Benötigt die Existenz von `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` für maßgeschneiderte Empfehlungen","Begrenzt auf ethische Einflussstrategien"],"pt":["Exige a existência de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para recomendações personalizadas","Limitado a estratégias de influência ética"],"ru":["Требует существования `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` для индивидуальных рекомендаций","Ограничен стратегиями этического влияния"],"ar":["يتطلب وجود `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` لتوصيات مُخصصة","محدود بالاستراتيجيات التأثيرية الأخلاقية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering/openspec-continue-change', 'community', 'gAmUssA', 'ai-assisted-engineering', 'gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering', 'openspec-continue-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.508Z', '2026-02-18T12:21:20.072Z', NULL, '{"id":"gAmUssA/ai-assisted-engineering/openspec-continue-change","name":"openspec-continue-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change 技术技能用于继续工作中的代码变更，通过创建下一个工件实现高效的代码管理","ja":"openspec-continue-change 技術スキルは、コードの変更を続行するために使用され、次のアーティファクトを作成することでコード管理を効率化します","ko":"openspec-continue-change 개발 기술은 코드 변경을 계속 수행하는 데 사용되며, 다음 아티팩트를 생성하여 코드 관리를 효율화합니다","es":"La habilidad openspec-continue-change permite continuar trabajando en cambios creando el siguiente artefacto. Selecciona un cambio para trabajar.","fr":"La compétence openspec-continue-change permet de continuer à travailler sur des modifications en créant le prochain artefact. Sélectionnez une modification pour travailler.","de":"Die Fähigkeit openspec-continue-change ermöglicht das Fortsetzen von Änderungen durch das Erstellen des nächsten Artefakt. Wählen Sie eine Änderung aus, an der Sie arbeiten möchten.","pt":"O OpenSpec permite continuar trabalhando em uma mudança, criando o próximo artefato e selecionando mudanças com facilidade.","ru":"OpenSpec позволяет продолжить работу над изменением, создавая следующий артефакт и выбирая изменения легко.","ar":"يسمح OpenSpec بالاستمرار في العمل على التغيير، وقم بإنشاء الملف التالي واختر التغييرات بسهولة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-continue-change 技术技能","ja":"openspec-continue-change 技術スキル","ko":"openspec-continue-change 개발 기술","es":"Continuar cambios con openspec","fr":"Continuer les modifications avec openspec","de":"Änderungen mit openspec fortsetzen","pt":"Continue Change com OpenSpec","ru":"Продолжить изменение с OpenSpec","ar":"استمرار التغ