,"description":{"zh":"Temporal 工作流编排模式提供了构建可靠分布式系统的基础，涵盖基本设计决策、恢复模式和最佳实践","ja":"Temporal ワークフロー オーケストレーション パターンは、信頼性の高い分散システムを構築するための基本設計決定、復元パターン、ベスト プラクティスを提供します","ko":"Temporal 워크플로우 오케스트레이션 패턴은 안정적인 분산 시스템을 구축하기 위한 기본 설계 결정, 복구 패턴 및 최적화된 방법을 제공합니다","es":"Descubre los patrones de orquestación de flujo de trabajo para construir sistemas distribuidos confiables con Temporal","fr":"Découvrez les modèles d''orchestration de flux de travail pour construire des systèmes distribués fiables avec Temporal","de":"Entdecken Sie die Muster der Workflow-Orchestrierung, um zuverlässige verteilte Systeme mit Temporal zu bauen","pt":"Orquestração de fluxo de trabalho com Temporal, abordando decisões de design fundamentais, padrões de resiliência e boas práticas para sistemas distribuídos ...","ru":"Оркестровка рабочих процессов с помощью Temporal, включающая основные решения по проектированию, шаблоны устойчивости и лучшие практики для надежных распреде...","ar":"إدارة تدفقات العمل مع Temporal، تغطية القرارات الأساسية للتصميم وأنماط الاستجابة وأفضل الأساليب لبناء أنظمة موزعة موثوقة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["多步骤过程管理","分布式事务支持","长时间运行的工作流支持","自动状态管理","恢复模式支持"],"ja":["多ステップ プロセスの管理","分散トランザクションのサポート","長時間実行されるワークフローのサポート","自動ステート管理","復元パターンのサポート"],"ko":["다단계 프로세스 관리","분산 트랜잭션 지원","장시간 실행되는 워크플로우 지원","자동 상태 관리","복구 패턴 지원"],"es":["Procesos multi-paso","Transacciones distribuidas","Flujos de trabajo de larga duración","Arquitectura de orquestación","Resiliencia y tolerancia a fallos","Mejores prácticas para sistemas distribuidos"],"fr":["Processus multi-étapes","Transactions distribuées","Flux de travail de longue durée","Architecture d''orchestration","Résilience et tolérance aux défaillances","Meilleures pratiques pour les systèmes distribués"],"de":["Mehrstufige Prozesse","Verteilte Transaktionen","Langfristige Workflows","Orchestrierungsarchitektur","Resilienz und Fehlertoleranz","Beste Praktiken für verteilte Systeme"],"pt":["Suporte a processos de vários passos","Transações distribuídas com semântica all-or-nothing","Fluxos de trabalho de longa duração com estado automático","Padrões de resiliência para sistemas distribuídos","Boas práticas para construir sistemas confiáveis"],"ru":["Поддержка многоступенчатых процессов","Распределенные транзакции с семантикой all-or-nothing","Долгосрочные рабочие процессы с автоматическим состоянием","Шаблоны устойчивости для распределенных систем","Лучшие практики для построения надежных систем"],"ar":["دعم العمليات متعددة الخطوات","عمليات توزيعية ذات معنى كل شيء أو لا شيء","تدفقات عمل طويلة الأجل ذات حالة تلقائية","أنماط الاستجابة لأنظمة موزعة","أفضل الأساليب لبناء أنظمة موثوقة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["工作流编排","分布式系统","Temporal","工作流管理","恢复模式","自动状态管理"],"ja":["ワークフロー オーケストレーション","分散システム","Temporal","ワークフロー管理","復元パターン","自動ステート管理"],"ko":["워크플로우 오케스트레이션","분산 시스템","Temporal","워크플로우 관리","복구 패턴","자동 상태 관리"],"es":["orquestación de flujo de trabajo","patrones de diseño","sistemas distribuidos","Temporal","resiliencia","tolerancia a fallos","mejores prácticas","arquitectura de software","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["orchestration de flux de travail","modèles de conception","systèmes distribués","Temporal","résilience","tolérance aux défaillances","meilleures pratiques","architecture logicielle","développement logiciel"],"de":["Workflow-Orchestrierung","Entwurfsmuster","verteilte Systeme","Temporal","Resilienz","Fehlertoleranz","beste Praktiken","Software-Architektur","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["orquestração de fluxo de trabalho","padrões de design","resiliência","sistemas distribuídos","reliable systems","temporal","workflow orchestration"],"ru":["оркестровка рабочих процессов","шаблоны проектирования","устойчивость","распределенные системы","надежные системы","temporal","workflow orchestration"],"ar":["إدارة تدفقات العمل","أنماط التصميم","الاستجابة","الأنظمة الموزعة","النظم الموثوقة","temporal","workflow orchestration"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"orchestrator","repoPath":"ollieb89/orchestrator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.509Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"workflow-orchestration-patterns","description":"Design durable workflows with Temporal for distributed systems. Covers workflow vs activity separation, saga patterns, state management, and determinism constraints. Use when building long-running processes, distributed transactions, or microservice orchestration.","bodyPreview":"# Workflow Orchestration Patterns\n\nMaster workflow orchestration architecture with Temporal, covering fundamental design decisions, resilience patterns, and best practices for building reliable distributed systems.\n\n## When to Use Workflow Orchestration\n\n### Ideal Use Cases (Source: docs.temporal.io)\n\n- **Multi-step processes** spanning machines/services/databases\n- **Distributed transactions** requiring all-or-nothing semantics\n- **Long-running workflows** (hours to years) with automatic state","body":"# Workflow Orchestration Patterns\n\nMaster workflow orchestration architecture with Temporal, covering fundamental design decisions, resilience patterns, and best practices for building reliable distributed systems.\n\n## When to Use Workflow Orchestration\n\n### Ideal Use Cases (Source: docs.temporal.io)\n\n- **Multi-step processes** spanning machines/services/databases\n- **Distributed transactions** requiring all-or-nothing semantics\n- **Long-running workflows** (hours to years) with automatic state persistence\n- **Failure recovery** that must resume from last successful step\n- **Business processes**: bookings, orders, campaigns, approvals\n- **Entity lifecycle management**: inventory tracking, account management, cart workflows\n- **Infrastructure automation**: CI/CD pipelines, provisioning, deployments\n- **Human-in-the-loop** systems requiring timeouts and escalations\n\n### When NOT to Use\n\n- Simple CRUD operations (use direct API calls)\n- Pure data processing pipelines (use Airflow, batch processing)\n- Stateless request/response (use standard APIs)\n- Real-time streaming (use Kafka, event processors)\n\n## Critical Design Decision: Workflows vs Activities\n\n**The Fundamental Rule** (Source: temporal.io/blog/workflow-engine-principles):\n- **Workflows** = Orchestration logic and decision-making\n- **Activities** = External interactions (APIs, databases, network calls)\n\n### Workflows (Orchestration)\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- Contain business logic and coordination\n- **MUST be deterministic** (same inputs → same outputs)\n- **Cannot** perform direct external calls\n- State automatically preserved across failures\n- Can run for years despite infrastructure failures\n\n**Example workflow tasks:**\n- Decide which steps to execute\n- Handle compensation logic\n- Manage timeouts and retries\n- Coordinate child workflows\n\n### Activities (External Interactions)\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- Handle all external system interactions\n- Can be non-deterministic (API calls, DB writes)\n- Include built-in timeouts and retry logic\n- **Must be idempotent** (calling N times = calling once)\n- Short-lived (seconds to minutes typically)\n\n**Example activity tasks:**\n- Call payment gateway API\n- Write to database\n- Send emails or notifications\n- Query external services\n\n### Design Decision Framework\n\n```\nDoes it touch external systems? → Activity\nIs it orchestration/decision logic? → Workflow\n```\n\n## Core Workflow Patterns\n\n### 1. Saga Pattern with Compensation\n\n**Purpose**: Implement distributed transactions with rollback capability\n\n**Pattern** (Source: temporal.io/blog/compensating-actions-part-of-a-complete-breakfast-with-sagas):\n\n```\nFor each step:\n  1. Register compensation BEFORE executing\n  2. Execute the step (via activity)\n  3. On failure, run all compensations in reverse order (LIFO)\n```\n\n**Example: Payment Workflow**\n1. Reserve inventory (compensation: release inventory)\n2. Charge payment (compensation: refund payment)\n3. Fulfill order (compensation: cancel fulfillment)\n\n**Critical Requirements:**\n- Compensations must be idempotent\n- Register compensation BEFORE executing step\n- Run compensations in reverse order\n- Handle partial failures gracefully\n\n### 2. Entity Workflows (Actor Model)\n\n**Purpose**: Long-lived workflow representing single entity instance\n\n**Pattern** (Source: docs.temporal.io/evaluate/use-cases-design-patterns):\n- One workflow execution = one entity (cart, account, inventory item)\n- Workflow persists for entity lifetime\n- Receives signals for state changes\n- Supports queries for current state\n\n**Example Use Cases:**\n- Shopping cart (add items, checkout, expiration)\n- Bank account (deposits, withdrawals, balance checks)\n- Product inventory (stock updates, reservations)\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Encapsulates entity behavior\n- Guarantees consistency per entity\n- Natural event sourcing\n\n### 3. Fan-Out/Fan-In (Parallel Execution)\n\n**Purpose**: Execute multiple tasks in parallel, aggregate results\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Spawn child workflows or parallel activities\n- Wait for all to complete\n- Aggregate results\n- Handle partial failures\n\n**Scaling Rule** (Source: temporal.io/blog/workflow-engine-principles):\n- Don''t scale individual workflows\n- For 1M tasks: spawn 1K child workflows × 1K tasks each\n- Keep each workflow bounded\n\n### 4. Async Callback Pattern\n\n**Purpose**: Wait for external event or human approval\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Workflow sends request and waits for signal\n- External system processes asynchronously\n- Sends signal to resume workflow\n- Workflow continues with response\n\n**Use Cases:**\n- Human approval workflows\n- Webhook callbacks\n- Long-running external processes\n\n## State Management and Determinism\n\n### Automatic State Preservation\n\n**How Temporal Works** (Source: docs.temporal.io/workflows):\n- Complete program state preserved automatically\n- Event History records every command and event\n- Seamless recovery from crashes\n- Applications restore pre-failure state\n\n### Determinism Constraints\n\n**Workflows Execute as State Machines**:\n- Replay behavior must be consistent\n- Same inputs → identical outputs every time\n\n**Prohibited in Workflows** (Source: docs.temporal.io/workflows):\n- ❌ Threading, locks, synchronization primitives\n- ❌ Random number generation (`random()`)\n- ❌ Global state or static variables\n- ❌ System time (`datetime.now()`)\n- ❌ Direct file I/O or network calls\n- ❌ Non-deterministic libraries\n\n**Allowed in Workflows**:\n- ✅ `workflow.now()` (deterministic time)\n- ✅ `workflow.random()` (deterministic random)\n- ✅ Pure functions and calculations\n- ✅ Calling activities (non-deterministic operations)\n\n### Versioning Strategies\n\n**Challenge**: Changing workflow code while old executions still running\n\n**Solutions**:\n1. **Versioning API**: Use `workflow.get_version()` for safe changes\n2. **New Workflow Type**: Create new workflow, route new executions to it\n3. **Backward Compatibility**: Ensure old events replay correctly\n\n## Resilience and Error Handling\n\n### Retry Policies\n\n**Default Behavior**: Temporal retries activities forever\n\n**Configure Retry**:\n- Initial retry interval\n- Backoff coefficient (exponential backoff)\n- Maximum interval (cap retry delay)\n- Maximum attempts (eventually fail)\n\n**Non-Retryable Errors**:\n- Invalid input (validation failures)\n- Business rule violations\n- Permanent failures (resource not found)\n\n### Idempotency Requirements\n\n**Why Critical** (Source: docs.temporal.io/activities):\n- Activities may execute multiple times\n- Network failures trigger retries\n- Duplicate execution must be safe\n\n**Implementation Strategies**:\n- Idempotency keys (deduplication)\n- Check-then-act with unique constraints\n- Upsert operations instead of insert\n- Track processed request IDs\n\n### Activity Heartbeats\n\n**Purpose**: Detect stalled long-running activities\n\n**Pattern**:\n- Activity sends periodic heartbeat\n- Includes progress information\n- Timeout if no heartbeat received\n- Enables progress-based retry\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Workflow Design\n\n1. **Keep workflows focused** - Single responsibility per workflow\n2. **Small workflows** - Use child workflows for scalability\n3. **Clear boundaries** - Workflow orchestrates, activities execute\n4. **Test locally** - Use time-skipping test environment\n\n### Activity Design\n\n1. **Idempotent operations** - Safe to retry\n2. **Short-lived** - Seconds to minutes, not hours\n3. **Timeout configuration** - Always set timeouts\n4. **Heartbeat for long tasks** - Report progress\n5. **Error handling** - Distinguish retryable vs non-retryable\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n\n**Workflow Violations**:\n- Using `datetime.now()` instead of `workflow.now()`\n- Threading or async operations in workflow code\n- Calling external APIs directly from workflow\n- Non-deterministic logic in workflows\n\n**Activity Mistakes**:\n- Non-idempotent operations (can''t handle retries)\n- Missing timeouts (activities run forever)\n- No error classification (retry validation errors)\n- Ignoring payload limits (2MB per argument)\n\n### Operational Considerations\n\n**Monitoring**:\n- Workflow execution duration\n- Activity failure rates\n- Retry attempts and backoff\n- Pending workflow counts\n\n**Scalability**:\n- Horizontal scaling with workers\n- Task queue partitioning\n- Child workflow decomposition\n- Activity batching when appropriate\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n**Official Documentation**:\n- Temporal Core Concepts: docs.temporal.io/workflows\n- Workflow Patterns: docs.temporal.io/evaluate/use-cases-design-patterns\n- Best Practices: docs.temporal.io/develop/best-practices\n- Saga Pattern: temporal.io/blog/saga-pattern-made-easy\n\n**Key Principles**:\n1. Workflows = orchestration, Activities = external calls\n2. Determinism is non-negotiable for workflows\n3. Idempotency is critical for activities\n4. State preservation is automatic\n5. Design for failure and recovery\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:22:48.079Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Distributed System Agents needing reliable workflow orchestration with Temporal","zh":"适合需要可靠工作流编排的分布式系统代理，使用 Temporal","ja":"Temporal を使用した信頼性の高いワークフロー オーケストレーションが必要な分散システム エージェントに適しています","ko":"Temporal을 사용하여 안정적인 워크플로우 오케스트레이션이 필요한 분산 시스템 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Sistemas Distribuidos que necesitan una orquestación de flujo de trabajo confiable con Temporal","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de systèmes distribués ayant besoin d''une orchestration de workflow fiable avec Temporal","de":"Perfekt für verteilte Systemagenten, die eine zuverlässige Workflow-Orchestrierung mit Temporal benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Sistemas Distribuídos que necessitam de orquestração de fluxo de trabalho confiável com Temporal","ru":"Идеально для распределенных системных агентов, которым требуется надежная оркестрация рабочих процессов с помощью Temporal","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التوزيع التي تحتاج إلى تنسيق عمل موثوق به مع Temporal"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to master workflow orchestration architecture, leveraging resilience patterns and best practices for building reliable distributed systems with multi-step processes, distributed transactions, and long-running workflows using Temporal","zh":"赋予代理掌握工作流编排架构的能力，利用弹性模式和最佳实践来构建可靠的分布式系统，包括多步骤流程、分布式事务和长时间运行的工作流，使用 Temporal","ja":"エージェントにワークフロー オーケストレーション アーキテクチャをマスターする能力を付与し、Temporal を使用して多ステップ プロセス、分散トランザクション、長時間実行されるワークフローを含む信頼性の高い分散システムを構築するための回復性パターンとベスト プラクティスを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 워크플로우 오케스트레이션 아키텍처를 마스터할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 Temporal을 사용하여 다단계 프로세스, 분산 트랜잭션 및 장기간 실행되는 워크플로우를 포함하는 안정적인 분산 시스템을 구축하기 위한弹性 패턴 및 최선의 관행을 활용한다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a dominar la arquitectura de orquestación de flujos de trabajo, aprovechando patrones de resistencia y mejores prácticas para construir sistemas distribuidos confiables con procesos de múltiples pasos, transacciones distribuidas y flujos de trabajo de larga duración que utilizan Temporal","fr":"Permet aux agents de maîtriser l''architecture d''orchestration de workflow, en exploitant les modèles de résilience et les meilleures pratiques pour construire des systèmes distribués fiables avec des processus multétapes, des transactions distribuées et des flux de travail à long terme utilisant Temporal","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Workflow-Orchestrierungsarchitektur zu meistern, indem es Resilienzmuster und Best Practices für den Bau zuverlässiger verteilter Systeme mit mehrschrittigen Prozessen, verteilten Transaktionen und lang laufenden Workflows mit Temporal nutzt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a dominar a arquitetura de orquestração de fluxo de trabalho, aproveitando padrões de resiliência e melhores práticas para construir sistemas distribuídos confiáveis com processos multietapa, transações distribuídas e fluxos de trabalho de longa duração usando Temporal","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью освоить архитектуру оркестрации рабочих процессов, используя шаблоны устойчивости и лучшие практики для построения надежных распределенных систем с многоступенчатыми процессами, распределенными транзакциями и долгосрочными рабочими процессами с помощью Temporal","ar":"تمكين العميل من إتقان بنية تنسيق العملية، واستخدام أنماط من الصلابة وأفضل الممارسات لبناء أنظمة موزعة موثوقة مع عمليات متعددة المراحل، وعملية توزيعية وعمليات طويلة الأمد باستخدام Temporal"},"useCases":{"en":["Orchestrating multi-step processes across machines and services","Implementing all-or-nothing semantics for distributed transactions","Managing long-running workflows with automatic state management"],"zh":["跨机器和服务编排多步骤流程","为分布式事务实现全部或无效语义","管理具有自动状态管理的长时间运行工作流"],"ja":["マシンとサービスを跨ぐ多ステップ プロセスのオーケストレーション","分散トランザクションにすべてまたは何もなしのセマンティクスを実現する","自動状態管理を備えた長時間実行されるワークフローの管理"],"ko":["머신과 서비스를 건너서 다단계 프로세스 오케스트레이션","분산 트랜잭션에 모든 또는 아무 것도 없는 의미를 구현","자동 상태 관리를 갖춘 장기간 실행되는 워크플로우 관리"],"es":["Orquestar procesos de múltiples pasos en varias máquinas y