u halten und effektiv zu kollaborieren","pt":"Mestre técnicas avançadas de Git para manter um histórico limpo e colaborar de forma eficaz","ru":"Освойте расширенные техники Git, чтобы поддерживать чистую историю и сотрудничать эффективно","ar":"استخدم تقنيات جيت المتقدمة للحفاظ على تاريخ نظيف والتعاون بفعالية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["清理提交历史","在分支之间应用特定提交","查找引入 bug 的提交","同时处理多个功能","从 Git 错误或丢失提交中恢复","管理复杂的分支工作流"],"ja":["コミット履歴のクリーンアップ","ブランチ間で特定のコミットを適用","バグを導入したコミットの検索","複数の機能を同時に作業","Git のミスや失われたコミットからの復旧","複雑なブランチワークフローの管理"],"ko":["커밋 기록 정리","브랜치 간에 특정 커밋 적용","버그를 도입한 커밋 찾기","複数 기능을同時에 작업","Git 오류 또는 손실된 커밋에서 복구","복잡한 브랜치 워크플로 관리"],"es":["Limpieza del historial de commits","Aplicación de commits específicos en ramas","Búsqueda de commits que introdujeron errores","Trabajo en múltiples características simultáneamente","Recuperación de errores de Git o commits perdidos","Gestión de flujos de trabajo de ramas complejas"],"fr":["Nettoyage de l''historique des commits","Application de commits spécifiques sur des branches","Recherche de commits qui ont introduit des bogues","Travail sur plusieurs fonctionnalités simultanément","Récupération d''erreurs Git ou de commits perdus","Gestion de flux de travail de branches complexes"],"de":["Bereinigung des Commit-Historie","Anwendung spezifischer Commits auf Branches","Suche nach Commits, die Fehler eingeführt haben","Arbeit an mehreren Funktionen gleichzeitig","Wiederherstellung von Git-Fehlern oder verlorenen Commits","Verwaltung komplexer Branch-Workflows"],"pt":["Limpeza de histórico de commits","Aplicação de commits específicos em branches","Encontrar commits que introduziram bugs","Trabalho em múltiplos recursos simultaneamente","Recuperação de erros ou commits perdidos","Gerenciamento de fluxos de trabalho complexos"],"ru":["Очистка истории коммитов","Применение определенных коммитов к веткам","Поиск коммитов, которые ввели ошибки","Работа над несколькими функциями одновременно","Восстановление после ошибок или потерянных коммитов","Управление сложными рабочими процессами"],"ar":["تنظيف تاريخ التعليقات","تطبيق تعليقات محددة على الفروع","العثور على التعليقات التي أدخلت أخطاء","العمل على plusieurs ميزات في نفس الوقت","استعادة الأخطاء أو التعليقات المفقودة","إدارة سير العمل المعقدة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git 高级工作流","Git 提交历史","Git 协作","Git 恢复","Git 分支管理","Git 工作流优化"],"ja":["Git アドバンスドワークフロー","Git コミット履歴","Git コラボレーション","Git 復旧","Git ブランチ管理","Git ワークフローの最適化"],"ko":["Git 고급 워크플로","Git 커밋 기록","Git 협업","Git 복구","Git 브랜치 관리","Git 워크플로 최적화"],"es":["Git avanzado","flujos de trabajo de Git","historial de commits","colaboración en Git","recuperación de errores de Git","ramas de Git","commits de Git","control de versiones","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["Git avancé","workflows Git","historique des commits","collaboration Git","récupération d''erreurs Git","branches Git","commits Git","contrôle de version","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Erweitertes Git","Git-Workflows","Commit-Historie","Git-Kollaboration","Wiederherstellung von Git-Fehlern","Git-Branches","Git-Commits","Versionskontrolle","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["git avançado","fluxos de trabalho git","técnicas de git","histórico de commits","colaboração git","recuperação de erros git","gerenciamento de branches","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["расширенный git","рабочие процессы git","техники git","история коммитов","сотрудничество git","восстановление после ошибок git","управление ветками","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["جيت متقدم","سير عمل جيت","تقنيات جيت","تاريخ التعليقات","التعاون جيت","استعادة الأخطاء جيت","إدارة الفروع","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"orchestrator","repoPath":"ollieb89/orchestrator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.509Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"git-advanced-workflows","description":"Master advanced Git workflows including rebasing, cherry-picking, bisect, worktrees, and reflog to maintain clean history and recover from any situation. Use when managing complex Git histories, collaborating on feature branches, or troubleshooting repository issues.","bodyPreview":"# Git Advanced Workflows\n\nMaster advanced Git techniques to maintain clean history, collaborate effectively, and recover from any situation with confidence.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Cleaning up commit history before merging\n- Applying specific commits across branches\n- Finding commits that introduced bugs\n- Working on multiple features simultaneously\n- Recovering from Git mistakes or lost commits\n- Managing complex branch workflows\n- Preparing clean PRs for review\n- Synchronizing diverged b","body":"# Git Advanced Workflows\n\nMaster advanced Git techniques to maintain clean history, collaborate effectively, and recover from any situation with confidence.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Cleaning up commit history before merging\n- Applying specific commits across branches\n- Finding commits that introduced bugs\n- Working on multiple features simultaneously\n- Recovering from Git mistakes or lost commits\n- Managing complex branch workflows\n- Preparing clean PRs for review\n- Synchronizing diverged branches\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Interactive Rebase\n\nInteractive rebase is the Swiss Army knife of Git history editing.\n\n**Common Operations:**\n- `pick`: Keep commit as-is\n- `reword`: Change commit message\n- `edit`: Amend commit content\n- `squash`: Combine with previous commit\n- `fixup`: Like squash but discard message\n- `drop`: Remove commit entirely\n\n**Basic Usage:**\n```bash\n# Rebase last 5 commits\ngit rebase -i HEAD~5\n\n# Rebase all commits on current branch\ngit rebase -i $(git merge-base HEAD main)\n\n# Rebase onto specific commit\ngit rebase -i abc123\n```\n\n### 2. Cherry-Picking\n\nApply specific commits from one branch to another without merging entire branches.\n\n```bash\n# Cherry-pick single commit\ngit cherry-pick abc123\n\n# Cherry-pick range of commits (exclusive start)\ngit cherry-pick abc123..def456\n\n# Cherry-pick without committing (stage changes only)\ngit cherry-pick -n abc123\n\n# Cherry-pick and edit commit message\ngit cherry-pick -e abc123\n```\n\n### 3. Git Bisect\n\nBinary search through commit history to find the commit that introduced a bug.\n\n```bash\n# Start bisect\ngit bisect start\n\n# Mark current commit as bad\ngit bisect bad\n\n# Mark known good commit\ngit bisect good v1.0.0\n\n# Git will checkout middle commit - test it\n# Then mark as good or bad\ngit bisect good  # or: git bisect bad\n\n# Continue until bug found\n# When done\ngit bisect reset\n```\n\n**Automated Bisect:**\n```bash\n# Use script to test automatically\ngit bisect start HEAD v1.0.0\ngit bisect run ./test.sh\n\n# test.sh should exit 0 for good, 1-127 (except 125) for bad\n```\n\n### 4. Worktrees\n\nWork on multiple branches simultaneously without stashing or switching.\n\n```bash\n# List existing worktrees\ngit worktree list\n\n# Add new worktree for feature branch\ngit worktree add ../project-feature feature/new-feature\n\n# Add worktree and create new branch\ngit worktree add -b bugfix/urgent ../project-hotfix main\n\n# Remove worktree\ngit worktree remove ../project-feature\n\n# Prune stale worktrees\ngit worktree prune\n```\n\n### 5. Reflog\n\nYour safety net - tracks all ref movements, even deleted commits.\n\n```bash\n# View reflog\ngit reflog\n\n# View reflog for specific branch\ngit reflog show feature/branch\n\n# Restore deleted commit\ngit reflog\n# Find commit hash\ngit checkout abc123\ngit branch recovered-branch\n\n# Restore deleted branch\ngit reflog\ngit branch deleted-branch abc123\n```\n\n## Practical Workflows\n\n### Workflow 1: Clean Up Feature Branch Before PR\n\n```bash\n# Start with feature branch\ngit checkout feature/user-auth\n\n# Interactive rebase to clean history\ngit rebase -i main\n\n# Example rebase operations:\n# - Squash \"fix typo\" commits\n# - Reword commit messages for clarity\n# - Reorder commits logically\n# - Drop unnecessary commits\n\n# Force push cleaned branch (safe if no one else is using it)\ngit push --force-with-lease origin feature/user-auth\n```\n\n### Workflow 2: Apply Hotfix to Multiple Releases\n\n```bash\n# Create fix on main\ngit checkout main\ngit commit -m \"fix: critical security patch\"\n\n# Apply to release branches\ngit checkout release/2.0\ngit cherry-pick abc123\n\ngit checkout release/1.9\ngit cherry-pick abc123\n\n# Handle conflicts if they arise\ngit cherry-pick --continue\n# or\ngit cherry-pick --abort\n```\n\n### Workflow 3: Find Bug Introduction\n\n```bash\n# Start bisect\ngit bisect start\ngit bisect bad HEAD\ngit bisect good v2.1.0\n\n# Git checks out middle commit - run tests\nnpm test\n\n# If tests fail\ngit bisect bad\n\n# If tests pass\ngit bisect good\n\n# Git will automatically checkout next commit to test\n# Repeat until bug found\n\n# Automated version\ngit bisect start HEAD v2.1.0\ngit bisect run npm test\n```\n\n### Workflow 4: Multi-Branch Development\n\n```bash\n# Main project directory\ncd ~/projects/myapp\n\n# Create worktree for urgent bugfix\ngit worktree add ../myapp-hotfix hotfix/critical-bug\n\n# Work on hotfix in separate directory\ncd ../myapp-hotfix\n# Make changes, commit\ngit commit -m \"fix: resolve critical bug\"\ngit push origin hotfix/critical-bug\n\n# Return to main work without interruption\ncd ~/projects/myapp\ngit fetch origin\ngit cherry-pick hotfix/critical-bug\n\n# Clean up when done\ngit worktree remove ../myapp-hotfix\n```\n\n### Workflow 5: Recover from Mistakes\n\n```bash\n# Accidentally reset to wrong commit\ngit reset --hard HEAD~5  # Oh no!\n\n# Use reflog to find lost commits\ngit reflog\n# Output shows:\n# abc123 HEAD@{0}: reset: moving to HEAD~5\n# def456 HEAD@{1}: commit: my important changes\n\n# Recover lost commits\ngit reset --hard def456\n\n# Or create branch from lost commit\ngit branch recovery def456\n```\n\n## Advanced Techniques\n\n### Rebase vs Merge Strategy\n\n**When to Rebase:**\n- Cleaning up local commits before pushing\n- Keeping feature branch up-to-date with main\n- Creating linear history for easier review\n\n**When to Merge:**\n- Integrating completed features into main\n- Preserving exact history of collaboration\n- Public branches used by others\n\n```bash\n# Update feature branch with main changes (rebase)\ngit checkout feature/my-feature\ngit fetch origin\ngit rebase origin/main\n\n# Handle conflicts\ngit status\n# Fix conflicts in files\ngit add .\ngit rebase --continue\n\n# Or merge instead\ngit merge origin/main\n```\n\n### Autosquash Workflow\n\nAutomatically squash fixup commits during rebase.\n\n```bash\n# Make initial commit\ngit commit -m \"feat: add user authentication\"\n\n# Later, fix something in that commit\n# Stage changes\ngit commit --fixup HEAD  # or specify commit hash\n\n# Make more changes\ngit commit --fixup abc123\n\n# Rebase with autosquash\ngit rebase -i --autosquash main\n\n# Git automatically marks fixup commits\n```\n\n### Split Commit\n\nBreak one commit into multiple logical commits.\n\n```bash\n# Start interactive rebase\ngit rebase -i HEAD~3\n\n# Mark commit to split with ''edit''\n# Git will stop at that commit\n\n# Reset commit but keep changes\ngit reset HEAD^\n\n# Stage and commit in logical chunks\ngit add file1.py\ngit commit -m \"feat: add validation\"\n\ngit add file2.py\ngit commit -m \"feat: add error handling\"\n\n# Continue rebase\ngit rebase --continue\n```\n\n### Partial Cherry-Pick\n\nCherry-pick only specific files from a commit.\n\n```bash\n# Show files in commit\ngit show --name-only abc123\n\n# Checkout specific files from commit\ngit checkout abc123 -- path/to/file1.py path/to/file2.py\n\n# Stage and commit\ngit commit -m \"cherry-pick: apply specific changes from abc123\"\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Always Use --force-with-lease**: Safer than --force, prevents overwriting others'' work\n2. **Rebase Only Local Commits**: Don''t rebase commits that have been pushed and shared\n3. **Descriptive Commit Messages**: Future you will thank present you\n4. **Atomic Commits**: Each commit should be a single logical change\n5. **Test Before Force Push**: Ensure history rewrite didn''t break anything\n6. **Keep Reflog Aware**: Remember reflog is your safety net for 90 days\n7. **Branch Before Risky Operations**: Create backup branch before complex rebases\n\n```bash\n# Safe force push\ngit push --force-with-lease origin feature/branch\n\n# Create backup before risky operation\ngit branch backup-branch\ngit rebase -i main\n# If something goes wrong\ngit reset --hard backup-branch\n```\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Rebasing Public Branches**: Causes history conflicts for collaborators\n- **Force Pushing Without Lease**: Can overwrite teammate''s work\n- **Losing Work in Rebase**: Resolve conflicts carefully, test after rebase\n- **Forgetting Worktree Cleanup**: Orphaned worktrees consume disk space\n- **Not Backing Up Before Experiment**: Always create safety branch\n- **Bisect on Dirty Working Directory**: Commit or stash before bisecting\n\n## Recovery Commands\n\n```bash\n# Abort operations in progress\ngit rebase --abort\ngit merge --abort\ngit cherry-pick --abort\ngit bisect reset\n\n# Restore file to version from specific commit\ngit restore --source=abc123 path/to/file\n\n# Undo last commit but keep changes\ngit reset --soft HEAD^\n\n# Undo last commit and discard changes\ngit reset --hard HEAD^\n\n# Recover deleted branch (within 90 days)\ngit reflog\ngit branch recovered-branch abc123\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/git-rebase-guide.md**: Deep dive into interactive rebase\n- **references/git-conflict-resolution.md**: Advanced conflict resolution strategies\n- **references/git-history-rewriting.md**: Safely rewriting Git history\n- **assets/git-workflow-checklist.md**: Pre-PR cleanup checklist\n- **assets/git-aliases.md**: Useful Git aliases for advanced workflows\n- **scripts/git-clean-branches.sh**: Clean up merged and stale branches\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:23:07.943Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Version Control Agents needing advanced Git workflow management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 Git 工作流管理功能的版本控制代理。","ja":"バージョン管理エージェントが高度な Git ワークフロー管理機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 Git 작업 흐름 관리 기능이 필요한 버전 제어 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de control de versiones que necesitan capacidades de gestión de flujo de trabajo de Git avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de contrôle de version ayant besoin de fonctionnalités de gestion de workflow Git avancées.","de":"Perfekt für Version Control Agents, die erweiterte Git-Workflow-Managementfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Controle de Versão que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho do Git.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов контроля версий, требующих расширенных возможностей управления рабочим процессом Git.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراقبة الإصدار الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات إدارة عملية العمل المتقدمة لـ Git."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to maintain clean commit history, collaborate effectively across branches, and recover from Git mistakes using techniques like cherry-picking and rebasing, all while managing complex branch workflows and preparing clean PRs for review.","zh":"赋予代理维护干净的提交历史、有效地跨分支协作以及使用 cherry-picking 和 rebasing 等技术从 Git 错误中恢复的能力，同时管理复杂的分支工作流并为审查准备干净的 PR。","ja":"エージェントがクリーンのコミット履歴を維持し、ブランチ間で効果的に協力し、cherry-picking や rebasing などのテクニックを使用して Git のミスから回復する能力を与え、複雑なブランチワークフローを管理し、レビューのためのクリーンな PR を準備します。","ko":"에이전트가 깨끗한 커밋 기록을 유지하고, 브랜치 간에 효과적으로 협력하며, 체리 픽킹 및 리베이스와 같은 기술을 사용하여 Git 오류에서 복구하는 기능을 부여하며, 복잡한 브랜치 작업 흐름을 관리하고, 검토를 위한 깨끗한 PR을 준비합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mantener un historial de confirmaciones limpio, colaborar de manera efectiva en diferentes ramas y recuperarse de errores de Git utilizando técnicas como cherry-picking y rebasing, todo mientras se gestionan flujos de trabajo de ramas complejas y se preparan solicitudes de revisión limpias.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maintenir un historique de validation propre, de collaborer efficacement à travers les branches et de se remettre des erreurs Git en utilisant des techniques comme le cherry-picking et le rebasing, le tout en gérant des flux de travail de branches complexes et en préparant des demandes de révision propres.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, ein sauberes Commit-Verlauf zu erhalten, effektiv über Branches hinweg zu kollaborieren und sich von Git-Fehlern zu erholen, indem Techniken wie Cherry-Picking und Rebasen verwendet werden, während komplexe Branch-Workflows verwaltet und saubere Pull-Requests für die Überprüfung vorbereitet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a manter um histórico de commits limpo, colaborar de forma eficaz entre branches e se recuperar de erros do Git usando técnicas como cherry-picking e rebasing, tudo enquanto gerencia fluxos de trabalho de branch complexos e prepara PRs limpas para revisão.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью поддерживать чистую историю коммитов, эффективно сотрудничать между ветками и восстанавливаться после ошибок Git с помощью техник, таких как cherry-picking и rebasing, при этом управляя сложными рабочими процессами веток и подготовкой чистых запросов на просмотр.","ar":"يتمكّن الوكيل من الحفاظ على سجل تعديلات نظيف، والتعاون بفعالية عبر الفروع، واستعادة البيانات من أخطاء جيت باستخدام تقنيات مثل cherry-picking و rebasing، مع إدارة سلاسل عمل الفروع المعقدة وإعداد طلبات المراجعة النظيفة."},"useCases":{"en":["Cleaning up commit history before merging","Applying specific commits across branches using cherry-pick","Recovering from Git mistakes or lost commits using reflog and reset"],"zh":["合并前清理提交历史","使用 cherry-pick 将特定提交应用于分支","使用 reflog 和 reset 从 Git 错误或丢失提交中恢复"],"ja":["マージ前のコミット履歴のクリーンアップ","cherry-pick を使用して特定のコミットをブランチに適用","reflog と reset を使用して Git のミスまたは失われたコミットから回復"],"ko":["병합 전 커밋 기록을 정리하는こと","체리 픽킹을 사용하여 특정 커밋을 브랜치에 적용하는 것","리플로그 및 리셋을 사용하여 Git 오류 또는 손실된 커밋에서 복구하는 것"],"es":["Limpiar el historial de confirmaciones antes de fusionar","Aplicar confirmaciones específicas en diferentes ramas usando cherry-pick","Recuperarse de errores de Git o confirmaciones perdidas usando reflog y reset"],"fr":["Nettoyer l''historique des validations avant de fusionner","Appliquer des validations spécifiques à travers les branches en utilisant cherry-pick","Se remettre des erreurs Git ou des validations perdues en utilisant reflog et reset"],"de":["Commit-Verlauf vor dem Zusammenführen bereinigen","Spezifische Commits über Branches hinweg mit Cherry-Picking anwenden","Sich von Git-Fehlern oder verlorenen Commits mithilfe von Reflog und Reset erholen"],"pt":["Limpar o histórico de commits antes de mesclar","Aplicar commits específicos em branches usando cherry-pick","Recuperar de erros do Git ou commits perdidos usando reflog e reset"],"ru":["Очистка истории коммитов перед слиянием","Применение определенных коммитов к веткам с помощью cherry-pick","Восстановление после ошибок Git или потерянных коммитов с помощью reflog и reset"],"ar":["تنظيف سجل التعديلات قبل الدمج","تطبيق التعديلات المحددة عبر الفروع باستخدام cherry-pick","استعادة البيانات من أخطاء جيت أو التعديلات المفقودة باستخدام reflog و reset"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation and configuration","Limited to Git version control system"],"zh":["需要 Git 安装和配置","仅限 Git 版本控制系统"],"ja":["Git のインストールと設定が必要","Git バージョン管理システムのみに限定"],"ko":["Git 설치 및 구성이 필요함","Git 버전 관리 시스템에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la instalación y configuración de Git","Limitado al sistema de control de versiones Git"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de Git","Limité au système de contrôle de version Git"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation und Konfiguration von Git","Begrenzt auf das Git-Versionierungssystem"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do Git","Limitado ao sistema de controle de versão Git"],"ru":["Требует установки и настройки Git","Ограничен системой контроля версий Git"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت جيت وتفصيله","محدود بنظام مراقبة الإصدار جيت"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('yashness/yash-full-stack-personal/runtime', 'community', 'yashness', 'yash-full-stack-personal', 'yashness/yash-full-stack-personal', 'runtime', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.509Z', '2026-02-18T12:23:39.781Z', NULL, '{"id":"yashness/yash-full-stack-personal/runtime","name":"runtime","description":{"zh":"Runtime是一种技术概念，指程序运行时的环境和资源。它包括local runtime和external store runtime等技术","ja":"ランタイムは、プログラムの実行時における環境とリソースを指します","ko":"런타임은 프로그램의 실행 시 환경과 리소스를 말합니다","es":"El runtime es un componente crucial para la ejecución de código. Aprende a utilizarlo de manera efectiva para mejorar el rendimiento de tu aplicación.","fr":"Le runtime est un composant essentiel pour l''exécution du code. Apprenez à l''utiliser de manière efficace pour améliorer les performances de votre application.","de":"Das Runtime ist ein wichtiger Bestandteil für die Ausführung von Code. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie es effektiv nutzen, um die Leistung Ihrer Anwendung zu verbessern.","pt":"O runtime refere-se ao tempo de execução de um programa ou aplicativo. Ele é crucial para otimizar o desempenho e melhorar a experiência do usuário.","ru":"Runtime относится к времени выполнения программы или приложения. Он имеет решающее значение для оптимизации производительности и улучшения пользовательского опыта.","ar":"Runtime يشير إلى وقت تشغيل برنامج أو تطبيق. وهو أمر بالغ الأهمية لتحسين الأداء وتحسين تجربة المستخدم.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Runtime 技术概述","ja":"ランタイムの概要","ko":"런타임 기술","es":"Runtime: Optimiza tu código en tiempo de ejecución","fr":"Runtime : Optimisez votre code à l''exécution","de":"Runtime: Optimieren Sie Ihren Code zur Laufzeit","pt":"Runtime: Otimização de Desempenho em Tempo de Execução","ru":"Runtime: Оптимизация Производительности Время Выполнения","ar":"Runtime: تحسين أداء وقت التشغيل","en":"runtime"},"description":{"zh":"Runtime是一种技术概念，指程序运行时的环境和资源。它包括local runtime和external store runtime等技术","ja":"ランタイムは、プログラムの実行時における環境とリソースを指します","ko":"런타임은 프로그램의 실행 시 환경과 리소스를 말합니다","es":"El runtime es un componente crucial para la ejecución de código. Aprende a utilizarlo de manera efectiva para mejorar el rendimiento de tu aplicación.","fr":"Le runtime est un composant essentiel pour l''exécution du code. Apprenez à l''utiliser de manière efficace pour améliorer les performances de votre application.","de":"Das Runtime ist ein wichtiger Bestandteil für die Ausführung von Code. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie es effektiv nutzen, um die Leistung Ihrer Anwendung zu verbessern.","pt":"O runtime refere-se ao tempo de execução de um programa ou aplicativo. Ele é crucial para otimizar o desempenho e melhorar a experiência do usuário.","ru":"Runtime относится к времени выполнения программы или приложения. Он имеет решающее значение для оптимизации производительности и улучшения пользовательского ...","ar":"Runtime يشير إلى وقت تشغيل برنامج أو تطبيق. وهو أمر بالغ الأهمية لتحسين الأداء وتحسين تجربة المستخدم.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["local runtime","external store runtime","线程列表管理","状态钩子访问"],"ja":["ローカルランタイム","外部ストアランタイム","スレッドリスト管理","ステートフックアクセス"],"ko":["로컬 런타임","외부 스토어 런타임","스레드 목록 관리","상태 훅 접근"],"es":["Acceso a la documentación oficial de assistant-ui","Uso de useLocalRuntime para un rendimiento óptimo","Gestión de threads con thread-list","Acceso a estado con state-hooks","Uso de useExternalStore para el almacenamiento externo"],"fr":["Accès à la documentation officielle d''assistant-ui","Utilisation de useLocalRuntime pour un rendement optimal","Gestion des threads avec thread-list","Accès à l''état avec state-hooks","Utilisation de useExternalStore pour le stockage externe"],"de":["Zugriff auf die offizielle Dokumentation von assistant-ui","Verwendung von useLocalRuntime für optimale Leistung","Thread-Verwaltung mit thread-list","Zugriff auf Zustand mit state-hooks","Verwendung von useExternalStore für externen Speicher"],"pt":["Otimização de desempenho em tempo de execução","Gerenciamento de threads","Acesso a estado","Loja externa","Execução local"],"ru":["Оптимизация производительности в время выполнения","Управление потоками","Доступ к состоянию","Внешний магазин","Местное выполнение"],"ar":["تحسين أداء وقت التشغيل","إدارة الخيوط","وصول إلى الحالة","متجر خارجي","تشغيل محلي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Runtime","local runtime","external store runtime","线程列表管理","状态钩子访问","技术概念"],"ja":["ランタイム","ローカルランタイム","外部ストアランタイム","スレッドリスト管理","ステートフックアクセス","技術概念"],"ko":["런타임","로컬 런타임","외부 스토어 런타임","스레드 목록 관리","상태 훅 접근","기술 개념"],"es":["runtime","optimización de código","rendimiento de aplicaciones","assistant-ui","useLocalRuntime","thread-list","state-hooks","useExternalStore"],"fr":["runtime","optimisation de code","performances des applications","assistant-ui","useLocalRuntime","thread-list","state-hooks","useExternalStore"],"de":["runtime","code-optimierung","anwendungsleistung","assistant-ui","useLocalRuntime","thread-list","state-hooks","useExternalStore"],"pt":["runtime","otimização de desempenho","tempo de execução","gerenciamento de threads","acesso a estado","loja externa","execução local"],"ru":["runtime","оптимизация производительности","время выполнения","управление потоками","доступ к состоянию","внешний магазин","местное выполнение"],"ar":["runtime","تحسين أداء","وقت تشغيل","إدارة الخيوط","وصول إلى الحالة","متجر خارجي","تشغيل محلي"]}},"owner":"yashness","repo":"yash-full-stack-personal","repoPath":"yashness/yash-full-stack-personal","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.509Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"runtime","description":"Guide for assistant-ui runtime system and state management. Use when working with runtimes, accessing state, or managing thread/message data.","version":"0.0.1","bodyPreview":"# assistant-ui Runtime\n\n**Always consult [assistant-ui.com/llms.txt](https://assistant-ui.com/llms.txt) for latest API.**\n\n## References\n\n- [./references/local-runtime.md](./references/local-runtime.md) -- useLocalRuntime deep dive\n- [./references/external-store.md](./references/external-store.md) -- useExternalStoreRuntime deep dive\n- [./references/thread-list.md](./references/thread-list.md) -- Thread list management\n- [./references/state-hooks.md](./references/state-hooks.md) -- State access","body":"# assistant-ui Runtime\n\n**Always consult [assistant-ui.com/llms.txt](https://assistant-ui.com/llms.txt) for latest API.**\n\n## References\n\n- [./references/local-runtime.md](./references/local-runtime.md) -- useLocalRuntime deep dive\n- [./references/external-store.md](./references/external-store.md) -- useExternalStoreRuntime deep dive\n- [./references/thread-list.md](./references/thread-list.md) -- Thread list management\n- [./references/state-hooks.md](./references/state-hooks.md) -- State access hooks\n- [./references/types.md](./references/types.md) -- Type definitions\n\n## Runtime Hierarchy\n\n```\nAssistantRuntime\n├── ThreadListRuntime (thread management)\n│   ├── ThreadListItemRuntime (per-thread item)\n│   └── ...\n└── ThreadRuntime (current thread)\n    ├── ComposerRuntime (input state)\n    └── MessageRuntime[] (per-message)\n        └── MessagePartRuntime[] (per-content-part)\n```\n\n## State Access (Modern API)\n\n```tsx\nimport { useAssistantApi, useAssistantState, useAssistantEvent } from \"@assistant-ui/react\";\n\nfunction ChatControls() {\n  const api = useAssistantApi();\n  const messages = useAssistantState(s => s.thread.messages);\n  const isRunning = useAssistantState(s => s.thread.isRunning);\n\n  useAssistantEvent(\"message-added\", (e) => {\n    console.log(\"New message:\", e.message);\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={() => api.thread().append({\n        role: \"user\",\n        content: [{ type: \"text\", text: \"Hello!\" }],\n      })}>\n        Send\n      </button>\n      {isRunning && (\n        <button onClick={() => api.thread().cancelRun()}>Cancel</button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Thread Operations\n\n```tsx\nconst api = useAssistantApi();\nconst thread = api.thread();\n\n// Append message\nthread.append({ role: \"user\", content: [{ type: \"text\", text: \"Hello\" }] });\n\n// Cancel generation\nthread.cancelRun();\n\n// Get current state\nconst state = thread.getState();  // { messages, isRunning, ... }\n```\n\n## Message Operations\n\n```tsx\nconst message = api.thread().message(0);  // By index\n\nmessage.edit({ role: \"user\", content: [{ type: \"text\", text: \"Updated\" }] });\nmessage.reload();\n```\n\n## Events\n\n```tsx\nuseAssistantEvent(\"thread-started\", () => {});\nuseAssistantEvent(\"thread-ended\", () => {});\nuseAssistantEvent(\"message-added\", ({ message }) => {});\nuseAssistantEvent(\"run-started\", () => {});\nuseAssistantEvent(\"run-ended\", () => {});\n```\n\n## Capabilities\n\n```tsx\nconst caps = useAssistantState(s => s.thread.capabilities);\n// { cancel, edit, reload, copy, speak, attachments }\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n```tsx\n// Get messages\nconst messages = useAssistantState(s => s.thread.messages);\n\n// Check running state\nconst isRunning = useAssistantState(s => s.thread.isRunning);\n\n// Append message\napi.thread().append({ role: \"user\", content: [{ type: \"text\", text: \"Hi\" }] });\n\n// Cancel generation\napi.thread().cancelRun();\n\n// Edit message\napi.thread().message(index).edit({ ... });\n\n// Reload message\napi.thread().message(index).reload();\n```\n\n## Common Gotchas\n\n**\"Cannot read property of undefined\"**\n- Ensure hooks are called inside `AssistantRuntimeProvider`\n\n**State not updating**\n- Use selectors with `useAssistantState` to prevent unnecessary re-renders\n\n**Messages array empty**\n- Check runtime is configured\n- Verify API response format\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:23:39.781Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents requiring seamless integration with local and external runtime environments.","zh":"适用于需要与本地和外部运行时环境无缝集成的高级AI代理。","ja":"ローカルおよび外部ランタイム環境とのシームレスな統合を必要とする高度なAIエージェントに適しています。","ko":"로컬 및 외부 런타임 환경과 무결점 통합을 요구하는 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avanzados que requieren una integración perfecta con entornos de tiempo de ejecución locales y externos.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents IA Avancés nécessitant une intégration transparente avec les environnements d''exécution locaux et externes.","de":"Ideal für erweiterte KI-Agenten, die eine nahtlose Integration mit lokalen und externen Laufzeitumgebungen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados que requerem integração perfeita com ambientes de tempo de execução local e externo.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, требующих бесшовной интеграции с локальными и внешними средами выполнения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدم الذي يتطلب تكاملًا بدون مشاكل مع بيئات تشغيل الوقت المحلية والخارجية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage useLocalRuntime and useExternalStoreRuntime for efficient thread list management and state access, utilizing APIs outlined in assistant-ui.com/llms.txt for optimized performance.","zh":"使代理能够利用useLocalRuntime和useExternalStoreRuntime实现高效的线程列表管理和状态访问，利用assistant-ui.com/llms.txt中概述的API实现优化的性能。","ja":"エージェントがuseLocalRuntimeとuseExternalStoreRuntimeを利用して効率的なスレッドリスト管理と状態アクセスを行えるようにし、assistant-ui.com/llms.txtに概説されているAPIを使用して最適化されたパフォーマンスを実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 useLocalRuntime과 useExternalStoreRuntime을 사용하여 효율적인 스레드 목록 관리 및 상태 접근을 가능하게 하며, assistant-ui.com/llms.txt에 요약된 API를 사용하여 최적화된 성능을 구현할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar useLocalRuntime y useExternalStoreRuntime para una gestión eficiente de listas de hilos y acceso a estados, utilizando las API descritas en assistant-ui.com/llms.txt para un rendimiento optimizado.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser useLocalRuntime et useExternalStoreRuntime pour une gestion efficace des listes de threads et l''accès à l''état, en utilisant les API décrites dans assistant-ui.com/llms.txt pour des performances optimales.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, useLocalRuntime und useExternalStoreRuntime für eine effiziente Threadlistenverwaltung und Zustandszugriff zu nutzen, wobei die in assistant-ui.com/llms.txt beschriebenen APIs für optimale Leistung verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a utilizar useLocalRuntime e useExternalStoreRuntime para gerenciamento eficiente de listas de threads e acesso a estado, utilizando APIs descritas em assistant-ui.com/llms.txt para desempenho otimizado.","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность использовать useLocalRuntime и useExternalStoreRuntime для эффективного управления списками потоков и доступа к состоянию, используя API, описанные в assistant-ui.com/llms.txt, для оптимизированной производительности.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من استخدام useLocalRuntime و useExternalStoreRuntime لإدارة فعالة لقوائم الخيوط ووصول إلى الحالة، باستخدام واجهات برمجة التطبيقات المحددة في assistant-ui.com/llms.txt من أجل أداء أمثل."},"useCases":{"en":["Managing thread lists for concurrent task execution","Accessing state hooks for real-time data updates","Integrating external stores for enhanced runtime capabilities"],"zh":["管理线程列表以执行并发任务","访问状态钩子以获取实时数据更新","集成外部存储以增强运行时功能"],"ja":["並行タスクの実行のためのスレッドリストの管理","リアルタイムデータ更新のための状態フックスのアクセス","ランタイム機能の強化のための外部ストアの統合"],"ko":["병렬 작업을 위한 스레드 목록 관리","실시간 데이터 업데이트 위한 상태 훅 접근","실행 시간 기능 강화 위한 외부 저장소 통합"],"es":["Gestión de listas de hilos para la ejecución de tareas concurrentes","Acceso a ganchos de estado para actualizaciones de datos en tiempo real","Integración de tiendas externas para capacidades de tiempo de ejecución mejoradas"],"fr":["Gestion des listes de threads pour l''exécution de tâches concurrentes","Accès aux crochets d''état pour des mises à jour de données en temps réel","Intégration de magasins externes pour des capacités de temps d''exécution améliorées"],"de":["Verwaltung von Threadlisten für die Ausführung von konkurrierenden Aufgaben","Zugriff auf Zustandshooks für Echtzeit-Datenaktualisierungen","Integration externer Speicher für erweiterte Laufzeitfähigkeiten"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de listas de threads para execução de tarefas concorrentes","Acesso a ganchos de estado para atualizações de dados em tempo real","Integração de lojas externas para capacidades de tempo de execução aprimoradas"],"ru":["Управление списками потоков для параллельного выполнения задач","Доступ к крючкам состояния для обновления данных в реальном времени","Интеграция внешних магазинов для расширенных возможностей среды выполнения"],"ar":["إدارة قوائم الخيوط للتشغيل المتزامن للمهام","وصول إلى مشابك الحالة لتحديثات البيانات في الوقت الفعلي","دمج مخازن خارجية لقدرات تشغيل محسنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires consultation of assistant-ui.com/llms.txt for latest API","Dependent on specific runtime environment configurations"],"zh":["需要查阅assistant-ui.com/llms.txt以获取最新的API","依赖于特定的运行时环境配置"],"ja":["最新のAPIを取得するためにassistant-ui.com/llms.txtを参照する必要がある","特定のランタイム環境構成に依存する"],"ko":["최신 API를 얻기 위해 assistant-ui.com/llms.txt를 참조해야 함","특정 런타임 환경 구성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere la consulta de assistant-ui.com/llms.txt para la última API","Depende de configuraciones de entorno de tiempo de ejecución específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite la consultation de assistant-ui.com/llms.txt pour la dernière API","Dépend de configurations d''environnement d''exécution spécifiques"],"de":["Erfordert die Konsultation von assistant-ui.com/llms.txt für die neueste API","Hängt von spezifischen Laufzeitumgebungs-Konfigurationen ab"],"pt":["Requer consulta do assistant-ui.com/llms.txt para a API mais recente","Dependente de configurações específicas do ambiente de tempo de execução"],"ru":["Требует консультации assistant-ui.com/llms.txt для получения последней версии API","Зависит от конкретных конфигураций среды выполнения"],"ar":["يتطلب استشارة assistant-ui.com/llms.txt من أجل الحصول على أحدث واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","يعتمد على تكوينات محددة لبيئة التشغيل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ollieb89/orchestrator/python-packaging', 'community', 'ollieb89', 'orchestrator', 'ollieb89/orchestrator', 'python-packaging', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.509Z', '2026-02-18T12:23:11.889Z', NULL, '{"id":"ollieb89/orchestrator/python-packaging","name":"python-packaging","description":{"zh":"Python, pyproject.toml PyPI.","ja":"Pythonpyproject.tomlPyPI.","ko":"Python pyproject.toml PyPI.","es":"Guía completa para crear y distribuir paquetes Python con pyproject.toml y publicar en PyPI","fr":"Guide complet pour créer et distribuer des paquets Python avec pyproject.toml et publier sur PyPI","de":"Umfassendes Handbuch zur Erstellung und Verteilung von Python-Paketen mit pyproject.toml und Veröffentlichung auf PyPI","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Python ","ja":"Python","ko":"Python ","es":"Empaquetado de Python: Guía Completa","fr":"Emballage Python: Guide Complet","de":"Python-Verpackung: Umfassendes Handbuch","en":"python-packaging"},"description":{"zh":"Python, pyproject.toml PyPI.","ja":"Pythonpyproject.tomlPyPI.","ko":"Python pyproject.toml PyPI.","es":"Guía completa para crear y distribuir paquetes Python con pyproject.toml y publicar en PyPI","fr":"Guide complet pour créer et distribuer des paquets Python avec pyproject.toml et publier sur PyPI","de":"Umfassendes Handbuch zur Erstellung und Verteilung von Python-Paketen mit pyproject.toml und Veröffentlichung auf PyPI","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Python","pyproject.toml","PyPI","Python","Python","wheel"],"ja":["Python","pyproject.toml","PyPI","Python","Python","wheel"],"ko":["Python ","pyproject.toml","PyPI","Python ","Python ","wheel"],"es":["Creación de paquetes Python","Estructuración de proyectos Python","Publicación en PyPI","Creación de paquetes instalables con dependencias","Construcción de wheels y distribuciones de fuente"],"fr":["Création de paquets Python","Structuration de projets Python","Publication sur PyPI","Création de paquets installables avec des dépendances","Construction de wheels et de distributions de source"],"de":["Erstellung von Python-Paketen","Strukturierung von Python-Projekten","Veröffentlichung auf PyPI","Erstellung von installierbaren Paketen mit Abhängigkeiten","Erstellung von Wheels und Quellcode-Verteilungen"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Python","pyproject.toml","PyPI","Python","Python","wheel","Python","Python"],"ja":["Python","pyproject.toml","PyPI","Python","Python","wheel","Python","Python"],"ko":["Python ","pyproject.toml","PyPI","Python ","Python ","wheel","Python ","Python "],"es":["empaquetado de python","pyproject.toml","paquetes python","pypi","desarrollo de software python","herramientas de empaquetado python"],"fr":["emballage python","pyproject.toml","paquets python","pypi","développement de logiciel python","outils d''emballage python"],"de":["python-verpackung","pyproject.toml","python-pakete","pypi","software-entwicklung python","verpackungstools python"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"orchestrator","repoPath":"ollieb89/orchestrator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.509Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-packaging","description":"Create distributable Python packages with proper project structure, setup.py/pyproject.toml, and publishing to PyPI. Use when packaging Python libraries, creating CLI tools, or distributing Python code.","bodyPreview":"# Python Packaging\n\nComprehensive guide to creating, structuring, and distributing Python packages using modern packaging tools, pyproject.toml, and publishing to PyPI.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Creating Python libraries for distribution\n- Building command-line tools with entry points\n- Publishing packages to PyPI or private repositories\n- Setting up Python project structure\n- Creating installable packages with dependencies\n- Building wheels and source distributions\n- Versioning and releasin","body":"# Python Packaging\n\nComprehensive guide to creating, structuring, and distributing Python packages using modern packaging tools, pyproject.toml, and publishing to PyPI.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Creating Python libraries for distribution\n- Building command-line tools with entry points\n- Publishing packages to PyPI or private repositories\n- Setting up Python project structure\n- Creating installable packages with dependencies\n- Building wheels and source distributions\n- Versioning and releasing Python packages\n- Creating namespace packages\n- Implementing package metadata and classifiers\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Package Structure\n- **Source layout**: `src/package_name/` (recommended)\n- **Flat layout**: `package_name/` (simpler but less flexible)\n- **Package metadata**: pyproject.toml, setup.py, or setup.cfg\n- **Distribution formats**: wheel (.whl) and source distribution (.tar.gz)\n\n### 2. Modern Packaging Standards\n- **PEP 517/518**: Build system requirements\n- **PEP 621**: Metadata in pyproject.toml\n- **PEP 660**: Editable installs\n- **pyproject.toml**: Single source of configuration\n\n### 3. Build Backends\n- **setuptools**: Traditional, widely used\n- **hatchling**: Modern, opinionated\n- **flit**: Lightweight, for pure Python\n- **poetry**: Dependency management + packaging\n\n### 4. Distribution\n- **PyPI**: Python Package Index (public)\n- **TestPyPI**: Testing before production\n- **Private repositories**: JFrog, AWS CodeArtifact, etc.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Minimal Package Structure\n\n```\nmy-package/\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── README.md\n├── LICENSE\n├── src/\n│   └── my_package/\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       └── module.py\n└── tests/\n    └── test_module.py\n```\n\n### Minimal pyproject.toml\n\n```toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"my-package\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A short description\"\nauthors = [{name = \"Your Name\", email = \"you@example.com\"}]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\ndependencies = [\n    \"requests>=2.28.0\",\n]\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\n    \"pytest>=7.0\",\n    \"black>=22.0\",\n]\n```\n\n## Package Structure Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Source Layout (Recommended)\n\n```\nmy-package/\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── README.md\n├── LICENSE\n├── .gitignore\n├── src/\n│   └── my_package/\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── core.py\n│       ├── utils.py\n│       └── py.typed          # For type hints\n├── tests/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── test_core.py\n│   └── test_utils.py\n└── docs/\n    └── index.md\n```\n\n**Advantages:**\n- Prevents accidentally importing from source\n- Cleaner test imports\n- Better isolation\n\n**pyproject.toml for source layout:**\n```toml\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Flat Layout\n\n```\nmy-package/\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── README.md\n├── my_package/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   └── module.py\n└── tests/\n    └── test_module.py\n```\n\n**Simpler but:**\n- Can import package without installing\n- Less professional for libraries\n\n### Pattern 3: Multi-Package Project\n\n```\nproject/\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── packages/\n│   ├── package-a/\n│   │   └── src/\n│   │       └── package_a/\n│   └── package-b/\n│       └── src/\n│           └── package_b/\n└── tests/\n```\n\n## Complete pyproject.toml Examples\n\n### Pattern 4: Full-Featured pyproject.toml\n\n```toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\", \"wheel\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"my-awesome-package\"\nversion = \"1.0.0\"\ndescription = \"An awesome Python package\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nlicense = {text = \"MIT\"}\nauthors = [\n    {name = \"Your Name\", email = \"you@example.com\"},\n]\nmaintainers = [\n    {name = \"Maintainer Name\", email = \"maintainer@example.com\"},\n]\nkeywords = [\"example\", \"package\", \"awesome\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Development Status :: 4 - Beta\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.8\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.9\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12\",\n]\n\ndependencies = [\n    \"requests>=2.28.0,<3.0.0\",\n    \"click>=8.0.0\",\n    \"pydantic>=2.0.0\",\n]\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\n    \"pytest>=7.0.0\",\n    \"pytest-cov>=4.0.0\",\n    \"black>=23.0.0\",\n    \"ruff>=0.1.0\",\n    \"mypy>=1.0.0\",\n]\ndocs = [\n    \"sphinx>=5.0.0\",\n    \"sphinx-rtd-theme>=1.0.0\",\n]\nall = [\n    \"my-awesome-package[dev,docs]\",\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/username/my-awesome-package\"\nDocumentation = \"https://my-awesome-package.readthedocs.io\"\nRepository = \"https://github.com/username/my-awesome-package\"\n\"Bug Tracker\" = \"https://github.com/username/my-awesome-package/issues\"\nChangelog = \"https://github.com/username/my-awesome-package/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\"\n\n[project.scripts]\nmy-cli = \"my_package.cli:main\"\nawesome-tool = \"my_package.tools:run\"\n\n[project.entry-points.\"my_package.plugins\"]\nplugin1 = \"my_package.plugins:plugin1\"\n\n[tool.setuptools]\npackage-dir = {\"\" = \"src\"}\nzip-safe = false\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\ninclude = [\"my_package*\"]\nexclude = [\"tests*\"]\n\n[tool.setuptools.package-data]\nmy_package = [\"py.typed\", \"*.pyi\", \"data/*.json\"]\n\n# Black configuration\n[tool.black]\nline-length = 100\ntarget-version = [\"py38\", \"py39\", \"py310\", \"py311\"]\ninclude = ''\\.pyi?$''\n\n# Ruff configuration\n[tool.ruff]\nline-length = 100\ntarget-version = \"py38\"\n\n[tool.ruff.lint]\nselect = [\"E\", \"F\", \"I\", \"N\", \"W\", \"UP\"]\n\n# MyPy configuration\n[tool.mypy]\npython_version = \"3.8\"\nwarn_return_any = true\nwarn_unused_configs = true\ndisallow_untyped_defs = true\n\n# Pytest configuration\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\ntestpaths = [\"tests\"]\npython_files = [\"test_*.py\"]\naddopts = \"-v --cov=my_package --cov-report=term-missing\"\n\n# Coverage configuration\n[tool.coverage.run]\nsource = [\"src\"]\nomit = [\"*/tests/*\"]\n\n[tool.coverage.report]\nexclude_lines = [\n    \"pragma: no cover\",\n    \"def __repr__\",\n    \"raise AssertionError\",\n    \"raise NotImplementedError\",\n]\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Dynamic Versioning\n\n```toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\", \"setuptools-scm>=8.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"my-package\"\ndynamic = [\"version\"]\ndescription = \"Package with dynamic version\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.dynamic]\nversion = {attr = \"my_package.__version__\"}\n\n# Or use setuptools-scm for git-based versioning\n[tool.setuptools_scm]\nwrite_to = \"src/my_package/_version.py\"\n```\n\n**In __init__.py:**\n```python\n# src/my_package/__init__.py\n__version__ = \"1.0.0\"\n\n# Or with setuptools-scm\nfrom importlib.metadata import version\n__version__ = version(\"my-package\")\n```\n\n## Command-Line Interface (CLI) Patterns\n\n### Pattern 6: CLI with Click\n\n```python\n# src/my_package/cli.py\nimport click\n\n@click.group()\n@click.version_option()\ndef cli():\n    \"\"\"My awesome CLI tool.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n@cli.command()\n@click.argument(\"name\")\n@click.option(\"--greeting\", default=\"Hello\", help=\"Greeting to use\")\ndef greet(name: str, greeting: str):\n    \"\"\"Greet someone.\"\"\"\n    click.echo(f\"{greeting}, {name}!\")\n\n@cli.command()\n@click.option(\"--count\", default=1, help=\"Number of times to repeat\")\ndef repeat(count: int):\n    \"\"\"Repeat a message.\"\"\"\n    for i in range(count):\n        click.echo(f\"Message {i + 1}\")\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"Entry point for CLI.\"\"\"\n    cli()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n**Register in pyproject.toml:**\n```toml\n[project.scripts]\nmy-tool = \"my_package.cli:main\"\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\npip install -e .\nmy-tool greet World\nmy-tool greet Alice --greeting=\"Hi\"\nmy-tool repeat --count=3\n```\n\n### Pattern 7: CLI with argparse\n\n```python\n# src/my_package/cli.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"Main CLI entry point.\"\"\"\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"My awesome tool\",\n        prog=\"my-tool\"\n    )\n\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--version\",\n        action=\"version\",\n        version=\"%(prog)s 1.0.0\"\n    )\n\n    subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", help=\"Commands\")\n\n    # Add subcommand\n    process_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"process\", help=\"Process data\")\n    process_parser.add_argument(\"input_file\", help=\"Input file path\")\n    process_parser.add_argument(\n        \"--output\", \"-o\",\n        default=\"output.txt\",\n        help=\"Output file path\"\n    )\n\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    if args.command == \"process\":\n        process_data(args.input_file, args.output)\n    else:\n        parser.print_help()\n        sys.exit(1)\n\ndef process_data(input_file: str, output_file: str):\n    \"\"\"Process data from input to output.\"\"\"\n    print(f\"Processing {input_file} -> {output_file}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n## Building and Publishing\n\n### Pattern 8: Build Package Locally\n\n```bash\n# Install build tools\npip install build twine\n\n# Build distribution\npython -m build\n\n# This creates:\n# dist/\n#   my-package-1.0.0.tar.gz (source distribution)\n#   my_package-1.0.0-py3-none-any.whl (wheel)\n\n# Check the distribution\ntwine check dist/*\n```\n\n### Pattern 9: Publishing to PyPI\n\n```bash\n# Install publishing tools\npip install twine\n\n# Test on TestPyPI first\ntwine upload --repository testpypi dist/*\n\n# Install from TestPyPI to test\npip install --index-url https://test.pypi.org/simple/ my-package\n\n# If all good, publish to PyPI\ntwine upload dist/*\n```\n\n**Using API tokens (recommended):**\n```bash\n# Create ~/.pypirc\n[distutils]\nindex-servers =\n    pypi\n    testpypi\n\n[pypi]\nusername = __token__\npassword = pypi-...your-token...\n\n[testpypi]\nusername = __token__\npassword = pypi-...your-test-token...\n```\n\n### Pattern 10: Automated Publishing with GitHub Actions\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/publish.yml\nname: Publish to PyPI\n\non:\n  release:\n    types: [created]\n\njobs:\n  publish:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n\n      - name: Set up Python\n        uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n        with:\n          python-version: \"3.11\"\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: |\n          pip install build twine\n\n      - name: Build package\n        run: python -m build\n\n      - name: Check package\n        run: twine check dist/*\n\n      - name: Publish to PyPI\n        env:\n          TWINE_USERNAME: __token__\n          TWINE_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.PYPI_API_TOKEN }}\n        run: twine upload dist/*\n```\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Pattern 11: Including Data Files\n\n```toml\n[tool.setuptools.package-data]\nmy_package = [\n    \"data/*.json\",\n    \"templates/*.html\",\n    \"static/css/*.css\",\n    \"py.typed\",\n]\n```\n\n**Accessing data files:**\n```python\n# src/my_package/loader.py\nfrom importlib.resources import files\nimport json\n\ndef load_config():\n    \"\"\"Load configuration from package data.\"\"\"\n    config_file = files(\"my_package\").joinpath(\"data/config.json\")\n    with config_file.open() as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n\n# Python 3.9+\nfrom importlib.resources import files\n\ndata = files(\"my_package\").joinpath(\"data/file.txt\").read_text()\n```\n\n### Pattern 12: Namespace Packages\n\n**For large projects split across multiple repositories:**\n\n```\n# Package 1: company-core\ncompany/\n└── core/\n    ├── __init__.py\n    └── models.py\n\n# Package 2: company-api\ncompany/\n└── api/\n    ├── __init__.py\n    └── routes.py\n```\n\n**Do NOT include __init__.py in the namespace directory (company/):**\n\n```toml\n# company-core/pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"company-core\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\".\"]\ninclude = [\"company.core*\"]\n\n# company-api/pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"company-api\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\".\"]\ninclude = [\"company.api*\"]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```python\n# Both packages can be imported under same namespace\nfrom company.core import models\nfrom company.api import routes\n```\n\n### Pattern 13: C Extensions\n\n```toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\", \"wheel\", \"Cython>=0.29\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[tool.setuptools]\next-modules = [\n    {name = \"my_package.fast_module\", sources = [\"src/fast_module.c\"]},\n]\n```\n\n**Or with setup.py:**\n```python\n# setup.py\nfrom setuptools import setup, Extension\n\nsetup(\n    ext_modules=[\n        Extension(\n            \"my_package.fast_module\",\n            sources=[\"src/fast_module.c\"],\n            include_dirs=[\"src/include\"],\n        )\n    ]\n)\n```\n\n## Version Management\n\n### Pattern 14: Semantic Versioning\n\n```python\n# src/my_package/__init__.py\n__version__ = \"1.2.3\"\n\n# Semantic versioning: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH\n# MAJOR: Breaking changes\n# MINOR: New features (backward compatible)\n# PATCH: Bug fixes\n```\n\n**Version constraints in dependencies:**\n```toml\ndependencies = [\n    \"requests>=2.28.0,<3.0.0\",  # Compatible range\n    \"click~=8.1.0\",              # Compatible release (~= 8.1.0 means >=8.1.0,<8.2.0)\n    \"pydantic>=2.0\",             # Minimum version\n    \"numpy==1.24.3\",             # Exact version (avoid if possible)\n]\n```\n\n### Pattern 15: Git-Based Versioning\n\n```toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\", \"setuptools-scm>=8.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"my-package\"\ndynamic = [\"version\"]\n\n[tool.setuptools_scm]\nwrite_to = \"src/my_package/_version.py\"\nversion_scheme = \"post-release\"\nlocal_scheme = \"dirty-tag\"\n```\n\n**Creates versions like:**\n- `1.0.0` (from git tag)\n- `1.0.1.dev3+g1234567` (3 commits after tag)\n\n## Testing Installation\n\n### Pattern 16: Editable Install\n\n```bash\n# Install in development mode\npip install -e .\n\n# With optional dependencies\npip install -e \".[dev]\"\npip install -e \".[dev,docs]\"\n\n# Now changes to source code are immediately reflected\n```\n\n### Pattern 17: Testing in Isolated Environment\n\n```bash\n# Create virtual environment\npython -m venv test-env\nsource test-env/bin/activate  # Linux/Mac\n# test-env\\Scripts\\activate  # Windows\n\n# Install package\npip install dist/my_package-1.0.0-py3-none-any.whl\n\n# Test it works\npython -c \"import my_package; print(my_package.__version__)\"\n\n# Test CLI\nmy-tool --help\n\n# Cleanup\ndeactivate\nrm -rf test-env\n```\n\n## Documentation\n\n### Pattern 18: README.md Template\n\n```markdown\n# My Package\n\n[![PyPI version](https://badge.fury.io/py/my-package.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/my-package/)\n[![Python versions](https://img.shields.io/pypi/pyversions/my-package.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/my-package/)\n[![Tests](https://github.com/username/my-package/workflows/Tests/badge.svg)](https://github.com/username/my-package/actions)\n\nBrief description of your package.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install my-package\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```python\nfrom my_package import something\n\nresult = something.do_stuff()\n```\n\n## Features\n\n- Feature 1\n- Feature 2\n- Feature 3\n\n## Documentation\n\nFull documentation: https://my-package.readthedocs.io\n\n## Development\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/username/my-package.git\ncd my-package\npip install -e \".[dev]\"\npytest\n```\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Pattern 19: Multi-Architecture Wheels\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/wheels.yml\nname: Build wheels\n\non: [push, pull_request]\n\njobs:\n  build_wheels:\n    name: Build wheels on ${{ matrix.os }}\n    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        os: [ubuntu-latest, windows-latest, macos-latest]\n\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n\n      - name: Build wheels\n        uses: pypa/cibuildwheel@v2.16.2\n\n      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3\n        with:\n          path: ./wheelhouse/*.whl\n```\n\n### Pattern 20: Private Package Index\n\n```bash\n# Install from private index\npip install my-package --index-url https://private.pypi.org/simple/\n\n# Or add to pip.conf\n[global]\nindex-url = https://private.pypi.org/simple/\nextra-index-url = https://pypi.org/simple/\n\n# Upload to private index\ntwine upload --repository-url https://private.pypi.org/ dist/*\n```\n\n## File Templates\n\n### .gitignore for Python Packages\n\n```gitignore\n# Build artifacts\nbuild/\ndist/\n*.egg-info/\n*.egg\n.eggs/\n\n# Python\n__pycache__/\n*.py[cod]\n*$py.class\n*.so\n\n# Virtual environments\nvenv/\nenv/\nENV/\n\n# IDE\n.vscode/\n.idea/\n*.swp\n\n# Testing\n.pytest_cache/\n.coverage\nhtmlcov/\n\n# Distribution\n*.whl\n*.tar.gz\n```\n\n### MANIFEST.in\n\n```\n# MANIFEST.in\ninclude README.md\ninclude LICENSE\ninclude pyproject.toml\n\nrecursive-include src/my_package/data *.json\nrecursive-include src/my_package/templates *.html\nrecursive-exclude * __pycache__\nrecursive-exclude * *.py[co]\n```\n\n## Checklist for Publishing\n\n- [ ] Code is tested (pytest passing)\n- [ ] Documentation is complete (README, docstrings)\n- [ ] Version number updated\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md updated\n- [ ] License file included\n- [ ] pyproject.toml is complete\n- [ ] Package builds without errors\n- [ ] Installation tested in clean environment\n- [ ] CLI tools work (if applicable)\n- [ ] PyPI metadata is correct (classifiers, keywords)\n- [ ] GitHub repository linked\n- [ ] Tested on TestPyPI first\n- [ ] Git tag created for release\n\n## Resources\n\n- **Python Packaging Guide**: https://packaging.python.org/\n- **PyPI**: https://pypi.org/\n- **TestPyPI**: https://test.pypi.org/\n- **setuptools documentation**: https://setuptools.pypa.io/\n- **build**: https://pypa-build.readthedocs.io/\n- **twine**: https://twine.readthedocs.io/\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n1. **Use src/ layout** for cleaner package structure\n2. **Use pyproject.toml** for modern packaging\n3. **Pin build dependencies** in build-system.requires\n4. **Version appropriately** with semantic versioning\n5. **Include all metadata** (classifiers, URLs, etc.)\n6. **Test installation** in clean environments\n7. **Use TestPyPI** before publishing to PyPI\n8. **Document thoroughly** with README and docstrings\n9. **Include LICENSE** file\n10. **Automate publishing** with CI/CD\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:23:11.889Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing advanced package creation and distribution capabilities.","zh":"适合需要高级包创建和分发能力的Python开发代理。","ja":"Pythonパッケージの高度な作成および配布機能を必要とするPython開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 패키지 생성 및 배포 기능이 필요한 Python 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing advanced package creation and distribution capabilities.","fr":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing advanced package creation and distribution capabilities.","de":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing advanced package creation and distribution capabilities.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Python que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de criação e distribuição de pacotes.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки Python, которым требуются расширенные возможности создания и распространения пакетов.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير بايثون الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانات متقدمة لإنشاء وتوزيع الحزم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create, structure, and distribute Python packages using modern packaging tools like pyproject.toml, and publish to PyPI, enabling efficient dependency management and version control through wheels and source distributions.","zh":"使代理能够使用现代包管理工具（如pyproject.toml）创建、结构化和分发Python包，并发布到PyPI，从而通过轮子和源代码分发实现高效的依赖管理和版本控制。","ja":"エージェントがpyproject.tomlなどのモダンパッケージングツールを使用してPythonパッケージを作成、構造化、配布し、PyPIに公開して、ホイールとソースディストリビューションを介した依存関係管理とバージョン管理を効率的に行えるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 pyproject.toml과 같은 모던 패키징 툴을 사용하여 Python 패키지를 생성, 구조화, 배포하고 PyPI에 발행하여 휠과 소스 배포를 통해 효율적인 의존성 관리와 버전 관리를 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Empowers agents to create, structure, and distribute Python packages using modern packaging tools like pyproject.toml, and publish to PyPI, enabling efficient dependency management and version control through wheels and source distributions.","fr":"Empowers agents to create, structure, and distribute Python packages using modern packaging tools like pyproject.toml, and publish to PyPI, enabling efficient dependency management and version control through wheels and source distributions.","de":"Empowers agents to create, structure, and distribute Python packages using modern packaging tools like pyproject.toml, and publish to PyPI, enabling efficient dependency management and version control through wheels and source distributions.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar, estruturar e distribuir pacotes Python usando ferramentas de empacotamento modernas como pyproject.toml, e publicar no PyPI, permitindo um gerenciamento eficiente de dependências e controle de versão por meio de rodas e distribuições de fontes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать, структурировать и распространять пакеты Python с помощью современных инструментов упаковки, таких как pyproject.toml, и публиковать в PyPI, что обеспечивает эффективное управление зависимостями и контроль версий с помощью колес и распространения исходного кода.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من إنشاء هيكلة وتوزيع حزم بايثون باستخدام