PI 문서 생성"],"es":["Diseño de APIs REST y GraphQL","Creación de APIs escalables y mantenibles","Establecimiento de estándares de diseño de API","Revisión de especificaciones de API","Migración entre paradigmas de API","Creación de documentación de API para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Conception d''API REST et GraphQL","Création d''API évolutives et maintenables","Établissement de normes de conception d''API","Révision de spécifications d''API","Migration entre les paradigmes d''API","Création de documentation d''API pour les développeurs"],"de":["Entwurf von REST- und GraphQL-APIs","Erstellung von skalierbaren und wartbaren APIs","Festlegung von API-Design-Standards","Überprüfung von API-Spezifikationen","Migration zwischen API-Paradigmen","Erstellung von API-Dokumentation für Entwickler"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de APIs REST e GraphQL","Criação de APIs escaláveis e intuitivas","Estabelecimento de padrões de design de API","Revisão de especificações de API antes da implementação","Criação de documentação de API amigável para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Разработка API REST и GraphQL","Создание масштабируемых и интуитивных API","Установление стандартов проектирования API","Проверка спецификаций API перед реализацией","Создание дружественной документации API для разработчиков"],"ar":["تطوير واجهات برمجة التطبيقات REST و GraphQL","إنشاء واجهات برمجة التطبيقات القابلة للتحجيم والمباشرة","تحديد معايير تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","مراجعة مواصفات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات قبل التنفيذ","إنشاء توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات ودية للمطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["API 设计","REST API","GraphQL API","API 设计原则","API 性能优化","API 文档"],"ja":["API デザイン","REST API","GraphQL API","API デザイン原則","API パフォーマンス最適化","API ドキュメント"],"ko":["API 설계","REST API","GraphQL API","API 설계 원칙","API 성능 최적화","API 문서"],"es":["diseño de api","principios de diseño de api","api rest","api graphql","desarrollo de api","escalabilidad de api","mantenimiento de api","documentación de api","estándares de diseño de api"],"fr":["conception d''api","principes de conception d''api","api rest","api graphql","développement d''api","évolution de l''api","maintenance de l''api","documentation de l''api","normes de conception d''api"],"de":["api-design","prinzipien des api-designs","rest-api","graphql-api","api-entwicklung","skalierbarkeit von apis","wartbarkeit von apis","api-dokumentation","api-design-standards"],"pt":["princípios de design de API","API REST","API GraphQL","desenvolvimento de API","escalabilidade de API","documentação de API"],"ru":["принципы проектирования API","API REST","API GraphQL","разработка API","масштабируемость API","документация API"],"ar":["مبادئ تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST","واجهة برمجة التطبيقات GraphQL","تطوير واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","قابلية تحجيم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"ugro","repoPath":"ollieb89/ugro","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"api-design-principles","description":"Master REST and GraphQL API design principles to build intuitive, scalable, and maintainable APIs that delight developers. Use when designing new APIs, reviewing API specifications, or establishing API design standards.","bodyPreview":"# API Design Principles\n\nMaster REST and GraphQL API design principles to build intuitive, scalable, and maintainable APIs that delight developers and stand the test of time.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new REST or GraphQL APIs\n- Refactoring existing APIs for better usability\n- Establishing API design standards for your team\n- Reviewing API specifications before implementation\n- Migrating between API paradigms (REST to GraphQL, etc.)\n- Creating developer-friendly API documentation\n-","body":"# API Design Principles\n\nMaster REST and GraphQL API design principles to build intuitive, scalable, and maintainable APIs that delight developers and stand the test of time.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new REST or GraphQL APIs\n- Refactoring existing APIs for better usability\n- Establishing API design standards for your team\n- Reviewing API specifications before implementation\n- Migrating between API paradigms (REST to GraphQL, etc.)\n- Creating developer-friendly API documentation\n- Optimizing APIs for specific use cases (mobile, third-party integrations)\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. RESTful Design Principles\n\n**Resource-Oriented Architecture**\n- Resources are nouns (users, orders, products), not verbs\n- Use HTTP methods for actions (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE)\n- URLs represent resource hierarchies\n- Consistent naming conventions\n\n**HTTP Methods Semantics:**\n- `GET`: Retrieve resources (idempotent, safe)\n- `POST`: Create new resources\n- `PUT`: Replace entire resource (idempotent)\n- `PATCH`: Partial resource updates\n- `DELETE`: Remove resources (idempotent)\n\n### 2. GraphQL Design Principles\n\n**Schema-First Development**\n- Types define your domain model\n- Queries for reading data\n- Mutations for modifying data\n- Subscriptions for real-time updates\n\n**Query Structure:**\n- Clients request exactly what they need\n- Single endpoint, multiple operations\n- Strongly typed schema\n- Introspection built-in\n\n### 3. API Versioning Strategies\n\n**URL Versioning:**\n```\n/api/v1/users\n/api/v2/users\n```\n\n**Header Versioning:**\n```\nAccept: application/vnd.api+json; version=1\n```\n\n**Query Parameter Versioning:**\n```\n/api/users?version=1\n```\n\n## REST API Design Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Resource Collection Design\n\n```python\n# Good: Resource-oriented endpoints\nGET    /api/users              # List users (with pagination)\nPOST   /api/users              # Create user\nGET    /api/users/{id}         # Get specific user\nPUT    /api/users/{id}         # Replace user\nPATCH  /api/users/{id}         # Update user fields\nDELETE /api/users/{id}         # Delete user\n\n# Nested resources\nGET    /api/users/{id}/orders  # Get user''s orders\nPOST   /api/users/{id}/orders  # Create order for user\n\n# Bad: Action-oriented endpoints (avoid)\nPOST   /api/createUser\nPOST   /api/getUserById\nPOST   /api/deleteUser\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Pagination and Filtering\n\n```python\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nclass PaginationParams(BaseModel):\n    page: int = Field(1, ge=1, description=\"Page number\")\n    page_size: int = Field(20, ge=1, le=100, description=\"Items per page\")\n\nclass FilterParams(BaseModel):\n    status: Optional[str] = None\n    created_after: Optional[str] = None\n    search: Optional[str] = None\n\nclass PaginatedResponse(BaseModel):\n    items: List[dict]\n    total: int\n    page: int\n    page_size: int\n    pages: int\n\n    @property\n    def has_next(self) -> bool:\n        return self.page < self.pages\n\n    @property\n    def has_prev(self) -> bool:\n        return self.page > 1\n\n# FastAPI endpoint example\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Query, Depends\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/api/users\", response_model=PaginatedResponse)\nasync def list_users(\n    page: int = Query(1, ge=1),\n    page_size: int = Query(20, ge=1, le=100),\n    status: Optional[str] = Query(None),\n    search: Optional[str] = Query(None)\n):\n    # Apply filters\n    query = build_query(status=status, search=search)\n\n    # Count total\n    total = await count_users(query)\n\n    # Fetch page\n    offset = (page - 1) * page_size\n    users = await fetch_users(query, limit=page_size, offset=offset)\n\n    return PaginatedResponse(\n        items=users,\n        total=total,\n        page=page,\n        page_size=page_size,\n        pages=(total + page_size - 1) // page_size\n    )\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Error Handling and Status Codes\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import HTTPException, status\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass ErrorResponse(BaseModel):\n    error: str\n    message: str\n    details: Optional[dict] = None\n    timestamp: str\n    path: str\n\nclass ValidationErrorDetail(BaseModel):\n    field: str\n    message: str\n    value: Any\n\n# Consistent error responses\nSTATUS_CODES = {\n    \"success\": 200,\n    \"created\": 201,\n    \"no_content\": 204,\n    \"bad_request\": 400,\n    \"unauthorized\": 401,\n    \"forbidden\": 403,\n    \"not_found\": 404,\n    \"conflict\": 409,\n    \"unprocessable\": 422,\n    \"internal_error\": 500\n}\n\ndef raise_not_found(resource: str, id: str):\n    raise HTTPException(\n        status_code=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND,\n        detail={\n            \"error\": \"NotFound\",\n            \"message\": f\"{resource} not found\",\n            \"details\": {\"id\": id}\n        }\n    )\n\ndef raise_validation_error(errors: List[ValidationErrorDetail]):\n    raise HTTPException(\n        status_code=status.HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY,\n        detail={\n            \"error\": \"ValidationError\",\n            \"message\": \"Request validation failed\",\n            \"details\": {\"errors\": [e.dict() for e in errors]}\n        }\n    )\n\n# Example usage\n@app.get(\"/api/users/{user_id}\")\nasync def get_user(user_id: str):\n    user = await fetch_user(user_id)\n    if not user:\n        raise_not_found(\"User\", user_id)\n    return user\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: HATEOAS (Hypermedia as the Engine of Application State)\n\n```python\nclass UserResponse(BaseModel):\n    id: str\n    name: str\n    email: str\n    _links: dict\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_user(cls, user: User, base_url: str):\n        return cls(\n            id=user.id,\n            name=user.name,\n            email=user.email,\n            _links={\n                \"self\": {\"href\": f\"{base_url}/api/users/{user.id}\"},\n                \"orders\": {\"href\": f\"{base_url}/api/users/{user.id}/orders\"},\n                \"update\": {\n                    \"href\": f\"{base_url}/api/users/{user.id}\",\n                    \"method\": \"PATCH\"\n                },\n                \"delete\": {\n                    \"href\": f\"{base_url}/api/users/{user.id}\",\n                    \"method\": \"DELETE\"\n                }\n            }\n        )\n```\n\n## GraphQL Design Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Schema Design\n\n```graphql\n# schema.graphql\n\n# Clear type definitions\ntype User {\n  id: ID!\n  email: String!\n  name: String!\n  createdAt: DateTime!\n\n  # Relationships\n  orders(\n    first: Int = 20\n    after: String\n    status: OrderStatus\n  ): OrderConnection!\n\n  profile: UserProfile\n}\n\ntype Order {\n  id: ID!\n  status: OrderStatus!\n  total: Money!\n  items: [OrderItem!]!\n  createdAt: DateTime!\n\n  # Back-reference\n  user: User!\n}\n\n# Pagination pattern (Relay-style)\ntype OrderConnection {\n  edges: [OrderEdge!]!\n  pageInfo: PageInfo!\n  totalCount: Int!\n}\n\ntype OrderEdge {\n  node: Order!\n  cursor: String!\n}\n\ntype PageInfo {\n  hasNextPage: Boolean!\n  hasPreviousPage: Boolean!\n  startCursor: String\n  endCursor: String\n}\n\n# Enums for type safety\nenum OrderStatus {\n  PENDING\n  CONFIRMED\n  SHIPPED\n  DELIVERED\n  CANCELLED\n}\n\n# Custom scalars\nscalar DateTime\nscalar Money\n\n# Query root\ntype Query {\n  user(id: ID!): User\n  users(\n    first: Int = 20\n    after: String\n    search: String\n  ): UserConnection!\n\n  order(id: ID!): Order\n}\n\n# Mutation root\ntype Mutation {\n  createUser(input: CreateUserInput!): CreateUserPayload!\n  updateUser(input: UpdateUserInput!): UpdateUserPayload!\n  deleteUser(id: ID!): DeleteUserPayload!\n\n  createOrder(input: CreateOrderInput!): CreateOrderPayload!\n}\n\n# Input types for mutations\ninput CreateUserInput {\n  email: String!\n  name: String!\n  password: String!\n}\n\n# Payload types for mutations\ntype CreateUserPayload {\n  user: User\n  errors: [Error!]\n}\n\ntype Error {\n  field: String\n  message: String!\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Resolver Design\n\n```python\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom ariadne import QueryType, MutationType, ObjectType\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\nquery = QueryType()\nmutation = MutationType()\nuser_type = ObjectType(\"User\")\n\n@query.field(\"user\")\nasync def resolve_user(obj, info, id: str) -> Optional[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Resolve single user by ID.\"\"\"\n    return await fetch_user_by_id(id)\n\n@query.field(\"users\")\nasync def resolve_users(\n    obj,\n    info,\n    first: int = 20,\n    after: Optional[str] = None,\n    search: Optional[str] = None\n) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Resolve paginated user list.\"\"\"\n    # Decode cursor\n    offset = decode_cursor(after) if after else 0\n\n    # Fetch users\n    users = await fetch_users(\n        limit=first + 1,  # Fetch one extra to check hasNextPage\n        offset=offset,\n        search=search\n    )\n\n    # Pagination\n    has_next = len(users) > first\n    if has_next:\n        users = users[:first]\n\n    edges = [\n        {\n            \"node\": user,\n            \"cursor\": encode_cursor(offset + i)\n        }\n        for i, user in enumerate(users)\n    ]\n\n    return {\n        \"edges\": edges,\n        \"pageInfo\": {\n            \"hasNextPage\": has_next,\n            \"hasPreviousPage\": offset > 0,\n            \"startCursor\": edges[0][\"cursor\"] if edges else None,\n            \"endCursor\": edges[-1][\"cursor\"] if edges else None\n        },\n        \"totalCount\": await count_users(search=search)\n    }\n\n@user_type.field(\"orders\")\nasync def resolve_user_orders(user: dict, info, first: int = 20) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Resolve user''s orders (N+1 prevention with DataLoader).\"\"\"\n    # Use DataLoader to batch requests\n    loader = info.context[\"loaders\"][\"orders_by_user\"]\n    orders = await loader.load(user[\"id\"])\n\n    return paginate_orders(orders, first)\n\n@mutation.field(\"createUser\")\nasync def resolve_create_user(obj, info, input: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Create new user.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Validate input\n        validate_user_input(input)\n\n        # Create user\n        user = await create_user(\n            email=input[\"email\"],\n            name=input[\"name\"],\n            password=hash_password(input[\"password\"])\n        )\n\n        return {\n            \"user\": user,\n            \"errors\": []\n        }\n    except ValidationError as e:\n        return {\n            \"user\": None,\n            \"errors\": [{\"field\": e.field, \"message\": e.message}]\n        }\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: DataLoader (N+1 Problem Prevention)\n\n```python\nfrom aiodataloader import DataLoader\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nclass UserLoader(DataLoader):\n    \"\"\"Batch load users by ID.\"\"\"\n\n    async def batch_load_fn(self, user_ids: List[str]) -> List[Optional[dict]]:\n        \"\"\"Load multiple users in single query.\"\"\"\n        users = await fetch_users_by_ids(user_ids)\n\n        # Map results back to input order\n        user_map = {user[\"id\"]: user for user in users}\n        return [user_map.get(user_id) for user_id in user_ids]\n\nclass OrdersByUserLoader(DataLoader):\n    \"\"\"Batch load orders by user ID.\"\"\"\n\n    async def batch_load_fn(self, user_ids: List[str]) -> List[List[dict]]:\n        \"\"\"Load orders for multiple users in single query.\"\"\"\n        orders = await fetch_orders_by_user_ids(user_ids)\n\n        # Group orders by user_id\n        orders_by_user = {}\n        for order in orders:\n            user_id = order[\"user_id\"]\n            if user_id not in orders_by_user:\n                orders_by_user[user_id] = []\n            orders_by_user[user_id].append(order)\n\n        # Return in input order\n        return [orders_by_user.get(user_id, []) for user_id in user_ids]\n\n# Context setup\ndef create_context():\n    return {\n        \"loaders\": {\n            \"user\": UserLoader(),\n            \"orders_by_user\": OrdersByUserLoader()\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### REST APIs\n1. **Consistent Naming**: Use plural nouns for collections (`/users`, not `/user`)\n2. **Stateless**: Each request contains all necessary information\n3. **Use HTTP Status Codes Correctly**: 2xx success, 4xx client errors, 5xx server errors\n4. **Version Your API**: Plan for breaking changes from day one\n5. **Pagination**: Always paginate large collections\n6. **Rate Limiting**: Protect your API with rate limits\n7. **Documentation**: Use OpenAPI/Swagger for interactive docs\n\n### GraphQL APIs\n1. **Schema First**: Design schema before writing resolvers\n2. **Avoid N+1**: Use DataLoaders for efficient data fetching\n3. **Input Validation**: Validate at schema and resolver levels\n4. **Error Handling**: Return structured errors in mutation payloads\n5. **Pagination**: Use cursor-based pagination (Relay spec)\n6. **Deprecation**: Use `@deprecated` directive for gradual migration\n7. **Monitoring**: Track query complexity and execution time\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Over-fetching/Under-fetching (REST)**: Fixed in GraphQL but requires DataLoaders\n- **Breaking Changes**: Version APIs or use deprecation strategies\n- **Inconsistent Error Formats**: Standardize error responses\n- **Missing Rate Limits**: APIs without limits are vulnerable to abuse\n- **Poor Documentation**: Undocumented APIs frustrate developers\n- **Ignoring HTTP Semantics**: POST for idempotent operations breaks expectations\n- **Tight Coupling**: API structure shouldn''t mirror database schema\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/rest-best-practices.md**: Comprehensive REST API design guide\n- **references/graphql-schema-design.md**: GraphQL schema patterns and anti-patterns\n- **references/api-versioning-strategies.md**: Versioning approaches and migration paths\n- **assets/rest-api-template.py**: FastAPI REST API template\n- **assets/graphql-schema-template.graphql**: Complete GraphQL schema example\n- **assets/api-design-checklist.md**: Pre-implementation review checklist\n- **scripts/openapi-generator.py**: Generate OpenAPI specs from code\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:29:12.723Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for API-focused Agents seeking to master REST and GraphQL API design principles for scalable and maintainable API development.","zh":"适合专注于 API 的代理寻求掌握 REST 和 GraphQL API 设计原则，以实现可扩展和可维护的 API 开发。","ja":"API に焦点を当てたエージェントが REST と GraphQL API デザインの原則をマスターするのに最適です。スケーラブルでメンテナンス可能な API 開発のために。","ko":"API에 중점을 둔 에이전트가 REST 및 GraphQL API 설계 원칙을 마스터하는 데 적합합니다. 확장 가능하고 유지 관리 가능한 API 개발을 위해","es":"Ideal para Agentes centrados en API que buscan dominar los principios de diseño de API REST y GraphQL para un desarrollo de API escalable y mantenible.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents axés sur l''API souhaitant maîtriser les principes de conception d''API REST et GraphQL pour un développement d''API évolutif et maintenable.","de":"Ideal für API-fokussierte Agenten, die die Prinzipien von REST- und GraphQL-API-Design für eine skalierbare und wartbare API-Entwicklung meistern möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes focados em API que buscam dominar os princípios de design de API REST e GraphQL para desenvolvimento de API escalável e mantível.","ru":"Идеально для агентов, ориентированных на API, стремящихся овладеть принципами дизайна REST и GraphQL API для масштабируемого и поддерживаемого развития API.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المهتمين بالواجهات البرمجية الذين يسعون إلى إتقان مبادئ تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST وGraphQL من أجل تطوير واجهة برمجة تطبيقات قابلة للتطوير والصيانة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design intuitive APIs using REST and GraphQL, ensuring scalability, maintainability, and usability, while also providing standards for API documentation and migration between API paradigms.","zh":"赋予代理使用 REST 和 GraphQL 设计直观的 API 的能力，确保可扩展性、可维护性和可用性，同时也为 API 文档和 API 范式之间的迁移提供标准。","ja":"REST と GraphQL を使用して直感的な API を設計するエージェントの能力を付与します。スケーラビリティ、メンテナンス性、ユーザビリティを確保し、API ドキュメントと API パラダイム間の移行の標準も提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 REST 및 GraphQL을 사용하여 직관적인 API를 설계할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 확장성, 유지 관리성, 사용 편의성을 보장同时 API 문서 및 API 패러다임 간의 마이그레이션을 위한 표준도 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar API intuitivas utilizando REST y GraphQL, garantizando escalabilidad, mantenibilidad y usabilidad, y proporcionando también estándares para la documentación de API y la migración entre paradigmas de API.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des API intuitives en utilisant REST et GraphQL, en garantissant l''évolutivité, la maintenabilité et l''utilisabilité, tout en fournissant des normes pour la documentation d''API et la migration entre les paradigmes d''API.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, intuitive APIs mit REST und GraphQL zu entwerfen, Skalierbarkeit, Wartbarkeit und Benutzerfreundlichkeit sicherzustellen und gleichzeitig Standards für die API-Dokumentation und den Wechsel zwischen API-Paradigmen bereitzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar APIs intuitivas usando REST e GraphQL, garantindo escalabilidade, manutenibilidade e usabilidade, além de fornecer padrões para documentação de API e migração entre paradigmas de API.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать интуитивные API с использованием REST и GraphQL, обеспечивая масштабируемость, поддерживаемость и удобство использования, а также предоставляя стандарты для документации API и миграции между парадигмами API.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تصميم واجهات برمجة تطبيقات直ه باستخدام REST وGraphQL، مما يضمن القدرة على التطوير والصيانة والاستعمال، بالإضافة إلى تقديم معايير لتدوين واجهة برمجة التطبيقات والانتقال بين أنماط واجهة برمجة التطبيقات."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing new REST or GraphQL APIs","Refactoring existing APIs for better usability","Establishing API design standards for development teams"],"zh":["设计新的 REST 或 GraphQL API","重构现有的 API 以提高可用性","为开发团队建立 API 设计标准"],"ja":["新しい REST または GraphQL API を設計する","既存の API をより良い可用性のためにリファクタリングする","開発チームのための API デザイン標準を確立する"],"ko":["새로운 REST 또는 GraphQL API 설계","기존 API를 더 나은 사용 편의성을 위해 리팩토링","개발 팀을 위한 API 설계 표준 설정"],"es":["Diseñar nuevas API REST o GraphQL","Reorganizar API existentes para una mejor usabilidad","Establecer estándares de diseño de API para equipos de desarrollo"],"fr":["Concevoir de nouvelles API REST ou GraphQL","Réorganiser les API existantes pour une meilleure utilisabilité","Établir des normes de conception d''API pour les équipes de développement"],"de":["Neue REST- oder GraphQL-APIs entwerfen","Bestehende APIs für bessere Benutzerfreundlichkeit neu gestalten","API-Designstandards für Entwicklerteams festlegen"],"pt":["Projetar novas APIs REST ou GraphQL","Reestruturar APIs existentes para melhor usabilidade","Estabelecer padrões de design de API para equipes de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Проектирование новых API REST или GraphQL","Перестройка существующих API для лучшей удобства использования","Установление стандартов дизайна API для команд разработки"],"ar":["تصميم واجهات برمجة تطبيقات جديدة REST أو GraphQL","إعادة هيكلة واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الحالية لتحسين سهولة الاستخدام","تحديد معايير تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات لفريق التطوير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of REST and GraphQL fundamentals","Limited to API design principles and does not cover implementation details"],"zh":["需要了解 REST 和 GraphQL 的基本原理","仅限于 API 设计原则，不涵盖实现细节"],"ja":["REST と GraphQL の基本原則を理解する必要がある","API デザインの原則に限定され、実装の詳細はカバーされない"],"ko":["REST 및 GraphQL의 기본 원리를 이해해야 함","API 설계 원칙에만 국한되며 구현 세부 사항은 포함되지 않음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los fundamentos de REST y GraphQL","Limitado a los principios de diseño de API y no cubre los detalles de implementación"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de base de REST et GraphQL","Limité aux principes de conception d''API et ne couvre pas les détails d''implémentation"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für die Grundlagen von REST und GraphQL","Begrenzt auf API-Designprinzipien und deckt keine Implementierungsdetails ab"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos fundamentos de REST e GraphQL","Limitado a princípios de design de API e não cobre detalhes de implementação"],"ru":["Требует понимания основ REST и GraphQL","Ограничен принципами дизайна API и не охватывает детали реализации"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم الأساسيات من REST وGraphQL","محدود بمبادئ تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات ولا يغطي تفاصيل التنفيذ"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('pliniou/loto-generator/skill-engine-developer', 'community', 'pliniou', 'loto-generator', 'pliniou/loto-generator', 'skill-engine-developer', 0, 0, 25, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z', '2026-02-18T12:28:55.395Z', NULL, '{"id":"pliniou/loto-generator/skill-engine-developer","name":"skill-engine-developer","description":{"zh":"性能优化专家负责优化应用的性能，包括速度、响应性、资源使用和用户体验的流畅性","ja":"パフォーマンススペシャリストは、アプリのパフォーマンスを最適化する責任があります。速度、レスポンス、リソース使用、ユーザーエクスペリエンスのスムーズ性など","ko":"성능 최적화 전문가는 애플리케이션의 성능을 최적화하는 역할을 맡습니다. 속도, 반응성, 리소스 사용, 사용자 경험의 부드러움 등","es":"El especialista en rendimiento se enfoca en optimizar el rendimiento de la aplicación, incluyendo velocidad, respuesta y uso de recursos. La misión es garantizar que la aplicación se ejecute de manera eficiente en una variedad de dispositivos Android.","fr":"Le spécialiste des performances se concentre sur l''optimisation des performances de l''application, notamment la vitesse, la réactivité et l''utilisation des ressources. La mission est de garantir que l''application s''exécute de manière efficace sur une variété d''appareils Android.","de":"Der Leistungs-Spezialist konzentriert sich auf die Optimierung der Leistung der Anwendung, einschließlich Geschwindigkeit, Reaktionszeit und Ressourcennutzung. Die Mission ist es, sicherzustellen, dass die Anwendung effizient auf einer Vielzahl von Android-Geräten ausgeführt wird.","pt":"Otimizar o desempenho do aplicativo é crucial para uma experiência do usuário suave e eficiente. Isso inclui melhorar o tempo de lançamento, renderização de frames e uso de recursos.","ru":"Оптимизация производительности приложения имеет решающее значение для обеспечения гладкой и эффективной пользовательской experiência. Это включает в себя улучшение времени запуска, рендеринга кадров и использования ресурсов.","ar":"تحسين أداء التطبيق ضروري لتقديم تجربة مستخدم سلسة و فعالة. هذا يشمل تحسين وقت الإطلاق و تعزيز إطار العرض و استخدام الموارد.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"性能优化专家：提高应用速度和响应性","ja":"パフォーマンススペシャリスト：アプリの速度とレスポンスを最適化","ko":"성능 최적화 전문가: 애플리케이션 속도와 반응성 개선","es":"Optimización de Rendimiento de Aplicaciones Móviles","fr":"Optimisation des Performances des Applications Mobiles","de":"Leistungsoptimierung von Mobile Apps","pt":"Otimização de Desempenho de Aplicativos","ru":"Оптимизация производительности приложений","ar":"تحسين أداء التطبيقات","en":"skill-engine-developer"},"description":{"zh":"性能优化专家负责优化应用的性能，包括速度、响应性、资源使用和用户体验的流畅性","ja":"パフォーマンススペシャリストは、アプリのパフォーマンスを最適化する責任があります。速度、レスポンス、リソース使用、ユーザーエクスペリエンスのスムーズ性など","ko":"성능 최적화 전문가는 애플리케이션의 성능을 최적화하는 역할을 맡습니다. 속도, 반응성, 리소스 사용, 사용자 경험의 부드러움 등","es":"El especialista en rendimiento se enfoca en optimizar el rendimiento de la aplicación, incluyendo velocidad, respuesta y uso de recursos. La misión es garant...","fr":"Le spécialiste des performances se concentre sur l''optimisation des performances de l''application, notamment la vitesse, la réactivité et l''utilisation des r...","de":"Der Leistungs-Spezialist konzentriert sich auf die Optimierung der Leistung der Anwendung, einschließlich Geschwindigkeit, Reaktionszeit und Ressourcennutzun...","pt":"Otimizar o desempenho do aplicativo é crucial para uma experiência do usuário suave e eficiente. Isso inclui melhorar o tempo de lançamento, renderização de ...","ru":"Оптимизация производительности приложения имеет решающее значение для обеспечения гладкой и эффективной пользовательской experiência. Это включает в себя улу...","ar":"تحسين أداء التطبيق ضروري لتقديم تجربة مستخدم سلسة و فعالة. هذا يشمل تحسين وقت الإطلاق و تعزيز إطار العرض و استخدام الموارد.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["优化应用启动时间","减少帧渲染时间","降低内存占用","减少电池消耗","改善用户体验"],"ja":["起動時間の最適化","フレームレンダリング時間の短縮","メモリ占有量の削減","バッテリー消費量の削減","ユーザーエクスペリエンスの向上"],"ko":["启动 시간 최적화","프레임 렌더링 시간 단축","메모리 사용량 감소","배터리 소모량 감소","사용자 경험 개선"],"es":["Análisis de tiempo de lanzamiento de la aplicación","Optimización del renderizado de frames para evitar lag en la interfaz de usuario","Monitoreo del uso de memoria y consumo de batería","Garantía de una experiencia de usuario suave en dispositivos de gama baja","Establecimiento de indicadores clave de rendimiento"],"fr":["Analyse du temps de lancement de l''application","Optimisation du rendu des frames pour éviter le lag de l''interface utilisateur","Surveillance de l''utilisation de la mémoire et de la consommation de batterie","Garantie d''une expérience utilisateur fluide sur les appareils de gamme inférieure","Établissement d''indicateurs clés de performance"],"de":["Analyse der Startzeit der Anwendung","Optimierung der Frame-Wiedergabe, um Benutzeroberflächen-Lag zu vermeiden","Überwachung des Speicher- und Batterieverbrauchs","Sicherstellung einer nahtlosen Benutzererfahrung auf Geräten der unteren Preisklasse","Festlegung von Leistungsindikatoren"],"pt":["Melhoria do tempo de lançamento do aplicativo","Otimização da renderização de frames para evitar lag","Redução do uso de memória e recursos","Melhoria do consumo de bateria","Aumento da responsividade do aplicativo"],"ru":["Улучшение времени запуска приложения","Оптимизация рендеринга кадров для избежания лага","Сокращение использования памяти и ресурсов","Улучшение потребления батареи","Повышение отзывчивости приложения"],"ar":["تحسين وقت الإطلاق للتطبيق","تحسين تعزيز إطار العرض لتجنب التأخير","تقليل استخدام الذاكرة و الموارد","تحسين استهلاك البطارية","زيادة استجابة التطبيق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["性能优化","应用性能","启动时间","帧渲染时间","内存占用","电池消耗","用户体验"],"ja":["パフォーマンス最適化","アプリパフォーマンス","起動時間","フレームレンダリング時間","メモリ占有量","バッテリー消費量","ユーザーエクスペリエンス"],"ko":["성능 최적화","애플리케이션 성능","启动 시간","프레임 렌더링 시간","메모리 사용량","배터리 소모량","사용자 경험"],"es":["optimización de rendimiento","aplicaciones móviles","tiempo de lanzamiento","renderizado de frames","uso de memoria","consumo de batería","experiencia de usuario","dispositivos Android"],"fr":["optimisation des performances","applications mobiles","temps de lancement","rendu des frames","utilisation de la mémoire","consommation de batterie","expérience utilisateur","appareils Android"],"de":["Leistungsoptimierung","mobile Anwendungen","Startzeit","Frame-Wiedergabe","Speicherverbrauch","Batterieverbrauch","Benutzererfahrung","Android-Geräte"],"pt":["otimização de desempenho","aplicativos android","velocidade do aplicativo","eficiência do aplicativo","experiência do usuário","desempenho do aplicativo"],"ru":["оптимизация производительности","приложения android","скорость приложения","эффективность приложения","пользовательский опыт","производительность приложения"],"ar":["تحسين الأداء","تطبيقات أندرويد","سرعة التطبيق","كفاءة التطبيق","تجربة المستخدم","أداء التطبيق"]}},"owner":"pliniou","repo":"loto-generator","repoPath":"pliniou/loto-generator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-engine-developer","description":"Desenvolvimento de engines e domínio (Kotlin puro).","bodyPreview":"You are the Performance Specialist, focused on optimizing the app’s performance, including speed, responsiveness, resource usage, and overall smoothness of the user experience. Your mission is to ensure the app runs efficiently on a variety of Android devices, from high-end to low-end, and provides a snappy, jank-free experience to users. Begin by establishing key performance indicators for the app: app launch time, frame render time (to avoid UI lag), memory footprint, battery consumption, and","body":"You are the Performance Specialist, focused on optimizing the app’s performance, including speed, responsiveness, resource usage, and overall smoothness of the user experience. Your mission is to ensure the app runs efficiently on a variety of Android devices, from high-end to low-end, and provides a snappy, jank-free experience to users. Begin by establishing key performance indicators for the app: app launch time, frame render time (to avoid UI lag), memory footprint, battery consumption, and network efficiency. Throughout development, monitor these metrics and guide the team in best practices to meet performance goals.\n\nTackle app startup performance first, as it’s the user’s first impression. Work with the team to keep the launch sequence lean: initialize only essential components on startup and defer any heavy loading to background threads or later in the app flow. For example, use SplashScreen API or a lightweight launch screen while doing minimal necessary work to get the first screen up. If certain data must be loaded at launch, ensure it’s done asynchronously (e.g. using coroutines or WorkManager for deferred initialization tasks). Consider utilizing Baseline Profiles to improve startup time – collaborate with the developers to generate a baseline profile for critical application paths (like application launch, navigation to main screens) so that Android’s runtime can pre-compile those code paths and avoid JIT overhead at runtime. Measuring cold start time (with logcat timing or Android Studio profilers) and optimizing it is part of your responsibility.\n\nEnsure UI rendering is smooth, aiming for consistent 60fps (or 90/120fps on high-refresh devices if possible). Identify any potential sources of jank (stutters) in the UI. Common culprits include heavy computations or blocking I/O on the main thread, excessive recompositions in Compose, or poor usage of lists (like not using lazy components). Use tools like Android Profiler and Systrace or the Compose specific Layout Inspector with recomposition counts to spot where frames are dropped. Advise the UI Developer to apply Compose performance best practices: for example, avoid recomposing entire screen when only a small part changes, by using granular state and keys. If a list scroll is janky, check that LazyColumn items have stable keys and that images are being loaded efficiently (perhaps using Coil with proper sizing and caching). For any expensive drawing, consider using LaunchedEffect or SideEffect to move work off the immediate composition path. Where animations are needed, prefer the Compose Animation APIs which are optimized, rather than hacking with manual delays. Make sure that any custom composables are annotated or structured to not recompute unnecessarily – e.g., if you have a custom view in Compose, mark it with @Stable or use DerivedStateOf if it’s deriving something from rapidly changing state to prevent redundant recompositions.\n\nManage memory usage to prevent bloats and potential OOM (Out of Memory) errors. Regularly profile memory while running typical user flows. Look out for memory leaks – use tools like LeakCanary during development to catch objects that are not being freed (common issues might be a ViewModel that holds a context longer than it should, or a Compose static object that captures an Activity reference). Also check for large bitmaps in memory; ensure images are loaded in appropriately scaled sizes (the Image loading library should downsample images to the view size). If the app uses caching (images or data), verify cache limits and that they aren’t over-consuming memory. The Performance Specialist can suggest using onTrimMemory and proper lifecycle management to release caches when the app goes to background or memory is low. Also consider the effect of multiple open screens – e.g., if a user navigates deep, make sure previous screens aren’t keeping huge amounts of data alive. In Compose, this might mean using Navigation properly so that composables out of view are disposed, or manually cleaning up state in onPause if needed.\n\nOptimize network and I/O operations for performance as well as for not impacting UI thread. Ensure all database queries and network calls are off the main thread (the Data Engineer should have done this, but double-check via profiling tools – the “Network” and “CPU” profilers can show if any heavy I/O coincides with user interactions). If the app downloads large data or streams, implement progress indications and consider chunking the work. Use caching headers and strategies to minimize redundant network fetches (e.g., OKHttp’s cache, or conditional GET requests to only fetch if data changed). The Performance Specialist can run tests on slow networks (simulate 3G or high latency) to see how the app behaves – ensure that spinners or placeholders are shown, and the UI remains interactive if possible (no locking up while waiting for network). Also monitor battery impact: avoid aggressive polling in WorkManager (sync at reasonable intervals, not too frequently), batch network calls together when possible (to let radio sleep in between), and utilize JobScheduler/WorkManager’s ability to batch under the hood.\n\nFocus also on scrolling and list performance if the app has feeds or lists. For endless lists, ensure pagination is implemented (e.g., Jetpack Paging library) rather than loading thousands of items at once. Make use of LazyColumn’s capabilities to only compose what''s on screen. Test on a low-end device or emulator with less memory to see if list scrolling stays smooth. If not, identify if the bottleneck is image decoding (perhaps enable crossfade only on Wi-Fi or high-end devices, etc.) or too complex composables per item (maybe simplify item layout or use snapshots for state). The goal is zero dropped frames even when data is loading in a list during scroll.\n\nImplement or oversee performance testing and monitoring. This could involve automated tests like Macrobenchmark (a Jetpack library that can measure startup and scroll performance in a controlled way on device) to catch regressions in frame timing or startup time. For example, you could have a macrobenchmark test that launches the app and measures how long until the content is fully drawn, and another that scrolls a long list and measures jank. Include these in the CI pipeline if feasible, or at least run them on each release candidate to ensure performance hasn’t degraded. Additionally, prepare the app for post-release performance monitoring: integrate analytics or performance monitoring SDKs (like Firebase Performance Monitoring or custom logging) that can track app start time, screen open times, and memory usage on user devices, to catch any outliers in the real world.\n\nAdvise on and implement any needed optimizations at the code level. This might involve algorithmic improvements (e.g., using efficient algorithms for large data operations, avoiding nested loops on big lists on the main thread), or using caching to prevent doing work repeatedly (like results that can be memoized). For instance, if a complex calculation is needed for display, consider computing it once in the ViewModel and caching the result rather than recalculating on each recomposition. Or if the same data is used in multiple places, ensure the repository or ViewModel shares the loaded data rather than fetching it twice. Also verify that the app isn’t doing unnecessary work when idle (for example, remove debug log spam or any development-only background tasks for release builds to save cycles).\n\nOptimize rendering performance for any custom drawings or animations. If the UI uses Canvas or custom graphics, ensure they redraw only when needed. If an animation is heavy, consider using androidx.compose.ui.graphics.GraphicsLayerScope to enable hardware layer caching if appropriate. Also manage the complexity of layouts – an excessively deep layout hierarchy or too many nested composables can slow down measure/layout phases, though Compose is generally efficient; still, watch out for any composables recomposing too often (perhaps use the ReusableContent API or remember keys to keep state where needed).\n\nLastly, keep an eye on release build optimizations. Make sure that R8 (code shrinker) is enabled and configured – this not only reduces app size but can inline and optimize bytecode. Check that ProGuard/R8 rules are properly set so that you’re not accidentally keeping things that bloat the app. Verify that the app’s binary size is reasonable, and strip out unnecessary resources (like if libraries bring in a lot of unused resources, consider using the Android App Bundle’s ability to split or remove unused languages, etc.). A smaller app typically loads faster and uses memory more efficiently due to fewer resources.\n\nIn sum, your job is to squeeze the best performance out of the app without sacrificing correctness or maintainability. By profiling regularly, identifying hotspots, and applying targeted optimizations or best practices, you prevent performance issues from affecting users. Every user interaction should feel crisp: taps responding immediately, transitions smooth, and data appearing quickly. You work across the team – with the UI Developer to refine rendering and layout, with the Data Engineer to ensure background work is optimal, with the Domain Expert to possibly adjust algorithms for speed, and with the Release Manager to include performance checks in release criteria. When you’ve done your job well, the app not only works correctly (thanks to QA) but also delivers a fast and pleasant experience that leaves a good impression."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:28:55.395Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Android Performance Tuning Agents specializing in resource optimization and user experience metrics.","zh":"适用于专注于资源优化和用户体验指标的Android性能优化代理。","ja":"Androidパフォーマンスチューニングエージェントのリソース最適化とユーザーエクスペリエンスメトリクスに特化したエージェントに不可欠です。","ko":"리소스 최적화 및 사용자 경험 메트릭에 특화된 안드로이드 성능 튜닝 에이전트에 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para Agentes de Ajuste de Rendimiento de Android que se especializan en la optimización de recursos y las métricas de experiencia del usuario.","fr":"Essentiel pour les Agents de Réglage de Performance Android spécialisés dans l''optimisation des ressources et les métriques d''expérience utilisateur.","de":"Wesentlich für Android-Leistungsabstimmungsagenten, die sich auf Ressourcenoptimierung und Benutzererfahrungsmetriken spezialisieren.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Otimização de Desempenho do Android especializados em otimização de recursos e métricas de experiência do usuário.","ru":"Необходим для агентов настройки производительности Android, специализирующихся на оптимизации ресурсов и метриках пользовательского опыта.","ar":"ضروري للوكلاء المحسّنين لأداء نظام التشغيل أندرويد المتخصصين في تحسين الموارد وأرقام معايير تجربة المستخدم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables deep analysis and optimization of Android app performance by establishing key KPIs like app launch time, frame render time, memory footprint, and battery consumption, ensuring smooth operation across diverse device specifications.","zh":"通过建立应用启动时间、帧渲染时间、内存占用和电池消耗等关键KPI，实现对Android应用性能的深入分析和优化，确保在不同设备规格下平滑运行。","ja":"アプリの起動時間、フレームレンダリング時間、メモリフットプリント、バッテリー消費などの主要KPIを確立することで、Androidアプリのパフォーマンスを深く分析し、最適化し、様々なデバイス仕様でスムーズに動作するようにします。","ko":"애플리케이션 시작 시간, 프레임 렌더링 시간, 메모리 사용량, 배터리 소비량 등의 주요 KPI를 설정하여 안드로이드 애플리케이션 성능을 깊이 분석 및 최적화하여 다양한 기기 사양에서 плав하게 작동하도록 합니다.","es":"Permite un análisis y optimización profundos del rendimiento de la aplicación de Android al establecer indicadores clave de rendimiento (KPI) como el tiempo de lanzamiento de la aplicación, el tiempo de renderizado de frames, la huella de memoria y el consumo de batería, garantizando un funcionamiento suave en diversas especificaciones de dispositivos.","fr":"Permet une analyse et une optimisation approfondies des performances de l''application Android en établissant des indicateurs clés de performance (KPI) tels que le temps de lancement de l''application, le temps de rendu des frames, l''empreinte mémoire et la consommation de batterie, garantissant un fonctionnement fluide sur diverses spécifications d''appareils.","de":"Ermöglicht eine tiefe Analyse und Optimierung der Leistung von Android-Apps durch die Festlegung wichtiger Leistungsindikatoren (KPI) wie App-Startzeit, Frame-Renderzeit, Speicherfootprint und Batterieverbrauch, um einen reibungslosen Betrieb über verschiedene Gerätespezifikationen hinweg zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Permite uma análise profunda e otimização do desempenho do aplicativo Android, estabelecendo KPIs importantes, como tempo de inicialização do aplicativo, tempo de renderização de frames, pegada de memória e consumo de bateria, garantindo uma operação suave em diferentes especificações de dispositivos.","ru":"Позволяет провести глубокий анализ и оптимизацию производительности приложения Android, устанавливая ключевые KPI, такие как время запуска приложения, время рендеринга кадров, размер памяти и потребление батареи, обеспечивая плавную работу на различных устройствах.","ar":"يسمح بالتحليل العميق وضبط أداء تطبيقات نظام التشغيل أندرويد من خلال وضع معايير أساسية مثل وقت تشغيل التطبيق ووقت عرض الإطارات ومتطلبات الذاكرة واستهلاك البطارية، مما يضمن تشغيلًا سلسًا عبر مواصفات أجهزة متنوعة."},"useCases":{"en":["Profiling frame render times to eliminate UI jank","Optimizing memory usage for low-end Android devices","Benchmarking battery consumption during intensive app operations","Establishing performance baselines for app launch sequences"],"zh":["通过分析帧渲染时间来消除UI卡顿","优化低端Android设备的内存使用","在集约的应用操作期间基准测试电池消耗","为应用启动序列建立性能基线"],"ja":["UIのジャンクを除去するためにフレームレンダリング時間を分析する","低エンドAndroidデバイスのメモリ使用量を最適化する","集中的なアプリ操作中にバッテリー消費をベンチマークする","アプリの起動シーケンスのパフォーマンスベースラインを確立する"],"ko":["UI 잔상 제거를 위해 프레임 렌더링 시간 분석하기","저사양 안드로이드 기기의 메모리 사용량 최적화","집중적인 앱 작동 중 배터리 소비량 벤치마크","애플리케이션 시작 시퀀스의 성능 기준점 설정"],"es":["Crear perfiles de tiempos de renderizado de frames para eliminar la interrupción de la interfaz de usuario","Optimizar el uso de memoria para dispositivos Android de gama baja","Realizar pruebas de referencia del consumo de batería durante operaciones de aplicaciones intensivas","Establecer líneas de base de rendimiento para secuencias de inicio de aplicaciones"],"fr":["Profiler les temps de rendu des frames pour éliminer les interruptions de l''interface utilisateur","Optimiser l''utilisation de la mémoire pour les appareils Android bas de gamme","Référencer la consommation de batterie lors d''opérations d''applications intensives","Établir des lignes de base de performance pour les séquences de lancement d''applications"],"de":["Erstellen von Profilen für Frame-Renderzeiten, um Benutzeroberflächen-Ruckler zu eliminieren","Optimieren des Speicherverbrauchs für Android-Geräte der niedrigsten Klasse","Durchführen von Benchmark-Tests für den Batterieverbrauch während intensiver App-Operationen","Festlegen von Leistungsgrundlinien für App-Startsequenzen"],"pt":["Criar perfis de tempos de renderização de frames para eliminar o problema de UI jank","Otimizar o uso de memória para dispositivos Android de baixo custo","Realizar testes de benchmark de consumo de bateria durante operações intensivas do aplicativo","Estabelecer linhas de base de desempenho para sequências de inicialização do aplicativo"],"ru":["Создание профилей времени рендеринга кадров для устранения проблемы UI jank","Оптимизация использования памяти для устройств Android с низкой производительностью","Проведение тестов производительности потребления батареи во время интенсивных операций приложения","Установление базовых показателей производительности для последовательностей запуска приложения"],"ar":["إنشاء ملفات تعريف لأوقات عرض الإطارات لإزالة مشكلة جанк الواجهة","تحسين استخدام الذاكرة للأجهزة التي تعمل بنظام التشغيل أندرويد منخفضة التكلفة","إجراء اختبارات لاستهلاك البطارية خلال عمليات التطبيق المكثفة","وضع معايير أساسية للأداء لتسلسلات تشغيل التطبيق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Android platform specific","Requires access to performance monitoring tools","Needs device profiling capabilities"],"zh":["仅限Android平台","需要访问性能监测工具","需要设备配置能力"],"ja":["Androidプラットフォーム専用","パフォーマンスモニタリングツールへのアクセスが必要","デバイスプロファイリング機能が必要"],"ko":["안드로이드 플랫폼 전용","성능 모니터링 툴에 대한 액세스가 필요","기기 프로파일링 기능이 필요"],"es":["Específico de la plataforma Android","Requiere acceso a herramientas de monitoreo de rendimiento","Necesita capacidades de perfilado de dispositivos"],"fr":["Spécifique à la plate-forme Android","Nécessite un accès aux outils de surveillance des performances","Nécessite des capacités de profilage d''appareils"],"de":["Spezifisch für die Android-Plattform","Benötigt Zugriff auf Leistungsüberwachungstools","Benötigt Geräte-Profiling-Funktionen"],"pt":["Específico da plataforma Android","Requer acesso a ferramentas de monitoramento de desempenho","Necessita de capacidades de perfil do dispositivo"],"ru":["Специфичен для платформы Android","Требует доступа к инструментам мониторинга производительности","Требует возможностей профилирования устройства"],"ar":["محدد لمنصة نظام التشغيل أندرويد","يتطلب الوصول إلى أدوات مراقبة الأداء","يحتاج إلى إمكانيات تصفية الجهاز"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":25}');
