l futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"zh":["支持RWA资产、加密货币、股票和指数","最高1000倍杠杆","自定义oracle","虚拟AMM","TWAP平滑"],"ja":["RWAアセット、暗号資産、株式、指数をサポート","最大1000倍のレバレッジ","カスタムオラクル","バーチャルAMM","TWAPスムージング"],"ko":["RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식, 지수를 지원","최대 1000배 레버리지","사용자 지정 오라클","가상 AMM","TWAP 스무딩"],"es":["Apalancamiento de hasta 1000x","Vault de liquidez centralizado","Oracle personalizado","AMM virtual","Suavizado de TWAP"],"fr":["Effet de levier allant jusqu''à 1000x","Vault de liquidité centralisé","Oracle personnalisé","AMM virtuel","Lissage de TWAP"],"de":["Hebel von bis zu 1000x","Zentraler Liquiditäts-Vault","Benutzerdefinierter Oracle","Virtueller AMM","TWAP-Glättung"],"pt":["Suporte a ativos RWA, criptomoedas, ações e índices","Posições alavancadas com até 1000x","Caixa de liquidez centralizada","Preços combinados com oracle personalizado, Virtual AMM e suavização TWAP"],"ru":["Поддержка активов RWA, криптовалют, акций и индексов","Левериджные позиции до 1000х","Центральная ликвидная ячейка","Цены, объединенные с индивидуальным оракулом, Virtual AMM и сглаживанием TWAP"],"ar":["دعم الأصول RWA والعملات المشفرة والأسهم والمؤشرات","مراكز مالية مع معاملات تصل إلى 1000 مرة","خزان سيولة مركزي","أسعار مجزأة مع أوراكل مخصص و AMM افتراضي وتحسين TWAP"]},"keywords":{"zh":["合成永续期货协议","RWA资产","加密货币","股票","指数","杠杆","自定义oracle","虚拟AMM","TWAP平滑"],"ja":["合成永続先物プロトコル","RWAアセット","暗号資産","株式","指数","レバレッジ","カスタムオラクル","バーチャルAMM","TWAPスムージング"],"ko":["합성 영속 선물 프로토콜","RWA 자산","암호화폐","주식","지수","레버리지","사용자 지정 오라클","가상 AMM","TWAP 스무딩"],"es":["protocolo de futuros sintéticos","trading descentralizado","apalancamiento","oracle personalizado","AMM virtual","TWAP","stablecoins","criptomonedas"],"fr":["protocole de futures synthétiques","trading décentralisé","effet de levier","oracle personnalisé","AMM virtuel","TWAP","stablecoins","cryptomonnaies"],"de":["synthetisches Futures-Protokoll","dezentrales Trading","Hebel","benutzerdefinierter Oracle","virtueller AMM","TWAP","Stablecoins","Kryptowährungen"],"pt":["futuros sintéticos perpétuos","ativos RWA","criptomoedas","ações","índices","posições alavancadas","caixa de liquidez centralizada"],"ru":["синтетические вечные фьючерсы","активы RWA","криптовалюты","акции","индексы","левериджные позиции","центральная ликвидная ячейка"],"ar":["المشتقات المالية المستمرة","الأصول RWA","العملات المشفرة","الأسهم","المؤشرات","المراكز المالية","خزان السيولة المركزي"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"specification","description":"Complete technical specification for Conventional Commits with all formal rules and requirements.","bodyPreview":"# Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0\n\n## Specification\n\nThe key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\" in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2119.txt).\n\n### Rule 1: Type Prefix\nCommits **MUST** be prefixed with a type, which consists of a noun, `feat`, `fix`, etc., followed by the OPTIONAL scope, OPTIONAL `!`, and REQUIRED terminal colon and space.\n\n###","body":"# Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0\n\n## Specification\n\nThe key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\", \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and \"OPTIONAL\" in this document are to be interpreted as described in [RFC 2119](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2119.txt).\n\n### Rule 1: Type Prefix\nCommits **MUST** be prefixed with a type, which consists of a noun, `feat`, `fix`, etc., followed by the OPTIONAL scope, OPTIONAL `!`, and REQUIRED terminal colon and space.\n\n### Rule 2: Feature Type\nThe type `feat` **MUST** be used when a commit adds a new feature to your application or library.\n\n### Rule 3: Fix Type\nThe type `fix` **MUST** be used when a commit represents a bug fix for your application.\n\n### Rule 4: Scope\nA scope **MAY** be provided after a type. A scope **MUST** consist of a noun describing a section of the codebase surrounded by parenthesis, e.g., `fix(parser):`\n\n### Rule 5: Description\nA description **MUST** immediately follow the colon and space after the type/scope prefix. The description is a short summary of the code changes, e.g., *fix: array parsing issue when multiple spaces were contained in string*.\n\n**Requirements for Description:**\n- Typically 50 characters or less\n- Starts with lowercase letter (unless scope uses parenthesis)\n- Written in imperative mood: \"add\" not \"added\" or \"adds\"\n- No period at the end\n\n### Rule 6: Body\nA longer commit body **MAY** be provided after the short description, providing additional contextual information about the code changes. The body **MUST** begin one blank line after the description.\n\n### Rule 7: Body Format\nA commit body is free-form and **MAY** consist of any number of newline-separated paragraphs.\n\n### Rule 8: Footers\nOne or more footers **MAY** be provided one blank line after the body. Each footer **MUST** consist of a word token, followed by either a `:<space>` or `<space>#` separator, followed by a string value (this is inspired by the [git trailer convention](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-interpret-trailers)).\n\n### Rule 9: Footer Token\nA footer''s token **MUST** use `-` in place of whitespace characters, e.g., `Acked-by` (this helps differentiate the footer section from a multi-paragraph body). An exception is made for `BREAKING CHANGE`, which **MAY** also be used as a token.\n\n### Rule 10: Footer Value\nA footer''s value **MAY** contain spaces and newlines, and parsing **MUST** terminate when the next valid footer token/separator pair is observed.\n\n### Rule 11: Breaking Changes Indication\nBreaking changes **MUST** be indicated in the type/scope prefix of a commit, or as an entry in the footer.\n\n### Rule 12: Breaking Change Footer\nIf included as a footer, a breaking change **MUST** consist of the uppercase text `BREAKING CHANGE`, followed by a colon, space, and description, e.g., *BREAKING CHANGE: environment variables now take precedence over config files*.\n\n### Rule 13: Breaking Change Prefix\nIf included in the type/scope prefix, breaking changes **MUST** be indicated by a `!` immediately before the `:`. If `!` is used, `BREAKING CHANGE:` **MAY** be omitted from the footer section, and the commit description **SHALL** be used to describe the breaking change.\n\n### Rule 14: Custom Types\nTypes other than `feat` and `fix` **MAY** be used in your commit messages, e.g., *docs: update ref docs.*\n\nRecommended additional types:\n- `build`: Changes to build system or external dependencies\n- `chore`: Changes to build process, dependencies, or tooling\n- `ci`: Changes to CI/CD configuration\n- `docs`: Documentation only changes\n- `style`: Changes that don''t affect code meaning (formatting, semicolons, etc.)\n- `refactor`: Code refactoring without feature or bug fix changes\n- `perf`: Code change that improves performance\n- `test`: Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests\n\n### Rule 15: Case Sensitivity\nThe units of information that make up Conventional Commits **MUST NOT** be treated as case sensitive by implementors, with the exception of `BREAKING CHANGE` which **MUST** be uppercase.\n\n### Rule 16: Breaking Change Synonym\n`BREAKING-CHANGE` **MUST** be synonymous with `BREAKING CHANGE`, when used as a token in a footer.\n\n## Formal Grammar\n\n```\n<commit> ::= <header>\n             <BLANK LINE>?\n             <body>?\n             <BLANK LINE>?\n             <footer>*\n\n<header> ::= <type> \"[\" <scope> \"]\" <breaking>? \":\" <space> <description>\n          | <type> <breaking>? \":\" <space> <description>\n\n<type> ::= \"feat\"\n        | \"fix\"\n        | \"chore\"\n        | \"docs\"\n        | \"style\"\n        | \"refactor\"\n        | \"perf\"\n        | \"test\"\n        | \"ci\"\n        | \"build\"\n        | <string>\n\n<scope> ::= <string>\n\n<breaking> ::= \"!\"\n\n<description> ::= <string>\n\n<body> ::= <string>\n\n<footer> ::= <token> (\":\" <space> | <space> \"#\") <value>\n\n<token> ::= <string-with-hyphens>\n\n<value> ::= <string-with-optional-newlines>\n\n<string> ::= <non-empty character sequence>\n\n<space> ::= \" \"\n\n<BLANK LINE> ::= \"\\n\"\n```\n\n## Intent of Conventional Commits\n\nThe intent of the Conventional Commits specification is to provide a lightweight convention on top of commit messages. This convention:\n\n1. Allows easy to parse commit history\n2. Enables automatic changelog generation\n3. Allows automatic semantic versioning determination\n4. Communicates the nature of changes to teammates, the public, and other stakeholders\n5. Allows tooling to trigger build and publish processes\n6. Makes it easier for people to contribute to your projects by allowing them to explore a more structured commit history\n\n## Semantic Versioning Relationship\n\n| Conventional Commit | Semantic Version Impact |\n|-------------------|------------------------|\n| `fix` type | `PATCH` release |\n| `feat` type | `MINOR` release |\n| `BREAKING CHANGE` (any type) | `MAJOR` release |\n| Other types (`docs`, `style`, etc.) | Development only, no version bump |\n\n## Relationship to SemVer\n\nThe Conventional Commits specification builds on top of [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/) (SemVer). SemVer uses three-part version numbers: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, where:\n- **MAJOR** indicates incompatible API changes (breaking changes)\n- **MINOR** indicates new functionality in a backwards compatible manner\n- **PATCH** indicates backwards compatible bug fixes\n\nConventional Commits provide a structured way to communicate which type of change is being made, enabling automated tools to determine the appropriate SemVer version bump.\n\n## Extensibility\n\nWhile the Conventional Commits specification defines the core types (`feat` and `fix`), projects may define additional types suited to their needs. The specification allows flexibility to extend beyond the core types while maintaining machine-readability.\n\n---\n\n**License**: [Creative Commons - CC BY 3.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/)\n\nSource: [Conventional Commits v1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:28:54.672Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents requiring precise commit message formatting, such as those using Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0","zh":"适合需要精确提交消息格式的AI代理，例如使用Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0的代理","ja":"Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0を使用するなど、正確なコミットメッセージ形式が必要なAIエージェントに適しています","ko":"정확한 커밋 메시지 형식이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. 예를 들어 Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0을 사용하는 에이전트","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que requieren un formato de mensaje de confirmación preciso, como aquellos que utilizan la especificación Conventional Commits v1.0.0","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA nécessitant un formatage de message de commit précis, tels que ceux utilisant la spécification Conventional Commits v1.0.0","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die ein präzises Commit-Nachrichten-Formatierung benötigen, wie z.B. solche, die die Conventional Commits-Spezifikation v1.0.0 verwenden","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que requerem formatação precisa de mensagens de commit, como aqueles que usam a Especificação de Commits Convencionais v1.0.0","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, требующих точного форматирования сообщений о коммитах, таких как те, которые используют Спецификацию конвенциональных коммитов v1.0.0","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يتطلب تنسيقًا دقيقًا لرسائل Commit، مثل تلك التي تستخدم مواصفة Commits التقليدية v1.0.0"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce standardized commit messages using RFC 2119 guidelines, ensuring consistency and clarity in version control systems, and supporting features like type prefixing with nouns like ''feat'' and ''fix''","zh":"赋予代理使用RFC 2119指南强制执行标准化提交消息的能力，确保版本控制系统的一致性和清晰度，并支持使用''feat''和''fix''等名词的类型前缀等功能","ja":"RFC 2119のガイドラインを使用して標準化されたコミットメッセージを適用する機能をエージェントに与え、バージョン管理システムの的一貫性と明確性を確保し、''feat''や''fix''などの名詞を使用したタイプのプレフィックスなどの機能をサポートする","ko":"RFC 2119 가이드라인을 사용하여 표준화된 커밋 메시지를 적용할 수 있는 기능을 에이전트에 부여하여 버전 관리 시스템의 일관성과 명확성을 보장하며, ''feat'' 및 ''fix''와 같은 명사를 사용한 类型 접두사와 같은 기능을 지원합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar mensajes de confirmación estandarizados utilizando las pautas de RFC 2119, garantizando la consistencia y la claridad en los sistemas de control de versiones y admitiendo características como el prefijo de tipo con sustantivos como ''feat'' y ''fix''","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des messages de commit standardisés en utilisant les directives de la RFC 2119, garantissant la cohérence et la clarté dans les systèmes de contrôle de version et prenant en charge des fonctionnalités comme le préfixe de type avec des noms comme ''feat'' et ''fix''","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, standardisierte Commit-Nachrichten mit den Richtlinien von RFC 2119 zu erzwingen, um Konsistenz und Klarheit in Versionskontrollsystemen sicherzustellen und Funktionen wie Typ-Präfixe mit Substantiven wie ''feat'' und ''fix'' zu unterstützen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor mensagens de commit padronizadas usando as diretrizes do RFC 2119, garantindo consistência e clareza nos sistemas de controle de versão e suportando recursos como prefixo de tipo com substantivos como ''feat'' e ''fix''","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать стандартизированные сообщения о коммитах с помощью руководящих принципов RFC 2119, гарантируя последовательность и ясность в системах контроля версий и поддерживая функции, такие как префикс типа с существительными, такими как ''feat'' и ''fix''","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من فرض رسائل Commit معيارية باستخدام إرشادات RFC 2119، مما يضمن الاتساق والوضوح في أنظمة التحكم في الإصدار ودعم الميزات مثل بادئة النوع مع الأسماء مثل ''feat'' و ''fix''"},"useCases":{"en":["Standardizing commit messages for collaborative projects","Automating commit validation for CI/CD pipelines","Generating changelogs based on commit history"],"zh":["为协作项目标准化提交消息","为CI/CD流水线自动提交验证","根据提交历史生成变更日志"],"ja":["コラボレーションプロジェクトのコミットメッセージを標準化する","CI/CDパイプラインの自動コミット検証","コミット履歴に基づいて変更ログを生成する"],"ko":["협업 프로젝트를 위한 커밋 메시지 표준화","CI/CD 파이프라인을 위한 자동 커밋 검증","커밋 기록을 기반으로 변경 로그 생성"],"es":["Estandarizar mensajes de confirmación para proyectos colaborativos","Automatizar la validación de commits para tuberías de CI/CD","Generar registros de cambios en función del historial de commits"],"fr":["Standardiser les messages de commit pour les projets collaboratifs","Automatiser la validation des commits pour les pipelines de CI/CD","Générer des journaux des modifications en fonction de l''historique des commits"],"de":["Standardisieren von Commit-Nachrichten für kollaborative Projekte","Automatisieren der Commit-Validierung für CI/CD-Pipelines","Erstellen von Änderungsprotokollen auf der Grundlage der Commit-Historie"],"pt":["Padronizar mensagens de commit para projetos colaborativos","Automatizar validação de commit para pipelines de CI/CD","Gerar registros de alterações com base no histórico de commit"],"ru":["Стандартизировать сообщения о коммитах для совместных проектов","Автоматизировать проверку коммитов для конвейеров CI/CD","Генерировать журналы изменений на основе истории коммитов"],"ar":["توحيد رسائل Commit للمشاريع التعاونية","تحويل صحة Commit إلى تلقائية لخطوط أنابيب CI/CD","توليد سجلات التغييرات بناءً على تاريخ Commit"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0","Limited to version control systems supporting commit messages"],"zh":["需要遵守Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0","仅限于支持提交消息的版本控制系统"],"ja":["Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0に準拠する必要がある","コミットメッセージをサポートするバージョン管理システムのみ"],"ko":["Conventional Commits Specification v1.0.0을遵守해야 함","커밋 메시지를 지원하는 버전 관리 시스템에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la adhesión a la especificación Conventional Commits v1.0.0","Limitado a sistemas de control de versiones que admiten mensajes de confirmación"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion à la spécification Conventional Commits v1.0.0","Limité aux systèmes de contrôle de version prenant en charge les messages de commit"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung der Conventional Commits-Spezifikation v1.0.0","Begrenzt auf Versionskontrollsysteme, die Commit-Nachrichten unterstützen"],"pt":["Exige aderência à Especificação de Commits Convencionais v1.0.0","Limitado a sistemas de controle de versão que suportam mensagens de commit"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения Спецификации конвенциональных коммитов v1.0.0","Ограничен для систем контроля версий, поддерживающих сообщения о коммитах"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بمواصفة Commits التقليدية v1.0.0","محدود لأنظمة التحكم في الإصدار التي تدعم رسائل Commit"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
