дка распределенных систем","Анализ дампов краха и стек-трасс","Оптимизация приложений"],"ar":["نهج منهجي للتصحيح","أدوات قوية لتحديد المشكلات","تحليل الأداء و الذاكرة","التصحيح الأنظمة الموزعة","تحليل مجمعات الحوادث و مسارات المكدس","تحسين التطبيقات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["调试策略","代码错误","开发效率","代码质量","系统地解决问题","强大的工具"],"ja":["デバッグ戦略","コードのエラー","開発効率","コード品質","体系的に問題を解決","強力なツール"],"ko":["디버깅 전략","코드 오류","개발 효율성","코드 품질","체계적으로 문제를 해결","강력한 도구"],"es":["depuración de código","estrategias de depuración","herramientas de depuración","análisis de rendimiento","solución de problemas","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["débogage de code","stratégies de débogage","outils de débogage","analyse de performances","résolution de problèmes","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Code-Debugging","Debugging-Strategien","Debugging-Tools","Leistungsanalyse","Fehlerbehebung","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["depuração de código","estratégias de depuração","ferramentas de depuração","análise de desempenho","depuração de sistemas distribuídos","otimização de aplicativos","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software"],"ru":["отладка кода","стратегии отладки","инструменты отладки","анализ производительности","отладка распределенных систем","оптимизация приложений","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تصحيح الكود","استراتيجيات التصحيح","أدوات التصحيح","تحليل الأداء","التصحيح الأنظمة الموزعة","تحسين التطبيقات","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"ki2pixel","repo":"render_signal_server","repoPath":"ki2pixel/render_signal_server","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"debugging-strategies","description":"Master systematic debugging techniques, profiling tools, and root cause analysis to efficiently track down bugs across any codebase or technology stack. Use when investigating bugs, performance issues, or unexpected behavior.","bodyPreview":"# Debugging Strategies\n\nTransform debugging from frustrating guesswork into systematic problem-solving with proven strategies, powerful tools, and methodical approaches.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Tracking down elusive bugs\n- Investigating performance issues\n- Understanding unfamiliar codebases\n- Debugging production issues\n- Analyzing crash dumps and stack traces\n- Profiling application performance\n- Investigating memory leaks\n- Debugging distributed systems\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. The S","body":"# Debugging Strategies\n\nTransform debugging from frustrating guesswork into systematic problem-solving with proven strategies, powerful tools, and methodical approaches.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Tracking down elusive bugs\n- Investigating performance issues\n- Understanding unfamiliar codebases\n- Debugging production issues\n- Analyzing crash dumps and stack traces\n- Profiling application performance\n- Investigating memory leaks\n- Debugging distributed systems\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. The Scientific Method\n\n**1. Observe**: What''s the actual behavior?\n**2. Hypothesize**: What could be causing it?\n**3. Experiment**: Test your hypothesis\n**4. Analyze**: Did it prove/disprove your theory?\n**5. Repeat**: Until you find the root cause\n\n### 2. Debugging Mindset\n\n**Don''t Assume:**\n- \"It can''t be X\" - Yes it can\n- \"I didn''t change Y\" - Check anyway\n- \"It works on my machine\" - Find out why\n\n**Do:**\n- Reproduce consistently\n- Isolate the problem\n- Keep detailed notes\n- Question everything\n- Take breaks when stuck\n\n### 3. Rubber Duck Debugging\n\nExplain your code and problem out loud (to a rubber duck, colleague, or yourself). Often reveals the issue.\n\n## Systematic Debugging Process\n\n### Phase 1: Reproduce\n\n```markdown\n## Reproduction Checklist\n\n1. **Can you reproduce it?**\n   - Always? Sometimes? Randomly?\n   - Specific conditions needed?\n   - Can others reproduce it?\n\n2. **Create minimal reproduction**\n   - Simplify to smallest example\n   - Remove unrelated code\n   - Isolate the problem\n\n3. **Document steps**\n   - Write down exact steps\n   - Note environment details\n   - Capture error messages\n```\n\n### Phase 2: Gather Information\n\n```markdown\n## Information Collection\n\n1. **Error Messages**\n   - Full stack trace\n   - Error codes\n   - Console/log output\n\n2. **Environment**\n   - OS version\n   - Language/runtime version\n   - Dependencies versions\n   - Environment variables\n\n3. **Recent Changes**\n   - Git history\n   - Deployment timeline\n   - Configuration changes\n\n4. **Scope**\n   - Affects all users or specific ones?\n   - All browsers or specific ones?\n   - Production only or also dev?\n```\n\n### Phase 3: Form Hypothesis\n\n```markdown\n## Hypothesis Formation\n\nBased on gathered info, ask:\n\n1. **What changed?**\n   - Recent code changes\n   - Dependency updates\n   - Infrastructure changes\n\n2. **What''s different?**\n   - Working vs broken environment\n   - Working vs broken user\n   - Before vs after\n\n3. **Where could this fail?**\n   - Input validation\n   - Business logic\n   - Data layer\n   - External services\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Test & Verify\n\n```markdown\n## Testing Strategies\n\n1. **Binary Search**\n   - Comment out half the code\n   - Narrow down problematic section\n   - Repeat until found\n\n2. **Add Logging**\n   - Strategic console.log/print\n   - Track variable values\n   - Trace execution flow\n\n3. **Isolate Components**\n   - Test each piece separately\n   - Mock dependencies\n   - Remove complexity\n\n4. **Compare Working vs Broken**\n   - Diff configurations\n   - Diff environments\n   - Diff data\n```\n\n## Debugging Tools\n\n### JavaScript/TypeScript Debugging\n\n```typescript\n// Chrome DevTools Debugger\nfunction processOrder(order: Order) {\n    debugger;  // Execution pauses here\n\n    const total = calculateTotal(order);\n    console.log(''Total:'', total);\n\n    // Conditional breakpoint\n    if (order.items.length > 10) {\n        debugger;  // Only breaks if condition true\n    }\n\n    return total;\n}\n\n// Console debugging techniques\nconsole.log(''Value:'', value);                    // Basic\nconsole.table(arrayOfObjects);                   // Table format\nconsole.time(''operation''); /* code */ console.timeEnd(''operation'');  // Timing\nconsole.trace();                                 // Stack trace\nconsole.assert(value > 0, ''Value must be positive'');  // Assertion\n\n// Performance profiling\nperformance.mark(''start-operation'');\n// ... operation code\nperformance.mark(''end-operation'');\nperformance.measure(''operation'', ''start-operation'', ''end-operation'');\nconsole.log(performance.getEntriesByType(''measure''));\n```\n\n**VS Code Debugger Configuration:**\n```json\n// .vscode/launch.json\n{\n    \"version\": \"0.2.0\",\n    \"configurations\": [\n        {\n            \"type\": \"node\",\n            \"request\": \"launch\",\n            \"name\": \"Debug Program\",\n            \"program\": \"${workspaceFolder}/src/index.ts\",\n            \"preLaunchTask\": \"tsc: build - tsconfig.json\",\n            \"outFiles\": [\"${workspaceFolder}/dist/**/*.js\"],\n            \"skipFiles\": [\"<node_internals>/**\"]\n        },\n        {\n            \"type\": \"node\",\n            \"request\": \"launch\",\n            \"name\": \"Debug Tests\",\n            \"program\": \"${workspaceFolder}/node_modules/jest/bin/jest\",\n            \"args\": [\"--runInBand\", \"--no-cache\"],\n            \"console\": \"integratedTerminal\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n### Python Debugging\n\n```python\n# Built-in debugger (pdb)\nimport pdb\n\ndef calculate_total(items):\n    total = 0\n    pdb.set_trace()  # Debugger starts here\n\n    for item in items:\n        total += item.price * item.quantity\n\n    return total\n\n# Breakpoint (Python 3.7+)\ndef process_order(order):\n    breakpoint()  # More convenient than pdb.set_trace()\n    # ... code\n\n# Post-mortem debugging\ntry:\n    risky_operation()\nexcept Exception:\n    import pdb\n    pdb.post_mortem()  # Debug at exception point\n\n# IPython debugging (ipdb)\nfrom ipdb import set_trace\nset_trace()  # Better interface than pdb\n\n# Logging for debugging\nimport logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef fetch_user(user_id):\n    logger.debug(f''Fetching user: {user_id}'')\n    user = db.query(User).get(user_id)\n    logger.debug(f''Found user: {user}'')\n    return user\n\n# Profile performance\nimport cProfile\nimport pstats\n\ncProfile.run(''slow_function()'', ''profile_stats'')\nstats = pstats.Stats(''profile_stats'')\nstats.sort_stats(''cumulative'')\nstats.print_stats(10)  # Top 10 slowest\n```\n\n### Go Debugging\n\n```go\n// Delve debugger\n// Install: go install github.com/go-delve/delve/cmd/dlv@latest\n// Run: dlv debug main.go\n\nimport (\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"runtime\"\n    \"runtime/debug\"\n)\n\n// Print stack trace\nfunc debugStack() {\n    debug.PrintStack()\n}\n\n// Panic recovery with debugging\nfunc processRequest() {\n    defer func() {\n        if r := recover(); r != nil {\n            fmt.Println(\"Panic:\", r)\n            debug.PrintStack()\n        }\n    }()\n\n    // ... code that might panic\n}\n\n// Memory profiling\nimport _ \"net/http/pprof\"\n// Visit http://localhost:6060/debug/pprof/\n\n// CPU profiling\nimport (\n    \"os\"\n    \"runtime/pprof\"\n)\n\nf, _ := os.Create(\"cpu.prof\")\npprof.StartCPUProfile(f)\ndefer pprof.StopCPUProfile()\n// ... code to profile\n```\n\n## Advanced Debugging Techniques\n\n### Technique 1: Binary Search Debugging\n\n```bash\n# Git bisect for finding regression\ngit bisect start\ngit bisect bad                    # Current commit is bad\ngit bisect good v1.0.0            # v1.0.0 was good\n\n# Git checks out middle commit\n# Test it, then:\ngit bisect good   # if it works\ngit bisect bad    # if it''s broken\n\n# Continue until bug found\ngit bisect reset  # when done\n```\n\n### Technique 2: Differential Debugging\n\nCompare working vs broken:\n\n```markdown\n## What''s Different?\n\n| Aspect       | Working         | Broken          |\n|--------------|-----------------|-----------------|\n| Environment  | Development     | Production      |\n| Node version | 18.16.0         | 18.15.0         |\n| Data         | Empty DB        | 1M records      |\n| User         | Admin           | Regular user    |\n| Browser      | Chrome          | Safari          |\n| Time         | During day      | After midnight  |\n\nHypothesis: Time-based issue? Check timezone handling.\n```\n\n### Technique 3: Trace Debugging\n\n```typescript\n// Function call tracing\nfunction trace(target: any, propertyKey: string, descriptor: PropertyDescriptor) {\n    const originalMethod = descriptor.value;\n\n    descriptor.value = function(...args: any[]) {\n        console.log(`Calling ${propertyKey} with args:`, args);\n        const result = originalMethod.apply(this, args);\n        console.log(`${propertyKey} returned:`, result);\n        return result;\n    };\n\n    return descriptor;\n}\n\nclass OrderService {\n    @trace\n    calculateTotal(items: Item[]): number {\n        return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Technique 4: Memory Leak Detection\n\n```typescript\n// Chrome DevTools Memory Profiler\n// 1. Take heap snapshot\n// 2. Perform action\n// 3. Take another snapshot\n// 4. Compare snapshots\n\n// Node.js memory debugging\nif (process.memoryUsage().heapUsed > 500 * 1024 * 1024) {\n    console.warn(''High memory usage:'', process.memoryUsage());\n\n    // Generate heap dump\n    require(''v8'').writeHeapSnapshot();\n}\n\n// Find memory leaks in tests\nlet beforeMemory: number;\n\nbeforeEach(() => {\n    beforeMemory = process.memoryUsage().heapUsed;\n});\n\nafterEach(() => {\n    const afterMemory = process.memoryUsage().heapUsed;\n    const diff = afterMemory - beforeMemory;\n\n    if (diff > 10 * 1024 * 1024) {  // 10MB threshold\n        console.warn(`Possible memory leak: ${diff / 1024 / 1024}MB`);\n    }\n});\n```\n\n## Debugging Patterns by Issue Type\n\n### Pattern 1: Intermittent Bugs\n\n```markdown\n## Strategies for Flaky Bugs\n\n1. **Add extensive logging**\n   - Log timing information\n   - Log all state transitions\n   - Log external interactions\n\n2. **Look for race conditions**\n   - Concurrent access to shared state\n   - Async operations completing out of order\n   - Missing synchronization\n\n3. **Check timing dependencies**\n   - setTimeout/setInterval\n   - Promise resolution order\n   - Animation frame timing\n\n4. **Stress test**\n   - Run many times\n   - Vary timing\n   - Simulate load\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Performance Issues\n\n```markdown\n## Performance Debugging\n\n1. **Profile first**\n   - Don''t optimize blindly\n   - Measure before and after\n   - Find bottlenecks\n\n2. **Common culprits**\n   - N+1 queries\n   - Unnecessary re-renders\n   - Large data processing\n   - Synchronous I/O\n\n3. **Tools**\n   - Browser DevTools Performance tab\n   - Lighthouse\n   - Python: cProfile, line_profiler\n   - Node: clinic.js, 0x\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Production Bugs\n\n```markdown\n## Production Debugging\n\n1. **Gather evidence**\n   - Error tracking (Sentry, Bugsnag)\n   - Application logs\n   - User reports\n   - Metrics/monitoring\n\n2. **Reproduce locally**\n   - Use production data (anonymized)\n   - Match environment\n   - Follow exact steps\n\n3. **Safe investigation**\n   - Don''t change production\n   - Use feature flags\n   - Add monitoring/logging\n   - Test fixes in staging\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Reproduce First**: Can''t fix what you can''t reproduce\n2. **Isolate the Problem**: Remove complexity until minimal case\n3. **Read Error Messages**: They''re usually helpful\n4. **Check Recent Changes**: Most bugs are recent\n5. **Use Version Control**: Git bisect, blame, history\n6. **Take Breaks**: Fresh eyes see better\n7. **Document Findings**: Help future you\n8. **Fix Root Cause**: Not just symptoms\n\n## Common Debugging Mistakes\n\n- **Making Multiple Changes**: Change one thing at a time\n- **Not Reading Error Messages**: Read the full stack trace\n- **Assuming It''s Complex**: Often it''s simple\n- **Debug Logging in Prod**: Remove before shipping\n- **Not Using Debugger**: console.log isn''t always best\n- **Giving Up Too Soon**: Persistence pays off\n- **Not Testing the Fix**: Verify it actually works\n\n## Quick Debugging Checklist\n\n```markdown\n## When Stuck, Check:\n\n- [ ] Spelling errors (typos in variable names)\n- [ ] Case sensitivity (fileName vs filename)\n- [ ] Null/undefined values\n- [ ] Array index off-by-one\n- [ ] Async timing (race conditions)\n- [ ] Scope issues (closure, hoisting)\n- [ ] Type mismatches\n- [ ] Missing dependencies\n- [ ] Environment variables\n- [ ] File paths (absolute vs relative)\n- [ ] Cache issues (clear cache)\n- [ ] Stale data (refresh database)\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/debugging-tools-guide.md**: Comprehensive tool documentation\n- **references/performance-profiling.md**: Performance debugging guide\n- **references/production-debugging.md**: Debugging live systems\n- **assets/debugging-checklist.md**: Quick reference checklist\n- **assets/common-bugs.md**: Common bug patterns\n- **scripts/debug-helper.ts**: Debugging utility functions\n\n## Note on Documentation Paths\n\nWhen referencing documentation in this project, use the current structure:\n- `docs/access/` - Authentication and UI documentation  \n- `docs/core/` - Architecture and configuration reference\n- `docs/ingestion/` - Email ingestion (Gmail Push only, IMAP retired)\n- `docs/ops/` - Deployment, monitoring, and troubleshooting\n- `docs/processing/` - File offload, routing engine, and outbound webhooks\n\n**Current active paths:**\n- `docs/features/` → **DEPRECATED** (moved to `docs/processing/` and `docs/ingestion/`)\n- `docs/v2/` → **DEPRECATED** (consolidated into main structure)\n\n**Key references for debugging:**\n- `docs/operations/depannage.md` - Production troubleshooting\n- `docs/quality/testing.md` - Test suite structure and coverage\n- `docs/complexity_hotspots.md` - Performance bottleneck identification\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:29:31.229Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Developer Support Agents needing systematic approaches to diagnose complex software issues.","zh":"非常适合需要系统性方法来诊断复杂软件问题的开发支持代理。","ja":"複雑なソフトウェアの問題を体系的に診断する必要がある開発サポートエージェントに最適です。","ko":"複잡한 소프트웨어 문제를 체계적으로 진단해야 하는 개발 지원 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Soporte de Desarrolladores que necesitan enfoques sistemáticos para diagnosticar problemas de software complejos.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Support de Développeurs ayant besoin d''approches systématiques pour diagnostiquer des problèmes de logiciel complexes.","de":"Perfekt für Entwickler-Support-Agenten, die systematische Ansätze benötigen, um komplexe Softwareprobleme zu diagnostizieren.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Suporte de Desenvolvedores que necessitam de abordagens sistemáticas para diagnosticar problemas de software complexos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов поддержки разработчиков, которым необходимы системные подходы для диагностики сложных проблем программного обеспечения.","ar":"مثالي لعمال دعم المطورين الذين يحتاجون إلى نهج منهجي لتشخيص مشاكل البرمجيات المعقدة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform debugging from guesswork into methodical problem-solving with proven strategies for tracking down elusive bugs, analyzing crash dumps and stack traces, profiling application performance, and investigating memory leaks in distributed systems.","zh":"使代理能够将调试从猜测转变为有方法的解决问题，使用经过验证的策略来跟踪难以捉摸的错误，分析崩溃转储和堆栈跟踪，分析应用程序性能，并在分布式系统中调查内存泄漏。","ja":"エージェントがデバッグを推測から体系的な問題解決に変えることを可能にし、難しいバグを追跡し、クラッシュダンプとスタックトレースを分析し、アプリケーションのパフォーマンスを分析し、分散システムでメモリ漏れを調査するための検証済みの戦略を使用します。","ko":"에이전트가 디버깅을 추측에서 체계적인 문제 해결로 전환 할 수 있도록 해주며,難한 버그를 추적하고, 크래시 덤프 및 스택 트레이스를 분석하고, 애플리케이션 성능을 프로파일링하며, 분산 시스템에서 메모리 누수를 조사하는 검증된 전략을 사용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes transformar la depuración de errores de un trabajo de adivinanza en una resolución de problemas metódica con estrategias probadas para rastrear errores difíciles de detectar, analizar volcados de memoria y trazas de pila, perfilar el rendimiento de la aplicación y investigar fugas de memoria en sistemas distribuidos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer le débogage d''un travail de devinette en une résolution de problèmes méthodique avec des stratégies éprouvées pour traquer des bogues insidieux, analyser les dumps de crash et les traces de pile, profiler les performances de l''application et enquêter sur les fuites de mémoire dans les systèmes distribués.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, das Debuggen von Fehlern von einem Rätselfall in eine methodische Problemlösung mit bewährten Strategien für die Verfolgung von schwer zu findenden Fehlern, Analyse von Absturzspeicherabbildern und Stack-Traces, Profiling der Anwendungsleistung und Untersuchung von Speicherlecks in verteilten Systemen umzuwandeln.","pt":"Permite que os agentes transformem a depuração de suposições em resolução de problemas metodológica com estratégias comprovadas para rastrear bugs difíceis de encontrar, analisar dumps de crash e rastros de pilha, perfil de desempenho de aplicativos e investigar vazamentos de memória em sistemas distribuídos.","ru":"Позволяет агентам преобразовать отладку из предположений в методическое решение проблем с помощью проверенных стратегий для отслеживания неуловимых багов, анализа дампов аварий и трассировок стека, профилирования производительности приложений и расследования утечек памяти в распределенных системах.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تحويل عملية تصحيح الأخطاء من افتراضات إلى حل منهجي للمشكلات باستخدام استراتيجيات متقنة لتعقب أخطاء مراوغة وتحليل ملفات تصادم وحفظ مسارات، وتحليل أداء التطبيقات والتحقيق في تسربات الذاكرة في الأنظمة الموزعة."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging production issues","Investigating performance bottlenecks","Analyzing crash dump files","Tracking down memory leaks","Debugging distributed system failures"],"zh":["生产问题调试","性能瓶颈调查","崩溃转储文件分析","内存泄漏跟踪","分布式系统故障调试"],"ja":["生产問題のデバッグ","パフォーマンスボトルネックの調査","クラッシュダンプファイルの分析","メモリ漏れの追跡","分散システムの故障デバッグ"],"ko":["生产 문제 디버깅","성능 병목 현상 조사","크래시 덤프 파일 분석","메모리 누수 추적","분산 시스템故障 디버깅"],"es":["Depuración de problemas de producción","Investigación de cuellos de botella de rendimiento","Análisis de archivos de volcado de memoria","Rastreo de fugas de memoria","Depuración de fallos del sistema distribuido"],"fr":["Débogage des problèmes de production","Enquête sur les goulots d''étranglement des performances","Analyse des fichiers de dump de crash","Traçage des fuites de mémoire","Débogage des défaillances du système distribué"],"de":["Debuggen von Produktionsproblemen","Untersuchung von Leistungsbottlenecks","Analyse von Absturzspeicherabbildern","Verfolgung von Speicherlecks","Debuggen von Fehlern in verteilten Systemen"],"pt":["Depuração de problemas de produção","Investigação de gargalos de desempenho","Análise de arquivos de dump de crash","Rastreamento de vazamentos de memória","Depuração de falhas de sistemas distribuídos"],"ru":["Отладка проблем производства","Расследование узких мест производительности","Анализ файлов дампов аварий","Отслеживание утечек памяти","Отладка сбоев распределенных систем"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء الإنتاج","تحقيق عيوب الأداء","تحليل ملفات تصادم","متابعة تسربات الذاكرة","تصحيح أخطاء الفشل في الأنظمة الموزعة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to system logs and diagnostics","Performance profiling requires runtime access","Distributed debugging needs system interconnectivity"],"zh":["需要访问系统日志和诊断","性能分析需要运行时访问","分布式调试需要系统互联"],"ja":["システムログと診断へのアクセスが必要","パフォーマンス分析には実行時アクセスが必要","分散デバッグにはシステムの相互接続が必要"],"ko":["시스템 로그 및 진단에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다.","성능 프로파일링에는 런타임 액세스가 필요합니다.","분산 디버깅에는 시스템 상호 연결이 필요합니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a registros y diagnósticos del sistema","El perfilado del rendimiento requiere acceso en tiempo de ejecución","La depuración distribuida requiere interconexión del sistema"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux journaux et diagnostics du système","Le profilage des performances nécessite un accès à l''exécution","Le débogage distribué nécessite l''interconnectivité du système"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Systemprotokolle und -diagnosen","Leistungsprofilierung erfordert Laufzeit-Zugriff","Verteilte Fehlersuche benötigt System-Interkonnektivität"],"pt":["Requer acesso a logs do sistema e de diagnóstico","Perfil de desempenho requer acesso em tempo de execução","Depuração distribuída precisa de interconexão de sistemas"],"ru":["Требует доступа к журналам системы и диагностики","Профилирование производительности требует доступа во время выполнения","Распределенная отладка требует системной взаимосвязи"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى سجلات النظام والتشخيص","تحليل الأداء يتطلب الوصول في وقت التشغيل","التصحيح الموزع يحتاج إلى اتصال الأنظمة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('joolbits/slabbed/slabbed-compat-safety-contract', 'community', 'joolbits', 'slabbed', 'joolbits/slabbed', 'slabbed-compat-safety-contract', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z', '2026-02-18T12:29:36.420Z', NULL, '{"id":"joolbits/slabbed/slabbed-compat-safety-contract","name":"slabbed-compat-safety-contract","description":{"zh":"Slabbed兼容性安全合约是一种确保模组包中Slabbed模组安全性和可预测性的机制","ja":"Slabbedの互換性安全契約は、モッドパックの中でSlabbedモッドの安全性と予測可能性を確保するメカニズムです","ko":"슬래브 호환성 안전 계약은 모드팩에서 슬래브 모드의 안전성과 예측 가능성을 보장하는 메커니즘입니다","es":"Slabbed es un contrato de seguridad de compatibilidad que mantiene la seguridad y la previsibilidad en modpacks","fr":"Slabbed est un contrat de sécurité de compatibilité qui maintient la sécurité et la prévisibilité dans les modpacks","de":"Slabbed ist ein Kompatibilitätssicherheitsvertrag, der die Sicherheit und Vorhersehbarkeit in Modpacks gewährleistet","pt":"O Slabbed Compat é um contrato de segurança que visa manter o Slabbed seguro e previsível em modpacks, evitando quebras nas regras de colocação e sobrevivência do vanilla","ru":"Slabbed Compat - это контракт безопасности, целью которого является поддержание Slabbed в безопасности и предсказуемости в модпаках, избегая нарушений правил размещения и выживания в vanilla","ar":"Slabbed Compat هو عقد سلامة يهدف إلى الحفاظ على Slabbed آمنًا ومتوقعًا في حزم التعديل، وتجنب كسر القواعد الأساسية لوضع وتنبؤ البقاء","en":"Put things on slabs!"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Slabbed兼容性安全合约","ja":"スラブ化の互換性安全契約","ko":"슬래브 호환성 안전 계약","es":"Slabbed: Contrato de seguridad de compatibilidad","fr":"Slabbed : Contrat de sécurité de compatibilité","de":"Slabbed: Kompatibilitätssicherheitsvertrag","pt":"Slabbed Compat: Contrato de Segurança para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Slabbed Compat: Контракт Безопасности для Разработчиков","ar":"Slabbed Compat: عقد سلامة للمطورين","en":"slabbed-compat-safety-contract"},"description":{"zh":"Slabbed兼容性安全合约是一种确保模组包中Slabbed模组安全性和可预测性的机制","ja":"Slabbedの互換性安全契約は、モッドパックの中でSlabbedモッドの安全性と予測可能性を確保するメカニズムです","ko":"슬래브 호환성 안전 계약은 모드팩에서 슬래브 모드의 안전성과 예측 가능성을 보장하는 메커니즘입니다","es":"Slabbed es un contrato de seguridad de compatibilidad que mantiene la seguridad y la previsibilidad en modpacks","fr":"Slabbed est un contrat de sécurité de compatibilité qui maintient la sécurité et la prévisibilité dans les modpacks","de":"Slabbed ist ein Kompatibilitätssicherheitsvertrag, der die Sicherheit und Vorhersehbarkeit in Modpacks gewährleistet","pt":"O Slabbed Compat é um contrato de segurança que visa manter o Slabbed seguro e previsível em modpacks, evitando quebras nas regras de colocação e sobrevivênc...","ru":"Slabbed Compat - это контракт безопасности, целью которого является поддержание Slabbed в безопасности и предсказуемости в модпаках, избегая нарушений правил...","ar":"Slabbed Compat هو عقد سلامة يهدف إلى الحفاظ على Slabbed آمنًا ومتوقعًا في حزم التعديل، وتجنب كسر القواعد الأساسية لوضع وتنبؤ البقاء","en":"Put things on slabs!"},"definition":{"en":"Put things on slabs!"},"features":{"zh":["确保模组包中Slabbed模组的安全性","防止破坏vanilla规则","避免全局钩子","仅扩展顶部支持","不保证与所有模组兼容","不处理特殊块"],"ja":["モッドパックの中でSlabbedモッドの安全性を確保する","vanillaルールの破壊を防ぐ","グローバルフックを避ける","トップサポートのみを拡張する","すべてのモッドとの互換性を保証しない","特別なブロックを処理しない"],"ko":["모드팩에서 슬래브 모드의 안전성을 보장한다","바닐라 규칙을破坏하지 않는다","전역 훅을 피한다","최상단 지원만 확장한다","모든 모드와의 호환성을 보장하지 않는다","특별한 블록을 처리하지 않는다"],"es":["Mantiene la seguridad y la previsibilidad en modpacks","No rompe las reglas de colocación/supervivencia de vanilla","No asume que todos los bloques parciales se comportan como losas","Evita ganchos globales que cambian comportamientos no relacionados","Soporta la extensión de la losa solo para bloques de vanilla"],"fr":["Maintient la sécurité et la prévisibilité dans les modpacks","Ne rompt pas les règles de placement/survie de vanilla","Ne suppose pas que tous les blocs partiels se comportent comme des dalles","Évite les crochets globaux qui changent les comportements non liés","Prend en charge l''extension de la dalle uniquement pour les blocs de vanilla"],"de":["Hält die Sicherheit und Vorhersehbarkeit in Modpacks aufrecht","Verletzt nicht die Platzierungs-/Überlebensregeln von Vanilla","Geht nicht davon aus, dass alle teilweise Blöcke wie Platten funktionieren","Vermeidet globale Hooks, die nicht verwandtes Verhalten ändern","Unterstützt die Erweiterung der Platte nur für Vanilla-Blöcke"],"pt":["Manter o Slabbed seguro e previsível em modpacks","Evitar quebras nas regras de colocação e sobrevivência do vanilla","Não assumir comportamento de blocos parciais como slabs","Evitar ganchos globais que alteram comportamentos não relacionados","Extender suporte apenas para blocos de topo"],"ru":["Поддержание Slabbed в безопасности и предсказуемости в модпаках","Избежание нарушений правил размещения и выживания в vanilla","Не предположение поведения частичных блоков как слэбов","Избежание глобальных хуков, изменяющих не связанное поведение","Расширение поддержки только для блоков верхней части"],"ar":["الحفاظ على Slabbed آمنًا ومتوقعًا في حزم التعديل","تجنب كسر القواعد الأساسية لوضع وتنبؤ البقاء","عدم افتراض سلوك الكتل الجزئية كما لو كانت ألواح","تجنب البرامج النصية العالمية التي تغير السلوك غير المرتبط","توسيع الدعم فقط للكتل العلوية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Slabbed兼容性安全合约","模组包安全性","vanilla规则","全局钩子","顶部支持","模组兼容性","安全合约","模组开发","游戏开发"],"ja":["Slabbedの互換性安全契約","モッドパックの安全性","vanillaルール","グローバルフック","トップサポート","モッドの互換性","安全契約","モッド開発","ゲーム開発"],"ko":["슬래브 호환성 안전 계약","모드팩 안전성","바닐라 규칙","전역 훅","최상단 지원","모드 호환성","안전 계약","모드 개발","게임 개발"],"es":["Slabbed","contrato de seguridad de compatibilidad","modpacks","seguridad","previsibilidad","compatibilidad","bloques de vanilla","colocación","supervivencia"],"fr":["Slabbed","contrat de sécurité de compatibilité","modpacks","sécurité","prévisibilité","compatibilité","blocs de vanilla","placement","survie"],"de":["Slabbed","Kompatibilitätssicherheitsvertrag","Modpacks","Sicherheit","Vorhersehbarkeit","Kompatibilität","Vanilla-Blöcke","Platzierung","Überleben"],"pt":["Slabbed Compat","segurança em modpacks","regras de colocação","sobrevivência em vanilla","blocos parciais","gancho global","desenvolvimento de mods"],"ru":["Slabbed Compat","безопасность в модпаках","правила размещения","выживание в vanilla","частичные блоки","глобальный хук","разработка модов"],"ar":["Slabbed Compat","سلامة في حزم التعديل","قواعد وضع","بقاء في البرية","كتل جزئية","برنامج نصي عالمي","تطوير التعديلات"]}},"owner":"joolbits","repo":"slabbed","repoPath":"joolbits/slabbed","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"slabbed-compat-safety-contract","description":"Define Slabbed’s compatibility guardrails to avoid breaking vanilla behavior or modded blocks while adding slab-top support.","bodyPreview":"# Slabbed — Compatibility Safety Contract\n\n## Goal\nKeep Slabbed safe and predictable in modpacks:\n- Do not break vanilla placement/survival rules outside slab-top support\n- Do not assume all partial blocks behave like slabs\n- Avoid global hooks that change unrelated behavior\n\n## Non-goals\n- Full “compat with every mod” promise\n- Special handling for stairs/fences/walls/trapdoors unless explicitly planned\n\n## Scope of support\nSlabbed extends “top support” only for:\n- Vanilla `SlabBlock` bottom/to","body":"# Slabbed — Compatibility Safety Contract\n\n## Goal\nKeep Slabbed safe and predictable in modpacks:\n- Do not break vanilla placement/survival rules outside slab-top support\n- Do not assume all partial blocks behave like slabs\n- Avoid global hooks that change unrelated behavior\n\n## Non-goals\n- Full “compat with every mod” promise\n- Special handling for stairs/fences/walls/trapdoors unless explicitly planned\n\n## Scope of support\nSlabbed extends “top support” only for:\n- Vanilla `SlabBlock` bottom/top/double variants\n- Explicitly whitelisted slab-like blocks (only if added later with clear criteria)\n\nSlabbed does NOT automatically treat as support:\n- stairs\n- fences\n- walls\n- trapdoors\n- panes\n- carpet-like custom shapes\nunless explicitly added later.\n\n## Hook strategy rules\n1) Prefer the narrowest hook that fixes the category.\n2) Prefer per-block/category hooks over global redirects if the global change impacts unrelated blocks.\n3) If using a shared helper predicate, it must be limited to slab semantics only.\n4) All slab semantics must route through `SlabSupport` (single source of truth).\n\n## Modded block safety\n- Never assume a modded slab extends vanilla `SlabBlock`.\n- If handling modded slabs later, gate by:\n  - interface/marker (preferred), or\n  - explicit registry whitelist, or\n  - shape predicate proven equivalent to slab top face\n- Do not attempt heuristic “any half height block counts” logic.\n\n## Vanilla behavior preservation (mandatory checks)\nAfter any new hook:\n- Baseline full-block lane must behave exactly like vanilla\n- Existing categories must not regress\n- No new placement allowed on air/liquids that vanilla forbids\n- No changes to collision behavior for slabs themselves\n\n## Failure protocol\nIf a hook causes unintended changes:\n1) Revert to last known good tag\n2) Reduce scope (targeted mixin)\n3) Add regression test notes to the test matrix\n4) Re-apply in smaller pieces\n\n## Output report format\nWhen invoking this contract during review, report:\n- Hook type: shared vs targeted\n- Potential blast radius (1–2 lines)\n- Vanilla behavior checks performed\n- Modded block assumptions made (must be “none” unless explicitly justified)\n\n## Stop conditions\n- If you cannot explain why a hook is safe in 2 sentences, it’s too broad\n- If a shared hook alters behavior outside slab contexts, revert and target\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:29:36.420Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Modpack Agents needing predictable slab placement and compatibility rules in Minecraft modding environments.","zh":"适合需要可预测的板块放置和兼容性规则的Modpack Agents在Minecraft模组环境中。","ja":"MinecraftのModpackエージェントが予測可能なスラブの配置と互換性ルールを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"Minecraft 모딩 환경에서 예측 가능한 슬라브 배치 및 호환성 규칙이 필요한 Modpack 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfect for Modpack Agents needing predictable slab placement and compatibility rules in Minecraft modding environments.","fr":"Perfect for Modpack Agents needing predictable slab placement and compatibility rules in Minecraft modding environments.","de":"Perfect for Modpack Agents needing predictable slab placement and compatibility rules in Minecraft modding environments.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Modpack que necessitam de colocação de lâminas previsível e regras de compatibilidade em ambientes de modding do Minecraft.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Modpack, которым необходима предсказуемая установка слэбов и правила совместимости в средах моддинга Minecraft.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الحزمة الذي يحتاج إلى وضع شريحة قابل للتنبؤ وقواعد التوافق في بيئات تعديل ماين كرافت."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce compatibility safety contracts, ensuring slabbed mods adhere to vanilla placement and survival rules, while avoiding global hooks and unrelated behavior changes, specifically for Vanilla SlabBlock bottom/to support.","zh":"赋予代理人执行兼容性安全合同的能力，确保板块化模组遵循原版放置和生存规则，同时避免全局钩子和无关的行为变化，特别是针对Vanilla SlabBlock底部/支持的场景。","ja":"エージェントに、互換性安全契約を強制する能力を与え、スラブ化モッドがバニラの配置とサバイバルルールに従い、グローバルフックと無関係な動作の変更を避けることを保証する、特にVanilla SlabBlockの底部/サポートの場合。","ko":"에이전트가 호환성 안전 계약을 적용할 수 있도록 하여, 슬라브화된 모드가 바닐라의 배치 및 생존 규칙을 따르며, 글로벌 후크 및 관련이 없는 동작 변경을 피하는 것을 보장하며, 특히 Vanilla SlabBlock의 하단/지원에 대한 경우입니다.","es":"Empowers agents to enforce compatibility safety contracts, ensuring slabbed mods adhere to vanilla placement and survival rules, while avoiding global hooks and unrelated behavior changes, specifically for Vanilla SlabBlock bottom/to support.","fr":"Empowers agents to enforce compatibility safety contracts, ensuring slabbed mods adhere to vanilla placement and survival rules, while avoiding global hooks and unrelated behavior changes, specifically for Vanilla SlabBlock bottom/to support.","de":"Empowers agents to enforce compatibility safety contracts, ensuring slabbed mods adhere to vanilla placement and survival rules, while avoiding global hooks and unrelated behavior changes, specifically for Vanilla SlabBlock bottom/to support.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor contratos de segurança de compatibilidade, garantindo que os mods com lâminas adiram às regras de colocação e sobrevivência vanilla, evitando ganchos globais e alterações de comportamento não relacionadas, especificamente para suporte de Vanilla SlabBlock inferior.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать соблюдение контрактов совместимости, гарантируя, что моды со слэбами соответствуют правилам размещения и выживания в vanilla, избегая глобальных хуков и изменений поведения, не связанных с этим, в частности для поддержки Vanilla SlabBlock нижнего уровня.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إ施دار عقود سلامة التوافق، مما يضمن أن mods الشريحة تتبع قواعد وضع الفانيللا وقواعد البقاء، وتجنب Hooks العالمية وتغييرات السلوك غير المرتبطة، على وجه التحديد لدعم Vanilla SlabBlock السفلي / الدعم."},"useCases":{"en":["Enforcing slab placement rules in modpacks","Validating mod compatibility with vanilla Minecraft","Debugging slab-related issues in custom modpacks"],"zh":["在模组包中强制板块放置规则","验证模组与原版Minecraft的兼容性","调试自定义模组包中的板块相关问题"],"ja":["Modpack内でのスラブ配置ルールの強制","モッドとバニラMinecraftの互換性の検証","カスタムModpack内のスラブ関連の問題のデバッグ"],"ko":["모드팩에서 슬라브 배치 규칙을 강제 적용하기","모드와 바닐라 Minecraft의 호환성을 검증하기","사용자 정의 모드팩에서 슬라브 관련 문제를 디버깅하기"],"es":["Enforcing slab placement rules in modpacks","Validating mod compatibility with vanilla Minecraft","Debugging slab-related issues in custom modpacks"],"fr":["Enforcing slab placement rules in modpacks","Validating mod compatibility with vanilla Minecraft","Debugging slab-related issues in custom modpacks"],"de":["Enforcing slab placement rules in modpacks","Validating mod compatibility with vanilla Minecraft","Debugging slab-related issues in custom modpacks"],"pt":["Implementar regras de colocação de lâminas em modpacks","Validar a compatibilidade de mods com o Minecraft vanilla","Depurar problemas relacionados à lâmina em modpacks personalizados"],"ru":["Принудительный установка слэбов в модпаках","Проверка совместимости модов с vanilla Minecraft","Отладка проблем, связанных со слэбами, в пользовательских модпаках"],"ar":["تنفيذ قواعد وضع الشريحة في حزم التعديل","تحقق من توافق تعديلات مع ماين كرافت الفانيللا","تصحيح أخطاء متعلقة بالشريحة في حزم التعديل المخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Does not guarantee full compatibility with every mod","Limited special handling for stairs, fences, walls, and trapdoors unless explicitly planned"],"zh":["不能保证与每个模组的完全兼容性","除非明确计划，否则楼梯、围栏、墙壁和陷阱门的特殊处理有限"],"ja":["すべてのモッドとの完全な互換性を保証することはできない","明示的に計画されていない限り、階段、フェンス、壁、トラップドアの特殊な処理は限定される"],"ko":["모든 모드와의 완전한 호환성을 보장할 수 없습니다","명시적으로 계획되지 않은 경우, 계단, 펜스, 벽, 함정문의 특수 처리가 제한적입니다"],"es":["Does not guarantee full compatibility with every mod","Limited special handling for stairs, fences, walls, and trapdoors unless explicitly planned"],"fr":["Does not guarantee full compatibility with every mod","Limited special handling for stairs, fences, walls, and trapdoors unless explicitly planned"],"de":["Does not guarantee full compatibility with every mod","Limited special handling for stairs, fences, walls, and trapdoors unless explicitly planned"],"pt":["Não garante a compatibilidade total com todos os mods","Manipulação especial limitada para escadas, cercas, paredes e portas armadilhadas, a menos que planejada explicitamente"],"ru":["Не гарантирует полную совместимость с каждым модом","Ограниченная специальная обработка для лестниц, заборов, стен и ловушек, если не запланировано явно"],"ar":["لا يضمن التوافق الكامل مع كل التعديلات","معالجة خاصة محدودة للسلالم والأسوار والجدران والأبواب المفخخة، إلا إذا كانت مخططا لها я