الممارسات","en":"test-driven-development"},"description":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）是一种软件开发过程，通过先写测试用例来驱动开发","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）は、テストケースを先に書くことで開発を促進するソフトウェア開発プロセス","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD)은 테스트 케이스를 먼저 작성하여 개발을 주도하는 소프트웨어 개발 프로세스","es":"TDD es una metodología de desarrollo que implica escribir las pruebas antes de escribir el código, asegurando un código más robusto y mantenible.","fr":"Le TDD est une méthodologie de développement qui consiste à écrire les tests avant d''écrire le code, garantissant ainsi un code plus robuste et maintenable.","de":"TDD ist eine Entwicklungsmethode, bei der die Tests vor dem Code geschrieben werden, um einen robusteren und wartbaren Code zu gewährleisten.","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por testes (TDD) é uma prática de desenvolvimento de software que envolve a escrita de testes antes do código","ru":"Разработка через тестирование (TDD) - это практика разработки программного обеспечения, которая включает в себя написание тестов до кода","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) هو ممارسة تطوير البرمجيات التي تتضمن كتابة الاختبارات قبل الكود","en":"築未科技 AI 對話窗口 - GitHub Pages 部署"},"definition":{"en":"築未科技 AI 對話窗口 - GitHub Pages 部署"},"features":{"zh":["编写测试用例","观看测试失败","编写最小代码通过测试","重构代码"],"ja":["テストケースの作成","テストの失敗を観察","最小限のコードでテストを通過","コードのリファクタリング"],"ko":["테스트 케이스 작성","테스트 실패 관찰","최소한의 코드로 테스트 통과","코드 리팩토링"],"es":["Escribe pruebas antes de escribir código","Asegura un código más robusto y mantenible","Mejora la calidad del código","Reduce errores y bugs","Facilita la refactorización"],"fr":["Écrivez des tests avant d''écrire du code","Assurez un code plus robuste et maintenable","Améliorez la qualité du code","Réduisez les erreurs et les bogues","Facilitez la refactoring"],"de":["Schreiben Sie Tests bevor Sie Code schreiben","Stellen Sie sicher, dass der Code robuster und wartbarer ist","Verbessern Sie die Code-Qualität","Reduzieren Sie Fehler und Bugs","Erleichtern Sie die Refactoring"],"pt":["Escrita de testes antes do código","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Redução de bugs e erros","Desenvolvimento mais rápido e eficiente"],"ru":["Написание тестов до кода","Улучшение качества кода","Снижение количества багов и ошибок","Быстрое и эффективное развитие"],"ar":["كتابة الاختبارات قبل الكود","تحسين جودة الكود","تقليل الأخطاء والعيوب","تطوير أسرع وأكثر فعالية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["测试驱动开发","TDD","软件开发","代码质量","开发效率","测试用例","重构"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発","TDD","ソフトウェア開発","コード品質","開発効率","テストケース","リファクタリング"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발","TDD","소프트웨어 개발","코드 품질","개발 효율성","테스트 케이스","리팩토링"],"es":["TDD","Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas","pruebas unitarias","pruebas de integración","código robusto","mantenimiento de código"],"fr":["TDD","Développement Dirigé par les Tests","tests unitaires","tests d''intégration","code robuste","maintenance de code"],"de":["TDD","Testgetriebene Entwicklung","Einheitstests","Integrationstests","robuster Code","Code-Wartung"],"pt":["TDD","Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes","Testes Automatizados","Qualidade do Código","Desenvolvimento de Software"],"ru":["TDD","Разработка через тестирование","Автоматизированные тесты","Качество кода","Разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["TDD","التطوير الموجه بالاختبار","الاختبارات الآلية","جودة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"faint45","repo":"zhewei-ai-chat-01","repoPath":"faint45/zhewei-ai-chat-01","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"test-driven-development","description":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code","bodyPreview":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD","body":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD just this once\"? Stop. That''s rationalization.\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don''t look at it\n- Delete means delete\n\nImplement fresh from tests. Period.\n\n## Red-Green-Refactor\n\n```dot\ndigraph tdd_cycle {\n    rankdir=LR;\n    red [label=\"RED\\nWrite failing test\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffcccc\"];\n    verify_red [label=\"Verify fails\\ncorrectly\", shape=diamond];\n    green [label=\"GREEN\\nMinimal code\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccffcc\"];\n    verify_green [label=\"Verify passes\\nAll green\", shape=diamond];\n    refactor [label=\"REFACTOR\\nClean up\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccccff\"];\n    next [label=\"Next\", shape=ellipse];\n\n    red -> verify_red;\n    verify_red -> green [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_red -> red [label=\"wrong\\nfailure\"];\n    green -> verify_green;\n    verify_green -> refactor [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_green -> green [label=\"no\"];\n    refactor -> verify_green [label=\"stay\\ngreen\"];\n    verify_green -> next;\n    next -> red;\n}\n```\n\n### RED - Write Failing Test\n\nWrite one minimal test showing what should happen.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\ntest(''retries failed operations 3 times'', async () => {\n  let attempts = 0;\n  const operation = () => {\n    attempts++;\n    if (attempts < 3) throw new Error(''fail'');\n    return ''success'';\n  };\n\n  const result = await retryOperation(operation);\n\n  expect(result).toBe(''success'');\n  expect(attempts).toBe(3);\n});\n```\nClear name, tests real behavior, one thing\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\ntest(''retry works'', async () => {\n  const mock = jest.fn()\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockResolvedValueOnce(''success'');\n  await retryOperation(mock);\n  expect(mock).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(3);\n});\n```\nVague name, tests mock not code\n</Bad>\n\n**Requirements:**\n- One behavior\n- Clear name\n- Real code (no mocks unless unavoidable)\n\n### Verify RED - Watch It Fail\n\n**MANDATORY. Never skip.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test fails (not errors)\n- Failure message is expected\n- Fails because feature missing (not typos)\n\n**Test passes?** You''re testing existing behavior. Fix test.\n\n**Test errors?** Fix error, re-run until it fails correctly.\n\n### GREEN - Minimal Code\n\nWrite simplest code to pass the test.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn();\n    } catch (e) {\n      if (i === 2) throw e;\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(''unreachable'');\n}\n```\nJust enough to pass\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(\n  fn: () => Promise<T>,\n  options?: {\n    maxRetries?: number;\n    backoff?: ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n    onRetry?: (attempt: number) => void;\n  }\n): Promise<T> {\n  // YAGNI\n}\n```\nOver-engineered\n</Bad>\n\nDon''t add features, refactor other code, or \"improve\" beyond the test.\n\n### Verify GREEN - Watch It Pass\n\n**MANDATORY.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test passes\n- Other tests still pass\n- Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n\n**Test fails?** Fix code, not test.\n\n**Other tests fail?** Fix now.\n\n### REFACTOR - Clean Up\n\nAfter green only:\n- Remove duplication\n- Improve names\n- Extract helpers\n\nKeep tests green. Don''t add behavior.\n\n### Repeat\n\nNext failing test for next feature.\n\n## Good Tests\n\n| Quality | Good | Bad |\n|---------|------|-----|\n| **Minimal** | One thing. \"and\" in name? Split it. | `test(''validates email and domain and whitespace'')` |\n| **Clear** | Name describes behavior | `test(''test1'')` |\n| **Shows intent** | Demonstrates desired API | Obscures what code should do |\n\n## Why Order Matters\n\n**\"I''ll write tests after to verify it works\"**\n\nTests written after code pass immediately. Passing immediately proves nothing:\n- Might test wrong thing\n- Might test implementation, not behavior\n- Might miss edge cases you forgot\n- You never saw it catch the bug\n\nTest-first forces you to see the test fail, proving it actually tests something.\n\n**\"I already manually tested all the edge cases\"**\n\nManual testing is ad-hoc. You think you tested everything but:\n- No record of what you tested\n- Can''t re-run when code changes\n- Easy to forget cases under pressure\n- \"It worked when I tried it\" ≠ comprehensive\n\nAutomated tests are systematic. They run the same way every time.\n\n**\"Deleting X hours of work is wasteful\"**\n\nSunk cost fallacy. The time is already gone. Your choice now:\n- Delete and rewrite with TDD (X more hours, high confidence)\n- Keep it and add tests after (30 min, low confidence, likely bugs)\n\nThe \"waste\" is keeping code you can''t trust. Working code without real tests is technical debt.\n\n**\"TDD is dogmatic, being pragmatic means adapting\"**\n\nTDD IS pragmatic:\n- Finds bugs before commit (faster than debugging after)\n- Prevents regressions (tests catch breaks immediately)\n- Documents behavior (tests show how to use code)\n- Enables refactoring (change freely, tests catch breaks)\n\n\"Pragmatic\" shortcuts = debugging in production = slower.\n\n**\"Tests after achieve the same goals - it''s spirit not ritual\"**\n\nNo. Tests-after answer \"What does this do?\" Tests-first answer \"What should this do?\"\n\nTests-after are biased by your implementation. You test what you built, not what''s required. You verify remembered edge cases, not discovered ones.\n\nTests-first force edge case discovery before implementing. Tests-after verify you remembered everything (you didn''t).\n\n30 minutes of tests after ≠ TDD. You get coverage, lose proof tests work.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Too simple to test\" | Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n| \"Already manually tested\" | Ad-hoc ≠ systematic. No record, can''t re-run. |\n| \"Deleting X hours is wasteful\" | Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt. |\n| \"Keep as reference, write tests first\" | You''ll adapt it. That''s testing after. Delete means delete. |\n| \"Need to explore first\" | Fine. Throw away exploration, start with TDD. |\n| \"Test hard = design unclear\" | Listen to test. Hard to test = hard to use. |\n| \"TDD will slow me down\" | TDD faster than debugging. Pragmatic = test-first. |\n| \"Manual test faster\" | Manual doesn''t prove edge cases. You''ll re-test every change. |\n| \"Existing code has no tests\" | You''re improving it. Add tests for existing code. |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Start Over\n\n- Code before test\n- Test after implementation\n- Test passes immediately\n- Can''t explain why test failed\n- Tests added \"later\"\n- Rationalizing \"just this once\"\n- \"I already manually tested it\"\n- \"Tests after achieve the same purpose\"\n- \"It''s about spirit not ritual\"\n- \"Keep as reference\" or \"adapt existing code\"\n- \"Already spent X hours, deleting is wasteful\"\n- \"TDD is dogmatic, I''m being pragmatic\"\n- \"This is different because...\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n\n## Example: Bug Fix\n\n**Bug:** Empty email accepted\n\n**RED**\n```typescript\ntest(''rejects empty email'', async () => {\n  const result = await submitForm({ email: '''' });\n  expect(result.error).toBe(''Email required'');\n});\n```\n\n**Verify RED**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nFAIL: expected ''Email required'', got undefined\n```\n\n**GREEN**\n```typescript\nfunction submitForm(data: FormData) {\n  if (!data.email?.trim()) {\n    return { error: ''Email required'' };\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Verify GREEN**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nPASS\n```\n\n**REFACTOR**\nExtract validation for multiple fields if needed.\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\nBefore marking work complete:\n\n- [ ] Every new function/method has a test\n- [ ] Watched each test fail before implementing\n- [ ] Each test failed for expected reason (feature missing, not typo)\n- [ ] Wrote minimal code to pass each test\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n- [ ] Tests use real code (mocks only if unavoidable)\n- [ ] Edge cases and errors covered\n\nCan''t check all boxes? You skipped TDD. Start over.\n\n## When Stuck\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| Don''t know how to test | Write wished-for API. Write assertion first. Ask your human partner. |\n| Test too complicated | Design too complicated. Simplify interface. |\n| Must mock everything | Code too coupled. Use dependency injection. |\n| Test setup huge | Extract helpers. Still complex? Simplify design. |\n\n## Debugging Integration\n\nBug found? Write failing test reproducing it. Follow TDD cycle. Test proves fix and prevents regression.\n\nNever fix bugs without a test.\n\n## Testing Anti-Patterns\n\nWhen adding mocks or test utilities, read @testing-anti-patterns.md to avoid common pitfalls:\n- Testing mock behavior instead of real behavior\n- Adding test-only methods to production classes\n- Mocking without understanding dependencies\n\n## Final Rule\n\n```\nProduction code → test exists and failed first\nOtherwise → not TDD\n```\n\nNo exceptions without your human partner''s permission.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:31:16.305Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code-Generation Agents requiring rigorous testing protocols like TDD for new features, bug fixes, and refactoring.","zh":"非常适合需要严格测试协议（如TDD）的代码生成智能体，用于新功能开发、错误修复和重构。","ja":"新機能、バグ修正、リファクタリングにおいて、TDDのような厳格なテストプロトコルを必要とするコード生成エージェントに最適です。","ko":"새 기능, 버그 수정 및 리팩토링을 위해 TDD와 같은 엄격한 테스트 프로토콜이 필요한 코드 생성 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de generación de código que requieren protocolos de pruebas rigurosos como TDD para nuevas características, correcciones de errores y refactorización.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de génération de code nécessitant des protocoles de test rigoureux comme TDD pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités, les corrections de bogue et la refactorisation.","de":"Ideal für Code-Generierungsagenten, die strenge Testprotokolle wie TDD für neue Funktionen, Fehlerbehebungen und Refactoring erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Geração de Código que requerem protocolos de teste rigorosos como TDD para novos recursos, correções de bugs e refatoração.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов генерации кода, требующих строгих протоколов тестирования, таких как TDD, для новых функций, исправления ошибок и рефакторинга.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء إنشاء التعليمات البرمجية الذين يتطلبون بروتوكولات اختبار صارمة مثل TDD للميزات الجديدة وإصلاح الأخطاء وإعادة الهيكلة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write minimal code that passes tests, ensuring robustness and reliability through the core principle of watching tests fail before passing, utilizing methodologies like writing the test first and validating behavior changes.","zh":"使智能体能够编写通过测试的最精简代码，通过‘先观察测试失败再通过’的核心原则，利用先编写测试和验证行为变更等方法，确保代码的健壮性和可靠性。","ja":"テストを最初に書き、動作変更を検証する手法を利用し、テストが合格する前に失敗することを確認するという核心原則を通じて、堅牢性と信頼性を確保し、エージェントがテストに合格する最小限のコードを書くことを可能にします。","ko":"테스트를 먼저 작성하고 동작 변경을 검증하는 방법론을 활용하여, 테스트가 통과하기 전에 실패하는 것을 지켜본다는 핵심 원칙을 통해 강건성과 신뢰성을 보장하며, 에이전트가 테스트를 통과하는 최소한의 코드를 작성할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes escribir código mínimo que pasa las pruebas, garantizando la robustez y la confiabilidad a través del principio fundamental de observar las pruebas fallidas antes de pasar, utilizando metodologías como escribir la prueba primero y validar los cambios de comportamiento.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire un code minimal qui passe les tests, garantissant la robustesse et la fiabilité grâce au principe fondamental de regarder les tests échouer avant de passer, en utilisant des méthodologies comme écrire le test en premier et valider les changements de comportement.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, minimalen Code zu schreiben, der die Tests besteht, und gewährleistet so Robustheit und Zuverlässigkeit durch das Kernprinzip, Tests scheitern zu lassen, bevor sie bestehen, unter Verwendung von Methoden wie dem Schreiben des Tests zuerst und der Überprüfung von Verhaltensänderungen.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a escrever código mínimo que passe nos testes, garantindo robustez e confiabilidade através do princípio central de observar os testes falharem antes de passarem, utilizando metodologias como escrever o teste primeiro e validar mudanças de comportamento.","ru":"Позволяет агентам писать минимальный код, который проходит тесты, обеспечивая надежность и достоверность через основной принцип наблюдения за неудачными тестами перед их прохождением, используя такие методики, как написание теста сначала и проверка изменений поведения.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من كتابة الحد الأدنى من التعليمات البرمجية التي تجتاز الاختبارات، مما يضمن المتانة والموثوقية من خلال المبدأ الأساسي المتمثل في مراقبة فشل الاختبارات قبل اجتيازها، باستخدام منهجيات مثل كتابة الاختبار أولاً والتحقق من تغييرات السلوك."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating unit tests for new features","Debugging existing codebase with TDD","Refactoring legacy code with test validation"],"zh":["为新功能自动化单元测试","使用TDD调试现有代码库","通过测试验证重构遗留代码"],"ja":["新機能の単体テストの自動化","TDDを使用した既存コードベースのデバッグ","テスト検証によるレガシーコードのリファクタリング"],"ko":["새 기능에 대한 단위 테스트 자동화","TDD로 기존 코드베이스 디버깅","테스트 검증을 통한 레거시 코드 리팩토링"],"es":["Automatización de pruebas unitarias para nuevas características","Depuración de la base de código existente con TDD","Refactorización de código legado con validación de pruebas"],"fr":["Automation des tests unitaires pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités","Débogage de la base de code existante avec TDD","Refactoring du code hérité avec validation de tests"],"de":["Automatisierung von Einheitstests für neue Funktionen","Fehlerbehebung der bestehenden Codebasis mit TDD","Refactoring von Legacy-Code mit Testvalidierung"],"pt":["Automatização de testes de unidade para novos recursos","Depuração de base de código existente com TDD","Refatoração de código legado com validação de teste"],"ru":["Автоматизация модульных тестов для новых функций","Отладка существующей кодовой базы с помощью TDD","Рефакторинг устаревшего кода с проверкой тестов"],"ar":["أتمتة اختبارات الوحدة للميزات الجديدة","تصحيح قاعدة التعليمات البرمجية الحالية باستخدام TDD","إعادة هيكلة التعليمات البرمجية القديمة مع التحقق من خلال الاختبار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Exceptions apply for throwaway prototypes, generated code, and configuration files, requiring human oversight"],"zh":["一次性原型、生成的代码和配置文件除外，这些情况需要人工监督"],"ja":["使い捨てプロトタイプ、生成されたコード、設定ファイルは例外であり、人的監視が必要です"],"ko":["일회용 프로토타입, 생성된 코드 및 구성 파일은 예외이며, 인간의 감독이 필요합니다"],"es":["Se aplican excepciones para prototipos desechables, código generado y archivos de configuración, que requieren supervisión humana"],"fr":["Des exceptions s''appliquent aux prototypes jetables, au code généré et aux fichiers de configuration, qui nécessitent une surveillance humaine"],"de":["Ausnahmen gelten für verworfene Prototypen, generierten Code und Konfigurationsdateien, die menschliche Aufsicht erfordern"],"pt":["Exceções aplicam-se a protótipos descartáveis, código gerado e arquivos de configuração, exigindo supervisão humana"],"ru":["Исключения применяются для одноразовых прототипов, сгенерированного кода и файлов конфигурации, требующих контроля человека"],"ar":["تستثنى النماذج الأولية التي يمكن التخلص منها، والتعليمات البرمجية المُنشأة، وملفات التكوين، والتي تتطلب إشرافًا بشريًا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('karstenheld3/SharePoint-GPT-Middleware/pdf-tools', 'community', 'karstenheld3', 'SharePoint-GPT-Middleware', 'karstenheld3/SharePoint-GPT-Middleware', 'pdf-tools', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z', '2026-02-18T12:32:31.083Z', NULL, '{"id":"karstenheld3/SharePoint-GPT-Middleware/pdf-tools","name":"pdf-tools","description":{"zh":"PDF工具是一款Azure Web App，使用Python爬取SharePoint内容到OpenAI Vector Stores，提供高效的PDF转换和分析功能","ja":"PDFツールは、Azure Web AppでSharePointの内容をOpenAI Vector StoresにクロールするPythonアプリケーションであり、高效なPDF変換と分析機能を提供","ko":"PDF 도구는 Azure Web App에서 SharePoint 콘텐츠를 OpenAI Vector Stores로 크롤링하는 Python 애플리케이션으로, 효율적인 PDF 변환 및 분석 기능을 제공","es":"El conjunto de herramientas PDF para Azure es una aplicación web en Python que convierte documentos de SharePoint en imágenes JPG para análisis de visión","fr":"L''ensemble d''outils PDF pour Azure est une application web Python qui convertit des documents SharePoint en images JPG pour analyse de vision","de":"Das PDF-Tool-Set für Azure ist eine Python-Webanwendung, die SharePoint-Dokumente in JPG-Bilder für die Bildanalyse konvertiert","pt":"O pdf-tools é um conjunto de ferramentas para converter PDFs em JPGs e realizar análise de visão com o Azure Web App em Python","ru":"Инструменты PDF - это набор инструментов для конвертации PDF в JPG и анализа зрения с помощью Azure Web App на Python","ar":"أدوات PDF هي مجموعة من الأدوات لتحويل ملفات PDF إلى JPG والتحليل المرئي باستخدام تطبيق Azure Web بالبايثون","en":"An Azure Web App in Python to crawl the content of SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"PDF工具：Azure Web App爬取SharePoint内容","ja":"PDFツール：Azure Web AppでSharePointの内容をクロール","ko":"PDF 도구: Azure Web App에서 SharePoint 콘텐츠 크롤링","es":"Herramientas PDF para Azure: Guía de conversión y análisis","fr":"Outils PDF pour Azure : Guide de conversion et d''analyse","de":"PDF-Tools für Azure: Leitfaden für Konvertierung und Analyse","pt":"Ferramentas PDF: Guia de Conversão e Análise","ru":"Инструменты PDF: Руководство по конвертации и анализу","ar":"أدوات PDF: دليل التحويل والتحليل","en":"pdf-tools"},"description":{"zh":"PDF工具是一款Azure Web App，使用Python爬取SharePoint内容到OpenAI Vector Stores，提供高效的PDF转换和分析功能","ja":"PDFツールは、Azure Web AppでSharePointの内容をOpenAI Vector StoresにクロールするPythonアプリケーションであり、高效なPDF変換と分析機能を提供","ko":"PDF 도구는 Azure Web App에서 SharePoint 콘텐츠를 OpenAI Vector Stores로 크롤링하는 Python 애플리케이션으로, 효율적인 PDF 변환 및 분석 기능을 제공","es":"El conjunto de herramientas PDF para Azure es una aplicación web en Python que convierte documentos de SharePoint en imágenes JPG para análisis de visión","fr":"L''ensemble d''outils PDF pour Azure est une application web Python qui convertit des documents SharePoint en images JPG pour analyse de vision","de":"Das PDF-Tool-Set für Azure ist eine Python-Webanwendung, die SharePoint-Dokumente in JPG-Bilder für die Bildanalyse konvertiert","pt":"O pdf-tools é um conjunto de ferramentas para converter PDFs em JPGs e realizar análise de visão com o Azure Web App em Python","ru":"Инструменты PDF - это набор инструментов для конвертации PDF в JPG и анализа зрения с помощью Azure Web App на Python","ar":"أدوات PDF هي مجموعة من الأدوات لتحويل ملفات PDF إلى JPG والتحليل المرئي باستخدام تطبيق Azure Web بالبايثون","en":"An Azure Web App in Python to crawl the content of SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores"},"definition":{"en":"An Azure Web App in Python to crawl the content of SharePoint sites into OpenAI Vector Stores"},"features":{"zh":["爬取SharePoint内容到OpenAI Vector Stores","PDF转换和分析功能","支持150 DPI和300 DPI的图像输出","两次降采样：Ghostscript和QPDF"],"ja":["SharePointの内容をOpenAI Vector Storesにクロール","PDF変換と分析機能","150 DPIと300 DPIの画像出力をサポート","2回のダウンサンプリング：GhostscriptとQPDF"],"ko":["SharePoint 콘텐츠를 OpenAI Vector Stores로 크롤링","PDF 변환 및 분석 기능","150 DPI 및 300 DPI의 이미지 출력을 지원","2회 다운샘플링: Ghostscript 및 QPDF"],"es":["Conversión de PDF a JPG para análisis de visión","Uso de 150 DPI para pantalla y 300 DPI para OCR","Redimensionamiento de dos pasos con Ghostscript y QPDF","Integración con OpenAI Vector Stores","Compatibilidad con sitios de SharePoint"],"fr":["Conversion de PDF en JPG pour analyse de vision","Utilisation de 150 DPI pour l''écran et 300 DPI pour l''OCR","Redimensionnement en deux étapes avec Ghostscript et QPDF","Intégration avec OpenAI Vector Stores","Compatibilité avec les sites SharePoint"],"de":["Konvertierung von PDF in JPG für Bildanalyse","Verwendung von 150 DPI für den Bildschirm und 300 DPI für OCR","Zweistufiges Downsizing mit Ghostscript und QPDF","Integration mit OpenAI Vector Stores","Kompatibilität mit SharePoint-Seiten"],"pt":["Conversão de PDF para JPG","Análise de visão com Azure Web App","Utilização de 150 DPI para tela e 300 DPI para OCR","Redimensionamento em duas etapas com Ghostscript e QPDF","Suporte a arquivos PDF de várias páginas"],"ru":["Конвертация PDF в JPG","Анализ зрения с помощью Azure Web App","Использование 150 DPI для экрана и 300 DPI для OCR","Двухпасовый ресайзинг с помощью Ghostscript и QPDF","Поддержка файлов PDF с несколькими страницами"],"ar":["تحويل ملفات PDF إلى JPG","تحليل الرؤية باستخدام تطبيق Azure Web","استخدام 150 DPI للشاشة و 300 DPI للOCR","تحجيم متغير في مرحلتين مع Ghostscript و QPDF","دعم ملفات PDF متعددة الصفحات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PDF工具","Azure Web App","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","Python","PDF转换","图像分析"],"ja":["PDFツール","Azure Web App","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","Python","PDF変換","画像分析"],"ko":["PDF 도구","Azure Web App","SharePoint","OpenAI Vector Stores","Python","PDF 변환","이미지 분석"],"es":["herramientas pdf","azure","python","conversión de pdf","análisis de visión","openai vector stores","sharepoint","desarrollo de aplicaciones web"],"fr":["outils pdf","azure","python","conversion de pdf","analyse de vision","openai vector stores","sharepoint","développement d''applications web"],"de":["pdf-tools","azure","python","pdf-konvertierung","bildanalyse","openai vector stores","sharepoint","webanwendungsentwicklung"],"pt":["ferramentas pdf","conversão pdf","análise de visão","azure web app","python","pdf para jpg","ocr","ghostscript","qpdf"],"ru":["инструменты pdf","конвертация pdf","анализ зрения","azure web app","python","pdf в jpg","ocr","ghostscript","qpdf"],"ar":["أدوات pdf","تحويل pdf","تحليل الرؤية","تطبيق azure web","بايثون","pdf إلى jpg","ocr","ghostscript","qpdf"]}},"owner":"karstenheld3","repo":"SharePoint-GPT-Middleware","repoPath":"karstenheld3/SharePoint-GPT-Middleware","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pdf-tools","description":"Apply when converting, processing, or analyzing PDF files","bodyPreview":"# PDF Tools Guide\n\nRules and usage for PDF tools in `[WORKSPACE_FOLDER]/../.tools/`.\n\n## MUST-NOT-FORGET\n\n- Check existing conversions before converting\n- Default output: `../.tools/_pdf_to_jpg_converted/[PDF_FILENAME]/`\n- Use 150 DPI for screen, 300 DPI for OCR\n- Two-pass downsizing: Ghostscript (images) then QPDF (structure)\n\n## PDF to JPG Conversion\n\n### Script: `DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/convert-pdf-to-jpg.py`\n\nConverts PDF pages to JPG images for vision analysis.\n\n**Usage:**\n```powershel","body":"# PDF Tools Guide\n\nRules and usage for PDF tools in `[WORKSPACE_FOLDER]/../.tools/`.\n\n## MUST-NOT-FORGET\n\n- Check existing conversions before converting\n- Default output: `../.tools/_pdf_to_jpg_converted/[PDF_FILENAME]/`\n- Use 150 DPI for screen, 300 DPI for OCR\n- Two-pass downsizing: Ghostscript (images) then QPDF (structure)\n\n## PDF to JPG Conversion\n\n### Script: `DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/convert-pdf-to-jpg.py`\n\nConverts PDF pages to JPG images for vision analysis.\n\n**Usage:**\n```powershell\npython DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/convert-pdf-to-jpg.py <input.pdf> [--output <dir>] [--dpi <dpi>] [--pages <range>]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n```powershell\npython DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/convert-pdf-to-jpg.py invoice.pdf\npython DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/convert-pdf-to-jpg.py invoice.pdf --dpi 200 --pages 1-2\npython DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/convert-pdf-to-jpg.py invoice.pdf --pages 1\n```\n\n**Output Convention:**\n- Default output: `../.tools/_pdf_to_jpg_converted/[PDF_FILENAME]/`\n- Each PDF gets its own subfolder named after the PDF file (without extension)\n- Files named: `[PDF_FILENAME]_page001.jpg`, `[PDF_FILENAME]_page002.jpg`, etc.\n- Check for existing subfolder to skip re-conversion\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `--output`: Output directory (default: `../.tools/_pdf_to_jpg_converted/`)\n- `--dpi`: Resolution (default: 150)\n- `--pages`: Page range - \"1\", \"1-3\", or \"all\" (default: all)\n\n## 7-Zip CLI Tools\n\nLocation: `../.tools/7z/`\n\n7-Zip is required to extract Ghostscript from its NSIS installer. The standalone `7za.exe` cannot extract NSIS archives.\n\n### Extract archive\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/7z/7z.exe\" x -y -o\"output_folder\" \"archive.zip\"\n```\n\n### Extract NSIS installer (like Ghostscript)\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/7z/7z.exe\" x -y -o\"output_folder\" \"installer.exe\"\n```\n\n### List archive contents\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/7z/7z.exe\" l \"archive.zip\"\n```\n\n## Poppler CLI Tools\n\nLocation: `../.tools/poppler/Library/bin/`\n\n### pdftoppm - PDF to Image\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/poppler/Library/bin/pdftoppm.exe\" -jpeg -r 150 \"input.pdf\" \"output_prefix\"\n```\n\n### pdftotext - Extract Text\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/poppler/Library/bin/pdftotext.exe\" \"input.pdf\" \"output.txt\"\n```\n\n### pdfinfo - Get PDF Metadata\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/poppler/Library/bin/pdfinfo.exe\" \"input.pdf\"\n```\n\n### pdfseparate - Split PDF Pages\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/poppler/Library/bin/pdfseparate.exe\" \"input.pdf\" \"output_%d.pdf\"\n```\n\n### pdfunite - Merge PDFs\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/poppler/Library/bin/pdfunite.exe\" \"page1.pdf\" \"page2.pdf\" \"merged.pdf\"\n```\n\n## QPDF CLI Tools\n\nLocation: `../.tools/qpdf/bin/`\n\n### Merge PDFs\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/qpdf/bin/qpdf.exe\" --empty --pages file1.pdf file2.pdf -- merged.pdf\n```\n\n### Split PDF (extract pages)\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/qpdf/bin/qpdf.exe\" input.pdf --pages . 1-5 -- output.pdf\n```\n\n### Decrypt PDF\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/qpdf/bin/qpdf.exe\" --decrypt --password=secret encrypted.pdf decrypted.pdf\n```\n\n### Repair PDF\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/qpdf/bin/qpdf.exe\" --replace-input damaged.pdf\n```\n\n### Linearize (optimize for web)\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/qpdf/bin/qpdf.exe\" --linearize input.pdf output.pdf\n```\n\n## Smart PDF Compression Script\n\n### Script: `DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/compress-pdf.py`\n\nIntelligent PDF compression that analyzes content and applies optimal strategy.\n\n**Usage:**\n```powershell\npython DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/compress-pdf.py <input.pdf> [--compression high|medium|low] [--output output.pdf]\n```\n\n**Examples:**\n```powershell\npython DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/compress-pdf.py report.pdf\npython DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/compress-pdf.py report.pdf --compression high\npython DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/compress-pdf.py report.pdf --compression low --output archive.pdf\n```\n\n**Compression levels:**\n- **high**: Target 50%+ reduction, aggressive (72 DPI)\n- **medium**: Target 25%+ reduction, balanced (150 DPI)\n- **low**: Target 10%+ reduction, preserve quality (300 DPI)\n\n**Features:**\n- Analyzes PDF structure (images, DPI, format, optimization status)\n- Predicts compression potential before processing\n- Escalates to more aggressive strategies if target not reached\n- Reverts to previous result if aggressive approach shows insufficient improvement\n\n**Output:** `../.tools/_pdf_output/[PDF_FILENAME]_compressed.pdf`\n\n## Simple PDF Downsizing Script\n\n### Script: `DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/downsize-pdf-images.py`\n\nDirect Ghostscript wrapper for manual DPI control.\n\n**Usage:**\n```powershell\npython DevSystemV2/skills/pdf-tools/downsize-pdf-images.py <input.pdf> [--output <dir>] [--dpi <dpi>] [--preset <preset>]\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `--output`: Output directory (default: `../.tools/_pdf_output/`)\n- `--dpi`: Resolution (default: 150)\n- `--preset`: Quality preset - screen (72), ebook (150), printer (300), prepress (300)\n\n**Output:** `../.tools/_pdf_output/[PDF_FILENAME]_[DPI]dpi.pdf`\n\n## Ghostscript CLI Tools\n\nLocation: `../.tools/gs/bin/`\n\n### Compress images (downsize PDF)\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/gs/bin/gswin64c.exe\" -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -dCompatibilityLevel=1.4 -dPDFSETTINGS=/screen -dDownsampleColorImages=true -dColorImageResolution=72 -dDownsampleGrayImages=true -dGrayImageResolution=72 -dDownsampleMonoImages=true -dMonoImageResolution=72 -dNOPAUSE -dQUIET -dBATCH -sOutputFile=output.pdf input.pdf\n```\n\n### Quality presets (`-dPDFSETTINGS`)\n- `/screen` - 72 DPI, smallest file size\n- `/ebook` - 150 DPI, medium quality\n- `/printer` - 300 DPI, high quality\n- `/prepress` - 300 DPI, color preserving\n\n### Remove all images (text only)\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/gs/bin/gswin64c.exe\" -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -dCompatibilityLevel=1.4 -dFILTERIMAGE=true -dNOPAUSE -dQUIET -dBATCH -sOutputFile=output.pdf input.pdf\n```\n\n## PDF Downsizing Workflow\n\nTwo-pass workflow for maximum compression:\n\n### Pass 1: Ghostscript (image compression)\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/gs/bin/gswin64c.exe\" -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -dCompatibilityLevel=1.4 -dPDFSETTINGS=/screen -dDownsampleColorImages=true -dColorImageResolution=72 -dDownsampleGrayImages=true -dGrayImageResolution=72 -dNOPAUSE -dQUIET -dBATCH -sOutputFile=temp.pdf input.pdf\n```\n\n### Pass 2: QPDF (structure optimization)\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/qpdf/bin/qpdf.exe\" --linearize --object-streams=generate --stream-data=compress --compress-streams=y --optimize-images --flatten-annotations=screen temp.pdf output.pdf\nRemove-Item temp.pdf\n```\n\n## PDF Analysis\n\nBefore optimizing, analyze the PDF to understand what''s consuming space.\n\n### Get PDF info\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/poppler/Library/bin/pdfinfo.exe\" \"input.pdf\"\n```\n\n### List all images with details\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/poppler/Library/bin/pdfimages.exe\" -list \"input.pdf\"\n```\n\nShows: page, dimensions, color space, compression, DPI, size. Use to determine if images can be further compressed.\n\n### Count images\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/poppler/Library/bin/pdfimages.exe\" -list \"input.pdf\" | Measure-Object\n```\n\n## Optimization Strategies (by effectiveness)\n\nTested on 6 real-world annual reports (50-100 MB each):\n\n**High compression (>50% reduction):**\n- JPEG2000 at 200 DPI: 77 MB → 4.5 MB (94% with screen, 86% with ebook)\n- Mixed content, not optimized: 84 MB → 34 MB (59%)\n- Mixed content: 49 MB → 21 MB (57%)\n\n**Moderate compression (10-50%):**\n- Already optimized PDF: 47 MB → 42 MB (10%)\n\n**Low compression (<10%):**\n- PDF with 10552 tiny images: 58 MB → 56 MB (4%) - many small UI elements\n- Image-only PDF at 115 DPI: 101 MB → 97 MB (4% at 100 DPI, 77% at 72 DPI)\n\n**Key factors affecting compression:**\n- **Image format**: JPEG2000 (jpx) compresses dramatically when converted to JPEG\n- **Image DPI**: High DPI (200+) benefits most from downsampling\n- **Already optimized**: PDFs marked \"Optimized: yes\" compress less\n- **Many small images**: Thousands of tiny icons/UI elements resist compression\n\n### Strategy 1: Aggressive (best for large reductions)\n```powershell\ncmd /c \"& ''../.tools/gs/bin/gswin64c.exe'' -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -dCompatibilityLevel=1.4 -dPDFSETTINGS=/screen -dDetectDuplicateImages=true -dCompressFonts=true -dSubsetFonts=true -dConvertCMYKImagesToRGB=true -dColorImageDownsampleType=/Bicubic -dNOPAUSE -dBATCH -sOutputFile=output.pdf input.pdf\"\n```\n\n### Strategy 2: Balanced (preserves more quality)\n```powershell\ncmd /c \"& ''../.tools/gs/bin/gswin64c.exe'' -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -dCompatibilityLevel=1.4 -dPDFSETTINGS=/ebook -dDetectDuplicateImages=true -dCompressFonts=true -dSubsetFonts=true -dConvertCMYKImagesToRGB=true -dNOPAUSE -dBATCH -sOutputFile=output.pdf input.pdf\"\n```\n\n### Strategy 3: Structure only (no quality loss)\n```powershell\n& \"../.tools/qpdf/bin/qpdf.exe\" --linearize --object-streams=generate --compress-streams=y --recompress-flate input.pdf output.pdf\n```\n\n## Key Optimization Flags\n\n- `-dDetectDuplicateImages=true` - Replace duplicate images with references\n- `-dCompressFonts=true` - Compress font data\n- `-dSubsetFonts=true` - Include only used glyphs\n- `-dConvertCMYKImagesToRGB=true` - Convert CMYK to RGB (smaller)\n- `-dColorImageDownsampleType=/Bicubic` - Better quality downsampling\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Analyze first**: Use `pdfimages -list` to understand image content before optimizing\n2. **Check existing conversions**: Before converting, check if subfolder exists in `_pdf_to_jpg_converted/`\n3. **Use appropriate DPI**: 72 for web/archive, 150 for screen, 300 for print/OCR\n4. **Convert specific pages**: Use `--pages` to avoid converting entire large PDFs\n5. **Clean up**: Delete old conversions when no longer needed\n6. **Two-pass for maximum compression**: Ghostscript (images) then QPDF (structure)\n\n## Setup\n\nFor initial installation, see `SETUP.md` in this skill folder.\n\n**Tool locations:**\n- 7-Zip: `../.tools/7z/`\n- Poppler: `../.tools/poppler/`\n- QPDF: `../.tools/qpdf/`\n- Ghostscript: `../.tools/gs/`\n- Installers: `../.tools/_installer/`\n- JPG output: `../.tools/_pdf_to_jpg_converted/`\n- PDF output: `../.tools/_pdf_output/`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:32:31.083Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced PDF content crawling and OpenAI Vector Store integration.","zh":"非常适合需要高级PDF内容爬取和OpenAI Vector Store集成的数据分析代理。","ja":"データ分析エージェントが高度なPDFコンテンツクロールとOpenAI Vector Store統合を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"데이터 분석 에이전트가 고급 PDF 콘텐츠 크롤링 및 OpenAI Vector Store 통합을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de rastreo de contenido en PDF e integración con OpenAI Vector Store.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse de Données ayant besoin de capacités avancées d''exploration de contenu PDF et d''intégration avec OpenAI Vector Store.","de":"Ideal für Datenanalyse-Agenten, die erweiterte Fähigkeiten zum Crawlen von PDF-Inhalten und zur Integration mit OpenAI Vector Store benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de rastreamento avançado de conteúdo em PDF e integração com o OpenAI Vector Store.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа данных, которым требуется продвинутый поиск контента в PDF и интеграция с OpenAI Vector Store.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء تحليل البيانات الذين يحتاجون إلى تقارير متقدمة لمحتوى PDF وتكامل مع متجر OpenAI Vector."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to crawl SharePoint sites and convert PDF content into vector stores using Python and OpenAI, enabling efficient data visualization and analysis through protocols like Ghostscript and QPDF.","zh":"使代理能够使用Python和OpenAI爬取SharePoint站点，并将PDF内容转换为向量存储，从而通过Ghostscript和QPDF等协议实现高效的数据可视化和分析。","ja":"PythonとOpenAIを使用してSharePointサイトをクロールし、PDFコンテンツをベクトルストアに変換することで、エージェントを強化し、GhostscriptやQPDFなどのプロトコルを介して効率的なデータ視覚化と分析を可能にします。","ko":"Python 및 OpenAI를 사용하여 SharePoint 사이트를 크롤링하고 PDF 콘텐츠를 벡터 저장소로 변환하여 Ghostscript 및 QPDF를 포함한 프로토콜을 통해 효율적인 데이터 시각화 및 분석을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes rastrear sitios de SharePoint y convertir contenido PDF en almacenes vectoriales utilizando Python y OpenAI, lo que posibilita una visualización y análisis eficiente de datos mediante protocolos como Ghostscript y QPDF.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''explorer les sites SharePoint et de convertir le contenu PDF en magasins vectoriels en utilisant Python et OpenAI, permettant une visualisation et une analyse efficaces des données via des protocoles tels que Ghostscript et QPDF.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, SharePoint-Websites zu crawlen und PDF-Inhalte mit Python und OpenAI in Vektorspeicher umzuwandeln, was eine effiziente Datenvisualisierung und -analyse durch Protokolle wie Ghostscript und QPDF ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a rastrear sites do SharePoint e converter o conteúdo em PDF em lojas de vetores usando Python e OpenAI, permitindo uma visualização e análise de dados eficientes por meio de protocolos como Ghostscript e QPDF.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью поиска сайтов SharePoint и преобразования контента PDF в векторные хранилища с помощью Python и OpenAI, обеспечивая эффективную визуализацию и анализ данных через протоколы seperti Ghostscript и QPDF.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تقصي مواقع SharePoint وتحويل محتوى PDF إلى مخازن متجهة باستخدام بايثون و OpenAI، مما يتيح رؤية وتحليل البيانات بكفاءة من خلال بروتوكولات مثل Ghostscript و QPDF."},"useCases":{"en":["Crawling SharePoint sites for PDF content","Converting PDF pages to JPG images for vision analysis","Integrating PDF data into OpenAI Vector Stores"],"zh":["爬取SharePoint站点的PDF内容","将PDF页面转换为JPG图像以进行视觉分析","将PDF数据集成到OpenAI Vector Stores"],"ja":["SharePointサイトのPDFコンテンツをクロールする","PDFページをJPG画像に変換して視覚分析を行う","PDFデータをOpenAI Vector Storesに統合する"],"ko":["SharePoint 사이트의 PDF 콘텐츠 크롤링","PDF 페이지를 JPG 이미지로 변환하여 비전 분석 수행","PDF 데이터를 OpenAI Vector Stores에 통합"],"es":["Rastreo de sitios de SharePoint para contenido PDF","Conversión de páginas PDF a imágenes JPG para análisis de visión","Integración de datos PDF en OpenAI Vector Stores"],"fr":["Exploration de sites SharePoint pour le contenu PDF","Conversion de pages PDF en images JPG pour l''analyse vision","Intégration de données PDF dans OpenAI Vector Stores"],"de":["Crawling von SharePoint-Websites für PDF-Inhalte","Konvertierung von PDF-Seiten in JPG-Bilder zur Bildanalyse","Integration von PDF-Daten in OpenAI Vector Stores"],"pt":["Rastreamento de sites do SharePoint para conteúdo em PDF","Conversão de páginas em PDF em imagens JPG para análise de visão","Integração de dados em PDF em lojas de vetores OpenAI"],"ru":["Поиск сайтов SharePoint для контента PDF","Преобразование страниц PDF в изображения JPG для анализа зрения","Интеграция данных PDF в векторные хранилища OpenAI"],"ar":["التقصي في مواقع SharePoint لمحتوى PDF","تحويل صفحات PDF إلى صور JPG لتحليل الرؤية","تكامل بيانات PDF في مخازن متجهة OpenAI"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Azure Web App setup","Python environment needed","Dependent on OpenAI Vector Stores and SharePoint site access"],"zh":["需要Azure Web App设置","需要Python环境","依赖于OpenAI Vector Stores和SharePoint站点访问"],"ja":["Azure Web Appの設定が必要","Python環境が必要","OpenAI Vector StoresとSharePointサイトへのアクセスに依存"],"ko":["Azure Web App 설정 필요","Python 환경 필요","OpenAI Vector Stores 및 SharePoint 사이트 액세스에 의존"],"es":["Requiere configuración de Azure Web App","Entorno Python necesario","Depende de OpenAI Vector Stores y del acceso al sitio de SharePoint"],"fr":["Nécessite la configuration d''Azure Web App","Environnement Python requis","Dépend d''OpenAI Vector Stores et de l''accès au site SharePoint"],"de":["Erfordert Einrichtung einer Azure Web App","Python-Umgebung erforderlich","Abhängig von OpenAI Vector Stores und SharePoint-Zugriff"],"pt":["Requer configuração do Azure Web App","Ambiente Python necessário","Dependente de lojas de vetores OpenAI e acesso ao site do SharePoint"],"ru":["Требуется настройка Azure Web App","Необходимо окружение Python","Зависит от векторных хранилищ OpenAI и доступа к сайту SharePoint"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد تطبيق Azure Web","بيئة بايثون ضرورية","يعتمد على مخازن متجهة OpenAI ووصول إلى موقع SharePoint"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
