n Sie, wie Sie APIs mit Designprinzipien für REST und GraphQL erstellen, um intuitive und skalierbare APIs zu erstellen","pt":"Domine os princípios de design de API REST e GraphQL para criar APIs intuitivas e escaláveis","ru":"Освойте принципы дизайна API REST и GraphQL, чтобы создавать интуитивные и масштабируемые API","ar":"استمتع بتصميم واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الممتازة والقابلة للتوسيع باستخدام مبادئ تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST و GraphQL","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["RESTAPI","GraphQLAPI","API","API","API","API"],"ja":["RESTAPI","GraphQLAPI","API","API","API","API"],"ko":["RESTAPI ","GraphQLAPI ","API ","API ","API ","API "],"es":["Diseño de APIs REST y GraphQL","Creación de APIs intuitivas y escalables","Establecimiento de estándares de diseño de API","Revisión de especificaciones de API","Migración entre paradigmas de API","Creación de documentación de API para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Conception d''API REST et GraphQL","Création d''API intuitives et évolutives","Établissement de normes de conception d''API","Révision de spécifications d''API","Migration entre les paradigmes d''API","Création de documentation d''API pour les développeurs"],"de":["Erstellung von REST- und GraphQL-APIs","Erstellung intuitiver und skalierbarer APIs","Festlegung von Designstandards für APIs","Überprüfung von API-Spezifikationen","Migration zwischen API-Paradigmen","Erstellung von API-Dokumentation für Entwickler"],"pt":["Design de API REST","Design de API GraphQL","Criação de APIs escaláveis","Criação de APIs intuitivas","Revisão de especificações de API","Migração entre paradigmas de API"],"ru":["Дизайн API REST","Дизайн API GraphQL","Создание масштабируемых API","Создание интуитивных API","Проверка спецификаций API","Миграция между парадигмами API"],"ar":["تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST","تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات GraphQL","إنشاء واجهات برمجة التطبيقات القابلة للتوسيع","إنشاء واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الممتازة","استعراض مواصفات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","هجرة بين أنماط واجهة برمجة التطبيقات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["API","RESTAPI","GraphQLAPI","API","API","API","API","API"],"ja":["API","RESTAPI","GraphQLAPI","API","API","API","API","API"],"ko":["API ","RESTAPI ","GraphQLAPI ","API ","API ","API ","API ","API "],"es":["diseño de API","principios de diseño de API","REST","GraphQL","API escalable","API mantenible","documentación de API","desarrollo de API"],"fr":["conception d''API","principes de conception d''API","REST","GraphQL","API évolutives","API maintenables","documentation d''API","développement d''API"],"de":["API-Design","Designprinzipien für APIs","REST","GraphQL","skalierbare API","wartbare API","API-Dokumentation","API-Entwicklung"],"pt":["princípios de design de API","API REST","API GraphQL","design de API","criação de APIs","revisão de especificações de API","migração de API","desenvolvimento de API","otimização de API"],"ru":["принципы дизайна API","API REST","API GraphQL","дизайн API","создание API","проверка спецификаций API","миграция API","разработка API","оптимизация API"],"ar":["مبادئ تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST","واجهة برمجة التطبيقات GraphQL","تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","إنشاء واجهات برمجة التطبيقات","استعراض مواصفات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","هجرة واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","تطوير واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","تحسين واجهة برمجة التطبيقات"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"orchestrator","repoPath":"ollieb89/orchestrator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"api-design-principles","description":"Master REST and GraphQL API design principles to build intuitive, scalable, and maintainable APIs that delight developers. Use when designing new APIs, reviewing API specifications, or establishing API design standards.","bodyPreview":"# API Design Principles\n\nMaster REST and GraphQL API design principles to build intuitive, scalable, and maintainable APIs that delight developers and stand the test of time.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new REST or GraphQL APIs\n- Refactoring existing APIs for better usability\n- Establishing API design standards for your team\n- Reviewing API specifications before implementation\n- Migrating between API paradigms (REST to GraphQL, etc.)\n- Creating developer-friendly API documentation\n-","body":"# API Design Principles\n\nMaster REST and GraphQL API design principles to build intuitive, scalable, and maintainable APIs that delight developers and stand the test of time.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new REST or GraphQL APIs\n- Refactoring existing APIs for better usability\n- Establishing API design standards for your team\n- Reviewing API specifications before implementation\n- Migrating between API paradigms (REST to GraphQL, etc.)\n- Creating developer-friendly API documentation\n- Optimizing APIs for specific use cases (mobile, third-party integrations)\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. RESTful Design Principles\n\n**Resource-Oriented Architecture**\n- Resources are nouns (users, orders, products), not verbs\n- Use HTTP methods for actions (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE)\n- URLs represent resource hierarchies\n- Consistent naming conventions\n\n**HTTP Methods Semantics:**\n- `GET`: Retrieve resources (idempotent, safe)\n- `POST`: Create new resources\n- `PUT`: Replace entire resource (idempotent)\n- `PATCH`: Partial resource updates\n- `DELETE`: Remove resources (idempotent)\n\n### 2. GraphQL Design Principles\n\n**Schema-First Development**\n- Types define your domain model\n- Queries for reading data\n- Mutations for modifying data\n- Subscriptions for real-time updates\n\n**Query Structure:**\n- Clients request exactly what they need\n- Single endpoint, multiple operations\n- Strongly typed schema\n- Introspection built-in\n\n### 3. API Versioning Strategies\n\n**URL Versioning:**\n```\n/api/v1/users\n/api/v2/users\n```\n\n**Header Versioning:**\n```\nAccept: application/vnd.api+json; version=1\n```\n\n**Query Parameter Versioning:**\n```\n/api/users?version=1\n```\n\n## REST API Design Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Resource Collection Design\n\n```python\n# Good: Resource-oriented endpoints\nGET    /api/users              # List users (with pagination)\nPOST   /api/users              # Create user\nGET    /api/users/{id}         # Get specific user\nPUT    /api/users/{id}         # Replace user\nPATCH  /api/users/{id}         # Update user fields\nDELETE /api/users/{id}         # Delete user\n\n# Nested resources\nGET    /api/users/{id}/orders  # Get user''s orders\nPOST   /api/users/{id}/orders  # Create order for user\n\n# Bad: Action-oriented endpoints (avoid)\nPOST   /api/createUser\nPOST   /api/getUserById\nPOST   /api/deleteUser\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Pagination and Filtering\n\n```python\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nclass PaginationParams(BaseModel):\n    page: int = Field(1, ge=1, description=\"Page number\")\n    page_size: int = Field(20, ge=1, le=100, description=\"Items per page\")\n\nclass FilterParams(BaseModel):\n    status: Optional[str] = None\n    created_after: Optional[str] = None\n    search: Optional[str] = None\n\nclass PaginatedResponse(BaseModel):\n    items: List[dict]\n    total: int\n    page: int\n    page_size: int\n    pages: int\n\n    @property\n    def has_next(self) -> bool:\n        return self.page < self.pages\n\n    @property\n    def has_prev(self) -> bool:\n        return self.page > 1\n\n# FastAPI endpoint example\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Query, Depends\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/api/users\", response_model=PaginatedResponse)\nasync def list_users(\n    page: int = Query(1, ge=1),\n    page_size: int = Query(20, ge=1, le=100),\n    status: Optional[str] = Query(None),\n    search: Optional[str] = Query(None)\n):\n    # Apply filters\n    query = build_query(status=status, search=search)\n\n    # Count total\n    total = await count_users(query)\n\n    # Fetch page\n    offset = (page - 1) * page_size\n    users = await fetch_users(query, limit=page_size, offset=offset)\n\n    return PaginatedResponse(\n        items=users,\n        total=total,\n        page=page,\n        page_size=page_size,\n        pages=(total + page_size - 1) // page_size\n    )\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Error Handling and Status Codes\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import HTTPException, status\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass ErrorResponse(BaseModel):\n    error: str\n    message: str\n    details: Optional[dict] = None\n    timestamp: str\n    path: str\n\nclass ValidationErrorDetail(BaseModel):\n    field: str\n    message: str\n    value: Any\n\n# Consistent error responses\nSTATUS_CODES = {\n    \"success\": 200,\n    \"created\": 201,\n    \"no_content\": 204,\n    \"bad_request\": 400,\n    \"unauthorized\": 401,\n    \"forbidden\": 403,\n    \"not_found\": 404,\n    \"conflict\": 409,\n    \"unprocessable\": 422,\n    \"internal_error\": 500\n}\n\ndef raise_not_found(resource: str, id: str):\n    raise HTTPException(\n        status_code=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND,\n        detail={\n            \"error\": \"NotFound\",\n            \"message\": f\"{resource} not found\",\n            \"details\": {\"id\": id}\n        }\n    )\n\ndef raise_validation_error(errors: List[ValidationErrorDetail]):\n    raise HTTPException(\n        status_code=status.HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY,\n        detail={\n            \"error\": \"ValidationError\",\n            \"message\": \"Request validation failed\",\n            \"details\": {\"errors\": [e.dict() for e in errors]}\n        }\n    )\n\n# Example usage\n@app.get(\"/api/users/{user_id}\")\nasync def get_user(user_id: str):\n    user = await fetch_user(user_id)\n    if not user:\n        raise_not_found(\"User\", user_id)\n    return user\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: HATEOAS (Hypermedia as the Engine of Application State)\n\n```python\nclass UserResponse(BaseModel):\n    id: str\n    name: str\n    email: str\n    _links: dict\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_user(cls, user: User, base_url: str):\n        return cls(\n            id=user.id,\n            name=user.name,\n            email=user.email,\n            _links={\n                \"self\": {\"href\": f\"{base_url}/api/users/{user.id}\"},\n                \"orders\": {\"href\": f\"{base_url}/api/users/{user.id}/orders\"},\n                \"update\": {\n                    \"href\": f\"{base_url}/api/users/{user.id}\",\n                    \"method\": \"PATCH\"\n                },\n                \"delete\": {\n                    \"href\": f\"{base_url}/api/users/{user.id}\",\n                    \"method\": \"DELETE\"\n                }\n            }\n        )\n```\n\n## GraphQL Design Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Schema Design\n\n```graphql\n# schema.graphql\n\n# Clear type definitions\ntype User {\n  id: ID!\n  email: String!\n  name: String!\n  createdAt: DateTime!\n\n  # Relationships\n  orders(\n    first: Int = 20\n    after: String\n    status: OrderStatus\n  ): OrderConnection!\n\n  profile: UserProfile\n}\n\ntype Order {\n  id: ID!\n  status: OrderStatus!\n  total: Money!\n  items: [OrderItem!]!\n  createdAt: DateTime!\n\n  # Back-reference\n  user: User!\n}\n\n# Pagination pattern (Relay-style)\ntype OrderConnection {\n  edges: [OrderEdge!]!\n  pageInfo: PageInfo!\n  totalCount: Int!\n}\n\ntype OrderEdge {\n  node: Order!\n  cursor: String!\n}\n\ntype PageInfo {\n  hasNextPage: Boolean!\n  hasPreviousPage: Boolean!\n  startCursor: String\n  endCursor: String\n}\n\n# Enums for type safety\nenum OrderStatus {\n  PENDING\n  CONFIRMED\n  SHIPPED\n  DELIVERED\n  CANCELLED\n}\n\n# Custom scalars\nscalar DateTime\nscalar Money\n\n# Query root\ntype Query {\n  user(id: ID!): User\n  users(\n    first: Int = 20\n    after: String\n    search: String\n  ): UserConnection!\n\n  order(id: ID!): Order\n}\n\n# Mutation root\ntype Mutation {\n  createUser(input: CreateUserInput!): CreateUserPayload!\n  updateUser(input: UpdateUserInput!): UpdateUserPayload!\n  deleteUser(id: ID!): DeleteUserPayload!\n\n  createOrder(input: CreateOrderInput!): CreateOrderPayload!\n}\n\n# Input types for mutations\ninput CreateUserInput {\n  email: String!\n  name: String!\n  password: String!\n}\n\n# Payload types for mutations\ntype CreateUserPayload {\n  user: User\n  errors: [Error!]\n}\n\ntype Error {\n  field: String\n  message: String!\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Resolver Design\n\n```python\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom ariadne import QueryType, MutationType, ObjectType\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\nquery = QueryType()\nmutation = MutationType()\nuser_type = ObjectType(\"User\")\n\n@query.field(\"user\")\nasync def resolve_user(obj, info, id: str) -> Optional[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Resolve single user by ID.\"\"\"\n    return await fetch_user_by_id(id)\n\n@query.field(\"users\")\nasync def resolve_users(\n    obj,\n    info,\n    first: int = 20,\n    after: Optional[str] = None,\n    search: Optional[str] = None\n) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Resolve paginated user list.\"\"\"\n    # Decode cursor\n    offset = decode_cursor(after) if after else 0\n\n    # Fetch users\n    users = await fetch_users(\n        limit=first + 1,  # Fetch one extra to check hasNextPage\n        offset=offset,\n        search=search\n    )\n\n    # Pagination\n    has_next = len(users) > first\n    if has_next:\n        users = users[:first]\n\n    edges = [\n        {\n            \"node\": user,\n            \"cursor\": encode_cursor(offset + i)\n        }\n        for i, user in enumerate(users)\n    ]\n\n    return {\n        \"edges\": edges,\n        \"pageInfo\": {\n            \"hasNextPage\": has_next,\n            \"hasPreviousPage\": offset > 0,\n            \"startCursor\": edges[0][\"cursor\"] if edges else None,\n            \"endCursor\": edges[-1][\"cursor\"] if edges else None\n        },\n        \"totalCount\": await count_users(search=search)\n    }\n\n@user_type.field(\"orders\")\nasync def resolve_user_orders(user: dict, info, first: int = 20) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Resolve user''s orders (N+1 prevention with DataLoader).\"\"\"\n    # Use DataLoader to batch requests\n    loader = info.context[\"loaders\"][\"orders_by_user\"]\n    orders = await loader.load(user[\"id\"])\n\n    return paginate_orders(orders, first)\n\n@mutation.field(\"createUser\")\nasync def resolve_create_user(obj, info, input: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Create new user.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Validate input\n        validate_user_input(input)\n\n        # Create user\n        user = await create_user(\n            email=input[\"email\"],\n            name=input[\"name\"],\n            password=hash_password(input[\"password\"])\n        )\n\n        return {\n            \"user\": user,\n            \"errors\": []\n        }\n    except ValidationError as e:\n        return {\n            \"user\": None,\n            \"errors\": [{\"field\": e.field, \"message\": e.message}]\n        }\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: DataLoader (N+1 Problem Prevention)\n\n```python\nfrom aiodataloader import DataLoader\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nclass UserLoader(DataLoader):\n    \"\"\"Batch load users by ID.\"\"\"\n\n    async def batch_load_fn(self, user_ids: List[str]) -> List[Optional[dict]]:\n        \"\"\"Load multiple users in single query.\"\"\"\n        users = await fetch_users_by_ids(user_ids)\n\n        # Map results back to input order\n        user_map = {user[\"id\"]: user for user in users}\n        return [user_map.get(user_id) for user_id in user_ids]\n\nclass OrdersByUserLoader(DataLoader):\n    \"\"\"Batch load orders by user ID.\"\"\"\n\n    async def batch_load_fn(self, user_ids: List[str]) -> List[List[dict]]:\n        \"\"\"Load orders for multiple users in single query.\"\"\"\n        orders = await fetch_orders_by_user_ids(user_ids)\n\n        # Group orders by user_id\n        orders_by_user = {}\n        for order in orders:\n            user_id = order[\"user_id\"]\n            if user_id not in orders_by_user:\n                orders_by_user[user_id] = []\n            orders_by_user[user_id].append(order)\n\n        # Return in input order\n        return [orders_by_user.get(user_id, []) for user_id in user_ids]\n\n# Context setup\ndef create_context():\n    return {\n        \"loaders\": {\n            \"user\": UserLoader(),\n            \"orders_by_user\": OrdersByUserLoader()\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### REST APIs\n1. **Consistent Naming**: Use plural nouns for collections (`/users`, not `/user`)\n2. **Stateless**: Each request contains all necessary information\n3. **Use HTTP Status Codes Correctly**: 2xx success, 4xx client errors, 5xx server errors\n4. **Version Your API**: Plan for breaking changes from day one\n5. **Pagination**: Always paginate large collections\n6. **Rate Limiting**: Protect your API with rate limits\n7. **Documentation**: Use OpenAPI/Swagger for interactive docs\n\n### GraphQL APIs\n1. **Schema First**: Design schema before writing resolvers\n2. **Avoid N+1**: Use DataLoaders for efficient data fetching\n3. **Input Validation**: Validate at schema and resolver levels\n4. **Error Handling**: Return structured errors in mutation payloads\n5. **Pagination**: Use cursor-based pagination (Relay spec)\n6. **Deprecation**: Use `@deprecated` directive for gradual migration\n7. **Monitoring**: Track query complexity and execution time\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Over-fetching/Under-fetching (REST)**: Fixed in GraphQL but requires DataLoaders\n- **Breaking Changes**: Version APIs or use deprecation strategies\n- **Inconsistent Error Formats**: Standardize error responses\n- **Missing Rate Limits**: APIs without limits are vulnerable to abuse\n- **Poor Documentation**: Undocumented APIs frustrate developers\n- **Ignoring HTTP Semantics**: POST for idempotent operations breaks expectations\n- **Tight Coupling**: API structure shouldn''t mirror database schema\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/rest-best-practices.md**: Comprehensive REST API design guide\n- **references/graphql-schema-design.md**: GraphQL schema patterns and anti-patterns\n- **references/api-versioning-strategies.md**: Versioning approaches and migration paths\n- **assets/rest-api-template.py**: FastAPI REST API template\n- **assets/graphql-schema-template.graphql**: Complete GraphQL schema example\n- **assets/api-design-checklist.md**: Pre-implementation review checklist\n- **scripts/openapi-generator.py**: Generate OpenAPI specs from code\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:34:01.722Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Developer Agents needing expertise in REST and GraphQL API design principles","zh":"适合需要REST和GraphQL API设计原则专业知识的开发者代理","ja":"RESTとGraphQL APIの設計原則の専門知識が必要な開発者エージェントに適しています","ko":"REST와 GraphQL API 설계 원리의 전문 지식이 필요한 개발자 에이전트에게 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollador que necesitan experiencia en principios de diseño de API REST y GraphQL","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant une expertise dans les principes de conception d''API REST et GraphQL","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsagenten, die Erfahrung in REST- und GraphQL-API-Designprinzipien benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedor que necessitam de especialização em princípios de design de API REST e GraphQL","ru":"Идеально для агентов-разработчиков, которым необходимы знания в области принципов проектирования REST и GraphQL API","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المطورين الذين يحتاجون إلى خبرة في مبادئ تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST و GraphQL"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design intuitive, scalable, and maintainable APIs using REST and GraphQL, creating developer-friendly API documentation and establishing API design standards for teams, all while leveraging API paradigms like REST to GraphQL migrations","zh":"赋予代理设计直观、可扩展和可维护的API的能力，使用REST和GraphQL，创建开发者友好的API文档，并为团队建立API设计标准，同时利用REST到GraphQL迁移等API范式","ja":"エージェントが直感的でスケーラブルでメンテナンス可能なAPIを設計できるようにし、RESTとGraphQLを使用して開発者フレンドリーなAPIドキュメントを作成し、チームのためのAPI設計標準を確立し、同時にRESTからGraphQLへの移行などのAPIパラダイムを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 직관적이고 확장 가능하며 유지 보수 가능한 API를 설계할 수 있도록 하며 REST와 GraphQL을 사용하여 개발자 친화적인 API 문서를 생성하고 팀의 API 설계 표준을 설정하며 동시에 REST에서 GraphQL로의 마이그레이션과 같은 API 패러다임을 활용함으로써","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar API intuitivas, escalables y mantenibles utilizando REST y GraphQL, creando documentación de API amigable para desarrolladores y estableciendo estándares de diseño de API para equipos, todo mientras aprovecha los paradigmas de API como las migraciones de REST a GraphQL","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des API intuitives, évolutives et maintenables en utilisant REST et GraphQL, en créant une documentation d''API conviviale pour les développeurs et en établissant des normes de conception d''API pour les équipes, tout en exploitant les paradigmes d''API tels que les migrations de REST à GraphQL","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, intuitive, skalierbare und wartbare APIs mit REST und GraphQL zu entwerfen, entwicklerfreundliche API-Dokumentation zu erstellen und API-Designstandards für Teams zu etablieren, während sie API-Paradigmen wie REST-zu-GraphQL-Migrationen nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar APIs intuitivas, escaláveis e mantenedoras usando REST e GraphQL, criando documentação de API amigável para desenvolvedores e estabelecendo padrões de design de API para equipes, tudo isso aproveitando paradigmas de API como migrações de REST para GraphQL","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать интуитивные, масштабируемые и поддерживаемые API с использованием REST и GraphQL, создавая документацию API, удобную для разработчиков, и устанавливая стандарты проектирования API для команд, все это при помощи использования парадигм API, таких как миграция с REST на GraphQL","ar":"يُمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تصميم واجهات برمجة التطبيقات المتوافقة والقابلة للتوسيع والصيانة باستخدام REST و GraphQL، مما يتيح إنشاء توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الصديق للمطورين وإنشاء معايير تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات للفرق، مع الاستفادة من سلاسل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات مثل الانتقال من REST إلى GraphQL"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing new REST or GraphQL APIs","Refactoring existing APIs for better usability","Establishing API design standards for teams","Reviewing API specifications before implementation","Migrating between API paradigms"],"zh":["设计新的REST或GraphQL API","重构现有的API以提高可用性","为团队建立API设计标准","在实现之前审查API规范","在API范式之间迁移"],"ja":["新しいRESTまたはGraphQL APIを設計する","既存のAPIをリファクタリングして使いやすさを向上させる","チームのためのAPI設計標準を確立する","実装前にAPI仕様をレビューする","APIパラダイム間で移行する"],"ko":["新的 REST 또는 GraphQL API를 설계한다","既存의 API를 리팩토링하여 사용 편의성을 향상시키다","팀의 API 설계 표준을 설정하다","구현 전에 API 사양을 검토하다","API 패러다임 사이에서 마이그레이션하다"],"es":["Diseñar nuevas API REST o GraphQL","Reorganizar API existentes para una mejor usabilidad","Establecer estándares de diseño de API para equipos","Revisar especificaciones de API antes de la implementación","Migrar entre paradigmas de API"],"fr":["Concevoir de nouvelles API REST ou GraphQL","Réorganiser les API existantes pour une meilleure convivialité","Établir des normes de conception d''API pour les équipes","Réviser les spécifications d''API avant la mise en œuvre","Migrer entre les paradigmes d''API"],"de":["Neue REST- oder GraphQL-APIs entwerfen","Vorhandene APIs für bessere Benutzerfreundlichkeit neu organisieren","API-Designstandards für Teams etablieren","API-Spezifikationen vor der Implementierung überprüfen","Zwischen API-Paradigmen migrieren"],"pt":["Projetar novas APIs REST ou GraphQL","Reestruturar APIs existentes para melhor usabilidade","Estabelecer padrões de design de API para equipes","Revisar especificações de API antes da implementação","Migrar entre paradigmas de API"],"ru":["Проектировать новые API REST или GraphQL","Рефакторить существующие API для лучшей удобства использования","Устанавливать стандарты проектирования API для команд","Просматривать спецификации API перед реализацией","Мигрировать между парадигмами API"],"ar":["تصميم واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الجديدة REST أو GraphQL","إعادة هيكلة واجهات برمجة التطبيقات الحالية لتحسين سهولة الاستخدام","إنشاء معايير تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات للفرق","مراجعة مواصفات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات قبل التنفيذ","الانتقال بين سلاسل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of REST and GraphQL fundamentals","Limited to API design principles, not implementation"],"zh":["需要REST和GraphQL基础知识","仅限API设计原则，不包括实现"],"ja":["RESTとGraphQLの基礎知識が必要","API設計原則のみ、実装は含まない"],"ko":["REST와 GraphQL의 기본 지식이 필요하다","API 설계 원칙만 해당되며 구현은 포함하지 않는다"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de los fundamentos de REST y GraphQL","Limitado a los principios de diseño de API, no a la implementación"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances sur les fondamentaux de REST et GraphQL","Limité aux principes de conception d''API, et non à la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse in REST- und GraphQL-Grundlagen","Begrenzt auf API-Designprinzipien, nicht auf Implementierung"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento dos fundamentos de REST e GraphQL","Limitado a princípios de design de API, não implementação"],"ru":["Требует знания основ REST и GraphQL","Ограничен принципами проектирования API, не реализацией"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة أساسيات REST و GraphQL","محدود بمبادئ تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات، وليس التنفيذ"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
