بفعالية","en":"debugging"},"description":{"zh":"调试技能是指使用系统化的方法来识别和解决软件问题，提高开发效率","ja":"デバッグスキルは、システム化された方法を使用してソフトウェアの問題を特定し解決することにより、開発効率を向上させる","ko":"디버깅 스킬은 시스템화된 방법을 사용하여 소프트웨어 문제를 식별하고 해결하여 개발 효율성을 높이는 것입니다","es":"Nuestro enfoque de depuración de código es una metodología sistemática para identificar y resolver bugs de manera eficiente.","fr":"Notre approche de débogage de code est une méthodologie systématique pour identifier et résoudre les bogues de manière efficace.","de":"Unser Fehlerbehebungsansatz ist eine systematische Methode, um Fehler effizient zu identifizieren und zu beheben.","pt":"O LLMProxy é uma ferramenta de depuração que ajuda a identificar e resolver erros de forma eficiente.","ru":"LLMProxy - это инструмент для отладки, который помогает выявить и решить ошибки эффективно.","ar":"LLMProxy هو أداة تصحيح أخطاء تساعد على تحديد وحل المشكلات بفعالية.","en":"Seamlessly route requests to your LLM backends—whether you''re using stream=false for standard JSON responses or stream=true for real-time token streaming via..."},"definition":{"en":"Seamlessly route requests to your LLM backends—whether you''re using stream=false for standard JSON responses or stream=true for real-time token streaming via Server-Sent Events (SSE). LLMProxy handles both modes out of the box, with zero buffering on streams, intelligent load balancing, and OpenAI-compatible API routing."},"features":{"zh":["系统化的调试过程","高效的BUG解决","提高开发效率","智能的错误跟踪","实时的错误报告"],"ja":["システム化されたデバッグプロセス","効率的なバグ解決","開発効率の向上","インテリジェントなエラートレーシング","リアルタイムのエラー報告"],"ko":["시스템화된 디버깅 프로세스","효율적인 버그 해결","개발 효율성 향상","지능형 오류 추적","실시간 오류 보고"],"es":["Reproducción del problema","Análisis de errores","Identificación de causas raíz","Resolución de bugs","Optimización de código"],"fr":["Reproduction du problème","Analyse des erreurs","Identification des causes profondes","Résolution des bogues","Optimisation du code"],"de":["Reproduktion des Problems","Fehleranalyse","Identifizierung der Ursachen","Behebung von Fehlern","Code-Optimierung"],"pt":["Reproduzir erros","Rastrear origens de erros","Corrigir problemas de produção","Entender comportamento inesperado","Uso de Server-Sent Events (SSE)","Compatibilidade com OpenAI"],"ru":["Репроизводить ошибки","Отслеживать источники ошибок","Исправлять проблемы производства","Понимать неожиданное поведение","Использование Server-Sent Events (SSE)","Совместимость с OpenAI"],"ar":["إعادة إنتاج الأخطاء","تتبع مصادر الأخطاء","إصلاح مشاكل الإنتاج","فهم السلوك غير المتوقع","استخدام Server-Sent Events (SSE)","التوافق مع OpenAI"]},"keywords":{"zh":["调试技能","软件开发","BUG解决","开发效率","系统化调试","错误跟踪","实时错误报告"],"ja":["デバッグスキル","ソフトウェア開発","バグ解決","開発効率","システム化されたデバッグ","エラートレーシング","リアルタイムエラー報告"],"ko":["디버깅 스킬","소프트웨어 개발","버그 해결","개발 효율성","시스템화된 디버깅","오류 추적","실시간 오류 보고"],"es":["depuración de código","desarrollo de software","identificación de errores","resolución de bugs","optimización de código","metodología de depuración","herramientas de depuración"],"fr":["débogage de code","développement de logiciels","identification des erreurs","résolution des bogues","optimisation du code","méthodologie de débogage","outils de débogage"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung","Software-Entwicklung","Fehleridentifizierung","Behebung von Fehlern","Code-Optimierung","Fehlerbehebungsansatz","Debugging-Tools"],"pt":["depuração de código","resolução de erros","LLMProxy","Server-Sent Events","OpenAI","produção de software","desenvolvimento de software","testes de software"],"ru":["отладка кода","решение ошибок","LLMProxy","Server-Sent Events","OpenAI","производство программного обеспечения","разработка программного обеспечения","тестирование программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تصحيح الأخطاء","حل المشكلات","LLMProxy","Server-Sent Events","OpenAI","إنتاج البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات","اختبار البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"aiyuekuang","repo":"LLMProxy","repoPath":"aiyuekuang/LLMProxy","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"debugging","description":"Systematic debugging methodology for finding and fixing bugs. Use when investigating issues, tracing errors, or fixing production problems.","bodyPreview":"# Debugging Skill\n\nMethodical problem-solving approach for identifying and resolving bugs efficiently.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Investigating bug reports\n- Tracing error origins\n- Fixing production issues\n- Understanding unexpected behavior\n\n---\n\n# 🔍 Systematic Debugging Process\n\n## 1. Reproduce the Issue\n\nBefore fixing, confirm you can reproduce:\n\n```markdown\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n1. Navigate to /dashboard\n2. Click \"Create New\" button\n3. Fill form with empty values\n4. Click submit\n5. **","body":"# Debugging Skill\n\nMethodical problem-solving approach for identifying and resolving bugs efficiently.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Investigating bug reports\n- Tracing error origins\n- Fixing production issues\n- Understanding unexpected behavior\n\n---\n\n# 🔍 Systematic Debugging Process\n\n## 1. Reproduce the Issue\n\nBefore fixing, confirm you can reproduce:\n\n```markdown\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n1. Navigate to /dashboard\n2. Click \"Create New\" button\n3. Fill form with empty values\n4. Click submit\n5. **Expected**: Validation error shown\n6. **Actual**: Page crashes with error\n```\n\n## 2. Isolate the Problem\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Is the bug in frontend or backend?    │\n│           ↓                             │\n│  Which component/function?              │\n│           ↓                             │\n│  What input triggers it?                │\n│           ↓                             │\n│  What''s the expected vs actual?         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## 3. Form Hypothesis\n\nBased on symptoms, hypothesize potential causes:\n- Recent code changes?\n- Data-related issue?\n- Race condition?\n- Configuration problem?\n- External dependency failure?\n\n## 4. Test Hypothesis\n\nAdd targeted logging or use debugger to verify:\n\n```go\n// Add strategic logging\nlog.Printf(\"[DEBUG] Handler input: %+v\", input)\nlog.Printf(\"[DEBUG] Database result: %+v, err: %v\", result, err)\nlog.Printf(\"[DEBUG] Response: %+v\", response)\n```\n\n## 5. Fix and Verify\n\n- Make minimal fix for root cause\n- Add regression test\n- Verify fix doesn''t break other functionality\n\n---\n\n# 🐛 Common Bug Patterns\n\n## Null/Nil Reference\n\n```go\n// ❌ Bug: Nil pointer dereference\nfunc (h *Handler) GetName(user *User) string {\n    return user.Name  // Crashes if user is nil\n}\n\n// ✅ Fix: Check for nil\nfunc (h *Handler) GetName(user *User) string {\n    if user == nil {\n        return \"\"\n    }\n    return user.Name\n}\n```\n\n## Off-by-One Errors\n\n```go\n// ❌ Bug: Index out of bounds\nfor i := 0; i <= len(items); i++ {\n    process(items[i])\n}\n\n// ✅ Fix: Correct boundary\nfor i := 0; i < len(items); i++ {\n    process(items[i])\n}\n```\n\n## Race Conditions\n\n```go\n// ❌ Bug: Data race\nvar counter int\ngo func() { counter++ }()\ngo func() { counter++ }()\n\n// ✅ Fix: Use sync primitives\nvar counter int64\ngo func() { atomic.AddInt64(&counter, 1) }()\ngo func() { atomic.AddInt64(&counter, 1) }()\n```\n\n## Memory Leaks\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bug: Event listener not cleaned up\nuseEffect(() => {\n  window.addEventListener(''resize'', handleResize);\n}, []);\n\n// ✅ Fix: Cleanup on unmount\nuseEffect(() => {\n  window.addEventListener(''resize'', handleResize);\n  return () => window.removeEventListener(''resize'', handleResize);\n}, []);\n```\n\n## Async/Await Issues\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Bug: Missing await\nasync function fetchData() {\n  const response = fetch(''/api/data'');  // Missing await\n  return response.json();  // Error: response is a Promise\n}\n\n// ✅ Fix: Proper async handling\nasync function fetchData() {\n  const response = await fetch(''/api/data'');\n  return response.json();\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔧 Debugging Tools\n\n## Go Debugging\n\n### Delve Debugger\n```bash\n# Install\ngo install github.com/go-delve/delve/cmd/dlv@latest\n\n# Debug\ndlv debug ./cmd/main.go\n\n# Set breakpoint\n(dlv) break main.go:42\n(dlv) continue\n(dlv) print variableName\n(dlv) next\n(dlv) step\n```\n\n### Printf Debugging\n```go\nimport \"github.com/davecgh/go-spew/spew\"\n\n// Pretty print complex structures\nspew.Dump(complexObject)\n\n// Or use JSON for readability\ndata, _ := json.MarshalIndent(obj, \"\", \"  \")\nlog.Printf(\"Object: %s\", data)\n```\n\n### Profiling\n```go\nimport _ \"net/http/pprof\"\n\n// Start pprof server\ngo func() {\n    log.Println(http.ListenAndServe(\"localhost:6060\", nil))\n}()\n\n// Access: http://localhost:6060/debug/pprof/\n```\n\n## Frontend Debugging\n\n### Browser DevTools\n- **Console**: Error messages, console.log output\n- **Network**: API requests/responses\n- **Sources**: Breakpoints, step debugging\n- **React DevTools**: Component state, props\n\n### React Query DevTools\n```tsx\nimport { ReactQueryDevtools } from ''@tanstack/react-query-devtools'';\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>\n      <MyApp />\n      <ReactQueryDevtools initialIsOpen={false} />\n    </QueryClientProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Strategic Console Logging\n```typescript\n// Group related logs\nconsole.group(''Form Submission'');\nconsole.log(''Form data:'', formData);\nconsole.log(''Validation result:'', validationResult);\nconsole.groupEnd();\n\n// Trace execution path\nconsole.trace(''How did we get here?'');\n\n// Measure performance\nconsole.time(''API Call'');\nawait fetchData();\nconsole.timeEnd(''API Call'');\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔬 Root Cause Analysis\n\n## The 5 Whys Technique\n\n```markdown\n**Problem**: User cannot login\n\n1. Why? → Login API returns 500 error\n2. Why? → Database query fails\n3. Why? → Connection pool exhausted\n4. Why? → Connections not being released\n5. Why? → Missing defer db.Close() in handler\n\n**Root Cause**: Resource leak due to missing cleanup\n**Fix**: Add proper connection release\n```\n\n## Bisect to Find Culprit\n\n```bash\n# Use git bisect to find the commit that introduced the bug\ngit bisect start\ngit bisect bad HEAD          # Current version is broken\ngit bisect good v1.0.0       # v1.0.0 was working\n\n# Git will checkout middle commit, test it, then:\ngit bisect good  # or\ngit bisect bad\n\n# Continue until culprit is found\ngit bisect reset  # When done\n```\n\n---\n\n# 📊 Logging Best Practices\n\n## Structured Logging\n\n```go\nimport \"go.uber.org/zap\"\n\nlogger, _ := zap.NewProduction()\ndefer logger.Sync()\n\nlogger.Info(\"request processed\",\n    zap.String(\"method\", r.Method),\n    zap.String(\"path\", r.URL.Path),\n    zap.Int(\"status\", status),\n    zap.Duration(\"duration\", time.Since(start)),\n    zap.String(\"request_id\", requestID),\n)\n```\n\n## Log Levels\n\n- **ERROR**: Failures requiring immediate attention\n- **WARN**: Unexpected but recoverable situations\n- **INFO**: Important business events\n- **DEBUG**: Detailed diagnostic information\n\n## What to Log\n\n✅ **Do Log**:\n- Request/response metadata (not sensitive data)\n- Error details with context\n- Performance metrics\n- Security events (login attempts, permission denials)\n\n❌ **Don''t Log**:\n- Passwords, API keys, tokens\n- Personal identifiable information (PII)\n- Credit card numbers\n- Health information\n\n---\n\n# 📚 References\n\n- [obra/systematic-debugging](https://github.com/obra/superpowers/blob/main/skills/systematic-debugging/SKILL.md)\n- [obra/root-cause-tracing](https://github.com/obra/superpowers/blob/main/skills/root-cause-tracing/SKILL.md)\n- [getsentry/find-bugs](https://github.com/getsentry/skills/tree/main/plugins/sentry-skills/skills/find-bugs)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:35:11.192Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring systematic debugging methodologies for complex software issues.","zh":"适用于需要系统调试方法的代码分析代理，用于解决复杂软件问题。","ja":"複雑なソフトウェアの問題を解決するために、体系的なデバッグ方法論を必要とするコード分析エージェントに適しています。","ko":"복잡한 소프트웨어 문제를 해결하기 위한 체계적인 디버깅 방법론을 필요로 하는 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis de Código que requieren metodologías de depuración sistemáticas para problemas de software complejos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant des méthodologies de débogage systématiques pour des problèmes de logiciel complexes.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die systematische Fehlersuche-Methoden für komplexe Softwareprobleme erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que requerem metodologias de depuração sistemáticas para problemas de software complexos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих систематических методологий отладки для сложных проблем программного обеспечения.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الكود الذي يتطلب منهجيات تحليل منهجية لمشاكل البرامج المعقدة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement methodical debugging processes including issue reproduction, error origin tracing, and production issue resolution. Provides structured frameworks for investigating bug reports and understanding unexpected system behavior through systematic analysis.","zh":"赋予代理实施系统调试流程的能力，包括问题重现、错误来源追踪和生产问题解决。为调查错误报告和理解系统行为提供了结构化框架。","ja":"エージェントに、問題の再現、エラーオリジンの追跡、および生産問題の解決を含む体系的なデバッグプロセスを実装する能力を与えます。バグレポートの調査と予期しないシステム動作の理解のための構造化フレームワークを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 체계적인 디버깅 프로세스를 구현할 수 있도록 하며, 문제 재현, 오류 원인 추적 및 생산 문제 해결을 포함합니다. 버그 보고서 조사 및 예기치 않은 시스템 동작 이해를 위한 구조화된 프레임워크를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar procesos de depuración metódicos que incluyen la reproducción de problemas, el seguimiento del origen de los errores y la resolución de problemas de producción. Proporciona marcos estructurados para investigar informes de errores y comprender el comportamiento del sistema inesperado a través del análisis sistemático.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des processus de débogage méthodiques comprenant la reproduction de problèmes, le traçage de l''origine des erreurs et la résolution de problèmes de production. Fournit des cadres structurés pour enquêter sur les rapports de bogue et comprendre le comportement système inattendu grâce à l''analyse systématique.","de":"Ermöglich es Agents, methodische Fehlersuche-Prozesse umzusetzen, einschließlich der Reproduktion von Fehlern, der Rückverfolgung von Fehlerursachen und der Behebung von Produktionsproblemen. Bietet strukturierte Rahmenbedingungen für die Untersuchung von Fehlerberichten und das Verständnis unerwarteten Systemverhaltens durch systematische Analyse.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar processos de depuração metódicos, incluindo reprodução de problemas, rastreamento da origem dos erros e resolução de problemas de produção. Fornece estruturas sistemáticas para investigar relatórios de bugs e entender o comportamento inesperado do sistema por meio da análise sistemática.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать методические процессы отладки, включая воспроизведение проблем, отслеживание источников ошибок и решение проблем производства. Предоставляет структурированные рамки для расследования отчетов об ошибках и понимания неожиданного поведения системы посредством системного анализа.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تنفيذ عمليات تحليل منهجية، بما في ذلك إعادة إنتاج المشاكل وتتبع مصدر الأخطاء وحل مشاكل الإنتاج. يوفر إطارات منهجية منظمة لتحقيق تقارير الأخطاء وفهم سلوك النظام غير المتوقع من خلال التحليل المنهجي."},"useCases":{"en":["Reproducing reported bugs using specific reproduction steps","Tracing error origins through systematic code analysis","Fixing production issues with methodical debugging approaches","Investigating unexpected system behavior patterns"],"zh":["使用特定的重现步骤重现报告的错误","通过系统代码分析追踪错误来源","使用有方法的调试方法解决生产问题","调查意外的系统行为模式"],"ja":["特定の再現手順を使用して報告されたバグを再現する","体系的なコード分析を使用してエラーオリジンを追跡する","方法的なデバッグアプローチを使用して生産問題を解決する","予期しないシステム動作パターンを調査する"],"ko":["특정 재현 단계를 사용하여 보고된 버그를 재현하는 것","체계적인 코드 분석을 통해 오류 원인을 추적하는 것","체계적인 디버깅 접근 방식을 사용하여 생산 문제를 해결하는 것","예기치 않은 시스템 동작 패턴을 조사하는 것"],"es":["Reproducir errores informados utilizando pasos de reproducción específicos","Rastrear los orígenes de los errores a través del análisis de código sistemático","Solucionar problemas de producción con enfoques de depuración metódicos","Investigar patrones de comportamiento del sistema inesperado"],"fr":["Reproduire des bogues signalés en utilisant des étapes de reproduction spécifiques","Traçer les origines des erreurs grâce à l''analyse de code systématique","Résoudre des problèmes de production avec des approches de débogage méthodiques","Enquêter sur les modèles de comportement système inattendus"],"de":["Gemeldete Fehler unter Verwendung spezifischer Reproduktionsschritte reproduzieren","Fehlerursachen durch systematische Code-Analyse zurückverfolgen","Produktionsprobleme mit methodischen Fehlersuche-Ansätzen beheben","Muster unerwarteten Systemverhaltens untersuchen"],"pt":["Reproduzir bugs relatados usando etapas de reprodução específicas","Rastrear origens de erros por meio de análise de código sistemática","Corrigir problemas de produção com abordagens de depuração metódicas","Investigar padrões de comportamento de sistema inesperados"],"ru":["Воспроизводить зарегистрированные ошибки с помощью определенных шагов воспроизведения","Отслеживать источники ошибок посредством системного анализа кода","Исправлять проблемы производства с помощью методических подходов к отладке","Изучать закономерности неожиданного поведения системы"],"ar":["إعادة إنتاج الأخطاء المُبلَغ عنها باستخدام خطوات إعادة الإنتاج المحددة","تتبع مصادر الأخطاء من خلال تحليل الكود النظامي","إصلاح مشاكل الإنتاج باستخدام نهج منهجي لتحليل الأخطاء","تحقيق نمط سلوك النظام غير المتوقع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to codebase and runtime environment","Dependent on accurate bug report information","Needs reproduction capability for intermittent issues"],"zh":["需要访问代码库和运行时环境","依赖于准确的错误报告信息","需要间歇性问题的重现能力"],"ja":["コードベースと実行時環境へのアクセスが必要","正確なバグレポート情報に依存している","間欠的な問題の再現能力が必要"],"ko":["코드베이스 및 런타임 환경에 대한 액세스가 필요함","정확한 버그 보고서 정보에 의존함","간헐적인 문제의 재현 기능이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la base de código y al entorno de ejecución","Depende de la información precisa de los informes de errores","Necesita capacidad de reproducción para problemas intermitentes"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la base de code et à l''environnement d''exécution","Dépend de l''exactitude des informations des rapports de bogue","Nécessite une capacité de reproduction pour les problèmes intermittents"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf den Codebase und die Laufzeitumgebung","Hängt von genauen Fehlerberichts-Informationen ab","Benötigt Reproduktionsfähigkeit für intermittierende Probleme"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao código-fonte e ao ambiente de execução","Depende de informações precisas de relatórios de bugs","Necessita de capacidade de reprodução para problemas intermitentes"],"ru":["Требует доступа к базе кода и среде выполнения","Зависит от точной информации в отчетах об ошибках","Требует возможности воспроизведения для периодических проблем"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة الشفرة وبيئة التشغيل","يعتمد على دقة المعلومات في تقارير الأخطاء","يحتاج إلى القدرة على إعادة الإنتاج لمشاكل متقطعة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('congwa/wdm/find-skills', 'community', 'congwa', 'wdm', 'congwa/wdm', 'find-skills', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z', '2026-02-18T12:36:13.841Z', NULL, '{"id":"congwa/wdm/find-skills","name":"find-skills","description":{"zh":"发现技能帮助您发现和安装来自开放代理技能生态系统的技能，实现智能数据管理","ja":"スキルを探す機能は、オープンエージェントスキルエコシステムからのスキルを検索してインストールし、スマートデータ管理を実現します","ko":"스킬 찾기 기능은 오픈 에이전트 스킬 생태계의 스킬을 검색하고 설치하여 스마트 데이터 관리를 구현합니다","es":"Find-skills es una herramienta de gestión de datos inteligente que ayuda a descubrir e instalar habilidades del ecosistema de habilidades de agente abierto.","fr":"Find-skills est un outil de gestion de données intelligent qui aide à découvrir et à installer des compétences de l''écosystème de compétences d''agent ouvert.","de":"Find-skills ist ein intelligentes Datenmanagement-Tool, das hilft, Fähigkeiten aus dem offenen Agenten-Fähigkeits-Ökosystem zu entdecken und zu installieren.","pt":"A ferramenta de gerenciamento de dados inteligente find-skills ajuda a descobrir e instalar habilidades do ecossistema de habilidades de agentes abertos","ru":"Интеллектуальный инструмент управления данными find-skills помогает обнаружить и установить навыки из экосистемы открытых навыков агентов","ar":"أداة إدارة البيانات الذكية find-skills تساعد على اكتشاف وتثبيت مهارات من نظام مهارات الوكلاء المفتوح","en":"款专为 Windsurf AI 开发环境打造的智能数据管理工具，提供 **AI 对话暂停反馈**、**智能存储清理** 和 **全面数据分析** 功能"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"发现技能 - 智能数据管理工具","ja":"スキルを探す - インテリジェントデータ管理ツール","ko":"스킬 찾기 -智能 데이터 관리 도구","es":"Descubre habilidades con find-skills","fr":"Découvrez les compétences avec find-skills","de":"Entdecken Sie Fähigkeiten mit find-skills","pt":"Encontre Habilidades - Ferramenta de Gerenciamento de Dad...","ru":"Найти Навыки - Интеллектуальный Инструмент Управления Дан...","ar":"ابحث عن مهارات - أداة إدارة بيانات ذكية","en":"find-skills"},"description":{"zh":"发现技能帮助您发现和安装来自开放代理技能生态系统的技能，实现智能数据管理","ja":"スキルを探す機能は、オープンエージェントスキルエコシステムからのスキルを検索してインストールし、スマートデータ管理を実現します","ko":"스킬 찾기 기능은 오픈 에이전트 스킬 생태계의 스킬을 검색하고 설치하여 스마트 데이터 관리를 구현합니다","es":"Find-skills es una herramienta de gestión de datos inteligente que ayuda a descubrir e instalar habilidades del ecosistema de habilidades de agente abierto.","fr":"Find-skills est un outil de gestion de données intelligent qui aide à découvrir et à installer des compétences de l''écosystème de compétences d''agent ouvert.","de":"Find-skills ist ein intelligentes Datenmanagement-Tool, das hilft, Fähigkeiten aus dem offenen Agenten-Fähigkeits-Ökosystem zu entdecken und zu installieren.","pt":"A ferramenta de gerenciamento de dados inteligente find-skills ajuda a descobrir e instalar habilidades do ecossistema de habilidades de agentes abertos","ru":"Интеллектуальный инструмент управления данными find-skills помогает обнаружить и установить навыки из экосистемы открытых навыков агентов","ar":"أداة إدارة البيانات الذكية find-skills تساعد على اكتشاف وتثبيت مهارات من نظام مهارات الوكلاء المفتوح","en":"款专为 Windsurf AI 开发环境打造的智能数据管理工具，提供 **AI 对话暂停反馈**、**智能存储清理** 和 **全面数据分析** 功能"},"definition":{"en":"款专为 Windsurf AI 开发环境打造的智能数据管理工具，提供 **AI 对话暂停反馈**、**智能存储清理** 和 **全面数据分析** 功能"},"features":{"zh":["AI对话暂停反馈","智能存储清理","全面数据分析","技能搜索","智能数据管理"],"ja":["AI会話の一時停止フィードバック","スマートストレージクリーンアップ","全面的データ分析","スキル検索","インテリジェントデータ管理"],"ko":["AI 대화 일시 중지 피드백","스마트 저장소 정리","종합 데이터 분석","스킬 검색","인텔리전트 데이터 관리"],"es":["Búsqueda de habilidades","Instalación de habilidades","Análisis de datos","Gestión de datos inteligente","Extensión de capacidades del agente"],"fr":["Recherche de compétences","Installation de compétences","Analyse de données","Gestion de données intelligente","Extension des capacités de l''agent"],"de":["Fähigkeitsuche","Fähigkeitsinstallation","Datenanalyse","Intelligentes Datenmanagement","Erweiterung der Agentenfähigkeiten"],"pt":["Descoberta de habilidades do ecossistema de habilidades de agentes abertos","Instalação de habilidades com facilidade","Gerenciamento de dados inteligente","Análise de dados completa","Otimização do desempenho do agente"],"ru":["Обнаружение навыков из экосистемы открытых навыков агентов","Установка навыков с легкостью","Интеллектуальное управление данными","Полный анализ данных","Оптимизация производительности агента"],"ar":["اكتشاف مهارات من نظام مهارات الوكلاء المفتوح","تثبيت مهارات بسهولة","إدارة بيانات ذكية","تحليل بيانات كامل","تحسين أداء الوكيل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["智能数据管理","AI对话暂停反馈","智能存储清理","全面数据分析","技能搜索","开放代理技能生态系统"],"ja":["インテリジェントデータ管理","AI会話の一時停止フィードバック","スマートストレージクリーンアップ","全面的データ分析","スキル検索","オープンエージェントスキルエコシステム"],"ko":["인텔리전트 데이터 관리","AI 대화 일시 중지 피드백","스마트 저장소 정리","종합 데이터 분석","스킬 검색","오픈 에이전트 스킬 생태계"],"es":["find-skills","habilidades de agente","ecosistema de habilidades","gestión de datos inteligente","desarrollo de agentes","búsqueda de habilidades"],"fr":["find-skills","compétences d''agent","écosystème de compétences","gestion de données intelligente","développement d''agents","recherche de compétences"],"de":["find-skills","Agentenfähigkeiten","Fähigkeits-Ökosystem","intelligentes Datenmanagement","Agenten-Entwicklung","Fähigkeitsuche"],"pt":["gerenciamento de dados inteligente","descoberta de habilidades","instalação de habilidades","análise de dados","otimização do desempenho do agente","ecossistema de habilidades de agentes abertos"],"ru":["интеллектуальное управление данными","обнаружение навыков","установка навыков","полный анализ данных","оптимизация производительности агента","экосистема открытых навыков агентов"],"ar":["إدارة بيانات ذكية","اكتشاف مهارات","تثبيت مهارات","تحليل بيانات كامل","تحسين أداء الوكيل","نظام مهارات الوكلاء المفتوح"]}},"owner":"congwa","repo":"wdm","repoPath":"congwa/wdm","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"find-skills","description":"Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like how do I do X, find a skill for X, is there a skill that can..., or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill.","bodyPreview":"# Find Skills\n\nThis skill helps you discover and install skills from the open agent skills ecosystem.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user:\n\n- Asks \"how do I do X\" where X might be a common task with an existing skill\n- Says \"find a skill for X\" or \"is there a skill for X\"\n- Asks \"can you do X\" where X is a specialized capability\n- Expresses interest in extending agent capabilities\n- Wants to search for tools, templates, or workflows\n- Mentions they wish they had help with a","body":"# Find Skills\n\nThis skill helps you discover and install skills from the open agent skills ecosystem.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user:\n\n- Asks \"how do I do X\" where X might be a common task with an existing skill\n- Says \"find a skill for X\" or \"is there a skill for X\"\n- Asks \"can you do X\" where X is a specialized capability\n- Expresses interest in extending agent capabilities\n- Wants to search for tools, templates, or workflows\n- Mentions they wish they had help with a specific domain (design, testing, deployment, etc.)\n\n## What is the Skills CLI?\n\nThe Skills CLI (`npx skills`) is the package manager for the open agent skills ecosystem. Skills are modular packages that extend agent capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools.\n\n**Key commands:**\n\n- `npx skills find [query]` - Search for skills interactively or by keyword\n- `npx skills add <package>` - Install a skill from GitHub or other sources\n- `npx skills check` - Check for skill updates\n- `npx skills update` - Update all installed skills\n\n**Browse skills at:** https://skills.sh/\n\n## How to Help Users Find Skills\n\n### Step 1: Understand What They Need\n\nWhen a user asks for help with something, identify:\n\n1. The domain (e.g., React, testing, design, deployment)\n2. The specific task (e.g., writing tests, creating animations, reviewing PRs)\n3. Whether this is a common enough task that a skill likely exists\n\n### Step 2: Search for Skills\n\nRun the find command with a relevant query:\n\n```bash\nnpx skills find [query]\n```\n\nFor example:\n\n- User asks \"how do I make my React app faster?\" → `npx skills find react performance`\n- User asks \"can you help me with PR reviews?\" → `npx skills find pr review`\n- User asks \"I need to create a changelog\" → `npx skills find changelog`\n\nThe command will return results like:\n\n```\nInstall with npx skills add <owner/repo@skill>\n\nvercel-labs/agent-skills@vercel-react-best-practices\n└ https://skills.sh/vercel-labs/agent-skills/vercel-react-best-practices\n```\n\n### Step 3: Present Options to the User\n\nWhen you find relevant skills, present them to the user with:\n\n1. The skill name and what it does\n2. The install command they can run\n3. A link to learn more at skills.sh\n\nExample response:\n\n```\nI found a skill that might help! The \"vercel-react-best-practices\" skill provides\nReact and Next.js performance optimization guidelines from Vercel Engineering.\n\nTo install it:\nnpx skills add vercel-labs/agent-skills@vercel-react-best-practices\n\nLearn more: https://skills.sh/vercel-labs/agent-skills/vercel-react-best-practices\n```\n\n### Step 4: Offer to Install\n\nIf the user wants to proceed, you can install the skill for them:\n\n```bash\nnpx skills add <owner/repo@skill> -g -y\n```\n\nThe `-g` flag installs globally (user-level) and `-y` skips confirmation prompts.\n\n## Common Skill Categories\n\nWhen searching, consider these common categories:\n\n| Category        | Example Queries                          |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Web Development | react, nextjs, typescript, css, tailwind |\n| Testing         | testing, jest, playwright, e2e           |\n| DevOps          | deploy, docker, kubernetes, ci-cd        |\n| Documentation   | docs, readme, changelog, api-docs        |\n| Code Quality    | review, lint, refactor, best-practices   |\n| Design          | ui, ux, design-system, accessibility     |\n| Productivity    | workflow, automation, git                |\n\n## Tips for Effective Searches\n\n1. **Use specific keywords**: \"react testing\" is better than just \"testing\"\n2. **Try alternative terms**: If \"deploy\" doesn''t work, try \"deployment\" or \"ci-cd\"\n3. **Check popular sources**: Many skills come from `vercel-labs/agent-skills` or `ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills`\n\n## When No Skills Are Found\n\nIf no relevant skills exist:\n\n1. Acknowledge that no existing skill was found\n2. Offer to help with the task directly using your general capabilities\n3. Suggest the user could create their own skill with `npx skills init`\n\nExample:\n\n```\nI searched for skills related to \"xyz\" but didn''t find any matches.\nI can still help you with this task directly! Would you like me to proceed?\n\nIf this is something you do often, you could create your own skill:\nnpx skills init my-xyz-skill\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:36:13.841Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, and Claude Code needing skill discovery and installation capabilities from the open agent skills ecosystem.","zh":"适合像Cursor、Windsurf和Claude Code这样的AI代理，需要从开放代理技能生态系统中发现和安装技能的能力。","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、Claude CodeなどのAIエージェントが、オープンエージェントスキルエコシステムからスキルを発見してインストールする機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트가 오픈 에이전트 스킬 생태계에서 스킬 발견 및 설치 기능을 필요로 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf y Claude Code que necesitan capacidades de descubrimiento e instalación de habilidades del ecosistema de habilidades de agentes abiertas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf et Claude Code qui ont besoin de capacités de découverte et d''installation de compétences de l''écosystème de compétences d''agents ouvert.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf und Claude Code, die Funktionen zur Entdeckung und Installation von Fähigkeiten aus dem offenen Agenten-Fähigkeits-Ökosystem benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf e Claude Code que necessitam de capacidades de descoberta e instalação de habilidades do ecossistema de habilidades de agentes aberto.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf и Claude Code, которым необходимы возможности обнаружения и установки навыков из открытого экосистемы навыков агентов.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و Windsurf و Claude Code الذين يحتاجون إلى القدرات اكتشاف وتثبيت المهارات من النظام البيئي مفتوح للمهارات الوكيل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to discover and install skills using AI 对话暂停反馈, 智能存储清理, and 全面数据分析 functionalities, enabling extended capabilities through tools, templates, and workflows with features like skill search and installation.","zh":"赋予代理发现和安装技能的能力，使用AI对话暂停反馈、智能存储清理和全面数据分析功能，通过工具、模板和工作流等功能实现扩展能力，如技能搜索和安装。","ja":"AIエージェントが、AI対話一時停止フィードバック、スマートストレージクリーンアップ、総合データ分析などの機能を使用してスキルを発見してインストールする能力を提供し、ツール、テンプレート、ワークフローなどの機能を使用してスキル検索やインストールなどの拡張機能を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 AI 대화 일시 중지 피드백, 스마트 스토리지 클리닝, 전반적인 데이터 분석 등의 기능을 사용하여 스킬을 발견하고 설치할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, 툴, 템플릿, 워크플로우 등의 기능을 통해 스킬 검색 및 설치와 같은 확장된 기능을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a descubrir e instalar habilidades utilizando funcionalidades de diálogo de IA de pausa de retroalimentación, limpieza de almacenamiento inteligente y análisis de datos completo, lo que permite capacidades extendidas a través de herramientas, plantillas y flujos de trabajo con funciones como búsqueda e instalación de habilidades.","fr":"Équipe les agents de découvrir et d''installer des compétences en utilisant des fonctionnalités de dialogue IA de pause de rétroaction, de nettoyage de stockage intelligent et d''analyse de données complète, permettant des capacités étendues via des outils, des modèles et des flux de travail avec des fonctionnalités comme la recherche et l''installation de compétences.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Fähigkeiten zu entdecken und zu installieren, indem sie Funktionen wie KI-Dialogpausen-Rückmeldung, intelligente Speicherbereinigung und umfassende Datenanalyse nutzen, und ermöglicht so erweiterte Fähigkeiten durch Werkzeuge, Vorlagen und Workflows mit Funktionen wie Fähigkeitsuche und -installation.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a descobrir e instalar habilidades usando funcionalidades de pause de diálogo de IA, limpeza de armazenamento inteligente e análise de dados completa, permitindo capacidades estendidas por meio de ferramentas, modelos e fluxos de trabalho com recursos como busca e instalação de habilidades.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обнаруживать и устанавливать навыки с помощью функций паузы диалога ИИ, интеллектуальной очистки хранилища и полной аналитики данных, что позволяет расширять возможности посредством инструментов, шаблонов и рабочих процессов с функциями, такими как поиск и установка навыков.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من اكتشاف وتثبيت المهارات باستخدام ميزات مثل إيقاف حوار الذكاء الاصطناعي، وتنظيف التخزين الذكي، وتحليل البيانات الشامل، مما يتيح القدرات الممتدة من خلال أدوات وقوالب وعمليات عمل مع ميزات مثل البحث عن المهارات وتثبيتها."},"useCases":{"en":["Discovering new skills for task automation","Installing skills for specialized capabilities","Searching for tools and templates to extend agent functionality","Analyzing data to determine the need for new skills","Extending agent capabilities through workflow integration"],"zh":["发现新的技能以实现任务自动化","安装技能以实现专门的能力","搜索工具和模板以扩展代理功能","分析数据以确定新的技能需求","通过工作流集成扩展代理能力"],"ja":["タスクの自動化のために新しいスキルを発見する","専門的な能力のためにスキルをインストールする","エージェントの機能を拡張するためのツールとテンプレートを検索する","新しいスキルの必要性を判断するためにデータを分析する","ワークフローの統合を通じてエージェントの能力を拡張する"],"ko":["작업 자동화를 위한 새로운 스킬 발견","전문적인 능력의ための 스킬 설치","에이전트 기능 확장을 위한 툴 및 템플릿 검색","새로운 스킬 필요성 판단을 위한 데이터 분석","워크플로우 통합을 통한 에이전트 능력 확장"],"es":["Descubrir nuevas habilidades para la automatización de tareas","Instalar habilidades para capacidades especializadas","Buscar herramientas y plantillas para ampliar la funcionalidad del agente","Analizar datos para determinar la necesidad de nuevas habilidades","Ampliar las capacidades del agente a través de la integración de flujos de trabajo"],"fr":["Découvrir de nouvelles compétences pour l''automatisation des tâches","Installer des compétences pour des capacités spécialisées","Rechercher des outils et des modèles pour étendre les fonctionnalités de l''agent","Analyser les données pour déterminer le besoin de nouvelles compétences","Étendre les capacités de l''agent via l''intégration de flux de travail"],"de":["Entdecken neuer Fähigkeiten für die Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Installieren von Fähigkeiten für spezielle Fähigkeiten","Suchen nach Tools und Vorlagen, um die Funktionalität des Agents zu erweitern","Analysieren von Daten, um den Bedarf an neuen Fähigkeiten zu bestimmen","Erweitern der Agentenfähigkeiten durch die Integration von Workflows"],"pt":["Descobrir novas habilidades para automação de tarefas","Instalar habilidades para capacidades especializadas","Pesquisar ferramentas e modelos para estender a funcionalidade do agente","Analizar dados para determinar a necessidade de novas habilidades","Estender as capacidades do agente por meio da integração de fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["Обнаружение новых навыков для автоматизации задач","Установка навыков для специализированных возможностей","Поиск инструментов и шаблонов для расширения функциональности агента","Анализ данных для определения необходимости новых навыков","Расширение возможностей агента посредством интеграции рабочего процесса"],"ar":["اكتشاف مهارات جديدة للتنمية التلقائية للمهام","تثبيت المهارات للقدرات المتخصصة","البحث عن أدوات وقوالب لتوسيع وظيفة الوكيل","تحليل البيانات لتحديد الحاجة إلى مهارات جديدة","توسيع قدرات الوكيل من خلال دمج سير العمل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to the open agent skills ecosystem","Dependent on user input for skill discovery","May require additional setup for skill installation"],"zh":["需要访问开放代理技能生态系统","依赖于用户输入以发现技能","可能需要额外的设置以安装技能"],"ja":["オープンエージェントスキルエコシステムへのアクセスが必要","スキルの発見にはユーザーの入力に依存する","スキルのインストールには追加の設定が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["오픈 에이전트 스킬 생태계에 대한 액세스가 필요함","스킬 발견에는 사용자 입력에 의존함","스킬 설치에는 추가 설정이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere acceso al ecosistema de habilidades de agentes abiertas","Depende de la entrada del usuario para el descubrimiento de habilidades","Puede requerir configuración adicional para la instalación de habilidades"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''écosystème de compétences d''agents ouvert","Dépend de la saisie de l''utilisateur pour la découverte de compétences","Peut nécessiter une configuration supplémentaire pour l''installation de compétences"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das offene Agenten-Fähigkeits-Ökosystem","Hängt von der Benutzereingabe für die Entdeckung von Fähigkeiten ab","Kann zusätzliche Einrichtung für die Installation von Fähigkeiten erfordern"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao ecossistema de habilidades de agentes aberto","Depende da entrada do usuário para descoberta de habilidades","Pode exigir configuração adicional para instalação de habilidades"],"ru":["Требует доступа к открытому экосистеме навыков агентов","Зависит от ввода пользователя для обнаружения навыков","Может потребовать дополнительной настройки для установки навыков"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى نظام بيئي مفتوح للمهارات الوكيل","يعتمد على إدخال المستخدم لاكتشاف المهارات","يمكن أن يتطلب إعدادا إضافيا لتثبيت المهارات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('charlietlamb/ferix/Convex Agents', 'community', 'charlietlamb', 'ferix', 'charlietlamb/ferix', 'Convex Agents', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z', '2026-02-18T12:35:35.790Z', NULL, '{"id":"charlietlamb/ferix/Convex Agents","name":"Convex Agents","description":{"zh":"Convex Agents是构建持久的AI代理的集中式中心，提供线程管理、工具集成等功能","ja":"Convex Agentsは状態を保持するAIエージェントを構築するための集中型ハブであり、スレッド管理、ツール統合などの機能を提供","ko":"Convex Agents는 지속적인 AI 에이전트를 구축하는 중앙 집중식 허브로서 스레드 관리, 도구 통합 등의 기능을 제공","es":"Convex Agents es un hub centralizado para habilidades de agentes que permite desarrollar agentes de IA con estado y persistencia","fr":"Convex Agents est un hub centralisé pour les compétences des agents qui permet de créer des agents IA persistants et à état","de":"Convex Agents ist ein zentraler Hub für Agentenfähigkeiten, der die Entwicklung von persistenten und stateful AI-Agenten ermöglicht","pt":"Os Agentes Convex são uma plataforma centralizada para construir agentes de IA persistentes e stateful, com recursos como gerenciamento de threads e integração de ferramentas","ru":"Конвекс-агенты - это централизованная платформа для построения устойчивых и stateful AI-агентов, с функциями seperti управление потоками и интеграция инструментов","ar":"وكلاء Convex هم منصة مركزية لبناء وكلاء ذكاء اصطناعي ثابت و stateful، مع ميزات مثل إدارة الخيوط وتكامل الأدوات","en":"A centralised hub for agent skills"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Convex Agents - 构建持久的AI代理","ja":"Convex Agents - 状態を保持するAIエージェントを構築","ko":"Convex Agents - 지속적인 AI 에이전트 구축","es":"Agentes Convex: Desarrolla IA con estado y persistencia","fr":"Agents Convex : Créez des agents IA persistants et à état","de":"Convex Agents: Entwickle persistente und stateful AI","pt":"Agentes Convex: Construa Agentes de IA Persistentes","ru":"Конвекс-агенты: Построение устойчивых AI-агентов","ar":"وكلاء Convex: بناء وكلاء ذكاء اصطناعي ثابت","en":"Convex Agents"},"description":{"zh":"Convex Agents是构建持久的AI代理的集中式中心，提供线程管理、工具集成等功能","ja":"Convex Agentsは状態を保持するAIエージェントを構築するための集中型ハブであり、スレッド管理、ツール統合などの機能を提供","ko":"Convex Agents는 지속적인 AI 에이전트를 구축하는 중앙 집중식 허브로서 스레드 관리, 도구 통합 등의 기능을 제공","es":"Convex Agents es un hub centralizado para habilidades de agentes que permite desarrollar agentes de IA con estado y persistencia","fr":"Convex Agents est un hub centralisé pour les compétences des agents qui permet de créer des agents IA persistants et à état","de":"Convex Agents ist ein zentraler Hub für Agentenfähigkeiten, der die Entwicklung von persistenten und stateful AI-Agenten ermöglicht","pt":"Os Agentes Convex são uma plataforma centralizada para construir agentes de IA persistentes e stateful, com recursos como gerenciamento de threads e integraç...","ru":"Конвекс-агенты - это централизованная платформа для построения устойчивых и stateful AI-агентов, с функциями seperti управление потоками и интеграция инструм...","ar":"وكلاء Convex هم منصة مركزية لبناء وكلاء ذكاء اصطناعي ثابت و stateful، مع ميزات مثل إدارة الخيوط وتكامل الأدوات","en":"A centralised hub for agent skills"},"definition":{"en":"A centralised hub for agent skills"},"features":{"zh":["线程管理","工具集成","流式响应","RAG模式","工作流编排"],"ja":["スレッド管理","ツール統合","ストリーミング応答","RAGパターン","ワークフロー編成"],"ko":["스레드 관리","도구 통합","스트리밍 응답","RAG 패턴","워크플로우 오케스트레이션"],"es":["Gestión de hilos","Integración de herramientas","Respuestas de streaming","Patrones RAG","Orquestación de flujos de trabajo"],"fr":["Gestion de threads","Intégration d''outils","Réponses de streaming","Modèles RAG","Orchestration de flux de travail"],"de":["Thread-Verwaltung","Tool-Integration","Streaming-Antworten","RAG-Muster","Workfluss-Orchestrierung"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de threads","Integração de ferramentas","Respostas em streaming","Padrões RAG","Orquestração de fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["Управление потоками","Интеграция инструментов","Потоковые ответы","Шаблоны RAG","Оркестровка рабочих процессов"],"ar":["إدارة الخيوط","تكامل الأدوات","استجابات بث","أنماط RAG","تنسيق سير العمل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Convex Agents","AI代理","持久的AI","线程管理","工具集成","流式响应"],"ja":["Convex Agents","AIエージェント","状態を保持するAI","スレッド管理","ツール統合","ストリーミング応答"],"ko":["Convex Agents","AI 에이전트","지속적인 AI","스레드 관리","도구 통합","스트리밍 응답"],"es":["agentes de ia","desarrollo de ia","estado y persistencia","convex agents","gestión de hilos","integración de herramientas"],"fr":["agents ia","développement ia","état et persistance","convex agents","gestion de threads","intégration d''outils"],"de":["ai-agenten","entwicklung von ai","zustand und persistenz","convex agenten","thread-verwaltung","tool-integration"],"pt":["agentes de ia","ia persistente","stateful ai","gerenciamento de threads","integração de ferramentas","desenvolvimento de ia"],"ru":["агенты ии","постоянный ии","stateful ии","управление потоками","интеграция инструментов","разработка ии"],"ar":["وكلاء ذكاء اصطناعي","ذكاء اصطناعي ثابت","ذكاء اصطناعي stateful","إدارة الخيوط","تكامل الأدوات","تطوير ذكاء اصطناعي"]}},"owner":"charlietlamb","repo":"ferix","repoPath":"charlietlamb/ferix","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.510Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Convex Agents","description":"Building AI agents with the Convex Agent component including thread management, tool integration, streaming responses, RAG patterns, and workflow orchestration","version":"1.0.0","tags":["convex","agents","ai","llm","tools","rag","workflows"],"bodyPreview":"# Convex Agents\n\nBuild persistent, stateful AI agents with Convex including thread management, tool integration, streaming responses, RAG patterns, and workflow orchestration.\n\n## Documentation Sources\n\nBefore implementing, do not assume; fetch the latest documentation:\n\n- Primary: https://docs.convex.dev/ai\n- Convex Agent Component: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@convex-dev/agent\n- For broader context: https://docs.convex.dev/llms.txt\n\n## Instructions\n\n### Why Convex for AI Agents\n\n- **Persiste","body":"# Convex Agents\n\nBuild persistent, stateful AI agents with Convex including thread management, tool integration, streaming responses, RAG patterns, and workflow orchestration.\n\n## Documentation Sources\n\nBefore implementing, do not assume; fetch the latest documentation:\n\n- Primary: https://docs.convex.dev/ai\n- Convex Agent Component: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@convex-dev/agent\n- For broader context: https://docs.convex.dev/llms.txt\n\n## Instructions\n\n### Why Convex for AI Agents\n\n- **Persistent State** - Conversation history survives restarts\n- **Real-time Updates** - Stream responses to clients automatically\n- **Tool Execution** - Run Convex functions as agent tools\n- **Durable Workflows** - Long-running agent tasks with reliability\n- **Built-in RAG** - Vector search for knowledge retrieval\n\n### Setting Up Convex Agent\n\n```bash\nnpm install @convex-dev/agent ai openai\n```\n\n```typescript\n// convex/agent.ts\nimport { Agent } from \"@convex-dev/agent\";\nimport { components } from \"./_generated/api\";\nimport { OpenAI } from \"openai\";\n\nconst openai = new OpenAI();\n\nexport const agent = new Agent(components.agent, {\n  chat: openai.chat,\n  textEmbedding: openai.embeddings,\n});\n```\n\n### Thread Management\n\n```typescript\n// convex/threads.ts\nimport { mutation, query } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nimport { agent } from \"./agent\";\n\n// Create a new conversation thread\nexport const createThread = mutation({\n  args: {\n    userId: v.id(\"users\"),\n    title: v.optional(v.string()),\n  },\n  returns: v.id(\"threads\"),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const threadId = await agent.createThread(ctx, {\n      userId: args.userId,\n      metadata: {\n        title: args.title ?? \"New Conversation\",\n        createdAt: Date.now(),\n      },\n    });\n    return threadId;\n  },\n});\n\n// List user''s threads\nexport const listThreads = query({\n  args: { userId: v.id(\"users\") },\n  returns: v.array(v.object({\n    _id: v.id(\"threads\"),\n    title: v.string(),\n    lastMessageAt: v.optional(v.number()),\n  })),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return await agent.listThreads(ctx, {\n      userId: args.userId,\n    });\n  },\n});\n\n// Get thread messages\nexport const getMessages = query({\n  args: { threadId: v.id(\"threads\") },\n  returns: v.array(v.object({\n    role: v.string(),\n    content: v.string(),\n    createdAt: v.number(),\n  })),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return await agent.getMessages(ctx, {\n      threadId: args.threadId,\n    });\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Sending Messages and Streaming Responses\n\n```typescript\n// convex/chat.ts\nimport { action } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nimport { agent } from \"./agent\";\nimport { internal } from \"./_generated/api\";\n\nexport const sendMessage = action({\n  args: {\n    threadId: v.id(\"threads\"),\n    message: v.string(),\n  },\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    // Add user message to thread\n    await ctx.runMutation(internal.chat.addUserMessage, {\n      threadId: args.threadId,\n      content: args.message,\n    });\n\n    // Generate AI response with streaming\n    const response = await agent.chat(ctx, {\n      threadId: args.threadId,\n      messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: args.message }],\n      stream: true,\n      onToken: async (token) => {\n        // Stream tokens to client via mutation\n        await ctx.runMutation(internal.chat.appendToken, {\n          threadId: args.threadId,\n          token,\n        });\n      },\n    });\n\n    // Save complete response\n    await ctx.runMutation(internal.chat.saveResponse, {\n      threadId: args.threadId,\n      content: response.content,\n    });\n\n    return null;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Tool Integration\n\nDefine tools that agents can use:\n\n```typescript\n// convex/tools.ts\nimport { tool } from \"@convex-dev/agent\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nimport { api } from \"./_generated/api\";\n\n// Tool to search knowledge base\nexport const searchKnowledge = tool({\n  name: \"search_knowledge\",\n  description: \"Search the knowledge base for relevant information\",\n  parameters: v.object({\n    query: v.string(),\n    limit: v.optional(v.number()),\n  }),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const results = await ctx.runQuery(api.knowledge.search, {\n      query: args.query,\n      limit: args.limit ?? 5,\n    });\n    return results;\n  },\n});\n\n// Tool to create a task\nexport const createTask = tool({\n  name: \"create_task\",\n  description: \"Create a new task for the user\",\n  parameters: v.object({\n    title: v.string(),\n    description: v.optional(v.string()),\n    dueDate: v.optional(v.string()),\n  }),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const taskId = await ctx.runMutation(api.tasks.create, {\n      title: args.title,\n      description: args.description,\n      dueDate: args.dueDate ? new Date(args.dueDate).getTime() : undefined,\n    });\n    return { success: true, taskId };\n  },\n});\n\n// Tool to get weather\nexport const getWeather = tool({\n  name: \"get_weather\",\n  description: \"Get current weather for a location\",\n  parameters: v.object({\n    location: v.string(),\n  }),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const response = await fetch(\n      `https://api.weather.com/current?location=${encodeURIComponent(args.location)}`\n    );\n    return await response.json();\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Agent with Tools\n\n```typescript\n// convex/assistant.ts\nimport { action } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nimport { agent } from \"./agent\";\nimport { searchKnowledge, createTask, getWeather } from \"./tools\";\n\nexport const chat = action({\n  args: {\n    threadId: v.id(\"threads\"),\n    message: v.string(),\n  },\n  returns: v.string(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const response = await agent.chat(ctx, {\n      threadId: args.threadId,\n      messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: args.message }],\n      tools: [searchKnowledge, createTask, getWeather],\n      systemPrompt: `You are a helpful assistant. You have access to tools to:\n        - Search the knowledge base for information\n        - Create tasks for the user\n        - Get weather information\n        Use these tools when appropriate to help the user.`,\n    });\n\n    return response.content;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation)\n\n```typescript\n// convex/knowledge.ts\nimport { mutation, query } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nimport { agent } from \"./agent\";\n\n// Add document to knowledge base\nexport const addDocument = mutation({\n  args: {\n    title: v.string(),\n    content: v.string(),\n    metadata: v.optional(v.object({\n      source: v.optional(v.string()),\n      category: v.optional(v.string()),\n    })),\n  },\n  returns: v.id(\"documents\"),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    // Generate embedding\n    const embedding = await agent.embed(ctx, args.content);\n\n    return await ctx.db.insert(\"documents\", {\n      title: args.title,\n      content: args.content,\n      embedding,\n      metadata: args.metadata ?? {},\n      createdAt: Date.now(),\n    });\n  },\n});\n\n// Search knowledge base\nexport const search = query({\n  args: {\n    query: v.string(),\n    limit: v.optional(v.number()),\n  },\n  returns: v.array(v.object({\n    _id: v.id(\"documents\"),\n    title: v.string(),\n    content: v.string(),\n    score: v.number(),\n  })),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const results = await agent.search(ctx, {\n      query: args.query,\n      table: \"documents\",\n      limit: args.limit ?? 5,\n    });\n\n    return results.map((r) => ({\n      _id: r._id,\n      title: r.title,\n      content: r.content,\n      score: r._score,\n    }));\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Workflow Orchestration\n\n```typescript\n// convex/workflows.ts\nimport { action, internalMutation } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nimport { agent } from \"./agent\";\nimport { internal } from \"./_generated/api\";\n\n// Multi-step research workflow\nexport const researchTopic = action({\n  args: {\n    topic: v.string(),\n    userId: v.id(\"users\"),\n  },\n  returns: v.id(\"research\"),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    // Create research record\n    const researchId = await ctx.runMutation(internal.workflows.createResearch, {\n      topic: args.topic,\n      userId: args.userId,\n      status: \"searching\",\n    });\n\n    // Step 1: Search for relevant documents\n    const searchResults = await agent.search(ctx, {\n      query: args.topic,\n      table: \"documents\",\n      limit: 10,\n    });\n\n    await ctx.runMutation(internal.workflows.updateStatus, {\n      researchId,\n      status: \"analyzing\",\n    });\n\n    // Step 2: Analyze and synthesize\n    const analysis = await agent.chat(ctx, {\n      messages: [{\n        role: \"user\",\n        content: `Analyze these sources about \"${args.topic}\" and provide a comprehensive summary:\\n\\n${\n          searchResults.map((r) => r.content).join(\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n\")\n        }`,\n      }],\n      systemPrompt: \"You are a research assistant. Provide thorough, well-cited analysis.\",\n    });\n\n    // Step 3: Generate key insights\n    await ctx.runMutation(internal.workflows.updateStatus, {\n      researchId,\n      status: \"summarizing\",\n    });\n\n    const insights = await agent.chat(ctx, {\n      messages: [{\n        role: \"user\",\n        content: `Based on this analysis, list 5 key insights:\\n\\n${analysis.content}`,\n      }],\n    });\n\n    // Save final results\n    await ctx.runMutation(internal.workflows.completeResearch, {\n      researchId,\n      analysis: analysis.content,\n      insights: insights.content,\n      sources: searchResults.map((r) => r._id),\n    });\n\n    return researchId;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Examples\n\n### Complete Chat Application Schema\n\n```typescript\n// convex/schema.ts\nimport { defineSchema, defineTable } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport default defineSchema({\n  threads: defineTable({\n    userId: v.id(\"users\"),\n    title: v.string(),\n    lastMessageAt: v.optional(v.number()),\n    metadata: v.optional(v.any()),\n  }).index(\"by_user\", [\"userId\"]),\n\n  messages: defineTable({\n    threadId: v.id(\"threads\"),\n    role: v.union(v.literal(\"user\"), v.literal(\"assistant\"), v.literal(\"system\")),\n    content: v.string(),\n    toolCalls: v.optional(v.array(v.object({\n      name: v.string(),\n      arguments: v.any(),\n      result: v.optional(v.any()),\n    }))),\n    createdAt: v.number(),\n  }).index(\"by_thread\", [\"threadId\"]),\n\n  documents: defineTable({\n    title: v.string(),\n    content: v.string(),\n    embedding: v.array(v.float64()),\n    metadata: v.object({\n      source: v.optional(v.string()),\n      category: v.optional(v.string()),\n    }),\n    createdAt: v.number(),\n  }).vectorIndex(\"by_embedding\", {\n    vectorField: \"embedding\",\n    dimensions: 1536,\n  }),\n});\n```\n\n### React Chat Component\n\n```typescript\nimport { useQuery, useMutation, useAction } from \"convex/react\";\nimport { api } from \"../convex/_generated/api\";\nimport { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \"react\";\n\nfunction ChatInterface({ threadId }: { threadId: Id<\"threads\"> }) {\n  const messages = useQuery(api.threads.getMessages, { threadId });\n  const sendMessage = useAction(api.chat.sendMessage);\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const [sending, setSending] = useState(false);\n  const messagesEndRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    messagesEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n  }, [messages]);\n\n  const handleSend = async (e: React.FormEvent) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    if (!input.trim() || sending) return;\n\n    const message = input.trim();\n    setInput(\"\");\n    setSending(true);\n\n    try {\n      await sendMessage({ threadId, message });\n    } finally {\n      setSending(false);\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"chat-container\">\n      <div className=\"messages\">\n        {messages?.map((msg, i) => (\n          <div key={i} className={`message ${msg.role}`}>\n            <strong>{msg.role === \"user\" ? \"You\" : \"Assistant\"}:</strong>\n            <p>{msg.content}</p>\n          </div>\n        ))}\n        <div ref={messagesEndRef} />\n      </div>\n\n      <form onSubmit={handleSend} className=\"input-form\">\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)}\n          placeholder=\"Type your message...\"\n          disabled={sending}\n        />\n        <button type=\"submit\" disabled={sending || !input.trim()}>\n          {sending ? \"Sending...\" : \"Send\"}\n        </button>\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- Never run `npx convex deploy` unless explicitly instructed\n- Never run any git commands unless explicitly instructed\n- Store conversation history in Convex for persistence\n- Use streaming for better user experience with long responses\n- Implement proper error handling for tool failures\n- Use vector indexes for efficient RAG retrieval\n- Rate limit agent interactions to control costs\n- Log tool usage for debugging and analytics\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n1. **Not persisting threads** - Conversations lost on refresh\n2. **Blocking on long responses** - Use streaming instead\n3. **Tool errors crashing agents** - Add proper error handling\n4. **Large context windows** - Summarize old messages\n5. **Missing embeddings for RAG** - Generate embeddings on insert\n\n## References\n\n- Convex Documentation: https://docs.convex.dev/\n- Convex LLMs.txt: https://docs.convex.dev/llms.txt\n- Convex AI: https://docs.convex.dev/ai\n- Agent Component: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@convex-dev/agent\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:35:35.790Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents seeking to build persistent, stateful interactions with features like thread management and workflow orchestration.","zh":"适用于高级AI代理，旨在建立持久、有状态的交互，具有线程管理和工作流编排等功能。","ja":"高度なAIエージェントが永続的なステートフルなやり取りを構築するために適しています。スレッド管理やワークフローオーケストレーションなどの機能を備えています。","ko":"고급 AI 에이전트가 지속적이고 상태가 있는 상호 작용을 구축하기에 적합하며, 스레드 관리 및 워크플로 오케스트레이션과 같은 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial avanzados que buscan crear interacciones persistentes y con estado, con características como gestión de hilos y orquestación de flujos de trabajo.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle avancés qui cherchent à établir des interactions persistantes et à état, avec des fonctionnalités telles que la gestion de threads et l''orchestration de flux de travail.","de":"Ideal für erweiterte KI-Agents, die beständige, statusbehaftete Interaktionen mit Funktionen wie Threadverwaltung und Workfloworchestrierung aufbauen möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados que buscam criar interações persistentes e com estado, com recursos como gerenciamento de threads e orquestração de fluxos de trabalho.","ru":"Идеально для продвинутых агентов ИИ, стремящихся создавать постоянные, имеющие состояние взаимодействия с функциями, такими как управление потоками и оркестровка рабочих процессов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمين الذين يسعون إلى إنشاء تفاعلات مستدامة وذات حالة، مع ميزات مثل إدارة الخيوط وتسلسل سير العمل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to integrate with tools, manage threads, and orchestrate workflows, leveraging Convex Agent Component and RAG patterns for streamlined interactions, all while supporting streaming responses for enhanced user experience.","zh":"赋予代理集成工具、管理线程和编排工作流的能力，利用Convex Agent Component和RAG模式实现简化的交互，同时支持流响应以增强用户体验。","ja":"エージェントがツールを統合し、スレッドを管理し、ワークフローをオーケストレートする能力を提供します。Convex Agent ComponentとRAGパターンを活用して、ストリーミング応答をサポートしながら、シームレスなやり取りを実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 도구를 통합하고 스레드를 관리하며 워크플로우를 오케스트레이션할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다. Convex 에이전트 구성 요소 및 RAG 패턴을 활용하여 스트리밍 응답을 지원하면서 상호 작용을 간소화합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes integrarse con herramientas, gestionar hilos y orquestar flujos de trabajo, aprovechando el componente Convex Agent y los patrones RAG para interacciones optimizadas, todo mientras se admite respuestas de streaming para una experiencia de usuario mejorada.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''intégrer des outils, de gérer des threads et d''orchestrer des flux de travail, en exploitant le composant Convex Agent et les modèles RAG pour des interactions fluides, le tout en prenant en charge les réponses de streaming pour une expérience utilisateur améliorée.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, sich in Tools zu integrieren, Threads zu verwalten und Workflows zu orchestrieren, indem es den Convex-Agent-Komponenten und RAG-Mustern für optimierte Interaktionen nutzt, und unterstützt dabei Streaming-Antworten für eine verbesserte Benutzererfahrung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se integrarem a ferramentas, gerenciar threads e orquestrar fluxos de trabalho, aproveitando o Componente do Agente Convex e os padrões RAG para interações simplificadas, tudo isso enquanto suporta respostas de streaming para uma experiência do usuário aprimorada.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью интегрироваться с инструментами, управлять потоками и оркестровать рабочие процессы, используя компонент агента Convex и шаблоны RAG для упрощенных взаимодействий, все это при поддержке потоковых ответов для улучшения пользовательского опыта.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من التكامل مع الأدوات وإدارة الخيوط وتسلسل سير العمل، واستخدام مكون العامل Convex وأنماط RAG لتفاعلات مبسطة، مع دعم الاستجابات المتدفقة لتجربة مستخدم محسنة."},"useCases":{"en":["Building persistent AI agent interactions","Integrating tools for advanced workflow orchestration","Implementing RAG patterns for efficient response generation","Managing threads for concurrent task execution"],"zh":["构建持久的AI代理交互","集成工具以实现高级工作流编排","实施RAG模式以实现高效的响应生成","管理线程以实现并发任务执行"],"ja":["永続的なAIエージェントのやり取りを構築する","ツールを統合して高度なワークフローオーケストレーションを実現する","RAGパターンを実装して効率的な応答生成を実現する","スレッドを管理してコンカレントタスクの実行を実現する"],"ko":["지속적인 AI 에이전트 상호 작용을 구축하는 것","도구를 통합하여 고급 워크플로 오케스트레이션을 구현하는 것","RAG 패턴을 구현하여 효율적인 응답 생성을 구현하는 것","스레드를 관리하여 동시 작업 실행을 구현하는 것"],"es":["Creación de interacciones de agentes de inteligencia artificial persistentes","Integración de herramientas para orquestación de flujos de trabajo avanzada","Implementación de patrones RAG para generación de respuestas eficientes","Gestión de hilos para ejecución de tareas concurrentes"],"fr":["Création d''interactions d''agents d''intelligence artificielle persistantes","Intégration d''outils pour une orchestration de flux de travail avancée","Mise en œuvre de modèles RAG pour une génération de réponses efficace","Gestion de threads pour l''exécution de tâches concurrentes"],"de":["Erstellung beständiger KI-Agents-Interaktionen","Integration von Tools für erweiterte Workflow-Orchestrierung","Implementierung von RAG-Mustern für effiziente Antwortgenerierung","Threadverwaltung für die Ausführung von konkurrierenden Aufgaben"],"pt":["Construir interações de agentes de IA persistentes","Integrar ferramentas para orquestração de fluxos de trabalho avançada","Implementar padrões RAG para geração eficiente de respostas","Gerenciar threads para execução de tarefas concorrentes"],"ru":["Создание постоянных взаимодействий агентов ИИ","Интеграция инструментов для продвинутой оркестровки рабочих процессов","Реализация шаблонов RAG для эффективной генерации ответов","Управление потоками для параллельного выполнения задач"],"ar":["بناء تفاعلات مستدامة للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","دمج الأدوات لتسلسل سير العمل المتقدم","تنفيذ أنماط RAG لتوليد استجابات فعال","إدارة الخيوط للتنفيذ المتزامن للمهام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Convex Agent Component installation","Needs access to the latest Convex documentation","Dependent on compatibility with specific AI agent frameworks"],"zh":["需要Convex Agent Component安装","需要访问最新的Convex文档","依赖于特定AI代理框架的兼容性"],"ja":["Convex Agent Componentのインストールが必要","最新のConvexドキュメントへのアクセスが必要","特定のAIエージェントフレームワークとの互換性に依存する"],"ko":["Convex 에이전트 구성 요소 설치가 필요합니다.","최신 Convex 문서에 액세스해야 합니다.","특정 AI 에이전트 프레임워크와의 호환성에 의존합니다."],"es":["Requiere la instalación del componente Convex Agent","Necesita acceso a la última documentación de Convex","Depende de la compatibilidad con marcos de agentes de inteligencia artificial específicos"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation du composant Convex Agent","A besoin d''un accès à la dernière documentation Convex","Dépend de la compatibilité avec des frameworks d''agents d''intelligence artificielle spécifiques"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation des Convex-Agent-Komponenten","Benötigt Zugriff auf die neueste Convex-Dokumentation","Hängt von der Kompatibilität mit bestimmten KI-Agents-Frameworks ab"],"pt":["Exige a instalação do Componente do Agente Convex","Necessita de acesso à documentação mais recente do Convex","Dependente da compatibilidade com estruturas de agente de IA específicas"],"ru":["Требует установки компонента агента Convex","Требует доступа к последней документации Convex","Зависит от совместимости с определенными фреймворками агентов ИИ"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت مكون العامل Convex","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى توثيق Convex الأحدث","يعتمد على التوافق مع إطارات الوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المحددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('faint45/zhewei-ai-chat-01/architecture-patterns', 'community', 'faint45', 'zhewei-ai-chat-01', 'faint45/zhewei-ai-chat-01', 'architecture-patterns', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.511Z', '2026-02-18T12:36:10.711Z', NULL, '{"id":"faint45/zhewei-ai-chat-01/architecture-patterns","name":"architecture-patterns","description":{"zh":"后端架构模式是设计可维护、可测试和可扩展系统的关键。了解Clean Architecture、Hexagonal Architecture和Domain-Driven Design等模式","ja":"バックエンドアーキテクチャパターンは、メンテナンス可能、テスト可能、スケーラブルなシステムを設計するための重要な概念です。Clean Architecture、Hexagonal Architecture、Domain-Driven Designなどのパターンを学びましょう","ko":"백엔드 아키텍처 패턴은 유지 보수 가능하고 테스트 가능하며 확장 가능한 시스템을 설계하는 데 중요한 개념입니다. Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, Domain-Driven Design 등의 패턴을 학습","es":"Aprende patrones de arquitectura backend comprobados para construir sistemas mantenibles y escalables","fr":"Maîtrisez les modèles d''architecture backend éprouvés pour concevoir des systèmes évolutifs et maintenables","de":"Meistern Sie bewährte Architekturmuster für Backend-Systeme, um wartbare und skalierbare Systeme zu entwerfen","en":"築未科技 AI 對話窗口 - GitHub Pages 部署"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"后端架构模式","ja":"バックエンドアーキテクチャパターン","ko":"백엔드 아키텍처 패턴","es":"Patrones de Arquitectura: Diseña Sistemas Escalables","fr":"Modèles d''Architecture: Conception de Systèmes Évolutifs","de":"Architekturmuster: Entwerfen von Skalierbaren Systemen","en":"architecture-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"后端架构模式是设计可维护、可测试和可扩展系统的关键。了解Clean Architecture、Hexagonal Architecture和Domain-Driven Design等模式","ja":"バックエンドアーキテクチャパターンは、メンテナンス可能、テスト可能、スケーラブルなシステムを設計するための重要な概念です。Clean Architecture、Hexagonal Architecture、Domain-Driven Designなどのパターンを学びましょう","ko":"백엔드 아키텍처 패턴은 유지 보수 가능하고 테스트 가능하며 확장 가능한 시스템을 설계하는 데 중요한 개념입니다. Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, Domain-Driven Design 등의 패턴을 학습","es":"Aprende patrones de arquitectura backend comprobados para construir sistemas mantenibles y escalables","fr":"Maîtrisez les modèles d''architecture backend éprouvés pour concevoir des systèmes évolutifs et maintenables","de":"Meistern Sie bewährte Architekturmuster für Backend-Systeme, um wartbare und skalierbare Systeme zu entwerfen","en":"築未科技 AI 對話窗口 - GitHub Pages 部署"},"definition":{"en":"築未科技 AI 對話窗口 - GitHub Pages 部署"},"features":{"zh":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","可维护性","可测试性","可扩展性"],"ja":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","メンテナンス可能","テスト可能","スケーラブル"],"ko":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","유지 보수 가능","테스트 가능","확장 가능"],"es":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","Sistemas mantenibles","Sistemas escalables","Refactorización de aplicaciones monolíticas"],"fr":["Architecture Clean","Architecture Hexagonale","Conception Orientée Domaine","Systèmes maintenables","Systèmes évolutifs","Réorganisation d''applications monolithiques"],"de":["Clean Architecture","Hexagonale Architektur","Domain-Driven Design","Wartbare Systeme","Skalierbare Systeme","Neustrukturierung von monolithischen Anwendungen"]},"keywords":{"zh":["后端架构模式","Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","软件架构","系统设计"],"ja":["バックエンドアーキテクチャパターン","Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","ソフトウェアアーキテクチャ","システム設計"],"ko":["백엔드 아키텍처 패턴","Clean Architecture","Hexagonal Architecture","Domain-Driven Design","소프트웨어 아키텍처","시스템 설계"],"es":["patrones de arquitectura","diseño de software","arquitectura backend","sistemas escalables","domain-driven design","clean architecture","hexagonal architecture"],"fr":["modèles d''architecture","conception de logiciels","architecture backend","systèmes évolutifs","conception orientée domaine","architecture clean","architecture hexagonale"],"de":["architekturmuster","software-design","backend-architektur","skalierbare systeme","domain-driven design","clean architecture","hexagonale architektur"]}},"owner":"faint45","repo":"zhewei-ai-chat-01","repoPath":"faint45/zhewei-ai-chat-01","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.511Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"architecture-patterns","description":"Implement proven backend architecture patterns including Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design. Use when architecting complex backend systems or refactoring existing applications for better maintainability.","bodyPreview":"# Architecture Patterns\n\nMaster proven backend architecture patterns including Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design to build maintainable, testable, and scalable systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new backend systems from scratch\n- Refactoring monolithic applications for better maintainability\n- Establishing architecture standards for your team\n- Migrating from tightly coupled to loosely coupled architectures\n- Implementing domain-driven design princ","body":"# Architecture Patterns\n\nMaster proven backend architecture patterns including Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design to build maintainable, testable, and scalable systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Designing new backend systems from scratch\n- Refactoring monolithic applications for better maintainability\n- Establishing architecture standards for your team\n- Migrating from tightly coupled to loosely coupled architectures\n- Implementing domain-driven design principles\n- Creating testable and mockable codebases\n- Planning microservices decomposition\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Clean Architecture (Uncle Bob)\n\n**Layers (dependency flows inward):**\n\n- **Entities**: Core business models\n- **Use Cases**: Application business rules\n- **Interface Adapters**: Controllers, presenters, gateways\n- **Frameworks & Drivers**: UI, database, external services\n\n**Key Principles:**\n\n- Dependencies point inward\n- Inner layers know nothing about outer layers\n- Business logic independent of frameworks\n- Testable without UI, database, or external services\n\n### 2. Hexagonal Architecture (Ports and Adapters)\n\n**Components:**\n\n- **Domain Core**: Business logic\n- **Ports**: Interfaces defining interactions\n- **Adapters**: Implementations of ports (database, REST, message queue)\n\n**Benefits:**\n\n- Swap implementations easily (mock for testing)\n- Technology-agnostic core\n- Clear separation of concerns\n\n### 3. Domain-Driven Design (DDD)\n\n**Strategic Patterns:**\n\n- **Bounded Contexts**: Separate models for different domains\n- **Context Mapping**: How contexts relate\n- **Ubiquitous Language**: Shared terminology\n\n**Tactical Patterns:**\n\n- **Entities**: Objects with identity\n- **Value Objects**: Immutable objects defined by attributes\n- **Aggregates**: Consistency boundaries\n- **Repositories**: Data access abstraction\n- **Domain Events**: Things that happened\n\n## Clean Architecture Pattern\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n```\napp/\n├── domain/           # Entities & business rules\n│   ├── entities/\n│   │   ├── user.py\n│   │   └── order.py\n│   ├── value_objects/\n│   │   ├── email.py\n│   │   └── money.py\n│   └── interfaces/   # Abstract interfaces\n│       ├── user_repository.py\n│       └── payment_gateway.py\n├── use_cases/        # Application business rules\n│   ├── create_user.py\n│   ├── process_order.py\n│   └── send_notification.py\n├── adapters/         # Interface implementations\n│   ├── repositories/\n│   │   ├── postgres_user_repository.py\n│   │   └── redis_cache_repository.py\n│   ├── controllers/\n│   │   └── user_controller.py\n│   └── gateways/\n│       ├── stripe_payment_gateway.py\n│       └── sendgrid_email_gateway.py\n└── infrastructure/   # Framework & external concerns\n    ├── database.py\n    ├── config.py\n    └── logging.py\n```\n\n### Implementation Example\n\n```python\n# domain/entities/user.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n@dataclass\nclass User:\n    \"\"\"Core user entity - no framework dependencies.\"\"\"\n    id: str\n    email: str\n    name: str\n    created_at: datetime\n    is_active: bool = True\n\n    def deactivate(self):\n        \"\"\"Business rule: deactivating user.\"\"\"\n        self.is_active = False\n\n    def can_place_order(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Business rule: active users can order.\"\"\"\n        return self.is_active\n\n# domain/interfaces/user_repository.py\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom domain.entities.user import User\n\nclass IUserRepository(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Port: defines contract, no implementation.\"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def find_by_id(self, user_id: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def find_by_email(self, email: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def save(self, user: User) -> User:\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def delete(self, user_id: str) -> bool:\n        pass\n\n# use_cases/create_user.py\nfrom domain.entities.user import User\nfrom domain.interfaces.user_repository import IUserRepository\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport uuid\n\n@dataclass\nclass CreateUserRequest:\n    email: str\n    name: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass CreateUserResponse:\n    user: User\n    success: bool\n    error: Optional[str] = None\n\nclass CreateUserUseCase:\n    \"\"\"Use case: orchestrates business logic.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, user_repository: IUserRepository):\n        self.user_repository = user_repository\n\n    async def execute(self, request: CreateUserRequest) -> CreateUserResponse:\n        # Business validation\n        existing = await self.user_repository.find_by_email(request.email)\n        if existing:\n            return CreateUserResponse(\n                user=None,\n                success=False,\n                error=\"Email already exists\"\n            )\n\n        # Create entity\n        user = User(\n            id=str(uuid.uuid4()),\n            email=request.email,\n            name=request.name,\n            created_at=datetime.now(),\n            is_active=True\n        )\n\n        # Persist\n        saved_user = await self.user_repository.save(user)\n\n        return CreateUserResponse(\n            user=saved_user,\n            success=True\n        )\n\n# adapters/repositories/postgres_user_repository.py\nfrom domain.interfaces.user_repository import IUserRepository\nfrom domain.entities.user import User\nfrom typing import Optional\nimport asyncpg\n\nclass PostgresUserRepository(IUserRepository):\n    \"\"\"Adapter: PostgreSQL implementation.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, pool: asyncpg.Pool):\n        self.pool = pool\n\n    async def find_by_id(self, user_id: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            row = await conn.fetchrow(\n                \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1\", user_id\n            )\n            return self._to_entity(row) if row else None\n\n    async def find_by_email(self, email: str) -> Optional[User]:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            row = await conn.fetchrow(\n                \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1\", email\n            )\n            return self._to_entity(row) if row else None\n\n    async def save(self, user: User) -> User:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            await conn.execute(\n                \"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at, is_active)\n                VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)\n                ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE\n                SET email = $2, name = $3, is_active = $5\n                \"\"\",\n                user.id, user.email, user.name, user.created_at, user.is_active\n            )\n            return user\n\n    async def delete(self, user_id: str) -> bool:\n        async with self.pool.acquire() as conn:\n            result = await conn.execute(\n                \"DELETE FROM users WHERE id = $1\", user_id\n            )\n            return result == \"DELETE 1\"\n\n    def _to_entity(self, row) -> User:\n        \"\"\"Map database row to entity.\"\"\"\n        return User(\n            id=row[\"id\"],\n            email=row[\"email\"],\n            name=row[\"name\"],\n            created_at=row[\"created_at\"],\n            is_active=row[\"is_active\"]\n        )\n\n# adapters/controllers/user_controller.py\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException\nfrom use_cases.create_user import CreateUserUseCase, CreateUserRequest\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nrouter = APIRouter()\n\nclass CreateUserDTO(BaseModel):\n    email: str\n    name: str\n\n@router.post(\"/users\")\nasync def create_user(\n    dto: CreateUserDTO,\n    use_case: CreateUserUseCase = Depends(get_create_user_use_case)\n):\n    \"\"\"Controller: handles HTTP concerns only.\"\"\"\n    request = CreateUserRequest(email=dto.email, name=dto.name)\n    response = await use_case.execute(request)\n\n    if not response.success:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=response.error)\n\n    return {\"user\": response.user}\n```\n\n## Hexagonal Architecture Pattern\n\n```python\n# Core domain (hexagon center)\nclass OrderService:\n    \"\"\"Domain service - no infrastructure dependencies.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        order_repository: OrderRepositoryPort,\n        payment_gateway: PaymentGatewayPort,\n        notification_service: NotificationPort\n    ):\n        self.orders = order_repository\n        self.payments = payment_gateway\n        self.notifications = notification_service\n\n    async def place_order(self, order: Order) -> OrderResult:\n        # Business logic\n        if not order.is_valid():\n            return OrderResult(success=False, error=\"Invalid order\")\n\n        # Use ports (interfaces)\n        payment = await self.payments.charge(\n            amount=order.total,\n            customer=order.customer_id\n        )\n\n        if not payment.success:\n            return OrderResult(success=False, error=\"Payment failed\")\n\n        order.mark_as_paid()\n        saved_order = await self.orders.save(order)\n\n        await self.notifications.send(\n            to=order.customer_email,\n            subject=\"Order confirmed\",\n            body=f\"Order {order.id} confirmed\"\n        )\n\n        return OrderResult(success=True, order=saved_order)\n\n# Ports (interfaces)\nclass OrderRepositoryPort(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def save(self, order: Order) -> Order:\n        pass\n\nclass PaymentGatewayPort(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def charge(self, amount: Money, customer: str) -> PaymentResult:\n        pass\n\nclass NotificationPort(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    async def send(self, to: str, subject: str, body: str):\n        pass\n\n# Adapters (implementations)\nclass StripePaymentAdapter(PaymentGatewayPort):\n    \"\"\"Primary adapter: connects to Stripe API.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, api_key: str):\n        self.stripe = stripe\n        self.stripe.api_key = api_key\n\n    async def charge(self, amount: Money, customer: str) -> PaymentResult:\n        try:\n            charge = self.stripe.Charge.create(\n                amount=amount.cents,\n                currency=amount.currency,\n                customer=customer\n            )\n            return PaymentResult(success=True, transaction_id=charge.id)\n        except stripe.error.CardError as e:\n            return PaymentResult(success=False, error=str(e))\n\nclass MockPaymentAdapter(PaymentGatewayPort):\n    \"\"\"Test adapter: no external dependencies.\"\"\"\n\n    async def charge(self, amount: Money, customer: str) -> PaymentResult:\n        return PaymentResult(success=True, transaction_id=\"mock-123\")\n```\n\n## Domain-Driven Design Pattern\n\n```python\n# Value Objects (immutable)\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Email:\n    \"\"\"Value object: validated email.\"\"\"\n    value: str\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        if \"@\" not in self.value:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid email\")\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Money:\n    \"\"\"Value object: amount with currency.\"\"\"\n    amount: int  # cents\n    currency: str\n\n    def add(self, other: \"Money\") -> \"Money\":\n        if self.currency != other.currency:\n            raise ValueError(\"Currency mismatch\")\n        return Money(self.amount + other.amount, self.currency)\n\n# Entities (with identity)\nclass Order:\n    \"\"\"Entity: has identity, mutable state.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, id: str, customer: Customer):\n        self.id = id\n        self.customer = customer\n        self.items: List[OrderItem] = []\n        self.status = OrderStatus.PENDING\n        self._events: List[DomainEvent] = []\n\n    def add_item(self, product: Product, quantity: int):\n        \"\"\"Business logic in entity.\"\"\"\n        item = OrderItem(product, quantity)\n        self.items.append(item)\n        self._events.append(ItemAddedEvent(self.id, item))\n\n    def total(self) -> Money:\n        \"\"\"Calculated property.\"\"\"\n        return sum(item.subtotal() for item in self.items)\n\n    def submit(self):\n        \"\"\"State transition with business rules.\"\"\"\n        if not self.items:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cannot submit empty order\")\n        if self.status != OrderStatus.PENDING:\n            raise ValueError(\"Order already submitted\")\n\n        self.status = OrderStatus.SUBMITTED\n        self._events.append(OrderSubmittedEvent(self.id))\n\n# Aggregates (consistency boundary)\nclass Customer:\n    \"\"\"Aggregate root: controls access to entities.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, id: str, email: Email):\n        self.id = id\n        self.email = email\n        self._addresses: List[Address] = []\n        self._orders: List[str] = []  # Order IDs, not full objects\n\n    def add_address(self, address: Address):\n        \"\"\"Aggregate enforces invariants.\"\"\"\n        if len(self._addresses) >= 5:\n            raise ValueError(\"Maximum 5 addresses allowed\")\n        self._addresses.append(address)\n\n    @property\n    def primary_address(self) -> Optional[Address]:\n        return next((a for a in self._addresses if a.is_primary), None)\n\n# Domain Events\n@dataclass\nclass OrderSubmittedEvent:\n    order_id: str\n    occurred_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.now)\n\n# Repository (aggregate persistence)\nclass OrderRepository:\n    \"\"\"Repository: persist/retrieve aggregates.\"\"\"\n\n    async def find_by_id(self, order_id: str) -> Optional[Order]:\n        \"\"\"Reconstitute aggregate from storage.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    async def save(self, order: Order):\n        \"\"\"Persist aggregate and publish events.\"\"\"\n        await self._persist(order)\n        await self._publish_events(order._events)\n        order._events.clear()\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/clean-architecture-guide.md**: Detailed layer breakdown\n- **references/hexagonal-architecture-guide.md**: Ports and adapters patterns\n- **references/ddd-tactical-patterns.md**: Entities, value objects, aggregates\n- **assets/clean-architecture-template/**: Complete project structure\n- **assets/ddd-examples/**: Domain modeling examples\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Dependency Rule**: Dependencies always point inward\n2. **Interface Segregation**: Small, focused interfaces\n3. **Business Logic in Domain**: Keep frameworks out of core\n4. **Test Independence**: Core testable without infrastructure\n5. **Bounded Contexts**: Clear domain boundaries\n6. **Ubiquitous Language**: Consistent terminology\n7. **Thin Controllers**: Delegate to use cases\n8. **Rich Domain Models**: Behavior with data\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Anemic Domain**: Entities with only data, no behavior\n- **Framework Coupling**: Business logic depends on frameworks\n- **Fat Controllers**: Business logic in controllers\n- **Repository Leakage**: Exposing ORM objects\n- **Missing Abstractions**: Concrete dependencies in core\n- **Over-Engineering**: Clean architecture for simple CRUD\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:36:10.711Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Software Development Agents needing expertise in Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture, and Domain-Driven Design patterns.","zh":"非常适合需要在 Clean Architecture、Hexagonal Architecture 和 Domain-Driven Design 模式方面拥有专业知识的软件开发代理。","ja":"クリーンアーキテクチャ、ヘキサゴナルアーキテクチャ、ドメイン駆動設計パターンに関する専門知識が必要なソフトウェア開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"클린 아키텍처, 헥사고날 아키텍처, 도메인 주도 설계 패턴에 대한 전문 지식이 필요한 소프트웨어 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de software que necesitan experiencia en patrones de Arquitectura Limpia, Arquitectura Hexagonal y Diseño Dirigido por Dominio.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement de logiciels ayant besoin d''expertise en modèles d''Architecture Propre, d''Architecture Hexagonale et de Conception Orientée Objet.","de":"Perfekt für Software-Entwicklungsagenten, die Expertenwissen in Mustern für Saubere Architektur, Hexagonale Architektur und Domain-Driven Design benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de Software que necessitam de especialização em Padrões de Arquitetura Limpa, Arquitetura Hexagonal e Domain-Driven Design.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов по разработке программного обеспечения, которым необходимы знания в области шаблонов Чистой Архитектуры, Гексагональной Архитектуры и Domain-Driven Design.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء تطوير البرمجيات الذين يحتاجون إلى خبرة في أنماط الهندسة المعمارية النظيفة والهندسة السداسية والتصميم الموجه للنطاق."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design maintainable, testable, and scalable systems using proven backend architecture patterns, including implementing domain-driven design principles and establishing architecture standards for teams, all while supporting migrations from tightly coupled to loosely coupled architectures.","zh":"赋予代理设计可维护、可测试和可扩展的系统的能力，使用经过验证的后端架构模式，包括实施领域驱动设计原则和为团队建立架构标准，同时支持从紧密耦合到松散耦合的架构迁移。","ja":"バックエンドアーキテクチャパターンの実証済みを使用して、メンテナンス可能、テスト可能、スケーラブルなシステムを設計するエージェントの能力を付与し、ドメイン駆動設計の原則を実施し、チームのアーキテクチャ標準を確立し、タイトに結合されたアーキテクチャから疎に結合されたアーキテクチャへの移行をサポートします。","ko":"검증된 백엔드 아키텍처 패턴을 사용하여 유지 보수 가능한, 테스트 가능한, 확장 가능한 시스템을 설계할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하며, 도메인 주도 설계 원칙을 구현하고 팀의 아키텍처 표준을 설정하며,緊密 결합 아키텍처에서 느슨한 결합 아키텍처로의 마이그레이션을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar sistemas mantenibles, probables y escalables utilizando patrones de arquitectura de backend probados, incluyendo la implementación de principios de diseño dirigido por dominio y el establecimiento de estándares de arquitectura para equipos, todo mientras se apoyan las migraciones de arquitecturas acopladas a arquitecturas sueltas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des systèmes maintenables, testables et évolutifs en utilisant des modèles d''architecture de backend éprouvés, y compris la mise en œuvre de principes de conception orientée objet et l''établissement de normes d''architecture pour les équipes, le tout en soutenant les migrations de l''architecture fortement couplée à l''architecture faiblement couplée.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, wartbare, testbare und skalierbare Systeme mit bewährten Backend-Architekturmuster zu entwerfen, einschließlich der Implementierung von Prinzipien des Domain-Driven Design und der Festlegung von Architekturstandards für Teams, und unterstützt dabei die Migration von eng gekoppelten zu lose gekoppelten Architekturen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar sistemas mantidos, testáveis e escaláveis, utilizando padrões de arquitetura de backend comprovados, incluindo a implementação de princípios de design orientado a domínio e o estabelecimento de padrões de arquitetura para equipes, tudo isso enquanto suporta migrações de arquiteturas fortemente acopladas para arquiteturas fracamente acopladas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать поддерживаемые, тестируемые и масштабируемые системы, используя проверенные шаблоны архитектуры бэкенда, включая реализацию принципов проектирования, ориентированного на домен, и установление стандартов архитектуры для команд, все это при поддержке миграций от тесно связанных к слабо связанным архитектурам.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تصميم أنظمة قابلة للصيانة والاختبار والمقياس باستخدام أنماط معمارية للخلفية مثبتة، بما في ذلك تنفيذ مبادئ التصميم الموجه للنطاق وإنشاء معايير معمارية للفرق، كل ذلك مع دعم الهجرات من الهياكل المعمارية المرتبطة بإحكام إلى الهياكل المعمارية المرتبطة بالرخاء."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing new backend systems from scratch with scalable architecture","Refactoring monolithic applications for better maintainability and testability","Establishing and enforcing architecture standards for development teams"],"zh":["从头开始设计具有可扩展架构的新后端系统","重构单体应用以提高维护性和可测试性","为开发团队建立和执行架构标准"],"ja":["スケーラブルなアーキテクチャを持つ新しいバックエンドシステムを一から設計する","メンテナンス性とテスト性を向上させるためにモノリシックアプリケーションをリファクタリングする","開発チームのアーキテクチャ標準を確立し、執行する"],"ko":["확장 가능한 아키텍처를 가진 새로운 백엔드 시스템을 처음부터 설계하는 것","유지 보수성과 테스트성을 향상시키기 위해 모놀리스 애플리케이션을 리팩토링하는 것","개발 팀의 아키텍처 표준을 설정하고 실행하는 것"],"es":["Diseñar nuevos sistemas de backend desde cero con arquitectura escalable","Reestructurar aplicaciones monolíticas para una mejor mantenibilidad y probabilidad","Establecer y hacer cumplir estándares de arquitectura para equipos de desarrollo"],"fr":["Concevoir de nouveaux systèmes de backend à partir de zéro avec une architecture évolutives","Réaménager des applications monolithiques pour une meilleure maintenabilité et testabilité","Établir et faire respecter des normes d''architecture pour les équipes de développement"],"de":["Entwerfen von neuen Backend-Systemen von Grund auf mit skalierbarer Architektur","Umstrukturieren von monolithischen Anwendungen für bessere Wartbarkeit und Testbarkeit","Festlegen und Durchsetzen von Architekturstandards für Entwicklerteams"],"pt":["Projetar novos sistemas de backend do zero com arquitetura escalável","Reestruturar aplicações monolíticas para melhor manutenção e testabilidade","Estabelecer e aplicar padrões de arquitetura para equipes de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Проектировать новые системы бэкенда с нуля с масштабируемой архитектурой","Рефакторинг монолитных приложений для лучшей поддержки и тестируемости","Устанавливать и обеспечивать соблюдение стандартов архитектуры для команд разработки"],"ar":["تصميم أنظمة خلفية جديدة من الصفر مع هندسة قابلة للتوسيع","إعادة هيكلة التطبيقات المونوليتية لتحسين الصيانة والاختبار","إنشاء معايير معمارية للفرق وتطبيقها"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of software development principles and patterns","Focused on backend architecture, may not apply to frontend or full-stack development directly"],"zh":["需要软件开发原则和模式的知识","专注于后端架构，可能不直接适用于前端或全栈开发"],"ja":["ソフトウェア開発の原則とパターンの知識が必要","バックエンドアーキテクチャに焦点を当てているため、フロントエンドまたはフルスタック開発には直接適用できない可能性がある"],"ko":["소프트웨어 개발 원칙과 패턴에 대한 지식이 필요함","백엔드 아키텍처에 중점을 두고 있으므로 프론트엔드 또는 풀스택 개발에는 직접 적용할 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de principios y patrones de desarrollo de software","Se centra en la arquitectura de backend, puede que no se aplique directamente al desarrollo de frontend o full-stack"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en principes et modèles de développement de logiciels","Se concentre sur l''architecture de backend, peut ne pas s''appliquer directement au développement de frontend ou full-stack"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von Software-Entwicklungsprinzipien und -mustern","Konzentriert sich auf die Backend-Architektur, kann möglicherweise nicht direkt auf die Entwicklung von Frontend oder Full-Stack angewendet werden"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de princípios e padrões de desenvolvimento de software","Focado em arquitetura de backend, pode não ser aplicável diretamente ao desenvolvimento de frontend ou full-stack"],"ru":["Требует знания принципов и шаблонов разработки программного обеспечения","Сосредоточен на архитектуре бэкенда, может не применяться напрямую к разработке фронтенда или фулл-стека"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة مبادئ وأنماط تطوير البرمجيات","يركز على هندسة الخلفية، قد لا يتم تطبيقها مباشرة على تطوير الواجهة الأمامية أو التطوير الكامل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
