o":["openspec-new-change","실험적인 아티팩트 주도 접근법","개발자 도구","코드 관리","소프트웨어 개발","실험 기술"],"es":["desarrollo de software","cambio de código","artefactos experimentales","flujo de trabajo de desarrollo","AskUserQuestion","kebab-case"],"fr":["développement de logiciels","changement de code","artéfacts expérimentaux","flux de travail de développement","AskUserQuestion","kebab-case"],"de":["Softwareentwicklung","Codeänderung","experimentelle Artefakte","Entwicklungsprozess","AskUserQuestion","kebab-case"],"pt":["openspec-new-change","abordagem experimental","arteefatos","desenvolvimento de software","ferramenta AskUserQuestion","kebab-case","desenvolvimento eficiente"],"ru":["открытое изменение нового изменения","экспериментальный подход","артефакты","разработка программного обеспечения","инструмент AskUserQuestion","kebab-case","эффективная разработка"],"ar":["التغيير الجديد المفتوح","النهج التجريبي","المكونات","تطوير البرمجيات","أداة AskUserQuestion","kebab-case","التطوير الفعال"]}},"owner":"Ejyke90","repo":"naija-conflict-tracker","repoPath":"Ejyke90/naija-conflict-tracker","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.511Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-new-change","description":"Start a new OpenSpec change using the experimental artifact workflow. Use when the user wants to create a new feature, fix, or modification with a structured step-by-step approach.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Start a new change using the experimental artifact-driven approach.\n\n**Input**: The user''s request should include a change name (kebab-case) OR a description of what they want to build.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no clear input provided, ask what they want to build**\n\n   Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** (open-ended, no preset options) to ask:\n   > \"What change do you want to work on? Describe what you want to build or fix.\"\n\n   From their description, derive a kebab-case name (e.g., \"add user authentic","body":"Start a new change using the experimental artifact-driven approach.\n\n**Input**: The user''s request should include a change name (kebab-case) OR a description of what they want to build.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no clear input provided, ask what they want to build**\n\n   Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** (open-ended, no preset options) to ask:\n   > \"What change do you want to work on? Describe what you want to build or fix.\"\n\n   From their description, derive a kebab-case name (e.g., \"add user authentication\" → `add-user-auth`).\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT proceed without understanding what the user wants to build.\n\n2. **Determine the workflow schema**\n\n   Use the default schema (omit `--schema`) unless the user explicitly requests a different workflow.\n\n   **Use a different schema only if the user mentions:**\n   - A specific schema name → use `--schema <name>`\n   - \"show workflows\" or \"what workflows\" → run `openspec schemas --json` and let them choose\n\n   **Otherwise**: Omit `--schema` to use the default.\n\n3. **Create the change directory**\n   ```bash\n   openspec new change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n   Add `--schema <name>` only if the user requested a specific workflow.\n   This creates a scaffolded change at `openspec/changes/<name>/` with the selected schema.\n\n4. **Show the artifact status**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n   This shows which artifacts need to be created and which are ready (dependencies satisfied).\n\n5. **Get instructions for the first artifact**\n   The first artifact depends on the schema (e.g., `proposal` for spec-driven).\n   Check the status output to find the first artifact with status \"ready\".\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions <first-artifact-id> --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n   This outputs the template and context for creating the first artifact.\n\n6. **STOP and wait for user direction**\n\n**Output**\n\nAfter completing the steps, summarize:\n- Change name and location\n- Schema/workflow being used and its artifact sequence\n- Current status (0/N artifacts complete)\n- The template for the first artifact\n- Prompt: \"Ready to create the first artifact? Just describe what this change is about and I''ll draft it, or ask me to continue.\"\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Do NOT create any artifacts yet - just show the instructions\n- Do NOT advance beyond showing the first artifact template\n- If the name is invalid (not kebab-case), ask for a valid name\n- If a change with that name already exists, suggest continuing that change instead\n- Pass --schema if using a non-default workflow\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:38:02.643Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Agile Development Agents needing streamlined project initialization with artifact-driven approaches.","zh":"Perfect for Agile Development Agents needing streamlined project initialization with artifact-driven approaches.","ja":"Perfect for Agile Development Agents needing streamlined project initialization with artifact-driven approaches.","ko":"Perfect for Agile Development Agents needing streamlined project initialization with artifact-driven approaches.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo Ágil que necesitan una inicialización de proyectos optimizada con enfoques impulsados por artefactos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement Agile ayant besoin d''une initialisation de projet simplifiée avec des approches impulsées par des artefacts.","de":"Perfekt für Agile-Development-Agents, die eine optimierte Projektinitialisierung mit artefaktgesteuerten Ansätzen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Ágil que precisam de inicialização de projeto simplificada com abordagens impulsionadas por artefatos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Agile-разработки, которым необходима упрощенная инициализация проектов с помощью подходов, ориентированных на артефакты.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التطوير المرنة التي تحتاج إلى تهيئة مشروع مبسطة باستخدام طرق مدفوعة بالتحف"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to derive kebab-case names from user descriptions and initiate new changes using the experimental artifact-driven approach, leveraging tools like the AskUserQuestion tool for open-ended user input and description parsing for project naming conventions.","zh":"Empowers agents to derive kebab-case names from user descriptions and initiate new changes using the experimental artifact-driven approach, leveraging tools like the AskUserQuestion tool for open-ended user input and description parsing for project naming conventions.","ja":"Empowers agents to derive kebab-case names from user descriptions and initiate new changes using the experimental artifact-driven approach, leveraging tools like the AskUserQuestion tool for open-ended user input and description parsing for project naming conventions.","ko":"Empowers agents to derive kebab-case names from user descriptions and initiate new changes using the experimental artifact-driven approach, leveraging tools like the AskUserQuestion tool for open-ended user input and description parsing for project naming conventions.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a derivar nombres en kebab-case a partir de descripciones de usuarios e iniciar nuevos cambios utilizando el enfoque experimental impulsado por artefactos, aprovechando herramientas como la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la entrada de usuario de preguntas abiertas y el análisis de descripciones para las convenciones de nomenclatura de proyectos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de dériver des noms en kebab-case à partir de descriptions d''utilisateurs et d''initier de nouvelles modifications en utilisant l''approche expérimentale impulsée par des artefacts, en exploitant des outils comme l''outil AskUserQuestion pour une saisie utilisateur à questions ouvertes et l''analyse de descriptions pour les conventions de dénomination de projets.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, kebab-case-Namen aus Benutzerbeschreibungen abzuleiten und neue Änderungen mit dem experimentellen, artefaktgesteuerten Ansatz zu initiieren, indem es Tools wie das AskUserQuestion-Tool für offene Benutzereingaben und die Beschreibungsparsing für Projektbenennungskonventionen nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a derivar nomes em kebab-case a partir de descrições de usuário e iniciar novas alterações usando a abordagem experimental impulsionada por artefatos, aproveitando ferramentas como a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para entrada de usuário aberta e análise de descrições para convenções de nomenclatura de projeto.","ru":"Позволяет агентам получать имена в формате kebab-case из описаний пользователей и инициировать новые изменения с помощью экспериментального подхода, ориентированного на артефакты, используя инструменты, такие как AskUserQuestion, для открытого ввода пользователем и парсинга описаний для соглашений об именах проектов.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من استخراج أسماء بالشكل kebab-case من وصفات المستخدم وبدء تغييرات جديدة باستخدام النهج التجريبي المعتمد على التحف، مستفيداً من أدوات مثل أداة AskUserQuestion للبيانات المفتوحة للمستخدم وتحليل الوصفات لأسماء المشاريع"},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing new projects with descriptive names","Parsing user input for project descriptions","Deriving kebab-case names for consistent project naming"],"zh":["Initializing new projects with descriptive names","Parsing user input for project descriptions","Deriving kebab-case names for consistent project naming"],"ja":["Initializing new projects with descriptive names","Parsing user input for project descriptions","Deriving kebab-case names for consistent project naming"],"ko":["Initializing new projects with descriptive names","Parsing user input for project descriptions","Deriving kebab-case names for consistent project naming"],"es":["Inicializar nuevos proyectos con nombres descriptivos","Analizar la entrada de usuario para descripciones de proyectos","Derivar nombres en kebab-case para una nomenclatura de proyectos coherente"],"fr":["Initialiser de nouveaux projets avec des noms descriptifs","Analyser la saisie utilisateur pour les descriptions de projets","Dériver des noms en kebab-case pour une dénomination de projets cohérente"],"de":["Neue Projekte mit beschreibenden Namen initialisieren","Benutzereingaben für Projektbeschreibungen parsen","Kebab-case-Namen für eine konsistente Projektbenennung ableiten"],"pt":["Inicializar novos projetos com nomes descritivos","Analizar a entrada do usuário para descrições de projeto","Derivar nomes em kebab-case para nomenclatura de projeto consistente"],"ru":["Инициализация новых проектов с описательными именами","Парсинг ввода пользователя для описаний проекта","Получение имен в формате kebab-case для последовательных соглашений об именах проектов"],"ar":["تهيئة مشاريع جديدة بأسماء وصفية","تحليل إدخال المستخدم لوصفات المشروع","استخراج أسماء بالشكل kebab-case لتسمية المشاريع المتسقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user input or description for project initialization","Limited to kebab-case naming convention"],"zh":["Requires user input or description for project initialization","Limited to kebab-case naming convention"],"ja":["Requires user input or description for project initialization","Limited to kebab-case naming convention"],"ko":["Requires user input or description for project initialization","Limited to kebab-case naming convention"],"es":["Requiere entrada de usuario o descripción para la inicialización del proyecto","Limitado a la convención de nomenclatura en kebab-case"],"fr":["Nécessite une saisie utilisateur ou une description pour l''initialisation du projet","Limité à la convention de dénomination en kebab-case"],"de":["Benötigt Benutzereingaben oder Beschreibungen für die Projektinitialisierung","Begrenzt auf die Kebab-case-Benennungskonvention"],"pt":["Requer entrada ou descrição do usuário para inicialização do projeto","Limitado à convenção de nomenclatura em kebab-case"],"ru":["Требует ввода или описания пользователя для инициализации проекта","Ограничен соглашением об именах в формате kebab-case"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال المستخدم أو الوصف لتهيئة المشروع","محدود بالاتفاقية لتسمية المشاريع بالشكل kebab-case"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('aiyuekuang/LLMProxy/code-review', 'community', 'aiyuekuang', 'LLMProxy', 'aiyuekuang/LLMProxy', 'code-review', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.511Z', '2026-02-18T12:38:46.447Z', NULL, '{"id":"aiyuekuang/LLMProxy/code-review","name":"code-review","description":{"zh":"代码审查技能是一种系统的代码审查过程，遵循Sentry、Trail of Bits和Google工程团队的行业最佳实践","ja":"コードレビュースキルは、Sentry、Trail of Bits、Googleエンジニアリングチームの業界標準に基づく体系的なコードレビュー過程です","ko":"코드 리뷰 스킬은 Sentry, Trail of Bits 및 Google 엔지니어링 팀의 산업 표준에 기반한 체계적인 코드 리뷰 프로세스입니다","es":"Nuestro sistema de revisión de código sigue las mejores prácticas de la industria para garantizar la calidad del código","fr":"Notre système de révision de code suit les meilleures pratiques de l''industrie pour garantir la qualité du code","de":"Unser Code-Überprüfungssystem folgt den Branchenbest Practices, um die Code-Qualität zu gewährleisten","pt":"O skill de revisão de código ajuda a garantir a qualidade do código, seguindo as melhores práticas da indústria","ru":"Навык код-ревью помогает обеспечить качество кода, следуя лучшим практикам отрасли","ar":"مهارة مراجعة الكود تساعد على ضمان جودة الكود، متبعة أفضل الممارسات في الصناعة","en":"Seamlessly route requests to your LLM backends—whether you''re using stream=false for standard JSON responses or stream=true for real-time token streaming via Server-Sent Events (SSE). LLMProxy handles both modes out of the box, with zero buffering on streams, intelligent load balancing, and OpenA..."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码审查技能 - 优化代码质量","ja":"コードレビュースキル - コード品質の最適化","ko":"코드 리뷰 스킬 - 코드 품질 최적화","es":"Revisión de código automatizada","fr":"Révision de code automatisée","de":"Automatisierte Code-Überprüfung","pt":"Revisão de Código - Melhore a Qualidade do Seu Código","ru":"Код-ревью - Улучшите качество вашего кода","ar":"مراجعة الكود - تحسين جودة الكود الخاص بك","en":"code-review"},"description":{"zh":"代码审查技能是一种系统的代码审查过程，遵循Sentry、Trail of Bits和Google工程团队的行业最佳实践","ja":"コードレビュースキルは、Sentry、Trail of Bits、Googleエンジニアリングチームの業界標準に基づく体系的なコードレビュー過程です","ko":"코드 리뷰 스킬은 Sentry, Trail of Bits 및 Google 엔지니어링 팀의 산업 표준에 기반한 체계적인 코드 리뷰 프로세스입니다","es":"Nuestro sistema de revisión de código sigue las mejores prácticas de la industria para garantizar la calidad del código","fr":"Notre système de révision de code suit les meilleures pratiques de l''industrie pour garantir la qualité du code","de":"Unser Code-Überprüfungssystem folgt den Branchenbest Practices, um die Code-Qualität zu gewährleisten","pt":"O skill de revisão de código ajuda a garantir a qualidade do código, seguindo as melhores práticas da indústria","ru":"Навык код-ревью помогает обеспечить качество кода, следуя лучшим практикам отрасли","ar":"مهارة مراجعة الكود تساعد على ضمان جودة الكود، متبعة أفضل الممارسات في الصناعة","en":"Seamlessly route requests to your LLM backends—whether you''re using stream=false for standard JSON responses or stream=true for real-time token streaming via..."},"definition":{"en":"Seamlessly route requests to your LLM backends—whether you''re using stream=false for standard JSON responses or stream=true for real-time token streaming via Server-Sent Events (SSE). LLMProxy handles both modes out of the box, with zero buffering on streams, intelligent load balancing, and OpenAI-compatible API routing."},"features":{"zh":["系统的代码审查过程","发现安全漏洞和错误","确保代码质量","遵循行业最佳实践","支持多种编程语言"],"ja":["体系的なコードレビュー過程","セキュリティの脆弱性やエラーの発見","コード品質の確保","業界標準に基づく","多くのプログラミング言語に対応"],"ko":["체계적인 코드 리뷰 프로세스","보안 취약점 및 오류 발견","코드 품질 보장","산업 표준에 기반","다수의 프로그래밍 언어 지원"],"es":["Proceso de revisión de código sistemático","Seguimiento de las mejores prácticas de la industria","Detección de errores y vulnerabilidades de seguridad","Mejora de la calidad del código","Compatibilidad con flujos de trabajo de desarrollo de software"],"fr":["Processus de révision de code systématique","Suivi des meilleures pratiques de l''industrie","Détection des erreurs et des vulnérabilités de sécurité","Amélioration de la qualité du code","Compatibilité avec les flux de travail de développement de logiciels"],"de":["Systematischer Code-Überprüfungsprozess","Einhaltung von Branchenbest Practices","Erkennung von Fehlern und Sicherheitslücken","Verbesserung der Code-Qualität","Kompatibilität mit Software-Entwicklungsworkflows"],"pt":["Revisão sistemática do código","Análise de vulnerabilidades de segurança","Detecção de bugs e odores de código","Garantia da qualidade do código","Compatibilidade com Sentry, Trail of Bits e Google"],"ru":["Систематический код-ревью","Анализ уязвимостей безопасности","Обнаружение багов и кодорах","Обеспечение качества кода","Совместимость с Sentry, Trail of Bits и Google"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود المنهجية","تحليل الثغرات الأمنية","اكتشاف الأخطاء وروائح الكود","ضمان جودة الكود","التوافق مع Sentry و Trail of Bits و Google"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码质量","安全漏洞","错误发现","行业最佳实践","编程语言","代码审查工具","代码优化"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード品質","セキュリティの脆弱性","エラー発見","業界標準","プログラミング言語","コードレビューツール","コード最適化"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 품질","보안 취약점","오류 발견","산업 표준","프로그래밍 언어","코드 리뷰 도구","코드 최적화"],"es":["revisión de código","calidad del código","mejores prácticas","desarrollo de software","seguridad del código","pruebas de código","análisis de código"],"fr":["révision de code","qualité du code","meilleures pratiques","développement de logiciels","sécurité du code","tests de code","analyse de code"],"de":["Code-Überprüfung","Code-Qualität","Branchenbest Practices","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Sicherheit","Code-Tests","Code-Analyse"],"pt":["revisão de código","qualidade do código","segurança do código","análise de código","desenvolvimento de software","melhoria da qualidade do código"],"ru":["код-ревью","качество кода","безопасность кода","анализ кода","разработка программного обеспечения","улучшение качества кода"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود","جودة الكود","أمان الكود","تحليل الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","تحسين جودة الكود"]}},"owner":"aiyuekuang","repo":"LLMProxy","repoPath":"aiyuekuang/LLMProxy","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.511Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"code-review","description":"Perform thorough code reviews with security, performance, and quality checks. Use when reviewing PRs, auditing code changes, or finding potential bugs.","bodyPreview":"# Code Review Skill\n\nSystematic code review process following industry best practices from Sentry, Trail of Bits, and Google engineering teams.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Reviewing pull requests\n- Auditing code for security vulnerabilities\n- Finding bugs and code smells\n- Ensuring code quality standards\n\n---\n\n# 🔍 Review Process\n\n## 1. Understand Context First\n\nBefore reviewing code:\n- Read the PR description and linked issues\n- Understand the business requirements\n- Check if there are relate","body":"# Code Review Skill\n\nSystematic code review process following industry best practices from Sentry, Trail of Bits, and Google engineering teams.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Reviewing pull requests\n- Auditing code for security vulnerabilities\n- Finding bugs and code smells\n- Ensuring code quality standards\n\n---\n\n# 🔍 Review Process\n\n## 1. Understand Context First\n\nBefore reviewing code:\n- Read the PR description and linked issues\n- Understand the business requirements\n- Check if there are related tests or documentation\n\n## 2. Review Checklist\n\n### ✅ Correctness\n- [ ] Does the code do what it''s supposed to do?\n- [ ] Are edge cases handled?\n- [ ] Is error handling appropriate?\n- [ ] Are there any obvious bugs?\n\n### ✅ Security\n- [ ] Input validation present?\n- [ ] No hardcoded secrets/credentials?\n- [ ] SQL injection prevention?\n- [ ] XSS prevention?\n- [ ] Authentication/authorization correct?\n- [ ] Sensitive data properly handled?\n\n### ✅ Performance\n- [ ] No N+1 queries?\n- [ ] Appropriate indexing?\n- [ ] No memory leaks?\n- [ ] Efficient algorithms used?\n- [ ] Caching considered where appropriate?\n\n### ✅ Code Quality\n- [ ] Code is readable and self-documenting?\n- [ ] No unnecessary complexity?\n- [ ] DRY - no code duplication?\n- [ ] Single responsibility principle followed?\n- [ ] Consistent naming conventions?\n\n### ✅ Testing\n- [ ] Unit tests for new functionality?\n- [ ] Edge cases tested?\n- [ ] Error paths tested?\n- [ ] Integration tests where needed?\n\n### ✅ Documentation\n- [ ] Public APIs documented?\n- [ ] Complex logic explained?\n- [ ] README updated if needed?\n\n---\n\n# 🐛 Common Issues to Look For\n\n## Go Code\n\n```go\n// ❌ Bad: Ignoring errors\nresult, _ := doSomething()\n\n// ✅ Good: Handle errors\nresult, err := doSomething()\nif err != nil {\n    return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to do something: %w\", err)\n}\n```\n\n```go\n// ❌ Bad: Defer in loop\nfor _, item := range items {\n    f, _ := os.Open(item)\n    defer f.Close()  // Won''t close until function returns\n}\n\n// ✅ Good: Close immediately or use closure\nfor _, item := range items {\n    func() {\n        f, _ := os.Open(item)\n        defer f.Close()\n        // process f\n    }()\n}\n```\n\n## TypeScript/React Code\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Bad: Missing dependency in useEffect\nuseEffect(() => {\n  fetchData(userId);\n}, []);  // userId missing\n\n// ✅ Good: Include all dependencies\nuseEffect(() => {\n  fetchData(userId);\n}, [userId]);\n```\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Bad: Inline object causing re-renders\n<Component style={{ margin: 10 }} />\n\n// ✅ Good: Stable reference\nconst style = useMemo(() => ({ margin: 10 }), []);\n<Component style={style} />\n```\n\n## SQL/Database\n\n```sql\n-- ❌ Bad: SQL injection risk\nquery := \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = \" + userInput\n\n-- ✅ Good: Parameterized query\nquery := \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1\"\ndb.Query(query, userInput)\n```\n\n---\n\n# 📝 Review Feedback Guidelines\n\n## Be Constructive\n\n```markdown\n// ❌ Bad feedback\n\"This code is wrong\"\n\n// ✅ Good feedback\n\"This might cause a race condition when multiple goroutines access `sharedMap`. \nConsider using `sync.RWMutex` or `sync.Map` for thread-safe access.\"\n```\n\n## Categorize Comments\n\n- **[Must Fix]**: Security issues, bugs, data loss risks\n- **[Should Fix]**: Performance issues, code smells\n- **[Suggestion]**: Style improvements, optional enhancements\n- **[Question]**: Seeking clarification\n\n## Provide Examples\n\n```markdown\n// Instead of just pointing out the issue, show the fix:\n\n**Issue**: Potential nil pointer dereference\n\n**Current code**:\n```go\nreturn user.Name\n```\n\n**Suggested fix**:\n```go\nif user == nil {\n    return \"\"\n}\nreturn user.Name\n```\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔐 Security Review Focus\n\n## OWASP Top 10 Checklist\n\n1. **Injection** - SQL, NoSQL, OS command injection\n2. **Broken Authentication** - Session management, credential storage\n3. **Sensitive Data Exposure** - Encryption, data masking\n4. **XML External Entities** - XXE attacks\n5. **Broken Access Control** - Authorization checks\n6. **Security Misconfiguration** - Default credentials, error messages\n7. **Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)** - Input/output encoding\n8. **Insecure Deserialization** - Object validation\n9. **Known Vulnerabilities** - Dependency versions\n10. **Insufficient Logging** - Audit trails\n\n---\n\n# 📚 References\n\n- [Google Code Review Guidelines](https://google.github.io/eng-practices/review/)\n- [getsentry/code-review](https://github.com/getsentry/skills/tree/main/plugins/sentry-skills/skills/code-review)\n- [trailofbits/differential-review](https://github.com/trailofbits/skills/tree/main/plugins/differential-review)\n- [obra/requesting-code-review](https://github.com/obra/superpowers/blob/main/skills/requesting-code-review/SKILL.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:38:46.447Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring systematic code review processes and industry best practices from Sentry, Trail of Bits, and Google engineering teams.","zh":"适用于需要系统代码审查流程和Sentry、Trail of Bits和Google工程团队行业最佳实践的代码分析代理的理想选择。","ja":"Sentry、Trail of Bits、Googleエンジニアリングチームの体系的なコードレビュー処理と業界のベストプラクティスを必要とするコード分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Sentry, Trail of Bits 및 Google 엔지니어링 팀의 체계적인 코드 리뷰 프로세스와 산업 최고의 실践이 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis de Código que requieren procesos de revisión de código sistemáticos y las mejores prácticas de la industria de los equipos de ingeniería de Sentry, Trail of Bits y Google.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant des processus de révision de code systématiques et les meilleures pratiques de l''industrie des équipes d''ingénierie de Sentry, Trail of Bits et Google.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die systematische Code-Überprüfungsprozesse und Branche-Best-Practices von den Ingenieursteams von Sentry, Trail of Bits und Google erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que exigem processos sistemáticos de revisão de código e as melhores práticas da indústria das equipes de engenharia da Sentry, Trail of Bits e Google.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих систематических процессов проверки кода и отраслевых лучших практик команд инженерии Sentry, Trail of Bits и Google.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل الشفرة التي تتطلب عمليات مراجعة شفرة منهجية وأفضل الممارسات في الصناعة من فرق الهندسة في Sentry و Trail of Bits و Google."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform thorough code audits for security vulnerabilities, identify bugs and code smells, and ensure adherence to code quality standards through intelligent load balancing and streaming via Server-Sent Events (SSE).","zh":"赋予代理执行彻底的代码审计以发现安全漏洞、识别错误和代码异味，并通过Server-Sent Events（SSE）中的智能负载平衡和流媒体确保遵守代码质量标准。","ja":"セキュリティ脆弱性を発見し、バグやコードの悪い匂いを識別し、Server-Sent Events（SSE）を介したインテリジェントな負荷分散とストリーミングによりコード品質標準の遵守を確実にするための徹底的なコード監査をエージェントに実行する力を与えます。","ko":"보안 취약점을 발견하고 버그 및 코드 냄새를 식별하고 Server-Sent Events(SSE)를 통한 지능형 로드 밸런싱 및 스트리밍을 통해 코드 품질 표준의 준수를 보장하는 철저한 코드 감사를 에이전트가 수행할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar auditorías de código exhaustivas para vulnerabilidades de seguridad, identificar errores y olores de código, y garantizar el cumplimiento de los estándares de calidad de código a través de un equilibrio de carga inteligente y transmisión mediante Server-Sent Events (SSE).","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des audits de code exhaustifs pour les vulnérabilités de sécurité, d''identifier les bogues et les odeurs de code, et de garantir le respect des normes de qualité de code via un équilibrage de charge intelligent et une transmission via les événements envoyés par le serveur (SSE).","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, umfassende Code-Audits für Sicherheitslücken durchzuführen, Fehler und Code-Gerüche zu identifizieren und die Einhaltung von Code-Qualitätsstandards durch intelligente Lastverteilung und Streaming über Server-Sent Events (SSE) zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Permite que os agentes realizem auditorias de código abrangentes para vulnerabilidades de segurança, identifiquem bugs e odores de código, e garantam a adesão aos padrões de qualidade de código por meio de balanceamento de carga inteligente e transmissão via Server-Sent Events (SSE).","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные аудиты кода для уязвимостей безопасности, выявлять ошибки и запахи кода, а также обеспечивать соблюдение стандартов качества кода за счет интеллектуального балансирования нагрузки и потоковой передачи через Server-Sent Events (SSE).","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إجراء تدقيقات شاملة للشفرة لتحديد الثغرات الأمنية والاخطاء وروائح الشفرة، وضمان الامتثال لمعايير جودة الشفرة من خلال تحسين التحميل والبث عبر Server-Sent Events (SSE)."},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing pull requests for compliance and quality","Auditing codebases for security vulnerabilities and performance issues","Ensuring code quality standards across large repositories"],"zh":["审核拉取请求以确保遵守和质量","审核代码库以发现安全漏洞和性能问题","确保大型存储库中的一致代码质量标准"],"ja":["コンプライアンスと品質を確保するためのプルリクエストのレビュー","セキュリティ脆弱性とパフォーマンスの問題を発見するためのコードベースの監査","大規模なリポジトリ全体での一貫したコード品質標準の確保"],"ko":["준수 및 품질을 보장하기 위한 풀 요청审查","보안 취약점 및 성능 문제를 발견하기 위한 코드베이스 감사","대형 저장소 전반에 걸친 일관된 코드 품질 표준 보장"],"es":["Revisar solicitudes de extracción para cumplimiento y calidad","Auditar bases de código para vulnerabilidades de seguridad y problemas de rendimiento","Garantizar los estándares de calidad de código en grandes repositorios"],"fr":["Réviser les demandes d''extraction pour la conformité et la qualité","Auditer les bases de code pour les vulnérabilités de sécurité et les problèmes de performances","Assurer les normes de qualité de code dans les grands référentiels"],"de":["Ziehen von Anfragen für Konformität und Qualität überprüfen","Codebasen für Sicherheitslücken und Leistungsprobleme auditen","Code-Qualitätsstandards in großen Repositorys gewährleisten"],"pt":["Revisar solicitações de pull para garantir conformidade e qualidade","Auditar bases de código para vulnerabilidades de segurança e problemas de desempenho","Garantir padrões de qualidade de código em repositórios grandes"],"ru":["Просмотр запросов на объединение для обеспечения соответствия и качества","Аудит кодовых баз для уязвимостей безопасности и проблем с производительностью","Обеспечение стандартов качества кода на больших репозиториях"],"ar":["استعراض طلبات الاندماج لضمان المطابقة والجودة","تدقيق قواعد الشفرة للثغرات الأمنية ومشاكل الأداء","ضمان معايير جودة الشفرة في مستودعات كبيرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with LLM backends","Depends on stream=false for standard JSON responses or stream=true for real-time token streaming"],"zh":["需要与LLM后端集成","依赖于stream=false进行标准JSON响应或stream=true进行实时令牌流式传输"],"ja":["LLMバックエンドとの統合が必要","stream=falseによる標準的なJSONレスポンスまたはstream=trueによるリアルタイムトークンストリーミングに依存"],"ko":["LLM 백엔드와의 통합이 필요","표준 JSON 응답을 위한 stream=false 또는 실시간 토큰 스트리밍을 위한 stream=true에 의존"],"es":["Requiere integración con backends LLM","Depende de stream=false para respuestas JSON estándar o stream=true para token de transmisión en tiempo real"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec les backends LLM","Dépend de stream=false pour les réponses JSON standard ou stream=true pour le jeton de transmission en temps réel"],"de":["Benötigt Integration mit LLM-Backends","Hängt von stream=false für Standard-JSON-Antworten oder stream=true für Echtzeit-Token-Streaming ab"],"pt":["Exige integração com backends LLM","Depende de stream=false para respostas JSON padrão ou stream=true para streaming de tokens em tempo real"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с бэкендами LLM","Зависит от stream=false для стандартных ответов JSON или stream=true для потоковой передачи токенов в реальном времени"],"ar":["يتطلب تكاملًا مع الخوادم الخلفية LLM","يعتمد على stream=false لاستجابات JSON القياسية أو stream=true للبث الفعلي لأشكال العلامات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
