成永续期货协议支持多种资产","利用稳定币作为抵押品","支持高达1000倍的杠杆"],"ja":["RWAアセット、暗号資産、株式、指数をサポート","開発者は革新的なアプリケーションを構築できます","合成永続先物プロトコルは多様な資産をサポート","スターブルコインを利用した担保","最大1000倍のレバレッジをサポート"],"ko":["RWA 자산, 암호화폐, 주식, 지수를 지원합니다","개발자는 혁신적인 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있습니다","합성 영속 선물 프로토콜은 여러 자산을 지원합니다","안정적인 코인을 이용한 담보","최대 1000배의 레버리지 지원"],"es":["Soporte para activos RWA, criptomonedas, acciones y índices","Posiciones apalancadas con hasta 1000x de apalancamiento","Bóveda de liquidez central como contraparte de todos los trades","Precios que combinan un oráculo personalizado, un AMM virtual y suavizamiento TWAP"],"fr":["Prise en charge des actifs RWA, des crypto-monnaies, des actions et des indices","Positions à effet de levier avec jusqu''à 1000x de levier","Coffre de liquidité central en tant que contrepartie de tous les trades","Prix qui combinent un oracle personnalisé, un AMM virtuel et un lissage TWAP"],"de":["Unterstützung für RWA-Assets, Kryptowährungen, Aktien und Indizes","Hebelwirkung mit bis zu 1000x Hebelwirkung","Zentrale Liquiditätsbörse als Kontrahent für alle Trades","Preise, die einen benutzerdefinierten Oracle, ein virtuelles AMM und TWAP-Glättung kombinieren"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de ideias em designs","Diálogo colaborativo natural","Refinamento de ideias por meio de perguntas","Apresentação de designs em seções","Verificação de designs após cada seção"],"ru":["Разработка идей в дизайн","Естественное сотрудничество","Уточнение идей посредством вопросов","Презентация дизайнов в разделах","Проверка дизайнов после каждого раздела"],"ar":["تحويل الأفكار إلى تصاميم","حوار تعاوني طبيعي","تحسين الأفكار من خلال أسئلة","عرض التصاميم في أقسام","التحقق من التصاميم بعد كل قسم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["合成永续期货协议","RWA资产","加密货币","股票","指数","合成金融","开发者","创新应用"],"ja":["合成永続先物プロトコル","RWAアセット","暗号資産","株式","指数","合成金融","開発者","革新的なアプリケーション"],"ko":["합성 영속 선물 프로토콜","RWA 자산","암호화폐","주식","지수","합성 금융","개발자","혁신적인 애플리케이션"],"es":["brainstorming","protocolo de futuros perpetuos","activos RWA","criptomonedas","acciones","índices","posiciones apalancadas","bóveda de liquidez central"],"fr":["brainstorming","protocole de futures perpétuels","actifs RWA","crypto-monnaies","actions","indices","positions à effet de levier","coffre de liquidité central"],"de":["brainstorming","perpetual-futures-protokoll","RWA-Assets","Kryptowährungen","Aktien","Indizes","hebelwirkung","zentrale liquiditätsbörse"],"pt":["brainstorming","desenvolvimento de ideias","design","diálogo colaborativo","refinamento de ideias","apresentação de designs"],"ru":["мозговой штурм","разработка идей","дизайн","естественное сотрудничество","уточнение идей","презентация дизайнов"],"ar":["تمحور الأفكار","تحويل الأفكار","تصاميم","حوار تعاوني","تحسين الأفكار","عرض التصاميم"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.511Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"brainstorming","description":"Use when creating or developing, before writing code or implementation plans - refines rough ideas into fully-formed designs through collaborative questioning, alternative exploration, and incremental validation. Dont use during clear mechanical processes","bodyPreview":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n- Check out the current project state first (files, d","body":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n- Check out the current project state first (files, docs, recent commits)\n- Ask questions one at a time to refine the idea\n- Prefer multiple choice questions when possible, but open-ended is fine too\n- Only one question per message - if a topic needs more exploration, break it into multiple questions\n- Focus on understanding: purpose, constraints, success criteria\n\n**Research with Experts:**\n\n- If the idea involves specialized knowledge, identify relevant experts\n- Delegate reesarch task to subagent using the `task(Researcher)` tool\n\n**Exploring approaches:**\n- Propose 2-3 different approaches with trade-offs\n- Present options conversationally with your recommendation and reasoning\n- Lead with your recommended option and explain why\n\n**Presenting the design:**\n- Once you believe you understand what you''re building, present the design\n- Break it into sections of 200-300 words\n- Ask after each section whether it looks right so far\n- Cover: architecture, components, data flow, error handling, testing\n- Be ready to go back and clarify if something doesn''t make sense\n\n## During Dicsussion\n\n**Question Presentation:**\n\n- Present questions and options clearly and concisely\n- Show question as a title, with options or details below\n- use numbered or lettered lists for options. Allowing the user to pick by number/letter\n- After presenting a section of the design, ask: \"Does this look right so far?\"\n\n**Ensure Consistency:**\n\n- Keep track of previous answers and design decisions\n- Refer back to earlier points to ensure alignment\n- Adjust the design based on feedback and new information\n\n**Shift in Direction:**\n\n- If the user indicates a significant change in direction, pause and reassess\n- Check if the user is referring to forking a previous question. If so, go back to that question and present alternatives again\n- Ask clarifying questions to understand the new direction\n- Confirm understanding before proceeding with the new direction\n\n## After the Design\n\n**Documentation:**\n\n- Write the validated design with the proscribed storage backend.\n- Use elements-of-style:writing-clearly-and-concisely skill if available\n- Commit the design document to git\n\n**Implementation (if continuing):**\n\n- Ask: \"Ready to set up for implementation?\" If yes:\n  - Use `superpowers_using_git_worktrees` skill to create isolated workspace\n  - Use `superpowers_writing_plans` to create detailed implementation plan\n- Otherwise, end the session\n\n## Key Principles\n\n- **One question at a time** - Don''t overwhelm with multiple questions\n- **Multiple choice preferred** - Easier to answer than open-ended when possible\n- **YAGNI ruthlessly** - Remove unnecessary features from all designs\n- **Explore alternatives** - Always propose 2-3 approaches before settling\n- **Incremental validation** - Present design in sections, validate each\n- **Be flexible** - Go back and clarify when something doesn''t make sense\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:39:06.183Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Design System Agents tasked with transforming abstract concepts into structured technical specifications.","zh":"设计系统代理将抽象概念转化为结构化的技术规格时至关重要。","ja":"抽象的な概念を構造化された技術仕様に変換することに従事する設計システムエージェントには不可欠です。","ko":"추상적인 개념을 구조화된 기술 사양으로 변환하는 데 종사하는 디자인 시스템 에이전트에게 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para los Agentes del Sistema de Diseño encargados de transformar conceptos abstractos en especificaciones técnicas estructuradas.","fr":"Essentiel pour les Agents de Système de Conception chargés de transformer des concepts abstraits en spécifications techniques structurées.","de":"Wesentlich für Design-System-Agents, die mit der Umwandlung abstrakter Konzepte in strukturierte technische Spezifikationen betraut sind.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Sistema de Design encarregados de transformar conceitos abstratos em especificações técnicas estruturadas.","ru":"Необходим для агентов системы дизайна, задачей которых является преобразование абстрактных концепций в структурированные технические спецификации.","ar":"ضروري لعمليات نظام التصميم المكلف بتحويل المفاهيم المجردة إلى مواصفات تقنية منظمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables collaborative, iterative refinement of ideas through natural dialogue, systematically breaking down high-level concepts into detailed design sections (200-300 words) with built-in validation checkpoints after each segment.","zh":"通过自然对话实现协作、迭代的想法改进，系统地将高层概念分解为详细的设计部分（200-300字），并在每个部分后提供内置的验证检查点。","ja":"自然な対話を通じて共同でアイデアを改良し、高レベルの概念を詳細な設計セクション（200-300語）に系統的に分解し、各セクションの後に組み込みの検証チェックポイントを提供する。","ko":"자연스러운 대화를 통해 협력적이고 반복적인 아이디어의 개선을 가능하게 하며, 높은 수준의 개념을詳細한 설계 섹션(200-300 단어)으로 체계적으로 분해하고, 각 섹션 후에 내장된 검증 확인점을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite un refino colaborativo e iterativo de ideas a través del diálogo natural, descomponiendo sistemáticamente conceptos de alto nivel en secciones de diseño detalladas (200-300 palabras) con puntos de control de validación integrados después de cada segmento.","fr":"Permet un raffinement collaboratif et itératif des idées à travers le dialogue naturel, en décomposant systématiquement les concepts de haut niveau en sections de conception détaillées (200-300 mots) avec des points de contrôle de validation intégrés après chaque segment.","de":"Ermöglicht ein kollaboratives, iteratives Verfeinern von Ideen durch natürliche Dialoge, indem hochstufige Konzepte systematisch in detaillierte Designabschnitte (200-300 Wörter) mit integrierten Validierungsprüfpunkten nach jedem Segment unterteilt werden.","pt":"Permite a refinaria colaborativa e iterativa de ideias por meio de diálogo natural, dividindo sistematicamente conceitos de alto nível em seções de design detalhadas (200-300 palavras) com pontos de verificação de validação integrados após cada segmento.","ru":"Позволяет осуществлять совместное, итеративное усовершенствование идей посредством естественного диалога, систематически разбивая высокоуровневые концепции на подробные разделы дизайна (200-300 слов) с встроенными контрольными точками проверки после каждого сегмента.","ar":"يسمح بالتطوير التعاوني والمتكرر للأفكار من خلال الحوار الطبيعي، وقسم Concepts عالية المستوى إلى أقسام تصميم مفصلة (200-300 كلمة) مع نقاط تحقق متكاملة بعد كل قسم."},"useCases":{"en":["Refining protocol mechanics for DeFi applications","Structuring technical documentation from initial concepts","Converting user stories into system architecture specs"],"zh":["为DeFi应用程序改进协议机制","从初始概念结构化技术文档","将用户故事转换为系统架构规格"],"ja":["DeFiアプリケーションのプロトコルメカニズムを改良する","初期概念から技術文書を構造化する","ユーザーストーリーをシステムアーキテクチャ仕様に変換する"],"ko":["DeFi 애플리케이션의 프로토콜 메커니즘을 개선하는 것","초기 개념에서 기술 문서를 구조화하는 것","사용자 스토리를 시스템 아키텍처 사양으로 변환하는 것"],"es":["Perfeccionar la mecánica de protocolos para aplicaciones DeFi","Estructurar la documentación técnica a partir de conceptos iniciales","Convertir historias de usuario en especificaciones de arquitectura de sistema"],"fr":["Affiner la mécanique de protocole pour les applications DeFi","Structurer la documentation technique à partir de concepts initiaux","Convertir les histoires d''utilisateurs en spécifications d''architecture de système"],"de":["Verfeinern der Protokollmechanik für DeFi-Anwendungen","Strukturieren der technischen Dokumentation aus anfänglichen Konzepten","Umwandeln von Benutzerstories in Systemarchitekturspezifikationen"],"pt":["Aperfeiçoamento da mecânica de protocolos para aplicações DeFi","Estruturação da documentação técnica a partir de conceitos iniciais","Conversão de histórias de usuário em especificações de arquitetura de sistema"],"ru":["Усовершенствование протокольной механики для приложений DeFi","Структуризация технической документации из начальных концепций","Преобразование историй пользователей в спецификации системной архитектуры"],"ar":["تحسين ميكانيكا البروتوكول لتطبيقات DeFi","هيكلة الوثائق الفنية من المفاهيم الأولية","تحويل قصص المستخدمين إلى مواصفات هندسة النظام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of current project context/files first","Iterative process mandates sequential approval per design section"],"zh":["需要先了解当前项目的上下文/文件","迭代过程需要每个设计部分的顺序批准"],"ja":["現在のプロジェクトのコンテキスト/ファイルを最初に理解する必要がある","反復プロセスでは設計セクションごとの順次承認が必要"],"ko":["현재 프로젝트의 컨텍스트/파일을 먼저 이해해야 함","반복 프로세스에서는 설계 섹션당 순차적 승인이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere una comprensión del contexto/proyecto actual/archivos primero","El proceso iterativo exige una aprobación secuencial por sección de diseño"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du contexte/projet actuel/fichiers d''abord","Le processus itératif exige une approbation séquentielle par section de conception"],"de":["Erfordert ein Verständnis des aktuellen Projekt/Kontext/Dateien zuerst","Der iterative Prozess erfordert eine sequenzielle Genehmigung pro Designabschnitt"],"pt":["Exige compreensão do contexto/projeto de arquivos atuais primeiro","O processo iterativo exige aprovação sequencial por seção de design"],"ru":["Требует понимания текущего контекста/файлов проекта сначала","Итеративный процесс требует последовательного утверждения каждого раздела дизайна"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم السياق/ملفات المشروع الحالي أولاً","يتطلب عملية متكررة موافقة متتالية لكل قسم من أقسام التصميم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/writing-git-commits', 'community', 'Paxeer-Network', 'Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'writing-git-commits', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.511Z', '2026-02-18T12:39:40.035Z', NULL, '{"id":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/writing-git-commits","name":"writing-git-commits","description":{"zh":"Git, Conventional Commits.","ja":"GitConventional Commits.","ko":"Git, Conventional Commits.","es":"Masters the art of semantic commit messages with Conventional Commits, enabling automated tooling and clear history","fr":"Maîtrisez l''art des messages de commit sémantiques avec Conventional Commits, permettant un outillage automatisé et un historique clair","de":"Meistern Sie die Kunst der semantischen Commit-Nachrichten mit Conventional Commits, ermöglichen Sie automatisierte Tools und eine klare Historie","pt":"Domine a arte de escrever mensagens de commit semânticas que comunicam intenção a humanos e máquinas","ru":"Освойте искусство написания семантических сообщений о коммитах, которые передают намерение как людям, так и машинам","ar":"استخدم مهارة كتابة رسائل الالتزام الدلالية التي تواصل النية مع البشر والآلات","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a cus..."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Git ","ja":"Git","ko":"Git ","es":"Comits de Git Efectivos","fr":"Commits Git de Qualité","de":"Effektive Git-Commits","pt":"Escrevendo Commits Git Eficazes","ru":"Написание эффективных коммитов Git","ar":"كتابة تعليقات جيت المحفوظة بفعالية","en":"writing-git-commits"},"description":{"zh":"Git, Conventional Commits.","ja":"GitConventional Commits.","ko":"Git, Conventional Commits.","es":"Masters the art of semantic commit messages with Conventional Commits, enabling automated tooling and clear history","fr":"Maîtrisez l''art des messages de commit sémantiques avec Conventional Commits, permettant un outillage automatisé et un historique clair","de":"Meistern Sie die Kunst der semantischen Commit-Nachrichten mit Conventional Commits, ermöglichen Sie automatisierte Tools und eine klare Historie","pt":"Domine a arte de escrever mensagens de commit semânticas que comunicam intenção a humanos e máquinas","ru":"Освойте искусство написания семантических сообщений о коммитах, которые передают намерение как людям, так и машинам","ar":"استخدم مهارة كتابة رسائل الالتزام الدلالية التي تواصل النية مع البشر والآلات","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collater..."},"definition":{"en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"zh":["Conventional Commits","Git","Semantic Commit","Automated Tooling","Clear History","Effective Collaboration"],"ja":["Conventional Commits","Git","Semantic Commit","Automated Tooling","Clear History","Effective Collaboration"],"ko":["Conventional Commits","Git ","Semantic Commit","Automated Tooling","Clear History","Effective Collaboration"],"es":["Comits semánticos","Especificación Conventional Commits","Automatización de herramientas","Historial claro","Colaboración efectiva"],"fr":["Commits sémantiques","Spécification Conventional Commits","Automatisation d''outils","Historique clair","Collaboration efficace"],"de":["Semantische Commits","Conventional Commits-Spezifikation","Automatisierung von Tools","Klare Historie","Effektive Zusammenarbeit"],"pt":["Mensagens de commit claras e concisas","Suporte a automação de ferramentas","Histórico claro e colaboração eficaz","Compatibilidade com Conventional Commits"],"ru":["Четкие и краткие сообщения о коммитах","Поддержка автоматизации инструментов","Четкая история и эффективное сотрудничество","Совместимость с Conventional Commits"],"ar":["رسائل الالتزام واضحة وموجزة","دعم آلي لأدوات الت 자동","سجل واضح وتعاون فعال","متوافق مع مواصفات الالتزامات التقليدية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git","Conventional Commits","Semantic Commit","Automated Tooling","Git Commit","Collaboration","Version Control"],"ja":["Git","Conventional Commits","Semantic Commit","Automated Tooling","Git Commit","Collaboration","Version Control"],"ko":["Git","Conventional Commits","Semantic Commit","Automated Tooling","Git ","Collaboration","Version Control"],"es":["comits de Git","Conventional Commits","semántica","automatización","colaboración","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["commits Git","Conventional Commits","sémantique","automatisation","collaboration","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Git-Commits","Conventional Commits","Semantik","Automatisierung","Zusammenarbeit","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["Commits Git","Conventional Commits","Mensagens de commit semânticas","Automatização de ferramentas","Colaboração de desenvolvimento","Desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Коммиты Git","Conventional Commits","Семантические сообщения о коммитах","Автоматизация инструментов","Сотрудничество разработчиков","Разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["التزامات جيت","مواصفات الالتزامات التقليدية","رسائل الالتزام الدلالية","آلية أدوات الت 자동","تعاون مبرمجي البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.511Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"writing-git-commits","description":"Expert guide to writing semantic commit messages following the Conventional Commits specification. Master clear, machine-readable commits that communicate intent and drive automation.","bodyPreview":"# Writing Great Git Commits\n\nYou are mastering the art of semantic commit messages that communicate intent to both humans and machines. Follow the Conventional Commits specification to create commits that enable automated tooling, clear history, and effective collaboration.\n\n## What is Conventional Commits?\n\n**Conventional Commits** is a lightweight specification for adding human and machine-readable meaning to commit messages. It provides a simple set of rules for creating an explicit commit hi","body":"# Writing Great Git Commits\n\nYou are mastering the art of semantic commit messages that communicate intent to both humans and machines. Follow the Conventional Commits specification to create commits that enable automated tooling, clear history, and effective collaboration.\n\n## What is Conventional Commits?\n\n**Conventional Commits** is a lightweight specification for adding human and machine-readable meaning to commit messages. It provides a simple set of rules for creating an explicit commit history that:\n\n- Enables automated tools to parse and act on commits\n- Makes it easier to understand code history at a glance\n- Aligns with Semantic Versioning (SemVer) for automated release management\n- Drives more organized development practices\n\n## Child Skills\n\n- **Summary**: Quick overview of the specification and core concepts\n  - → See `./summary/SKILL.md`\n    - or if needed `skill_use(superpowers_writing_git_commits_summary)`\n\n- **Examples**: Real-world commit message examples for different scenarios\n  - → See `./examples/SKILL.md`\n    - or if needed `skill_use(superpowers_writing_git_commits_examples)`\n  \n- **Specification**: Complete technical specification with all rules and requirements\n  - → See `./specification/SKILL.md`\n    - or if needed `skill_use(superpowers_writing_git_commits_specification)`\n  \n- **FAQ**: Frequently asked questions and practical guidance\n  - → See `./faq/SKILL.md`\n    - or if needed `skill_use(superpowers_writing_git_commits_faq)`\n\n## Basic Structure\n\nEvery commit message should follow this format:\n\n```\n<type>[optional scope]: <description>\n\n[optional body]\n\n[optional footer(s)]\n```\n\n## Core Commit Types\n\n- **feat**: Introduces a new feature (maps to `MINOR` in SemVer)\n- **fix**: Patches a bug (maps to `PATCH` in SemVer)\n- **BREAKING CHANGE**: Major breaking change (maps to `MAJOR` in SemVer)\n- **docs**: Documentation changes\n- **style**: Code style changes (formatting, missing semicolons, etc.)\n- **refactor**: Code refactoring without feature changes\n- **perf**: Performance improvements\n- **test**: Adding or updating tests\n- **chore**: Build, dependencies, or tooling changes\n- **ci**: CI/CD configuration changes\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse the Conventional Commits specification when:\n- Creating semantic commit messages for version-controlled code\n- Working in teams that need clear commit history\n- Building automated tools that parse commit messages\n- Integrating with semantic versioning practices\n- Generating automated CHANGELOGs\n- Communicating the nature of changes to stakeholders\n\n## How to Apply It\n\n1. **Read the Summary** for quick understanding of the core concept\n2. **Review Examples** to see how different scenarios map to commit types\n3. **Check the Specification** for detailed rules and technical requirements\n4. **Consult the FAQ** for answers to common questions and best practices\n\n## Key Principles\n\n✅ **Be Clear**: Commit messages should clearly communicate what changed and why\n✅ **Be Consistent**: Use the same convention across all commits\n✅ **Be Structured**: Follow the type/scope/description format\n✅ **Be Atomic**: One logical change per commit when possible\n✅ **Be Machine-Readable**: Enable automated tooling and analysis\n\n## Integration with Your Workflow\n\nThis skill is referenced by `/project:do:commit` to guide the creation of semantic commits that maintain a clear, organized commit history and enable automated tooling for release management and changelog generation.\n\n---\n\n**License**: [Creative Commons - CC BY 3.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/)\n\nSource: [Conventional Commits v1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T12:39:40.035Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing standardized commit message formatting and automated tooling integration.","zh":"非常适合需要标准化提交消息格式和自动化工具集成的开发代理。","ja":"標準化されたコミットメッセージのフォーマットと自動化ツールの統合を必要とする開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"표준화된 커밋 메시지 형식 및 자동화 도구 통합이 필요한 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo que necesitan un formato de mensaje de confirmación estandarizado y una integración de herramientas automatizadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''un format de message de validation standardisé et d''une intégration d''outils automatisés.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die ein standardisiertes Commit-Nachrichten-Format und eine automatisierte Integration von Werkzeugen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de formatação de mensagens de commit padronizadas e integração de ferramentas automatizadas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходима стандартизированная форматировка сообщений о коммитах и интеграция автоматизированных инструментов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النموزجيون الذين يحتاجون إلى تنسيق رسائل الالتزام المعيارية وتكامل الأدوات الآلية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create semantic commit messages following the Conventional Commits specification, enabling clear history, effective collaboration, and automated tooling using commit messages that communicate intent to both humans and machines.","zh":"赋予代理创建遵循约定提交规范的语义化提交消息的能力，从而实现清晰的历史记录、有效的协作和自动化工具，使用提交消息传达意图给人类和机器。","ja":"エージェントがConventional Commitsの仕様に従ったセマンティックコミットメッセージを作成する能力を提供し、クリアな履歴、効果的なコラボレーション、コミットメッセージを使用した自動化ツールを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 약定的 커밋 규격에 따라 의미있는 커밋 메시지를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, 명확한 기록, 효과적인 협업 및 커밋 메시지를 사용한 자동화 도구를 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear mensajes de confirmación semánticos siguiendo la especificación Conventional Commits, lo que permite una historia clara, una colaboración efectiva y una automatización de herramientas utilizando mensajes de confirmación que comunican la intención a humanos y máquinas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des messages de validation sémantiques suivant la spécification Conventional Commits, ce qui permet une histoire claire, une collaboration efficace et une automatisation d''outils à l''aide de messages de validation qui communiquent l''intention aux humains et aux machines.","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, semantische Commit-Nachrichten zu erstellen, die der Konventionellen Commits-Spezifikation folgen, sodass eine klare Historie, eine effektive Zusammenarbeit und eine Automatisierung von Werkzeugen mithilfe von Commit-Nachrichten ermöglicht wird, die die Absicht sowohl Menschen als auch Maschinen mitteilen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criarem mensagens de commit semânticas seguindo a especificação Conventional Commits, permitindo uma história clara, colaboração eficaz e integração de ferramentas automatizadas usando mensagens de commit que comunicam intenção tanto para humanos quanto para máquinas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать семантические сообщения о коммитах в соответствии со спецификацией Conventional Commits, обеспечивая ясную историю, эффективное сотрудничество и автоматизированное использование инструментов посредством сообщений о коммитах, передающих намерения как людям, так и машинам.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء رسائل الالتزام الدلالية اتباعًا لمواصفات الالتزامات التقليدية، مما يتيح تاريخًا واضحًا وتعاونًا فعالًا وتكامل أدوات آلي باستخدام رسائل الالتزام التي تت沟ب النية إلى البشر والآلات على حد سواء."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit message validation","Generating change logs based on commit history","Standardizing commit messages for collaborative projects"],"zh":["自动化提交消息验证","根据提交历史生成变更记录","标准化协作项目的提交消息"],"ja":["コミットメッセージの検証を自動化する","コミット履歴に基づいて変更ログを生成する","コラボレーションプロジェクトのコミットメッセージを標準化する"],"ko":["커밋 메시지 검증 자동화","커밋 기록을 기반으로 변경 로그 생성","협업 프로젝트를 위한 커밋 메시지 표준화"],"es":["Automatización de la validación de mensajes de confirmación","Generación de registros de cambios en función de la historia de confirmaciones","Estandarización de mensajes de confirmación para proyectos colaborativos"],"fr":["Automatisation de la validation des messages de validation","Génération de journaux de modifications en fonction de l''historique de validation","Standardisation des messages de validation pour les projets collaboratifs"],"de":["Automatisierung der Überprüfung von Commit-Nachrichten","Erstellung von Änderungsprotokollen auf der Grundlage der Commit-Historie","Standardisierung von Commit-Nachrichten für gemeinsame Projekte"],"pt":["Automatizar a validação de mensagens de commit","Gerar registros de alterações com base na história de commits","Padronizar mensagens de commit para projetos colaborativos"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверку сообщений о коммитах","Генерировать журналы изменений на основе истории коммитов","Стандартизировать сообщения о коммитах для совместных проектов"],"ar":["تأتمتة التحقق من صحة رسائل الالتزام","توليد سجلات التغييرات على أساس تاريخ الالتزامات","تقييس رسائل الالتزام للمشاريع التعاونية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to Conventional Commits specification","Limited to Git version control system"],"zh":["需要遵守约定提交规范","仅限于Git版本控制系统"],"ja":["Conventional Commitsの仕様に従わなければならない","Gitバージョン管理システムのみに限定される"],"ko":["약定的 커밋 규격을遵守해야 함","Git 버전 관리 시스템에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la adhesión a la especificación Conventional Commits","Limitado al sistema de control de versiones Git"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion à la spécification Conventional Commits","Limité au système de contrôle de version Git"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung der Konventionellen Commits-Spezifikation","Begrenzt auf das Git-versionskontrollsystem"],"pt":["Exige aderência à especificação Conventional Commits","Limitado ao sistema de controle de versão Git"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения спецификации Conventional Commits","Ограничен системой контроля версий Git"],"ar":["يتطلب اتباعًا لمواصفات الالتزامات التقليدية","محدود بنظام التحكم في الإصدار Git"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
